window.AKK_THE_BEAUTIFUL_STEPMOTHER_FROM_THE_EIGHTIES_MARRYING_A_FACTORY_DIRECTOR_TO_RAISE_KIDS_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_THE_BEAUTIFUL_STEPMOTHER_FROM_THE_EIGHTIES_MARRYING_A_FACTORY_DIRECTOR_TO_RAISE_KIDS_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":301,"title":"Chapter 301: Clue","paragraphs":["The other person glanced back at him and laughed, \"You even have to ask such a simple question, you're really dumb.\"","And they call it the best elementary school in the city center. It doesn't seem as impressive as the rumors say.","\"Teacher, my tummy hurts, I need to poop.\"","\"Why do you have so many problems?\"","Zhou Zehan immediately let out two loud \"pfft—\" farts in a row, startling the man who quickly changed his tune. Waving a hand in front of his nose and rolling down the window with the other, he said, \"Kid, don't you dare poop in my car. Lao Wang, find a place to pull over.\"","The man driving looked around warily, and seeing no other cars, finally stopped.","Zhou Zehan immediately said, \"Teacher, I don't have any paper.\"","The two men's faces turned green. \"What paper? Just use a couple of tree leaves!\"","Zhou Zehan wrinkled his nose in disdain. \"No way, that's dirty.\"","After saying that, he looked left and right, picked up a notebook nearby, tore off two sheets of paper, and said, \"I'll use this.\"","The two men hurriedly waved him off, telling him to hurry up.","Zhou Zehan, clutching his stomach, got out of the car and followed one of the men to the side to do his business.","There was nothing around, just empty space and a broken road.","He looked around, twisted his butt, and squatted down. Seeing the man come closer, he said, \"Teacher, stay farther away. My poop is really smelly.\"","He then let out a few more farts.","The man halted his steps, immediately turned around, and walked away. \"Hurry the hell up!\"","Seeing the man turn his back, a glint flashed in the little boy's eyes.","...","Downtown.","The police had already begun their search.","Child trafficking incidents had been happening for a long time. There had been children going missing before, though not many. This time, with so many disappearing at once, the entire police station was in an uproar.","A team led by Captain Li began a carpet search.","Even though there were no surveillance cameras, there was only one main road leading out of the city.","The worry now was that if they had already left the city, finding them would be difficult.","In this era without cameras, once a vehicle left the city center, it meant these children would be extremely hard to recover.","Searching for them would be like looking for a needle in a haystack.","This was also why human traffickers were so rampant during this time.","The police contacted all roads to set up blockades and investigations.","However, as time passed, there was no news.","The parents had started causing a commotion, especially the parents of Class Four. Upon hearing their children were missing, some nearly fainted.","Besides their children, the school principal's granddaughter, Chu Xiang'er, and Director Li's grandson, Li Youcai, were also missing.","The whole school was in chaos.","The principal seemed to have aged ten years overnight, and Director Li was collapsed on the ground, wailing and crying for her parents.","She only had this one precious grandson. If he were really sold to some remote village, how could she go on living!","The disappearances of Jiang Jiu and Xiao Han were also full of oddities.","Because the group that went missing were clearly from the fourth grade.","So why would Xiao Han and Jiang Jiu disappear with them?","After collecting herself, Si Nian began to speculate.","At a time like this, it was crucial not to panic, or important clues could easily be overlooked.","Although Xiao Han seemed a bit slow, he wasn't that foolish. She had taught him not to talk to strangers, not to take food from strangers, let alone go with them.","For him to be taken away so quietly, these people must have drugged the children?","But with so many children and the traffickers having only one van.","They definitely couldn't have fit everyone, and traffickers never operated in large groups.","From this, she guessed the traffickers were few in number, maybe two or three.","But even two or three people would find it almost impossible to drug and quietly take away so many children at once.","Especially not the Second Child. He would only ask others for food, but if someone offered it to him, he would absolutely not take it!","So there must have been someone helping, drugging a group of children simultaneously, which was why they left so quickly.","In other words, among their group of teachers, there was very likely an accomplice.","The only person in the whole school capable of such a heinous act was probably just one.","Teacher Xu.","Si Nian immediately looked in Teacher Xu's direction.","She stood at the back of the crowd, head bowed, watching the wailing Director Li and the parents, her lips pressed tightly together.","She seemed to be holding something back.","Si Nian clenched her fists.","Yes, it must be her.","She pulled aside the dazed Wang Xiaoli and walked to the entrance.","\"What is it, Teacher Si?\"","Si Nian asked, \"Do you know if anything has happened around Teacher Xu recently? The more specific, the better.\"","She had heard from Wang Xiaoli that she and Teacher Xu lived in the same building.","Wang Xiaoli usually complained about Teacher Xu to her when she had nothing better to do.","They were the type who couldn't stand the sight of each other anyway.","Hearing this, Wang Xiaoli came to her senses and said, \"You're asking about her, could it be...\"","Si Nian gave her a look, and she immediately stopped.","After thinking carefully, Wang Xiaoli said, \"Teacher Xu isn't doing so great either. Even though the fourth-grade parents demanded she come back to teach and she kept her job, these past few days some parents have been blocking her at her building demanding refunds.\"","\"You know about Director Li's tutoring class, right?\"","Si Nian nodded.","Wang Xiaoli continued, \"Because of the school situation, the Li family closed the tutoring class to lay low. Now lots of people are clamoring for refunds. Not sure if the Li family is unwilling to pay or what, but the parents Teacher Xu referred there came to her for the money. Teacher Xu is so stingy, of course she refused. Then she got threatened...\"","\"Threatened?\" Si Nian was surprised.","\"Yes,\" Wang Xiaoli said. \"Someone wrote on our building with paint, telling her to pay back the money, cursing her. I heard if Teacher Xu didn't pay, they'd take her son to settle the debt! Those people hired debt collectors to help, it's really scary. Now everyone in our building avoids her, afraid of getting involved.\"","\"Teacher Xu referred so many kids over the years. With that much money, the Li family doesn't want to pay it back. Those people don't dare mess with the Li family, so they go after her. She's only putting on a brave face. Her husband is even talking about divorcing her...\"","Wang Xiaoli could go on and on about gossip.","But it was useful.","Si Nian suddenly understood why Li Youcai and the principal's granddaughter Chu Xiang'er were kidnapped.","They seemed like the two children Teacher Xu valued most. No one would ever suspect her.","But thinking about it carefully, during the last competition, Li Youcai had even pushed her. Probably after it blew up, Director Li also shifted the blame onto her.","Plus the principal lecturing her every other day.","With her already ruthless personality, it would be strange if Teacher Xu didn't resent them and turn to the dark side.","The Eldest Child leaving Class Four was definitely the right move.","But why were the Second Child and Jiang Jiu dragged into this?","With Jiang Jiu missing, the Jiang family was also in an uproar!","Division Commander Jiang hadn't yet recovered from the earlier incident of his subordinate's child going missing. He never expected the traffickers would dare kidnap his own grandson. He flew into a rage and mobilized his forces, determined to bring these people to justice.","For a time, the entire city center was on edge.","The news that the division commander's grandson and several schoolchildren had been kidnapped by traffickers quickly spread far and wide.","After learning the situation from Wang Xiaoli, Si Nian immediately went to find Captain Li and his team, who were preparing to set out.","\"Sister-in-law, don't worry. I will definitely help you find Xiaohan!\" Captain Li looked at her, full of remorse."]},{"number":302,"title":"Chapter 302: Abducted and Taken Home","paragraphs":["When Zhou Yueshen left, he had asked Captain Li to keep an eye on things. Worried about the children, Captain Li had often arranged patrols near Old East Street.","Who could have guessed that even so, the child still went missing.","Captain Li's expression was extremely grim.","Si Nian nodded and said, \"Captain Li, I came to tell you something.\"","She shared her suspicions with Captain Li.","After hearing her out, Captain Li's face changed dramatically: \"Is such a thing really possible?\"","Si Nian nodded: \"It would be best if we could get something out of Teacher Xu, but I'm afraid she might stubbornly deny everything. So, I hope you won't make this public for now. Investigate privately whether she has had any undisclosed contact with anyone recently.\"","\"I understand, sister-in-law. Don't worry, leave this matter to me!\"","Captain Li never expected school teachers to be involved in such a scheme.","This would explain why so many children could disappear without a trace, completely unnoticed.","Captain Li's face was dark.","The car drove further and further into the remote countryside. Even Jiang Jiu began to sense something was wrong.","They had been driving for several hours, and these older siblings still hadn't woken up.","The man in the front passenger seat was asleep, and the other was driving in silence.","Zhou Zehan looked at the mountains drawing closer outside, feeling a sense of familiarity, as if he had seen them before, but he couldn't quite place it at the moment.","He scribbled and drew with a pen for a while, then complained of car sickness, leaning against the window and retching.","The driver kept glancing at the two children in the rearview mirror. Seeing them quiet and well-behaved, looking listless, he let his guard down even more.","Soon, the car began to sway and bump violently.","As dusk fell, the scenery outside became indistinguishable.","Jiang Jiu, tired, had fallen asleep. Perhaps being next to Second Child gave him a strong sense of security.","Although things felt off, seeing that Second Child wasn't saying anything, he didn't dwell on it, leaning on Second Child's shoulder and snoring loudly.","Second Child pressed against the car window, straining to see the passing landscape.","The two men, thinking he was just carsick, didn't pay it much mind.","Soon, the car stopped.","The two men got out with flashlights. Zhou Zehan also saw someone approaching with a flashlight to talk.","He could faintly hear the group discussing prices, haggling over some amount.","He was just about to toss out the note in his hand when he heard the approaching old man speak in an excited tone.","The voice sounded familiar.","Zhou Zehan stopped and looked carefully. Suddenly, he realized this man was Old Man Wang from their village!","Turning to look, he was stunned—wasn't this his hometown, Xingfu Village?","In the distance, he could even see the pig farm his father ran. Because someone had to keep watch at night, lights were on, making it clearly visible.","In the whole village, only his family and his father's pig farm could afford to use electricity at night.","When he went to bed at night, he would always look over from the second floor of his house.","Plus, his house was the closest to the village entrance. Now, his eyes adjusted to the darkness, and he could vaguely make out his own home.","Soon, a trafficker came over, carrying a sleeping boy, and boasted, \"Let me tell you, this kid is very smart, top of his class. You should pay at least 500. He'll have no problem taking care of you in your old age!\"","Just as the trafficker and the buyer were haggling fiercely, Zhou Zehan suddenly scrambled out of the car window and shot off like an arrow toward the pig farm.","The traffickers were dumbfounded. Reacting, they hurriedly gave chase.","But who would have thought this little kid could run so incredibly fast?","The two men were unfamiliar with the area. Combined with the poor, dark road, their speed dropped drastically.","In no time, Zhou Zehan had dashed far ahead.","The two men watched, stunned.","Coming to their senses, their faces turned green with anger: \"That little brat! Hurry up and catch him!\"","\"Forget it, we have enough 'goods' anyway. Less trouble is better. Let's finish selling and get out of here,\" the other said, finding it troublesome.","\"No way! If we're discovered, we're done for. Hurry up!\"","Hearing this, the other immediately joined the chase.","Sure enough, they soon saw Zhou Zehan at the gate of a farm, yelling and making a racket.","\"Uncle Wang! Uncle Liu! Uncle Zhang! Open up! There are traffickers chasing me!\"","The man's face turned green. Knowing he was exposed, he dropped all pretense, shouting at Zhou Zehan, \"You little runt! No one in this village will save you. Come with me quietly, and I might still find you a good family.\"","He said this while charging over with a club. But the next second, the iron gate swung open, and several burly men rushed out wielding machetes.","Seeing Zhou Zehan at the gate, they had no time to be shocked. Brandishing their machetes, they charged at the man.","\"How dare you, you trafficker! You even dare to kidnap our boss's son? Looking to die?\"","The scrawny trafficker was quickly kicked to the ground, letting out a pig-like squeal.","Zhou Zehan didn't care about his fate. He urgently pulled a few men toward the village entrance: \"Uncle Wang, Uncle Liu, my friend is still in the car! And lots of other classmates.\"","He gestured exaggeratedly, depicting a car full of classmates slumped over asleep. Sure enough, when they arrived, they saw the other trafficker holding a child and talking to the buyer, \"This is the youngest one we have on the truck, still doesn't understand much. If you teach him well now, he'll definitely treat you like his own father and be filial...\"","Zhou Zehan looked over and saw he was holding Jiang Jiu.","Furious, he rushed over and slammed into the trafficker.","The trafficker had been planning to quickly sell the child and then find his partner to leave.","He never expected so many people to suddenly appear and was completely stunned.","By the time he reacted, he was surrounded by a group of burly men and given a severe beating.","Zhou Zehan, still seething, also ran over and delivered a couple of hard kicks.","How dare they try to sell Jiang Jiu too! It made him furious.","Jiang Jiu rubbed his eyes awake. Seeing so many people, he was still confused: \"Wh-where is this?\"","\"Second Child?\"","Zhou Zehan patted his head and said, \"This is my hometown. I'll take you to my house to play later. Let me tell you, my house is really big too!\"","\"Really? You brought me to your hometown to play?\"","The two children chatted away as if no one else was around, while beside them, the two traffickers were soon beaten to a pulp on the ground.","Old Man Wang was also stunned. After being punched several times, he came to his senses and cried, \"I'm not in cahoots with traffickers! They said these kids were orphans from the city, unwanted, that they were pitiful with no parents to find... I just spent money to buy one to take care of me in my old age...\"","Village Chief Huo was quickly alerted, and the entire village came running. Seeing Second Child had returned home, everyone was bewildered.","But upon hearing he had been kidnapped and brought back, everyone fell silent.","Good grief. Finally made it to the city, only to get kidnapped right back to where he started."]},{"number":303,"title":"Chapter 303: Looking Around, Gun in Hand, Heart Adrift (Bonus Chapter)","paragraphs":["It's hard to say whether it was his misfortune or his luck.","Village Chief Huo hurriedly had someone call the police and also phoned the city breeding farm.","Because when Zhou Yueshen left, he had entrusted the farm to him.","The two parties were in frequent contact.","Yu Dong had heard about Zhou Zehan's disappearance and kidnapping and was rallying relatives, friends, and all available resources to search for him.","Just as they were about to set out, they received Village Chief Huo's call saying the child had been found, in Xingfu Village.","Zhou Zehan paid no mind to the commotion outside, leading Jiang Jiu off to tour his family's pig farm.","The two even fed the piglets together.","They were very happy.","Finally tired, they went to sleep in his father's office.","The other children, who were still unconscious, were taken in by villagers.","Early the next morning, Si Nian, Captain Li, and people from the school and military arrived in Xingfu Village with great fanfare.","Over a dozen cars roared and sped along, startling passing villagers who stared dumbfounded.","Having lived so many years, it was the first time they had witnessed such a spectacle.","Everyone followed to watch.","When Captain Wang and the others arrived, the two scrawny traffickers were tied to a tree stump, beaten black and blue, half-dead.","Several tall, burly men stood nearby carrying cleavers, their eyes fierce.","For a moment, it was hard to tell who the real criminals were.","The group of children had also woken up. Opening their eyes in an unfamiliar environment, several kids were completely bewildered.","The timid ones were already crying.","No matter how the villagers tried to soothe them, it didn't work.","Only when the parents arrived did the children, as if grasping a lifeline, throw themselves into their arms and burst into tears.","Si Nian looked at Xingfu Village, falling silent for a long, long time.","No matter how she looked at it, the situation felt surreal.","Not seeing her son, she hurried forward to ask the farm workers, \"Xiao Zhang, Xiao Liu, where's Little Han?\"","\"That's right, where's Jiang Jiu? Where has my grandson gone?\" Old Mrs. Jiang and her husband were also frantic with worry.","\"Sister-in-law, don't worry. Second Child and his classmate are resting in the Boss's office.\"","The worker led the group over.","Sure enough, they soon saw the two children hugging each other and sleeping soundly on the bed in Zhou Yueshen's office.","The two were sleeping deeply, not even stirred by so many people entering.","Their faces were rosy, clearly unharmed.","Si Nian and the Jiang family simultaneously breathed a sigh of relief.","Captain Li wiped the sweat from his brow, also relieved, and said, \"Sister-in-law, since the children are fine, I'll take those traffickers to the station first. If anything comes up, contact me anytime.\"","Si Nian nodded.","Captain Li left with his men.","The villagers also reported the incident to the police.","Although Old Man Wang insisted he was adopting the children, buying and selling carry the same penalty, so he was also arrested.","Meanwhile, the search team, following the trail, had pursued it all the way to Xingfu Village, just running into the group about to leave.","\"Huh? Captain, what are you all doing here too?\" The newcomers drew their guns, looking around in confusion.","Seeing two hooded men at the back and many vehicles parked around, they were somewhat bewildered.","\"What are you doing here?\" Captain Li was also puzzled.","One of them pulled a few crumpled pieces of paper from his pocket and said, \"While searching along the road, we found some paper left by a child. It had a route drawn on it, and we followed it here.\"","Captain Li was taken aback, took the papers, opened them, and looked. Indeed, the paper simply depicted a road and the approximate shapes of the mountains alongside it.","Although it looked odd, upon closer comparison, it matched the shapes of the mountains they had passed.","The side was marked with 1234, labeling several mountains.","It also stated there were two traffickers in the vehicle.","It just had a strange smell.","He picked it up and sniffed.","Si Nian also walked over, leading Second Child who was rubbing his eyes, and asked, \"What's wrong?\"","\"A child left some paper clues, and my search team found them,\" Captain Li said. \"It just has a strange smell.\"","Upon hearing this, Zhou Zehan looked over and let out an \"Oh!\"","\"Uncle Li, that's my toilet paper.\"","Captain Li: \"...\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","The search team member who had been repeatedly examining and comparing the paper: \"...\"","Posted three chapters today. I'll see if I can write one or two more tonight. Adding gift changes. Not pushing myself, I never know how much I can write. Finally, the Gift Ranking Battle lasts three days! One vote from you, one vote from me, the Village Chief debuts tomorrow! Defend first place, charge, charge, charge!!!"]},{"number":304,"title":"Chapter 304: Mockery","paragraphs":["The Si household was bustling early in the morning when Zhang Cuimei received a call from her younger sister, Zhang Xiaoyun, informing her that Si Nian's adopted son had been kidnapped.","Zhang Xiaoyun worked at the Public Security Bureau. As soon as she arrived at the station that morning, she heard about the child abduction case at the Foreign Language Primary School. When she learned that one of the children was Si Nian's adopted son, she almost laughed out loud.","She immediately called Zhang Cuimei to share the news.","Back when she heard Si Nian was going to teach at the Foreign Language Primary School, she had privately asked Zhang Cuimei to help get her own son enrolled.","But Zhang Cuimei said Si Nian wouldn't even acknowledge her anymore.","She felt that her sister had raised a daughter who turned out to be nothing but an ungrateful wretch.","Upon hearing the news, Zhang Cuimei was first shocked, then sneered coldly: \"It's just an adopted son, not her own flesh and blood. Good riddance if he's gone.\"","\"Sis, you better be careful. If she can't find anyone to help, she might come bothering you and brother-in-law. I heard she's been pouring her heart and soul into those Zhou family kids, even managed to send all those country bumpkins to the Foreign Language Primary School.\"","\"Hmph!\" Zhang Cuimei retorted immediately, \"I won't help her. Even if she kneels and begs me, I won't lift a finger.\"","\"Back then, Sisi just made a momentary mistake, and she apologized! We even went to beg Si Nian and returned all the money! But her!\" Zhang Cuimei fumed, \"She showed no regard for our years of raising her, insisted on sending Sisi to jail, made Sisi suffer terribly in prison! What face does she have now to ask for our help?\"","\"So you're washing your hands of it?\" Zhang Xiaoyun gloated. \"Didn't I hear she only married into that family to take care of the kids? Now that a child is kidnapped, maybe the man will divorce her. She wouldn't dare come back and try to steal Fu Yang from your Sisi, would she?\"","\"How dare she!\" Zhang Cuimei raged. \"She's just damaged goods, already been married. How could she possibly be worthy of competing with Sisi for Fu Yang?\"","Lately, Zhang Cuimei had been at odds with her husband, who was rarely home.","On top of that, the Fu family clearly wanted nothing to do with them and even planned for Fu Yang to divorce their daughter once he returned.","Zhang Cuimei's resentment now ran deeper than any ghost's.","If Si Nian dared to show up now, she'd tear her to pieces.","She hung up the phone, immediately went to warn the guards at the gate, telling them under no circumstances to let Si Nian in if she came.","Then, seething with anger, she stormed over to Old East Street, eager to dash any hope Si Nian might have—they would absolutely not help her.","Sure enough, when she arrived at the Zhou residence, she saw two children, one big and one small, standing at the door.","The younger one, Yaoyao, seemed a bit frightened upon seeing her and hid behind Zhou Zedong.","Zhou Zedong frowned at the visitor.","He knew who this was—his mother's adoptive mother.","She was always very harsh with Mom, definitely not a good person.","\"Where's Si Nian? Where has she gone off to?\" Zhang Cuimei saw the two children standing dumbly at the door and paid them no mind as she asked.","Only then did Zhou Zedong look at her. \"My mom isn't home. Do you need something from her?\"","\"Not home? Fine, it's just as well. I don't want to see her anyway.\" Zhang Cuimei snorted coldly. She was genuinely worried that Si Nian might come begging, and if outsiders saw...","If she didn't help, it would look bad, and she was afraid of gossip.","After much thought, she decided to come herself and warn her.","\"Tell your mother not to come pestering us about your brother being kidnapped. Our Si family will absolutely not help her. She should give up that idea!\"","Hearing this, Zhou Zedong's eyes turned cold.","He knew his brother was missing and had suspected it might be a kidnapping.","Such things happened in their village when they were young; those taken never came back.","But he had kept comforting himself that his brother would surely be okay.","He never expected someone to just blurt it out like that.","The Eldest Child's expression turned sinister, his fists clenched.","Looking at her gloating, disdainful face, he said coldly, \"My mom would never beg you.\"","\"Hah, easy for you to say. Who knows where your father has gone? Maybe he's abandoned you all. Without your father, who else can help you?\" Zhang Cuimei had made inquiries. Zhou Yueshen had disappeared for quite some time, no one knew what happened.","It wasn't strange these days for men to abandon their wives and children.","In a situation like this, who could Si Nian turn to for help besides familiar acquaintances like them?","Even if Director Li was willing to help, that child might not necessarily be found.","\"Your brother is definitely not coming back. Serves you right! Blame Si Nian for doing too many wicked things, dragging you all down to suffer the consequences!\" All the resentment Zhang Cuimei had bottled up lately came pouring out.","Seeing Zhou Zedong's face grow paler and paler actually made her feel increasingly pleased.","Zhou Zedong's eyes reddened. \"You're lying! My brother will definitely be found!\"","Yaoyao, hearing that her second brother would never come back, was scared and started wailing.","Zhang Cuimei sneered, \"How am I lying? Aren't there plenty of kidnapping cases these days? Have you ever heard of anyone being found? You're just dreaming!\"","\"Don't you dare say bad things about my brother!\" Zhou Zedong charged at her angrily and shoved her.","Caught off guard, Zhang Cuimei fell to the ground with a cry of \"Ouch!\"","\"You little brat! Truly raised by a mother who doesn't know how to raise children!\"","\"Serves you right that your brother was kidnapped. You'll never see him again in this lifetime—\"","As soon as the words left her mouth, an icy female voice sounded from behind. \"Who are you saying 'serves right' to be kidnapped?\"","Zhang Cuimei froze, turned her head, and saw Si Nian walking towards them, holding a child's hand.","Seeing his brother, the younger boy immediately ran over.","\"Brother! Yaoyao! I'm back!\"","\"Xiao Han!\" Zhou Zedong's eyes widened in surprise and disbelief at the sight of his brother.","When he heard his brother had been taken by traffickers, he felt like the sky had fallen.","Thank goodness his brother was okay, thank goodness he was back...","Zhou Zedong's eyes were bloodshot, tears falling pattering down.","He hugged Zhou Zehan tightly, choking up, \"I'm sorry, Xiao Han. It's all my fault. From now on, I'll never go off to play by myself without you guys again. It's all my mistake.\"","Back in their village when they were little, there were child kidnappings, so Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan had always been inseparable.","But after moving to the city, he had grown complacent.","He thought his brother had made friends and didn't need him watching all the time.","Not keeping him company at home was bad enough, but even when going out to play, he got absorbed in number games.","And then he lost his brother.","He was truly useless.","Zhou Zedong's crying was heartbreaking.","Si Nian's cold gaze remained fixed on Zhang Cuimei.","She had heard Zhang Cuimei's taunting voice from afar.","The incident with the younger boy being kidnapped had hit the Eldest Child the hardest.","Last night, before she left, the look in his eyes had been utterly despairing.","And at a time like this, Zhang Cuimei came to pour oil on the fire and add insult to injury.","She was rotten to the core!","Si Nian had originally thought this person was merely selfish.","But now it seemed her assessment had been too generous.","Zhang Cuimei stared at her, rigid.","I really never imagined I could be so unlucky, to be caught red-handed while speaking ill of someone.","Grandma Jiang and Division Commander Jiang naturally heard it too, staring at her in disbelief with clear displeasure in their eyes.","Who on earth would curse a child like that?","It was simply too vicious!"]},{"number":305,"title":"Chapter 305: Teacher Xu Was Arrested","paragraphs":["\"Niannian, who is she?\"","Si Nian clenched her fists and said coldly, \"Division Commander Jiang, Auntie Jiang, you should know her too. She is my former foster mother, from Fu Yang's wife's maiden family.\"","\"What?\" Division Commander Jiang was stunned upon hearing this name.","\"Battalion Commander Si's family?\" Although he had been retired for a while, he was formerly the old division commander of the South China Military Region. Naturally, he knew of Si's father.","At this moment, his expression turned even uglier.","For a military family member to say such unforgivable things—it was simply shameful!","Zhang Cuimei hadn't noticed these two people initially. When she heard Si Nian address the man as \"Division Commander,\" she was completely dumbfounded.","Division Commander?","Division Commander?","Where did a Division Commander come from? Why hadn't she ever heard of this?","Could they be bluffing her?","Is a figure like a Division Commander someone you can just casually know?","Before Zhang Cuimei could recover her wits, several police cars drove up with sirens wailing.","Captain Li, leading the group, got out of the car and stepped forward. \"Sister-in-law, Uncle Jiang, the traffickers have already been taken in for interrogation. I know you've all had a huge scare, but the children might still need to go to the station to give statements.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, a few more cars pulled up.","Yu Dong ran over hurriedly with a group of brothers, along with Fu Qianqian and her mother.","\"Si Nian, Si Nian, are you okay? Is the child back?\"","Fu Qianqian rushed to the front, looking at her with concern.","Si Nian shook her head. \"I'm fine. He's been found.\"","Seeing the child, Ms. Zheng also breathed a sigh of relief. \"Niannian, you've suffered. When Qianqian and I heard about this early this morning, we asked your Uncle Fu to help look for him. Thank goodness the child is safe.\"","Yu Dong also rushed over, and the group shouted in unison, \"Sister-in-law!\"","\"Sister-in-law, we're late!\"","Si Nian looked up and saw people from the farm, as well as Yu Dong and the brothers from Zhou Yueshen's former auto repair shop.","Everyone looked at them with concern.","In this moment, even though Zhou Yueshen wasn't there, she still felt the warmth of being protected and cared for.","Zhang Cuimei was already scared witless by the imposing presence of these dozens of big, burly men.","It wasn't until Ms. Zheng let out a surprised \"Huh?\" from the side. \"Cuimei, why are you here? Did you hear about what happened and come over to help too?\"","Zhang Cuimei froze. Her mouth gaped open but no words came out, and she was sweating profusely.","Her in-laws were here; she couldn't exactly say she had come over to mock Si Nian, could she?","It was simply too awkward.","However, before she could find a suitable excuse, she heard the other woman exclaim in surprise, \"Division Commander Jiang, Mrs. Jiang, why are you here too?\"","After speaking, Ms. Zheng realized that behind them was the Jiang residence.","Having rushed over with her daughter just now, she hadn't paid attention to the location.","Only now did she realize that Si Nian's home was actually right next to the Jiangs'.","She looked astonished.","Division Commander Jiang nodded, then immediately gave a cold snort. \"Little Zheng, you really found yourself a 'good' set of in-laws!\"","Ms. Zheng was a bit confused.","Subconsciously, she glanced at Zhang Cuimei.","She saw that Zhang's face was pale and covered in cold sweat.","Her heart instantly skipped a beat.","Meanwhile, Zhang Cuimei was completely stupefied. All color drained from her face, as if she had been struck by lightning!","This man is a Division Commander?","A real Division Commander?","It's over—","\"Cuimei, what on earth is going on?\" Ms. Zheng asked anxiously.","Zhang Cuimei stammered, \"Mis... misunderstanding, it's a misunderstanding. You heard wrong. I also heard about the incident and hurried over to check on the child...\"","After she finished speaking, everyone stared at her with mockery.","Zhang Cuimei couldn't even keep up her own lie. She braced herself and said, \"Really, it was nothing...\"","\"You're lying! You clearly said my brother deserved to be trafficked, that my mom is immoral, and you told my mom to give up hope because you definitely wouldn't help us find my brother...\" Zhou Zedong shouted angrily.","The entire scene fell into a deathly silence.","Captain Li, Division Commander Jiang's family, Yu Dong's group, Fu Qianqian, Ms. Zheng, and everyone else glared at Zhang Cuimei with fury.","With such a serious incident, it was one thing not to help.","But to rush over just to mock them!","It was simply too wicked, too vicious.","Captain Li said angrily, \"Comrade Zhang, you are crossing the line. That is just a child. How could you say a child deserves it? How are you any different from the traffickers?\"","Yu Dong glared at her furiously. \"Are you even human? How could you say such outrageous things!\"","Fu Qianqian looked shocked. \"Auntie Si, how could you be like this?\"","Ms. Zheng looked utterly disappointed. \"Zhang Cuimei, I misjudged you. Have some decency!!\"","Division Commander Jiang said, \"I didn't expect a military family member to be someone so morally corrupt. It's truly shameful. If Battalion Commander Si has such poor judgment, he might as well stop being a Battalion Commander!\"","Si Nian looked at her with disgust. \"Get out. From now on, I have no ties with your Si family. Do not come to my house again!\"","Zhang Cuimei's head was buzzing.","Her mind was filled with only two words: It's over—","...","The traffickers were caught, and once they sobered up, they were quickly interrogated.","Sure enough, they had help.","Before long, Teacher Xu, who was packing her things to flee, was caught by the men Captain Li had sent to monitor her in advance.","At the entrance of the police station, many family members were waiting to judge the traffickers' atrocities.","When Teacher Xu was escorted out of the car, she looked up to see a row of parents staring at her with bloodshot eyes and livid faces.","The parents of the abducted children rushed over and slapped her several times. \"You vicious woman! You scum! We trusted you so much, spoke up for you, and let you return to the school to teach. Yet you conspired with traffickers to abduct our children! How did we ever wrong you? Bitch, go to hell!\"","Teacher Xu was slapped into a daze; her scalp and cheeks burned with agonizing pain.","But under the extreme terror she felt, she could barely feel the physical pain anymore.","\"I... I didn't! I was forced! I didn't mean to! I was forced to do it! I'm an innocent victim too...\"","How could the crowd listen to this? They slapped her several more times.","\"You are the scum of society. Go die.\"","\"We will never believe you again.\"","Teacher Xu was escorted into the station.","As soon as she entered, she saw the two captured traffickers.","Her legs gave out, and she collapsed to the ground.","\"Teacher Xu, the witness testimony and physical evidence are all here. What else do you have to say?\"","\"Why did you harm so many children? Don't you know that aiding traffickers in abducting people is a serious crime?\"","\"You really have guts as big as the sky, drugging seven at once!\"","Teacher Xu looked sluggish. \"Seven... seven? I didn't drug seven of them. You're talking nonsense. I only drugged five. Those other two kids have nothing to do with me!\"","At this moment, Si Nian and all the parents of the abducted children arrived.","Hearing this, the police shouted, \"You're still lying! There were clearly seven children in the van!\"","\"I... I really don't know how those two kids got in the van. It has nothing to do with me!\"","Teacher Xu's face was a mess of tears and snot. \"I do hate Si Nian, but her children really have nothing to do with me. I didn't do it on purpose, either. They forced me to do it. They said if I didn't help them, they would abduct my son. I had no choice!\"","\"Those two children were probably taken by them out of their own greed, who knows.\"","Hearing this, the two human traffickers flew into a rage.","\"Bitch, you're full of shit! We originally only wanted you to swap two people. You were the one who drugged so many children and handed them over to us, telling us to leave quickly. We were startled too, alright?\"","\"That's right! She didn't pay back her debts, so someone took her son and sold him to us. She said she would help us find better ones, and that's why we agreed.\"","\"It has nothing to do with us! How could we dare to abduct so many people at once!\"","Hearing this, Si Nian and Grandma Jiang simultaneously looked at the two children. \"Little Han, Jiang Jiu, how on earth did you two get abducted onto that vehicle?\"","\"Are they lying?\"","The two children were still a bit dazed and exchanged a glance upon hearing this.","Then Jiang Jiu said, \"We were playing hide-and-seek, and Second Brother and I hid inside the vehicle. Later, Xiao Liu and the others couldn't find us. We got sleepy and fell asleep. When I woke up, I was in Second Brother's hometown.\"","Jiang Jiu still didn't know that these people were human traffickers.","At this moment, his face was full of confusion.","Only then did it click, and he let out an \"Ah.\"","\"Grandma, are they human traffickers? Aren't they teachers?\"","Grandma Jiang: \"......\"","\"Alright, you don't need to speak anymore.\" How embarrassing.","(Keep the gifts coming, and the bonus chapters won't stop!! Come on, come on, you'll get to see the older man soon~~~~ For such an awesome author, are you really not going to give a ten thousand 'Generate Power for Love' boost?)"]},{"number":306,"title":"Chapter 306: Teacher Xu's Departure","paragraphs":["Si Nianye also twitched the corners of her mouth, not knowing whether to laugh or cry.","But then she got very angry after reacting. She tugged at Second Child's ear and said, \"Let's see if you dare to hide in someone else's car randomly in the future.\"","Second Child said guiltily, \"Mom, I was wrong. I, I won't dare to do it again.\"","Hearing that the two kids said they had hidden in the car while playing hide - and - seek, the others were all looking blank.","Hiding in a human trafficker's car?","No one plays better than you guys.","However, it was also because of these two kids that all the abducted people in this car were rescued.","Naturally, everyone cast grateful glances at the two kids.","The police came to ask questions. \"We heard from the search - and - rescue team that someone among you left clues on the road?\"","The other kids looked at each other and all shook their heads blankly.","When they woke up, they were already in the village.","They had no idea what had happened.","Only after hearing that they had been abducted by human traffickers did they belatedly feel scared.","How could they know about this?","Hearing this, Captain Zhang and the search - and - rescue team members twitched the corners of their mouths looking at the clue (a piece of paper) in his hand.","They turned their heads away and pretended not to see.","Zhou Zehan quickly raised his hand and said, \"Me, me, me. It was me who left the clues.\"","\"After we woke up from playing hide - and - seek, we found ourselves in their car.\" Zhou Zehan pointed at the two human traffickers.","The two human traffickers' faces turned green.","They wracked their brains but never thought that the two kids would leave clues for the police.","It meant that even if they weren't caught in Happy Village, they wouldn't be able to escape for long.","Were they deceived by this kid from the very beginning?","\"Oh?\" The person asking questions became interested. \"Then how did you secretly leave clues for the police?\"","Zhou Zehan said, \"I pretended to have a stomachache and then went to poop. I just took the paper out of the car by the way.\"","\"Hahaha, interesting. You're really a smart...\" The person asking questions was laughing when suddenly his hand froze and the laughter stopped abruptly.","\"Wait, what did you say?\" His hand trembled.","\"To poop.\" Zhou Zehan pointed at his hand and said, \"This is the paper I used to wipe my butt, Uncle Policeman.\"","The person asking questions: \"......\"","Someone couldn't help but let out a \"pfft\" laugh.","The policeman asking questions really wanted to throw away the paper in his hand immediately, but it was an important piece of evidence.","For the moment, he didn't know whether to throw it or not.","\"Hahaha, it's so funny!\"","\"Captain Zhang, you've got this today.\"","\"Hahaha...\"","\"This kid is so smart. Who would have thought there would be clues on the butt - wiping paper?\"","The two human traffickers' faces were contorted with anger. \"You little brat, you tricked us! Didn't you say you were doing your homework?\"","They really thought this kid was a bookworm who loved studying.","Because the nickname for the Foreign Language Primary School outside was the \"bookworm school\".","So even in that situation, when the kid said he was doing his homework, they didn't think much about it.","Unexpectedly, the other side was secretly leaving clues.","He was just a seven - or eight - year - old kid. How could he think of all these?","Moreover, didn't he always regard them as teachers?","Why did he know they were human traffickers and talk to them so calmly while leaving clues?","The more they thought about it, the more impossible it seemed. He didn't look like such a smart person at all.","\"Doing homework?\" Zhou Zehan laughed. \"We were going out to play. I'm not my elder brother. Who would take homework when going out to play? Hahaha! You guys are so stupid!\"","Two human traffickers were hit hard.","\"You... Then how did you know we were human traffickers?\"","Zhou Zehan replied, \"I didn't know.\"","The human traffickers exclaimed, \"What?\"","Zhou Zehan continued, \"Although I didn't know you were human traffickers, I was sure you weren't teachers.\"","The two traffickers glanced at each other and asked, \"You knew from the beginning that we weren't teachers?\"","Zhou Zehan nodded.","The police were also surprised and inquired, \"How did you figure it out?\"","Zhou Zehan explained, \"They called themselves 'Laozi'! Would a teacher address themselves like that?\"","The police thought, \"It makes sense.\"","The human traffickers admitted, \"It makes sense.\"","Everyone agreed, \"It really makes sense.\"","The human traffickers were fuming and said, \"You knew we weren't good people, yet you still dared to ask us for water?\"","Zhou Zehan said, \"Because I get diarrhea when I drink soda.\"","The human traffickers were speechless. \"Fine, so this is how you treat us. Are you playing with the little bit of kindness left in us?\"","Hearing this, Si Nian was also stunned.","Previously, when she took the child out to play and saw someone selling soda, seeing that Xiaohan wanted to drink it, she bought him a bottle. As a result, the child had diarrhea after drinking it and never dared to drink it again.","Unexpectedly, a bottle of soda became his tool for self - rescue.","The others were also shocked.","The faces of the human traffickers turned green.","The police said in admiration, \"Although you didn't know they were human traffickers, you were certain they weren't teachers and guessed they were bad people. So you pretended not to know and started looking for a chance to escape, right?\"","After saying that, the police added with admiration, \"Such courage is really astonishing.\"","Zhou Zehan blushed at the praise and wriggled behind Si Nian, saying, \"Even if you praise me, I won't be very happy.\"","The two human traffickers were completely heart - broken. They, two adults, had been led around by a child.","It was so embarrassing.","\"However, there's still one question. Why didn't you leave the province but instead sent the child to Happy Village?\"","The human traffickers were in despair and said, \"We originally planned to leave the province. But someone pulled some strings and contacted us, saying that there was an old man in Happy Village who was willing to use his pension to buy a child. We thought it was on the way, and we could sell the child and leave, so we sent the child there.\"","Who would have known that the child abducted from the city was actually from the countryside.","If they had known, they wouldn't have gone there even if they were beaten to death.","The corner of the policeman's mouth twitched, and he waved his hand, signaling to take them away.","With Teacher Xu arrested, the case of the missing children at the Foreign Language Primary School was finally closed.","This incident spread quickly and was talked about all over the city center.","Originally, people thought she was just a feudal - minded teacher, but who would have thought that she had hidden evil intentions and almost ruined several families.","\"I heard that she did this for the sake of her son. It's really a pity for a mother's love.\"","\"Pity my foot! For the sake of her own son, she almost got seven or eight students abducted to the countryside, causing so many families to be broken. What a pity? Are you out of your mind?\"","\"The human traffickers only wanted two children at first. She abducted so many children in order to take revenge on the school. Such a ruthless person doesn't deserve the title of teacher at all.\""]},{"number":307,"title":"Chapter 307: The World Would Fall Apart Without Me","paragraphs":["\"It's strange, wasn't she closest to Director Li? How did she end up kidnapping even Director Li's grandson?\"","\"You all don't know, do you? I heard the people she referred to the tutoring class all demanded refunds from her. To repay the money, Teacher Xu borrowed from loan sharks. That's why her son was taken and sold off. She probably blames Director Li for pushing her into a corner, which is why she sought revenge.\"","\"Apparently, the school was about to fire her, but it was the parents of Class Four who insisted Teacher Xu be reinstated, leading to the kidnapping case. I think those parents are accomplices and should be arrested too.\"","\"Exactly, serves them right. They only cared about their own children's grades, disregarded others' lives, and almost harmed their own kids in the end. What goes around comes around, karma spares no one.\"","While everyone enjoyed the gossip, this time no one stepped forward to speak up for her.","After Teacher Xu was arrested, the school immediately stepped forward and revoked her teaching qualification.","They also stated that if any parents were dissatisfied, the school would cooperate with withdrawal procedures.","That shut everyone up for good.","Teacher Xu was finally out of the picture.","The Zhou Zhedong and Zhou Zehan brothers became famous throughout the school.","As soon as Si Nian arrived at school, she saw many gifts piled on her desk.","There were fruits, eggs, and all sorts of children's clothes and toys.","They covered the entire desk.","She was utterly bewildered.","Wang Xiaoli beside her covered her mouth, laughing enviously. \"Hahaha, Teacher Si, surprised? Or shocked?\"","Si Nian: \"More like shocked. Where did all this come from?\"","\"These are gifts from the parents, led by Director Li and the principal, to thank your Xiao Han for saving their children.\"","\"After this incident, Director Li seems like a changed person. She just came by to say she was too ashamed to face you after all the trouble she caused before, so she just left the gifts and went away.\"","Si Nian: \"......\" Reformed?","Although it was somewhat unexpected, if Director Li stopped causing trouble for her from now on, then she would have no more enemies at the school.","Most people at the school were actually quite nice. It was just that oddball Teacher Xu and that inexplicable Director Li.","Although inexplicable, she truly doted on her grandson.","Now that Li Youcai had been saved by her own son, it would be really unreasonable if Director Li still targeted her.","Si Nian breathed a sigh of relief, feeling a sense of pride akin to \"my children have finally grown up.\"","The kids have grown up and already know how to solve their mother's problems.","Seeing everyone gathered around Si Nian chatting and laughing, Li Fengxian walked into the office, her face immediately darkening.","Everyone fell silent upon seeing her.","How could they forget? There was still Li Fengxian, the young lady who harbored such intense jealousy and hatred towards Si Nian.","With a dark expression, Li Fengxian walked towards Si Nian, striking a pose as if declaring war.","Everyone unconsciously gulped.","Truly, one trouble barely ends before another begins.","With a thud.","Li Fengxian's hand slammed onto Si Nian's desk. \"Si Nian! Don't get too cocky.\"","Everyone: Here it comes, the declaration of war?","Although I admit your child did my nephew a huge favor, I haven't acknowledged you yet. In the next midterm exams, I will definitely have my class surpass yours. Then I can move up to the elite class and be with Teacher Wu, teaching side by side... Pah! I mean, teach together!","The corner of Si Nian's mouth twitched. \"No need to wait until then.\"","Li Fengxian glared at her. \"What do you mean? Are you conceding defeat without a fight?\"","Si Nian said helplessly, \"I'm only teaching for half a year before I leave. Whoever takes over for me then is irrelevant. If you're really that capable, I can recommend you for the position.\"","Li Fengxian let out an \"Ah?\" \"Really?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Really.\"","...","Meanwhile, the children from Class Four, holding flowers and candy, arrived at the door of Class One.","They were blocked at the entrance by Class One students, who looked at them warily. \"What do you want?\"","After this incident, students from other classes unanimously believed the Class Four students were too bad, corrupted by Teacher Xu.","Their families had told them not to play with anyone from Class Four.","Class Four had finally managed to isolate itself from the entire school through its own actions.","They used to be proud top students, academic elites who naturally looked down on students from other classes, often looking at them with disdain.","Yet at this moment, these children blushed, stammering, \"W-we're sorry. We know we were wrong. We won't bother Zhou Zhedong anymore. This is candy and flowers we bought with our pocket money to thank him and his brother.\"","\"Please, let us see him.\"","\"If possible, we'd like to ask him to come back to our class.\"","\"Zhou Zhedong, we're sorry.\"","Inside the classroom, a vein throbbed on Zhou Zhedong's temple.","He was more accustomed to a cold, studious environment.","This kind of enthusiasm was really hard to take.","...","Class One.","Jiang Jiu and Zhou Zehan stood on the podium, talking animatedly.","Zhou Zehan, \"You have no idea how thrilling it was when we were in the kidnappers' car. That car was driving as fast as an airplane. Everyone passed out, only I stayed awake. Right then I thought, this world would fall apart without me...\"","Zhou Zehan clutched his chest, wearing a look of great ambition. \"With a left hook and a right kick, I sent those two kidnappers flying out of the car. Then I got into the driver's seat, gulped down a bottle of soda, stepped on the gas, and raced back to my hometown (had to make a pit stop for stomach issues, but that's not the point).\"","\"I rallied all the folks from Happiness Village. Everyone held machetes, and we chopped the pursuing kidnappers into pieces.\"","\"We finally achieved victory and liberated all the victims.\"","\"The villagers saw me as the Monkey King, gave me a golden staff, cheered for me, gave me little red flowers...\"","Classmates: \"Wow—\"","\"So amazing!\"","\"Heavens, Second Brother is awesome!\"","\"Does Second Brother's family really have a pig farm?\"","Jiang Jiu immediately stepped forward, gesturing exaggeratedly. \"Of course! I saw it with my own eyes. Second Brother's family has a pig farm this big, with a hundred thousand piglets. I even helped Second Brother feed the pigs. Second Brother's house is a castle, with a rockery in front (the back hill) and a garden in the back (the vegetable plot)... Yes! Second Brother is a prince!\"","Jiang Jiu: \"Second Brother kissed me on the cheek, and I woke up. Second Brother is the prince from Snow White!\"","Classmates: \"Wow—\"","Second Child stood with hands on hips, nose in the air.","\"Second Brother, I want you to kiss me too.\"","\"Second Brother, me too, me too!\"","...","Si Nian struggled to carry the gifts home, and soon the two children returned.","Seeing the room piled high with so many presents, and their little sister lying amidst a heap of candy, occasionally picking one to pop in her mouth, then squinting her eyes in blissful enjoyment.","Second Child threw his backpack aside, let out a cheer, and dove right in."]},{"number":308,"title":"Chapter 308: Thanks (Bonus Update)","paragraphs":["\"Wow, is this heaven?\"","Jiang Jiu had intended to follow them inside when he heard a familiar yet strange voice from behind: \"Xiao Jiu...\"","Si Nian looked at the child rolling on the floor, feeling both amused and helpless.","No matter how clean the floor was, he was certainly making it dirty now.","She then looked at Zhou Zedong: \"Xiao Dong, aren't you going to help sell the pancakes?\"","Zhou Zedong put down his schoolbag, glanced at his younger siblings, and said, \"Mom, I'll go help as soon as I put my bag away.\"","Si Nian paused, understanding that the child was worried about his brother and had deliberately brought them home before going out.","Si Nian smiled and patted his head. \"In a couple of days, Mom will buy you and your brother a bicycle each. Then you can ride to school.\"","Hearing this, even Zhou Zedong couldn't help but widen his eyes in surprise.","\"Really?\"","\"Of course. You have to study and run the business. Running back and forth isn't safe either. Xiao Dong, don't forget you're still a child too.\"","Zhou Zedong pursed his lips and said, \"Mom, I'll grow up very soon.\"","Si Nian nodded with a smile and let him go out.","When Second Child heard he was getting a bicycle, he was so excited he started howling and jumping on the spot. Seemingly remembering something, he rummaged through his schoolbag, pulled out a bunch of his little red flowers, stuck them all over his clothes, then covered his pants with them too. He spun around in a circle and presented himself to Si Nian. \"Mom, do I look different today?\"","Si Nian was just about to go to the kitchen to cook. Hearing this, she stopped and turned to look at him.","She saw the child covered from head to toe in little red flowers.","She burst out laughing. \"You silly kid, you're so funny.\"","She was about to say something else when someone knocked on the door.","Si Nian looked over and saw Jiang Jiu scurrying in, looking awkward as he hid behind Second Child.","A lean man was still standing at the door.","The man looked to be in his late twenties, wearing a white shirt and somewhat plain, wooden-framed glasses.","He was carrying some gifts.","He had delicate, handsome features and very fair skin.","The kind of fair that looked like he hadn't seen the sun in years.","Si Nian recognized him instantly.","The man looked so much like Jiang Jiu, he was practically an enlarged version of him.","It was impossible not to know who he was.","She was just a bit surprised.","She had heard from Granny Jiang that the child's parents were both scientific researchers. Due to the special nature of their work, they rarely came home, fully devoted to their careers.","In short, the child saw them very little, which was why Jiang Jiu had been staying with them all along.","So he was back.","Then again, after such a major incident with the child, it would be abnormal if the biological father didn't return.","\"Hello, I am Jiang Jiu's father, Jiang Wenqing. I've come to express my thanks. Is it convenient to come in?\" Jiang Wenqing was very polite.","Si Nian felt the name was somewhat familiar, but couldn't place it immediately. After all, she had no memory of this person, so she nodded. \"Please, come in.\"","Jiang Wenqing walked in, placed the gifts to the side, and then suddenly bowed ninety degrees to Si Nian, startling her.","\"Jiang, Comrade Jiang, what are you doing?\"","Jiang Wenqing adjusted his glasses and said solemnly and gratefully, \"I've heard everything about what happened to Xiao Jiu from my parents. Thank you so very much. You saved my child. You are the lifesavers of our Jiang family. This great kindness is beyond repayment.\"","Si Nian shook her head. \"I share responsibility for this matter. I wasn't watching the two children closely enough, which led to the incident. I feel very bad about it myself. Comrade Jiang, there's no need for this.\"","Jiang Wenqing adjusted his glasses again and straightened up.","He was quite tall, lean but clearly over six feet.","Si Nian glanced again at Jiang Jiu, who was still half a head shorter than her own son, pouting and looking stubborn but actually quite wronged.","\"This, Xiao Jiu...\"","Jiang Wenqing gave a bitter smile. \"It's my fault. I haven't been back for two years. Before, it was always just phone calls. It's normal for the child to resent me and not want to talk to me.\"","\"I heard from my mother that Xiao Jiu likes to play with your son. I'm really sorry for the trouble.\"","Si Nian shook her head. \"Not at all. My Second Child really enjoys playing with him too.\"","Jiang Wenqing nodded and handed her the gifts. \"I still have some matters to attend to, so I shouldn't stay long. If Xiao Jiu wants to play, I won't disturb him. This is a small token of thanks.\"","After saying this, Jiang Wenqing took another look at his son, who refused to look at him, then turned and left dejectedly.","\"Little Jiang, was that your dad?\"","Jiang Jiu pouted and reluctantly grunted, \"Mhm.\"","\"Then why didn't you talk to him?\" Second Child scratched his head, confused.","Jiang Jiu squirmed. \"I, I don't like him. I don't want to talk to him.\"","Second Child was shocked. \"Why not? He's your dad.\"","Jiang Jiu said, \"He's not a good dad. He never comes home to see me, and he never plays with me. All the other kids have their dads playing with them, but I don't. Waaah...\"","Second Child immediately shut his mouth.","Alright, put that way, he himself was still the happiest.","Even though Dad was very busy every day at first, after Mom came, Dad also tried very hard to make time to care for them and take them to school.","Little Jiang is so pitiful.","He comforted Jiang Jiu like a little adult, patting his head. \"It's okay. You have two dads now. You're my brother, so my dad is your dad too. My dad is really nice. When he comes back, I'll have him take you for a ride on his motorcycle. It's so much fun!\"","Jiang Jiu wiped his tears. \"R-really?\"","Second Child: \"Really.\"","Jiang Jiu immediately cheered up, and the three children went back to rolling around in the candy.","Si Nian had originally wanted to offer some comfort, but it seemed there was no need for her to step in now.","She smiled helplessly and shook her head.","Jiang Wenqing went to the school to inquire about Zhou Zedong.","Coming home, besides seeing his son, he also had a task Brother Zhang had asked him to help with.","Now that he had gotten the address, he had intended to pay a visit.","But as he walked, he found himself back at the Zhou family's house.","He adjusted his glasses and looked down carefully. Huh? Isn't this the Zhou family?","So the family who saved his son and the family of the child Brother Zhang had taken a liking to were the same one?","Jiang Wenqing: \"...\"","\"Hey! Who are you?\" Yu Dong hurried over and saw a decent-looking man standing at his boss's family's doorstep. He immediately became wary.","He looked the man up and down. Not bad looking, he had to admit.","A frail, scholarly type, just standing there dumbly at the boss's door.","Such an obvious attempt to flirt with the boss's wife—he saw right through it.","Great, taking advantage of the boss being away, these men just can't stay put, can they?","He might be good-looking, but so frail. Trying to seize the opportunity while the boss is dealing with trouble to make a move, huh?","Absolutely despicable.","The love between the boss and his wife shall be protected by me, the Zhu Shimao of Yunnan-Guizhou-Sichuan Province!","Jiang Wenqing adjusted his glasses again. \"You, you are?\"","Yu Dong: \"I asked you first!\"","Jiang Wenqing adjusted his glasses. \"I am Jiang Wenqing. And you are?\"","Yu Dong: \"...\"","\"Uncle Yu, what are you all doing?\" Eldest Child came home and, seeing the two men standing at the door, asked curiously.","Only then did Yu Dong remember his purpose. Slapping his forehead as it dawned on him, he began shouting towards the house, \"Sister-in-law! Something's happened, something terrible!\"","Another six thousand words down. More updates tomorrow (you can bury me in gifts!)."]},{"number":309,"title":"Chapter 309: The Most Miserable Man in the Entire Text: Zhou Yueshen","paragraphs":["The piercing scream startled Si Nian, nearly making her cut her finger.","She put down the kitchen knife and poked her head out from the kitchen.","She saw Yu Dong rushing in, flustered and panicked.","Walking out, she asked, \"What's wrong?\"","\"The Boss is out...\" Yu Dong didn't finish his sentence, noticing the handsome young man who had been standing at the door had actually walked inside.","His eyes widened. His feeling was right, this guy actually walked into Eldest Sister-in-law's house so brazenly?","Were they already acquainted?","Yu Dong covered his mouth, pulled Si Nian aside, and whispered, \"Eldest Sister-in-law! The Boss is in trouble!\"","Si Nian's heart skipped a beat. \"What?\"","Yu Dong hurriedly told her in a low voice what he had found out about Zhou Yueshen's situation.","Actually, the Boss had told him in advance before returning to the Northwest this time: if he didn't come back within a month, he would send someone with a message.","Yu Dong hadn't thought much of it at the time, figuring it was a peaceful era now. Once the Boss finished handling matters in the Northwest, there shouldn't be any problems.","He might even be back in a few days.","Who would have thought a whole month had passed, and he still hadn't returned.","The incident with the Second Child made him realize this family couldn't manage without a man, so he contacted friends in the Northwest overnight to ask about the situation. That's when he learned the Boss had actually taken on a secret mission.","No matter what he asked, the other party just said they didn't know.","Yu Dong then knew something major had happened.","He exhausted all his connections to roughly understand the situation over there.","It was roughly that the illegal miners and poachers who had once wreaked havoc and killed in the uninhabited zone many years ago had reappeared.","Having been sent to the military district for discipline in his rebellious youth, he was well aware of the severity of this matter.","Back then, among the three most famous rising stars in the military district, besides the Boss and Wang Jianguo, there was also the most popular son of a senior officer, Yang Yingjie.","He died during the mission to crack down on the illegal mining operation.","If Yang Yingjie hadn't died, he might have been the youngest senior officer by now.","This incident was a huge blow to the Boss and Wang Jianguo as well. Back then, the two of them also swore a solemn oath to sever the commercial chain of these illegal miners. Of course, it was only after they entered the zone countless times, suffering unknown losses of troops and heavy casualties, that they finally won a brief peace.","The scene from back then was still vivid in his mind. Even the two strongest military kings in the district had nearly lost their lives then.","Wang Jianguo's face was scarred by explosions, and the Boss was shot in the chest.","If these two men weren't tough as nails, they probably wouldn't have survived either.","It was precisely because of this incident that they stepped on some powerful people's toes.","Despite being injured, the Boss was still assigned a mission from above.","In the end, the men he trusted died or were injured, leaving him alone.","When they first joined the army, everyone was filled with passionate blood, loyal to the country and willing to die for it.","But the higher they climbed, the clearer they saw the darkness of this world lay right there.","And the Boss personally witnessed this darkness. After his sister passed away and the children lost their support, he took the initiative to retire from the military.","However, at his level, wanting to leave wasn't easy.","Back then, several major factions were vying for the chief position. If he hadn't been severely wounded at the time, he might not have been able to withdraw unscathed.","Perhaps worried that Zhou Yueshen might be recruited by others, that scheming old fox Chief Yang didn't let him leave so easily. So as long as he demanded his return one day, Zhou Yueshen had no choice but to go back.","But Yu Dong never expected that this old fox, having secured his position for so many years now, still wouldn't let the Boss go.","He actually made him enter that dangerous place again.","Although these years have been peaceful, it's precisely because of the era's openness, without the life-and-death struggles of the past, that some people making money on the edge of danger have become bolder.","The Boss is already that old. After slaughtering pigs for so many years, finally becoming a boss himself, and now he still has to risk his life to save those so-called important personnel.","Just thinking about it made Yu Dong feel it was utterly pitiful.","After listening, Si Nian also fell silent.","Her eyes held an indescribable complexity.","Although she had heard from Aunt Jiang about Fu Yang entering the uninhabited zone and going missing, and guessed that Zhou Yueshen's return might be related to this matter, she never imagined Zhou Yueshen was actually going to save him!","Zhou Yueshen, how foolish!","The male lead you're saving, because of him in the future, your three children become major villains, either dying or going to prison.","Making you, with white hair, send off your black-haired children.","Just thinking about it made Si Nian feel a suffocating tightness in her chest.","Although it wasn't directly caused by the male lead, one must know all the changes in the children were because of Lin Sisi.","And how much did the male lead, with his supreme power, help Lin Sisi in order to protect her?","Si Nian originally thought Zhou Yueshen was just an inconsequential background character in the novel, his existence merely setting the stage for the children's corruption.","She never knew he was actually the one who bore the most, the biggest victim.","And that drama queen Fu Yang ended up stepping over him to reach the peak of his life.","Si Nian was truly furious.","She had relied too much on the plot, thinking Zhou Yueshen would definitely return, not thinking deeper.","Consistently believing he must be safe.","Even if the male lead was in trouble, he wouldn't die, and even if he did, Si Nian wouldn't care.","Who knew the person saving his life was her own old man.","She was actually somewhat angry at being deceived by Zhou Yueshen. He clearly said he'd be back soon, yet the time kept getting delayed.","Although she understood Zhou Yueshen didn't want them to worry, she still couldn't help feeling resentful, not wanting to think about him.","She certainly wouldn't do something like traveling a thousand miles to find her husband, as Lin Sisi would.","But now, the anxiety and anger in her heart were almost bursting through her chest.","She felt both heartache and anger.","Yet Si Nian understood better than anyone that military orders are hard to defy.","To leave, Zhou Yueshen had long been prepared.","The one who wasn't prepared was her.","Si Nian took a deep breath, suppressing the sour ache in her chest. \"I understand.\"","Yu Dong was still gesturing animatedly, emphasizing the severity of the situation.","He didn't expect Si Nian to accept it so quickly, and couldn't help but utter a confused \"Huh?\"","He hadn't recovered yet.","Although no bad news about the Boss had come yet, entering the uninhabited zone was already the worst news possible.","Was Eldest Sister-in-law really this calm?","It must be because she's been staying here and doesn't know what a perilous place the uninhabited zone is.","Yes, that's right, it must be that."]},{"number":310,"title":"Chapter 310: Invitation","paragraphs":["Yu Dong tried to comfort himself this way.","But he didn't know that Si Nian had always been fascinated by natural landscapes and had watched many documentaries.","And the forbidden zones of human death were what she was most obsessed with.","So she had once written to Zhou Yueshen in a letter, saying she wanted to see the deserts and salt lakes, to experience the desolation of the northwest.","In the future, after development, many people would travel to the northwest, and there were even stories of people crossing uninhabited zones.","But in reality, even in the future era of developed transportation and pervasive internet, countless people who ventured into uninhabited zones still went missing or died.","There were far too many such news reports.","Si Nian had once watched a documentary about poaching incidents and the brazenness of illegal miners operating in the uninhabited zones of the old era.","She never expected that Zhou Yueshen was living in that very era.","Si Nian took a deep breath, wanting to comfort herself.","But the incident of the Second Child's attempted abduction had already warned her that the plot was not all-powerful. What she had changed was only the present of a few people, while the plot itself had already undergone earth-shattering changes.","She could no longer be certain of Zhou Yueshen's safety.","Although she arrogantly believed that her feelings for Zhou Yueshen weren't that deep—he just happened to be her type, happened to be suitable for her, so they were just partnering up to get through life.","But people have emotions.","Especially towards a man she had shared a bed with countless times.","How could she remain unmoved?","Jiang Wenqing, seeing that both their expressions looked rather grim, stepped forward worriedly and asked, \"Comrade Si, has something happened?\"","Yu Dong, as if suffering from a persecution complex, immediately looked at him warily.","Si Nian took a deep breath and said, \"It's nothing. Comrade Jiang, are you here to pick up Xiaojiu?\"","Jiang Wenqing figured it must be their private matter and didn't press further. He shook his head and said, \"No, I just went to the school. I originally wanted to inquire about a child's situation. I didn't expect that child to be from your family, so I came back.\"","Si Nian was taken aback. \"A child from my family?\"","Jiang Wenqing explained the matter concerning Brother Zhang to her.","\"Brother Zhang has difficulty getting around. I happened to be on holiday this time, so I thought I'd help him look into the situation. But it seems now my help isn't needed anymore.\"","He had just been to the school and had already learned the general situation from the teacher.","The teacher who bullied the children was already in prison.","Naturally, there was no need for him.","But thinking about the child Brother Zhang valued, he still wanted to come and see for himself.","Who would have thought it was actually the family that saved his own son.","After listening, Si Nian was slightly stunned.","\"You mean Little Dong?\" she asked, looking towards the Eldest Child who had just returned.","Jiang Wenqing nodded.","Zhou Zedong also looked at him curiously.","He had just learned from his younger brother that this man was Xiaojiu's irresponsible father.","He didn't expect the man was actually looking for him.","Jiang Wenqing then told Si Nian about Brother Zhang's idea. \"Our researcher positions are specially recruited. Either that, or we train them from a young age if they're the right age. If you have any intentions in this regard, I can help.\"","Although it's true that researchers are very busy, focused on work and unable to tend to family matters.","But such a job is also one in ten thousand.","Not only is the salary high, but it also commands great respect.","In this era, if a family has a scientific researcher, the whole family benefits from the glory.","Moreover, the requirements are extremely strict, and ordinary families basically have no such opportunity.","Even relying on sheer talent is a one-in-ten-thousand chance.","That's also why they are severely short of people.","Si Nian never expected that the Eldest Child would be noticed by someone at such a young age.","Around the moment she heard him say he was from the Guangming Research Base, she fell completely silent.","Wasn't that the very place where the Eldest Child would work in the future?","Although his specific work wasn't detailed in the novel, this name was mentioned.","So no matter how much she tried to change things, the Eldest Child would ultimately be noticed by people from the base.","Their career paths and future growth lines were fixed.","Even if she changed things, those characters who were supposed to appear in the future would still appear.","No wonder the name Jiang Wenqing felt familiar earlier.","Wasn't he the Eldest Child's future teacher?","Si Nian had a headache.","In the novel, when the Eldest Child went astray, it was this teacher who came out to advise and help him, protecting him single-handedly, which spared the Eldest Child from being executed by firing squad.","However, this Jiang Wenqing in the novel was also a character with a tragic past. It was written that his family was destroyed and its members lost, so he advised the work-obsessed Eldest Child not to neglect his family for the sake of work, or he would regret it for a lifetime.","By that time, the Eldest Child had grown up, was taciturn and didn't like to talk.","Harder to get along with than an old man.","He believed that only by making significant contributions and achieving something would no one dare to bully the three siblings.","But precisely because of this, he overlooked his younger brother's rebellion and his sister's accident.","Ultimately, he ended up with the same fate as Jiang Wenqing.","Si Nian simply couldn't imagine that this handsome young man before her would be the Eldest Child's future teacher from the novel—the one who was never without alcohol, slovenly, and whose heart was never in his work.","The novel said Jiang Wenqing had experienced the destruction of his family and the loss of its members. Could it be referring to the incident of Jiangjiu being kidnapped?","If the Second Child hadn't come, and Jiangjiu would still have encountered the kidnapping, then Jiangjiu might really have been sold...","Wait a minute, wait a minute... In the novel, it was written that later, after the Second Child became part of the underworld, he had a very good brother by his side named Wang Jiu. The two ventured together and also died together under the blades of their enemies...","Si Nian: ......","What the hell is all this?"]},{"number":311,"title":"Chapter 311: Wherever Mom Goes, We Follow","paragraphs":["This plot is getting too much for her to sort through.","Si Nian tilted her head and looked at the three little beans staring at her.","She let out a heavy sigh.","\"I can't make this decision for the children. Of course, it would be even better if the children themselves had any inclination to develop in that direction.\"","Zhou Zedong asked doubtfully, \"Mom, research? What's that?\"","Jiang Wenqing looked at him; it was the child who had led him in earlier.","So, this was the child Brother Zhang valued so much.","He gave him a once-over. The boy wasn't old, but his eyes held determination, and his expression was calm, lacking the innocence and curiosity on the faces of his own son and the other child nearby.","It was just a simple question in return.","Jiang Wenqing was taken aback for a moment. \"We are scientific and technological workers, intellectuals with professional knowledge engaged in scientific research.\"","Zhou Zedong lowered his head in thought.","It sounded very impressive.","\"Can you make a lot of money?\" he asked Jiang Wenqing.","Jiang Wenqing was stunned again, then smiled. \"Of course. My monthly salary is 300 yuan.\"","Zhou Zedong immediately wrinkled his nose, seeming somewhat disdainful. \"Then I'd rather be a pig butcher. My dad earns more in a day.\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","Of all the people to learn from, you had to learn from your dad.","And you want to butcher pigs.","One wants to farm, the other wants to butcher pigs.","Future great villain, where has your towering ambition gone?","Jiang Wenqing was choked up. \"Well... it's not the same... this isn't something just anyone can do.\"","Zhou Zedong: \"My dad isn't just anyone.\"","Jiang Wenqing: \"My apologies.\"","Yu Dong: What on earth are you apologizing for?","Si Nian said with a headache, \"How about this, Xiao Dong is still young. Let's discuss this matter later.\"","Jiang Wenqing nodded slightly, agreeing it was reasonable.","He took the reluctant Jiang Jiu and went home.","Yu Dong didn't stay long either. After confirming that the other party was just a neighbor and posed no threat to his position as the 'right-hand man,' he hurriedly left again.","In the evening, the family sat around the dining table. Si Nian, unusually, took the initiative to bring up the man with the lowest presence in this household: \"Xiao Dong, Xiao Han, do you miss your dad?\"","The two children were taken aback. Even Zhou Zehan, who had been eating heartily, stopped.","They exchanged a glance.","\"Mom, what's wrong with Dad?\"","Earlier, they had seen Uncle Yu come in a hurry saying something had happened.","Could it be something happened to Dad?","Worry flashed in the children's eyes.","Is Dad okay?","Si Nian shook her head. \"He's fine. It's just that your dad has been away for so long now, Mom is missing him a little.\"","The Second Child immediately said, \"Mom, I miss Dad too. When will Dad come back?\"","Because Zhou Yueshen was rarely home in the past, the two children were used to it.","Now, hearing Si Nian mention it, they realized Dad hadn't been back for a very long time.","Si Nian shook her head. \"Mom isn't sure either. If, I'm just saying if... if something happened to Dad, could you temporarily put aside your studies and go with Mom to see him?\"","It wasn't that she was unwilling to go find Zhou Yueshen, to go see him.","It was just that she had three children in her care.","It wasn't as simple as just packing up and leaving whenever she wanted.","The Eldest Child immediately stood up, walked to Si Nian's side, took her hand and said, \"Mom, I want to go. I want to go with Mom. Wherever Mom goes, I go.\"","The Second Child quickly nodded in agreement. \"Yes, wherever Mom goes, we go.\"","Si Nian's heart warmed. Although the children were young, their unconditional support made her feel reassured.","She made a decision on the spot. \"Alright, then once I find out news about your dad, we'll go find him.\"","Come to think of it, it had always been Zhou Yueshen who took care of their clothing and food — that is, all their material needs — and it was always him making the effort to get closer to them.","But this time, Si Nian decided, she would go to him.","In the following days, Si Nian called Yu Dong and asked him to help find out about Zhou Yueshen's situation in the northwest.","Occasionally, she would also ask Grandma Jiang about Fu Yang's situation.","If Zhou Yueshen really went to rescue Fu Yang, then once Fu Yang was saved, Zhou Yueshen's mission should be about over too.","Sure enough, not long after, she learned the news that Fu Yang had been rescued.","Although she had been rescued, she heard that he had been seriously injured and his condition was critical—between life and death.","Grandma Jiang and Commander Jiang were very worried and had already sent people ahead.","Commander Jiang got the news first because he had connections over there.","It was said even the Fu family didn't know about Fu Yang's accident yet.","Fu's father probably knew but hadn't told the family, afraid they would worry, so no news had spread yet.","As expected, after getting news about Fu Yang, Yu Dong also received a call from a companion.","They said there was already secret information suggesting there was news about Zhou Yueshen, but the specific situation was unclear.","Because Zhou Yueshen himself still couldn't be contacted.","Si Nian knew he must be injured or something had happened; otherwise, his first move would definitely be to send word to her.","Yu Dong also planned to go see what the heck was going on, as the distance from here to the northwest was really too far.","When Si Nian said she wanted to go together, Yu Dong was quite happy, saying the boss would be thrilled to see her.","Moreover, if she brought the children along, maybe the old commander wouldn't have the face to keep demanding the boss stay and work for him.","Since the duration was uncertain, Si Nian asked the principal for leave.","In principle, the principal definitely wouldn't approve such a long leave, but considering her difficult situation and the fact that she had done him a favor, he told her to find a teacher willing to substitute for her.","If she found someone willing, he would let her go.","Si Nian immediately went to Li Fengxian and asked if she would be willing to substitute for her for a while.","Li Fengxian was still studying hard, striving to snatch first place in the final exams. Hearing Si Nian ask her to substitute, she was immediately like: ? There's such a good thing?","Si Nian also asked for leave for the two children for a period.","The Eldest Child naturally didn't care; he wasn't afraid of falling behind in his studies.","The Second Child, after all, had already been through first grade once, so there was no need for extreme worry.","So, Si Nian asked Yu Dong to help buy train tickets, and asked Grandma Jiang to help feed their Da Huang. Then she packed her luggage, waiting for Comrade Yu Dong to get ready so they could go visit Zhou Yueshen.","Only then did Grandma Jiang learn that Zhou Yueshen had gone to the northwest military region. Hearing Si Nian say she was afraid it was also related to this incident, Grandma Jiang was worried. She had her husband call to ask about the situation. They said Fu Yang was already recuperating from his injuries, so her husband (referring to Zhou Yueshen) must be fine too, and they arranged for someone over there to receive them.","Otherwise, it would be inconvenient for her to travel alone with so many children.","Si Nian was very grateful for this.","Jiang Jiu, however, was very reluctant. Although Second Brother said they would be back soon, hearing those words scared him.","That's what his mom and dad had said to him when they left.","But he couldn't stop Second Brother from going to see his dad. In the end, he said he wanted to go too.","He declared that Second Brother's dad was his dad too.","Before he could finish, his grandma tossed him back into the house.","Doesn't want to spare an extra glance for his own dad at home, but wants to travel a thousand miles to see someone else's dad.","Really filial piety to the point of killing her (sarcastic).","Report! I want to advance-draw a gift from the future.","It's the final day of the Gift Domination Contest! If the total gift value exceeds twenty thousand, I'll write two extra chapters tonight. We're currently at sixteen thousand, let's go, my dear supporters! Whether this village chief can secure that recommendation spot depends entirely on you all! The second place is chasing way too close, it's honestly nerve-wracking. Everyone, please hit that 'Prompt Update' button more often—it might just pop up the option to send a 'Power of Love' gift! Thank you all so much for your support of Shanzi!"]},{"number":312,"title":"Chapter 312: Departure","paragraphs":["Yu Dong bought them sleeper tickets. The Yu family had money and connections, so he handled such matters with ease.","However, he bought himself a seat ticket, saying he was too worried to sleep.","He also worried that Si Nian, like him, would be too concerned about the Boss to sleep, so he comforted her: \"Don't worry, Eldest Sister-in-law. I've heard the authorities are taking this matter very seriously now, it's not like the old days anymore. Maybe once they know you're coming to the northwest, the Boss will be busy getting back.\"","Given the long journey, Si Nian didn't bring much. However, worried about temperature differences, she had all the children wear jackets in case it got cold on the train at night.","Xiao Dong and Xiao Han carried their own backpacks, stuffed with a change of clothes and their homework.","They also carried a small bag with Yao Yao's clothes. Si Nian herself only carried a suitcase, not much at all.","She didn't want the hassle of lugging around numerous bags.","Fortunately, the children were all older now, saving her a lot of trouble.","Still, she had to be careful; pickpockets were rampant in train stations during this era.","The money she brought was sewn into the lining of her clothes.","With Yu Dong's help, Si Nian felt considerably more at ease.","Yu Dong didn't bring anything himself; he had friends over there and could just borrow whatever he needed.","Si Nian was Zhou Yueshen's family member. Zhou Yueshen was a regiment commander, and they had housing in the family compound there, so Si Nian wasn't worried about having nowhere to stay.","Yu Dong was deeply moved. He used to think Eldest Sister-in-law was too noble, not someone their Boss was worthy of, always feeling like the Boss was somewhat of a simp.","Not only did he give all his money to Eldest Sister-in-law, but even when buying clothes, he had to ask her for money, and then he'd spend it all on her, not buying a single thing for himself.","Although others said the Boss seemed hard to get along with, even suspecting he might have abusive tendencies,","in Yu Dong's eyes, the Boss's status at home was pathetically low.","But then, Sister-in-law was so beautiful; this was all what the Boss deserved.","He never expected Eldest Sister-in-law would come along this time, especially since the northwest was so far.","She had even put aside important work.","The Boss's efforts finally hadn't been in vain.","Even such an unattainable flower had been moved.","He decided then and there: he would learn from the Boss!","With Yu Dong carrying Yao Yao and Si Nian holding the two brothers' hands, no one dared to target them.","However, the crowd was massive. Once at the station, Si Nian didn't let the excited Zhou Zehan run around, making him hold her hand tightly.","It was Zhou Zehan's first time on a train. Though very curious, he knew to be obedient and held on tight.","In those days, orderly queues were practically impossible. Once the train arrived, people surged forward, squeezing in like zombies drawn to flesh.","Both children clung tightly to her.","After boarding, finding their assigned carriage, and walking in, they finally breathed a sigh of relief.","Si Nian's berth was the bottom one because it was inconvenient for her to sleep with Yao Yao otherwise.","The two children's berths were right next to hers.","Yu Dong had arranged everything perfectly, terrified this family might suffer any inconvenience.","The journey was long. Yu Dong even went and bought a bag of snacks,","saying he was afraid the children would get hungry.","There was hot water on the train. Si Nian had brought milk powder, made some for Yao Yao, and let her sit on the bed to drink it.","After finishing, the train started moving, rocking and swaying, lulling Yao Yao to sleep in no time, her mouth still making faint sucking motions unconsciously.","Si Nian covered her with a blanket. She herself didn't sleep, worried she wouldn't be able to sleep later.","Zhou Zedong, relatively calm, had already picked up a book to read.","The Second Child, on the upper berth, was excitedly chattering in a low voice, calling to him, \"Brother~ Brother, I won't fall, right? If I fall, you have to catch me!\"","Yu Dong had wandered off somewhere, probably bored and walking around the carriages.","Si Nian looked at the scenery outside the window. In an era without phones, being on a train was pure torture.","She had intended not to sleep, but ended up dozing off anyway.","When she woke up, Yu Dong and Zhou Zedong, one big and one small, were playing a numbers game.","Yu Dong's brows were furrowed like mountains, seemingly unable to believe he, an adult, couldn't beat a child.","His face was full of unwillingness.","From the upper berth, the Second Child's snores were also quite loud.","This kid, developing the bad habit of snoring at such a young age.","Si Nian turned over and went back to sleep.","Meanwhile, at the Fu residence.","The news of Fu Yang's accident reached them two days later.","Upon hearing her son had ventured deep into an uninhabited zone, Fu's mother nearly fainted.","Lately, she had been feeling chest tightness and shortness of breath, a constant sense of foreboding.","Because her son hadn't been in contact.","She initially thought he couldn't contact home due to a mission.","She never expected an accident.","In the past, her son often went on missions for ten days or half a month without returning.","But this was the first time she had felt this way.","And sure enough, something had happened.","Now she was clamoring to go see her son.","Fu Qianqian, though not particularly fond of her brother, couldn't ignore such a serious matter.","She immediately requested leave to go with her mother to take care of Fu Yang.","Father Fu was a high-ranking officer and definitely couldn't leave.","He could only let his wife and daughter go.","Meanwhile, the Si household had long been in complete turmoil.","Si's Father had been vying for a promotion for half a year, gifting who-knows-how-many presents. After forming a marriage alliance with the Fu family, the promotion seemed like a sure thing.","But recently, for some unknown reason, his superiors suddenly started finding fault with him everywhere.","Even the leader who had previously hinted at giving him the position because of the Fu family now seemed like a different person.","Not only did he give the position to Si's Father's arch-rival, but he also demoted him.","He said Si's Father's recent work had been increasingly poor, that he was very disappointed, etc., leaving Si's Father utterly bewildered.","His own subordinate had leapfrogged to become his superior.","Si's Father was nearly driven mad with anger. Relying on his status as the Fu family's in-law, he made a scene with his superiors.","Normally, the other side might have been afraid of him.","But this time, not only were they unafraid, they told him to go ahead and complain wherever he wanted.","Furious, Si's Father, refusing to believe it, immediately went to the Fu residence to seek an explanation from Officer Fu.","After all, they were in-laws and had years of friendship; Si's Father believed the Fu family couldn't possibly not help him.","Father Fu already had a terrible headache over his son's situation, and now Si's Father was causing trouble, adding to his annoyance.","Seeing Si's Father insist on an explanation, he told him to go back and ask his own wife what she had done.","Father Fu himself had a good relationship with the Jiang family. Division Commander Jiang had been his superior before. After Division Commander Jiang retired, Father Fu took the high-ranking position. His son had also served under Division Commander Jiang before.","Forget the connection with Division Commander Jiang; just the incident where his wife came back and told him how Zhang Cuimei had said Si Nian's son being kidnapped served her right was enough to make things difficult for Si's Father.","And now he still had the nerve to come seeking an explanation.","Father Fu felt secondhand embarrassment for him.","Si's Father was also stunned. He hadn't been fond of going home lately; every time he did, his wife would make sarcastic remarks, and they'd argue at the slightest disagreement. He found it annoying and simply stopped going back.","He never expected his wife had caused such a mess, making him dizzy with anger.","He increasingly felt he and Zhang Cuimei were fundamentally incompatible. Years of affection seemed to vanish in that moment.","Not a trace of tenderness remained, only full of rage and anger.","And Zhang Cuimei, right then, was precisely because of this matter, visiting Lin Sisi and pouring out her bitterness.","She said she hadn't meant it at the time, was just too angry, and never expected the Fu family and the Jiangs to overhear.","She also complained that Si Nian knew such important people but never told her.","Lin Sisi offered comforting words, but inwardly, she was filled with anxiety.","Although her parents had promised during this time that they would help her leave early."]},{"number":313,"title":"Chapter 313: Meeting","paragraphs":["But lately, she kept having strange dreams—sometimes about Si Nian, other times about Fu Yang. In the dreams, it wasn't Si Nian and Fu Yang living sweetly together, but herself and Fu Yang.","She also dreamed that Fu Yang got into trouble during a mission, and she rushed thousands of miles to take care of him, thoroughly moving him.","Then she heard her mother say Fu Yang had gone on a mission to the northwest.","The Lin family hadn't agreed to let her visit before, so Lin Sisi thought those were just illusions and dreams caused by her strong resentment toward Si Nian.","But now, dreaming of such things again made her wonder.","After all, she was different from others—she was a person who had been reborn.","Since something like rebirth could happen, other bizarre occurrences weren't impossible to understand.","Sure enough, after some probing just now, she heard from Zhang Cuimei that there had been no news from Fu Yang for a long time.","She was in no mood to listen to Zhang Cuimei's complaints about these things.","She interrupted her and told her to go back and use her connections to ask about Fu Yang's situation.","Saying she was very worried about Fu Yang.","Si's Mother couldn't bear to tell Lin Sisi that the Fu family wanted a divorce, afraid her daughter couldn't withstand the blow.","Life here was already hard enough for her; if she found out, what if she did something drastic?","Now, seeing her still thinking of Fu Yang, Si's Mother felt a pang of bitterness in her heart.","Her Sisi had suffered far too much.","She remembered everyone, yet no one cared about her.","Heavy-hearted, she returned home, only to learn the news of Fu Yang's accident as soon as she arrived.","Si's Mother was also incredulous.","She hadn't expected her daughter to guess correctly.","Liu Dongdong had just learned about this from Si's Father. Si's Father had returned with a grim face, left again shortly after, asking where Zhang Cuimei was—it looked like a fight was brewing.","But she didn't care; these two bickering wasn't without its benefits for her anyway.","She happened to learn about this from Si's Father.","Seeing Zhang Cuimei return, she hurriedly told her that Mother Fu and Fu Qianqian had already left to take care of Fu Yang.","Zhang Cuimei hadn't expected something to really happen and panicked momentarily.","Her son-in-law was in trouble; as the mother-in-law, she couldn't just sit idly by.","Of course, the main purpose was also to worry about someone taking advantage of the situation.","After all, a man is most vulnerable when injured.","She naturally had to keep an eye out.","Although the Fu family intended to divorce, her daughter would be out of prison soon.","There might still be room for reconciliation then.","Under Liu Dongdong's persuasion, Zhang Cuimei set off for the northwest with Liu Dongdong.","The train stopped and started, and Si Nian spent most of the journey sleeping.","She didn't let the Second Child run around, as train abductions were not uncommon.","Seeing her seriousness, the Second Child didn't dare to cause trouble, amusing himself by talking to himself for hours on end.","Or playing games with Yao Yao.","Zhou Zedong spent his time either reading or playing number games. Over two days, Yu Dong hadn't beaten him once.","And so, they arrived safely at the terminal station.","The train station was still crowded, but just outside, someone was waiting for them.","It was Zhou Yueshen's orderly. Zhou Yueshen was on a mission, but this orderly wasn't qualified for that level of task, so he had stayed at the base. He was the one who had contacted Yu Dong.","Now, seeing the regiment leader's wife and several children, he stood there dumbfounded, speechless.","Yu Dong nudged him: \"What are you standing there for, Lao Zhu? Call her 'sister-in-law.'\"","Only then did he snap out of it, hurriedly calling out \"sister-in-law\" and introducing himself as Lao Zhu, Regiment Leader Zhou's orderly.","Si Nian told him not to be so formal.","But inwardly, she couldn't help but click her tongue in surprise.","Zhou Yueshen even had an orderly—quite impressive.","The three children also looked astonished.","\"Is the boss back?\" Yu Dong asked hurriedly as they got into the car.","Lao Zhu, who had just been stealing glances at his regiment leader's stunningly beautiful young wife in the back, thinking no wonder the leader was reluctant to come back—he wouldn't want to either if it were him—immediately straightened his face at the question, shaking his head. \"A rescue team was sent in. They rescued Regiment Leader Fu a couple of days ago, but he's still unconscious. The regiment leader and Brigade Commander Wang haven't...\" He suddenly realized he might have said too much and clamped his mouth shut.","Yu Dong's fists clenched involuntarily.","The three children seemed to sense something, all falling silent in unison.","The rest of the journey passed in silence.","Si Nian arrived at Zhou Yueshen's quarters.","Because arrangements had been made in advance, she got in easily.","However, before she could even finish unpacking and settling in, she saw Yu Dong rushing back in a panic, shouting excitedly, \"Sister-in-law, this is amazing! As soon as you arrived, the boss is back! You really are his lucky star!\"","Si Nian was surprised. \"He's back? Where?\"","\"I just got the news, not too clear on the details yet, but he probably went straight to the hospital. I heard many people were injured by explosions.\"","Si Nian froze for a moment, then instructed the Eldest Child and Second Child to watch over the sleeping Yao Yao before hurriedly following Yu Dong to the hospital.","The two children, in an unfamiliar environment, were exceptionally well-behaved.","Sure enough, just as they entered the hospital, a group of medical staff rushed in pushing a number of injured people on stretchers.","Watching one bloodied person after another being wheeled in, Si Nian felt her scalp prickle. Fighting back fear, she strained to see each face clearly.","Finally, near the end, she spotted a familiar figure being helped in.","Though covered in dust and stained with blood, the tall stature and familiar outline—Si Nian recognized him at a glance.","She stood there dumbly, watching the man being helped onto a stretcher. Only when he came closer did she snap back to reality.","Zhou Yueshen, in a daze, caught sight of a familiar figure and thought he was seeing things.","He was so exhausted he was about to fall asleep, but the next second, his eyes flew open.","And indeed, he met Si Nian's familiar face.","Zhou Yueshen instantly drew a sharp breath. \"Nian Nian?\"","Si Nian looked at him, covered in blood—she didn't know if it was his or others'.","Because one person couldn't possibly lose that much blood and still be alive, right?","Though she had been comforting herself all along, seeing it with her own eyes still terrified her.","Her eyes reddened involuntarily, and before she knew it, tears were pattering down onto the man's body.","Zhou Yueshen immediately panicked. Forgetting for the moment how she had gotten here, he hurriedly comforted her, \"I'm fine, don't worry.\"","Si Nian, choked with emotion and scared stiff—though her mouth remained the only hard part of her—retorted, \"Who's worried about you? It'd be better if something happened to you, make it easier for me to find someone else.\"","Zhou Yueshen choked, coughing up a mouthful of bloody foam.","He thought, if he ever died one day, it definitely wouldn't be because of a mission.","It would be because of her.","From anger."]},{"number":314,"title":"Chapter 314: This Is Not My Mouth Let Me Explain","paragraphs":["Zhou Yueshen's eyes were filled with remorse as he looked at her, wanting to explain, but before he could speak, Si Nian cut him off, telling him to go get treatment first.","She wasn't cruel enough to make an injured man apologize to her here.","Her anger was real, and her heartache was equally real.","The examination results came out. Although it looked serious, the doctor said they were all superficial wounds.","It was just that the blood loss was quite significant. Logically, that amount of blood loss would have made an ordinary person pass out, but Commander Zhou had remained conscious the whole time. Even while his wounds were being treated, his eyes were open, seeming to hold a hint of melancholy.","According to the doctor, he hadn't slept a wink for at least three days.","A normal person... never mind, given all the circumstances, Commander Zhou didn't seem like a normal person.","He had only just fallen asleep after taking medicine.","While explaining the situation to Si Nian, the doctor kept stealing glances at her.","Although people weren't very clear about Commander Zhou's family background, they had heard he was remarried with three children.","Many had always felt it was a bit of a pity.","After all, those who had been in the military unit for a while knew some things about Zhou Yueshen.","Everyone had always believed that Yang Yujie had remained unmarried, waiting for his return.","People never quite understood why he remained completely unmoved by someone like Yang Yujie, with her excellent conditions.","What was wrong with Yang Yujie? She came from a good family, had high status; any other man would probably be overjoyed.","But Commander Zhou showed no intention of reciprocating.","Now, however, everyone seemed to understand.","Although they didn't know the background of Commander Zhou's wife, in terms of poise and looks, she was in no way inferior to Yang Yujie.","If Si Nian hadn't spoken to Commander Zhou earlier, no one would have thought of her as Commander Zhou's wife.","But seeing Commander Zhou's anxious attitude and the tone he used when speaking to her, what else was there not to understand?","Zhou Yueshen slept restlessly, constantly remembering that Si Nian was waiting for him, which made him unwilling to fall asleep.","His dreams were filled with scenes of her looking at him with disappointment.","He woke up not long after.","A dull ache throbbed at his temples.","The hospital room was empty.","All was quiet.","He was momentarily dazed, as if not fully processing it.","It seemed like he had just seen her a second ago.","But the next moment he opened his eyes, she was gone.","Could seeing Si Nian just now have been a dream?","During this time in the uninhabited zone, he had missed her every single moment.","Once a person has tasted sweetness, being in such a harsh environment again makes one yearn intensely for that warmth and happiness.","If he had never possessed it, perhaps he would have been fearless.","But, ironically, he had once possessed it.","Zhou Yueshen lowered his gaze, feeling he was somewhat bewitched, actually hallucinating from missing someone.","He was even surprised at himself.","However, the next second, he heard a hushed voice from outside the door, \"Quiet now, Little Han, your father is still resting. Don't disturb him.\"","Si Nian entered the room carrying a food container, holding their daughter's hand, with their two sons following behind—a neat, complete family.","Seemingly surprised he had woken so soon, she asked, \"Zhou Yueshen, you're awake already? Why not sleep a bit more?\"","Zhou Yueshen looked up at them.","Watching her place the food container on the table beside him, she said, \"The doctor said you haven't slept for days. Don't you like sleeping? Staying up late at your age. I bought you some food.\"","\"Dad! Are you okay?\"","\"Daddy, daddy, I missed you so much~ Mom said you got hurt.\" The Second Child's eyes welled up with tears.","\"Dada, dada, hug hug~\" Yaoyao stretched her arms out towards him.","Zhou Yueshen's body was wrapped in bandages, wounds from bomb fragments, large and small, covering half his upper body. His back was straight, medical tape on the veins of his hand.","His frame and face were somewhat thinner than before. Just as he was about to reach out to hold his daughter, Si Nian patted her head and said, \"Be good, Yaoyao. Daddy is sick and can't hold you. Wait until Daddy is better.\"","Yaoyao blinked her big eyes at Zhou Yueshen.","Zhou Yueshen looked at them. Although it was an unfamiliar environment, their presence made him feel as if he were at home. A warm atmosphere enveloped him, and the faintly aching wounds no longer hurt.","He couldn't quite articulate this feeling, only that his chest felt full.","He told the children in a gentle voice that he was fine, then looked at Si Nian beside him.","Si Nian was also looking at him, her expression calm, as usual.","When their eyes met, for a moment he didn't know what to say.","The April nights in the northwest were still cold. She wore a fitted coat, tall and slender, her bright features illuminating the dim hospital room.","The earlier sense of aloofness seemed to vanish in an instant.","Zhou Yueshen's slightly chapped thin lips parted. He subtly observed her expression, then called her name, \"Nian Nian.\"","His gaze was complex, but filled more with guilt.","Si Nian rarely saw so much emotion on his usually stoic face.","She gave an \"Mhm\" and asked, \"What is it?\"","\"How did you get here?\" Zhou Yueshen patted the children who had gathered close, his gaze still tenderly fixed on her. He had thought earlier it was a hallucination from missing her too much, after all, the northwest was so far away, how could she have come?","Yet not only had she come, but she had also brought the children.","It must have been a long, arduous journey, surely full of hardships.","This time, his delay had been too long. It was only right for her to be angry.","It was his fault.","He remembered she had cried, and his heart was deeply moved.","Si Nian had actually already calmed down, but hearing his familiar, gentle voice, her heart still ached, with an impulse to cry. She never knew she was such a crybaby.","Her lips moved, and after a moment, she blurted out, \"I dreamed you had an accident, came to collect your body.\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","Si Nian: ? This isn't my mouth talking, let me explain.","Yu Dong, who had just walked in, was so shocked his jaw nearly dropped.","He had thought Sister-in-law had truly fallen for the boss, but who knew she had actually come to collect his body.","No wonder she had been expressionless the whole journey, eating, drinking, and sleeping as usual.","He had thought she was putting on a brave front.","Turns out she genuinely wasn't worried.","Zhou Yueshen looked at her rather helplessly and said, \"Nian Nian wishes for me to die?\"","The Eldest Child and the Second Child looked at Si Nian in horror.","Mom wishes for Dad to die? Why? Is it because Dad is too old and she doesn't like him anymore?","Ah, they don't want Dad to die.","Si Nian quickly made a spitting sound, \"Pah, pah, nothing of the sort.\" As she spoke, she glared at Zhou Yueshen. \"Can't the food shut your mouth?\" The children are here, saying such things frightens them.","Zhou Yueshen reached out to take the food container, let out a low chuckle, and looked at them, feeling his heart completely full.","His injuries weren't serious, all superficial, but his left leg was fractured and needed recuperation, so he couldn't get out of bed for now.","Yu Dong also brought him some fruit. Soon, many people came to visit him, breaking the family's quiet moment.","Seeing the visitor wearing a crisp military uniform and the insignia on his shoulders, Si Nian stood up, leading the children aside.","She listened to their conversation.","The visitor was quite old, in his fifties, with stern eyes and a powerful, resonant voice.","He didn't seem surprised to see her and the children."]},{"number":315,"title":"Chapter 315: You Only Know How to Torment Me","paragraphs":["Yet Zhou Yueshen remained in that half-reclining, boss-like posture, not moving an inch.","\"Lao Jiang told me your wife and children were coming to visit and asked me to arrange things. I didn't expect them to arrive so soon,\" Chief Yang said.","Zhou Yueshen's gaze towards him was cold, as if looking at a stranger. \"Yes, thank you for your trouble, Chief. This is my wife, Si Nian, and my three children.\"","His expression softened considerably when he looked at Si Nian. \"Nian Nian, this is Chief Yang.\"","Si Nian subtly withdrew her gaze and offered a greeting. After all, he was a Chief; she couldn't afford to be disrespectful.","At that moment, Yang Yujie rushed in frantically, losing her usual composure. \"Zhou Yueshen, you're not—\" Her words cut off as she spotted Si Nian and the others standing to the side.","Si Nian stared back at her, with a hint of a spectator's amusement.","Yang Yujie was stunned.","She had just returned from a mission and learned the news of Zhou Yueshen's team's successful rescue. Hearing he was injured, she had rushed to the hospital immediately.","She never imagined that Si Nian and his three children, who should have been thousands of miles away, would be here.","Yang Yujie was completely bewildered.","Chief Yang withdrew his gaze, gave the pale-faced Yang Yujie a once-over, but said nothing.","He then turned to Si Nian with a sigh. \"Little Zhou is a fortunate man. In that case, I won't disturb your family reunion. Yujie, come out. I need a word with you.\"","Yang Yujie bit her lip, glanced at Zhou Yueshen once more, and seeing him with his eyes downcast, followed Chief Yang out with a grim expression.","Zhou Yueshen hadn't looked at her once from start to finish.","The ward fell into a deathly silence.","\"Daddy, Daddy, is she the auntie who secretly wrote you letters?\" It was Zhou Zehan's curiosity that finally broke the quiet.","Zhou Yueshen snapped back to reality, remembering his two sons had also seen Yang Yujie's letters before, and felt a pang of awkwardness.","He cleared his throat with a fist, momentarily at a loss for how to respond, silently pleading with his son to stop.","As it was, Si Nian was still angry with him.","Si Nian, however, withdrew her gaze and said, \"Little Han, you still remember that after all this time?\"","Zhou Zehan huffed, \"Writing letters to Daddy... I don't like her.\" He looked puzzled at Zhou Yueshen. \"Daddy, do you like her?\"","Zhou Yueshen choked slightly. \"Of course not.\"","\"Then why did she write to you?\" Zhou Zehan didn't understand.","Zhou Yueshen felt a headache coming on.","Si Nian pinched his little cheek. \"Stop grilling your father. He needs to rest.\"","The sky darkened quickly. In the northwest, night fell later. Back home, the children would have been asleep by now.","Knowing Zhou Yueshen needed quiet to recuperate, Si Nian didn't let the children bother him. She asked Yu Dong, who had come by, to take them back to sleep.","They hadn't rested since taking the train during the day, and the children could barely keep their eyes open.","Yu Dong was perceptive. Knowing the couple hadn't seen each other for almost two months, they must have a lot to talk about.","After all, absence makes the heart grow fonder. He immediately assured her he would take care of everything properly.","Si Nian watched him leave before sitting down to tidy up the food containers.","Zhou Yueshen kept glancing at her. When she looked back, he would avert his eyes.","He seemed to be hesitating to speak.","Si Nian sighed. \"Just say whatever you want to say. Why do you look like I'm forbidding you to speak?\"","Did she seem that fierce?","Really, this old man in his thirties was putting on such a weak, helpless, and pitiful act.","Yet he sat there solid as a mountain.","Zhou Yueshen, caught out, flashed a look of embarrassment. \"Nian Nian, still angry?\"","Si Nian sat beside him. \"Not anymore.\"","\"I'm not that petty, Zhou Yueshen,\" she added.","\"If you keep this up, people will think I'm mistreating you.\" Just look at the pitying glance Yu Dong had thrown him on his way out.","Zhou Yueshen's low voice rumbled. \"How could they? I'm just worried you're unhappy, that you'll upset yourself.\"","Si Nian glared at him. Seeing the many unbandaged wounds on his face, the broken skin and red scratches, she felt a shameful softness in her heart. \"I'm not angry anymore. When I saw you back and you spoke to me earlier, I thought, you being alive is stronger than anything.\"","Hearing this, Zhou Yueshen felt a wave of tenderness in his heart, and his mood lifted unconsciously.","He didn't know why he felt so happy.","\"It must have been hard on you. Did you suffer much on the way here?\" he asked.","Si Nian complained, \"Of course. My backside still hurts from sitting. I thought I could rest a bit once we arrived, but we'd just gotten here when you returned. I rushed over non-stop to see you, bought you food... I'm utterly exhausted now.\"","Her voice carried an unconscious note of grievance and petulance.","Truthfully, having been lying around for days on the train, she had slept quite comfortably.","But she couldn't let the old man know she slept well, or she'd seem heartless.","So she added, \"Mm, I couldn't sleep well on the train at all.\"","Zhou Yueshen's gaze grew even more guilt-ridden. \"My fault.\"","He knew that him being overdue for so long without returning or sending letters must have worried her.","He just never imagined she would travel thousands of miles to come.","His heart beat uncontrollably. Listening to her recount the events on the train with that aggrieved tone, he felt a sour, unbearable ache.","He reached out, pulled her into his arms, and held her tightly.","Si Nian, afraid of touching his wounds, quickly pushed against him. \"Your injuries.\"","Zhou Yueshen tightened his arms around her, as if only this could prove she was truly here before him now.","He had never imagined a day would come when someone would travel such a distance for someone like him.","At this moment, he would die willingly.","\"Minor injuries. Don't worry.\"","His deep voice fell from above her head. The night was chilly, but his embrace was wonderfully warm.","It had been too long since they'd held each other, and with the children around, it felt awkward.","Now, she found herself somewhat addicted to it.","\"Is everything alright at home?\" he asked.","Si Nian, her attention diverted, began softly recounting the events of the past period.","She didn't hide the incident of the Second Child being kidnapped, telling him how truly scared she had been at the time.","Zhou Yueshen's arm around her tightened further. Finding the sitting position uncomfortable, Si Nian simply climbed onto the bed, pulled the blanket over them, and leaned against the man's shoulder as she talked.","Both of them savored this moment of intimacy.","Zhou Yueshen, with his injuries, couldn't move much, lying stiffly straight.","Seeing him immobilized, a mischievous thought arose in Si Nian's mind. Her hand wandered, rubbing against his chest one moment, then touching his Adam's apple the next, quietly laughing at the way it bobbed unconsciously.","Hearing her laughter, Zhou Yueshen took her hand and turned his head to look at her helplessly. \"Stop messing around.\"","Si Nian immediately put on a wronged expression. \"After being apart for so long, I can't even touch you anymore? Our feelings have cooled after all.\"","Zhou Yueshen, resigned, placed her small hand back on him. \"It's not that.\"","It wasn't that she couldn't touch him, it was just that his current condition made movement difficult.","\"I don't believe you. You're not as good to me as before. You used to kiss me first. Now when I take the initiative, you complain. Fine, fine... I'll leave tomorrow.\"","She began her tea-scented talk.","Zhou Yueshen drew in a sharp breath, lowered his gaze to look at her for a few seconds, then suddenly reached out, his hand cupping the back of her head. He kissed her fiercely, his lips grazing hers as he murmured, \"Nian Nian, you always provoke me.\"","—S—u—p—p—o—r—t— t—h—e— A—u—t—h—o—r—. What, you ask why the village chief is still doing this even after the competition is over? Well, every little bit helps."]},{"number":316,"title":"Chapter 316: You Are My Whole World","paragraphs":["Si Nian opened her eyes and looked up.","Their gazes met and intertwined.","Zhou Yueshen's palm pressed down on her slightly, still holding her in place.","Si Nian's head was tilted up slightly. His thumb brushed against the corner of her lips. \"How could I ever want you to leave? You are my entire world.\"","Si Nian's eyes grew hot.","The older man claimed he wasn't good with sweet talk, but when he spoke words of love, it was utterly devastating.","He always made her feel cherished and adored.","The hospital room was quiet, their breaths audible. His warm breath fanned her face. Si Nian's hands subconsciously tightened their grip on the blanket, her fingertips turning white.","Everything seemed understood without words.","Zhou Yueshen watched her for a few seconds, his hand pressing down again as he lowered his head to capture her lips.","Her hair was scattered in disarray across the white sheets.","Si Nian tilted her head back, accepting his kiss. Even injured, Zhou Yueshen was restless. Stirred by passion, his hand slid downward, pressing her waist against him with considerable force.","Si Nian instinctively grabbed his powerful arm, and only when her fingers touched the bandages on his body did she snap back to reality.","She didn't want him exerting himself while injured, and besides, they were still in a hospital room.","Si Nian's eyes flew open. She gave him a little push, and Zhou Yueshen pulled back, creating some distance.","Looking up, Si Nian could see his sharply defined jawline. His lips glistened faintly with moisture, looking rather indecent.","Zhou Yueshen's complexion seemed to have darkened a shade, perhaps from the strong ultraviolet rays here.","His arms, when flexed, were powerfully built, feeling like solid rock.","To avoid fanning the flames, Si Nian restrained her own desire. She reached out and touched the side of his face. \"Zhou Yueshen, I'm a little sleepy.\"","Zhou Yueshen had been about to lower his head for another kiss. Hearing this, he paused, then gently pecked her lips. He drew her into the crook of his arm, resting his chin on the top of her head, and softly replied, \"Alright, sleep.\"","Si Nian was genuinely tired. It was very late now, and the hospital, which had been somewhat noisy during the day, was utterly silent.","Leaning against the man's chest, she grew drowsy in no time.","But in her half-asleep state, her gaze fell on the curtain drawn around the bed at the back of the room.","She meant to ask what was behind it, but she was too tired. His large, warm hand patted her back gently and rhythmically, as if soothing a child, and she drifted off to sleep in an instant.","The blanket was small, and the bed was a single, but fortunately, Si Nian was petite. Holding her, Zhou Yueshen could manage to sleep.","He pulled the blanket over her, listening to her breathing gradually even out.","Soon, the door was pushed open softly. It was the nurse on duty coming in with his medicine.","Then, she saw Commander Zhou, who was supposed to be the patient, sitting by the bed. On the hospital bed, a small figure lay curled up under the slightly raised covers, seemingly fast asleep.","The nurse was stunned and instinctively looked at Zhou Yueshen.","His eyes were lowered, his expression indifferent.","Only when she entered did he glance her way.","One look from him was enough for the nurse to immediately lower her voice. \"Commander Zhou, here is your medicine.\"","Zhou Yueshen gave a slight nod. \"Leave it there.\"","He seemed calm, but his voice was very low.","As if afraid of disturbing the person sleeping on the bed.","The nurse was inwardly amazed. She quietly set the medicine down, then picked up another dose and walked behind the curtain.","The next second, she met the somewhat bloodshot, restrained eyes of the man on the bed inside.","The nurse was startled. \"Fu...\"","Zhou Yueshen glanced sideways toward the curtain.","When Si Nian woke up the next morning, she found the curtain around the inner bed had been drawn back.","Inside was an iron bed, but it was empty.","She was taken aback for a moment.","As she stirred, a deep, male voice came from above her head. \"Awake?\"","She looked up. Zhou Yueshen was half-leaning against the headboard, a newspaper in his hand, but his eyes were on her.","Si Nian made an affirmative sound but kept staring at the bed behind the curtain. \"Was someone there yesterday?\"","She felt rather embarrassed now. She had thought Zhou Yueshen was the only one in the room yesterday, and her attention had been entirely on him.","Seeing the other bed now made her worried.","If someone had been there, then wouldn't they have heard the two of them being intimate in the room last night?","Zhou Yueshen glanced at the empty bed, his expression inscrutable. \"Mm,\" he affirmed. \"There was.\"","Si Nian's face immediately flushed with embarrassment.","\"Then why didn't you tell me?\" She shifted the blame onto him.","Zhou Yueshen let out a low chuckle, his chest vibrating slightly. \"I didn't know at the time either.\"","If the nurse hadn't gone in to change the other patient's dressing last night, he genuinely hadn't noticed.","Normally, there was only one bed in the room, but with many injured recently, it had gotten crowded, and extra beds had been added.","It wasn't really that strange.","Zhou Yueshen looked down at her. Si Nian's face was full of shame.","He found her utterly adorable. Last night, she had been so bold and daring when provoking him, and now she was feeling shy.","A woman who was only fierce within her own nest.","Seeing him still smiling, Si Nian felt even more indignant.","She had a strong feeling Zhou Yueshen had done it on purpose.","But she had no proof.","Because he seemed to be in an exceptionally good mood today.","Just then, a nurse walked in. \"Commander Zhou, it's time to change your dressing.\"","Zhou Yueshen put down the newspaper. \"Alright, leave it here.\"","Then he looked at Si Nian. \"Nian Nian.\"","Si Nian: \"?\" Why are you calling me?","The nurse instantly understood and, after leaving, immediately gossiped with her colleagues: \"Oh my, Commander Zhou and his stunningly beautiful wife are so deeply in love. Commander Zhou is incredibly gentle, holding her while reading the newspaper.\"","\"Goodness, when I went in last night, I was shocked, you know? The injured Commander Zhou was sitting by the bed, coaxing her to sleep. What kind of family status is that...\"","Zhou Yueshen waited until the nurse had left before looking at her, his voice deep. \"Nian Nian, I haven't let anyone else change my dressing.\"","Si Nian: \"...So? Call her back. I'm not that petty.\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","\"Sister-in-law, I've brought you breakfast!\"","Fortunately, Yu Dong chose that moment to rush in, giving Zhou Yueshen a way out.","He was carrying breakfast in one hand, holding Yaoyao with the other, and the two brothers followed behind.","Yaoyao's hair was a complete mess, clearly uncombed, and she was clutching a small biscuit in her hand.","Seeing them, she let go of Yu Dong's hand and ran over on her little legs, offering the half-eaten biscuit to Si Nian. \"Mama, eat biscuit.\"","Si Nian smiled and patted her head, then hurried to get up and wash up.","Zhou Yueshen glanced at the medicine beside him, remained silent for a moment, and began changing the dressing himself.","\"Dad, Dad, we'll help you.\" Zhou Zedong and his brother hurried over to assist him.","Yu Dong set the food aside. Noticing the newspaper on the table, he picked it up, glanced at it, and burst out laughing. \"It's a story paper! Boss, you read this stuff? 'Wife discovers husband in hospital having affair with nurse, poisons him in a fit of rage'... Haha, that's hilarious.\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\""]},{"number":317,"title":"Chapter 317: Fu Yang Awakens","paragraphs":["After washing up, Si Nian walked out and asked curiously, \"What's so funny? What are you talking about?\"","Yu Dong was about to speak, but Zhou Yueshen interrupted in a deep voice, \"Nothing much. You must be hungry, let's eat first.\"","Si Nian had originally thought to wash up and then come out to help him, but she didn't expect the man to be so quick, having already changed everything.","His bandaging skill was no worse than a hospital nurse's.","It seemed he was used to treating his own wounds.","She walked over, pulled up the small table, and opened the things Yu Dong had bought.","Inside were five or six steamed buns the size of a man's fist, millet porridge, some stir-fried cabbage, and a few eggs.","It looked simple and ordinary, but the portions were generous.","Yu Dong had packed it from the cafeteria; the troops basically ate these things every day.","Si Nian peeled an egg for Yao Yao to eat, and peeled another one for Zhou Yueshen, placing it in his bowl.","Zhou Yueshen finished it in two bites and added some cabbage to her bowl.","The military canteen food wasn't bad; the nutrition was balanced.","It was just that the flavor was a bit lacking, no spiciness.","The Second Child noticed his father's action and also stretched his bowl over, \"Dad, I want some too.\"","Zhou Yueshen gave him a chopstickful as well, and also added some for Zhou Zedong and Yao Yao.","The Second Child didn't eat quietly, chattering excitedly about his fun experiences at school while eating.","The whole ward was lively and bustling.","Meanwhile, in the single room next door, a nurse had also delivered breakfast.","Fu Yang, pale-faced, was half-leaning against the headboard, his head turned to look at the scenery outside the window. His complexion was poor, and he had lost weight, the arrogance and aloofness he had when he first arrived gone.","The cheerful laughter and liveliness from the children next door made his room seem even emptier and quieter.","He looked somewhat pitiful.","It was said he had applied to switch to a private room from the shared ward overnight.","Originally, everyone thought this young master from the city was unwilling to lower himself to share a room with others, but now she seemed to understand a little.","The nurse carried the food in, \"Regiment Commander Fu, I've brought your breakfast.\"","Fu Yang looked out the window, but his eyes were vacant, as if not really seeing anything, his thoughts elsewhere.","The nurse called twice before he heard, coming back to himself somewhat dazedly, \"Just put it there.\"","The nurse glanced at him again. There was no denying that Regiment Commander Fu was indeed handsome with an exceptional aura. When he first arrived in their northwest region, he had caused quite a stir, with many people wanting to catch a glimpse of his extraordinary looks.","Back then, he just seemed different from their regiment commanders here. Their commanders were rough and burly. But this commander seemed like a true officer, his bearing clearly indicating he came from a prominent family, lofty and unattainable.","Yet, just over a month later, this favored son of heaven seemed to have suffered some great blow. His skin had darkened, his face looked terrible and pale, he had become terribly thin, and his whole person was filled with a sense of despondency.","Could it be that the failure of the no-man's-land mission and his injuries had dealt him too heavy a blow?","It was said when he was rescued, his life was hanging by a thread.","If Regiment Commander Zhou and the others had arrived any later, perhaps Regiment Commander Fu wouldn't have made it back.","It was said before that there were rumors from the troops about some friction between Regiment Commander Fu and Regiment Commander Zhou. Now, having been saved by Regiment Commander Zhou, he probably didn't feel good about it either.","Him showing such an expression now was somewhat understandable.","For the next two days, Zhou Yueshen's ward remained very lively.","Every day there was the children's cheerful laughter and the delicious smell of food.","Si Nian thought that since Zhou Yueshen's place had cooking facilities, she might as well buy some nourishing ingredients herself so his wounds would heal faster.","Staying in the hospital all the time wasn't ideal anyway.","She seasoned her cooking well, and every day when she carried it into the hospital, the aroma wafted everywhere.","Especially for Fu Yang next door, who now looked at the cabbage and plain porridge in his own bowl and found it utterly tasteless.","His expression grew colder and gloomier.","Things he once disdained and wouldn't give a second glance were now forever out of his reach.","Fu Yang's state of mind was complex, filled mostly with a tearing pain.","He never knew he could feel this way because of one person.","Even when Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen showed affection in front of him before, he only felt somewhat uncomfortable.","He didn't think he felt uncomfortable because he liked Si Nian; he just felt displeased seeing his former fiancée being intimate with another man before his eyes.","But that night, waking from a deep sleep and hearing that familiar voice, he knew immediately it was her. He was even pleasantly surprised, thinking that Si Nian had come to see him.","Then he thought it impossible; the northwest was so far away.","Until he heard Zhou Yueshen's voice and realized she had come from thousands of miles away, not for him.","Although Si Nian gave him a different feeling now, Fu Yang still felt she was very much like before. When she was good to someone, she gave her all, willing to do anything for them.","It was like that before, and it was like that now.","Only the object of her affection was no longer him.","Before coming to the northwest, he was aloof, cold and detached, and alone.","He looked down on matters of love between men and women.","But now, witnessing it firsthand, he realized how truly lonely he was.","It was as if everything around him was cold and dark, with only their family enveloped in warmth and happiness.","He saw Si Nian walk past the door of his ward carrying things without looking back, and he heard her clear, tinkling laughter from time to time, or her sweet nothings with the man.","The happiness on her face wasn't fake.","It was just that he had been blinded by his own pride, truly believing someone would spend their whole life considering him irreplaceable.","A clear realization was the most deadly.","He was unwilling to believe it, yet had to admit he had long lost to Zhou Yueshen, both in ability and in love.","Something everyone else knew, only he had been deceiving himself.","Si Nian had long since had no place for him in her heart...","In the past, Fu Yang would have certainly thought it didn't matter at all.","But he didn't understand why, on the day Si Nian truly didn't like him anymore, he would feel such pain.","As if something very important had completely disappeared from his world...","When Mother Fu and Fu Qianqian rushed to the military hospital, it was already noon.","When she saw her son lying alone on the worn-out hospital bed, his face gaunt, her heart ached and tears streamed down her face.","\"Xiao Yang, are you okay? Mom's here, Mom came to see you, wuwuwu...\" She hurried over, took her son's hand, and cried.","Fu Yang's once slender, fair hands were now covered in scars, which broke her heart.","Although her son had grown up in the military, he rarely got injured.","Let alone lying in bed now, unable to get up, covered in wounds.","Mother Fu knew the living conditions for soldiers in remote border areas were the harshest and most brutal, but seeing it with her own eyes was still hard to bear.","Fu Qianqian, usually loud and sharp-tongued, was quiet now, calling out softly, \"Brother.\"","Fu Yang collected his thoughts and looked at the two of them.","Their arrival brought some life and warmth to this lifeless ward.","Fu Yang managed a slight twitch at the corner of his mouth.","Only someone who has faced death knows how important the people who care about you are.","He used to find it bothersome, but now he feels its warmth and preciousness."]},{"number":318,"title":"Chapter 318: Your face used to be always gloomier than shit.","paragraphs":["He patted his mother's shoulder, comforting her, \"Mom, I'm fine.\"","\"How did you get here?\"","\"Your father said you went missing in the uninhabited zone. You really scared me to death! If something happened to you, how could I go on living!\" Fu's mother cried, tears and mucus streaming down her face, completely losing her usual ladylike demeanor.","Fu Yang's voice was gentle, \"There's no mission without danger. I'm fine now, aren't I? Don't cry anymore.\"","His change surprised both mother and daughter.","Fu Qianqian never knew her brother could be so gentle.","She was momentarily stunned: \"Brother, what's wrong with you? You weren't like this before.\"","Fu Yang still maintained his calm tone, \"Me before?\"","Fu Qianqian nodded emphatically, \"Yes, your face used to be meaner than shit.\"","Fu Yang: \"...\"","Zhou Yueshen had a fractured leg. No matter how tough a man is, at a time like this, he could only lie still obediently.","Si Nian arrived at the hospital carrying bone soup and heard a familiar voice from the next room.","At first, she thought she misheard.","Otherwise, why would she hear Fu Qianqian's voice here?","So, she instinctively and curiously peeked her head towards the room and glanced inside.","Just in time to hear Fu Qianqian say, \"Yes, your face used to be meaner than shit.\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","She knew Fu Yang was staying in the hospital but hadn't paid attention to exactly where.","Fu Yang was narcissistic enough on his own, and to prevent him from getting the wrong idea, Si Nian had deliberately kept to herself, focusing only on her own affairs.","She hadn't mentioned him to Zhou Yueshen either.","But she never expected him to be just on the other side of the wall.","Thinking about how Zhou Yueshen had been whispering sweet nothings to her in the room these past few days...","She thought it was because they hadn't seen each other for too long.","But now: Hah...","This secretly sentimental old man.","Si Nian didn't look further, withdrew her gaze, and entered the room.","The injuries on Zhou Yueshen's upper body were healing quickly. Apart from the wounds on his waist and abdomen, bandages had been removed from many places after just a few days, though the scars were still quite shocking.","After a few days of rest, coupled with having his wife and children by his side, the old man's complexion didn't look like someone who often stayed up late at all. He looked very well, clearly someone in robust health.","He was currently sitting by the bed, holding a small handkerchief and wiping the face of a drowsy Yaoyao.","Si Nian found it troublesome to bring the children back and forth, so she usually went home alone, leaving the kids for Zhou Yueshen to look after.","Fortunately, there was another bed in the ward, where the Eldest Child, the Second Child, and Yaoyao slept at night.","During the day, Yaoyao also napped a lot. She would fall asleep on Zhou Yueshen after playing until she was tired. She had just woken up from her nap and was sitting on the bed, rubbing her eyes with her chubby little hands.","The Eldest Child and the Second Child were sitting nearby doing their homework, one serious, the other daydreaming.","Seeing Si Nian arrive, Xiao Han was the first to dash over, very thoughtfully helping Si Nian carry the lunchbox.","\"Mom, Mom, I've finished all my homework. I can write from one to one hundred now. If you don't believe me, ask Dad.\"","Zhou Yueshen finished wiping his daughter's face, heard this, and looked at Si Nian.","\"Xiao Han is doing much better than before.\"","Praised by his dad, Xiao Han unconsciously puffed out his chest, his nose practically pointing to the sky.","Si Nian ruffled the little one's head, \"I stewed some bone soup. Drink it while it's hot.\" She took out bowls and chopsticks for everyone, then asked Zhou Yueshen, \"Did the doctor say when you can be discharged?\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded, \"In a couple more days. Can't wait to leave?\"","Staying in the hospital room every day wasn't ideal.","Si Nian shook her head. Hearing Zhou Yueshen say he could be discharged early, she thought it better to wait until he recovered a bit more.","Just as they were all drinking the rich and fragrant bone soup, Wang Jianguo walked in, one arm in a sling, tall and burly like a bear.","He was even a few inches taller than Zhou Yueshen.","He lumbered in, his nose twitching, \"I knew it! I smelled meat from way down the hall. I was wondering when the cafeteria started cooking such delicious food. So it's you, sneaking a feast all by yourself!\"","As soon as he entered, the entire room felt cramped.","Si Nian turned to look at him. He seemed quite injured as well. He was very tall and large. She considered herself not very short, but at this moment, she still felt he was like a giant.","The Second Child had already exaggeratedly opened his mouth into an 'O' shape.","He thought the tallest, biggest man he had ever seen was his dad.","He never imagined there could be someone even taller and burlier than Dad.","He was stunned. So cool!","Could he become this tall and mighty in the future?","\"Is this your wife and your three kids?\" Wang Jianguo, upon entering, met the gazes of the children and Si Nian. He stopped in his tracks, scratching his buzz cut.","Zhou Yueshen gave a slight nod, seemingly already accustomed to his familiar tone.","He didn't pay him much mind, instead introducing him to Si Nian beside him, \"Nian Nian, this is Wang Jianguo, my former comrade-in-arms. He's not a good guy, don't bother with him.\"","Wang Jianguo: \"... Over a decade of good brotherhood, and that's how you introduce me?\"","Si Nian couldn't help but laugh. She didn't expect Zhou Yueshen to have such a love-hate friend in the military.","Although Zhou Yueshen said not to bother with him, if he truly disliked the man, he wouldn't have bothered saying so much.","It seemed their relationship must be very good indeed.","Seeing the other man was also injured, he was probably one of the personnel involved in this mission.","Si Nian pulled over a stool, \"Comrade Wang, please have a seat.\"","\"Now that's what I call gracious!\" Wang Jianguo snorted, pulling the stool and sitting down. The two of them were quite a pair—one with a broken leg, the other with a broken arm.","Si Nian got a bowl and served him some soup. Although it was bone soup, it also contained trotters, stewed until soft and glutinous, melting in the mouth.","Wang Jianguo had already been salivating. These past few days injured, he'd been eating steamed buns and cabbage.","Now his mouth was practically watering. He didn't stand on ceremony, thanked her, and took it.","He drank it down in two gulps, then chewed on the meat, smacking his lips, \"Hiss~ This meat is stewed so tender. I've never had such delicious pig's trotters. Where did you buy them, sister?\"","Si Nian said, \"I stewed them myself. I thought since Yueshen hurt his bones, I should nourish him.\"","Wang Jianguo wanted another bowl but felt too embarrassed to ask. He could only stare at Zhou Yueshen with envy and jealousy, \"Old Zhou, you're living the good life, no wonder you wouldn't come back even when we asked.\"","Wang Jianguo thought to himself, if it were me, I wouldn't come back either.","Even though they weren't his biological children, the fact that three kids traveled all this way to visit him showed how important he was in their hearts.","Not to mention having such a beautiful, young wife.","These past few days, although lying in his own ward, he had heard about Zhou Yueshen's wife and children visiting. They said Battalion Commander Zhou seemed like a changed man, revolving around his wife and sons every day, coaxing his daughter to sleep, coaxing his wife to sleep... It sounded downright unbelievable.","He refused to believe it, which is why he came over.","And got proven wrong.","Wang Jianguo was genuinely envious.","He was unmarried at his age. It wasn't that he had no interest in women, just that the person he liked didn't like him back.","And he didn't want to just marry anyone to make do. That wouldn't be fair to himself or the other person.","And so, time passed, and he was already in his thirties.","Seeing that former bachelor, who had once been even more single than himself, now settled with a wife, child, and a warm home, he couldn't help but feel a pang of envy.","It seemed that married life wasn't as difficult as he had imagined.","Meanwhile, Zhang Cuimei and Liu Dongdong had also arrived just outside the military compound."]},{"number":319,"title":"Chapter 319: Everything goes black","paragraphs":["Since the two were not direct relatives, they were stopped outside the military compound.","After all, an army base isn't a place you can just waltz into. If you haven't made arrangements in advance, you need to verify your identity to get in.","Zhang Cuimei had arrived putting on airs, never expecting to be barred from entering.","Her own husband was in the military, and she lived in the family quarters.","Usually, it was her who stopped others from entering; when had it ever been her turn to be blocked at the gate?","Besides, Fu Yang was a regiment commander, and she was his mother-in-law.","She was deeply displeased.","However, no matter how much she objected, the guards at the gate couldn't let her in.","This wasn't South China; no one here knew she was Fu Yang's mother-in-law.","Before they could get any response, they instead encountered Si Nian, who was leading her son out to buy groceries.","When Zhang Cuimei saw Si Nian, she almost thought her eyes were playing tricks on her.","Otherwise, how could Si Nian, who should be thousands of miles away, be here? Shouldn't she be teaching at that downtown primary school right now?","For a moment, she thought it was just someone who looked like Si Nian, but upon seeing the child she was holding—who was unmistakably the Zhou family's second son—she had to believe her own eyes. Her voice rose sharply: \"Si Nian, what are you doing here!\"","If she hadn't genuinely traveled for two days and nights by train to reach this place, Zhang Cuimei would have thought she was still in Yun-Gui-Chuan City.","Had Si Nian already learned about Fu Yang's accident and rushed over?","She was so close to Fu Qianqian; if something really happened to Fu Yang, she'd definitely be among the first to know.","Considering this possibility, Zhang Cuimei's face turned green with anger: \"Have you no shame? You're married, yet you traveled all the way to the northwest to pester Fu Yang? He and Sisi are married now, what exactly are you trying to do!\"","Zhang Cuimei couldn't think of any other reason.","Fu Yang gets injured, and Si Nian shows up.","What kind of coincidence is that in this world?","Si Nian was also somewhat stunned. Why was Zhang Cuimei here?","She quickly collected herself. Presumably, the Si family had also heard about Fu Yang's accident and traveled all this way.","The novel mentioned Lin Sisi coming, but Lin Sisi was in prison now, so she definitely couldn't make it.","The Si family naturally wouldn't pass up such a good opportunity to curry favor.","Zhang Cuimei had really invested in this trip.","Si Nian noticed someone behind her and glanced over.","It was Liu Dongdong.","Liu Dongdong, it must be said, was dressed quite fashionably, but awkwardly, her hairstyle was exactly the same as Si Nian's.","Si Nian raised an eyebrow.","She remembered that the last time she saw Liu Dongdong, her hairstyle was different, wasn't it?","Not only that, the long journey hadn't left her looking haggard; instead, she wore a subtle no-makeup makeup look that most people wouldn't notice.","The fact that Liu Dongdong could get Zhang Cuimei to bring her here showed that her position in the Si family was now firmly established.","She had completely gained the trust of both husband and wife.","This time, Lin Sisi couldn't come, but Liu Dongdong did.","On the surface, she seemed to be accompanying Zhang Cuimei, but her real target was Fu Yang.","Yet, no one suspected her motives.","Si Nian felt that if her opponent weren't Lin Sisi but Liu Dongdong, she probably wouldn't be so easy to deal with.","Otherwise, in the novel, Lin Sisi wouldn't have been brought down by Liu Dongdong.","If not for the protagonist's halo, she would have been finished many times over.","Si Nian didn't like Lin Sisi, but she had no fondness for Liu Dongdong either.","Both went to great lengths trying to snatch what belonged to others. She didn't understand what kind of family would instill such twisted values.","But Si Nian didn't want to meddle either. Hearing Zhang Cuimei's words, she wasn't angry: \"Auntie Si, do you have a persecution complex? Whenever I appear somewhere, you assume I'm here for Fu Yang?\"","\"Fu Yang might be a golden treasure, a good son-in-law in your eyes, but to me, he's a piece of shit.\" Si Nian borrowed Fu Qianqian's words.","Zhang Cuimei snorted coldly: \"Putting on such airs. If you're not here for Fu Yang, why did you travel all this way?\"","Then, she angrily turned to the guard who had stopped her, \"Look at what you're doing! She has no relation to the Fu family, yet you let her in. I'm Regiment Commander Fu's mother-in-law, and you won't let me in? Is there no justice?\"","Liu Dongdong was also surprised to see Si Nian here.","But then she felt a pang of panic. If Si Nian was here, had she really beaten them to it?","She hadn't forgotten Fu Yang's special regard for Si Nian. If Si Nian really traveled all this way to visit Fu Yang, he might very well soften.","Liu Dongdong firmly believed that Si Nian, who had driven Lin Sisi to such a desperate state, was no ordinary opponent.","Although she seemed married to Zhou Yuenshen, all her actions were drawing closer to Fu Yang.","Now she had even arrived before them. What made it even more incomprehensible was that Si Nian had brought Zhou Yuenshen's adopted son along.","Wasn't she afraid of causing suspicion, or worried that Zhou Yuenshen might find out?","Liu Dongdong felt something was off, but panic and resentment dominated her mind. She echoed Zhang Cuimei, \"Comrade Si, you are married. Although I heard your husband has been away on a long trip and hasn't returned for a while, it really isn't appropriate for you to travel so far to visit another man, is it?\" After saying this, she deliberately cast an apologetic glance at the guard.","Hearing this, Si Nian almost laughed: \"It's inappropriate for me, but appropriate for you?\"","Liu Dongdong was stunned, then flustered.","She had kept her feelings for Fu Yang well hidden; no one had discovered them yet.","Otherwise, the Si family wouldn't have kept her around.","But Si Nian's single sentence instantly sent a wave of panic through her.","It felt like being put on a spit over a fire.","As if Si Nian had seen right through her intentions. Her face paled, her eyes reddened, and she looked at Si Nian with a meek, pleading expression, saying, \"Don't say such things. I'm just here to accompany Auntie Zhang. She's alone and not in the best health; I came along to take care of her.\"","Zhang Cuimei was deeply moved by these words.","She felt even more that Si Nian, whom she had raised from childhood, was inferior to Liu Dongdong. \"Don't go too far! I asked Dongdong to come with me. You ruined my Sisi, and now you won't even spare her only friend?\"","She thought Si Nian's mockery of Liu Dongdong was because Liu Dongdong was her daughter's good friend.","A surge of anger rose within her.","Zhang Cuimei's display of defending Liu Dongdong would make even a dog shake its head in disbelief, let alone Si Nian.","Although she felt Zhang Cuimei deserved it, she couldn't stand Liu Dongdong's hypocritical act either. She said, \"I'm just a bit puzzled. A nanny who came to take care of you still found time to doll herself up. Those in the know would think she came to care for you; those who don't might think she's here for a date.\"","Hearing this, Zhang Cuimei instinctively sized up Liu Dongdong.","She noticed that Liu Dongdong had, at some point, powdered her face, tinted her lips, pinned pretty hair clips in her hair, and even changed her jacket.","She had been utterly exhausted along the journey. After all, she was getting on in years, and such a long train ride had naturally taken its toll. Her mind, moreover, was completely preoccupied with worry over whether something had happened to her prized prospective son-in-law, so she hadn't paid attention to these details at all.","If Si Nian hadn't pointed it out, she likely wouldn't have noticed."]},{"number":320,"title":"Chapter 320: Stunned","paragraphs":["A strange glint flashed in Zhang Cuimei's eyes.","Liu Dongdong wiped her tears and said, \"Si Nian, I know you hold a grudge against me because I helped Sisi back then, but why must you slander me like this? I have absolutely no designs on Mr. Fu. It's just that after coming to the city, people looked down on me for being rustic, and I just wanted to look a little nicer. Is it a crime to dress up these days?\"","\"Auntie Zhang said she would introduce me to a potential match, and I'm extremely grateful for that. How could I possibly repay kindness with betrayal? I'm not that kind of person. You've already ruined the relationship between Uncle Si and Sisi, and now you want to sabotage the relationship between Auntie and me too?\"","Her words immediately made Zhang Cuimei's face darken.","Thinking of her husband's attitude lately and his indifference towards Sisi, she instantly understood—Si Nian must have said something to her husband in private.","She must still resent the incident where Sisi stole the money, and she probably resents me too for marrying her off. That's why she's acting like this.","And now she's even framing Liu Dongdong, who has taken care of them for so long. Zhang Cuimei trembled with anger, her lips quivering.","She simply thought Si Nian was utterly vicious.","Seeing Zhang Cuimei like this, Si Nian felt she was truly beyond saving.","The guard on the side, seeing the conversation getting more and more out of line, also looked displeased. Comrade Si had become quite well-known in the military district these past few days.","She was Commander Zhou's wife.","Commander Zhou was a hero in their military district, respected and revered by everyone.","Even though he had been away for many years, his reputation still thundered.","Moreover, right after returning, he completed a major mission, saving several people, quelling the unrest in the no-man's land, and wiping out the gang of ore thieves. Everyone held him in high esteem.","He couldn't understand why this middle-aged woman was dragging her name through the mud with Commander Fu, and saying such increasingly unpleasant things.","He couldn't help but speak up, \"Commander's wife...\"","Before he could finish, Si Nian interrupted him, \"You really think you're something, don't you? What's there about your relationship as a nanny with the employer's family that's worth me sabotaging? Am I supposed to compete with you to be a nanny?\"","After saying this, ignoring Liu Dongdong's ashen and ugly expression, Si Nian turned to the guard and said, \"By the way, I heard Commander Fu is preparing for a divorce. They've come all this way, probably to pester Commander Fu. Don't let them in and add to Commander Fu's burden. After all, Commander Fu is seriously injured. Who would be responsible if he got so angry he passed out?\"","The guard immediately straightened his face, vowing he would absolutely not let them in.","Zhang Cuimei was so angry she felt dizzy.","She became even more convinced that Si Nian had come for Fu Yang.","And now she was even preventing her from meeting her son-in-law.","She even knew Fu Yang wanted to divorce her daughter.","This whole matter was probably her doing behind the scenes!","Zhang Cuimei swayed unsteadily, nearly falling over.","Si Nian wasn't just trying to scare her. Just as she was leaving earlier, she had overheard Fu Yang's mother talking to him about divorcing Lin Sisi.","Probably because of the awful things Zhang Cuimei said at her doorstep last time, which made Mrs. Fu see this family's true colors, she was now eagerly hoping her son would get a divorce quickly.","When Fu Yang heard that Zhang Cuimei had come, he also frowned.","He originally didn't want to deal with her, but since she had come all the way to the northwest, it would be unreasonable not to see her.","So he told them to let her in.","Hearing she could enter, Zhang Cuimei even shot a triumphant look at Si Nian.","Si Nian didn't care either. She took Second Child, who was carrying a small vegetable basket, and went out.","As soon as Zhang Cuimei entered the ward, she started complaining and pouring out her grievances. \"Xiao Fu, you have no idea how outrageous that girl Si Nian is. I knew she hadn't given up on you, but I never thought she'd be so shameless. Coming all this way to see you is one thing, but now she's even using your name to cause trouble! It's infuriating.\"","Fu Yang had sent his mother and Fu Qianqian to get something to eat. They had come a long way and hadn't eaten a bite before coming to see him. Since he couldn't get out of bed, he had to ask someone to take them. He was just about to rest when Zhang Cuimei burst in, noisily complaining about Si Nian.","His face immediately darkened.","Now, the name Si Nian was a taboo in his eyes.","Especially after realizing that his past assumptions—that all of Si Nian's actions were for his sake—were just his own wishful thinking, such things felt deeply humiliating to him.","Everyone in the military compound knew Si Nian had come for Zhou Yueshen.","The deep affection between the husband and wife had already become a beautiful story.","If he still narcissistically claimed it was because of him, then he really must be sick.","And before he could even recover from that blow, Zhang Cuimei was here saying things that could cause misunderstandings again.","If Si Nian still had even a shred of feeling for him, just a shred, knowing he was in this hospital, seriously injured, she couldn't possibly not come to see him.","But these past few days, he had seen Si Nian pass by his ward door with his own eyes, without even glancing his way.","Fu Yang understood very clearly that Si Nian no longer liked him.","If he hadn't personally heard Zhou Yueshen and Si Nian confess their true feelings to each other that night, hearing Zhang Cuimei's words today, he might have actually believed it.","\"Auntie Zhang!\" he coldly interrupted her. \"Si Nian has nothing to do with me. She didn't come here for me. I hope you remember that from now on and stop speaking ill of her!\"","Zhang Cuimei was stunned. Hearing Fu Yang actually reprimand her to defend Si Nian, her face instantly paled. Thinking Fu Yang was just avoiding suspicion, she hurriedly tried to placate him, \"That's not what I meant. It's all that wretched girl Si Nian's fault. Her coming all this way is causing misunderstandings. Don't worry, I'll make her leave right away.\"","Fu Yang looked at her as if she were an idiot. \"What right do you have to make her leave? Do you think this is still your home?\"","Zhang Cuimei choked, then said, \"She must have gotten in by relying on your status. With just a word from you, she would definitely leave.\"","Fu Yang sneered, \"I don't have that kind of power.\"","Thinking he, as a man, found it awkward to do such a thing, Zhang Cuimei immediately said, \"Don't worry, I'll handle this for you.\"","With that, she hurried out and pointed at the guard, ordering, \"That woman named Si Nian—you are not allowed to let her in.\"","The guard thought he had misheard. \"What?\"","\"Are you deaf?\" Zhang Cuimei said impatiently. \"Let me repeat: Do not let Si Nian and her son in!\"","\"On what grounds?\" the guard asked, incredulous.","An outsider was actually ordering them around, telling them not to let the Commander's wife in? Was she out of her mind?","Zhang Cuimei snorted coldly, \"On the grounds that I am Commander Fu's mother-in-law! You all know my status now, right?\""]},{"number":321,"title":"Chapter 321: The Majesty of Zhang Cuimei","paragraphs":["The guard was dumbfounded. Life was tough for everyone here, and even the wives in the family quarters were known for their simplicity and gentle temperaments. No one had ever been as arrogant as Zhang Cuimei.","Snapping back to reality, his face immediately darkened. \"I don't give a damn if you're Commander Fu's mother-in-law or whatever. Our commander's wife wants to come in, who are you to decide?\"","\"What?\" Zhang Cuimei thought she had misheard, digging at her ear in disbelief. \"Do you know who you're talking to? And besides, how could Si Nian possibly be the commander's wife? She's lying! She's already married. She married some country butcher, chose to be a stepmother to three kids, and has nothing to do with Commander Fu! That shameless brat! My daughter is the commander's wife!\"","She thought Si Nian was lying and claiming to be Fu Yang's wife, and she cursed furiously.","There were quite a few people coming and going at the moment, and they all turned to look at her.","The guard's face was as dark as storm clouds. He spat on the ground. \"Where did this madwoman come from, insulting our commander's wife? Get the hell out of here!\"","The guard was extremely rude, grabbing Zhang Cuimei and shoving her out.","Zhang Cuimei stumbled and landed hard on her backside with a thud, crying out in pain.","A military wife returning from shopping asked curiously, \"What's going on here?\"","\"Some crazy woman from who-knows-where keeps causing trouble for Commander Zhou's wife. Now she even tried to stop us from letting the wife in. She's insane!\"","Everyone knew Commander Zhou was a hero of the military district. Bullying Si Nian was like picking a fight with the entire district!","\"What? Commander Zhou's wife? How dare she! I heard Commander Zhou dotes on his wife. If he hears about this, he'll be furious.\"","Everyone stared at Zhang Cuimei in disbelief.","Others might not know, but they were well aware.","Many of their husbands and sons had served under Zhou Yueshen before.","Plenty had been put through the wringer by him.","Just hearing his name was enough to make them shudder.","That was precisely why the higher-ups had called him back from afar for this training exercise.","And now someone actually dared to challenge Commander Zhou?","\"You... you people...\" Zhang Cuimei stammered, not finishing her sentence before suddenly realizing something, her eyes nearly popping out of her head. \"Wait, what Commander Zhou? I'm talking about Commander Fu! What on earth is going on here?\"","The crowd looked at her as if she were an idiot. \"Lady, where are you from? You don't even know our Commander Zhou? Our Commander Zhou is one of the Three Elite Officers of the Northwest Military District, a great hero now. The Commander Fu you're talking about is the one from the South China Military District, right? I heard our Commander Zhou even went to rescue him. What kind of authority are you trying to throw around here?\"","\"Com... Commander Zhou?\" Zhang Cuimei's face went slack with shock, stuttering as an impossible thought flashed through her mind.","No, it couldn't be. Zhou Yueshen had been discharged long ago, hadn't he?","Besides, with his poor background, how could he possibly be a commander?","The next moment:","\"She dared to bully Yueshen's wife? Has she lost her mind?\"","\"I heard she's Commander Fu's mother-in-law, putting on airs as soon as she arrived.\"","\"Commander Fu seems like a decent man. How did he end up with a mother-in-law like this? Does she think this military district is her family's?\"","\"Xiao Wang, how did someone like this even get in? We're putting our foot down today—anyone who lets her in is going against us! Let's see how much official clout Commander Fu has to get her back in here!\"","The ones speaking were all wives from the family quarters. Their husbands and sons had all participated in the recent mission. If it weren't for Zhou Yueshen, they might not have come back at all.","They held him in the highest respect. While they might not know Si Nian well, she was one of their own. How could an outsider bully her?","Xiao Wang was more than happy to comply, saying fiercely, \"Don't worry, sisters. I'll definitely keep an eye on this lunatic. If she dares to insult the commander's wife again, I'll treat her as an unlawful element.\"","Zhang Cuimei stood there as if struck by lightning."]},{"number":322,"title":"Chapter 322: Retribution","paragraphs":["Liu Dongdong pretended to have only just realized what was happening and followed along. She didn't really want to leave Fu Yang, but since Zhang Cuimei had come out, it wouldn't be appropriate for an unmarried girl like her to stay alone in a room with Commander Fu; people would inevitably gossip.","So not long after Zhang Cuimei left, she followed as well.","She just intentionally kept her distance.","Because Fu Yang's attitude made her feel that something wasn't quite right.","Although she also hoped Si Nian would be driven away, it wasn't good for her to actively help. She didn't want to seem as overbearing as Zhang Cuimei and risk being disliked.","But she never expected that her intuition would save her this time. She never imagined that Si Nian's husband was actually a regiment commander in this military district.","Others might be unwilling to believe it, but Liu Dongdong had heard before that Zhou Yueshen used to be a soldier.","She just never thought about it in this context, since Zhou Yueshen had long been discharged and returned to the village.","Now, learning that he held a position here that was no less impressive than Fu Yang's...","This filled Liu Dongdong with both shock and jealousy.","She felt Si Nian's fate was just too good.","She originally thought that even if Si Nian married a butcher who could make money, there wasn't much to envy.","But she never expected Zhou Yueshen to have this additional layer of status.","This also explained clearly why Si Nian appeared here with the Zhou family's son.","And why Fu Yang's expression turned so ugly whenever Si Nian was mentioned.","So Si Nian wasn't here to see him at all, but to see Zhou Yueshen.","Liu Dongdong's heart was a tumult of mixed feelings.","Seeing Zhang Cuimei's fate, she felt relieved that she hadn't rushed forward immediately.","Otherwise, she might have been thrown out too by now.","If Zhou Yueshen was really a regiment commander here, then even Fu Yang probably couldn't really stand up for her.","Plus, Fu Yang didn't have much goodwill towards the Si family to begin with, so it was even less likely he'd step in to help.","Liu Dongdong pretended to run over in a panic, stopping just inside the iron gate as if someone had blocked her, and called out with feigned concern, \"Auntie Zhang, are you alright? How did things turn out like this?\"","Zhang Cuimei snapped back to reality and tried to re-enter, but was stopped. Her face turned pale then flushed, looking utterly terrible. Just as she was about to say something, Liu Dongdong spoke up, \"Don't worry, Auntie Zhang, I'll go find Commander Fu right now and put in a good word for you. They'll definitely let you back in.\"","After saying that, she turned and ran off.","Zhang Cuimei's expression was grim, and her heart was even more panicked.","She hadn't fully processed the fact that Si Nian's husband was a regiment commander in the Northwest Military District; her mind was still reeling.","So she didn't dwell on the fact that Liu Dongdong hadn't come out to support her.","Only when she saw the two guards looking at her with disdain did she belatedly realize how shameful her earlier behavior had been. She wished she could find a hole to crawl into.","She couldn't help but resent Si Nian in her heart. Why hadn't she told her about this beforehand? If she had, she wouldn't have had to lose so much face!","Maybe she deliberately didn't say anything, just to make her look bad.","Considering this possibility made Zhang Cuimei so angry her nose felt crooked.","April in the northwest was still very cold. She stood at the gate, unable to enter, yet unwilling to leave.","She could only hope Liu Dongdong would hurry back.","Her legs grew stiff from standing, but still there was no sign of Liu Dongdong.","Muttering a curse about her uselessness under her breath, she was hungry, tired, and couldn't stand it any longer.","She approached again. Even when the guards blocked her, she didn't get angry this time, having lost her previous arrogance. Instead, she fawned, \"Comrades, I've thought it over, and I was indeed too impulsive earlier. I realize my mistake now. To be honest, that girl Nian Nian is my daughter. I was just misunderstanding her earlier, which is why I got so angry. Please don't take it to heart.\"","Hearing this, the two guards exchanged glances, their expressions turning even more contemptuous. \"Even a vicious tiger doesn't harm its own cub. What kind of mother treats her daughter like that? Do you think we're fools?\"","Just then, Si Nian returned from buying groceries. The two guards immediately saluted, \"Regiment Commander's wife.\"","Si Nian raised an eyebrow, glanced at Zhang Cuimei's ashen face, and asked, \"What's going on now?\"","\"This crazy woman is making trouble here, ma'am. Don't worry, we won't let her in.\"","Given her previous behavior towards Si Nian, the two guards didn't dare let her in, afraid she'd cause trouble for Si Nian.","Zhang Cuimei grew anxious. \"But I didn't know the full story then! How can you blame it all on me?\"","\"Right, Nian Nian, hurry up and tell them to let me in. I am, after all, your adoptive mother. Zhou Yueshen is my son-in-law. How can they treat me like this!\"","The two guards looked at her suspiciously, then turned to Si Nian for confirmation. \"Regiment Commander's wife, is that true?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"That's right, she is my adoptive mother.\" Zhang Cuimei immediately snorted smugly, thinking, 'Good — you know your place.'","But then she heard Si Nian continue, \"However, we severed ties long ago. You can treat it as if she's not.\"","With that, ignoring Zhang Cuimei's drastically changing expression, Si Nian took the curious Second Child by the hand and walked inside.","Zhang Cuimei, coming back to her senses, grew frantic and tried to chase after them.","Unexpectedly, the two guards immediately stepped forward, blocking her path and making a gesture as if to draw their weapons.","Zhang Cuimei was so frightened her legs nearly gave way, a mix of cowardice and fury.","Watching Si Nian's retreating back, not once looking back, she was nearly driven mad. \"Si Nian! You heartless, ungrateful wretch! Treating me like this will bring you retribution!\"","Si Nian returned to the ward. The Second Child ran angrily to Zhou Yueshen to complain, \"Dad, Dad, that nasty grandma at the gate is picking on Mom again! She even yelled at Mom!\"","Zhou Yueshen was taken aback. \"Grandma?\"","Si Nian put the groceries aside. The hospital had a dedicated cooking area. Since Zhou Yueshen had arranged it, she could cook there, so sometimes she didn't need to go back to where Zhou Yueshen was staying.","She explained, \"It's my adoptive mother, Zhang Cuimei. She heard Fu Yang was injured and came to visit. Seeing me here, she thought I was pestering Fu Yang again and said some unpleasant things.\"","On the way back, the Second Child had said how much he hated Zhang Cuimei and asked why Mom didn't yell back.","Si Nian said, if a dog bites us, can we bite it back? She didn't want to get entangled with Zhang Cuimei.","But the Second Child was still holding his breath, saying that even if you can't bite a dog back, you can hit it back.","Si Nian thought her son made a good point, but the thing was, Zhang Cuimei was, after all, her adoptive mother and an elder. Zhang Cuimei could scold her, but if Si Nian scolded her back, it would be considered disrespectful and defiant.","Si Nian was more adept at making her opponents retreat in disarray without tarnishing her own reputation. Of course, in the Second Child's eyes, it just meant Mom got yelled at and couldn't yell back, which was utterly frustrating.","Now he was complaining to his father with an aggrieved air, almost wishing his father would go and beat up Zhang Cuimei.","Zhou Yueshen's brow furrowed slightly.","Although he knew the Si family wasn't sincere towards Si Nian, he hadn't expected them to be this absurd.","Si Nian had been married to him for so long, yet they still thought she was hung up on Fu Yang.","What a nuisance.","His voice was low. \"We're going back in a couple of days. Pay her no mind.\"","When Fu Qianqian and Fu's mother returned, they were quite surprised to see Liu Dongdong.","\"Dongdong? What are you doing here?\"","Liu Dongdong hurriedly explained the reason.","Hearing that Zhang Cuimei had brought her, Fu's mother's expression didn't brighten; instead, it became somewhat unnatural.","She couldn't figure out what Zhang Cuimei was doing coming here.","Feeling displeased but unable to vent her anger at Liu Dongdong, she only said, \"Tell Zhang Cuimei she doesn't need to pretend to be kind. Our Xiao Yang doesn't need her help. You should hurry back.\"","She was thoroughly annoyed by the pestering, feeling the Si family was like vampires, following them wherever they went.","Liu Dongdong bit her lip and lowered her head. \"Auntie Zhang said that Regimental Commander Fu is injured now, his body is weak, and conditions here in the northwest are harsh. The food surely can't compare to what's at home, so she sent me over. The soup I make is quite liked by Regimental Commander Fu and can help nourish him. I know this is very presumptuous, but Auntie Zhang just hopes Regimental Commander Fu can recover quickly...\"","These words struck right at Mother Fu's heart.","Earlier, when they went to the cafeteria to eat, they only had stir-fried cabbage and greasy meat. The taste was mediocre and not really to their liking.","Her son was already picky with food—no wonder he had lost so much weight in just over a month.","He looked terribly pale too.","Mother Fu's heart ached for him.","The problem was, neither she nor her daughter knew how to cook.","Liu Dongdong's appearance was simply a godsend.","Although she was very annoyed with Zhang Cuimei, she also wanted her son to recover quickly so they could leave. The medical facilities here weren't great, and she worried her son might suffer some lasting effects, which would be a terrible loss.","Besides, her son had indeed eaten the things Liu Dongdong brought before.","Mother Fu immediately let her stay but pretended not to hear anything about Zhang Cuimei.","Liu Dongdong gratefully promised she would take good care of Fu Yang, not mentioning a word about Zhang Cuimei being stopped outside.","Fu Qianqian, a toothpick dangling from her mouth, watched her thoughtfully.","Liu Dongdong was very pleased. Just as she stepped out, she saw Si Nian leading a child into the neighboring ward and was startled.","So Zhou Yueshen was injured too.","But since Si Nian had come in, she must have seen Zhang Cuimei being stopped outside earlier.","She was truly heartless. Although Zhang Cuimei wasn't a great person, she had raised her for eighteen years after all.","Now she herself got in but didn't let Zhang Cuimei in. It spoke volumes.","In Liu Dongdong's eyes, this behavior was nothing but ingratitude.","She went to the entrance, saw Zhang Cuimei looking disheveled, but didn't go out. As if forgetting there was a door right beside her, she stood inside and told Zhang Cuimei, with added drama, that she had tried asking Fu Yang for her, but the Fu family didn't want to offend Zhou Yueshen and refused.","She also said she pleaded with Si Nian, but Si Nian even scolded her, saying Zhang Cuimei deserved it.","This nearly made Zhang Cuimei faint from anger.","Seeing her hatred for Si Nian reach its peak, Liu Dongdong then sent her away, telling her to find a hotel to rest first. She said she really wanted to go out but couldn't get back in if she did, and besides, Mother Fu wanted someone to help cook and nourish Fu Yang. This was a good chance to improve relations between the two families.","Sure enough, Zhang Cuimei, in her rage, was completely fooled and didn't suspect a thing. She even told Liu Dongdong not to come out, adding gratefully, \"It's a good thing I brought you along, Dongdong. Otherwise, I really wouldn't know what to do.\"","She also instructed her to keep an eye out and not let any other women get close to Fu Yang before leaving.","...","When Si Nian went to cook in the afternoon, she saw Liu Dongdong busy in the kitchen.","She raised an eyebrow. She had just heard that Zhang Cuimei had left, but Liu Dongdong was still here?","Could it be that Zhang Cuimei deliberately left her behind to take care of Fu Yang?","Liu Dongdong saw her and was also startled.","For some reason, she felt a fear of Si Nian's gaze.","Now, seeing Si Nian's thoughtful scrutiny, she hurriedly lowered her head, picked up the chicken soup, and quickly left.","Si Nian turned her head and glanced at Liu Dongdong's hurried retreating figure.","Fu Qianqian, bored, offered her brother a few words of symbolic comfort and then went out to wander around.","She ended up getting lost. Just as she was about to ask someone for directions, she caught a whiff of a familiar, tantalizing aroma.","She was astonished, immediately following her nose toward the source of the smell.","And then she ran right into Si Nian, who was in the middle of cooking.","\"Holy crap? Si Nian?\" Fu Qianqian's expression was one of utter shock."]},{"number":323,"title":"Chapter 323: Looking down one's nose at others","paragraphs":["...","After being ignored by Si Nian, Fu Qianqian was immediately certain!","This was no hallucination!","This was definitely Si Nian!","Yes, absolutely!","Because only that little bitch Si Nian would ignore her so impolitely.","Fu Qianqian ground her teeth in anger, no longer caring about her shock. She stomped over, staring at her with wide eyes. Her first sentence wasn't asking why she was here, but rather: \"What are you making? It smells so good! Did you come to the Northwest to be a chef? Are you not a teacher anymore? You couldn't possibly be here to see my brother, right?\"","Si Nian rolled her eyes at her. \"Do you think that's possible?\"","Fu Qianqian said firmly, \"Definitely impossible.\"","If Si Nian were here to see her brother, his ego would have inflated to the heavens, and he would have already been confidently mocking Si Nian for pestering him again.","Si Nian didn't hide anything from Fu Qianqian and told her about Zhou Yueshen.","Since Fu Yang was saved by Zhou Yueshen, he definitely knew Zhou Yueshen's identity.","It was only a matter of time before outsiders knew as well.","After hearing this, Fu Qianqian looked shocked: \"When I saw your man, I thought his physique was better than my older brother's. I didn't expect him to be in this line of work too! So, are you making this for him? Speaking of which, I just rushed over here and haven't even had time to eat yet. Sigh, life away from home is not easy.\"","Si Nian found it amusing. When she saw her coming over just now, she still had a toothpick in her mouth, looking exactly like she had just finished a meal. It was just that she was so shocked that the toothpick fell out, and it was still lying on the ground now.","She only came to cook after the medical staff had finished, so as not to occupy their kitchen.","Fu Qianqian had probably eaten less than half an hour ago.","However, she didn't expose her and said, \"Didn't I just see Liu Dongdong come to the kitchen to cook? Did she not make portions for you guys?\"","Upon hearing this name, Fu Qianqian couldn't help but curl her lip and say, \"I find her an eyesore just looking at her. She acts so wronged every single day. My mom is soft-hearted, so when she sees her acting pitiful, she feels embarrassed to refuse. She's always coming to our place to deliver soup, but the soup she makes tastes terrible. Yours is still the best. Only someone like my brother, who isn't a picky eater, could swallow it down.\"","After saying that, she realized something and hurriedly covered her mouth, carefully checking Si Nian's expression.","Liu Dongdong's soup was so awful, yet her brother drank it, but he wouldn't drink Si Nian's. Wouldn't Si Nian be infuriated if she knew?","Oh dear, her big mouth.","Si Nian, however, looked entirely indifferent, as if she didn't care at all, and said, \"It seems Liu Dongdong is highly regarded by Fu Yang. Zhang Cuimei has already been kicked out, but she's still here.\"","Si Nian was actually a little worried. Now that Lin Sisi was in trouble and had gone to prison, it gave Liu Dongdong the opportunity to steal her man.","Originally in the novel, even when the two were together, they were almost broken up, let alone now.","It wasn't that she was worried about Fu Yang; a man like that deserved to suffer a bit.","But if Liu Dongdong really managed to rise to power, Fu Qianqian would probably die of frustration.","Hearing this, Fu Qianqian looked surprised: \"Your adoptive mother? I didn't hear her mention that. I was wondering why I hadn't seen her.\"","Si Nian paused. \"Liu Dongdong didn't ask you guys to help let Zhang Cuimei in?\"","Fu Qianqian shook her head blankly.","Si Nian fell into deep thought.","She could roughly guess the situation.","She said to her seriously, \"Qianqian, although whether your brother lives or dies is none of my business, you and Aunt Fu are still decent people. I have to warn you: be careful of Liu Dongdong.\"","Fu Qianqian froze: \"Why?\"","Si Nian turned her head back to continue cooking and said, \"Why do you think a woman would travel thousands of miles to take care of a man? Is it really just because Zhang Cuimei asked her to come?\"","Fu Qianqian immediately slapped her forehead. \"I knew there was something weird about this Liu Dongdong! Now that you mention it, I realize she's acting just like you used to.\"","Si Nian's face darkened, and she no longer wanted to talk to her.","After Fu Qianqian spoke, her face scrunched up in a frown, clearly very dissatisfied with Liu Dongdong.","After waiting for a long while, she suddenly blurted out, \"Wait, what do you mean my mom and I are decent people? Is that how you describe us?\"","Si Nian was speechless. It took her this long to finally react.","Her reflex arc was far too long.","\"Forget it, since you warned me to be careful of Liu Dongdong, I won't stoop to your level. Let's go eat first.\"","Although she didn't like Lin Sisi, Liu Dongdong wasn't much better.","She really hated such pretentious and artificial people; she always felt their minds were full of petty schemes.","Not to mention, even though Lin Sisi had gone to prison, the two of them had already filed their marriage report. This meant that Liu Dongdong was making these moves while fully aware that her brother was married, which was simply disgusting.","She had also heard that Liu Dongdong was Lin Sisi's good friend.","Tsk tsk, this bunch really was one weirder than the next.","Si Nian was worried about Da Huang. Although she had asked someone to help feed him, Da Huang was a fierce dog after all, and she still wanted to hurry back.","Fortunately, Zhou Yueshen recovered quickly. In just a few days, his external wounds had basically healed.","It was just that he still needed to use crutches for his leg.","But for a man like him, that wasn't a problem.","They were unfamiliar with this place and worried about causing any trouble, so they wanted to leave as soon as possible.","Zhou Yueshen's discharge procedures from the military had also been completed.","Now, he would never have to come back again.","She had originally worried that she would encounter Yang Yujie making things difficult for her upon coming here, but ever since Yang Yujie visited on the first day, she had never come back, probably afraid of people gossiping.","Until they were discharged from the hospital.","Whenever Fu Qianqian had free time, she would run over to chat with her, laughing heartily, completely ignoring whether her own brother lived or died.","However, hearing that they were about to be discharged and pack up to leave, she felt very reluctant to part with them, because her brother was severely injured and couldn't leave yet.","Si Nian simply reminded her to be careful of Liu Dongdong, if she didn't want Liu Dongdong to become her sister-in-law.","Fu Qianqian's face immediately darkened, vowing that she would rather her brother stay single for the rest of his life than be with Liu Dongdong.","With Liu Dongdong being watched so closely, she naturally didn't dare to make any moves.","Even when she brought things to the door, Fu Qianqian intercepted them and refused to let her in.","Fu Qianqian brought food to her brother. Looking at his handsome face, she suggested, \"Brother, why don't you disfigure your face?\"","Fu Yang looked at her as if she were being utterly ridiculous.","What kind of sister asks her brother to disfigure himself?","However, these past few days, it wasn't just Liu Dongdong; many nurses also kept taking advantage of changing his dressings and nursing him to get handsy with him.","He was also getting a bit annoyed.","He couldn't help but think of Zhou Yueshen again.","Zhou Yueshen had a resounding reputation in the military district, but ever since Si Nian arrived, basically no one went to bother him.","Si Nian's presence alone was enough to make those people feel ashamed of their own inferiority and not dare to approach him anymore.","All the unwanted romantic attention had come to him instead.","Hearing his sister's words, he actually hesitated for a rare moment."]},{"number":324,"title":"Chapter 324: Dahuang Is Sick","paragraphs":["\"If nothing else works, you might as well eat something good,\" Fu Qianqian said, seeing his twisted expression and realizing she had gone too far.","Whether it was Lin Sisi or Liu Dongdong, each one was more bizarre than the last.","She really didn't know what kind of taste her brother had.","While others attracted admirers, he only seemed to attract the crazy and unhinged.","Maybe it was because Si Nian had been too good to him in the past and he hadn't respected her, so now he was getting his retribution.","How did the saying go? A pitiful person must have their hateful aspects.","Although she pitied her brother, she had to admit that he had once been even more cruel to Si Nian.","Fu Yang's expression turned even uglier.","The family compound was huge, housing a school, a preschool, and more.","The buildings were mostly three or four stories high.","Since Zhou Yueshen was alone, the apartment assigned to him wasn't large. It had one bedroom, a living room, and a cooking area inside.","The house was quite old. Having been unoccupied for a while, it smelled of dust.","Zhou Yueshen hadn't brought much with him when he arrived.","Si Nian hadn't brought much either, and with Yu Dong helping them, they barely had to carry anything.","The residents of the family compound originally wanted to treat Zhou Yueshen to a meal when they heard he was discharged from the hospital.","Although they had grown distant after not seeing each other for so many years, he had saved them after all, and they couldn't just do nothing to show their gratitude.","Who knew they would instead learn the news of Zhou Yueshen's retirement from the army.","Everyone was dumbfounded.","Zhou Yueshen had made such a great contribution, and with the chief's high regard for him, if he stayed, he might have become a brigade commander just like Wang Jianguo.","His future could be described as bright and promising.","Yet, at such a crucial moment, he unexpectedly retired.","Furthermore, it was rumored that the chief had intended for either him or Wang Jianguo to be his successor.","No one could understand it.","They even asked Si Nian to persuade him not to be impulsive.","Si Nian expressed that she respected Zhou Yueshen's decision. She could actually guess some of his reasons; staying might have its benefits, but it wouldn't necessarily be a good thing.","Besides, he still had a pig farm. If he didn't go back, the pig farm would go bankrupt.","Others might think they were being too impulsive and that it wasn't worth it.","But in Si Nian's eyes, they no longer needed such fame and fortune.","Seeing that they wouldn't listen, everyone found it hard to say anything more.","After all, they weren't very familiar with each other.","Moreover, looking at Si Nian's temperament and attire, anyone could tell she wasn't someone who lived a hard life.","Perhaps her family was wealthy, and they simply didn't need to risk their lives for fame and wealth.","On the one hand, they envied Zhou Yueshen. They had heard he came from a rural background, yet he had found such a young and elegant wife.","He had truly reached the pinnacle of life.","Zhou Yueshen interacted with few people, and he didn't tell anyone about his departure. He only went to visit Wang Jianguo, who was still in the hospital.","After having Yu Dong buy train tickets for the next day, the group packed their luggage and left the Northwest.","It was two days later when they arrived in Yunguichuan City.","Before they even entered the house, Si Nian realized that their Da Huang was missing.","The whole family's expressions changed.","They anxiously contacted Grandma Jiang, only to learn that Da Huang had fallen ill. Worried that something bad might happen, she had searched for a long time before finding a veterinary station and sending him there.","The family didn't even have time to rest and hurried over.","Grandma Jiang said with a face full of guilt, \"After you left, Da Huang stopped eating and drinking. The next day, his leg went lame. I was scared to death and hurried to take him to the animal hospital, but whenever strangers approached him, he became extremely aggressive, and no one dared to touch him.\"","\"The doctor said there's no hope. Da Huang has lost his will to live. You... you need to be mentally prepared...\"","After Grandma Jiang finished speaking, tears of guilt fell from her eyes.","She also liked Da Huang. If something happened to Da Huang, she would never find peace for the rest of her life.","Hearing this, Si Nian's face turned pale, and her heart leaped into her throat.","Da Huang wasn't an ordinary dog; he was a Tibetan Mastiff, and a fully grown one at that.","Even if someone in the city could treat dogs, there was nothing they could do for a large, fierce breed like a Tibetan Mastiff.","Zhou Yueshen also furrowed his brows tightly. Da Huang had never been sick since they brought him home.","This was the first time, and it was unexpectedly this serious.","The children's eyes instantly turned red upon hearing the news.","\"Mom, is Da Huang really going to die?\"","\"Waaah, Da Huang, please don't die~\"","Grandma Jiang didn't know what to say and could only lead the group of three over.","From a distance, the family saw Da Huang locked in an iron cage. He was lying there listlessly, as if he had lost all his vitality, looking like he was on his last breath.","They couldn't even tell if he was still breathing.","They hurriedly ran over, but before they could get close, Da Huang in the cage seemed to sense something. He suddenly opened his eyes wide, scrambled to his feet, and looked in their direction.","Then, under the group's astonished gazes, his tail started wagging. He paced frantically back and forth in the cage, letting out whines toward them.","Just a moment ago, they thought he was gone, but the next second, he resurrected on the spot.","This completely startled the old doctor nearby.","He had just issued a notice of death, and the very next second, the dog came back to life?","The family quickly ran over. Da Huang let out eager whines and sniffed all over them.","It was as if the terminally ill dog from a moment ago hadn't been him at all.","When the doctor learned they were Da Huang's owners, he seemed to understand what had happened.","He explained that Da Huang thought they had gone on a long trip without him and had abandoned him. Unable to cope, he developed various negative emotions, which led to his loss of the will to live.","The word \"depression\" wasn't commonly used yet, but Si Nian guessed that was probably what it was.","She felt deeply guilty toward Da Huang.","At the time, she had thought they wouldn't be gone for long, so she overlooked how heavily their departure would impact Da Huang.","This oversight had led to today's situation.","Filled with remorse, she wiped her tears of guilt and apologized to him.","However, Da Huang didn't seem angry at all. As long as they were back, he forgave them without hesitation.","The world of dogs was just that pure and kind.","As long as you turn around, they will always be there.","The family took the dog back home. To make it up to Da Huang, Si Nian had the factory deliver a large piece of bone and stewed a big pot for him.","Da Huang regained his original, vibrant self.","It seemed a new family had moved into the house next door; Si Nian noticed the lights were on at night.","But she didn't think much of it.","Once back, she was busy getting ready for her classes.","After all, having taken such a long leave of absence, she felt a sense of shame if she didn't proactively return to work.","The two children also returned to school for their classes.","Zhou Yueshen stayed home to recover from his injuries, keeping Da Huang company and soothing his wounded little heart.","However, the incident where Eldest Child took first place, as well as the abduction case involving Second Child, had spread during the time they were away.","It was unknown who had dug up the fact that the two were brothers.","The two children were targeted by reporters.","As soon as Si Nian returned to the school, she heard from the vice director that reporters wanted to interview the two children.","Si Nian naturally disagreed. The two children were still young, and she didn't want their peaceful lives to be disrupted.","The vice director—no, the vice director who had already been promoted to director—expressed his refusal, also not wishing for the two children to be disturbed.","But Si Nian never expected that these reporters would find their way to her home.","And drop a bombshell on her.","\"Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan aren't your biological children, are they? Someone approached us, claiming to be their true blood relatives.\""]},{"number":325,"title":"Chapter 325: The Mystery of Origins (A Four-Thousand-Word Chapter)","paragraphs":["Si Nian hadn't fully recovered her senses, but she subconsciously started searching her memory for information about the relatives of the Eldest Child and the Second Child.","In the novel, their mother had passed away shortly after giving birth to Yao Yao, and their father had gone missing.","Therefore, everyone subconsciously treated them as orphans.","In this era, it was extremely difficult to find someone. Since the children's father couldn't be found, the three children could only be taken care of by their relatives.","Eventually, they ended up in Zhou Yueshen's hands.","Later on, although Zhou Yueshen made a lot of money, he kept a low profile, and very few people knew the true extent of his wealth.","The Second Child and Yao Yao died early, so there was no further plotline for them.","Although the Eldest Child became a scientific researcher, he was also low-key, and eventually, something happened to him too. The so-called blood relatives never appeared from beginning to end.","But now, they had suddenly popped up.","There were only two possibilities: either it was a scammer, or someone saw the two children becoming famous in the newspaper and changed their mind.","But no matter what, Si Nian didn't have a good impression of this person.","What kind of good person could a man be if he abandoned his three flesh-and-blood children and left without ever checking on them?","She had been too careless before. The two children were so young; she shouldn't have put them in the public eye.","She had underestimated the speed at which newspapers spread information in this era.","She looked at the reporter and said, \"That's right, the children are not our biological kids. They are orphans who were abandoned. My husband is their uncle. Because the three children were abandoned and couldn't survive on their own, he took them in. Now, the children's household registration is under our name.\"","The other party was about to speak but was interrupted by Si Nian. \"As far as I know, the children's mother passed away in her early years, and before her death, she was abandoned by her husband. Other than that, they have no other relatives. If they do, it's only that scumbag father who abandoned his wife and children. But I believe that a man with even a shred of conscience wouldn't have the face to come knocking on our door to claim them.\"","Si Nian continued, \"A legitimate newspaper agency like yours certainly wouldn't help such an immoral man claim his children, right?\"","The reporter's mouth was full of questions, but they were choked back into his throat.","If they helped the other party now, wouldn't they be aiding an evildoer? Wouldn't that be immoral?","The reporter's mouth twitched.","Si Nian ignored them and went inside the house.","Zhou Yueshen happened to be walking out. He seemed to have heard the noise outside. Looking at the reporters lingering at the door, he frowned slightly. \"Reporters?\"","Si Nian was surprised. \"How did you know?\"","Zhou Yueshen narrowed his eyes. \"There have been people wandering around nearby these past few days, all unfamiliar faces.\"","Zhou Yueshen hadn't been here for long, but he was already familiar with the environment.","He could tell at a glance who he had seen before and whose behavior was suspicious.","Since they were so obviously watching his house, he naturally noticed.","He had Yu Dong investigate in the morning, and the news came back that they were reporters.","They said it was because the Second Child's kidnapping incident had caused such a big stir, which attracted these people.","Si Nian's expression grew more serious.","She hadn't even noticed.","They might have even been secretly photographed.","Being secretly photographed in the 1980s was truly a rare occurrence.","But this wasn't a pleasant surprise.","To be able to mobilize reporters to do this, the identity of the Eldest Child's father must not be simple.","A scammer probably couldn't pull this off.","She pushed Zhou Yueshen inside, and the two went up to the study on the third floor. Looking down from there, they could see the reporters outside who still hadn't left. She told him about the situation.","Si Nian lowered the curtains, feeling a bit curious. \"Do you know who your sister's husband is?\"","Zhou Yueshen stood to the side, his gaze fixed in the direction downstairs. Hearing this, he raised his eyes to look at her.","A few seconds later.","He lowered his eyes and then placed his crutch aside.","He crouched down, picked up her untied shoelaces, and tied them.","At the sudden action, Si Nian was stunned for a moment.","She reflexively looked down. From above, she could see the top of the man's head, his sturdy shoulders, and his gloomy complexion.","Her heart skipped a beat.","She suddenly realized that the situation regarding Zhou Yueshen's eldest sister, who had never been mentioned, seemed not to be that simple.","Zhou Yueshen stood up. He actually didn't need to use a crutch much anymore, except that going upstairs was a bit troublesome.","His voice was deep as he said, \"This matter is a bit complicated.\"","Si Nian listened quietly as he continued, \"My sister never got married.\"","Si Nian was shocked. \"Never got married?\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded slightly. \"It was many years ago. I was away from home all year round, so I wasn't very clear about the situation at home.\"","\"The other party was an educated youth sent down to the countryside. In those years, investigations were strict, and many people from prominent families, or even those slightly connected, were sent to farms and cowsheds.\"","\"That man was one of them.\"","Zhou Yueshen slowly recounted the story.","At that time, only Zhou Tingting and his sister Zhou Lan were at home.","Zhou Lan took a liking to an educated youth from the neighboring village. He was handsome and educated. Because too much time had passed, many people only remembered his name was Zhiyuan, but his surname was completely unknown.","The two got together not long after, and the following year, she gave birth to Zhou Zedong.","But unfortunately, the man's family soon used their connections to return to the city.","After that, the two spent less time together and more time apart. After Zhou Lan got pregnant with Yao Yao, the man disappeared and never went back.","Abandoned, Zhou Lan vented her resentment towards the man on the slightly older Eldest Child.","This caused the Eldest Child to be withdrawn and sensitive from a young age.","Not long after, Zhou Lan passed away.","When Zhou Yueshen returned and learned of this, he found someone to investigate.","Only then did he find out that the man had actually used someone else's name.","Furthermore, the two had never married; they only claimed so to the public.","He even learned from some people who had gone down to the countryside together that this man seemed to have a wife and children. In other words, Zhou Lan had been a mistress, bore him three children, and was ultimately abandoned.","Zhou Yueshen wanted to find him, but even with his connections, searching for someone with a fake name who had been gone for so long was like looking for a needle in a haystack.","Zhou Yueshen simply treated him as if he were dead.","He never expected that someone would suddenly pop up, claiming to be the blood relative of the children. It was truly laughable.","After hearing this, Si Nian sighed endlessly.","No wonder she had never heard anyone mention Zhou Lan since coming to the Zhou family.","She had originally thought it was out of respect for the dead that no one brought up the past.","She hadn't expected the truth to be like this.","However, this further confirmed that the man was definitely not a good person.","\"For him to be able to hide his identity so easily without being discovered, he probably has a solid background,\" Si Nian said.","Zhou Yueshen raised his eyes and looked at her. \"You're worried he might be able to take the children back.\"","Si Nian said, \"Yes. The Eldest Child has excellent academic grades. Although the Second Child doesn't stand out in that aspect, he was also in the newspaper and became a little hero. The other party is actively getting reporters to bother us right now but isn't showing his face. I'm afraid he has ideas about the two children, but he probably doesn't want us to know who he really is yet.\"","\"To have this kind of ability, he must certainly not be simple.\"","Zhou Yueshen picked up the crutch placed to the side and said, \"Don't worry. Without my agreement, no one can take them away.\"","\"Be careful recently.\"","He spoke seriously.","Si Nian could see his earnestness and also became serious.","Meanwhile, the newly moved-in neighbors next door had also returned.","Fang Hui held her son's hand as they walked home. They had only recently moved in and were still missing a lot of household items. Since she didn't know how to cook, they had been buying all their meals outside.","Seeing reporters staking out near the entrance, she frowned with faint dissatisfaction. \"It's just a competition. Do these reporters really need to make such a big fuss?\"","Beside her stood a boy around seven years old. He was dressed in a little tailored suit and a hat, looking every bit the refined young master of a wealthy family.","Facing these reporters, Fang Hui felt nothing but disdain.","Having moved in a few days ago, she had noticed the reporters right away. Back in Jing City, she used to run into people like them all the time.","After all, her son was a genius. He had won a youth math competition at the age of five, and by seven, he had skipped grades to enter the fourth grade, earning the title of the youngest prodigy.","He had been quite famous back in Jing City and had even appeared on television.","They had moved here because of a minor incident. When she first spotted the reporters, she assumed they were staking out her son.","To her surprise, when she confidently approached them, she discovered they were actually waiting for the family next door.","Fang Hui hadn't expected their target to be anyone other than her son. She felt a surge of frustration and embarrassment.","After asking around the neighborhood, she learned that the family next door was surnamed Zhou. The husband ran a pig farm, the wife was a foreign language teacher, and they had three children—two boys and a girl.","The eldest child had participated in some math competition, won first place, and even made it into the newspaper.","The second child had helped the police catch human traffickers after being abducted, and received a reward as well.","In short, they were quite a high-profile family.","But to Fang Hui, who hailed from Jing City, this was nothing to brag about.","Countless children won awards in Jing City. The fact that something like this could make the news only proved how small and provincial this place was.","She scoffed at it with disdain.","Yet, they had been staking out for so long. Just a moment ago, when she and her son walked right past them, the reporters remained completely oblivious to her son—a true genius. This differential treatment left Fang Hui feeling a bit unsettled.","At this moment, the Eldest Child and the Second Child also returned.","Jiang Jiu was trailing along beside them.","Jiang Jiu was biting into a stick of cotton candy, while the other two boys were carrying a pile of scrap wood in their arms.","The Second Child had mentioned that food cooked over a wood fire tasted better. On their way back, they happened to pass by the tube-shaped apartment building and spotted some discarded wood left out by another family, so they gathered it and brought it home.","Both little guys were covered in dirt.","Hearing the noise, Fang Hui turned her head and swept a glance over them.","Seeing the grubby children, she instinctively pulled her son closer, creating some distance between them.","Once the boys walked past, she looked down at her son and said, \"Bowen, do you see that? If you don't listen to Mommy and study hard, you'll end up just like them, scavenging for trash.\"","Fang Bowen was only seven, yet his eyes already carried a hint of arrogance. He frowned as he cast a glance at the Second Child and the others.","Initially, he had been quite happy to see kids his own age.","Having been here for a while, the only other children around were the grandson of the Jiang family next door and the kids from the tube-shaped apartments.","His mother wouldn't let him play with the kids from the tube-shaped apartments, claiming it would lower his status.","Instead, she told him to go play with the Jiang family's grandson.","But when he tried talking to Jiang Jiu, the boy seemed foolish and slow. He didn't know his multiplication tables or basic arithmetic. He didn't seem smart at all.","He didn't like playing with dummies.","Seeing a few kids his age now, he hadn't expected them to be so filthy, let alone picking up garbage.","His brow furrowed tightly at the sight.","After saying her piece, Fang Hui ignored the three boys who had turned to look at her in confusion. Holding her head high, she led her son through their front gate.","However, just as she stepped inside, she heard a commotion from next door.","\"Mom, Mom! Xiao Jiang and I brought back so much firewood. Can we make wood-fired chicken now?\"","She instinctively looked over, only to see the grubby kids from earlier standing in the courtyard next door, hollering excitedly.","Fang Hui stared in disbelief.","She had genuinely thought those boys were just street urchins scavenging for trash.","After all, this place was poor and underdeveloped.","Poor kids scavenging for garbage were everywhere.","She never expected them to be the children from the family next door.","Living in a house like that, how could they be so unhygienic?","Fang Hui recalled the gossip she had heard from the neighbors. Apparently, even though the husband ran a farm, he was originally from the countryside.","No wonder the children were raised like this.","Did kids like these really warrant reporters staking out their house?","What a fuss over nothing.","After resting for two days, Zhou Yueshen headed to the breeding farm.","When he wasn't too busy, he would bring Da Huang along. The farm was spacious, allowing Da Huang to run around freely without the worry of knocking into anyone.","Basking in its owner's affection, Da Huang's coat had even grown a few shades shinier.","Whenever the little piglets went into hiding, it would track them down and herd them back.","It was a great help to everyone.","Finishing his cigarette, Zhou Yueshen stood by the side of the road. His features were strikingly handsome as he stood against the wind, calling out to the bounding Da Huang.","Da Huang immediately trotted back, its tongue lolling out happily.","When Zhou Yueshen was busy, it wasn't allowed to run off.","Just then, Yu Dong walked over and reported, \"Boss, I looked into it. They're from the Youth Newspaper. But I asked around, and it wasn't anyone from the city who contacted them.\"","Zhou Yueshen's hand, which had been patting Da Huang's head, paused. He ground out his cigarette butt beneath his boot before speaking. \"Not from within the city?\"","He had guessed that the other party had some influence, but he hadn't expected them to be from outside the city.","Someone from the outside was interfering?","\"Right. The guy refused to talk, so I had someone rough him up a bit. That squeezed out a little useful information. Although we still don't know exactly who it is, rumor has it they're from over there.\"","Yu Dong's eyes flickered as he alluded to a place he was reluctant to name.","Jing City?","Zhou Yueshen lowered his gaze in deep thought.","No wonder he had scoured the entire city years ago and couldn't find a single trace of the three children's father.","He was actually from Jing City.","But if he was from over there, how did he find out about the children?","Could it be that he had been keeping tabs on them all along...?","Seeing him fall silent, Yu Dong instinctively glanced up. Zhou Yueshen's expression was icy, his eyes dark and chilling.","Yu Dong shuddered, genuinely startled.","\"Old Xiao is over there. Have him look into it,\" Zhou Yueshen said.","Yu Dong's expression turned solemn. To mobilize Old Xiao meant the boss was playing for keeps.","It made sense. Years ago, that man had ruined Sister Zhou's life and abandoned the three children.","Now that the kids were finally living a good life, he had the audacity to come knocking so brazenly.","Anyone would be furious.","Suddenly recalling something, Yu Dong added, \"By the way, the deal for the adjacent land has been finalized. Isn't our pig farm big enough? Why are we buying more land? Are you planning to expand?\"","Zhou Yueshen withdrew his gaze and replied thoughtfully, \"It was Niannian's suggestion, but it's a good one. I do plan to expand.\"","His business operations were still far too small...","After Si Nian chased off the reporters with her sarcastic remarks, they hadn't shown their faces again.","However, while out grocery shopping that day, she ran into the new neighbors who had just moved in next door.","Several women from the tube-shaped apartments had surrounded her, chatting eagerly.","Their faces were full of fawning flattery.","They clearly hadn't noticed Si Nian, as they continued gossiping, \"What's so impressive about that? Compared to your Bowen, it's nothing! Entering the fourth grade at just seven years old—he's an absolute prodigy!\""]},{"number":326,"title":"Chapter 326: My Sister is Amazing (A 4000-Word Chapter)","paragraphs":["\"Yeah, that kid is from the countryside. To be honest, I think his grades are inflated. After all, his stepmother is a teacher, so cheating wouldn't be too hard for him, right?\"","\"Exactly! A country bumpkin squeezing his way into a foreign language elementary school, while our kids only get to attend a regular one.\"","Si Nian noticed that one of the women speaking was the middle-aged lady who had previously come to their door to borrow their Da Huang.","She hadn't lent the dog at the time, which offended the woman.","However, she had heard from Grandma Jiang that this was just how the woman was—always looking to take petty advantages. She had tried to curry favor with Grandma Jiang before, but after being ignored, she stopped going over.","Later, seeing that Si Nian's family had moved in, she wanted to try her luck with them, only to be rebuffed.","Now that another new family had moved in—one willing to give her the time of day—she was naturally eager to cling to them.","It was also Si Nian's first time getting a clear look at the new neighbor and her child.","The child looked to be about six or seven years old, quite young. He wore a little suit and small leather shoes. He was a handsome boy, but there was an arrogant look in his eyes, making it obvious at a glance that he wasn't easy to get along with.","The woman wore red high heels, an elegant white blouse tucked into a leather skirt, and a coat draped over her shoulders. Her hair was slightly curled, and she wore exquisite makeup.","She was slightly older than Si Nian, dressed maturely, and looked extremely fashionable.","The haughtiness in her eyes perfectly mirrored her child's.","Si Nian didn't care if others gossiped about her, but hearing them belittle Eldest Child's hard work to such an extent was something she naturally could not tolerate.","\"That's right, my son might not compare to someone else's who is in the fourth grade at the age of seven. But it's still better than being ten years old and still in the first grade.\"","\"We may be from the countryside, but it's truly pathetic that some people's sons can't even compare to a country boy.\"","\"No wonder he can only attend a regular elementary school. After all, with poor parental genes, you can't really blame the child. Auntie Wang, instead of looking down on others, you'd be better off improving your own child first. How can someone who can't even beat us have the nerve to criticize others? Where do you get the audacity? So shameless.\"","Although Si Nian didn't interact much with these people, she had lived here for a while and often bumped into them when walking by.","She would smile and greet those with a good attitude.","Everyone minded their own business without offending each other.","The only bad apple was this Auntie Wang.","Although Auntie Wang didn't like the Zhou family and had no fond feelings toward them, she usually didn't dare offend them either.","Since the Si family was close to the Jiang family, she would normally just gossip behind their backs to satisfy her itching tongue.","But when Fang Hui happened to ask, she simply couldn't hold back her complaints.","Little did she expect Si Nian to overhear her. Being caught red-handed, her face instantly flushed red with extreme embarrassment.","Fang Hui sized Si Nian up, a flash of astonishment at her beauty crossing her eyes.","The Zhou family hadn't been back for long.","Even though they lived close by, this was their first time meeting face-to-face.","Logically speaking, as a newcomer, she should have taken the initiative to visit and say hello to build good relations with the neighbors.","She had already visited the Jiang family.","But she had yet to visit the Zhous.","The incident with the reporter's interview had made her feel somewhat uncomfortable.","Perhaps because they both had children of a similar age, she couldn't help but subconsciously compare them.","Her own son was so outstanding, yet his thunder had been stolen by someone else, which inexplicably left her with a poor impression of them.","Instead, it stirred up a sense of competitiveness within her.","Now, seeing that Si Nian was actually younger and prettier than herself, she pursed her lips.","After a brief pause, she stepped forward and initiated a greeting, \"Hello, my name is Fang Hui. I'm your new neighbor. I hope we can look out for each other from now on.\"","Si Nian did not reach out to shake her hand. She didn't consider herself magnanimous enough to befriend someone who had just been discussing her son's supposed flaws with others.","She replied indifferently, \"There's no need for that. Excuse me, I'm very busy.\"","Fang Hui's smile stiffened. Her outstretched hand froze in midair, caught in the awkward dilemma of whether to withdraw it or not.","Si Nian ignored her reaction. She simply gave a curt nod as a greeting and bypassed the group to leave.","The women standing nearby hurriedly comforted Fang Hui, \"That woman is just like that. Relying on the fact that her family made money from a pig farm and that she's a teacher, she acts all high and mighty. Comrade Fang, please don't take it to heart.\"","Fang Hui smiled. \"It's alright. Perhaps what we said earlier upset her. Thank you for making introductions for me, I'm sorry to have dragged you into this.\"","The group immediately felt that she was the epitome of kindness and grace.","Si Nian had been here for so long but rarely ever spoke to them.","She always put on an aloof and unreachable front; those who didn't know better would think she was some wealthy heiress.","In contrast, Fang Hui—who came from Beijing, exuded an air of nobility, and even worked at a newspaper agency—was so approachable.","Their favorable impression of Fang Hui skyrocketed instantly.","As soon as Second Child and Jiang Jiu returned home, they took their little sister out to play.","Because their mother didn't allow them to wander too far, they could only stroll around the neighborhood.","Naturally worried, Zhou Zedong grabbed a book and followed them outside.","Today, Si Nian had received a definitive reply from the school. To participate in the college entrance examination, she had to achieve a passing score in the mock exam next Wednesday.","High schools all had score requirements, as no one wanted to drag down their school's average. Naturally, they wouldn't accept someone with poor academic performance.","The high school the original owner of her body had attended was the best in the city, commonly known as City First High School.","However, they refused to accept her, so Si Nian settled for the next best options and reached out to the second and third-ranked schools.","Ultimately, she received a notification from the second-ranked school.","With limited time, she had bought quite a few books to study.","When the older children weren't home, she would hold Yaoyao and read with her.","Even though the little girl could sit still, it looked rather pitiful for her to be cooped up.","So today, she let Eldest Child and Second Child take her out to play.","This also gave her the perfect opportunity to focus on doing some practice questions in peace.","Jiang Jiu and Second Child held Yaoyao's hands, one on the left and one on the right, saying they were going to take her to play at the tube-shaped apartment building.","There were still many kids at the tube-shaped apartment building who liked to play with them. He had previously boasted to others about how pretty his little sister was, and today he was deliberately bringing her over to show her off.","He even specifically put her cutest little hair clip on her.","Yaoyao had grown quite a bit taller and was already walking very steadily.","The little munchkin's hair had grown longer and was very silky. It was tied into a tiny bun at the back with a pink bow clipped to her head. Beneath her straight bangs were a pair of big, grape-like eyes. Although her face looked round, she had a distinct chin—her mother called it an oval face.","She had just gotten a little chubby, making it less obvious, but Second Child loved his plump little sister; she was soft and incredibly comfortable to hug.","He had prepared some marbles, planning to teach his sister how to play with them.","However, upon arriving, they found that their spot had been taken by Da Zhuang and his gang again.","They wanted to find other children to play with, only to realize that those kids were ignoring them.","Instead, they were all gathered around a richly dressed child who was about the same age as him.","Zhou Zehan still remembered him; he was the son of their new neighbor.","Da Zhuang mocked him, \"Oh, isn't this Zhou Zehan? Are you here to show off those few broken English words of yours again? Let me tell you, we have Bowen now. He knows multiple languages and is a genius. My mom said he is already in the fourth grade at seven years old, so stop embarrassing yourself here.\"","Da Zhuang's mother had told him that Fang Bowen's family came from a big city and was very wealthy, instructing him to make sure he built a good relationship with him.","Da Zhuang had now become Fang Bowen's lackey.","\"You know English?\" Fang Bowen stepped forward, confronting Zhou Zehan, who was slightly taller than him.","Didn't his mother say they were from the countryside? He heard that primary schools in the countryside didn't even teach English yet, unlike in the city.","He had been here for quite some time, and among the children he knew, hardly any could speak English.","This made Fang Bowen extremely disappointed.","Even the kids in Class Four, the best fourth-grade class he had joined, weren't that impressive.","And they called it an elite class.","Those people were so much older, yet so stupid.","He didn't like interacting with people older than him.","At this moment, hearing Da Zhuang say that Zhou Zehan knew English, he immediately stepped forward.","\"Are you that good? Then let me test you. If you can answer correctly, I'll give the playground to you guys.\"","Fang Bowen spoke up, and without waiting for them to refuse, he blurted out a sentence in fluent English: \"Do you know which country English originated from?\"","Zhou Zedong closed the book in his hands and looked up at him.","He had just returned to school and heard that a major event had happened while they were away.","A seven-year-old little genius had transferred to their school from the distant Jing City.","He heard that the other party had started participating in math competitions at the age of four, a true genius.","As soon as he arrived, he snatched the position of English representative from Li Youcai.","Although he hadn't paid much attention, he could guess at this moment that it was probably the child standing before him, who was about the same age as his younger brother.","He had only heard such fluent English from his mother.","Zhou Zehan: \"Uh... um... uh...\"","Jiang Jiu: \"Uh... um... uh...\"","After all, the two of them weren't cut out for studying. Although they had learned from Si Nian for a long time, they only knew some basic vocabulary. In addition, the other party's intonation was different from what the teacher taught and very fast, leaving them momentarily dumbfounded.","The smile on Fang Bowen's lips widened. \"I thought you were really good, but it turns out you're just so-so. I learned such simple English when I was four.\"","Da Zhuang and the others immediately took the lead in laughing out loud.","Zhou Zehan's little face turned red.","\"Brother is so dumb!\" Yaoyao pinched Zhou Zehan's thigh and said, \"The birthplace of English is of course the UK.\"","Although she was still young, she could understand that her brother was being mocked by others.","But what she understood even less was why her brother couldn't answer such a simple question when he studied with their mother every day.","So strange.","As soon as these words came out, Fang Bowen, who had just pulled a smug smile, froze. He swiftly shifted his gaze to the little chubby girl in the middle.","He wasn't surprised that she answered the question.","Rather, he was shocked that she understood what he had asked.","But this child looked no more than three years old.","When he learned English, he was already four.","And it was taught step-by-step from a young age by a foreign professor his mother had hired.","Not to mention him, even Zhou Zedong, Zhou Yuehan, and the rest of their group all snapped their heads to look at their sister.","She was staring at them with a distressed look on her face.","Zhou Zedong's eyes flickered. He naturally knew the question the other party had asked.","He also knew that his idiot brother definitely couldn't answer it.","But he never expected that his sister would be able to answer it.","At this moment, he rarely revealed a bit of astonishment.","Zhou Zehan, on the other hand, didn't think there was anything strange about it. He slapped his forehead and said, \"Is that what it meant? Bro, is that what it meant?\"","Zhou Zedong didn't want to pay attention to him. He continued to stare at his sister, deep in thought.","Da Zhuang and the others couldn't understand it at all. To them, it was just gibberish, but it sounded pretty cool. At this moment, they didn't take Yaoyao seriously either, laughing and saying, \"Even your brother doesn't understand, what the heck do you know, right Bowen?\"","Fang Bowen's little face had tensed up at some point, his eyes staring straight at Yaoyao. \"How did you understand what I meant?\"","Yaoyao tilted her head in confusion, her round little face incredibly cute. \"I just understood it.\"","Mom wrote these every day and also listened to the radio. Her brothers were learning too, and when Mom took her to school, she also learned.","So she naturally understood it.","Fang Bowen didn't quite believe it and said, \"Then let me ask you again: What is your name? How old are you this year? Who did you learn English from?\"","Yaoyao bobbed her head and said, \"My name is Yaoyao, and I am three years old this year. My mother taught me how to do it. My mother is really amazing, and my brother is clumsy, which is embarrassing for my mother.\"","As soon as this milky toddler accent came out, everyone was dumbfounded.","The entire courtyard of the tube-shaped apartment building fell into a dead silence.","Even Zhou Zehan's eyes widened in disbelief.","His sister could actually speak English, and even say such a long paragraph.","Good heavens, since when was his sister so amazing?","How come he didn't know?","In his memory, his sister had only just learned to speak not long ago.","She didn't even know that many words.","Fang Bowen gasped.","It was one thing to be able to introduce herself, but she could actually say so many words that weren't even taught in primary school.","Da Zhuang and his group were also stunned.","Wait, was English this simple?","It was one thing for the seven-year-old Fang Bowen to know it.","How could even the three-year-old sister of that show-off Zhou Zehan know it too?","And she sounded really impressive.","\"Sister Yaoyao, you... you're so amazing...\" Jiang Jiu, who had been shocked speechless, finally found his voice and stared at Yaoyao with admiration.","Yaoyao shyly scratched her little pigtails.","\"Not amazing. Eldest brother is more amazing, second brother is not amazing.\"","Zhou Zehan: \"......\"","Fang Bowen's expression was ugly.","He originally thought that since they were the same age, he could come and mock Zhou Zehan.","He didn't expect that instead of mocking him, he would be slapped in the face by his three-year-old sister.","He felt very uncomfortable right now.","Was their mother very amazing?","But why couldn't that eight-year-old Zhou Zehan understand?","Yet his sister could understand.","Although Zhou Zehan was despised by his sister, he wasn't sad at all.","Seeing that the other party couldn't speak, his nose was pointing up to the sky right now.","When he went home, he was practically floating as he walked.","Zhou Yueshen had just led Da Huang to the door when he saw his son smiling radiantly.","He stopped and waited for them to approach.","\"Did you go out to play?\" He let go of Da Huang's iron chain and picked up his daughter.","Second Child nodded heavily, his eyes bright as he said, \"Dad, my sister is so amazing, she can speak English.\""]},{"number":327,"title":"Chapter 327: Yaoyao Is Not a Little Fool","paragraphs":["Zhou Yueshen's eyes and brows softened as he looked at his daughter. \"Yaoyao can speak English?\"","Yaoyao wrapped her small arms around her father's neck and nodded, saying, \"Yes, Mommy taught me.\"","Zhou Yueshen didn't overthink it. After all, Si Nian did frequently teach the children English. Although Yaoyao was still young, he had heard that early childhood was the period when learning ability was at its strongest.","In such an environment, it wasn't strange that Yaoyao could speak a little.","He patted his daughter's head with his large hand and praised her gently, \"Yaoyao is so smart.\"","Yaoyao blushed at her father's praise.","Suddenly, so many people were praising her. Was she really that smart?","But back when she was in Xingfu Village, others used to call her a little mute and a little fool.","Yaoyao couldn't speak back then, but she could still feel their malice.","She also knew that idiot was a bad word.","But things were different now. Everyone praised her for being awesome!","Daddy also said she was smart.","She wasn't an idiot at all.","Zhou Yueshen held his daughter in one arm, took the Second Child by the hand, and went inside the house.","He asked, \"Where is Mommy?\"","He had come back relatively early today.","Usually, he didn't return until it was dark, and if it was too late, he would just rest at the pig farm.","He had recently negotiated a piece of land, and expanding the site also required a lot of time.","Zhou Yueshen was quite busy.","It was almost like going back to his schedule in Xingfu Village.","The Second Child said, \"Mommy has an exam to prepare for, so she told us to go out and play.\"","Only then did Zhou Yueshen remember that Si Nian was taking the college entrance examination.","In the blink of an eye, it had already been over four months since they moved here.","The college entrance examination was on July 7th.","It was already April, so there wasn't much time left.","Si Nian not only had to busy herself with preparing lessons but also had to study.","She had to take care of the three children at home and cook every day.","Truth be told, she was the one working the hardest in the family.","Zhou Yueshen frowned slightly, his thick eyebrows knitting together, and stopped Xiao Han, who was just about to run upstairs to call his mother.","He made a shushing sound and said, \"Don't go disturb Mommy.\"","Zhou Zehan immediately stopped in his tracks.","He had originally wanted to go tell Mommy that Daddy was back.","But since Daddy told him not to disturb her, he didn't dare to go.","After saying that, Zhou Yueshen placed his daughter on the sofa to watch TV by herself, rolled up his sleeves, and went into the kitchen.","The kitchen was spotlessly clean, the countertops were neat, and there were many boxes of seasonings arranged perfectly.","There was a window in the kitchen that used to have an old wire mesh screen.","Si Nian had mentioned that it wasn't well-ventilated, so Zhou Yueshen had replaced it with a casement window.","It was open right now. Because they were on the first floor and the kitchen tended to be damp, the window was left open every day, except when it rained.","From this angle, one could see the front gate, making it easy to notice if anyone came by.","With the breeze blowing in from outside, the kitchen was perfectly dry and completely free of any strange odors.","Si Nian lived a refined lifestyle; she had even hung a white lace sheer curtain on the kitchen window.","Even the apron was custom-made, adorned with little pink flowers.","Zhou Yueshen put on the apron, which was clearly several sizes too small for him, washed the rice, and set it to cook. Then, he dug out some fresh vegetables from the refrigerator.","He didn't know how to cook many dishes, just some ordinary ones.","He couldn't compare to Si Nian.","But it was still edible.","It was just that the meat he sliced was as thick as a person's pinky finger.","He cut it with alternating layers of fat and lean meat, uniform in size and with clear textures.","The meat was bacon that had been smoked previously.","Si Nian loved eating it too.","Zhou Yueshen washed some green chilies, along with garlic and ginger.","He sauteed them until fragrant before adding the pork.","In no time, the bacon was stir-fried until it was crystal clear.","Back when he was in the Northwest, he and his brothers loved eating it this way.","He also stir-fried a plate of shredded potatoes, made scrambled eggs with tomatoes, and prepared a bowl of sour soup.","A simple dinner was ready.","In a jar to the side, there were pickled radishes made by Si Nian.","Sour, spicy, crisp, and fragrant, pairing them with the sour soup was the whole family's favorite.","It was just a bit spicy, so the children couldn't eat much of it.","As a result, a single batch made by Si Nian would last a long time.","After finishing cooking, Zhou Yueshen broke out in a hot sweat.","He took off his tank top to wipe the sweat from his forehead and stopped his son, who was eager to eat and about to run upstairs to call Mommy.","In a deep voice, he said, \"Go sit down. Daddy will go.\"","The Second Child really wanted to go, but he couldn't beat his dad to it.","He had no choice but to go to the kitchen to serve himself some rice.","Zhou Yueshen went upstairs and washed his face before heading toward the study.","The study was on the third floor.","Before Si Nian had even finished going through her practice questions, she smelled the aroma of meat and thought it was the neighbors cooking.","Seeing that it was getting late, she figured it was about time to cook, so she closed her book and stretched lazily.","She gazed out the window for a moment, pondering what to have for dinner tonight.","Just then, a large hand rested on her shoulder.","Si Nian paused slightly and turned her head to look.","With his large palm pressing gently on her shoulder, Zhou Yueshen looked down at her. \"Are you done? Let's eat.\"","Si Nian kept her head turned, meeting his dark eyes.","She was somewhat surprised. \"You're back so early today?\"","And you even cooked?","Zhou Yueshen didn't cook often. It wasn't that he didn't want to, but rather that the children didn't like his cooking.","They said his food wasn't as delicious as Mommy's.","After feeling rebuffed a few times, Zhou Yueshen switched to helping her instead.","When he was at home, he always acted as her assistant.","He hummed in affirmation.","\"I finished work early today, so I came back earlier.\"","Si Nian noticed he was bare-chested, the heat radiating off his body toward her.","Fortunately, the older man showered every day, so there was no foul smell of sweat.","It was just that the scars on his chest seemed more prominent, new ones and old ones, the most conspicuous being a ferocious gunshot wound right in the middle of his chest.","When he moved, his firm chest muscles would always bulge.","They felt rock-hard to the touch, just like stone.","He would never take his shirt off outside.","After all, the scars looked terrifying.","But at home, there was no need to worry; everyone was used to it.","The Second Child admired his dad very much.","He even said that the scars on his dad's chest were a warrior's medals, and that he wanted to have some of his own in the future.","It left Si Nian not knowing whether to laugh or cry.","Si Nian withdrew her gaze and put her books away.","Since the wind tended to pick up at night, she conveniently closed the study window as well.","Otherwise, leaving it open for two days would result in a layer of dust.","Zhou Yueshen took her hand; it was a bit cold.","From holding a pen for too long, her muscles were a bit stiff.","He pressed down gently, and the sudden soreness made Si Nian cry out, \"Ah! That hurts!\"","Zhou Yueshen was amused by her startled reaction and chuckled, \"Your muscles have been tense for too long. If I don't massage them, they'll hurt tomorrow.\"","Si Nian did feel that her hand had been quite sore these past few days.","She held chalk to write all through her classes, and after class, she still had to prepare lessons.","When she got home, she had to do practice questions.","However, she didn't think much of it. After all, back in the day, in order to get into a prestigious university, she had stayed up late every night reading and studying. There were times when she wrote until her tenosynovitis flared up, and read until she was dizzy and her vision blurred.","She wasn't a character in a novel; she didn't possess such astonishing talent.","Like the vast majority of ordinary people, she had to give it her all just to get into a top university.","In this era, a degree from a prestigious university carried even more weight than in the future. As long as she managed to get into one, doing whatever she wanted in the future would be easy.","Even though Zhou Yueshen made a lot of money, and Si Nian really wanted to just slack off.","But no one could say for sure what the future held.","Therefore, if she was going to take the exam, she was going to aim for the best.","But every era had its brilliant minds.","Even though she had already gone to college once before, too much time had passed, and she had forgotten a lot of things."]},{"number":328,"title":"Chapter 328: Am I Very Stupid","paragraphs":["This era was different from the future, so naturally she couldn't take things lightly.","She simply relaxed and said, \"Then press a bit more.\"","Zhou Yueshen had large hands, and her frame was delicate; it felt as if his rough, big hands could snap her bones with just a gentle squeeze.","He lightened his force, using his thumbs to press down on the tense areas of her arms.","Before long, a large patch of Si Nian's arm had turned red.","After the pain faded, an unexpected, satisfying soreness took over.","Her arms felt significantly more relaxed.","Si Nian was very satisfied with her older husband's service. If it weren't for her son calling them down to eat, she would have wanted a full-body massage.","Zhou Yueshen kneaded her small hands and asked, \"Are they still sore?\"","Si Nian replied, \"A bit better.\"","She moved her neck around and said, \"My neck is even more sore. You have to rub it for me again tonight.\"","Zhou Yueshen said okay.","He held her hand and led her downstairs.","The three little ones were already sitting obediently at the dining table, waiting for dinner.","Si Nian rubbed their little heads apologetically, \"Mommy was so busy today that I forgot the time. You guys must be hungry.\"","\"Mommy, I'm not hungry. I was waiting to eat with Mommy,\" the Second Child said immediately.","Yaoyao sat on the stool, her short little legs dangling and swinging happily. Holding a small spoon, she said, \"Mama, I want to eat meat.\"","Si Nian's gaze fell on the three dishes and one soup on the table.","The dishes looked pretty good.","It was just that the meat was sliced so thickly that it looked rather intimidating.","Although she quite liked eating cured meat, she only liked the thinly sliced kind, which was mostly lean.","Her older husband really was something. How could anyone eat slices this thick?","Fortunately, the three children had experienced hunger before, so they all loved eating meat.","They didn't find it too greasy even though it was so fatty.","Si Nian picked out a slightly leaner piece for her daughter.","Only then did she sit down.","Just as she picked up her bowl, Zhou Yueshen placed a piece of meat into it with his chopsticks, saying, \"You've been tired lately. Eat more to nourish yourself.\"","He remembered that Si Nian loved cured meat, so he had stir-fried a large plate of it today.","Si Nian: \".......\"","\"I appreciate the gesture, but you can take the meat back.\"","She turned around and transferred it back into her older husband's bowl.","Zhou Yueshen thought she disliked his cooking and said, \"I made it according to the method you used before. The taste shouldn't be bad.\"","Si Nian: \"I don't mean that. It's just that this meat is too fatty.\"","The Second Child, biting into a piece of fatty meat, took a moment to say, \"It's not fatty, it's yummy~\"","Si Nian rolled her eyes at him.","Seeing his father's distressed face, Zhou Zedong reminded him, \"Mommy only likes eating the lean parts.\"","Si Nian was immediately touched: \"Our Xiaodong understands Mommy the best.\"","Zhou Yueshen froze.","Because in this era, he rarely saw anyone who didn't like eating fatty meat.","People in rural areas loved fatty meat; when they bought meat, they always chose the fattiest cuts.","Not only could it be rendered into lard, but they also loved eating the crispy pork cracklings.","The men would stuff it into their mouths chopstick by chopstick.","The children loved it too, so Si Nian often cooked it.","But in comparison, Si Nian always cut it into smaller pieces.","Just now, he was wondering if he had cut it too thickly.","Now, his son's words suddenly woke him up to reality.","Zhou Yueshen ate the fat and placed the lean meat into her bowl.","Si Nian looked at him in amusement.","But she didn't mind and started eating.","Come to think of it, she was like this when she was a child too. She didn't like eating fatty meat.","Her father would also eat the fat and give her the lean pieces.","Perhaps people from this era all liked to do this.","After dinner, the children went to wash up.","Zhou Yuehan remembered again how his younger sister was more amazing than he was.","He tugged at Si Nian and asked, \"Mommy, did you secretly teach sister English?\"","Si Nian yawned. She had been planning to go upstairs to find her older husband for a massage, but her son's interruption made her swallow half her yawn. She asked in confusion, \"Hmm? Secretly teach your sister to speak English?\"","The Second Child pouted his lips so high that you could hang a bottle on them.","He was actually very happy and proud to see his sister being so amazing.","But after the pride faded, he felt a bit sad inside.","It was one thing for his older brother to be better than him, but how could even his little sister be better than him?","Right after dinner, he wanted to find his sister to teach her how to play marbles.","But his sister didn't want to learn, saying it wasn't fun.","She insisted on following their older brother.","Their older brother was there looking at math problems. What was so interesting about that?","He would fall asleep just looking at them.","Watching his older brother and younger sister getting along so affectionately, Xiaohan suddenly felt very lonely.","Not the loneliness of being invincible.","But the loneliness of being incompetent.","He suddenly felt that his brother and sister were not from the same world as him.","He gestured with his hands and said, \"Sister can speak thaaat much English, but I can't. I can only say words and sing English songs.\"","\"Big brother is also good at studying and gets certificates.\"","After finishing, he lowered his head dejectedly and asked Si Nian, \"Mommy, am I very stupid?\"","Si Nian turned to face him, bent down slightly, and placed her hands on the little guy's slumped shoulders.","Although she was still a bit confused about Yaoyao speaking English.","But seeing that the Second Child seemed to have taken quite a hit.","He hadn't been this sad when his older brother was being so amazing.","She immediately comforted him, \"Of course Xiaohan is not an idiot.\"","She said, \"Everyone is different. Some people are good at Chinese, some are good at math. Although our Xiaohan isn't good at Chinese or math, Xiaohan is good at sports!\"","\"Even though your brother is good at studying, he can't outrun you, right?\"","\"All roads lead to Rome. If the path of studying doesn't work out, we won't force it. Choosing the path that suits you best is the most important thing, isn't it?\"","The Second Child looked at her, seemingly understanding but also not quite grasping it.","But he felt in his mother's eyes that the gap between him and his siblings wasn't as huge as everyone made it out to be.","In his mother's eyes, he seemed just as amazing as his brother and sister.","The Second Child's mood instantly lifted, \"Mommy, Mommy, I'm also very amazing, right?\"","Si Nian nodded: \"Of course you are.\"","Which other family's child could run five thousand meters without panting?","The little guy was a natural-born athlete and didn't even know it.","It's just that people with well-developed limbs are usually simple-minded.","It was understandable that his academic performance wasn't good.","Si Nian wouldn't force him or put too much pressure on him either.","As someone who had been forced to study before, she knew that kind of pain deeply.","Naturally, she wouldn't project that onto her child.","Xiaohan was instantly happy and wasn't sleepy at all despite it being late at night. If it weren't so late, he would have loved to go out and run a few laps to prove his strength.","Si Nian then heard about what happened during the day from Zhou Zedong.","She looked at Yaoyao, who was being held in his arms.","Yaoyao sat in her brother's arms, staring intently at the math problem in his hands.","Her eyes were sparkling bright.","She remembered that she used to hold the child whenever she read books before.","Yaoyao would also stare at them, but Si Nian just assumed she was bored and didn't think much of it.","But now, a certain thought sprouted in her mind.","She had heard of a type of child who appeared slow and developed later than normal children.","But in reality, they were hidden geniuses.","Geniuses often had some sort of physical or behavioral quirk, like an eccentric personality or being unable to speak.","Yaoyao started speaking very late, which was originally thought to be a developmental issue.","But looking at it now, perhaps that wasn't the case.","So Si Nian pointed at the content in the book and asked Yaoyao, \"Baby, do you know what this is?\"","Yaoyao raised her little head, looked at Si Nian, and said, \"I know, Mama. This is a function.\"","Popularity voting for the three Zhou siblings is now open—please click the heart below to vote."]},{"number":329,"title":"Chapter 329: Dad Is the Big Bad Guy","paragraphs":["Si Nian was quite surprised.","She had only asked casually, not actually expecting the little girl to understand.","But to her surprise, Yaoyao actually answered it.","English was one thing. After all, she was a teacher, taking her to school every day and often playing cassette tapes. It wasn't strange for a child to pick up a few words after hearing them so much.","But she had never mentioned math. Where did the little dumpling learn that?","Si Nian asked the question exactly as she thought it.","Sitting in her older brother's lap, Yaoyao bit her finger and said, \"Brother taught Yaoyao. It's very simple. Given the parabola y=-(1/2)X2+(5-√m2)...\"","She bobbed her head side to side as she pointed at the formula in the book and read it aloud.","Si Nian felt a tingle of shock run down her spine as she listened.","She proceeded to point at several other problems in the book that Zhou Zedong had been studying and quizzed Yaoyao. Without exception, the little girl understood every single one.","Si Nian had thought Zhou Zedong was the smartest genius she had ever met. In her era, geniuses only appeared on TV or in books; she had never met one in real life.","But now, she had two right by her side.","And they were just children.","The shock it gave her was nothing short of massive.","Zhou Zedong was also startled by his sister. Sometimes, when she sat next to him while he did his exercises, she would get bored, lean over to watch, or ask him what something was.","He thought she was just curious, so he casually taught her how to read a few words.","Little did he know that while she hadn't learned many words, she had memorized the formulas.","And she actually understood them?","Zhou Zedong wasn't like his younger brother, who could be easily fooled.","From his sister's sudden display today, he realized that she might possess a brain even smarter than his own.","Si Nian returned to her room.","Wearing a grave expression.","Zhou Yueshen had just come out of the shower, a towel draped over his shoulders.","Seeing Si Nian frowning, he strode over. \"What's wrong?\"","Si Nian told him about Yaoyao.","Zhou Yueshen wasn't surprised. Instead, he said, \"Xiaodong used to be like this too.\"","Although Xiaodong had started his education relatively late, he seemed to love reading since he was very little.","His family originally had some books left behind by his father, but his mother had burned them all.","He had secretly hidden a few away. Zhou Yueshen had seen them; they were all filled with formulas and physics knowledge.","Stuff that you basically wouldn't learn until college.","Zhou Zedong was obsessed with them and would often hold them up to read.","By the time Zhou Yueshen took him in, the boy had already finished reading those books.","According to him, he had gotten his hands on those books when he was three or four years old.","They belonged to his father.","At the time, Zhou Yueshen was entirely focused on investigating information about the boy's heartless father and didn't pay much attention to it.","He only assumed the child still held onto some lingering attachment to his father.","Only later did he discover that the boy actually understood them.","He didn't know if reading those books was the reason, but when Zhou Zedong started school, he was much smarter than ordinary children. He could solve problems on his own without the teacher having to explain them.","Zhou Yueshen realized this child was extraordinary.","He also guessed that the man must have been an intellectual.","And one who had attended college at that.","In that era, the prestige of attending college went without saying.","Having seen Zhou Zedong's talent, it wasn't so strange that Yaoyao, constantly immersed in an environment where the whole family was studying, would pick up these things.","Zhou Yueshen was a man who had seen the world.","Si Nian had initially been a bit worried, fearing she might not guide the children properly.","But hearing Zhou Yueshen's calm response, her heart suddenly settled.","She felt she had been making a fuss over nothing.","This was a world within a book, after all. It would be stranger if everything were exactly like reality.","In the novel, Yaoyao hadn't spoken even when she started school; she had always been silent and withdrawn.","Even if she had a gift, no one would have been able to notice it.","Without the right person to guide them, it was indeed very easy for these children to go astray.","Obviously, these three siblings were a prime example.","Si Nian relaxed and asked Zhou Yueshen to boil some hot water for her, saying she wanted to take a bath.","Her wooden bathtub had been moved over, and the master bedroom had its own en-suite bathroom.","Si Nian's wooden tub was placed inside. Whenever she had free time, she would take a bath to dispel the cold from her body.","She was a bit tired today and wanted to relax.","They didn't have a water heater installed at home, so they still had to boil their own water for baths.","There was often hot water boiling in the pot.","Just enough for the whole family to wash up at night.","Zhou Yueshen fetched the hot water for her, tested the temperature, and told her to go bathe.","Si Nian dug out a new four-piece bedding set and asked the man to change the sheets.","She said that since the weather was getting hotter, they needed to change them frequently; otherwise, sweat would easily breed bacteria.","She had always loved cleanliness, which Zhou Yueshen completely understood.","Watching her enter the bathroom to soak in the tub, he opened the bedding set and began to change the sheets.","He then carried the used bedding downstairs, scrubbed it clean, and hung it out to dry before heading back upstairs.","He thought about how, with so many children in the house, they had to change and wash the bedding and clothes every few days.","Although the kids could wash their own clothes, whenever he wasn't home, Si Nian's responsibilities would multiply.","Zhou Yueshen remembered passing by Granny Jiang's house next door and seeing the washing machine sitting by her door.","Although he had never used one, he knew it worked just by plugging it in.","You just put the clothes in, take them out, and hang them to dry.","It was incredibly easy.","Granny Jiang's family was wealthy and had everything, so the old couple didn't hire anyone to take care of them; they did everything themselves.","These home appliances saved them a lot of time.","He pondered getting one tomorrow so Si Nian would have a much easier time.","Smoothing out the wrinkles on the bedsheets, Zhou Yueshen stood up to close the window.","But he noticed that the window of the family who had newly moved in next door was still open.","It looked like a study. From his angle, he could see a child sitting at a desk, studying.","Zhou Yueshen was slightly surprised. City kids really were different, studying so late into the night.","Speaking of which, he had also heard from Si Nian earlier that Xiaodong had been studying late every night to prepare for his math competition.","He suddenly understood why city kids had such excellent grades, far surpassing rural children.","Now it seemed it wasn't without reason.","Zhou Yueshen closed the window and lit a mosquito coil.","Si Nian had bought the mosquito coils; she was a magnet for mosquitoes.","Back in the countryside, she was constantly getting bitten.","Her fair skin was always dotted with red marks.","Later, she went to the department store in the city and bought this type of mosquito coil. A box cost several yuan, but the scent wasn't cheap or pungent at all. After using it for a while, the room would carry a faint, pleasant fragrance.","Since using it, Si Nian hadn't been bitten again.","Just as he lit it, Si Nian walked out, drying her hair with a towel.","Zhou Yueshen subconsciously turned his head.","He saw her wearing the silk nightgown he had bought for her previously.","It featured delicate cutouts and a low-cut neckline with spaghetti straps, paired with a thin silk robe draped loosely over her shoulders.","The emerald green color accentuated her fair complexion, and fresh out of the bath, her skin looked incredibly dewy and supple.","Although Si Nian was tall, she had a petite frame.","This was the reason she always maintained a soft, voluptuous allure, perfectly curvy and beautifully proportioned.","Her hair had grown much longer, almost reaching her waist. Because it was so thick, it always took a long time to dry with a towel.","Si Nian had bought herself a hairdryer, but she usually preferred letting it air dry naturally.","It was black and silky smooth.","She looked exactly like a breathtaking beauty emerging from the bath, which was the ultimate stimulation for a grown man in his prime.","Zhou Yueshen's Adam's apple bobbed slightly.","Now that the weather was warmer, Si Nian had switched to wearing flimsy nightgowns again.","In the past, Zhou Yueshen wouldn't have dared to steal a second glance.","But now, he had grown bolder.","He stared so intently that he only snapped back to reality when the lighter burned his hand, sending a sharp pain through his fingers.","Si Nian sat down at the vanity, towel-drying her hair.","Zhou Yueshen did not use skincare products or even face creams; the various bottles and jars on the table all belonged to her.","Face creams, hair serums, body lotions. She had it all.","After every shower, she would apply them from head to toe.","But today, Si Nian was feeling a bit exhausted, so she took out the hair dryer and handed it to Zhou Yueshen, asking him to dry her hair for her.","Zhou Yueshen had never used a hair dryer himself.","Si Nian had only bought it after going to the city.","It was an item only wealthy people could afford.","He took a few steps forward and stood behind Si Nian, his tall figure looking a bit stiff and awkward in that moment.","His large hands took the hair dryer, plugged it in, and studied the switch for a moment.","Only then did he begin drying her hair.","He kept the hair dryer at a safe distance, afraid the heat would burn her.","Meanwhile, Si Nian opened her jars and bottles, applying the lotions to her body.","She was not actually someone who obsessed over skincare. In her original world, she stayed up late year-round, leaving her complexion dull, sallow, and lifeless.","No skincare product ever helped.","It was not that she could not afford high-end brands.","But nothing ever worked on her.","But after coming to this era, she discovered that the skincare products here were incredibly cheap and came in large quantities.","Moreover, the results were exceptionally good.","She did not even apply them every day, just occasionally, yet the original owner's skin was so tender it felt as soft as water.","Seeing such great results naturally gave her the motivation to keep it up.","By now, she had developed a pretty good habit of it.","As she applied the products, the rich fragrance almost made Zhou Yueshen dizzy.","He had always thought Si Nian smelled wonderful.","But it had never been quite this overwhelming before.","Enduring the strong, sweet scent, he finished drying her hair.","Then, Si Nian applied essential oils to her locks.","Zhou Yueshen sat to the side, watching her. He could not help but think that being a woman was truly a lot of trouble.","From the time she started her shower to the moment she finished her routine, Si Nian had spent nearly two hours.","By now, the children were already sound asleep.","Seeing her ball her hands into fists to lightly tap her own shoulders, he stood up and placed his large hands on her shoulders. Didn't you say you were sore? Let me give you a massage.","Si Nian murmured an agreement. She was actually quite sleepy, but the thought of the soothing relief a massage would bring was too tempting to resist.","She lay face down on the bed, telling the man to be gentle.","Although it felt incredibly comfortable afterward, it had hurt quite a bit the last time he massaged her hands.","Zhou Yueshen agreed.","Not wanting to hurt her, he lightened his grip.","However, when the man pressed a particular knot in her neck, Si Nian still let out a sharp cry of pain.","Next door, Second Child, who had just fallen asleep from sheer excitement, was startled awake.","Thinking he had misheard, he quickly got up and pressed his ear against the wall.","Because this house was more soundproof than their home in the village, he could not hear very clearly.","But soon, he heard his mother's miserable cry again.","Second Child was terrified.","Without even bothering to put on his shoes, he hopped out of bed and dashed to his parents' bedroom door in just three seconds.","Through the door, he heard his mother say weakly, Zhou Yueshen, be gentle! That hurts so much!","Second Child's face immediately went pale, and he began to pound on the door.","Zhou Yueshen and Si Nian were both startled by the sudden noise.","The moment Zhou Yueshen opened the door, his son fiercely headbutted him. Dad is a bad guy! You are not allowed to bully Mom!","He kept trying to headbutt Zhou Yueshen while swinging his little fists at him.","Zhou Yueshen was stunned for a second before he felt a mix of exasperation and amusement.","Si Nian hurriedly sat up and saw Second Child charging at Zhou Yueshen, looking absolutely furious and ready to beat him up.","However, because Zhou Yueshen had easily lifted him by the collar, the boy's arms and legs were just flailing and kicking in mid-air.","His head was still jutting forward in a headbutting motion.","For a moment, she found it both hilarious and deeply touching.","She guessed that her voice must have been too loud just now, making Second Child mistakenly think that Zhou Yueshen was hitting her, which was why he had rushed over to her rescue.","She quickly said, Xiao Han, that is enough. Your dad was not hitting me.","Xiao Han refused to believe her. With red eyes, he glared at Zhou Yueshen. I do not believe you! I heard Mom crying out!","Mom even said it hurt!","Dad is a big bad guy!","I am going to protect Mom!","Si Nian did not know whether to laugh or cry. Alright, alright, it is really not what you think. Why would your dad ever lay a hand on me? Have you ever seen him hit me? He was just giving me a massage.","Xiao Han finally stopped kicking and thrashing. Still dangling in mid-air with his collar pulling at his neck, he stared at his father with lingering suspicion. Really?","He had heard people say before that his dad looked incredibly fierce.","They even said the reason he would not be able to find a wife was because he was abusive.","Even though Second Child had never been hit by his father, constantly hearing such gossip had planted a subconscious fear in him that his dad was someone not to be messed with.","His mother was such a delicate woman; there was no way she could win in a fight against his dad.","Even though his dad could probably send him flying with a single punch.","He was not afraid at all.","He had to protect his mom.","Zhou Yueshen lightly rapped his knuckles against his son's small head, then carried him back to his room and plopped him down.","Alright, go to sleep. Stop interrupting us.","No sooner had he spoken than Zhou Yuehan darted right back into Si Nian's room like a wisp of smoke. He stood next to her and declared, No, I want to sleep with Mom. I need to keep an eye on Dad.","Despite his bold words, his little face flushed red.","Wow, I am so smart, he thought to himself.","This way, Mom will let me sleep in her bed.","Plus, I get to protect her.","Mom had only ever let his little sister sleep with her; she had not let him do it yet.","He really wanted to sleep next to Mom too.","When his older brother woke up tomorrow, he would be so jealous!","Zhou Yuehan was already fantasizing about the look of sheer awe on his brother's face.","However, before he could revel in his triumph, Zhou Yueshen, his face dark with annoyance, tossed him right back out the door.","With a sharp click, the door shut firmly, shattering his dreams into pieces.","Si Nian looked helplessly at the unreasonably strict man. If Xiao Han wants to sleep here, just let him. It is no big deal.","Zhou Yueshen's face was still dark as he replied, He is already eight years old. We cannot coddle him.","Si Nian shook her head in resignation. Rolling her shoulders, she realized they actually felt much better.","She let out a yawn, pulled the covers up, and lay down. Alright, alright. Let us go to sleep early too. If the kids hear anything else, they are just going to misunderstand again.","It was a good thing her son was too young to understand. If an adult had heard the sounds she made earlier, their imagination would surely run wild.","Si Nian coughed lightly, feeling a wave of embarrassment.","Zhou Yueshen rubbed his fingers together, still feeling somewhat unsatisfied.","But knowing it was indeed getting late, he murmured his agreement in a low voice.","He pulled the light cord to turn it off, walked over to Si Nian's side of the bed, and lay down. He was not wearing anything; the man was accustomed to sleeping naked.","After being exposed to the cool air all evening, his muscles were chilly to the touch.","Si Nian turned her head to glance at him in the dark. She could not see clearly, but pressing against him felt quite comfortable, so she instinctively snuggled closer.","Zhou Yueshen usually rested his hand on her waist while they slept. When she rubbed against him, his hand subconsciously tightened, gripping her waist firmly.","Si Nian tilted her head up to look at him. Zhou Yueshen pulled her slightly upward, lowering his body and tilting his head to press his lips against her neck.","Her neck was a sensitive spot for Si Nian. She let out a soft moan and whispered, It is too late.","Zhou Yueshen sucked gently at her skin before replying, Good night."]},{"number":330,"title":"Chapter 330: Daily Life 02","paragraphs":["Early the next morning, Zhou Yueshen went out and bought a new washing machine.","Even though it was Sunday, he still had to go to the breeding farm later.","Being the boss meant working 365 days a year with no days off.","After a good night's sleep, Second Child had already forgotten about what happened the previous night.","Seeing a washing machine at their doorstep, he excitedly circled around it and asked Zhou Yueshen if it was indeed a washing machine.","He said he had seen one at Grandma Jiang's house.","He also mentioned that Little Jiang never had to wash clothes.","Zhou Yueshen picked him up and taught him how to use it. Second Child was intrigued and learned earnestly, declaring that since his older brother didn't know how to use it and only he did, he would take charge of washing all the family's dirty clothes from now on.","Zhou Yueshen patted his little head.","Other children usually hated doing chores, but his own son fought to do them.","This would actually lighten Si Nian's burden quite a bit.","Zhou Yueshen told him to help his mother more often.","Second Child boasted that he was the absolute most hardworking boy ever.","The weather was beautiful today, and the early morning sun already illuminated half the courtyard.","The vegetables they had planted earlier had all sprouted, looking lush and green under the sunlight.","Zhou Yueshen had built a small fence around the pond; after all, with many children around, it could be dangerous.","Inside were the little fish fry that Zhou Zehan was raising.","By now, they had grown plump and healthy, swimming happily in the water, quietly waiting for their little master to feed them.","Oh, and the rabbits they kept had given birth to a litter of bunnies, eight in a single litter.","Their previous hutch was no longer big enough.","Having raised them for so long, and since the two children had practically brought them up, no one could bear to eat them.","But having too many wasn't a good idea either.","Si Nian planned to take them to the market to sell.","Even though they were domestically raised now, they still carried wild rabbit genes.","They could fetch a good price.","Da Huang was lying on the side sleeping, while a group of half-grown bunnies nestled snugly on his belly, sleeping soundly.","They had clearly treated him as their own nest.","They were even closer to him than to their own parents.","Perhaps because he had watched them grow up with his own eyes, Da Huang was exceptionally tolerant of them.","The entire courtyard was brimming with vitality.","Zhou Yueshen put his son down to let him figure things out on his own, then had someone bring over some wooden boards and started hammering away in the yard.","Beside him lay Si Nian's design blueprint.","It was a wooden house she had designed for Da Huang.","The previous incident where Da Huang got depressed had made the whole family feel guilty towards him.","Si Nian also felt that she had neglected Da Huang way too much.","Right now, Da Huang was the darling of the family.","So, Si Nian decided to build him a wooden house.","However, she only knew how to draw the plans, not how to build it, so she handed the task over to Zhou Yueshen.","Following the drawing, Zhou Yueshen quickly built a framework.","Passersby who saw him hammering away to build a doghouse sighed in disbelief.","It was just a beast meant for guarding the door, yet he was building it a doghouse; it was truly too extravagant.","He probably didn't even treat his own parents this well.","They saw such a big house belonging to the Zhou family, yet only the couple lived there themselves.","They hadn't even brought their parents over to show some filial piety.","Instead, they valued a dog so much; it was truly incomprehensible.","Next door, Fang Hui was also leading her son out to attend his tutoring classes.","Even though they hadn't been here long, she had already enrolled her son in tutoring classes for every subject.","Even in this small city, she couldn't let him slack off.","Seeing the Zhou family's man working in the yard, and the little boy wearing slippers with his hair looking like a bird's nest, shouting and yelling happily in the courtyard, Fang Hui withdrew her gaze.","Just as she pulled her son to leave, she noticed he was staring inside too.","Fang Hui said, \"Bowen, do you see that? You must never be like that child, all sloppy and unkempt. That kind of child is the most annoying.\"","Fang Bowen withdrew his gaze and gave a soft \"Mm.\"","He said he understood.","Fang Hui pulled her son away.","Zhou Yueshen had finished the doghouse by the time Si Nian got up, yawning.","She brewed a cup of floral tea, and Second Child immediately ran over, saying, \"Mom, Mom, look at our newly bought washing machine!\"","\"It's the same brand as the one at Little Jiang's house.\"","\"Dad bought it.\"","\"From now on, Mom won't ever have to wash clothes again!\"","Surprised, Si Nian walked over and inspected the twin-tub washing machine, which was very fashionable for the current era but looked a bit old-fashioned in her eyes.","She was also very happy.","How could she not be happy about something that freed up her hands!","Zhou Yueshen was cleaning up the leftover wood scraps, while Da Huang wagged his tail and excitedly circled his new home.","He was obviously thrilled.","Si Nian felt that today was truly a good day; waking up, the house had gained quite a few nice things.","\"What made you think of buying a washing machine?\" She hadn't even thought of it herself.","Zhou Yueshen replied, \"The weather is getting hotter, and we need to wash clothes more frequently. With a washing machine, doing the laundry will be easier for you.\"","Si Nian agreed it made a lot of sense and nodded. Seeing that it was already eight o'clock, she asked, \"You don't have to go to work today?\"","Zhou Yueshen shook his head slightly. \"I do. I'm heading over right now.\"","Si Nian looked a bit disappointed. \"I was thinking that since it's Sunday today, I'd take Little Dong and Little Han to buy bicycles. If they had bicycles, it would be more convenient for them to go out.\"","She was thinking about how Eldest Child had to run around doing business every day, which was quite tiring.","Zhou Yueshen's expression shifted slightly. He patted Second Child, who was looking up at him, and said, \"I probably won't have time today. Some workers are coming over later, and I need to keep an eye on things.\"","Because he was expanding the site and the surrounding area was all wasteland, he had hired quite a few workers to go over there.","Si Nian felt it was a pity, but knowing he was busy with work, she didn't say much more.","After eating a simple breakfast, Zhou Yueshen drove off.","Si Nian hadn't gone out shopping in a long time, so she specially put on some makeup.","Since arriving in this era, she didn't have much time to put on makeup.","But women loved beauty, let alone when going out shopping.","She applied light makeup and changed into a dress.","When she walked downstairs in high heels, Jiang Jiu and Zhou Zehan, who were lying on the floor playing marbles, opened their mouths in an \"O\" shape.","\"Mom is so pretty!\"","\"Auntie is a fairy!\"","Si Nian felt overjoyed being flattered by the children.","She rubbed their heads and smiled, \"Let's go, Mom is taking you to buy bicycles.\"","She had her own bicycle, but it was too big for the two children to ride.","It wasn't impossible for Si Nian to ride alone with Yaoyao, but she couldn't just leave her two sons behind and make them walk by themselves.","So she walked to school with her two sons every day.","If she bought them bicycles now, the whole family could ride to school together.","Hearing that his eldest brother and Second Brother were going to buy bicycles, Jiang Jiu immediately dashed home to ask his grandmother for money, saying he wanted to buy a bicycle too.","His grandmother disagreed, saying he was still too young and riding a bicycle was too dangerous.","She would still drop him off at school herself.","Jiang Jiu felt wronged, complaining that Second Brother and his eldest brother both had one, but he didn't.","Grandma Jiang explained that Eldest Child and Second Child were different; they were brave, and they often rode their mother's bicycle, so they knew how to ride.","He had never even touched one, so it was too dangerous.","Jiang Jiu felt even sadder.","Feeling aggrieved, he ran back to his room.","Jiang Wenqing, who had just returned home, didn't see his son and noticed his mother looking distressed.","He asked for the reason.","Grandma Jiang told him about the matter.","She added, \"Besides, the Eldest Child and Second Child have their parents to teach them how to ride bicycles. They've been running around outside since they were little, so they are bold. Si Nian follows them around too. With my old bones, how could I possibly learn to ride a bicycle? I can't just run chasing after my grandson, can I?\"","Although her heart ached for her grandson, there was nothing she could do.","Ever since her grandson was abducted last time, she had been extra careful with everything.","Hearing this, Jiang Wenqing felt a pang of heartache and went upstairs to knock on his son's door.","After knocking for a long time, Jiang Jiu finally opened the door with red eyes.","Seeing his father, the boy instinctively tried to shut the door, but Jiang Wenqing stopped him.","Jiang Jiu pouted, glaring angrily at his heartless father.","His eyes were full of resistance.","He didn't like his dad at all. He liked Second Brother's dad. Second Brother's dad was amazing; he raised rabbits and fish for Second Brother and even built a new house for Da Huang.","Second Brother's mom would also buy him new clothes, bicycles, and toys.","But he had no dog, no rabbit, no fish, and not even a bicycle.","He was truly the most pitiful child in the world.","Jiang Jiu felt like his heart was broken.","Jiang Wenqing hurriedly said, \"Little Jiu, I heard your grandma say that you want to buy a bicycle?\"","Jiang Jiu replied, \"Why are you asking? You won't buy me one anyway.\"","After saying that, he angrily tried to close the door again.","Jiang Wenqing said, \"Who said I won't buy you one?\"","Jiang Jiu: \"Grandma said so.\"","Jiang Wenqing: \"What Grandma says doesn't count. Dad will buy it for you, okay?\"","Jiang Jiu froze, looking at him in disbelief. \"R-really?\"","Jiang Wenqing breathed a sigh of relief and immediately smiled. \"Of course it's true.\"","He added, \"Dad has been transferred back to the research institute in the city. From now on, I will come home every day. Dad knows how to ride a bicycle. I'll teach you how to ride it then, alright?\"","A flash of pleasant surprise crossed Jiang Jiu's eyes, but he quickly hid it. He wasn't that happy; it was just... just that this way, people wouldn't call him an orphan without a father or mother anymore.","He was still young after all. Even though he was acting awkward, he couldn't hide the joy in his eyes.","He hurriedly ran to find the Second Child and the others, asking them to wait for him.","\"Second Brother, my dad said he will buy me a bicycle too.\"","\"My dad said he won't leave anymore and will come home every day.\"","\"Second Brother, Second Brother, my dad will also teach me how to ride a bicycle from now on.\"","He said happily.","The Second Child was happy for him but also felt a little sad, saying, \"That's great! My dad is very busy every day and has to go to the pig farm, so only Mom can teach us how to ride.\"","Si Nian walked out and interrupted the two children. \"What are you talking about? Let's go.\"","Although Zhou Zedong was also happy, he didn't show his emotions as openly as his younger brother.","He held his younger sister's hand and followed beside Si Nian.","Zhou Zehan and Jiang Jiu held hands, skipping and bouncing ahead.","They were clearly very excited about buying bicycles.","Jiang Wenqing stood at the door. Seeing his son come out, he finally stepped forward to greet them.","Hearing that he was going to take Jiang Jiu to buy a bicycle, Si Nian nodded.","No wonder Little Jiang Jiu looked so happy.","The group went to the department store.","Children's bicycles were quite popular; after all, there were many wealthy people in the city.","Children from well-off families would start riding bicycles to school by themselves at a very young age.","As soon as the children arrived at the department store, they let themselves loose and started picking out bicycles.","This reminded Si Nian of the first time she brought them to the mall, when they were so timid that they didn't even dare to try on a piece of clothing.","The Little Han of today had undergone a heaven-and-earth transformation.","Soon, the two children pushed over a red and a blue bicycle.","The Second Child said happily, \"Mom, I want this red one. It's so cool.\"","Si Nian rubbed his head and said okay.","Jiang Jiu glanced at Second Brother, then looked at Si Nian rubbing his head.","A hint of envy flashed in his eyes.","Gripping the handlebars of the bicycle, he looked unconfidently at his bespectacled father, who had little presence beside him.","He couldn't bring himself to call out to him.","Jiang Wenqing didn't make things difficult for him and asked, \"Does Little Jiu like this one?\"","Jiang Jiu immediately nodded. \"I want this one. Second Brother said red and blue are the most handsome!\"","Jiang Wenqing smiled. \"Alright, Dad will buy it for you.\"","Zhou Zedong pushed over a slightly larger black bicycle.","He then took out the money he had made from selling pancakes recently and handed it to Si Nian, saying, \"Mom, I have a hundred yuan here.\"","The bicycle he had chosen happened to cost exactly a hundred yuan.","This way, Si Nian wouldn't have to pay out of her own pocket.","Si Nian accepted his money without the slightest sense of guilt, claiming it was to save up for his future wife.","Jiang Jiu and the Second Child, who had no money, exchanged a glance.","Eldest Brother wasn't playing fair.","After buying the bicycles, Jiang Wenqing had other matters to attend to and originally wanted to take his son home first.","But his son was unwilling, so he had to head back first by himself.","The department store would pack the bicycles and deliver them to their home, so there was nothing to worry about.","Si Nian immediately led the children up to the third floor.","Summer was coming, so of course, they needed to buy new clothes.","In no time, the children's hands were full of various shopping bags.","Jiang Jiu struggled to hoist the bags onto his shoulders, glancing at Eldest Brother and Second Brother, who didn't even change their expressions. He didn't dare to utter a word of complaint.","Si Nian wasn't just buying for herself; she bought for the children too.","With full outfits for everyone, the children ended up covered in bags.","Passersby kept staring at the children and snickering covertly.","They found it amusing and felt envious of Si Nian.","When they got home, the three children collapsed onto the sofa in exhaustion.","However, once the bicycles were delivered, it was as if they were pumped full of adrenaline.","Even Zhou Zedong, who was studying, put down his book. The three children excitedly started learning how to ride their bicycles in the courtyard.","Fang Hui brought her son home from his classes and saw the children riding bicycles in the courtyard.","They were branded ones, quite expensive.","One look and it was obvious they were newly bought.","Fang Bowen also looked over, a trace of envy flashing in his eyes.","He instinctively said, \"Mom, I also...\"","Fang Hui immediately cut in, \"Son, riding a bicycle is too dangerous. We won't copy them. I bought you a violin. You can start learning it as soon as we get back.\"","Fang Bowen shut his mouth.","The next day, Zhou Zehan put his little bunnies into his schoolbag and sneakily started a small business with Jiang Jiu.","Few of their classmates had ever seen rabbits, and even if they had, they were only the dirty ones at the wet market.","They were nothing like the ones Zhou Zehan raised, which were chubby, white, spotlessly clean, and incredibly cute.","The little girls were instantly won over. They surrounded Zhou Zehan, their faces flushed with excitement. \"Second Brother, can you give me one? I want one too.\"","\"Yes, Second Brother, I want one too. I'll take good care of it.\"","\"Second Brother's family is my family.\"","Zhou Zehan said, \"I raised these myself. I can't give them to you for free; you have to pay for them.\"","Eldest Brother had started his pancake business.","He could do business too.","Hmph, it just so happened that Mom said he had too many little rabbits and couldn't keep them all.","She even said they had to be sold.","Originally, Zhou Zehan was reluctant. He felt that the bunnies were so cute, and since he had raised them himself, it would be too pitiful to eat them.","He could only sell them to children who loved small animals just as much as he did.","Everyone asked him how much they cost.","Zhou Zehan said they were two yuan each.","His were wild rabbits, not just your ordinary rabbits.","Two yuan was too much for people in the countryside.","But for a place like this, which was almost equivalent to an aristocratic elementary school, it was nothing at all.","Even if they could come up with the money, Zhou Zehan still refused, saying he would only sell it to them if their entire families agreed.","The children said they would take it home to show their families. If their families agreed, the sale would go through, and if not, they would return it to him.","And so, the group of children carefully cradled the little rabbit all the way home and told their dumbfounded families,","\"Second Brother said this is no ordinary rabbit. This is the rabbit from Wang Wei's poems.\""]},{"number":331,"title":"Chapter 331: No. 2 Middle School (Revised)","paragraphs":["Soon, all nine of Second Child's little white rabbits were snatched up.","Not only did his classmates want them, but students from other classes also caught wind of it and rushed over to buy his wild rabbits.","Upon returning home, Second Child immediately handed the money over to Si Nian.","He proudly announced that all his little rabbits were sold out.","He also added that the next litter of little rabbits had already been pre-ordered by students from other classes.","In his notebook, he had even written down things like So-and-so from Class X pre-ordered one little rabbit.","Si Nian found it highly amusing.","This was fine, too. Rather than selling them at the farmer's market to be made into spicy diced rabbit, it was better to sell them to other children who also loved animals.","It would help foster the children's compassion.","She accepted the money, claiming it was to help him save up for a wife in the future.","Second Child was overjoyed, saying that he finally had as much money to marry a wife as his older brother did.","He declared that when he grew up, he would definitely marry a wife as beautiful as his mother.","Si Nian had an exam on Wednesday, so she took a day off.","After finishing her morning classes, she prepared to head home.","Just as she was about to return to the office to pack her things, she heard singing coming from inside.","It was a radio. Since she often needed it to teach English, the school had assigned her one, and she had bought quite a few cassette tapes for it.","However, it was obvious that what she was hearing right now wasn't from a tape, but rather sounded like a foreign radio station.","She had heard that the school's radios were all imported and of the highest specifications.","But she had never tuned into a foreign station before. It was too much trouble anyway; using tapes was much easier.","Si Nian initially thought another teacher was listening to it.","Yet, when she opened the office door and walked in, she saw that the sound was coming directly from her own desk.","Looking up, she saw Yaoyao standing in front of the desk, with only the top half of her little head visible over the edge.","Her two little pigtails stuck high up in the air, and one chubby little hand was pressing buttons on the radio, switching to another station after just a short while.","Si Nian was taken aback for a moment. Beside her, Wang Xiaoli saw her return and smiled, \"Teacher Si, are your classes over? Yaoyao has been very good today as usual. I didn't even have to look after her; she's just been playing with your radio all by herself all morning.\"","Then, sounding somewhat puzzled, she added, \"But how come your radio has so many functions? I saw your Yaoyao switching between so many stations, and she seems to really love listening to them. Teach me how to do it next time, so I can go back and set it up for my daughter to listen to tomorrow.\"","Si Nian opened her mouth, then closed it again.","Radios were such antiques. She had only encountered them back when she was in middle school, but as she grew up, they had gradually become obsolete.","It was only after coming to this era that she started learning how to use one.","Normally, she only used it to play tapes.","Even with the radio at home, she only knew how to tune into the local city stations.","She had absolutely no idea how to tune into foreign ones.","She coughed awkwardly and said, \"I'm not too sure either. Yaoyao probably just pressed the buttons randomly.\"","After saying that, she walked over, picked Yaoyao up, and turned off the radio.","Yaoyao had been humming along to the song on the radio, only to be interrupted.","Seeing it was Si Nian, she immediately hugged her neck happily. \"Mama, you're done with class!\"","Si Nian smiled and pinched her little cheek. \"Yes, I am. What has Yaoyao been up to?\"","Sitting in her arms, Yaoyao counted on her fingers. \"Yaoyao listened to lots of songs. They were Michael's songs, they sounded so good! Mama, do you know Michael?\"","After saying that, she moved her little feet to the beat. \"Boom, clap, boom, clap, boom, clap... Not my lover Billie Jean is not my lover...\"","Her milky little voice rang out rhythmically, instantly making Wang Xiaoli burst into laughter.","\"Teacher Si, your Yaoyao is just too cute!\"","Si Nian was once again shocked internally. Of course she had heard this song; it was Michael's classic hit.","The easygoing Wang Xiaoli simply assumed Si Nian had taught her and didn't think much of it.","After all, Yaoyao followed Si Nian to class every day, and sometimes even sat in on other teachers' classes, so it wasn't strange that she had picked up a few things.","Normally, she would often sit at Si Nian's desk, humming songs and drawing pictures.","So it seemed even less out of the ordinary.","Si Nian took a deep breath and asked Yaoyao, \"Then how did Yaoyao tune into the station?\"","Could it really have been random button pressing?","Yaoyao shook her head and said, \"No, Mama, I learned it from Teacher Wu.\"","There was a Teacher Wu in the office. She heard her brother say he was Dr. Turtle, who came from a foreign country.","He was also very nice to her and would give her candy to eat.","When Mama wasn't around, he would come over and talk to her.","That day, when Teacher Wang went to get her food, she saw Teacher Wu come back carrying a radio. Then he pressed a few buttons, and a sound completely different from the one on Mama's radio came out.","He could even switch between them easily, which was super fun.","So she learned how to do it, and to her surprise, she really managed to make a lot of foreigners' voices play.","It was so much fun.","As Yaoyao talked about this, her eyes brightened, as if she had discovered a whole new world.","However, afraid that Mama would be angry, she only secretly listened to it when Mama wasn't around.","She just hadn't expected Mama to come back so early today.","After hearing this, Si Nian breathed a slight sigh of relief. So it was Wu Ren'ai who had taught her.","That was fine then. Otherwise, if the child had figured out how to tune it all by herself, it would have been truly unimaginable.","Si Nian packed up her things and prepared to take her home.","Just as they stepped out of the office, they bumped into Wu Ren'ai, who had just finished his class.","Wu Ren'ai's face lit up with joy, and he hurriedly straightened his suit to greet her. \"Nian... ahem... Teacher Si, heading home?\"","Si Nian nodded, polite but distant. \"Yes, I have no classes this afternoon, so I'm heading back early.\"","Just as Wu Ren'ai was about to say something, he heard her add, \"Thank you for teaching my Yaoyao how to use the radio, so she wouldn't be so bored alone in the office.\"","Wu Ren'ai was a bit bewildered, question marks practically popping up over his head. \"Radio?\"","Si Nian nodded and said, \"Yes. If there's nothing else, I'll be going now.\"","Even after she had left, Wu Ren'ai still hadn't recovered his wits. When had he ever taught Yaoyao how to tune a radio?","As soon as he returned to the office, Wang Xiaoli immediately came over and said, \"Teacher Wu, could you... could you teach me how to tune into foreign radio stations? I can't figure this thing out. I see Yaoyao listening to it every day, and she's even learned quite a few songs. I was thinking of playing it for my daughter when I get home.\"","Wu Ren'ai was even more dumbfounded. \"Foreign radio stations?\"","\"Yes, I just heard little Yaoyao say that you were the one who taught her.\"","Wu Ren'ai finally snapped back to reality, but he truly had never taught Yaoyao how to tune a radio.","Because of the special requirements of his work, the radios they bought were not ordinary ones and could tune into foreign stations. Of course, he mainly used it for his own studies; it certainly wouldn't be needed for regular classes.","Having developed the habit of listening to the radio while abroad, he would also tune in when he was free after coming back.","Only now did he realize what they meant.","He had indeed played it in the office once before. At the time, seeing the little one, Yaoyao, standing at Si Nian's desk and staring at him eagerly, he thought the child was hungry. Feeling sorry for her, he even bought her some candy to eat.","So she wasn't staring at him because she was hungry, but because she was curious about the radio station he was listening to?","But he had only listened to it that one time. How did the child learn how to do it?","Wasn't she only three years old?","Wu Ren'ai's mind was filled with giant question marks.","Si Nian also brought the radio back into the house.","She figured it was a good thing that her child loved listening to it.","Of course, she was also curious about how exactly Yaoyao had tuned it.","The radio they had at home was an old-fashioned model and didn't have these features.","She had to admit, American products were indeed a bit more advanced.","Once inside, she asked Yaoyao to give her a demonstration.","Sure enough, Yaoyao pressed her little fingers here and there, and then, to Si Nian's utter bewilderment, she picked up the signal of a foreign radio station.","Si Nian quickly accepted the fact that she was just an ordinary person.","Seeing how much her daughter liked it, she let her keep listening.","She then went downstairs to cook.","In the afternoon.","As soon as Fang Hui returned home, she heard a familiar English song drifting over from next door.","She subconsciously looked toward her neighbor's house and saw a radio that looked anything but cheap sitting on the desk in Si Nian's study.","She had seen this kind of radio at an elementary school in Beijing; she heard it was imported from abroad and incredibly expensive.","Ordinary people couldn't even buy one.","Recently, Fang Hui had enrolled her son in quite a few tutoring classes and even hired a private tutor to come to the house, which had cost her a lot of money.","She was truly reluctant to spend money on such a radio.","But the thought that Si Nian's family had one made her grit her teeth, grab some money, and head out.","Before long, Fang Hui returned carrying a brand-new radio.","Si Nian was standing at the courtyard gate and happened to see Fang Hui carrying the exact same model of radio. Upon seeing her, Fang Hui lifted her chin and greeted, \"Comrade Si, you finished classes so early today?\"","Si Nian gave a casual response and didn't say much else.","Fang Hui didn't add anything either and happily carried her radio home.","However, when she turned the radio on, she discovered that no matter how many cassette tapes she played or how she tuned it, she couldn't get the same audio as Si Nian's radio.","Fang Hui was furious, thinking she had bought a fake.","...","On Wednesday, Si Nian asked Zhou Yueshen to take Yaoyao with him.","Because she had an exam to take, there was no one to look after Yaoyao.","Zhou Yueshen was a bit worried and asked if he should escort her to the exam.","Si Nian said there was no need.","Zhou Yueshen took Yaoyao and Da Huang to the pig farm.","As soon as Yaoyao arrived, she was surrounded by a bunch of grown men who stared at Zhou Yueshen with sheer envy. They simply couldn't believe that their fierce, rugged-looking boss could have such an adorably soft and sweet daughter.","\"Come here, little darling Yaoyao, let Uncle give you a hug.\"","\"So cute, I want to have a daughter too.\"","\"How about Uncle takes you out to play?\"","A group of older men stared at Yaoyao with fawning expressions.","Just as Yaoyao was about to reach out her hands, Zhou Yueshen pressed her into his embrace and swept a murderous gaze over his group of sleazy subordinates.","Zhou Yueshen's eyes and brows clearly showed a look of disgust as he said unhappily, \"You guys stink too much. Stay away from my daughter.\"","Everyone subconsciously raised their arms to sniff themselves, saying, \"I don't stink, I just took a shower yesterday.\"","Zhou Yueshen couldn't be bothered with them and took long, purposeful strides toward his office with his daughter in his arms.","Meanwhile, Si Nian rode her bicycle to the No. 2 Middle School.","The exam was scheduled for exactly nine o'clock.","She didn't arrive early, either.","By the time she got there, a dozen or so people were already waiting outside.","Aside from students repeating the year, there were also transfer students.","Si Nian had previously attended No. 1 Middle School. The invigilator was a senior year homeroom teacher, who called roll and announced which school each student had come from.","When it was her turn, the teacher glanced at her. \"No. 1 Middle School, huh? How come a student from No. 1 Middle School is coming to our school instead of going back there?\"","It was well known that No. 1 Middle School was the best high school in the entire city, having always firmly suppressed them in rankings.","Moreover, the students from No. 1 Middle School were proud and completely looked down on any other school.","Their reputation as the eternal second place was quite famous in the city.","Si Nian didn't hide the truth, saying, \"Because the school wouldn't accept me.\"","She knew that these schools would definitely verify the reasons, and lying would only bring trouble upon herself.","Her words caused several teachers to pause in surprise.","Then, they looked at her with sympathy. \"No. 1 Middle School is a bit harsh, but don't worry. If they won't keep you, there's always a place that will. Our school will never give up on any student who works hard and strives to learn.\"","They assumed that Si Nian's grades were too poor, which was why the school hadn't accepted her.","After all, anyone with decent grades could repeat a year, even at No. 1 Middle School.","But if No. 1 Middle School refused to take her, it must have been out of fear that her poor grades would drag down their college admission rates.","In this day and age, there weren't many who could make it into a university anyway.","Although their school had requirements too, they weren't nearly as strict. As long as a student was willing to put in the effort and their grades weren't outrageously bad, they were willing to give the kid a chance.","Thus, Si Nian successfully earned the sympathetic gazes of a group of teachers.","Most of the others were from this school, with only a few from other schools, along with the transfer students.","Since they were all in their senior year, they were tested together.","Soon, Si Nian followed the group into the classroom to prepare for the exam.","There were only a dozen or so people, so everyone's seats were spaced far apart to prevent cheating.","Si Nian was assigned a seat in the middle.","Not long after she sat down, the test papers were handed out.","Upon receiving her paper, Si Nian first looked it over and found that it generally wasn't difficult.","She picked up her pen and began to write.","She already had a solid foundation, and coupled with her extensive reading, she barely had to think about these questions.","Si Nian also wanted to finish the exam as quickly as possible.","Because grades were her stepping stone; only by getting in could she negotiate terms with the school.","If she didn't even have good grades, the school would never accept a student like her who skipped classes to self-study at home.","Although the principal of the Foreign Language Elementary School had said he would help her, Si Nian still gave up on the idea of using the back door.","She had the ability, so there was no need to pull strings.","To avoid trouble, she chose to handle everything herself.","Several teachers paced back and forth, invigilating the exam.","It was extremely strict.","The other students were sweating profusely, but Si Nian felt completely at ease.","After all, she had been a teacher herself, so her mental fortitude was much stronger than that of the average person.","However, just as she was about to finish writing, an accident occurred.","A boy who had raised his hand to go to the restroom suddenly tossed a small slip of paper to the examinee sitting in front of her.","Who knew that the paper would roll right next to Si Nian.","The boy in front of her turned pale, completely at a loss for what to do.","Before Si Nian could even react, she saw a teacher walking toward her with a stern expression.","The teacher then picked up the slip of paper from the floor and asked severely, \"You there, stand up. What is the meaning of this?\"","Si Nian was also stunned.","She had no idea where this piece of paper came from; she had been entirely engrossed in answering the questions.","However, seeing everyone looking at her, she stood up anyway.","The other teachers hurried over and opened the slip of paper. Sure enough, there were answers written inside.","Their expressions instantly changed.","They stared at Si Nian in disbelief.","They truly hadn't expected that she would cheat.","Just a moment ago, they had felt sorry for her plight because No. 1 Middle School refused to take her.","To think she turned out to be this kind of person.","The teachers' faces instantly turned grim."]},{"number":332,"title":"Chapter 332: Release","paragraphs":["Si Nian calmly reassured them, \"Teachers, please don't get angry just yet.\"","She knew that incidents like this would naturally infuriate any teacher.","After all, cheating was a disgraceful act.","However, Si Nian also knew that these teachers were generally quite good-natured. They were only exceptionally angry because they had just comforted her moments ago, only for her to seemingly turn around and cheat.","Thus, she started by calmly trying to defuse the situation.","Although she hadn't noticed exactly where the piece of paper came from, she did recall a student raising his hand complaining of a stomachache.","Normally, students weren't allowed to use the restroom during an exam. But if someone was truly unwell, the teachers couldn't force them to hold it in—who would take responsibility if something happened? Besides, this wasn't a major official examination.","That student had just walked right past her desk.","She was almost certain that the note had been dropped by him.","However, she didn't know him at all, so the cheat sheet couldn't possibly be for her.","Si Nian lifted her gaze and swept a glance over the people around her.","The surrounding students were all staring at her, their faces filled with shock and bewilderment.","However, the boy sitting directly in front of her kept his head lowered and did not look back.","Given that the paper had rolled to her feet, it was inevitably meant for the student sitting in front of her. The sender had simply been too nervous and accidentally tossed it a bit too far, causing it to land by her side.","When she first arrived for the exam, she had purposefully observed this group of test-takers.","Many of them were students retaking their exams from the Second High School, so it was highly likely that quite a few of them knew each other.","It certainly wasn't out of the realm of possibility for them to collude and cheat.","The teachers demanded, \"What do you have to say for yourself? Who passed you these answers?\"","Si Nian replied, \"I suspect it was dropped by the boy who just walked by to go to the restroom. No one else would have had the opportunity. But I can guarantee these answers weren't meant for me. They were likely intended for a student sitting in front of me, who failed to catch the note, allowing it to fall by my desk.\"","The boy sitting in front of her instantly stiffened. He whipped around furiously and snapped, \"You're talking nonsense! I don't even know him, so why would we pass answers to each other? It's obvious that you were the one cheating, and now you're trying to frame someone else!\"","Si Nian sized him up, her gaze sweeping over the designer logo on his clothes. She said mildly, \"I only mentioned a student sitting in front of me. I never named you specifically, so why are you so quick to get defensive? Besides, the reason I dare to say this is because I have basically finished my paper and have no need for an answer sheet. Teachers, you can inspect my test paper and then compare it with his. The truth will be obvious.\"","The teachers exchanged glances, finding her logic sound.","To ensure they didn't wrongly accuse anyone, the teachers stepped forward and took both of their test papers to compare.","Sure enough, Si Nian had already reached the final section of her exam. The answers she had filled out in the previous sections were neat and meticulously written.","More importantly, they were all correct.","The teachers shot her a look of surprise.","When they pulled out the boy's test paper, however, it was more than half empty. Any question with even a slight degree of difficulty had been left blank.","After a quick comparison with the answers written on the cheat sheet, the truth was glaringly obvious.","The teachers' expressions instantly darkened.","\"Wang Wei, how do you explain this?\"","The boy named Wang Wei turned pale but stubbornly refused to admit it. \"It's true that I don't know how to answer the questions, but that doesn't mean I was cheating! What right do you have to falsely accuse me? That piece of paper wasn't even found on me!\"","\"Maybe she's been cheating this whole time! Otherwise, how could she have finished so quickly? The exam hasn't even been going on for an hour!\" He glared at Si Nian with sheer resentment.","The teachers exchanged another glance, feeling a bit perplexed themselves. They had noticed that Si Nian's answers were almost entirely correct. Yet, these questions were notoriously difficult past exam problems, easily on par with the actual college entrance examination.","For Si Nian to achieve such a high accuracy rate, she shouldn't have needed to retake her exams in the first place.","Furthermore, the First High School had refused to admit her. This made the teachers worry that there might be some hidden issues regarding her academic background.","They couldn't help but look at Si Nian.","\"Si Nian, could you tell us exactly why the First High School refused to admit you? Or perhaps you could tell us about your past academic records?\"","Si Nian replied, \"I find it strange too. My grades were always consistently in the top three of my entire school...\"","Before she could even finish her sentence, Wang Wei scoffed. \"Tch, anyone can brag. Top three of your school? And you still couldn't get into a university? Do you think we're all idiots?\"","The teachers also looked incredibly skeptical. Let alone the First High School, even in their own school, any student who ranked in the top three was considered extraordinary.","How could the First High School possibly reject a student of that caliber?","Si Nian shot the boy a sideways glance and said, \"I have no reason to lie. The teachers can easily look into my records and verify this. As for last year, it wasn't that I failed to get into a university; it was that I didn't take the college entrance examination at all.\"","\"As to why the First High School wouldn't accept me, I truly can't think of any other reason than the fact that I am already married. But surely there is no rule in this day and age that forbids married individuals from taking the college entrance examination, is there?\"","Si Nian stroked her chin thoughtfully.","Everyone was stunned.","The teachers were equally dumbfounded.","\"Wait, hold on a second. You're married?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Yes, I've been married for almost a year now.\"","Everyone was rendered speechless.","\"The First High School is known for its strict traditions. If you are indeed married, their refusal isn't entirely impossible to understand. So, did you miss the college entrance exam because you got married?\"","Si Nian replied, \"That is my private matter, so I'd rather not elaborate. In short, if the school suspects I'm lying, you are more than welcome to investigate. Right now, everyone is in the middle of an exam, and I don't want to hold up anyone's time. I only hope to have my name cleared.\"","Her words successfully redirected everyone's attention away from her personal life and back to the cheating incident.","Seeing how confident and resolute she was, the boy sitting in front of her began to panic.","Still, he remained as stubborn as a mule, insisting, \"I don't care what your excuses are! The paper landed by your desk, which means it was for you! You can't just drag me into this. I have nothing to hide!\"","For a moment, the gazes of everyone in the room shifted back and forth between the two of them.","Right at that moment, the boy who had been escorted to the restroom by a teacher returned.","He looked rather pale and unwell.","Had the cheating not been exposed, everyone might have simply assumed that his stomachache was due to exam nerves.","But in light of what had just happened, the true reason behind his pale complexion was suddenly open to interpretation.","Sure enough, upon seeing a group of teachers gathered at the desks, his face drained of even more color.","\"Fan Cong, did you drop this cheat sheet just now? Who exactly are you helping to cheat?\" a teacher demanded sternly.","Fan Cong instantly panicked, his eyes subconsciously darting toward Wang Wei.","Wang Wei's face darkened, and he deliberately looked away, pretending not to notice.","Si Nian observed the newcomer. He was wearing faded, washed-out clothes, thick square-framed glasses, and a pair of worn-out, misshapen liberation shoes.","He was clearly from a completely different social class compared to the boy in front of her, who was dressed in name-brand clothing.","Fan Cong stammered, \"Teacher, what are you talking about? I don't understand what you mean. I wasn't cheating.\"","With everyone refusing to confess, the teachers were beginning to lose their patience!","\"You were the only one who just walked past this aisle. If it wasn't you, who else could it be?\"","Fan Cong's lips trembled. Lowering his head, he said, \"I really don't know anything about it. My stomach was hurting, and all I could think about was rushing to the restroom. A teacher even went with me. The teacher can vouch for whether I cheated or not.\"","Since no one had actually witnessed the act, the teachers couldn't jump to conclusions about who the culprit was, though they were growing increasingly frustrated.","Just as they were about to lose their tempers, Si Nian spoke up. \"Teachers, it's actually quite simple to get to the bottom of this.\""]},{"number":333,"title":"Chapter 333: Rotten wood cannot be carved.","paragraphs":["Since there is a note, it must have his handwriting on it. We'll know for sure once we compare it with his test paper. I believe the difference in handwriting will be quite obvious. Secondly, since the student in front of me accused me of cheating, let's compare the answers written by the entire class, including this student, with my test paper. If anyone has written the exact same answers as I have, I will submit to whatever punishment you deem fit.","As soon as she finished speaking, the faces of the two boys turned pale.","The teachers also found her logic sound. After all, with exam questions, there are many ways to solve them; it was impossible for two people to have 100% identical answers.","They immediately compared the handwriting, and sure enough, it was a perfect match for Fan Cong's.","The teachers were no fools. Their expressions darkened instantly. Fan Cong, how do you explain this?","With the evidence held against him, Fan Cong was speechless.","However, no matter how much the teachers questioned him, he refused to admit who he had written it for.","Naturally, he lost his eligibility to repeat the year.","Si Nian hadn't wanted to meddle, but as Fan Cong was leaving, the boy in front of her glared at her with a cold, sinister gaze.","This made her change her mind.","Teachers, when I first arrived, I noticed that no one seemed very familiar with each other. For someone to be willing to throw away their future just to help someone cheat, they must have either been paid off or threatened. We mustn't let the real cheater get away.","The teachers' expressions changed immediately.","It was true; Fan Cong would rather be expelled than reveal the other party, unless he was truly being threatened.","Some of the teachers knew the boy. He was timid and submissive, not very brave, and while his grades were decent, his psychological state was poor. He tended to underperform whenever he got nervous.","With a little effort, he could have gotten into university.","But now, he was giving up even the chance of going to university rather than naming the person who had asked for the help.","Everyone's gaze instantly fell upon Wang Wei, who sat in front.","Wang Wei had just breathed a sigh of relief, but upon hearing this, he was nearly scared to death, his scalp tingling with fear.","Originally, if the teachers couldn't find anything, there would have been nothing they could do.","But this woman just had to bring it up.","Damn it, he never should have messed with her!","Following this incident, the other students became nervous. No one dared to try any more little tricks.","Si Nian continued writing her exam. Soon, she finished, stood up, and handed in her paper in one fluid motion.","She was the first student to turn in her test.","Perhaps the teachers still had some lingering doubts, as they had stood by her side while she completed the last few questions.","The more they watched, the more astonished they became.","Chinese and Mathematics had been held in the morning.","The afternoon was for Physics and English.","English was Si Nian's specialty, so it was naturally a breeze for her. She finished it in less than half an hour.","While everyone else was still struggling with what was, for them, the most difficult subject, she had already handed in her paper.","Si Nian successfully earned the bewildered stares of all her classmates and teachers.","Originally, the teachers had intended to give it a cursory glance.","Good heavens, they were in for a shock.","There was technical vocabulary that even they didn't know...","What on earth was going on?","***","Meanwhile, in prison.","Lin Sisi didn't get the good news from Si's Mother about a school accepting her. Instead, she received news that the couple was planning to divorce.","Liu Dongdong said sadly, Ever since you went to prison, Sisi, the relationship between Uncle and Auntie has been getting worse and worse. For some reason, Uncle Si is always visiting Si Nian now and even giving her money in secret. Auntie was furious when she found out, and they've been fighting and having a cold war. Now they're getting a divorce.","But don't worry. No matter what, Uncle Si is still your biological father; he definitely won't ignore you. I've already told him about you taking the Gaokao. Auntie also went to the school to find a teacher—it's First High School. The teacher said they're willing to take you. You just need to go and take the exam when the time comes.","Lin Sisi's expression was grim when she heard the news about her parents' divorce.","It was only after hearing the latter part that her expression improved slightly.","While in prison, she didn't know exactly what was happening even with her family's frequent visits, and she certainly couldn't change anything.","Now, her only thought was to get out as soon as possible.","Based on her knowledge of the future, as long as she could get out, she would definitely be successful.","At the very least, she wouldn't end up worse than Si Nian!","She had learned to be smart. In the future, she wouldn't go looking for trouble with Si Nian. She would work hard in secret and then amaze everyone!","Just as she was about to say something, she suddenly noticed some red marks on Liu Dongdong's neck.","Having lived through two lifetimes, she naturally knew what those were.","Lin Sisi said suspiciously, Dongdong, your neck...","Startled, Liu Dongdong covered her neck. Then, under Lin Sisi's questioning gaze, her face flushed with embarrassment. I... I have a boyfriend...","Lin Sisi breathed a sigh of relief for some reason. For a moment there, a certain unpleasant thought had actually crossed her mind.","Thank goodness.","Since it was a boyfriend, it definitely wasn't what she had been thinking.","***","When Si Nian returned home, she was surprised to find Zhou Yueshen there.","At that moment, he was sitting on the sofa watching the two children practice their calligraphy.","The Second Child's handwriting was truly hideous. Since he was still young, he needed to practice more.","Calligraphy was a great way to cultivate one's character and improve focus, but most people found it hard to stick with.","Take the Second Child, for example—he hadn't even been sitting there for half an hour before his restlessness kicked in.","Normally, Zhou Zedong would indulge him and wouldn't scold him.","After all, he was young himself and couldn't bring himself to be hard on his brother.","But Zhou Yueshen was quite strict.","This character is crooked. You can't use brute force when you write.","Zhou Zehan didn't understand and was completely confused; no matter how he wrote, it still looked the same.","Zhou Yueshen simply set down Yao Yao, who was playing with toys in his lap, and took the boy's hand to teach him stroke by stroke.","His expression was stern, and he carried a natural air of pressure and authority when teaching.","Zhou Zehan was terrified, his little face scrunched up as he shifted uncomfortably, feeling very out of his element.","But he didn't dare to rebel.","Zhou Yueshen taught him for a while, his brow furrowing slightly as he finally understood the saying, Rotten wood cannot be carved.","The Second Child looked at his father blankly.","Zhou Yueshen didn't scold him, though. He remained patient and taught him for a bit longer until he noticed Si Nian had returned. Only then did he let up. Take a break. Xiao Dong, you teach your brother in a bit.","The Second Child cast a pleading look toward Si Nian.","Si Nian pretended not to see it.","Even though she doted on the Second Child, the boy really did need to study hard. You couldn't just give up completely because someone lacked talent.","She had said those things before to encourage him, but she couldn't let the Second Child give up on his studies because of them.","Zhou Yueshen stood up, the sternness in his eyes fading away. His lips curled up slightly into a handsome arc as he walked toward Si Nian on his long legs.","Finished with the exam? How did it go?","Si Nian said, It was okay. There shouldn't be any problems.","Zhou Yueshen naturally believed in her. Si Nian's abilities had always been exceptional, and he had seen it for himself.","There was no need to worry.","Zhou Yueshen leaned down and gave her a light peck on the forehead. You rest today. I'll cook.","Si Nian was happy to have the break and nodded.","Zhou Yueshen ate dinner with them and then went out to work again.","He had likely been worried that Yao Yao would be bored staying there for too long, so he had brought the child back first. He had made dinner while he was at it.","The Second Child pulled a long face. Daddy is so scary. He kept staring at me.","His hand was still sore.","He had intended to act spoiled with Si Nian, but she didn't indulge him this time. Instead, she said sternly, \"Xiao Han, practicing your handwriting is a good thing. It's only natural that you find it a bit difficult since you've just started, but it will get better after a while. Once your handwriting improves, Mommy will reward you with a little red flower.\"","Zhou Zehan's eyes lit up. \"Really? I can get a little red flower for writing, too?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Of course. The little red flowers you earned before were used up when I bought you the toys and the bicycle, so your tally has been reset to zero. If you work hard this time, you might even overtake your brother soon.\"","Zhou Zedong's hand, which was holding his chopsticks, paused for a moment.","Zhou Zehan was already cheering up. His previous resentment had vanished, and he immediately declared that he would practice for a while longer after finishing his meal.","Si Nian smiled. Using reverse psychology on the Second Child really did work every single time.","The results came out the following afternoon."]},{"number":334,"title":"Chapter 334: Where do you work","paragraphs":["Si Nian hurried to the school as soon as class was over.","This time, she brought Yao Yao along. The little girl was used to following her around everywhere and remained quite calm.","Since she had a child with her, no one thought much of it, especially since Si Nian had already mentioned she was married yesterday.","However, having such a big child after only half a year of marriage made the looks people gave her somewhat peculiar.","After all, Si Nian appeared to be only eighteen or nineteen, yet she already had a three-year-old daughter.","Although many people in their area married early, they usually stayed home to look after the children. It was rare for someone married to still attend school.","Once they understood why No. 1 High School hadn't accepted her, everyone felt it made sense.","Having a child out of wedlock was considered shameful in any era.","Especially in this rather conservative period.","A school with strict discipline like No. 1 High naturally wouldn't accept her.","People sized her up.","The boys thought: She really is a girl with no self-respect.","The girls thought: She's so pitiful, she must have been deceived by a bad man.","Si Nian: ...Let me explain.","Some looked down on her, while others felt sympathy.","Fortunately, the teacher soon called students in one by one. Probably to protect everyone's self-esteem, the grades weren't announced publicly.","Instead, each student went in for a private talk.","Si Nian saw some beaming with joy, while others walked out dejected.","She was just about to sit down when the teacher came over and called her: \"Si Nian, is Si Nian here?\"","Si Nian quickly answered and walked in.","Inside were the same few teachers from yesterday.","They were gathered around, discussing her test papers.","\"I think her Chinese is excellent. She could join our class; we teach Chinese well.\"","\"What are you talking about? Her math and physics are even better. Class 2 offers more opportunities to excel.\"","\"Nonsense, her English is clearly the best—it's a perfect score! She might even become a diplomat someday.\"","They argued over which class she should join.","The department head finally coughed and said, \"Alright, alright. Let her choose which class she wants to join. It's not for you all to pick and choose.\"","Top students always received preferential treatment.","It was never about others choosing her, but about her choosing them.","Although they were also surprised to learn Si Nian was married,","frankly, so what if she's married? As long as she loves learning, she's a good student and deserves this opportunity.","Especially one as academically outstanding as her.","Letting her slip away would haunt them for life.","Seeing Si Nian enter, the teachers stopped their squabbling. Some coughed, others adjusted their glasses, using small gestures to cover their awkwardness.","\"Hello, teachers,\" Si Nian greeted.","The department head said, \"Hello, Si Nian. Your papers have been graded. You performed excellently in all subjects. Although physics is slightly weaker, it's negligible. You are eligible to join any of the four top classes for senior year.\"","The other teachers immediately looked at her with hopeful anticipation.","Trying to ignore their eager, expectant gazes, Si Nian steeled herself and said, \"Well, teachers, I'm fine with any class, but I might not be able to attend classes in person.\"","The office fell silent for a moment.","The department head, having seen his share of situations, asked her why.","Si Nian explained, \"Because I have a job outside, and I also need to take care of my child. It's not very convenient for me to come to class every day. So, I plan to study at home and just come to take the college entrance exam.\"","The department head was actually quite opposed to the idea, but seeing the three-year-old little bean Si Nian held by the hand—","not even as old as his own daughter...","His heart softened.","He thought Si Nian really had it tough.","She was just a kid herself, having to juggle childcare, work, and studies.","Just hearing about it made one feel for her.","He said, \"Are you short on money? If it's a financial issue, we can discuss the tuition fees. You're still young; you shouldn't let work interfere with your studies.\"","Although her grades were indeed excellent, the college entrance exam was only a few months away.","This was no time for any slip-ups.","Moreover, she was so outstanding, and coming from No. 1 High, her English in particular left him amazed.","Putting other subjects aside, with Si Nian's English level, she might actually stand a chance against No. 1 High's students.","Perhaps their perpetually second-place school could finally turn things around this year and even surpass No. 1 High.","Just the thought of that possibility made the department head grin involuntarily.","While English was emphasized now, honestly, not many students excelled at it.","The overall education level wasn't very high. Their city, surrounded by mountains, developed slower than the big cities outside.","This meant many children from mountainous areas started learning English quite late.","Some even felt it was a \"foreign language\" and unnecessary to learn.","As a result, even fewer students performed well in English.","The top students from that one foreign language primary school downtown all went to No. 1 High.","Very few came to No. 2 High. The whole school only had a handful of students with decent English scores.","Forget the students; after looking at Si Nian's English paper and reading her essay, he knew this was no ordinary level.","Many of their school's teachers with college or university degrees couldn't match her.","Si Nian shook her head and said, \"Teacher, I'm not short on money. It's just that this job isn't easy to quit—I signed a contract. And work is secondary; the main thing is I can take care of my child there.\"","She could bring her child to work, but she couldn't very well bring a child to class.","The department head immediately said, \"That's not a big problem. Our school can intercede on your behalf. Any reasonable boss would understand and not make things difficult for you. Where do you work?\"","Si Nian explained, \"Really, it's not necessary. Please don't worry. I can study effectively at home. I can't promise I'll get first place, but I can guarantee a top-five ranking.\"","The department head said apologetically, \"Ah, it's not about that. I just want you to learn as much as possible and worry this might hinder your studies. Since you're unwilling, I won't force you.\"","If Si Nian's grades were poor, he would definitely object.","But with her results right there, everything was negotiable.","\"In that case, I'll assign you to Class 1. Xiao Wang, you'll be Si Nian's homeroom teacher from now on.\" He then turned to Si Nian. \"Si Nian, this is Teacher Wang, your homeroom teacher. He's our school's youngest and best English teacher, a top graduate from the downtown foreign language primary school.\"","Teacher Wang looked about twenty-six or twenty-seven. He coughed lightly and said, \"Nothing worth mentioning, really.\"","Si Nian smiled and agreed.","Senior year didn't involve much new teaching anyway; it was mostly practice tests and problem-solving.","Although Teacher Wang agreed she didn't have to attend class, she had to come once a week to collect practice papers and complete them. If her performance fell below standard, she would have to return to school for classes.","It sounded strict, but it was clearly for her own good.","Si Nian naturally had no objections.","Not only that, he also gave her the previous set of practice papers to complete and bring back next time.","Basically, she didn't have to come to class, but the homework was mandatory.","Si Nian felt a headache coming on, but she couldn't very well refuse.","It seemed her workload had just increased.","With that settled, Si Nian was finally free to leave.","But she had only taken two steps when she was called back.","The department head asked with a concerned look, \"By the way, Si Nian, where exactly do you work?\""]},{"number":335,"title":"Chapter 335: Scenery","paragraphs":["After finishing, afraid that Si Nian would find him annoying, he explained: \"We must have this work certificate, otherwise it will be hard to explain to the principal.\"","Although he had the authority to let students in, Si Nian's situation was truly special.","If he couldn't provide a reasonable justification, the principal probably wouldn't agree.","Si Nian thought about it and felt it made sense, so she said: \"I work at the Foreign Language Elementary School...\"","\"Foreign Language Elementary School? The one downtown?\" Several teachers immediately looked at her.","Si Nian hesitated slightly.","Unexpectedly, her expression was interpreted by everyone as awkwardness.","Someone blurted out, \"Could it be you work there as a cleaner?\"","The Foreign Language Elementary School wasn't easy to get into; it was considered the city's first elite school. Rumor had it even the cleaners needed qualifications, otherwise they couldn't get in.","They didn't hire anyone below a bachelor's degree, and there were even returned overseas PhDs teaching there. It was incredibly prestigious.","Many principals from other schools tried to build good relations with the principal of Foreign Language Elementary School, hoping the school would put in a good word for them in front of the children.","\"I heard the kids there this year are all extraordinary. One child won two first places in the city-wide elementary school competition. The other day, a four-year-old prodigy from the capital city transferred in. It's really impressive.\"","\"Isn't Foreign Language Elementary School your old school, Teacher Wang?\"","Teacher Wang puffed out his chest proudly and said, \"Yes, our school produces a couple of outstanding talents every year. It really is remarkable.\"","If he hadn't attended Foreign Language Elementary School for a few years and learned the basics early, he probably wouldn't be an English teacher now.","Thanks to his parents' concern for face back then, they insisted on sending him there.","Now he felt he hadn't wasted their earnest efforts.","So, mentioning his alma mater filled Teacher Wang with immense pride.","The corner of Si Nian's mouth twitched.","Did she really look like a cleaner?","\"You've all done the talking, leaving her no chance to speak,\" the department head said. Although also surprised, he wasn't as exaggerated as the other teachers. He shot them a glare.","He was also worried that Si Nian might actually be a cleaner and didn't want her to feel that her self-esteem had been hurt.","Girls of that age cared about face.","He understood.","So he didn't press further, saying, \"Alright, you can go back to your work. Just remember to come once a week.\"","Si Nian smiled, nodded, and left.","Soon, the other students were also assigned.","Just then, the principal happened to come by and asked about the situation.","The department head immediately mentioned Si Nian, saying there was an exceptionally outstanding student in this batch, but her circumstances were somewhat complicated.","The principal said he hadn't encountered anything too complex; he'd accept students even without hands or feet. How complicated could it be?","The department head then explained the situation: this child had quite a background, coming from No.1 High School, but because she got married, No.1 High School didn't want her anymore, so she came to No.2 High School.","Unexpectedly, her grades were exceptionally good.","But because she had a child and also worked at Foreign Language Elementary School—probably doing cleaning or odd jobs—and couldn't get away, she couldn't attend school regularly and had to study at home.","Upon hearing this, the principal frowned, his V-shaped brows knitting together. It really was complicated.","But these were minor issues. He said he was very familiar with the principal of Foreign Language Elementary School and would just make a phone call to sort it out.","His student, he would spoil her himself.","The department head knew the principal was easygoing; as long as there was a passable reason, he wouldn't make things difficult.","The principal immediately took out a small notebook from his pocket, put on his glasses, flipped through it to find the phone number of the Foreign Language Elementary School principal, and dialed.","\"Principal Chu! Ah, yes, it's me, Old Wang... Ah, I just haven't chatted with you in a while and missed you. It's been ages since we all got together. Even though you're not very ethical, always recommending kids only to No.1 High School, and our school, ranked second, has suffered thanks to you, but I won't hold it against you...\"","Seeing the conversation was about to turn into an argument, Teacher Wang hurriedly reminded him, \"Dad, get to the point. That's my student. It'd be best if Principal Chu could assign her less work. Otherwise, with her taking care of a child and having to do so many test papers, she might get exhausted. I'd feel guilty.\"","Principal Wang then remembered his purpose for the call and quickly brought up the matter.","Under the curious gazes of everyone present...","There seemed to be a very, very long silence on the other end...","Soon, they saw Principal Wang's wide, grinning mouth close. His expression shifted from surprise to something complicated, and then he hung up the phone.","Everyone's hearts sank.","Could it be that Principal Chu of Foreign Language Elementary School didn't agree?","Everyone knew Principal Chu was close with the principal of No.1 High School; they were good buddies who often drank together.","He probably couldn't stand to see them doing well.","\"Principal, how did it go?\"","\"Dad, say something!\"","Teacher Wang thought, if the other principal really didn't agree, he could at least give Si Nian fewer test papers in the future.","He couldn't let Si Nian think they were as heartless as No.1 High School.","Principal Wang said with a complex expression, \"This... this student Si, she's not a cleaner.\"","\"Ah? She's not?\"","\"Then what is she?\"","\"Dad, could you finish your sentence?\"","Principal Wang said meaningfully, \"Principal Chu said that Si Nian is an English teacher at No.1 High School.\"","Everyone was dumbfounded.","Teacher Wang, who had just been showing off in front of Si Nian about being a former student of Foreign Language Elementary School, was petrified.","Under everyone's stunned gazes, Principal Wang straightened his suit and stood up.","\"Principal, where are you going?\"","Principal Wang said, \"Going home to change clothes. Principal Chu 'personally' invited me for drinks tonight.\"","Before the others could recover from the shock of Si Nian being a teacher at Foreign Language Elementary School, they were stunned again.","They had only ever heard of other principals inviting Principal Chu for drinks. This was the first time they'd heard of Principal Chu personally inviting their principal for drinks.","...","A few days later, Lin Sisi also received the books and test papers the school asked her parents to deliver.","It was Zhang Cuimei who delivered them.","She said the school gave them to her to pass on to Lin Sisi.","Although they agreed to accept Lin Sisi, they weren't willing to deliver the materials to her personally.","But they were worried that if Lin Sisi fell behind while in prison, it would lower the school's college admission rate in the Gaokao (the National College Entrance Examination).","That's why they contacted Zhang Cuimei.","Zhang Cuimei looked haggard and thin.","She and her husband had been arguing about divorce recently.","The divorce was initiated by her husband.","Originally, they were just in a cold war, but recently her husband suddenly brought up divorce, blaming her for causing trouble with Si Nian and being seen by Division Commander Jiang and Mother Fu, which embarrassed him.","He used this as grounds for divorce.","He also said she had become too malicious. No matter what, Si Nian was the daughter they had raised for over ten years. Not helping her in that situation was bad enough, but she even cursed her.","He said she was heartless and ungrateful.","Zhang Cuimei was furious and bewildered.","She felt her husband had completely sided with Si Nian.","She was filled with both anger and hatred.","She believed Si Nian was the one who had destroyed her family.","Her daughter in prison, her husband wanting a divorce.","It was all because of her.","Zhang Cuimei wiped her tears and said, \"Your father has completely given up on you. Haven't you noticed he hasn't visited you in a long time? Sisi, I've decided, if your father and I really divorce, you'll come with me.\"","The news of Principal Wang and Principal Chu going arm-in-arm to the state-run restaurant for dinner and drinks somehow got out. Soon, the gossip reached the ears of Principal Liu of No.1 High School.","Principal Liu (huff) (cold laugh): I don't believe it.","Later, Principal Liu secretly went to the state-run restaurant and saw the two of them chatting and laughing happily.","Principal Liu: (...expletive)","#Firmly refusing to believe he's been cuckolded by Lao Wang next door#","#Principal Liu's face gets slapped#","#Principal Liu drowns his sorrows alone#"]},{"number":336,"title":"Chapter 336: My Son Scored 98 Points","paragraphs":["As soon as she said this, she thought Lin Sisi would be moved.","Who knew Lin Sisi's face would instantly darken: \"Mom, what are you saying?? Divorce! How can you and Dad be getting divorced? If it really comes to it, just apologize to Dad, give in a little. It's not a big deal, is it?\"","\"If you get divorced, how am I supposed to face people in the Fu family? Our family's circumstances are already not as good as the Fu family's. His side of the family looks down on me. If you two divorce, what will happen to me!\"","Lin Sisi was frantic. Even though she didn't have deep feelings for her parents, she didn't want them to divorce either.","Let alone go with Zhang Cuimei.","Zhang Cuimei was just a minor public servant.","But Si's Father, after all, was a military officer.","If they divorced, Zhang Cuimei would have to move out of the military family compound.","Then what would life be like for her, and for me if I were with her, in the compound afterwards?","Lin Sisi strongly opposed it.","Hearing this, Zhang Cuimei looked at Lin Sisi in disbelief.","She thought that when she told her daughter about her husband's unfair treatment, her daughter would surely feel for her and stand by her side.","She never expected her to also tell her to lower her head and admit fault.","But Zhang Cuimei, used to being tough, how could she possibly swallow her pride?","Originally, when her husband mentioned divorce, she hadn't taken it seriously.","Theirs was a military marriage; without major issues, her husband couldn't just divorce her arbitrarily. The higher-ups wouldn't approve it.","But this time, perhaps because of the things she had said, which were overheard by Division Commander Jiang and Mother Fu, who then targeted her behind her back...","The higher-ups actually hinted to Si's Father that the Si family's conduct was improper, leaving the decision to him.","That is to say, once Si's Father made his decision, she would really have to get divorced.","Before, when her husband stopped coming home daily, people had already noticed, gossiping about whether Si's Father had someone on the outside.","If they really divorced, how many people would laugh at her and gloat over her misfortune.","If even her daughter wouldn't stand by her side...","Noticing Zhang Cuimei's ugly expression, Lin Sisi realized she had been too harsh and hurriedly comforted her: \"Mom, it's not that I'm unwilling to be with you. I just think this is bad for you. Look, if you divorce, my life in the Fu family will be incredibly difficult. And with Dad favoring Si Nian, if anything happens in the future, no one will protect me, and I'll have no maternal family to rely on. I've already lived eighteen years of hardship; I'm really afraid of losing you...\"","Hearing this, Zhang Cuimei's heart ached sharply.","Yes, if she left, what would become of her daughter?","Even if her daughter came with her, they would still live in the military family compound. If that man found a stepmother for her, her life would surely be even harder.","Si's Mother made up her mind. So what if he had a woman outside? For her daughter's sake, she would die before agreeing to divorce her husband.","Early May, the weather was getting nicer, temperatures rising, and everyone started wearing short sleeves and skirts.","Si Nian put away the thick quilts and laid out the lighter ones in the doorway to air.","Da Huang lay nearby, basking in the sun.","Just then, there was a knock at the door.","Si Nian looked over and saw it was Fang Hui from next door.","Fang Hui was still in professional attire, looking very much the white-collar professional.","In one hand, she carried some fruit; in the other, a radio.","A quick glance confirmed it was the same model as the one at their school.","Si Nian raised an eyebrow slightly, stepped forward, and opened the door. \"Comrade Fang, is there something you need?\"","Although the two families lived close by, there was a sense of distance, and they had always maintained a mutually non-intrusive way of getting along.","Fang Hui disdained flattering others, but this time she had no choice.","Fang Hui said, \"I bought a radio, but I'm not very good at using it. I heard you, Teacher Si, are a foreign language teacher at the foreign language elementary school. Could you teach me how to tune it?\"","She had bought it after seeing how good Si Nian's radio was, but after buying it, she couldn't figure out how to use it.","She had wanted to ask the shop owner, but the owner said he didn't know either.","She couldn't return it either, which infuriated Fang Hui.","Such an expensive item, she couldn't bear to just let it go to waste.","That's why she had swallowed her pride and come knocking.","\"About that incident last time, please don't take it to heart. I was just unfamiliar and asked without thinking it would offend you. I'm truly sorry. These fruits are a small apology.\"","She was referring to the time she had gossiped about Si Nian with others in the tube-shaped apartment building.","Si Nian offered a thin, insincere smile.","If she was really sorry, why wait until now to apologize? It had been so long.","Still, one shouldn't hit a person who comes with a smile. She said, \"You're too polite, Comrade Fang. I generally don't bother with people who enjoy gossiping about others behind their backs.\"","Fang Hui's face darkened for a moment. This was a veiled jab, mocking her.","She really wanted to turn and leave, but thinking of her purpose, she held back.","She forced an awkward laugh and said, \"Yes, yes, let's just let bygones be bygones. As for this radio, could I trouble you, Teacher Si, to help me tune it...\"","She lifted the radio. \"I'm really quite embarrassed. I only realized after buying it that you, Teacher Si, have one too. But please don't misunderstand, I didn't buy it because I saw you had one. It's just that my son did quite well on his recent tests, so I bought it as a gift for him...\"","\"I heard your ten-year-old eldest son is also in fourth grade at the foreign language elementary school. I wonder how his test scores were? My son didn't do too well this time; he lost two points on his English composition...\"","Si Nian nodded seriously. \"That's indeed not too great.\"","Fang Hui thought she had misheard and emphasized, \"My son scored ninety-eight. He only lost two points on the English composition. He ranked first in the class.\"","Si Nian nodded. \"And so?\"","Question marks seemed to pop up above Fang Hui's head. If she had said this to anyone else, they would have been showering her with praise and envy by now.","Why was she so calm?","Unwilling to give up, she said, \"Although he's first in the class, he's still two points short. I'm not very satisfied.\"","Si Nian said, \"Then have him repeat the grade.\"","Fang Hui couldn't smile anymore. \"Never mind. It's just two points. I'm not that strict. But, Teacher Si, how much did your son score? My son's ninety-eight is first in the class. Your son probably isn't worse than mine, right?\"","Now it was Si Nian's turn to smile. \"You're too kind. Although my son scored a hundred, your son is also quite good.\"","Fang Hui: \"...\"","Si Nian secretly enjoyed her somewhat twisted expression for a moment. Actually, she could understand Fang Hui. Having a four-year-old son who was such a genius made her think her son was the best in the world.","He couldn't be surpassed in the slightest.","But while showing off was one thing, belittling other people's children to elevate her own was something Si Nian couldn't agree with.","Especially when the child being belittled was her own.","When she was young, her parents were always comparing her to others—either this family's daughter was more outstanding, or that family's son had better grades and was more filial.","In short, she was always the worst.","She really disliked this kind of disparaging upbringing.","Fang Hui was probably encountering for the first time a situation where her bragging was surpassed by someone else.","Her expression was truly spectacular.","She managed an ugly smile. \"It seems your son is really amazing. Even though he's already ten, my son can't compare to him.\"","Si Nian said calmly, \"Sorry, I don't like comparing my son to others. He's not a commodity.\""]},{"number":337,"title":"Chapter 337: Dragon Boat Festival","paragraphs":["Fang Hui lost all desire to stay. Forgetting her original purpose, she gave a couple of awkward laughs and went back home.","That evening.","Eldest Child took a red pen and drew three little red flowers on the wooden board with his name that Si Nian had set up.","Looking at his younger brother's single red flower, he was in a great mood.","Second Child stomped his feet in anger. His older brother had taken first place in math, Chinese, and English tests, earning three little red flowers at once.","He only had one. He had originally wanted to go out and play with Jiang Jiu, but now he wasn't in the mood. He immediately took out his copybook and started practicing his handwriting.","Mom said that once he finished practicing a whole book, she would give him a flower.","If he couldn't compete in quality, he would win with quantity.","Yaoyao was playing with the radio on the side, and foreign nursery rhymes started playing.","His thoughts were disturbed again, and he couldn't help but hum along.","He didn't know where Mom had bought so many cassette tapes. His younger sister had been playing them constantly these past few days, and he had learned how to hum them.","After Yaoyao finished singing one song, she stood on her tiptoes to change to another.","After listening for a while, she got bored and took out the colored pens Si Nian had bought her to draw and write.","In no time, she had drawn some cute cartoon characters.","Previously, her drawings were based on family members.","But after reading more books, she started imitating the cartoon characters in them.","After drawing, she would even write captions, like a conversation between several children.","If Si Nian saw this now, she would realize this was basically a comic book.","However, at this moment, Si Nian was still in the study working on her exam papers.","The family was happily busy with their own things.","Meanwhile, next door at the Fang house, the atmosphere was extremely tense.","Fang Bowen was currently being made to stand as punishment, holding an English book.","Fang Hui held a bamboo cane in her hand, her face dark and ugly.","\"If you don't finish memorizing these one hundred words tonight, don't even think about eating!\"","\"Since you were little, I've spent so much money hiring teachers and tutors for you, letting you enjoy the best education, yet you can't even compare to someone from the countryside!\"","\"The son of Si Nian next door scored a hundred on his English test! Aren't you ashamed!\"","Fang Bowen's eyes were red, but he didn't dare to cry out loud.","The window was open, and a breeze blew in from outside.","He could hear the sounds of Zhou Zehan and Jiang Jiu playing hide-and-seek in the yard next door.","He zoned out for a moment, only snapping back to reality when a sharp pain hit his face from a slap.","Fang Hui was staring at him with a dark expression.","Zhou Yueshen had been busy expanding the breeding farm recently.","Si Nian was also busy every day, especially with the Dragon Boat Festival approaching.","Her family had written to her, asking if she was doing well and if she wanted them to send her some zongzi.","Si Nian had just replied saying there was no need, as she planned to make them herself. But two days later, her older brother brought over a bag of glutinous rice and bamboo leaves from home.","It was obvious they had picked the leaves themselves; they were very tender and had a fresh fragrance.","However, before Si Nian had time to make the zongzi, the school gave them zongzi gift boxes.","It had to be said, a wealthy school really was different.","The gift boxes were very high-end.","Si Nian placed them in the front basket of her bicycle and brought them home.","Not only did the adults get them, but the children also received small gift boxes.","The school did a particularly good job in this regard.","Second Child and Jiang Jiu held their zongzi, looking extremely happy.","\"Mom, Mom, such big zongzi! I've never eaten zongzi before!\"","Second Child loved chewy, sticky foods, but they didn't make zongzi at home, and his dad wasn't one to celebrate holidays. In previous years, their holidays were just like any other day.","He had only ever seen his classmates bring zongzi to school to eat.","Si Nian saw how excited he was. Second Child was from the countryside, and although the school teachers were nice, they certainly didn't have the means to give out such things.","Receiving a gift from the school for the first time, he was naturally overjoyed.","Si Nian said, \"I was planning to make zongzi myself, and I even bought the leaves. I didn't expect the school to give out so many.\"","Second Child's eyes immediately lit up. \"Mom, you know how to make zongzi?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Of course I do. But the zongzi Mom makes don't have anything inside, just plain white glutinous rice.\"","Si Nian liked to eat simple zongzi without various fillings, otherwise they were too rich.","Especially the savory ones.","Although the gift boxes from the school were nice, they weren't the kind she liked to eat.","She planned to pick out a few to have her older brother take back for her family to taste.","Hearing this, Second Child immediately shoved his zongzi into Jiang Jiu's hands, ran to Si Nian's side, and looked up at her, saying, \"Mom, Mom, I want to make them too! Let's make zongzi, okay?\"","He loved cooking with his mom. Before, on New Year's Day, Mom had taken him to make dumplings and even cooked tangyuan for him!","Holidays were Second Child's favorite days.","Because in the past, he could only watch other children sit in their yards making zongzi with their parents, and now it was finally his turn.","He wanted to make big, round zongzi!","Hearing this, Jiang Jiu didn't want his either, but he couldn't throw it away. He also leaned over and said, \"Second brother's mom, I want to make them too!\"","Seeing how happy the children were, Si Nian immediately made a decision. She would soak the bamboo leaves today and then make zongzi.","The two children happily linked arms and ran home. \"We're going to make zongzi!\"","As soon as they reached the door, they saw Fang Hui from next door.","She was holding Fang Bowen's hand and carrying a birthday cake in her other hand.","Second Child's gaze was immediately drawn to it.","What was that? It looked so delicious.","Seemingly noticing his gaze, Fang Hui stopped and greeted Si Nian. \"Teacher Si, what a coincidence. Do you also have time off for the Dragon Boat Festival?\"","Si Nian gave a slight nod. \"Yes.\"","Fang Hui lifted the cake in her hand. \"Today is my Bowen's birthday. Do you want to come to our house and have some cake together? I see your son seems to really want some.\"","She looked at Second Child with a teasing smile.","Second Child immediately withdrew his gaze from the cake, feeling a bit guilty.","But in his heart, he couldn't help thinking: So this is a cake. People really have cakes on their birthdays. He had never celebrated a birthday before.","Fang Bowen was so lucky.","Fang Bowen slightly raised his chin and said, \"This is the cake my mom ordered for me. One piece costs twenty yuan, and it has chocolate on top.\"","Second Child immediately opened his mouth wide.","His nine little white rabbits had only sold for eighteen yuan.","This cake was more expensive than his little rabbits.","Fang Hui waited for her son to finish speaking before smiling and saying, \"Yes, a child can't finish it all by himself. Why don't you guys come over too?\"","She seemed afraid that Si Nian would refuse, so she looked at Zhou Zehan and said, \"Little boy, do you really want to eat it too? Do you want to come to Auntie's house?\"","Second Child hesitated for a moment, then took two steps back and said, \"I'm not going. I'm going to make zongzi with my mom tonight.\"","Although the cake looked delicious, Second Child was a person who kept his distance.","He would only go to the homes of people he was very familiar with, like Little Jiang's house.","Last time, this auntie had even called him a garbage picker. He didn't like her.","Si Nian also said, \"No thank you, Comrade Fang. I have many children, so it wouldn't be polite to intrude. You guys go ahead and eat. We still have to make zongzi tonight.\"","After saying that, she nodded slightly and stepped forward to open the door.","The two children skipped inside.","\"We're making zongzi!\"","\"Little Jiang, let me tell you, not only can I make zongzi, but I can also make dumplings! My mom taught me everything!\"","\"Second brother is so amazing! Second brother, teach me!\"","\"Okay, but you have to wash your hands first...\"","The voices of the two children gradually faded into the distance.","Fang Hui hadn't actually wanted to invite them to eat anyway. Seeing them head inside, she simply walked away.","Fang Bowen pulled his gaze away from Jiang Jiu and Zhou Zehan, who were roughhousing in the courtyard.","His lips were pressed into a tight line."]},{"number":338,"title":"Chapter 338: Watching a Movie Together","paragraphs":["Upon returning home, he finally couldn't help but ask.","\"Mom, are we going to make zongzi?\"","Fang Hui replied dismissively, \"Make what zongzi? How boring. What's the point of making them? Only poor people spend time doing this kind of thing. If you want to eat some, I'll buy them tomorrow.\"","Fang Bowen pressed his lips together and said, \"I don't.\"","Upon returning home, the Second Child couldn't help but ask Si Nian, \"Mom, do we get to eat cake on our birthdays?\"","After saying that, afraid that Si Nian would think he was still craving someone else's cake, he quickly explained, \"Mom, I don't want such an expensive cake for my birthday.\"","Si Nian didn't expect him to still be thinking about this. Seeing his slight envy, she rubbed his head and asked, \"Does Xiao Han want to celebrate his birthday?\"","The Second Child nodded immediately, \"I do!\"","He saw that when his classmates celebrated their birthdays, others would even give them gifts.","If he celebrated his birthday, surely someone would give him gifts too.","He said, \"My brother and I even have the same birthday, but we've never celebrated it.\"","Although he and his brother were three years apart, both of their birthdays fell on the first day of the sixth lunar month.","Si Nian had previously seen the three children's birthdays on the household register. The Second Child and the eldest child shared the same birthday, while Yaoyao's was a month later in July.","Given Zhou Yueshen's situation, he probably wasn't the type to celebrate birthdays either.","There weren't many families in the countryside who cared about the ritual of celebrating birthdays.","No wonder Xiao Han was so envious.","She said, \"When your birthday comes, Mom will make a cake for you and your brother.\"","\"When the time comes, you can invite your friends over to play and celebrate. Does Xiao Han have any friends he wants to invite?\"","Oh my gosh, Mom knows how to make cakes!","Zhou Zehan was incredibly excited. He immediately counted on his fingers, \"The first one is definitely Shitou, then little Jiang, and my classmates... Oh right, right, and Little Pig from the tube-shaped apartment building.\"","Jiang Jiu's ears twitched: The first one wasn't him, but Shitou.","He had heard the name Shitou from his second brother many times. Every time his second brother talked about his hometown, he would mention Shitou.","He said they used to go up the mountain together to chop wood, cut pig grass, and catch loaches and small crabs...","Furthermore, Shitou would help his second brother take care of their younger sister.","The younger sister also liked Shitou very much.","Their whole family liked Shitou.","Jiang Jiu felt a little sour in his heart.","Was Shitou more likable than him?","The others were fine, but Shitou was indeed a bit far away.","They couldn't exactly make him travel all that way just to celebrate a birthday.","Si Nian felt helpless but didn't want to ruin her son's excitement.","However, she hadn't seen that little guy in a long time either, and she actually missed him.","Aunt Zhang and her family had taken good care of her in the past.","Si Nian planned to share some zongzi with them to take back. Tomorrow happened to be a holiday, so she would go buy some clothes and toys for Shitou and her younger brothers, and then have her eldest brother deliver them.","Si Nian then looked at Zhou Zedong and asked, \"What about Xiao Dong? Who do you want to invite for your birthday?\"","She also wanted to know if Xiao Dong had any friends.","She had been worried that the eldest child still hadn't made any friends, but to her surprise, he asked, \"Mom, can I invite Brother Chen and Fatty?\"","His younger brother was inviting all students, but he didn't have any friends at school.","He was only somewhat familiar with Brother Chen and his crew.","But Brother Chen and the others were street punks, and he was afraid Si Nian wouldn't be happy about it.","Si Nian immediately smiled, \"Of course you can!\"","Saying this, she rubbed the two children's heads and let them go play on their own.","Si Nian first washed the bamboo leaves clean and soaked them in water.","Then she soaked the glutinous rice.","Soaking the glutinous rice required at least three hours, so she soaked it before starting to cook dinner.","Since it was a holiday, Si Nian told the children to go take a bath so they could wear new clothes tomorrow.","The Second Child immediately followed Jiang Jiu home to freeload off his bathtub.","He heard that Jiang Jiu's house even had a showerhead that could dispense hot water, which was super convenient.","Zhou Zedong stayed home to bathe his younger sister and then washed himself.","He wasn't as thick-skinned as his younger brother to go bathe at someone else's house.","Just as they finished cleaning up, Zhou Yueshen returned.","He was carrying a bag of sliced mutton in his hand.","He placed it in the kitchen, smelling strongly of mutton.","\"Our pig farm slaughtered a sheep today, so we can eat mutton tomorrow.\"","People in the countryside couldn't afford mutton. It was only after coming to the city that Zhou Yueshen noticed the people here ate mutton for the Dragon Boat Festival.","In just this short period, over a hundred sheep had been sent to their breeding farm to be slaughtered.","A perfectly good pig farm now reeked of mutton.","He heard that the slaughterhouse saw the holiday approaching and took the opportunity to raise their prices. It used to cost ten yuan to slaughter a sheep, but now they were charging twenty.","Since they did everything themselves at his pig farm, word somehow got out, and more and more people started coming.","He had to go over at three in the morning; there were still ten sheep left to slaughter.","It wasn't that they couldn't do it tomorrow morning, but everyone wanted to celebrate the holiday.","So tonight, he had no choice but to head over in the early hours.","Hearing this, Si Nian felt they were working too hard and said, \"Alright, I'll make some extra zongzi later for you to take and share with everyone.\"","As the boss's wife, she had to show some appreciation during the holiday.","Zhou Yueshen had already prepared bonuses for everyone. Hearing Si Nian's words, he didn't really want to trouble her.","However, seeing the children rubbing their hands together, already eager to make zongzi, he didn't say much more and gave a slight nod.","After everyone finished dinner, Si Nian saw that the glutinous rice was about done soaking and started making them.","Jiang Jiu clamored to make zongzi and refused to go home.","Hearing that Si Nian was making zongzi, Grandma Jiang and her whole family came over.","Jiang Wenqing was sitting next to his son, listening to him teach how to wrap zongzi.","Even when his son occasionally criticized him with a \"Dad is so dumb,\" he didn't get angry; instead, he laughed very happily.","Grandma Jiang looked like a wealthy lady, but surprisingly, she was quite skilled at making zongzi.","Si Nian thought about the elderly couple and figured Jiang Wenqing probably wasn't the type to cook either, so she suggested they come over the next morning for a mutton hotpot to celebrate the Dragon Boat Festival together.","Before Grandma Jiang could politely decline, Jiang Jiu happily said, \"Yes, yes! I want to celebrate the holiday with Second Brother!\"","\"Auntie, I want to sleep with Second Brother tonight!\"","In order to avoid going home tonight, the little guy had already changed into his pajamas. He even wore a nightcap on his head, making his fair little face look especially cute.","Si Nian was a bit of a sucker for good looks, and every time she saw Jiang Jiu, she felt this child was just too delicate and adorable.","If he were a girl, she would definitely snatch him up to be her son's wife.","Since Zhou Yueshen had to leave in the early hours of the morning, Si Nian shooed him off to bed.","Zhou Yueshen was initially reluctant. After all, with everyone busy here, how could he possibly sleep?","It wasn't until Si Nian secretly whispered in his ear that they would go watch a movie together tomorrow that he finally returned to his room.","Watch a movie?","He had never been to the movies with Si Nian.","He heard that this was something only couples deeply in love would do.","Zhou Yueshen immediately went to sleep.","Everyone worked busily for the evening and made two large pots of zongzi.","After giving some to the Jiang family, Si Nian packed a large bag for Zhou Yueshen to take to the factory, leaving the rest for their own family to eat."]},{"number":339,"title":"Chapter 339: The Dilemma of an Old Man","paragraphs":["After sending the kids, who were sleeping haphazardly on the sofa, off to bed, Si Nian was also exhausted. She washed up casually and lay down.","She had changed to a soft quilt today, which was light and comfortable. As soon as Si Nian lay down, she let out a comfortable sigh.","However, barely two seconds later, a pair of domineering and powerful arms wrapped around her waist. Si Nian then realized that Zhou Yueshen was actually awake.","She asked in surprise, \"Did I wake you?\"","Zhou Yueshen shook his head.","Then, under Si Nian's suspicious gaze, he said in a low voice, \"Nian Nian, what clothes should I wear tomorrow?\"","Si Nian was speechless.","Could it be that he hadn't slept until now because he was agonizing over what to wear to the movies?","Si Nian immediately felt both exasperated and amused. \"You can wear anything. We're just watching a movie, not walking a runway.\"","Zhou Yueshen didn't have a good sense of style, and he was afraid that if he dressed poorly, he would embarrass her.","After all, movie theaters were places for couples. People going on dates would definitely dress up carefully.","Although he had never been, back when he was in the military, whenever his comrades went on a date, they would shave a day in advance and buy new clothes.","They were very particular about it.","They said it was a sign of respect for the woman.","Even though they were married, he couldn't just be careless.","He was afraid Si Nian would think he didn't value her.","Seeing the genuine struggle in his eyes, Si Nian didn't want to make things difficult for him. \"How about this: I'll pick something out for you, and you can just change into it when you get back tomorrow.\"","Zhou Yueshen sighed, feeling that as a man in his thirties, he was somehow still so clumsy and foolish.","He didn't even know what to wear.","Si Nian stared at his expression and thought that this older man was actually quite cute.","Just because she mentioned going to watch a movie, he lost sleep over not knowing what to wear.","Anyone who didn't know better would think he had just started dating.","This adorable contrast really hit the spot for her, and she couldn't help but feel a surge of affection.","Self-consciousness really is a man's best dowry.","Si Nian's gaze shifted downward, landing perfectly on Zhou Yueshen's flawless jawline and rolling Adam's apple.","His bronze skin was full of masculine hormones.","This kind of skin tone was hard to pull off; after all, being too dark could ruin everything.","But Zhou Yueshen's tan was very even, not patchy.","His skin was also extremely firm and had a nice sheen to it.","Seduced by his masculine beauty, Si Nian swallowed hard. She deliberately patted his chest and kissed his chin. On the surface, she was comforting him, but in reality, she was taking advantage of him, as if their roles had been reversed.","Zhou Yueshen was amused by her.","His chest vibrated slightly, making the hand resting on it tingle.","Caught in the act, Si Nian flew into a flustered rage, raising her head to kiss Zhou Yueshen.","She blocked out his laughter.","Since she rarely took the initiative, Zhou Yueshen naturally wasn't going to let her off easy.","In a brief moment of distraction, Si Nian wondered if this man had been so worried that he got up to smoke a few cigarettes.","But there was no smell of smoke in the room—did he hide in the bathroom to smoke?","Zhou Yueshen never smoked in front of the children. When his nicotine craving hit, he always found a private place to deal with it.","He rarely let them see.","Given the nature of his work, it was impossible for him to completely avoid tobacco and alcohol.","However, he was a restrained man and not the type to get addicted.","After a long time, Zhou Yueshen released the now-weakened Si Nian. He pulled the blanket up to cover the scattered marks on her skin and pulled her into his embrace.","Si Nian drifted off to sleep in a daze, but she couldn't shake the feeling that she had gotten the short end of the stick.","She was the one who had tried to take advantage of the man, so how did she end up being the one devoured entirely?","Well, she had originally wanted Zhou Yueshen to go to sleep earlier, but instead of sleeping early, they ended up staying up late.","Zhou Yueshen didn't sleep at all. Once she fell asleep, he got up and prepared to head out.","Si Nian still remembered to remind him to take the zongzi. She grabbed onto him but was too tired to speak.","Zhou Yueshen looked down at his wife. After watching her for a while, he realized she was truly exhausted. Her fair, pinkish face still carried the afterglow of their intimacy. His throat couldn't help but bob, feeling dry and parched. With difficulty but great gentleness, he agreed.","He tucked the blanket around her before leaving.","Thinking about the upcoming movie date, Zhou Yueshen immediately got busy as soon as he arrived at work.","He moved faster than the others, but since there were more workers now, he didn't need to do much of the physical labor himself.","He just needed to keep an eye on things and manage them.","Today, as everyone arrived still yawning, they saw that he had already tossed a large bag of zongzi to Yu Dong to distribute, and had changed his clothes and started working with a cleaver.","Everyone was startled awake, all sleepiness vanishing instantly.","The miserable bleating of sheep rang out through the night, only ending when a white glow emerged on the horizon.","Zhou Yueshen tossed aside his blood-soaked sleeves and apron, squatting in front of the water pipe to wash his hands.","The bosses who received their meat bright and early were very happy. They even gave extra tips and gifted them zongzi.","Zhou Yueshen accepted a cigarette from them, exchanged a few polite pleasantries, and returned to his office.","Yu Dong walked over munching on two zongzi. \"Boss, do you have any white sugar? The zongzi sister-in-law made are fragrant, but they aren't sweet.\"","Zhou Yueshen had already changed his clothes and washed his hair under the tap, leaving it still slightly damp and gleaming.","Hearing this, he shot him a glance. \"No. Your sister-in-law doesn't like sweet zongzi.\"","Yu Dong nearly choked on his zongzi.","He peeled another zongzi and popped it into his mouth. As he was peeling a second one, Zhou Yueshen swept a glance over him.","Zhou Yueshen snatched the zongzi on the desk. Those were the ones he had saved for himself.","He had left in such a hurry that morning that he hadn't had time to eat.","He had chosen the two best-wrapped ones.","He could tell at a glance that Si Nian had wrapped them.","She was very deft and skillful.","After finishing his meal, Zhou Yueshen began grooming his stubble and hair.","A man's stubble grows fast; if not shaved for two days, it pops right out.","It made him look old.","As Zhou Yueshen shaved, he wondered if there were any hair salons on the way back where he could drop by for a haircut.","His hair grew fast.","However, he had gone a bit overboard last night, and he wondered if Si Nian was up yet.","Zhou Yueshen finished the two zongzi and dressed himself immaculately.","It made everyone else look rather sloppy in comparison.","Let alone everyone else, even Yu Dong felt something was off.","The way his boss was acting, it looked like he was going on a date.","Zhou Yueshen handed everyone a ten-yuan bonus and then dismissed them.","Yu Dong kept thinking about it, feeling that something good was going to happen today.","So, he brazenly followed Zhou Yueshen home.","Si Nian woke up early.","The children were wearing new clothes, and Zhou Zedong had even taken his younger brother to the barbershop at the entrance of Old East Street to get a haircut.","They looked much more handsome and neat.","Right now, they were sitting at the door, dipping their zongzi in white sugar and eating.","Da Huang also had two in its bowl.","It smacked its lips, seemingly finding them a bit sticky.","The early morning was filled with laughter and cheerful noise; it was incredibly lively.","Si Nian and Grandma Jiang were in the kitchen stewing lamb. They made a massive pot.","Lamb has a strong gamey smell, but with a little preparation, it becomes exceptionally fragrant.","With the addition of mint, the aroma was out of this world.","The entire street smelled of stewed lamb.","Lunch was served right as Zhou Yueshen arrived home.","Yu Dong managed to score a free lamb meal, praising Si Nian's cooking as being even better than a restaurant chef's.","After lunch, Fu Qianqian arrived, dressed to the nines and carrying a handbag.","Yu Dong, who had originally been sent away and made it to the door, circled back around and returned, claiming he forgot his keys and that his family had all gone back to their hometown.","Zhou Yueshen had pondered it all night, but he never could have imagined that the movie date Si Nian mentioned was actually a family outing.","It was one thing for the kids to be here.","But why were Yu Dong and Fu Qianqian here too?","The romantic date I had spent all night imagining was completely shattered, with two sons and a daughter wedged right between us..."]},{"number":340,"title":"Chapter 340: Quarrel","paragraphs":["Zhou Yueshen didn't even know what the movie was about. The whole time, he was either buying snacks for his daughter or taking his sons to the bathroom.","Si Nian and Fu Qianqian sat together with popcorn between them, eating and laughing.","Yu Dong had wanted to sit next to them, but on one side of Fu Qianqian was a couple he couldn't split up, and on the other was his sister-in-law, whom he didn't dare disturb.","So the seating order went: sister-in-law, Xiao Han, Xiao Dong, Yaoyao, the Boss... and finally himself at the very end.","It felt like he and Fu Qianqian were separated by thousands of miles.","Let alone chatting, they wouldn't even be able to hear each other if they shouted across the aisle.","After the movie, Si Nian and Fu Qianqian were still discussing the plot.","But a disagreement quickly turned into an argument.","The reason was surprisingly that Si Nian thought the male lead was too ugly and didn't deserve the female lead.","Fu Qianqian thought he looked fine.","So Si Nian criticized Fu Qianqian for having low standards.","And just like that, they started arguing.","The two men and three children watched helplessly as the two women stood in the middle of the street arguing.","Absolutely no one dared to interrupt.","In the end, Fu Qianqian stormed off in a huff.","Yu Dong hurriedly chased after her.","This left behind one man and three kids.","They were all carefully stealing glances at Si Nian's expression.","Even the usually energetic Second Child was as quiet as a mouse.","Si Nian considered herself to have a pretty gentle personality, but for some reason, talking to Fu Qianqian always easily led to bickering.","Seeing that things had quieted down, she subconsciously turned to look at Zhou Yueshen and the children.","She saw them staring at her, either in silence or with a bit of fear.","Si Nian was speechless. Had she gone too far just now?","Come to think of it, it wasn't strange that she thought the male lead was unattractive; after all, everyone has different aesthetic tastes.","There was really nothing to argue about.","She coughed awkwardly. Darlings, did Mommy scare you?","The kids looked at each other and then shook their heads vigorously.","Si Nian immediately looked at Zhou Yueshen, asking him with her eyes: Was I really that fierce just now?","Zhou Yueshen's eyes held a hint of helplessness. He stepped forward, put an arm around her, and gently changed the subject, It's fine. Are you hungry? Do you want to go get something to eat first?","The more Si Nian thought about it, the more she felt she had crossed a line. She shook her head and said, Was I really out of line just now? I even drove Fu Qianqian away in anger.","After all, every time Fu Qianqian came over, she would bring her so many nice things.","Even if she thought Fu Qianqian's taste was bad, she shouldn't have said it out loud.","Fu Qianqian had a proud personality to begin with; she was someone who couldn't stand being contradicted.","Si Nian pondered whether she should go to the department store to buy a gift and apologize to Fu Qianqian.","It was also a good time to buy some things to take back for the family.","On the other side, the furious Fu Qianqian was being comforted by Yu Dong.","She had been very angry at first, but after Yu Dong reasoned with her, she realized that she might have been a bit unreasonable herself.","Throwing a tantrum in front of Si Nian's entire family didn't give her any face.","A proud person like Si Nian must have felt deeply humiliated.","That must be why she got so angry and insulted her taste.","The more she thought about it, the more she regretted it. What if Si Nian refused to hang out with her anymore because of this?","She was still looking forward to eating her free mung bean cakes.","Thus, the haughty young lady felt a rare pang of guilt and dragged Yu Dong to buy a gift for Si Nian, saying she wanted to apologize.","Then, the two parties unexpectedly ran into each other again at the department store.","Both women were holding gifts, their faces full of awkwardness.","Fu Qianqian said, I'm sorry, I shouldn't have disrespected you in front of your whole family.","Si Nian said, I'm sorry, I shouldn't have said your taste is bad.","Si Nian and Fu Qianqian fell silent.","Everyone else also fell silent.","Although the process was a tiny bit awkward, the two quickly made up and went shopping arm in arm.","Since Zhou Yueshen and Yu Dong were following them, they didn't have to worry about the kids.","They dumped all the responsibilities onto the two men.","One moment a kid wanted ice cream, the next moment another needed to poop.","In the end, even the children's hands were full of shopping bags before the two women finally wrapped things up, still wanting more, and made plans for their next outing.","Who said women had poor stamina?","Yu Dong felt that this was even more exhausting than running a five-kilometer race with weights.","At any rate, it was nothing like the date he had imagined.","...","After Si Nian took the gifts home, she soon received a phone call from her parents.","This time, instead of writing a letter, they called her directly.","With them were Aunt Wang and Shitou, who was crying his eyes out.","Second Child fought to speak with Shitou. As the two little guys talked, they started crying again, acting as if they would never see each other again in this lifetime.","Watching them, Si Nian couldn't help but want to laugh.","Telephone bills were expensive. It didn't matter on her end, but if they kept talking, she feared Aunt Zhang would feel the pinch in her wallet.","The two children promised to write letters to each other in the future before finally handing the phone back to Si Nian.","Si Nian exchanged a few pleasantries with Aunt Zhang, assuring her that everything was fine, and then talked to her parents about her plans for the second half of the year.","She had successfully enrolled in school and now only needed to wait for the college entrance examination.","She asked about things at home, and her parents said everything was going well. They had saved quite a bit of money over the past six months, but they wanted to keep it for the children's future education.","Si Nian thought this was a waste and simply suggested that her parents and eldest brother come to the city to buy a house. Houses were cheap now, and in a decade or two, they would make a fortune from demolition and relocation compensations.","Why cling to that little bit of savings?","Keeping money and being reluctant to spend it was conservative, but it was also the most wasteful approach.","It just so happened that in the second half of the year, she could introduce her two younger brothers to study at the foreign language elementary school.","And if she went to college, her parents could also help her take care of the kids.","When her parents heard her telling them to buy a house, they were startled at first, thinking it was impossible.","How could the little bit of money they had saved afford a house?","Besides, living expenses in the city were so high.","Si Nian didn't force them to buy a house, but she urged them to bring their business to the city.","Opening a small storefront here would save time and effort compared to running along mountain roads every day to sell things back home, not to mention there would be much more foot traffic.","In short, she could only make the suggestion; whether they actually did it or not was up to them.","Everything comes with risks.","Si Nian couldn't make any guarantees either.","Although her current home was very large, the house was bought by Zhou Yueshen, so she couldn't possibly invite her whole family to come and live in the Zhou residence.","Even if Zhou Yueshen didn't say anything, the neighbors would surely gossip if they found out.","Her parents wouldn't feel at ease staying there either.","Therefore, Si Nian preferred that they work hard themselves to buy a house here.","Of course, not everyone pursued a life of wealth and glory.","If her parents just wanted to live an ordinary, peaceful life in the countryside, she wouldn't have any objections.","As long as you are comfortable with your life, it doesn't matter where you live.","If you focus too much on profit and success, you are destined to never be satisfied.","The holiday quickly passed.","Si Nian lay in her cozy bed and sighed up at the ceiling.","It was another day of not wanting to go to work.","But thinking about her salary of ninety yuan a month, she dragged herself up anyway.","Human beings die for wealth just as birds die for food.","She comforted herself by comparing it to her past life, where she worked from dawn till dusk, worked overtime, and attended social events, only to exhaust herself for a mere ten thousand yuan a month leaving her with only five thousand in savings after paying for housing."]},{"number":341,"title":"Chapter 341: He Is the Saddest Person","paragraphs":["Living a life like this, with a car and a house, was already incredibly comfortable.","She couldn't be too greedy.","Upon waking up, she first drank a cup of floral tea to nourish her skin and enhance her beauty.","Then she went downstairs to heat up some zongzi, boiled some sweet potatoes and eggs, and made a little white rice porridge.","A healthy and nutritious breakfast was complete.","Si Nian didn't eat out every day; most of the time, she was quite diligent.","If she woke up earlier than the children, she would make it herself; if she woke up late, the Eldest Child would make it.","The Eldest Child's breakfast-making skills were already perfected.","Si Nian recalled that when she went to the movies a few days ago, she saw Brother Chen and his friends squatting at the entrance of the cinema selling jianbing.","It was quite pitiful.","The Eldest Child had told her that these kids were orphans who had never been to school. As long as they could remember, they had made a living by picking up trash in the neighborhood.","Later, when the textile factory moved in, they would squat at the entrance every day, picking up fabric scraps to sell.","They didn't make much money, but it kept them from starving.","Now that they had started their jianbing business, they were actually making quite a bit of money.","Without any adults around, Si Nian initially worried that the kids, having tasted success, would squander their earnings on food and play.","But to her surprise, she saw them every day squatting in crowded places selling jianbing. When there was no one at the school, they went to the cinema entrance...","If someone tried to chase them away, they would just push their cart and run.","The kids ran fast and had never been caught.","Judging by the money her son brought back, they were definitely earning a lot.","If they didn't spend it recklessly, it would amount to a considerable sum.","There was still a lot of stewed mutton in the fridge. Because Zhou Yueshen had brought back too much, they hadn't finished it, so she froze it.","Eating mutton every day wasn't good; it caused internal heat.","So, Si Nian packed some in a bag along with some zongzi, and asked the Eldest Child to take it to the kids to try.","Since the Eldest Child considered them friends, they were definitely trustworthy.","Zhou Zedong took the mutton without refusing and rode his bicycle to deliver it.","Brother Chen and the others were currently preparing to set up their stall. They had a large pot filled with fermented dough. After some recipe development, they now had not only egg fillings, but also pork, chive fillings, and more... all placed in bowls and covered with a thin film.","Although the stall was an old one they rented, due to Zhou Zedong's requirements, they wiped it down every day until it was sparkling clean and reflective.","When Zhou Zedong came over carrying a bag of mutton and zongzi, it startled them.","\"Brother Dong, what is this?\" Fatty ran over first and took a sniff.","It smelled incredibly fragrant.","Zhou Zedong kept it brief. \"This is mutton my mom cooked. It's been frozen, so you just need to heat it up to eat. She told me to bring it to you.\"","Brother Chen and the others exchanged glances, their faces full of astonishment.","Before they could ask more, Zhou Zedong got on his bicycle, ready to leave.","After riding a couple of steps, he thought of something and backed up.","A hint of conflict appeared on his usually expressionless little face: \"Right, on the first of next month, come over to my house to play.\"","The three of them were still entirely focused on the mutton, so hearing this, they froze for a moment.","\"Go to Brother Dong's house to play?\"","\"Why?\"","\"Brother Dong's house is so big, I'm scared to go.\"","Brother Chen was also surprised, because previously Zhou Zedong hadn't allowed them near his mother.","Thinking of Zhou Zedong's big house, he lowered his eyes, a trace of envy flashing in them.","Seeing his two brothers looking overwhelmed by the favor, he rolled his eyes at them.","\"Useless. Who cares why we're going? Let's eat the mutton first.\"","The three had never eaten mutton before. As soon as they opened it, the perfectly marbled slices of mutton were embedded in the frozen fat, looking chewy and bouncy.","A rich meaty aroma flooded their noses, and all three couldn't help but swallow their saliva.","So much mutton, enough for them to eat their fill!","You have to know, they had seen people eating at restaurants, and in a one-yuan bowl of mutton noodles, there were only one or two paper-thin slices!","Brother Dong's mother was truly wealthy and generous.","The three were both envious and thrilled.","The Second Child was also thinking about his own birthday, starting to invite his good friends a month in advance.","Everything was going fine at first, and his classmates had all agreed to go to his house to play. But when he went to the tube-shaped apartment building, Zhou Zehan realized they were all ignoring him.","Now they only played with Fang Bowen.","They even called him stupid and said he loved to brag.","They told him that he and Jiang Jiu were no longer allowed to come to their apartment building.","If it was Da Zhuang who said this, Zhou Zehan definitely wouldn't care.","But being told this by people he considered good friends was hurtful.","He didn't understand. They were people who had hung out and played together every day, so how could they just suddenly say they hated him?","Was it just because he wasn't as great as Fang Bowen?","He had even confidently promised his mother that he was going to invite his friends from the apartment building to his house for his birthday.","Zhou Zehan was very upset. When he went home that night, he only ate three bowls of rice and stopped, saying he had no appetite.","\"......\"","These past few days, the Second Child didn't go to the apartment building to play, nor did he like going out much.","Jiang Jiu ran over to look for him to play, but was rejected, being told that playing with just the two of them wasn't fun.","Jiang Jiu looked at him for a while, hesitating to speak, but ultimately went home feeling disappointed.","Si Nian already felt that something was wrong with the Second Child, and seeing this, she couldn't help but focus her attention on him.","How did the little guy, who usually ran all over the place with Jiang Jiu right after school, suddenly become so quiet?","His mood seemed worse than before, and he wouldn't even go play when Jiang Jiu asked him to.","Si Nian was a bit curious about what had happened.","She asked, \"Xiao Han, what's wrong? Why haven't you gone out to play these past few days?\"","The Second Child sat on the threshold, propping his chin on his hands. He let out a heavy sigh like an old man and said listlessly, \"Little Pig and the others won't play with me anymore. They only play with Fang Bowen, and they called me a liar who loves to brag.\"","Zhou Zehan felt he hadn't bragged, because everything he said was true.","But everyone treated him like a liar and hated him.","After coming to the city, everything had been smooth sailing for him, and he got along well with everyone.","Those people wouldn't scold him either.","Back in the countryside, because his previous stepmother had poisoned him, everyone stayed far away from him and refused to play with him.","He only had one good friend, Shitou.","Therefore, when Zhou Zehan came to the city and was able to make friends, he cherished it exceptionally.","He just didn't expect the boat of friendship to capsize so quickly.","Not only did everyone stop playing with him, but they also insulted him.","After hearing this, Si Nian fell silent.","Then, she patted his head and gently taught him, \"Xiao Han, do you feel like you've lost a lot of things?\"","Zhou Zehan nodded.","\"Cherishing your friends is a good thing, but it's not right to only care about what you've lost while ignoring the people who are still by your side.\"","Zhou Zehan took his hands away and sat up straight. \"The people still by my side?\"","Si Nian said, \"Yes, besides Little Pig and the others, do you not have any other friends?\"","Zhou Zehan quickly shook his head and said, \"No, Mom, I still have Jiang Jiu and my classmates.\"","\"Exactly. Since you still have them, why be sad over the people who left you, and ignore the people who care about you?\" Si Nian said. \"There is a saying that you have to let go of something to gain something else. While you lost them, you also gained friends who trust you the most. The fact that they stopped playing with you after being provoked by a few words from someone else shows that they didn't trust you. But did Xiao Jiu and the others stop trusting you?\"","Zhou Zehan shook his head blankly.","\"Why are you wasting your tears on people who don't even trust you?\"","\"Mom...\" Zhou Zehan bit his lip.","\"Little Jiu came looking to play with you just now, but you ignored him because of those people who don't believe in you. He is the one who truly has a right to be hurt.\""]},{"number":342,"title":"Chapter 342: Shame","paragraphs":["\"Mom, I know I was wrong.\"","Si Nian said, \"Xiao Han, you don't need to tell me you were wrong. The person you should be apologizing to isn't me.\"","Zhou Zehan immediately lowered his head in shame.","Si Nian rubbed his head. \"Mom wants you to make friends, but I hope you make friends like Shitou and Xiao Jiu. This time you've seen Little Pig and the others for who they really are, so you won't suffer this kind of loss again.\"","Zhou Zehan nodded heavily and said, \"Mom, I'm going to find Xiao Jiang to apologize and tell him I'm sorry. I'll never play with Little Pig and his group again.\"","Si Nian patted his shoulder and watched him run out before returning to her room to work on her test papers.","No matter how much authority she had in front of the children, she still had to bow her head to the test papers.","Jiang Jiu was locking himself in his room, secretly grieving.","Ever since Little Pig and the others stopped playing with his second brother, his second brother hadn't taken him out to play for days.","Actually, Jiang Jiu had never really liked the people in the tube-shaped apartment building, because they had always ostracized him and wouldn't let him go over there.","It was only because his second brother took him there that he played with Little Pig and the others.","Whenever they bought food, they would share it with Little Pig and the rest.","Who knew that Little Pig and the others would turn on them so quickly.","He didn't like Little Pig and the others, so he wasn't sad about them at all.","He felt that as long as his second brother played with him, everything was fine.","Who would have thought his second brother would be so upset over Little Pig and the others.","And that he would stop playing with him, too.","Jiang Jiu felt very helpless and didn't know what to do.","He could only secretly wipe his tears at home.","\"Xiao Jiang, Xiao Jiang, are you home?\" Zhou Zehan's loud voice rang out from downstairs.","Jiang Jiu thought he was hallucinating. He quickly got up, ran to the window, and pushed it open on his tiptoes.","He blinked and saw his second brother standing at his door, talking to his grandmother.","Forgetting his sadness, he immediately shouted back, \"Second Brother, Second Brother, I'm home!\"","With that, he wiped his tears and snot, and ran downstairs in his slippers, his footsteps thumping.","\"Second Brother, you're looking for me.\" He squeezed in front of his grandmother and asked Zhou Zehan with bright eyes.","Zhou Zehan nodded. He dug around in his pants pocket, pulled out a few dimes, and said, \"Xiao Jiang, let's go buy some pancakes. Let's get egg pancakes.\"","Jiang Jiu's eyes lit up. He hurriedly turned around to run back and change his shoes, not forgetting to tell Zhou Zehan, \"Second Brother, wait for me right there. I'll change my shoes right away.\"","After saying that, he ran out before his shoes were even put on properly, telling Grandma Jiang that they were going to buy egg pancakes.","Seeing her grandson suddenly so happy, Grandma Jiang was pleased too. She told them to walk slowly and watch out for cars.","The two walked out of the Jiang family's gate, and Zhou Zehan suddenly stopped.","Under Jiang Jiu's confused gaze, he crouched down to tie his shoelaces for him.","\"There. Xiao Jiang, next time you have to remember to tie your shoelaces, or you'll trip and fall.\"","Zhou Zehan clapped his hands and said with a smile.","Jiang Jiu looked at him with a worried face. \"Second Brother, are you not sad anymore?\"","Zhou Zehan paused, then shook his head and said, \"I'm not sad anymore. Mom said that Little Pig and the others didn't trust me, so they aren't friends worth keeping. I'll never play with them again.\"","After saying that, he added guiltily, \"Xiao Jiang, please don't be mad at me. I know I was wrong. I shouldn't have stopped playing with you just because of Little Pig and the others.\"","\"I'll buy you two pan-fried pancakes as an apology, okay?\"","Jiang Jiu immediately agreed happily, \"Okay, okay!\"","\"Then let's go buy pancakes.\"","Children's anger comes fast and goes fast. In a moment, they were holding hands and skipping away to buy pancakes.","However, they were too late; the pancake stall had already closed for the day.","The two of them didn't get to eat any.","Zhou Zehan felt a little sad, blaming himself.","Seeing Jiang Jiu's face full of disappointment, he made up his mind to go home tonight and learn how to make pancakes from his older brother.","Tomorrow, he would make pancakes himself to apologize to Xiao Jiang.","Acting on his words, as soon as he got home, Zhou Zehan pestered his brother, saying he wanted to learn how to make pancakes.","Zhou Zedong didn't want to bother with him at first, feeling that his younger brother was too clumsy for such delicate work.","He figured it was just a passing whim.","But annoyed by his constant pestering, he wrote down a recipe for him to learn by himself.","His thought was that if his brother couldn't make it even with the recipe, he simply had no talent for it.","He would probably give up after trying twice.","Who knew that his younger brother would stay in the kitchen for over an hour without coming out.","He couldn't help but worry, so he hurried in to check.","Only to see his brother holding a pitch-black pancake and eating it.","Seeing him come in, he even handed the burnt, black pancake over and said, \"Brother, try this. I feel like it's a bit different from yours. It doesn't smell as good...\"","Zhou Zedong: \"...\"","Where on earth did his brother get the confidence to compare this charred, black mess with his own beautiful egg pancakes?","When Si Nian went downstairs, she saw her daughter sitting in the living room watching TV.","There was a faint smell of egg pancakes coming from the kitchen.","She walked over and saw the two brothers making pancakes.","It was a scene of one calmly teaching while the other was in a frantic rush.","She smiled and didn't disturb them.","After countless attempts throughout the evening, Second Child finally succeeded.","However, he couldn't eat anymore that night. Because he couldn't bear to waste food, all the failed attempts had gone into his stomach.","When Zhou Yueshen returned home that night, he was a little surprised to see that the most gluttonous Second Child wasn't at the dinner table.","\"Where is Xiao Han?\"","Si Nian told him about what happened in the afternoon.","Zhou Yueshen was silent for a moment.","Zhou Zedong also couldn't understand why his brother was so upset for so long just because someone wouldn't play with him.","He didn't care at all about what outsiders thought of him.","Nor did he like them.","So he couldn't understand it.","When it was time for bed that night, Si Nian talked to Zhou Yueshen about the two boys' upcoming birthdays.","She asked if he would have time.","Zhou Yueshen hadn't really thought about celebrating birthdays, as he had never celebrated his own growing up, but hearing it was for the two boys, he became a bit more serious.","\"I probably won't have time during the day, but I'll try my best to come back early in the evening.\"","Si Nian didn't make things difficult for him. Although the children were important, without Zhou Yueshen's day-and-night hard work, how could they live such a stable and comfortable life?","Showing a rare moment of tender affection, she massaged Zhou Yueshen's shoulders and said, \"You've been working so hard expanding the breeding farm lately. Let me give you a massage as a reward.\"","After she previously discovered that the area where Zhou Yueshen's farm was located would be demolished, she had found an opportunity to suggest that he expand it.","But she had only mentioned it casually. At the time, she said that while delivering food, she had heard someone was going to build a factory there. If the land next to them was bought for a factory, it would definitely be too noisy being so close, which would affect their pig farming.","She hadn't expected Zhou Yueshen to take it to heart.","Ever since returning from the Northwest, he had started expanding, finding people to buy up the nearby land for the expansion.","Previously, when Zhou Yueshen was in the village, his business covered the surrounding villages and neighboring counties. He had some partnerships in the city, but because it was too far and transportation was troublesome, there weren't many partners.","But after coming to the city, thanks to Yu Dong's wide network of connections, they were now partnering with many markets, restaurants, and cafeterias."]},{"number":343,"title":"Chapter 343: Lin Sisi Released from Prison","paragraphs":["With increased traffic came a natural increase in demand.","Even if Zhou Yueshen didn't expand, others would step in to snatch the business.","Why not make the money?","However, these things couldn't be done just on a whim; Zhou Yueshen had also spent a long time preparing.","The expansion wasn't even fully completed yet.","It would require a massive amount of ongoing investment.","Si Nian had originally wanted to give the man a massage, but who knew this older man's muscles would be as hard as rocks? After pressing for just a little while, her fingers ached terribly.","She pouted and was just about to give up when the man pulled her into his arms.","Si Nian met his gaze. Seeing that he was about to lean in for a kiss, her breath hitched. Aren't you tired?","He was a thirty-year-old man who worked from dawn to dusk every day. How could he still think about that every single night?","Ever since they returned from the Northwest, barely a day had gone by without it.","Si Nian was genuinely worried she was going to suffer from kidney deficiency.","She wasn't even twenty yet and was already facing kidney deficiency, this couldn't go on.","Zhou Yueshen wrapped his arms around Si Nian, tucked a lock of her beautiful black hair behind her ear, and lowered his head to kiss her. His deep voice rang in her ear, Didn't you say this was a reward?","I can't massage you anymore, who told your muscles to be like stones? Si Nian used one hand to block his face, shrinking her neck back from the ticklish sensation.","Si Nian was speechless. Did this older man have no sense of shame anymore?","Where did the man who used to blush at the slightest touch go?","That night, Si Nian finally understood.","You just couldn't spoil a man.","Give him an inch, and he'll take a mile.","He used to be such a clean-living, ascetic, and good man.","Yet, she had classes the next day and had to pretend that nothing had happened.","But riding her bicycle was out of the question.","Zhou Yueshen seemed a bit guilty as well. The next day, he waited to drive her to school before leaving.","Si Nian couldn't be bothered to pay attention to him.","In early June, there was one piece of good news and one piece of bad news.","The good news was that the two children were about to celebrate their first birthdays.","The bad news was that Lin Sisi was about to be released from prison.","Si Nian heard from Fu Qianqian that Lin Sisi was also going to take the college entrance examination.","Originally, her parents had planned to have her brother divorce Lin Sisi. However, Si's Mother blocked them in front of the entire military compound, begging them not to tell Lin Sisi about it. She promised that once Lin Sisi took the college entrance exam, the Si family would agree to the divorce.","Mr. and Mrs. Fu weren't willing at first, but passersby had overheard everything. If they forced a divorce at such a critical time, it would look like they were kicking the Si family while they were down. If Lin Sisi performed poorly on her exams because of it, the Fu family would be blamed as the culprits.","With their strong sense of morality, Mr. and Mrs. Fu had no choice but to agree.","Although they disliked Lin Sisi, getting divorced right after being released from prison would indeed be a massive shock to her.","If a divorce really caused Lin Sisi to fail the college entrance exam, the two elders would feel uneasy about it.","They didn't want to owe the Si family anything.","They were going to divorce sooner or later, anyway.","As for Fu Yang, ever since he returned, he had buried himself in military training. Rumor had it that the trip to the Northwest had dealt him a heavy blow.","Although he was excellent in the military, part of it was due to his father being a commander. No one dared to offend him, and he was even given priority protection during dangerous missions.","But after going to the Northwest, he had almost lost his life.","Fu Yang seemed to have realized just how blessed his previous living environment had been.","Now, he was trying to step out of his comfort zone.","As for Lin Sisi, the wife who went to prison right after marrying into the family, he had long forgotten about her.","Si Nian knew that Lin Sisi was bound to be released, but she hadn't expected it to be this soon.","It was the same in the book. After Lin Sisi married Fu Yang, she studied hard and took the college entrance exam.","She successfully got into a top-tier university.","She won the approval of everyone in the military compound.","College students were highly sought after in this era.","Coupled with her marriage to Fu Yang, it was no exaggeration to say she had reached the pinnacle of life.","Her future after that was smooth sailing, like a fish in water.","However, with so many things happening this time, Lin Sisi hadn't had the chance to lay a solid foundation.","She had also lost all her dignity.","She had also heard that Si's Father and Si's Mother were in the middle of a messy divorce.","Their home was in complete chaos, so they had no time to bother her, which Si Nian was more than happy to see.","But it seemed Lin Sisi wasn't completely stupid. She knew that the only way to salvage her future now was to get into college.","Si Nian just didn't know what kind of tricks she would pull next.","On the day of her release, only Zhang Cuimei went to pick her up.","Lin Sisi learned from Zhang Cuimei that her father no longer cared about his biological daughter because of Si Nian.","She still found it hard to believe that he wouldn't even come to pick her up upon her release.","Her resentment toward Si Nian deepened. She spoke so loftily about cutting ties with the Si family, yet secretly she was driving a wedge between father and daughter.","Originally, Lin Sisi thought Si's Father just felt a bit guilty toward Si Nian. She figured that no matter how guilty he felt, she was his biological daughter, so he definitely wouldn't side with Si Nian.","She never expected that after less than a year in prison, her father would completely forget his own flesh and blood.","She was his only biological child!","Lin Sisi pinned all the blame on Si Nian.","Remembering that Si Nian had said she was going to take the college entrance exam, Lin Sisi quickly asked Zhang Cuimei about it.","Zhang Cuimei sneered, Don't worry, I've already spoken to their teachers. They won't accept her! The school doesn't want her, so she has no right to take the college entrance exam!"]},{"number":344,"title":"Chapter 344: Genius Cultivation Class","paragraphs":["Zhang Cuimei shared her daughter's thoughts. For a time, she also believed that Si Nian had been badmouthing them to her husband behind their backs, which led to their family's current predicament.","She hated Si Nian to death in her heart.","So how could she possibly let Si Nian take the college entrance examination?","It just so happened that she had some connections with the teachers at No. 1 High School, and with just a few words, she got it sorted out.","Now, all she had to do was wait for her daughter to take the college entrance exam and become a university student.","There was no way her husband would give up a daughter with a bright future to care about an adopted daughter with no blood ties.","Over at the school.","Si Nian sneezed twice in a row.","She rubbed her nose, wondering who was gossiping about her behind her back again.","\"Teacher Si, this is the school's list for the next batch of contestants. The deputy director just asked me to give it to you and said you'll be their English teacher.\"","Si Nian took a look and saw her own son's name right in the first row.","She was a bit surprised. Looking further down, there were actually about a dozen people in total.","Among them was Fang Bowen's name.","\"This many people?\"","Wang Xiaoli said, \"You probably don't know yet. These children all have IQs over 140. Because they differ so much from the other students in their regular classes, some parents requested that they skip grades. After consideration by the principal and the school leaders, they plan to establish a genius cultivation class. As long as they meet the requirements in this class, they can directly skip a grade or be recommended for admission to middle school.\"","\"You should have heard earlier that a seven-year-old little genius joined our fourth grade. This child is excellent in every aspect and learns incredibly fast. He already knows everything the teachers teach. Now his parents are demanding he go straight to the fifth grade.\"","\"Perhaps because other students felt demoralized, some parents also developed a sense of competition. Unwilling to let their children study for so many years, they proposed skipping grades. The principal took their feedback, and after recommendations from various teachers, this class was formed.\"","\"This class will be led by the best teachers in our school, and they will have priority in participating in future city-wide competitions. Not only that, but the school has also invited professor-level teachers to personally teach these children... You are the best English teacher in our school besides Teacher Wu, so naturally, you are included.\"","Grade skipping wasn't something unheard of.","However, it was truly rare for one school to have so many.","It was likely that Fang Bowen's situation had sparked this competitive mentality.","Still, it wasn't necessarily a bad thing.","Eldest Child learned fast and could already grasp middle school knowledge, so there was no need for him to stay cooped up in elementary school.","Because this level of knowledge offered him no room for progress.","The school had acted quickly too; the child hadn't been here long, and they immediately took measures when the situation arose.","This would not only organize these exceptional children but also provide them with a better education.","Of course, this didn't mean it was unfair to the other students; it was just that ordinary teaching methods were no longer suitable for these children.","The principal understood this principle well, hence the measures taken.","Gathering children of similarly high levels together might yield better results.","\"This competition is a team event, involving not only our city but also other major cities. You surely know about Jing City, a gathering place for geniuses. I heard this competition is held specifically for these little geniuses. Not only can they win prize money, but they might also get recommended for admission to Peking University or Tsinghua University.\"","Speaking of this, the teacher clicked her tongue in praise, \"I saw it, your son's name is in there too. You must seize this great opportunity.\"","Si Nian nodded and didn't say much.","Although it sounded very tempting, the corresponding pressure would also be immense.","After all, the world is vast and full of wonders. Geniuses are rare, but they do exist.","Just the boy next door, Fang Bowen, being only seven years old, was already quite astonishing.","Not to mention those coming from other cities.","No wonder the school was focusing so much on cultivating these children this time. It wasn't just to make a name for the school, but also to secure better futures for the kids.","She agreed without hesitation.","She wouldn't be staying for long. If she could really guide this batch of students, then the knowledge she had acquired in her previous life would be put to good use.","On the other side.","Lin Sisi had already entered No. 1 High School and started her studies.","Even while in prison, she had studied very hard.","But Lin Sisi knew that such grades were far from enough to get her into a prestigious university.","She was now thankful for her knowledge and experience from her previous life, which let her know exactly what to do to best suit herself.","Learning these subjects didn't seem that difficult anymore.","Although the people in the family compound still avoided her like the plague, Lin Sisi believed that as long as she got into a prestigious university, all those judgmental looks would vanish.","At the same time, she was secretly having people look into news about Si Nian.","She originally thought that since Si Nian was rejected by No. 1 High School, it would be difficult for her to take the college entrance exam.","But unexpectedly, she had actually gotten into No. 2 High School.","She hadn't given up and was still planning to take the college entrance exam.","Lin Sisi's expression turned somewhat ugly.","The thing she worried about the most had still happened...","...","The news about the genius cultivation class was finalized quickly.","Every class teacher was given one nomination spot.","Of course, parental consent was required. After all, skipping grades placed a huge amount of pressure on any student.","Most parents of highly excelling students were happy to agree, as the teachers for the genius cultivation class were the best in the school.","Not only that, the school also invited two professors specifically to guide these students.","Many parents were extremely envious, which also stirred up the competitive spirit among some students.","However, the requirements to enter this class were exceptionally high. Only children who were at the top of their class in every subject and could score an IQ of 130 or above on the test had a chance.","Although an internal list had already been released, for the sake of fairness, the school also gave others a chance to take the test.","All children wanting to enter the genius cultivation class had to undergo the test first.","Zhou Zedong had little interest in the genius cultivation class, but upon hearing that he could skip grades and go straight to middle school or high school, he agreed without hesitation.","He felt that continuing in his current class like this was just a waste of time.","He had this idea ever since he heard that Fang Bowen from next door had skipped three grades straight into the fourth grade.","He wanted to finish his studies earlier so that he could start making money.","The test was held the next day.","Since it was held at their own school, Si Nian could personally accompany her son to take the test.","Soon, a group of participating children arrived.","The list recommended a dozen or so of the more outstanding students in the school.","However, there were fifty or sixty kids who showed up for the test.","It seemed many parents wanted their children to enter this class and enjoy the priority treatment.","Si Nian also saw Fang Hui from next door leading Fang Bowen, which wasn't surprising at all.","She glanced over the others and spotted several familiar faces.","For example, Chu Xiang'er, Li Youcai...","Class Four alone had three participants.","And the invigilators this time were not teachers, but the two professors invited by the school.","Rumor had it that the school had spent a fortune to hire them.","The first round of the test was very simple; there was only one question.","But no one knew what the question was.","Soon, parents led their children inside one after another, only to walk back out looking disappointed.","Fang Hui was right in front of them.","When Fang Bowen came out, a proud look was plastered across her face.","Catching sight of Si Nian, she smiled and said, Teacher Si, you brought your son to try out for this class too? Don't be nervous, though. My Bowen said it really isn't that difficult.","With that, she took her son's hand and walked away, basking in the envious gazes of the crowd.","Si Nian couldn't even be bothered to acknowledge her.","Soon, it was Zhou Zedong's turn."]},{"number":345,"title":"Chapter 345: Possibly Even More Skilled Than Him","paragraphs":["In less than a minute, he walked out.","Si Nian didn't know what the test was about, but seeing him finish so quickly made her a bit worried. \"How was it? Was it difficult?\"","Zhou Zedong shook his head and said, \"Mom, it wasn't hard.\"","When he went in, the two professors only asked him one question. He answered it correctly without even having to think, and then he passed.","Si Nian breathed a sigh of relief.","The first round took an entire morning. Out of about fifty students, only twenty remained.","Si Nian had a class to teach in the afternoon, so she asked Wang Xiaoli to help keep an eye on things.","Wang Xiaoli carried Yaoyao to the competition venue.","A group of children was lining up to go inside.","Seeing her brother, Yaoyao immediately gestured that she wanted to be put down.","Wang Xiaoli knew Zhou Zedong was Yaoyao's brother, so she let her go over to play. Just as she was about to follow, she was held back by a parent. \"Oh, if it isn't Teacher Wang! Thanks to your recommendation, my son was able to participate in this competition. If he gets into the genius cultivation class, I will definitely have to thank you properly.\"","Wang Xiaoli saw that it was the parent of one of her students and immediately smiled and exchanged pleasantries.","Having someone from her own class make it into the genius cultivation class would be a matter of great pride for her as well.","After exchanging just a few words, she turned her head, only to find Yaoyao was gone.","Meanwhile, the students had all lined up and entered the classroom.","Yaoyao followed behind them, but even standing on her tiptoes, she couldn't see her brother.","She had clearly just seen him.","As soon as she was squeezed inside, she heard the teacher telling the children to find a seat, sit nicely, and not run around.","She wasn't much taller than the desks. She stood there blankly for a moment, and seeing everyone else sit down, she mimicked them and found a seat for herself.","She sat at the desk with her little arms crossed, her back perfectly straight, and her chin lifted—a very proper posture.","Zhou Zedong was checking his paper and pen when he heard people murmuring, \"Isn't that Teacher Si's daughter? How did she get in here?\"","\"Is she taking the test too?\"","\"No way, isn't she only three years old?\"","The students didn't dare to speak up loudly. The professors were older and gave off a strong sense of authority, so they only whispered.","If Zhou Zedong hadn't been sitting close by, he wouldn't have heard them. He looked up and saw that in the very first seat of the first row, his little sister was sitting perfectly upright with her small chest puffed out.","Zhou Zedong: \"...\"","Just as he was about to speak, the two professors at the front spoke up: \"Quiet, quiet! No talking!\"","It was the professor in the front who spoke.","Everyone immediately shut their mouths.","They had come to participate in this competition specifically for the reputation of these two professors.","Their families had repeatedly emphasized that they needed to behave well.","So, they instantly fell silent.","The two professors swept their gazes across the room. Seeing that everyone was present, they began handing out the test papers.","Just as the papers were distributed, a milky, childish voice rang out: \"Old Teacher, is this for me?\"","Only then did the two professors notice that right under their noses sat a tiny little munchkin.","Yaoyao held up a large test paper to show them.","The two of them adjusted their glasses and looked closely. Something wasn't right.","Why was this child so small?","Was this child here during the morning assessment?","He remembered there were a few seven or eight-year-old children in this batch of candidates.","But the little bean in front of them looked no more than two or three years old.","However, seeing her perfectly straight posture, the old professor felt a bit bewildered for a moment. He let out a sound of surprise, \"Little girl, where did you come from? Whose child is this?\"","Yaoyao tilted her head and answered somewhat blankly, \"Old Teacher, I am my mommy's child.\"","Someone in the room let out a snicker.","Zhou Zedong hurriedly stood up and said, \"Teacher, she is my little sister.\"","Although he was very confused—shouldn't his sister be with their mom right now? Why was she here?","But to prevent any accidents, he needed to get her out of there first. Zhou Zedong asked, \"My sister might have walked into the wrong classroom. I'm sorry, Teacher, may I escort my sister out first?\"","The old professor looked at the little dumpling in front of him, then looked at Zhou Zedong. He still had some impression of this boy; when he came in that morning, he had answered the question they gave him in just a few seconds.","He was one of the fastest to answer among all the participants today.","Hearing that this was his little sister, the professor was a bit surprised, but he still said, \"No, the exam is about to start. No one is allowed to leave. Let your sister sit here for now; her parents can come and pick her up later.\"","After saying that, he patted the little girl who was staring at him with her big, blinking eyes, thinking to himself that this child was absolutely adorable.","His voice softened by a few degrees: \"Little one, do you want to wait here until your brother finishes his exam?\"","Yaoyao tilted her head and asked, \"Can't Yaoyao take the test?\"","The old professor was amused by the little one's well-behaved demeanor and laughed heartily. \"Of course not. You're still too young. You have to grow at least this tall and know how to read before you can participate in the competition.\"","The surrounding children snickered out loud.","Yaoyao pouted her lips and said unhappily, \"I know a lot of words, and I can also sing and draw~\"","The old professor burst into laughter and teased, \"Oh my, that's quite impressive! You're such a capable little kid.\"","The surrounding children laughed even louder.","Yaoyao's appearance had eased everyone's nervous tension.","Being laughed at, the little girl's face flushed red. Extremely upset, she emphasized angrily, \"I really do know how to read! I know a lot of words.\"","\"Alright, alright, the teacher knows. You sit nicely and wait quietly for your brother to take his exam. No making noise, okay? Otherwise, the teacher will have to send you out.\"","Yaoyao pouted her lips high. She knew that the Old Teacher in front of her didn't believe her at all.","She wanted to prove herself.","So, she pointed her little finger at the fountain pen in the old professor's breast pocket and said, \"Then, Old Teacher, let me play with this.\"","The old professor had a granddaughter of his own and had little resistance against cute little girls. Without hesitation, he handed her the expensive fountain pen from his pocket to play with.","Only then did he turn a stern gaze toward the others and continue distributing the test papers for the exam.","Yaoyao scribbled and drew on the test paper. She thought these questions were really simple—not nearly as hard as the ones her brother read at home.","If she solved them, everyone wouldn't laugh at her anymore.","She looked left and right, mimicking the surrounding students by pretending to read the test paper seriously.","She even nodded slightly, as if she already knew how to do it.","Her little act was incredibly amusing.","Seeing that she wasn't talking, the two professors didn't chase her out.","They actually found the little girl quite entertaining.","Everyone else also shifted their attention away. Because Si Nian often brought Yaoyao to class, and sometimes other teachers who helped watch her would bring her into their classrooms, several of the children taking the exam had seen Yaoyao before and didn't find it particularly strange.","They sat up straight and focused on their own work.","Only Fang Bowen, sitting not far away, stared at Yaoyao for quite a while.","Others might not know, but he did.","Zhou Zehan's little sister was very good at English—perhaps even better than him.","..."]},{"number":346,"title":"Chapter 346: Taken by Surprise","paragraphs":["Yaoyao was holding the teacher's fountain pen, scribbling and drawing. However, before she could finish a few questions, Teacher Wang came looking for her.","Teacher Wang had searched all around outside, worried that the child might have run off to play by herself.","Turning her head, she spotted the little girl sitting inside the examination classroom.","Teacher Wang was completely dumbfounded.","Feeling incredibly awkward, she hurriedly knocked on the classroom door and apologized to the two professors.","The two professors were easygoing; seeing that an adult had arrived, they safely handed the child over to her.","Yaoyao really wanted to finish writing before leaving, but seeing Teacher Wang's urgent gaze, she knew this was not a place she could stay.","Mommy had said she needed to listen to her teachers and not cause trouble for them.","She had no choice but to put down the pen, drooping her little head in disappointment, and was led away by Wang Xiaoli, looking back with every step.","The old professor picked up the fountain pen left on the desk, capped it, and tucked it securely into his breast pocket.","Just as he was about to turn around, he noticed that the test paper was not filled with random scribbles, but rather several strings of crooked numbers.","He let out a surprised huh and picked it up to take a closer look.","What he saw gave him quite a start.","These were actually not scribbles at all, but the answers to the math problems.","And the answers were correct.","In disbelief, the old professor continued reading down the page, seeing that the multiple-choice questions a, b, c, and d were all filled out.","The letters a, b, c, and d were written much more neatly than the numbers.","It certainly did not look like something a three-year-old child could write.","The ink was not yet dry; it was clearly written with his own fountain pen.","However, since the child did not really know how to use a fountain pen, there were ink smudges everywhere.","The old professor could hardly conceal his astonishment.","Getting these few questions right was not particularly difficult.","But for a child who was only three or four years old, it was highly unusual.","These were not standard elementary school math problems; they were questions the professors had designed themselves based on the levels of the participating children.","Some of them might even stump junior high or high school students.","Was this child simply unbelievable?","He quickly handed it to the other professor. Lao Zhu, take a look at what this child did.","The other man took it, puzzled, but was equally shocked after looking at it.","The two huddled together, muttering to themselves for a long time, only snapping out of it when a child came up to hand in their paper.","The child handing in the paper was none other than the boy the little girl had called her brother.","Zhou Zedong handed in his test paper and was about to leave when the two men called out to him.","The old professor asked in surprise, Student Zhou Zedong, was that child just now your sister? Your biological sister?","Zhou Zedong stopped, turned to look at the two men, and said, She is my sister.","The two old professors exchanged a glance, as if they had understood something.","They immediately broke into bright smiles. Student Zhou Zedong, for the next examination, could you bring your sister over for us to see?","Zhou Zedong looked at them suspiciously. Noticing the test paper in their hands, he seemed to realize something. He withdrew his gaze and said, I have to ask my mom about this.","The two old professors immediately urged him to go ask his mom.","They said that since his sister was young and highly gifted, she needed to be nurtured from an early age.","Hearing this, Zhou Zedong's heart stirred.","If that was the case, could his sister be like Fang Bowen, starting school at a very young age, and be in the fourth grade by the time she was his younger brother's age?","Despite these thoughts, Zhou Zedong kept a straight face and walked out calmly.","In the afternoon, Si Nian heard from Teacher Wang that Yaoyao had accidentally wandered into the examination classroom for the genius cultivation class. However, the two professors were not angry and had a very good attitude, saying that Yaoyao was very likable.","Si Nian wondered to herself if Yaoyao had seen Xiaodong in the classroom and followed him inside.","Fortunately, she didn't cause any trouble.","Since they were going back relatively late in the afternoon, Si Nian decided to wait for her two sons to go home together.","She happened to run into Grandma Jiang, who was there to pick up her grandson.","They exchanged a few pleasantries, and then Zhou Zedong, Zhou Zehan, and Jiang Jiu came over pushing their bicycles.","Grandma Jiang, standing nearby, saw Zhou Zedong and asked curiously, Xiaodong, I heard you're participating in the examination for that genius cultivation class, right? How did it go? Was it very hard?","Zhou Zedong shook his head and said, Grandma Jiang, it wasn't hard.","Grandma Jiang sighed in amazement. She had heard this child was smart, but she didn't expect him to be this incredible.","If her own grandson had such good grades, she would wake up laughing from her dreams.","Unfortunately, her grandson didn't seem to have any talent for studying, and his grades were truly mediocre.","Otherwise, she would have been very tempted by this genius cultivation class and would have loved to send her grandson there.","Little Niannian, your Xiaodong is really something else. No wonder I even heard my son say his team leader wants to take your son in. Unlike our Xiaojiu, who can barely pass his exams. I really want to ask your Xiaodong to help tutor him.","Grandma Jiang felt a bit frustrated at her grandson's failure to meet expectations.","Si Nian smiled and rubbed Zhou Zedong's head. Auntie Jiang, you're exaggerating. Xiaojiu is also very smart; he just might not have his heart set on studying. Look at my Xiaohan, isn't he the same?","If he could be tutored, I would have had Xiaodong teach him a long time ago.","Hearing this, Grandma Jiang felt it made sense.","She had heard that the Second Child's grades were about the same as her own grandson's anyway.","Zhou Zedong looked at his younger brother and Jiang Jiu, withdrew his gaze, and said, Mom, our professor said he wants you to bring my sister to take the examination. The professor said she is very smart and needs to be nurtured from an early age.","Si Nian froze. What?","Zhou Zedong recounted what had happened that afternoon.","Si Nian had heard from Wang Xiaoli about her daughter entering the classroom.","But she hadn't mentioned any of this.","For a moment, she and Grandma Jiang just stared at each other wide-eyed.","Jiang Jiu and the Second Child also exchanged a glance.","What?","Their sister could also get into the genius cultivation class?","If their sister graduated, would they still be in elementary school?","...","Si Nian hadn't expected this to happen. Ever since she discovered Yaoyao's talent, she knew this child was definitely as extraordinary as Zhou Zedong.","At first, she was a bit worried.","But after hearing Zhou Yueshen's unfazed tone, she stopped minding it.","She figured that since Yaoyao was still young and not yet in school, even if she was unbelievably smart, only they would know about it for now.","When she started first grade and revealed her talent, Si Nian could just say she taught her herself. After all, the child would be seven by then, and since Si Nian was a teacher, it wouldn't be strange for a child who had studied under her for a few years to be smarter than average.","Just like the Eldest Child, who was now showing extraordinary talent without anyone finding it too strange.","Because he was already ten years old.","A highly capable seven- or eight-year-old child could be called a genius.","But a two- or three-year-old like Yaoyao, who grasped things the moment she heard them, wasn't just a genius; it was completely heaven-defying.","On one hand, she wanted to protect Yaoyao and ensure she had a happy childhood.","On the other hand, being nurtured from a young age in the genius cultivation class would also be beneficial for them.","Si Nian planned to discuss it with Zhou Yueshen and did not immediately answer her son.","Zhou Zedong didn't ask any further questions.","Anyway, whether his sister was good at studying or not didn't matter to him.","Even if his sister didn't go to school, he would work hard to make money and support them.","He didn't pursue fame or fortune.","Zhou Yueshen came back very late again that night.","Si Nian stayed up specifically to wait for him.","Zhou Yueshen parked his car outside and made very little noise as he entered.","Da Huang heard the sound, got up, and wagged his tail.","The daily ritual of petting the little dog's head upon returning home could not be skipped.","Zhou Yueshen tossed it two bones, then walked over to the nearby faucet and turned on the water to wash his hands."]},{"number":347,"title":"Chapter 347: Chapter 342: Acting Coquettishly","paragraphs":["When he came upstairs, Si Nian saw that he was covered in mud and was a little surprised. \"What happened here?\"","How did a pig butcher get covered in mud?","Zhou Yueshen replied, \"It's not very convenient to get water over at the breeding farm, so we made a reservoir. I spent all day digging it today.\"","Si Nian sighed, \"You do everything yourself. Why don't you hire some people?\"","Previously, back in their hometown when she went to deliver food, this older man would slaughter the pigs and keep watch at night all by himself.","Zhou Yueshen had a good income, but he wasn't the type to just enjoy himself as soon as he made money.","Zhou Yueshen tugged lightly at his collar, took off his clothes, and threw them into the bathroom. Then, he rummaged through the wardrobe for a change of clothes.","\"I can do it myself, there's no need to hire anyone. It's far over there, and commuting every day is a hassle.\" Zhou Yueshen found his clothes, closed the wardrobe door, and with a stride of his long legs, walked into the bathroom.","Si Nian followed him. Zhou Yueshen looked travel-worn, with mud still in his hair. He draped his clean clothes over a rack to the side. Instead of using Si Nian's laundry soap, he poured out a little laundry detergent and squatted down to wash his clothes. \"Are you going to No. 2 High School tomorrow? Should I drive you over?\"","No. 2 High School was quite far from here; it took over half an hour by bicycle.","Si Nian had to go there once a week.","Zhou Yueshen still remembered her mentioning this.","Si Nian shook her head. Not minding that the man was dirty, she reached out to brush the mud out of his hair. \"No need, I can just take the bus.\"","\"But what about you? You could have just taken them off and washed them in the washing machine. Washing clothes this late, aren't you tired?\"","Zhou Yueshen said, \"I'm not tired. You guys use the washing machine. These are too dirty, they have mud on them.\"","Si Nian and the others changed and washed their clothes every day, keeping them perfectly clean. If Zhou Yueshen threw these clothes into the washing machine, the machine would get dirty.","It wouldn't be good if it ended up dirtying her clothes later.","After casually finishing the washing, he straightened up.","He was still using a clothes hanger on the side that had already been bent out of shape.","Si Nian looked at him in silence.","At this moment, she felt a little unhappy, though she didn't know why.","Just as Zhou Yueshen finished hanging his clothes, a hand reached up and grasped his wrist. Zhou Yueshen lowered his eyes and looked at her hand—white, slender, and beautiful.","Looking up at her, he saw she was frowning.","Si Nian looked back at him.","\"If you do this next time, I won't use the washing machine either.\"","He didn't use the hangers she bought, and he didn't use the washing machine she bought.","He was terrified that if he used them, she would be disgusted.","Si Nian didn't like this.","It made her seem very harsh.","She tightened her grip on Zhou Yueshen's wrist and tugged it downward.","She said firmly, \"Use mine.\"","Zhou Yueshen froze for a moment and didn't move.","Si Nian frowned, and just as she was about to withdraw her hand, Zhou Yueshen caught it backhand. Squeezing her hand, he leaned down, kissed her forehead, and said, \"Okay, I'll use yours.\"","Looking at his features so close at hand, the gloom in Si Nian's heart dissipated instantly.","She didn't mind that the man hadn't showered yet and still had specks of mud on him; she hugged him. \"Don't do this anymore. You look like you're working too hard.\"","It made her feel terribly uncomfortable to watch.","It was as if the whole family's standard of living was improving.","Yet he alone remained exactly the same.","Everything seemed to be just to accommodate her.","Afraid of dirtying her pajamas, Zhou Yueshen didn't press close. He put one arm around her waist and said in a low voice, \"It's not hard work.\"","Si Nian buried her face in his chest.","She didn't respond. Zhou Yueshen was too tall; he had to bend down to make it easier for her to hug him.","She was rarely this clingy, making him completely reluctant to push her away. He casually grabbed a hanger, hung up his clothes, and walked out with one arm still around her.","Si Nian raised her hands and wrapped them around his neck.","A large hand rubbed her soft hair, and Zhou Yueshen said in a deep voice, \"Nian Nian, I'm going to take a shower first.\"","Only then did Si Nian give a sound of agreement.","Zhou Yueshen touched her face, and she suddenly realized she seemed to have been acting spoiled just now.","Slightly disgusted by her own sentimentality, she quickly let go and said okay.","Zhou Yueshen found her little self-disgusted expression amusing.","He showered quickly. Si Nian was working on some test papers when Zhou Yueshen came out.","Zhou Yueshen didn't expect her to still be writing. His thick, handsome eyebrows raised slightly.","He wondered why she hadn't gone to bed yet; it turned out she was still rushing to finish her homework.","\"Nian Nian, you're not done yet?\"","If he remembered correctly, the test papers were due tomorrow.","Si Nian hummed twice with a guilty conscience, absolutely refusing to admit that her procrastination made her not want to do it, dragging it out until the very last day to rush her homework.","Actually, she had been writing for a whole evening. Although it wasn't difficult, there was a lot assigned, so it still took quite a bit of time.","Zhou Yueshen stepped forward to take a look; Si Nian was scribbling away at an essay.","When Zhou Yueshen came over, she awkwardly reached out to block it, not letting him see.","She felt embarrassed.","Even though she was only nineteen here and still a young girl.","In reality, she was an older leftover woman.","Writing this kind of sentimental essay right now, she was too embarrassed to even look at it herself.","Nor did she want this older man to see it.","She just felt quite ashamed.","Zhou Yueshen gave a low chuckle, straightened up, and didn't disturb her.","Si Nian finished the essay in about ten minutes, so tired that her back and waist ached.","Of course, this backache wasn't entirely from sitting too long, but because she had been tormented by the man for too long previously and hadn't recovered yet.","Coupled with having to work, do test papers, read, and study recently, her waist really couldn't take it.","Zhou Yueshen had dug up a book from somewhere and was half-leaning against the bed, casually flipping through it.","Seeing that she was done, he made some room. Si Nian walked over, leaned into the crook of his arm, and glanced at the book.","It was a book she had borrowed from the library and hadn't had time to read yet.","It covered high school physics concepts.","She raised an eyebrow. \"You can understand this?\"","Zhou Yueshen lowered his eyes to look at her and said in a deep voice, \"Mm.\"","Si Nian started to get a little curious. Although the three siblings weren't Zhou Yueshen's biological children, they were his biological sister's. All three children were extremely gifted. Even if the father was incredible, it was impossible for the mother's genetics to not play a part.","By that logic, Zhou Yueshen should also be quite smart.","However, given his past circumstances, it didn't seem like he had been to school. How could he understand these things?","Zhou Yueshen seemed to guess her thoughts and said, \"The military also has academies. Due to certain reasons, I studied there for a few years.\"","Si Nian understood. No wonder his handwriting was so strong, vigorous, and beautiful.","It didn't look like the handwriting of someone who had never been to school.","Thinking of this, Si Nian took the opportunity to tell him about Yaoyao's situation: \"I'm a bit worried. Last time the two kids were on the news, reporters came knocking on our door.\"","After hearing this, Zhou Yueshen also frowned, not quite agreeing. \"Yaoyao is only three years old. There's no rush.\"","Si Nian thought so too. Although the professors meant well and cherished talent.","But Yaoyao was indeed too young. Last time, Little Dong and Little Han being on the news attracted the attention of reporters. If Yaoyao also drew attention, it would be troublesome; after all, she was still so young.","Si Nian said, \"That reporter from last time never came back, which I find strange. Since that man knows the children are here, why doesn't he come to the door himself?\""]},{"number":348,"title":"Chapter 348: Birthday","paragraphs":["Originally, she thought the other party had seen how well the two children were doing and regretted it, so upon seeing them in the news, he wanted to take them back.","But since that day, no reporters had come.","Nor had anyone visited their home.","Si Nian could not help but feel puzzled.","Was her guess wrong?","Zhou Yueshen's dark eyes flickered.","He closed his book.","\"I had someone look into it. This man is not in this city.\"","Si Nian was slightly surprised. \"Not in this city?\"","\"Yes,\" Zhou Yueshen replied. \"I checked the children's father's records before. They were fake. He is not a local.\"","\"Then where is he from?\"","Zhou Yueshen said, \"Jing City.\"","Although it was unclear why the other party would use a fake identity to go down to the countryside, it was a time of strict crackdowns and chaos. Many university professors, wealthy farmers, and anyone slightly involved had run into trouble.","Many families were torn apart, and it wasn't until the situation improved later on that things gradually got better.","Si Nian fell silent for a moment. Jing City?","Wasn't that the capital?","Anyone who could use connections to replace someone else going down to the countryside in that era without being noticed was probably no ordinary person.","In the novel, the children were all very low-profile.","After all, none of them lived long enough to become famous.","The Eldest Child was also uninterested in fame and fortune. He never appeared in the public eye, so no news of him ever spread.","Naturally, that Scumbag Dad wouldn't have paid attention to them either.","It really proved that one shouldn't be too high-profile.","\"What if he comes back to claim the children?\" Si Nian began to worry again.","If he really was some big shot coming back to snatch the children, how could cannon fodder like them possibly fight him off?","Zhou Yueshen had a little money and quite a few connections, but Jing City was the kind of place straight out of a novel, usually reserved for big bosses who unlocked new maps. She was genuinely a bit worried.","Zhou Yueshen chuckled softly. \"Don't be afraid.\"","Si Nian sighed. She was just the villain's stepmother; all she wanted was to live a peaceful life with his old father.","If there had to be any struggles, she hoped it would be the children fighting against their Scumbag Dad once they grew up.","She and Zhou Yueshen could just peacefully retire.","She didn't want to provoke anyone else.","Unwilling to talk about this troublesome matter, Si Nian said to Zhou Yueshen, \"Zhou Yueshen, you should hire more people.\"","Zhou Yueshen listened to whatever she said and agreed without any hesitation.","He was a very agreeable man.","Satisfied, Si Nian pulled the blanket over herself. Having worked on exam papers all night, she was very tired.","Burying her face in the man's chest, she mumbled drowsily, emphasizing, \"Don't work so hard. Be better to yourself.\"","Deep in the night, the man's pupils were strikingly bright in the darkness.","\"Okay.\"","...","Si Nian went to the Second Middle School to hand in her homework.","Teacher Wang collected her papers, verbally telling her not to work too hard, but ended up assigning her another pile of homework.","Si Nian found it very strange. Previously, the teacher's eyes had held a trace of pity when looking at her. For some reason, her gaze now carried a bit more oddity and conflict.","At any rate, it wasn't as natural anymore.","It didn't seem like the look a teacher gives a student.","It was full of weirdness.","She didn't dwell on it and hurried back to the Foreign Language Primary School.","Only ten people remained for the final test.","The remaining ten children sat in the classroom, and her own son was among them.","Although there weren't many people, the genius cultivation class was officially established.","Si Nian only then realized that the tests over the past few days weren't exams at all.","These questions were all IQ test questions.","In other words, making it through this test proved that these children truly had extremely high IQs.","As expected of a novel, geniuses sat in rows.","Li Youcai got in as well.","This child was arrogant and spoiled by his family.","But he was genuinely smart.","Si Nian had heard before that Li Youcai had won first place in several consecutive math competitions.","This time, he had lost miserably when up against her son, likely just because his mental endurance was too poor, causing him to lose his composure and underperform.","It wasn't strange that he could get in now.","She was just a little worried about whether any trouble would arise.","However, the events that followed proved that Si Nian was overthinking it.","Ever since Li Youcai was almost trafficked by Teacher Xu and her accomplices, he hadn't caused trouble for Zhou Zedong again.","When Teacher Xu's trial began, he attended.","He learned that the people Teacher Xu wanted to harm at the time were him and Xiang'er.","It was only because his grandmother had made her pay compensation and his own attitude towards her had been poor that Teacher Xu had harbored a grudge.","Xiang'er was innocent, but because her grandfather was the principal.","Teacher Xu had been reprimanded by the principal and targeted by his grandmother, so she ended up hating her too.","Li Youcai and Chu Xiang'er were childhood sweethearts, and he liked Chu Xiang'er very much.","Chu Xiang'er was his reverse scale. Teacher Xu had almost caused Xiang'er to be sold to country folks as a child bride. If it weren't for Zhou Zedong's younger brother saving them by a stroke of luck, they might never have made it home.","So he no longer hated Zhou Zedong.","He wanted to compete with him fairly.","Over the past few days, when he passed by the first grade, he heard Zhou Zehan saying that he and his brother were going to celebrate their birthday and inviting friends to come over.","That was how he found out Zhou Zedong was having a birthday.","He figured that with Zhou Zedong's terrible temper, he definitely didn't have a single friend.","His younger brother was different, though; his brother was very popular in the first grade and would surely invite many friends over.","Wouldn't it be incredibly awkward for Zhou Zedong to have no friends at all?","Li Youcai took the initiative to approach Zhou Zedong and said, \"I heard you're celebrating your birthday tomorrow?\"","Zhou Zedong looked up, baffled. Seeing it was him, his brows visibly furrowed.","He didn't speak.","Li Youcai was already used to Zhou Zedong's cold treatment. In the past, he would have been furious.","But he had grown stronger and no longer felt angry.","Instead, he felt that Zhou Zedong was quite pitiful. He must have become like this because no one played with him.","Comforting himself like this made him feel much better.","In a condescending tone, he offered, \"Tomorrow, Xiang'er and I will go celebrate your birthday. I see your brother invited a lot of friends. It's quite pathetic that you don't have any friends.\"","Zhou Zedong was speechless.","Too lazy to bother with him, he packed his books and prepared to leave.","The ignored Li Youcai: \"...\"","Early the next morning, Si Nian went to buy cake molds.","Making a cake was relatively simple. Compared to buying one outside, she preferred letting the children and their little friends experience the fun of baking a cake together.","Jiang Jiu had heard the night before that there would be cake today. He got up in the morning, didn't even wash his face, and came knocking on the Zhou family's door with sleep still in his eyes.","The Second Child rubbed his eyes and opened the window. As soon as Jiang Jiu saw Zhou Zehan, he shouted loudly, \"Second Brother, happy birthday!\"","\"Hurry up and get out of bed, we're making a cake!\"","Children were always very interested in novel things.","For example, Jiang Jiu never lacked cakes to eat, but he had never made one with his own hands before."]},{"number":349,"title":"Chapter 349: Li Youcai's Apology","paragraphs":["In the past, he thought cake was quite delicious, but eating it alone made him lose his appetite after just two bites.","But it was different now.","Even though it wasn't exactly his birthday, it felt even better than his birthday.","Zhou Zehan changed into the new clothes Si Nian had bought for him. As soon as he went downstairs, he started showing off to Jiang Jiu, \"Look, these are the new clothes my mom bought me. There's even a Karting Cat on them.\"","Jiang Jiu's face was full of envy. He carefully reached out to touch the Karting Cat and said, \"I want clothes with a kitty on them too.\"","Zhou Zehan loved this outfit. Normally, he couldn't bear to wear it because his mom said she bought it for his birthday. It was a festive red, so he had specially saved it for today.","He had been looking forward to his birthday for a whole month.","Seeing how much he treasured it, Jiang Jiu liked it even more.","He wished he could immediately go home and ask his grandmother to buy him the exact same one.","\"Second Brother, can I try it on? If it looks good on me, I want to buy one for my birthday too.\"","\"Sure!\" Zhou Zehan was very generous with him and immediately took off the clothes, handing them over for him to wear.","Jiang Jiu stood in the yard and tried them on. However, he had a small frame. Although Zhou Zehan was thin, he had a larger frame. Even though they were the same age, Zhou Zehan was now half a head taller than him.","The clothes were extremely oversized on Jiang Jiu.","They didn't fit well at all.","But he still loved them.","When Si Nian finally returned with the baking molds and it was time to make the cake, the two boys immediately followed closely behind her.","Jiang Jiu said he wanted to make a cake with his own hands as a birthday gift for Zhou Zehan.","It was because Zhou Zehan had previously made him an egg pancake.","He was very touched and had always kept that in mind.","Aside from these things, Si Nian had also bought a lot of snacks, treats, and fruits.","They were meant to entertain the two boys' friends.","However, right now, only Jiang Jiu had arrived.","Zhou Zedong also led his little sister downstairs.","He had once again tied his sister's hair into two little pigtails pointing up at the sky.","But since her hair had grown longer, it looked a bit comical.","The little girl didn't know about vanity yet, so she didn't mind it at all.","Si Nian went to bake the cake base first. She had bought the cream and other toppings ready-made, along with some chocolates that children loved.","The cake base was very simple to make; it only required low-gluten flour and eggs.","They just didn't have an oven at home, but a large iron wok could do the job too.","Si Nian succeeded on her first try.","Now, they were just waiting for the little friends to come over and decorate the cake.","Zhou Zehan and Jiang Jiu couldn't wait any longer. The two boys ran to the door and paced back and forth.","Their faces clearly read: Why aren't they here yet?","However, Grandma Jiang and Grandpa Jiang came over quickly, bringing a toy car for both him and Zhou Zedong.","Zhou Zehan was extremely happy.","This was the first time he had ever received a birthday gift.","When he called them Grandpa and Grandma, his little mouth was as sweet as honey.","He amused the two elders so much that they burst into laughter.","Soon, a group of children arrived hand in hand, chattering away like a flock of little sparrows.","\"Second Brother!\"","\"Second Brother, happy birthday~\"","\"Wow, Second Brother, your family is so rich! Such a big house! Wow, is this your Da Huang? It's huge, even bigger than a tiger.\"","Four or five little kids clamored around Zhou Zehan, looking everywhere and gasping in constant admiration.","Zhou Zehan was so proud his nose pointed up to the sky: \"Yes, this is my Da Huang, and here are my Dabai and Xiaobai. Come over here, these are the fish I keep... On the second floor is my room. Yes, my brother and I share a room because my brother is afraid of ghosts, but I'm not. The third floor is my study room; I read and do my homework here every day.\"","Second Child took the little friends on a tour of his house.","The group of children also took out their gifts for him. Some gave pens, some gave notebooks, and some gave marbles.","Second Child received an armful of gifts, smiling so widely he couldn't close his mouth.","Si Nian walked out of the kitchen and watched the group of little munchkins marveling at the house with envious expressions. Then she looked at Second Child's smug little appearance and couldn't help but want to laugh: \"Alright, Xiaohan, take your classmates to sit down. We can decorate the cake in a bit.\"","Only then did Zhou Zehan rein in his excitement, hurriedly pulling everyone to the sofa to chat.","The entire living room was buzzing with chatter.","Zhou Zedong took a glance and then withdrew his gaze.","He checked the time and frowned slightly.","Why weren't Brother Chen and the others here yet?","Had he mentioned it too early, and they all forgot about it?","Just as he walked outside, he saw Brother Chen and the other two standing at the door, blocking two shivering figures.","Zhou Zedong swept a glance over them; it was Li Youcai and Chu Xianger.","He frowned, \"What are you doing?\"","Brother Chen said: \"Dongzi, good thing you're here. We just got here and saw these two guys acting sneaky at your door, looking like they were going to steal something, so we stopped them immediately.\"","Hearing this, Li Youcai and Chu Xianger's faces turned green.","Chu Xianger hurriedly explained: \"No, Classmate Zhou, I just heard from Youcai that today is your birthday, and I wanted to take the opportunity to thank your brother for helping us last time.\"","Li Youcai gulped, not understanding how Zhou Zedong could know these people who obviously looked like hooligans.","Brother Chen and the others were also dumbfounded when they heard this.","\"Huh?\"","\"Today is your birthday?\"","Zhou Zedong nodded somewhat unnaturally, \"Yes, come on in.\"","Seeing the surprise on their faces, he added, \"My mom asked me to invite you over.\"","After saying that, he frowned and looked at Li Youcai and Chu Xianger.","He had never had a good impression of Class Four, let alone Li Youcai.","Even though he had already ruthlessly retaliated for what happened before.","He still didn't want any contact with these two.","He also couldn't understand why people who had always hated him would suddenly show up at his door on their own initiative.","\"Xiaodong, are your friends here?\" Just as he was about to send them away, he heard Si Nian's voice behind him.","Zhou Zedong withdrew his gaze: \"Mom, this is Brother Chen, Fatty, and the others.\"","Si Nian smiled and nodded, looking at the children.","Facing Si Nian, Brother Chen and the other two felt a bit at a loss for what to do.","They were usually the most hated kids in the area, akin to rats crossing the street, yelled at and scolded by everyone.","Because of fighting over territory, they frequently got into brawls.","They knew very well that kids like them were the least liked.","Right now, they were very worried that Zhou Zedong's mother would despise them.","Moreover, they hadn't even brought gifts.","Si Nian said: \"Xiaochen, Xiaopang, don't be shy. Hurry inside and play. You can help Xiaodong make the cake later.\"","No one had ever invited them into their home so warmly.","Brother Chen blanked out for a moment, then snapped back to reality. He hurriedly waved his hands, but seeing how grimy and black his hands were, he pulled them back. Uncomfortable and stiff, he said, \"No, it's fine. We just came to take a look, we'll leave now.\"","None of them brought gifts, how could they have the nerve to enter someone's house?","No matter how ignorant they were about social etiquette, they knew they should bring gifts for someone's birthday.","Zhou Zedong frowned and didn't speak.","Although he felt it shouldn't be like this, he wasn't good at asking people to stay.","It was Si Nian who smiled and said: \"It's not easy coming all the way here. Come inside and have a seat. Xiaodong, entertain them for a bit.\"","After saying that, Si Nian glanced at Li Youcai and Chu Xianger.","She knew these were her son's classmates from Class Four.","But her son's experience in Class Four wasn't exactly good, and he had even been targeted.","Li Youcai was Li Fengxian's grandson, so he had probably participated in it too.","She did not have a good impression of the Li family.","Seeing the child appear here at this moment, she was actually quite surprised.","\"You two little ones, are you here for Xiaodong?\" Si Nian asked out of politeness.","Li Youcai and Chu Xianger exchanged a glance and nodded.","Chu Xianger offered the gift box she was holding and said, \"Auntie, this is an apology gift for Classmate Zhou, and we also want to wish him a happy birthday.\"","Beside her, Li Youcai looked a bit awkward, but he still brought out the present from behind his back. \"This, this is a calligraphy copybook I got for him. I was ignorant before and ruined his copybook, and, and I bullied him. I'm sorry...\"","Before he could even finish his sentence, the prideful Li Youcai's face flushed bright red.","Si Nian froze for a moment, recalling that her son did indeed have a copybook that was ruined not too long ago.","She had sensed something was wrong at the time because her son always cherished his belongings. How could he have gotten it so dirty?","So it turned out to be the doing of the child standing right in front of her.","Si Nian frowned, her smile fading a bit.","Even though the boy had admitted his mistake, to Si Nian, that kind of bullying behavior was still unforgivable.","She did not accept their gifts. Instead, she looked at Zhou Zedong. \"Xiaodong, do you accept their apology?\"","Zhou Zedong also had not expected Li Youcai to come over and apologize.","He was slightly surprised.","His gaze fell on the copybook in Li Youcai's hands. He had seen this edition before; it was very expensive.","Even more expensive than the one his mother had bought for him.","Although he disliked Li Youcai, it was not to the point of hatred.","After all, compared to himself, Li Youcai had suffered a much worse fate later on.","For a moment, Zhou Zedong could not even muster up any resentment, though his attitude remained aloof. \"It's in the past. You don't need to apologize.\"","Zhou Zedong continued, \"Because I deliberately made you lose face at the competition and purposely stole your points. If we are talking about going too far, I was worse than you.\"","Although everyone could have guessed it, his direct admission still took the group by surprise.","\"So now neither of us owes the other anything, and I don't want your copybook either.\"","With that said, Zhou Zedong walked back inside.","Although they had buried the hatchet, it did not mean he would accept their gifts and hang out with them.","The two children stood awkwardly for a moment before turning to leave as well.","Si Nian brought out some molds to make a cake for the kids.","The entire Zhou household was bustling and lively.","Next door, Fang Bowen, who had been working on his homework problems, heard the laughter of the children. He glanced back and, seeing that Fang Hui was not around, hurriedly got up and ran to the window. Hiding behind the curtains, he peeked out from the second-floor study to look at the house next door."]},{"number":350,"title":"Chapter 350: As Tall as a Mountain","paragraphs":["He saw Zhou Zehan and a group of children in the courtyard, squeezing icing and making a cake.","He had never made a cake before. Every birthday, his mother would have it ready for him, and he would just eat it whenever he wanted.","He had never made one together with friends.","Nor did he understand what was so fun about it.","Yet, he just couldn't look away, entirely mesmerized for a moment.","Fang Hui walked in and frowned when she saw her son standing by the window.","She stepped forward.","She caught sight of the noisy Zhou family next door.","She pulled the window shut in disgust, saying, It's too noisy. Let's keep it closed so it doesn't distract you from your studies.","Fang Bowen reluctantly withdrew his gaze, sat back on his stool, and continued doing his exercises.","The Eldest Child and the Second Child's respective teams were getting ready for a cake-making competition.","The children scrambled about clumsily, and in no time, their hands were covered in frosting.","On Zhou Zedong's side, however, things were orderly as he methodically piped the frosting to trace out a pattern.","A beautiful little cake quickly took shape.","The Second Child, who had been loudly boasting that he would definitely win, turned completely red in the face.","Soon, Zhou Yueshen returned.","He had bought an electronic watch for each of the two children.","This way, they could check the time whenever they wanted.","Not only Zhou Zehan, but even Zhou Zedong broke into a happy smile.","This was the first time they had ever received a birthday present from their father.","Now they had everything that other children had.","Zhou Yueshen had not expected his two sons to have so many friends.","While slightly surprised, he also felt gratified.","His sharp, stern features softened a bit.","Back in Xingfu Village, the two kids had always kept to themselves and barely had any friends.","At least Xiaohan played well with Shitou from next door, but Xiaodong had never interacted with anyone his own age.","After moving to the city, he had initially worried that the two boys would find it even harder to get along with city folks.","He feared they might be ostracized.","But looking at it now, he had overthought things.","The situation had improved tremendously.","The group of children instantly fell silent upon seeing Zhou Yueshen.","This huge uncle, who was as tall as a mountain, was actually the father of the easygoing Second Brother (and the difficult-to-approach Zhou Zedong).","It was truly astonishing.","Their dad was so tall; did that mean they would also grow as tall as a mountain in the future?","Moreover, he was terrifying. A single punch from him could probably send them flying.","If he were their dad, they would have nightmares every night.","They probably wouldn't dare throw tantrums ever again.","Seeing the kids hiding behind his sons, seemingly a bit frightened, Zhou Yueshen straightened up and decided not to disturb them.","He went into the kitchen to help Si Nian cook.","Si Nian hadn't expected him to be back so early today and was a little surprised.","Didn't you say you wouldn't be back until tonight?","Zhou Yueshen helped her wash the vegetables and said in a deep voice, I'll go over after celebrating their birthdays.","In the past, he always put work first, thinking that just keeping the children fed was enough.","Now he knew that beyond providing for them, the most important thing was the children's physical and mental well-being.","If simply taking some time to care for them could make the children feel happy and secure, Zhou Yueshen was more than willing to do so.","Being from a poor rural village, Zhou Yueshen had indeed been influenced by his background.","Because as long as they had money, they could improve their lives.","He used to think the exact same way.","After all, there was nothing harder in this world than having no money.","But later, Si Nian taught him that while money was incredibly powerful, neglecting to care for your children was absolutely unacceptable.","Soon, with the couple working together, they prepared a large table full of dishes.","Si Nian's hands grew sore from cooking, so in the end, Zhou Yueshen took over, frying each dish one by one following her instructions.","Although there were more wealthy people these days, such a lavish feast was usually only enjoyed during major holidays.","For the children's first real birthday celebration, both of them went all out.","Looking at the grand feast, even the worldly little ones opened their mouths in awe.","They were extremely envious.","It turned out that Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan's family really was this rich; they could eat fish and shrimp even when it wasn't a holiday.","The classmates of the Second Child felt an even deeper admiration for the Second Brother.","In contrast, Brother Chen and his two friends felt uncomfortable at every turn.","They knew Zhou Zedong lived here, but since the family had only moved recently, they assumed they were just ordinarily wealthy.","They had always thought the gap between them wasn't that big.","But now, seeing that a casual birthday meal consisted of things they had never seen in their entire lives,","Their feelings of inferiority reached a peak at this moment.","They felt an urge to turn and flee.","Because they profoundly experienced what the word unworthy meant.","They were even more afraid of being looked down upon once they sat at the dinner table.","They heard that his younger brother's friends were all classmates from the Foreign Language Primary School. Who didn't know about that school? It was a place where only the children of rich families could attend.","Even though they lived in the city, let alone the Foreign Language Primary School,","They couldn't even afford to attend a regular primary school.","So those kids were very happy and didn't act like them at all.","All they could see in themselves was overwhelming inferiority.","Because Zhou Zedong didn't like to talk much, unlike the Second Child who would liven up the atmosphere, the three of them stood stiffly in the back, staring at each other, not knowing what to do or how to act.","Their silence was heartbreaking.","Having interacted with many children, Si Nian could roughly understand what they were thinking.","In the past, the Eldest Child and the Second Child weren't much different from them.","Even though she tried her best to show a friendly attitude, she still couldn't ease their nervousness.","She simply called out to the Second Child.","The Second Child was still bragging, but upon hearing her call him, he immediately ran over with eager eyes.","He thought Si Nian had prepared another new gift for him.","Si Nian was amused by his expectant and endearing little expression. She patted his head and said, Xiaohan, help entertain your brother's friends while your brother helps me serve the dishes.","Receiving his orders, Zhou Zehan nodded immediately. Mom, I'll take good care of them.","He also really liked Brother Chen and the others, because every time he went to buy a pancake, Brother Chen and his friends would make it a bit larger for him out of respect for his brother.","This made the Second Child feel quite proud.","He immediately went over and pulled the group to the table, saying that since they were older brothers, they should sit down first.","Then, a bunch of little followers crowded around them too.","They chattered away, asking if the next time they went to buy pancakes, they could be made as big as the Second Brother's.","They also expressed their admiration, asking how they made their pancakes taste so good.","They mentioned that the Second Brother even secretly ate them during class.","Their endless chatter made Brother Chen and his two friends feel socially anxious.","Well, they suddenly understood why Zhou Zedong didn't like to talk.","But the enthusiasm of the group of children dissolved the awkwardness the three of them felt.","Little Pig and his gang from the tube-shaped apartment building had originally wanted to come over and laugh at Zhou Zehan.","They thought that since they weren't playing with him anymore, Zhou Zehan definitely wouldn't have any friends coming to celebrate his birthday.","Running over now, they caught a whiff of a mouth-watering aroma.","It smelled like a grand feast.","They only ever smelled something like this during the Chinese New Year.","The group of kids couldn't help but cling to the iron gate and peek inside.","Just in time to see the dining table full of little kids, eating and chatting happily."]},{"number":351,"title":"Chapter 351: Competitor","paragraphs":["On the table nearby, there were two cakes.","When they celebrated their birthdays, their parents would only buy them a tiny piece just to taste.","But Zhou Zehan's family had two whole cakes.","Thinking of the sweet, soft, and glutinous cakes, the children unconsciously licked their lips.","They felt a bit of regret. If they had known earlier, they wouldn't have rejected Zhou Yuehan; maybe they would have been able to eat all that cake.","For a moment, all of them started to feel regretful.","Inside the house, the initially shy children completely changed their expressions the moment they took their first bite of food.","They didn't lack food at home, and some even had to be coaxed into eating.","But right now, each of them turned into a big eater, unable to stop.","It was simply because Second Brother's mother's cooking was too delicious!","It was even better than the food made by the head chefs at the state-run restaurants.","They shoveled rice into their mouths in large bites and fought to grab the dishes.","The large table of food was quickly wiped clean.","Even the last greasy plate was scraped clean by Second Child to mix with his rice.","Si Nian originally thought that these little munchkins wouldn't be able to eat much, so she hadn't made a lot.","Seeing this, she finally understood the origin of the saying that half-grown boys can eat their fathers into poverty.","However, they couldn't eat too much, as it wasn't easy for young children to digest.","After eating, the group of children played a game of eagle catching chicks in the courtyard.","Little Pig and the others, who still hadn't left the doorway, felt even more envious watching this.","They had originally wanted to wait at the door, hoping Zhou Zehan would see them and take the initiative to invite them inside.","Who knew that Zhou Zehan only focused on eating and didn't even glance outside, which made them so angry they almost fell backwards.","Now that they finally saw the people come out, they were actually playing games!","The group's interest was piqued again.","They wanted to play too.","In the past, when they were at the tube-shaped apartment building, Zhou Zehan always stood in the front, making them feel very secure.","They had never been caught.","But now.","They couldn't even enter the gates of the Zhou family's home.","Little Pig wanted to play and also wanted to eat that cake. He swallowed hard and immediately stepped forward, saying, \"Zhou Zehan, open the door. We're here to celebrate your birthday.\"","\"Before, we said we wouldn't play with you because you were bragging. As long as you stop bragging and share your cake with us, we'll forgive you and let you play at the apartment building in the future.\"","\"Yeah, we'll still play with you.\"","The other children echoed in agreement.","Hearing this, the group of children inside looked toward the door.","They saw a group of dirty children.","Even on such a hot day, their noses were running.","A few children frowned in disgust.","They asked Zhou Zehan, \"Second Brother, who are they?\"","\"Yeah, are they your friends too?\"","\"Why did they say you were bragging?\"","They were a bit confused.","Zhou Zehan also hadn't expected Little Pig and the others to come over. He was initially a bit surprised, but he didn't expect them to actually say he was bragging and demand that he share the cake he made with his friends with them.","Instantly, his little face darkened, and he became unhappy. \"I don't need you to celebrate my birthday, and I won't share my cake with you either. I'm never playing with you guys again.\"","\"What?\"","Little Pig and his group were stunned, looking at him in disbelief.","\"You're not playing with us anymore? Is it because we said you were bragging? But you do love to brag, we weren't wrong.\"","\"Yeah, why are you so stingy? Before, when you and Jiang Jiu had no friends and no one would play with you, we were the ones who let you play together with us.\"","Previously, because they wouldn't play with him, Second Child had been sad for quite a while.","Hearing these words now, however, he wasn't sad at all.","He even found them a bit annoying.","\"Before, when Da Zhuang fought with you over territory, I was the one who helped you win it back.\"","\"I wasn't bragging either. Anyway, I'm never playing with you again, just leave.\"","The few children didn't expect him to actually stop playing with them. Besides being surprised, they also felt they had lost a lot of face.","Their little faces flushed red.","They had come to his door to find him, taking the initiative to forgive him and let bygones be bygones, yet he was actually giving them so little face.","It was simply too much.","The children flew into a rage out of humiliation, and Little Pig took the lead, saying, \"Fine, you said it. From now on, you and Jiang Jiu are not allowed to come play at our apartment building!\"","\"Right, we don't even care to play with you anyway.\"","\"Don't be fooled by him either, Zhou Zehan is just a big braggart.\"","Little Pig and the others didn't think saying that was enough, so they directed their words at Zhou Zehan's friends.","They wished his friends would be like them and stop playing with Zhou Zehan.","Zhou Zehan's face grew a bit uglier.","He didn't expect Little Pig and the others to burn their bridges and be so excessive.","He was really stupid to have actually felt sad for several days over people like this.","Mom was right; such people simply weren't worth it.","Jiang Jiu was the first to step forward, saying angrily, \"Second Brother wasn't bragging. Everything Second Brother said was true. Second Brother's family really does have a lot of pigs.\"","The few classmates exchanged glances and chimed in, \"Yeah, Second Brother is a hero and can even fight human traffickers. Jiang Jiu has even ridden a pig with Second Brother.\"","\"Second Brother, we believe you.\"","\"They are really annoying, we won't play with them.\"","After saying that, they stuck their tongues out at Little Pig and the others, and the group skipped back into the house.","Little Pig and his group were furious.","They didn't expect these people to actually still play with Zhou Zehan.","Having not gotten to eat the cake and being rejected by Zhou Zehan, whom they were trying to appease, the group left with long faces.","Si Nian didn't want the children to stay at the house for too long, fearing their parents would worry.","So she had the two children make their wishes and eat the cake early.","Although the appearance wasn't great, the taste of the cake was undeniably there.","The group of children ate until their bellies were round.","By noon, afraid their families would worry, they finally said their goodbyes and went home.","After celebrating the two children's birthdays, Zhou Yueshen also continued to go to the factory to busy himself.","In mid-June, there was thunderstorm weather.","For the past few days, there had been thunder and rain every day.","Zhou Yueshen stayed at the breeding farm and had no way to come back.","Because the breeding farm they had built previously was rather simple, it was now leaking.","The breeding farm also became damp, and the piglets fell ill.","Let alone him, the large and small breeding farms in the city were all more or less affected by this rain.","What was worse, there were even rumors of a swine fever outbreak.","As a result, people were now afraid to eat pork, and the price of pork dropped for a time.","With Zhou Yueshen not coming home for several days, Si Nian was also worried.","Since she had a day off and saw the weather was nice, she took a trip to the breeding farm.","As a result, Zhou Yueshen wasn't there, but she ran into a few young people who had gone there to apply for a job.","There were both men and women.","Only then did she find out that Yu Dong had quit.","It wasn't because Yu Dong didn't want to help or had a falling out with Zhou Yueshen.","Rather, it was because his family had issued a strict order for him to return and inherit the family business.","Because his father had fallen ill.","Yu Dong had no choice but to leave first.","Yu Dong himself was like the second-in-command at the breeding farm and also acted as Zhou Yueshen's assistant.","Now that he was gone, Zhou Yueshen's workload naturally increased.","He couldn't get away.","He needed to hire an assistant, and they had to be educated and capable of handling business operations.","Si Nian took a look; there were two men and three women.","They all looked to be quite old.","Because they needed to have knowledge in this area, when Yu Dong had looked for people to recruit, the requirement was that they had to be over 25 years old.","Those who came were all between twenty-five and thirty-five years old.","The two women looked even older than Zhou Yueshen.","Dressed in sharp suits, they looked every bit the part of professional business representatives.","The salary offered must have been quite generous.","They knew of the breeding farm, as it had quite a reputation, but they simply hadn't expected the location to be so remote.","When they saw Si Nian in the office, they looked her up and down, clearly viewing her as a competitor."]},{"number":352,"title":"Chapter 352: Why not let everyone be unhappy together","paragraphs":["But that wasn't all; two of the women were actually acquaintances.","After looking around, the younger-looking woman immediately sneered, \"Sister-in-law, see? I told you that you're too old for this. It's not suitable. They only want to hire young people. If it were me, I'd still have a chance. If they actually pick you, they must be blind.\"","After saying that, she critically eyed the shabby office.","\"Such a huge pig farm, yet I didn't expect it to be so remote. Mom and Dad didn't want you to suffer this hardship, which is why they asked me to take this job instead of you. But you just wanted to keep it all to yourself. Well, look at us now. If I can't get it, don't even think you will either.\"","She stared at Si Nian, vigilance in her eyes.","Although the surrounding work environment wasn't great.","Despite her complaints, she was still very envious of this job.","A starting salary of 80 a month.","That was more than double what she made at her old factory.","With such high pay, a little hardship was manageable.","Since she had been laid off, her parents had tried to persuade her sister-in-law to give her this opportunity, but who knew her sister-in-law would refuse.","The two of them had never really seen eye to eye to begin with.","Now that they were competitors, the jealousy was even more intense.","Seeing that there was another young and beautiful woman in the office, she was initially surprised. In her panic, she couldn't help but mock her sister-in-law.","Seeing how young the other applicants were, how could a thirty-five-year-old woman like her have any chance?","She herself was only 29.","The woman she called sister-in-law didn't look too good.","Originally, this job was introduced to her by the son of the boss at the restaurant where her husband worked, because she already did sales and business work.","She hadn't expected the news to reach her mother-in-law's family.","They even insisted she give the job to her younger sister-in-law.","Her husband was an apprentice at the restaurant and didn't make much. They had three children to raise, and her previous job didn't pay well either, so their current financial pressure was immense.","She had finally gotten this opportunity, but now not only was her younger sister-in-law fighting her for it, there were also so many other competitors.","They were older, which made doing sales difficult, so it was easy to get laid off as you aged.","Her sister-in-law had already been laid off, and who knew when it would be her turn.","Companies only wanted young, pretty, and educated women, as it made socializing and negotiating business much easier.","Hearing her sister-in-law's words now, her heart went cold.","She said with a bitter face, \"Don't talk about people like that.\"","The other two men disdained bickering with women, but when their eyes fell on Si Nian, they couldn't help but take a few extra glances.","It was simply because this woman was too stunning.","As a competitor, she gave them a huge sense of crisis.","However, the job requirements stated that the applicant needed to be educated.","This girl was still young, looking about eighteen or nineteen.","She definitely hadn't gone to college.","How much education could she have?","Thinking of their own qualifications, they breathed a slight sigh of relief.","Si Nian quietly observed everyone's expressions.","She found it quite interesting.","She took the initiative to strike up a conversation. \"Are you all experienced veterans?\"","The first woman who spoke was named Li Yanhong. She immediately raised her chin and said disdainfully, \"Nonsense. When I was out doing sales, you were probably still in elementary school. My performance at my previous company was top-notch!\"","Wearing a suit, she did have somewhat of a white-collar aura.","Si Nian glanced at her.","Unexpectedly, the two men nearby laughed. \"What kind of proper woman shows her face in public all day long? Everyone knows what that means. 'Top-notch'? You aren't even afraid of being laughed at for saying that!\"","\"If she were my wife, I would absolutely never let her do this kind of work outside...\" The other man also shook his head, his face full of disapproval.","The two exchanged a glance, revealing a knowing and disgusting smile.","In this era, mindsets were still feudal. They still believed that women belonged inside the home and men belonged outside. If a woman came out to do business, run sales, and drink with clients, what was the difference between her and a prostitute?","If their own women did this kind of work, they would be too ashamed to face anyone.","From the very beginning, they hadn't taken these two older women seriously.","Because everyone knew that at this age, many companies wouldn't hire them.","Sales required young and pretty people, otherwise they would quickly be eliminated.","After all, no client wanted to sit and drink with a wrinkled, aging face.","The two men sneered. Even though they were born of women themselves, they still looked down on them.","Li Yanhong's face flushed red with anger at their words.","Her sister-in-law awkwardly lowered her head.","They both knew exactly what the two men meant, but it was rarely pointed out so explicitly to their faces. To them, this was a deep insult.","\"Filthy! It's because of filthy-minded, stinking men like you that so many people point fingers at women!\"","Li Yanhong said angrily, \"We earn money with our own skills. What's so shameful about that?\"","\"Whatever you men can do, we women can do just as well.\"","\"We are not the kind of people who make illicit trades just for business.\"","The two men scoffed and laughed out loud. \"That sure sounds nice.\"","\"Even if someone like you wanted to make illicit trades, the boss probably wouldn't even look twice at you.\"","\"Women are better off staying at home to serve their husbands and raise their children.\"","Hearing the two sides arguing endlessly, Si Nian slightly shook her head.","Li Yanhong happened to catch this.","She immediately flared up, \"What are you shaking your head for? Don't think that just because you're young and pretty, I'll lose to you!\"","Si Nian: \"Thanks for the compliment.\"","Li Yanhong: \"...\"","Seeing that she was about to start arguing again, her sister-in-law hurriedly pulled her back and whispered, \"Stop talking. Don't fight with them.\"","Li Yanhong swatted her hand away, her face full of anger, finding everyone displeasing to the eye.","\"Miss, don't mind her. Yanhong just has this kind of temper. Those of us in sales inevitably get gossiped about by a man or two behind our backs. You just have to get used to it.\"","Hearing this, Li Yanhong rolled her eyes at her.","After listening, Si Nian asked in return, \"Why should you get used to being insulted?\"","Wang Qiaomei let out a confused sound. When she reacted, she couldn't give a clear reason, so she said gently, \"We can't stop other people's mouths. It's best to just live our own lives. If you take everything too seriously, life becomes too hard.\"","Si Nian looked at her and observed her for a moment.","Wang Qiaomei was the oldest person present, and her face showed the weathering of time. She was indeed older, and doing sales might not make her very popular unless she was extremely capable or very eloquent.","However, she looked honest and sincere; she wasn't a bad person.","Si Nian casually picked up the old man's cup from the table, poured herself some tea, took a sip, and said, \"I actually think cursing back is quite nice.\"","\"Rather than being unhappy all by yourself, it's better to make everyone unhappy together.\"","She put down the cup and smiled at Wang Qiaomei. \"Don't you agree?\"","Wang Qiaomei froze.","Li Yanhong gave her a stunned look.","Wang Qiaomei then sighed and said, \"You are still young. My sister-in-law is just like that. She offended too many people over the years, which is why she was laid off.\"","\"You're still young and naive, but when you get older, you'll know just how hard it is to find a job.\"","Hearing this, Li Yanhong's face darkened."]},{"number":353,"title":"Chapter 353: Are you with Mr. Zhou","paragraphs":["She didn't refute it.","Si Nian asked, \"Did you two work at the same company before?\"","Wang Qiaomei nodded. \"Yes, but our factory hasn't been doing well. They've been laying people off for the past two years, so we had to find a backup plan.\"","Si Nian nodded and didn't say anything else.","Everyone fell into silence once again.","Fortunately, steady footsteps soon echoed from outside.","Everyone hurriedly stood up.","The man who walked in was very tall; he even had to tilt his head slightly to get through the door. The moment his towering figure entered, the room suddenly felt cramped and imposing.","Instantly, the four people who had been noisy just moments ago all held their breath.","Zhou Yueshen's gaze swept lightly over the group before landing in the back.","Si Nian craned her neck to look out.","These people weren't tall. Even the two men were only about 1.7 meters.","Zhou Yueshen stood at the very front. His tall, slender figure stood against the light, bringing a sense of oppression.","He exuded an intimidating presence.","However, this feeling disappeared in a flash.","The expressions of the applicants grew tense.","It seemed none of them expected the boss of the breeding farm to be such a tall, formidable man.","In their minds, bosses were usually bald, with big ears and potbellies.","Rarely were they like this.","Li Yanhong was bold. She was the first to recover and spoke up, \"Hello, President Zhou. I'm here to interview for the salesperson position.\"","Zhou Yueshen lifted his eyes.","He gave her a cursory glance.","Giving a slight nod, he said, \"Please, take a seat.\"","Li Yanhong's tense body immediately relaxed. Not daring to speak any nonsense, she nodded quickly and stepped aside. In such a suffocating atmosphere, Si Nian couldn't help but let out a small cough.","Good heavens, this interview scene brought her right back to when she graduated from college and went to company interviews. She completely empathized with them.","She sat back down. Li Yanhong walked over, sat beside her, and shot her a glance. Thinking Si Nian was too scared to speak, Li Yanhong let out a cold snort.","She muttered in a low voice, \"If you don't even have the courage to speak, why did you even come to an interview... Go back and practice more.\"","With one sentence, she secretly mocked all the other interviewees.","Si Nian wasn't angry; instead, she smiled. Ignoring the woman, she looked at Zhou Yueshen, who was walking toward her, and said, \"Thanks for your concern.\"","Li Yanhong rolled her eyes.","Seeing Zhou Yueshen approaching, she immediately corrected her posture and sat up straight.","Then she heard him take two steps forward and ask in a deep voice, \"Why are you here?\"","\"Hello, I heard you are hiring... ah?\" Before Li Yanhong could finish her sentence, she realized something was wrong.","She looked up at Zhou Yueshen with a bewildered expression.","Only then did she realize he wasn't looking at her, but at the young woman beside her.","Li Yanhong was stunned.","Si Nian gave her an amused look.","Looking at Zhou Yueshen, his expression remained unchanged, but there was sweat on his forehead.","Si Nian said, \"It's been raining every day lately. I saw you hadn't come home and got worried, so I came to check on you.\"","Zhou Yueshen frowned, looked at her for a few seconds, and said with a hint of apology in his voice, \"Sorry, I've been a bit busy these past few days.\"","\"Sit down for a while.\"","Si Nian murmured an agreement.","She held her cup and took another sip.","Zhou Yueshen's gaze paused on the cup for two seconds before sweeping over the other people.","Li Yanhong's mouth hung open for a long time before she stammered, \"You... you're not here for the interview.\"","Si Nian asked in return, \"When did I ever say I was here for the interview?\"","The others also looked extremely surprised.","They hadn't expected that she wasn't an applicant.","Li Yanhong's face turned pale. \"Could it be that you are President Zhou's daugh...\"","Zhou Yueshen shot a glance at her.","Li Yanhong: \"...ter?\"","Zhou Yueshen's face darkened.","Si Nian burst into laughter, almost choking on her water.","Zhou Yueshen gave her a mild look and patted her back with his large hand.","He was afraid she would choke.","Li Yanhong's face was extremely ugly. Just moments ago, she had treated Si Nian as a competitor, but she never imagined that not only was Si Nian not an applicant, she also had a close relationship with the boss.","Didn't that mean she had just dug her own grave?","Li Yanhong looked green around the gills.","The look Zhou Yueshen gave her wasn't very friendly either.","His tone was cold and emphatic: \"She is my wife.\"","Li Yanhong: \"...\"","The hostility meter was instantly maxed out—","\"Alright, I won't disturb you guys anymore.\"","Seeing Li Yanhong's colorful expressions, Si Nian found it amusing. She put down her cup and patted the man's hand, telling him to get back to work.","Only then did Zhou Yueshen straighten up and withdraw his gaze.","He didn't bother holding it against Li Yanhong.","He picked up the resumes from the side and looked through them.","After casually scanning them for a moment, he asked the group to introduce themselves.","Li Yanhong and Wang Qiaomei were from the same company, but due to a round of layoffs, Li Yanhong had been let go.","Wang Qiaomei was still employed, but her salary wasn't high.","Hearing that she was the wife of his subordinate Yu Dong, Zhou Yueshen glanced at her and gave a slight nod.","Wang Qiaomei breathed a small sigh of relief.","Zhou Yueshen asked Li Yanhong, \"What was the reason for your layoff?\"","Li Yanhong hesitated for a moment and said awkwardly, \"I offended a few clients...\"","Si Nian couldn't help but smile again.","Zhou Yueshen glanced at her, then lowered his eyes, picked up the water cup next to her, and took a sip.","It was filled with floral tea, very fragrant.","Aside from that, there was a faint, familiar delicate scent.","He took another sip, his voice deep. \"And you two?\"","The two men's pasts were much more impressive. They had worked at a major company for half a year, won outstanding employee awards at other companies, and were college graduates.","Speaking of their experiences and educational backgrounds, both were very proud, holding their heads high with their chests puffed out.","In this day and age, college graduates were highly sought after.","If there were no major issues, a company would definitely be reluctant to let them go.","Zhou Yueshen pierced right through their facade with one sentence: \"Half a year is the internship period. You didn't pass?\"","The two of them froze instantly.","Their expressions then became subtle.","Zhou Yueshen set their resumes down directly and said in a low tone, \"You two can leave.\"","The two men's faces instantly turned ugly, and they asked in shock, \"Why? What's wrong with us? If you're dissatisfied with something, just say it directly. This is baffling, and we don't accept it!\"","\"Yeah, you have to give us a reason, right?\"","Zhou Yueshen put down the cup, leaned against the table, and said with an indifferent expression, \"If you couldn't meet the company's standards after a six-month internship, I don't think I have that much time to train you.\"","The faces of the two men flushed a deep red.","Zhou Yueshen ignored them after that.","The two men left, looking utterly humiliated.","The remaining Li Yanhong and Wang Qiaomei tensed up, their hearts pounding wildly.","Zhou Yueshen looked at Li Yanhong. \"You easily offend clients?\"","Li Yanhong's heart sank halfway.","Seeing her expression, Zhou Yueshen knew he was pretty much spot on.","Wang Qiaomei interjected, \"President Zhou, it wasn't like that. The previous situation was a bit complicated.\"","Zhou Yueshen's expression didn't change, nor did he respond.","Si Nian looked at him as well.","At that moment, Zhou Yueshen suddenly turned his head and glanced at her.","He was actually asking for her opinion.","Si Nian was taken aback for a second. Her gaze swept over the two nervous women.","She raised an eyebrow at Zhou Yueshen. \"You're really letting me choose?\"","Zhou Yueshen gave a slight nod. \"Mhm.\"","Si Nian saw how casual he was being.","She sighed.","Then, she shifted her gaze back to the two women, let it hover for a moment, and stopped.","She pointed at one of them and said, \"If it were up to me, I'd pick her.\"","Zhou Yueshen: So mad, so mad, do I really look that old?"]},{"number":354,"title":"Chapter 354: Choice","paragraphs":["Zhou Yueshen glanced in the direction she was pointing.","He paused.","The other two women were also stunned.","Wang Qiaomei tilted her head, looking at Li Yanhong beside her in sheer disbelief.","She never expected that Si Nian would choose her.","Let alone Wang Qiaomei, even Li Yanhong herself was completely bewildered.","After all, she had just offended Si Nian and said the wrong things.","It had been a continuous string of bad luck.","On top of that, her sister-in-law had been recommended by the factory manager's assistant earlier.","Her heart had long grown cold with disappointment.","She had already mentally prepared herself for rejection.","Yet, she never imagined that Si Nian would actually choose her.","Right now, her mouth was slightly agape. She stared at Si Nian in disbelief, unable to process what had just happened.","Zhou Yueshen's gaze swept over Li Yanhong.","\"Tell me why.\"","He was asking Si Nian.","If she chose Li Yanhong, she definitely had her reasons and thoughts.","Zhou Yueshen was curious.","He had noticed earlier that when Li Yanhong was speaking, Si Nian was smiling.","Even though the woman's words were quite unpleasant to hear.","But Si Nian had her own reasons for choosing her.","Having spent so much time with this older man, Si Nian understood what he meant.","She replied, \"I think she has her own bottom line and knows how to protect herself. In sales, you inevitably meet all kinds of clients. For a salesperson, someone with true capability never needs to grovel or swallow their pride to please others. Doing so only makes others look down on you.\"","\"If you can't hold your bottom line, encountering difficult clients will bring you massive trouble. I believe that when it comes to work, personal safety comes first, and the job comes second. If a company can't even guarantee the safety of its own employees, then there really is no point in staying there.\"","\"Of course, even though she offended someone, the fact that she managed to stay at her previous factory for so many years under such circumstances proves she has real skills. She isn't the type to offend clients for no reason. It must have been because the other party said something truly awful, or she was harassed and pushed beyond her limits...\"","Nowadays, many men did not respect women much, but Si Nian believed that you could always find another job, whereas being insulted and harassed would leave a lifelong shadow.","Brave people might dare to fight back, but she herself had not possessed such courage in the past.","To dare to stand up and fight back against men in this era, Si Nian felt that Li Yanhong was a relatively brave and assertive person.","Only this kind of person wouldn't suffer losses.","The more timid you are, the more people think you are easy to bully.","She believed that Zhou Yueshen wouldn't want to see his subordinates being bullied either.","Although Li Yanhong's words might not have been very pleasant, the fact that she worked at her former factory for so long despite offending people showed she had her own merits.","As soon as she said this, Li Yanhong's eyes immediately turned red.","She never expected someone to see through her and understand her so quickly.","Especially since she had just disliked Si Nian and treated her like a rival.","Filled with shame, Li Yanhong said, \"My temper isn't great, but I'm not without a sense of propriety. Some clients like to get handsy and say nasty things. Even knowing I'm married with a child, they still harass me. Naturally, I won't be polite to them.\"","\"You are right. Work is work, and personal life is personal life. I am serious about my job, but if it affects my life, I will not choose to tolerate it. Although we are sales personnel and indeed need to serve our clients attentively, I don't believe this requires selling out my body and dignity in exchange for a business opportunity.\"","This was exactly what she had told her leader before.","But how did her leader reply? He said that letting someone touch her wouldn't make her lose a piece of flesh, and asked why she was being so dramatic.","He even said that girls prettier than her weren't as aloof as she was.","This was completely unacceptable to Li Yanhong.","Si Nian nodded slightly without speaking. She looked at Zhou Yueshen beside her.","Zhou Yueshen took a cup from the side, poured another cup of tea, and handed it to her.","His hands were large; although his fingers were long and slender, they were also calloused.","They were a bit tanned, but the skin tone was very even.","The joints were distinct and strong.","Si Nian really liked Zhou Yueshen's hands because they were always burning hot. When he held her in the winter, it was very warm.","She reached out to take it and took a sip.","Her heart skipped a beat.","The two of them had been drinking from the same cup all along.","Zhou Yueshen withdrew his gaze.","He looked at the two women and didn't say much.","\"It'll be you then.\"","Li Yanhong still found it hard to believe, as if a pie had just fallen from the sky and hit her.","Her whole body felt dizzy.","After the shock came ecstasy.","She looked at Si Nian with excitement.","She was just short of kneeling down before her.","Beside them, Wang Qiaomei's face looked awful. Unable to accept this, she said, \"How... how could this be? I just spoke up for you earlier, and Yanhong talked to you like that, yet you actually chose her.\"","She refused to believe that she had spoken up for Si Nian, yet wasn't chosen.","Instead, the aunt who had mocked her was chosen.","Wang Qiaomei found it very hard to accept this fact in her heart.","Si Nian glanced at her. Seeing her face full of disbelief and indignation, she paused.","She said, \"This has nothing to do with how she treated me. We are looking for sales personnel. Public business has nothing to do with private matters.\"","\"You did speak up for me, but that doesn't mean I have to choose you.\"","\"Haven't you realized that you have a huge problem? When you are mocked and insulted by a man, your first reaction is shame and self-doubt. You don't think the person who insulted you has a problem; instead, you look for the cause within yourself. Li Yanhong, on the other hand, is the exact opposite.\"","\"With your personality, I don't think you are very suitable to be a salesperson.\"","Wang Qiaomei still found it hard to accept and said, \"What they said wasn't really wrong, though. After all, many people in this industry are like that.\"","Si Nian was left speechless.","If even she herself thought this way, if she was someone who looked down on herself, what else could Si Nian say?","Seeing her stay silent, Wang Qiaomei thought she had made a valid point and continued, \"You and Yanhong share the same view, and it's wrong. Because with tempers like yours, it's very easy to offend people. That's exactly why Yanhong was laid off.\"","\"For us in sales, suffering a little grievance isn't anything strange. As long as the job is done well and it helps the company, it's all worth it.\"","Si Nian: ...","So even back in this era, things like PUA were already happening?","After Wang Qiaomei finished speaking, she didn't look at Si Nian. After all, it was because of this very issue that she and Li Yanhong had a bad relationship and couldn't see eye to eye.","Now that Si Nian was siding with Li Yanhong, she assumed Si Nian was just like her.","Neither of them had the slightest selfless thought of dedicating themselves to the company. How could a company possibly want such people?","Wang Qiaomei looked at Zhou Yueshen and advised, \"Mr. Zhou, although I know saying this might not be very nice to Yanhong, she really does offend people easily. It would be a true pity if such a great job opportunity was handed to her only to be messed up.\"","\"Yanhong, the reason I didn't yield this job to you is precisely because of this. I didn't want to fight you for it, but your temper really isn't suitable, otherwise you wouldn't have been fired.\"","Li Yanhong had been very happy, but upon hearing these words, her face darkened.","\"Yes, Sister-in-law, you're right, I was laid off, but what you said is too ugly. The factory's business hasn't been good this year, and since the two of us are older, one of us had to go. Mom advised me that you and Eldest Brother have many children and a lot of pressure, and she was afraid you wouldn't be able to afford food if you lost your job. I thought it wasn't easy for you and Eldest Brother, so I left voluntarily. Otherwise, did you think you could stay so easily?\"","Li Yanhong was furious. Although she and Wang Qiaomei didn't get along, she had a good relationship with her eldest brother. Plus, they had three children, and her eldest brother's apprentice salary was low.","If Wang Qiaomei also lost her job, their family's life would definitely be difficult.","She originally didn't really want to leave either, after all, jobs were hard to find.","At that time, the leadership talked to the two of them, implying that it would sound too bad to just let them go directly, so they hinted that they should discuss it privately themselves.","When she went back, her mother persuaded her, and she hesitated before agreeing.","She voluntarily gave up the opportunity.","Thinking she was still young and could easily find another job.","But her sister-in-law thought she was laid off because she offended a client.","She originally couldn't be bothered to explain.","Wang Qiaomei was still haggling over this matter.","She didn't even think about it. If it hadn't been for her bad temper over the years, making those people afraid to offend her, how much disadvantage would Wang Qiaomei have suffered when going out to socialize?","Hearing this, Wang Qiaomei was stunned.","Then she said in disbelief, \"No, impossible, how come I didn't know about this.\"","\"If you don't believe me, go ask my mom. If I was really laid off for offending someone, I would have been fired long ago.\"","\"My temper is bad, but I also have a lot of clients under me. When I left, I even asked the factory to assign all my clients to you. I dislike you, but you are my sister-in-law after all, my eldest brother's wife. I couldn't leave them to someone else, I'm not stupid.\"","Wang Qiaomei's expression turned even uglier.","At the time, when the company gave her the list of Li Yanhong's clients to manage, she thought it was because Li Yanhong had left and no one else in the factory could do it, so they could only give it to her.","She had even felt smug about it, thinking her long-time efforts had finally paid off.","She never expected this to be the case.","Wang Qiaomei's face looked extremely bad.","She lowered her head, her face full of defeat.","So what was the point of her persistence for so long?","She had always thought she was the one looking after her sister-in-law at the factory.","Because of her bad temper, she easily offended people.","But she forgot that it was precisely because of Li Yanhong's bad temper that those people didn't dare to give them attitude.","She had even forgotten that with Li Yanhong's big temper, why hadn't she resisted or fought for herself when the company laid her off, but just left?","Now she suddenly understood.","It was her who had always thought too badly of her.","Wang Qiaomei's face was full of shame.","She couldn't say a single word.","Zhou Yueshen interrupted the two.","\"If you have any problems, go back and solve them yourselves.\"","The implication was that this was not the place for them to argue.","The two women immediately fell silent.","If they kept talking, Li Yanhong's opportunity would be gone later.","Although this place was remote and the environment was harsh.","Who else could offer a base salary of 90?","Si Nian could also see that Li Yanhong was the kind of person with a sharp tongue but a soft heart, but she really didn't expect her to make sacrifices for her family.","Although the relationship between the two wasn't great, when those two men mocked them women, it was Li Yanhong who stood up to defend their rights.","She wasn't just defending herself, but all women.","At that time, Si Nian thought, no matter how bad this person is, she can't be that bad.","In contrast to Wang Qiaomei.","Si Nian originally just thought her thinking was restricted, but her heart was good.","But she didn't expect her to be so inflexible.","She was already thirty-four or thirty-five years old.","Forget it.","When the two left, Si Nian looked at Zhou Yueshen.","\"Wang Qiaomei was introduced by Yu Dong. If you don't choose her, will it be bad?\"","She chose Li Yanhong just out of her personal opinion.","It didn't mean her choice was the right one.","But Zhou Yueshen didn't object either.","Si Nian was a little worried.","He didn't have to listen to her about everything.","After all, she didn't understand the work at the breeding farm.","Besides, the person was introduced by Yu Dong, so he must have had his own thoughts.","Zhou Yueshen raised his eyes: \"You made the right choice.\"","\"I have no objections because I was planning to choose her anyway.\"","Si Nian raised her eyebrows.","She thought Zhou Yueshen had been provoked by Li Yanhong.","He should have had a bad impression in his heart.","Who told Li Yanhong to say she was his daughter.","The old man's face turned green at that moment.","She rarely saw his emotions leak out, with such exaggerated facial expressions.","This was the first time.","It was enough to prove how explosive Li Yanhong's words were to him.","Thinking about it, Si Nian couldn't help it.","She wanted to laugh.","Although she was a bit younger, she couldn't possibly be Zhou Yueshen's daughter.","Probably.","Si Nian looked at the man's outfit and understood a bit more.","When would this old man throw away his old-fashioned army green jacket?","Seeing her laugh again, Zhou Yueshen glanced at her.","\"Are you very happy?\"","Si Nian immediately put away her smile.","Zhou Yueshen organized the resumes and put them aside, \"Have you had lunch?\"","Si Nian put down her water cup, she was full from drinking water, and she answered honestly: \"Not yet, have you eaten?\"","Zhou Yueshen didn't say whether he had eaten or not.","He just said: \"Someone will cook later, I'll go get food for you.\"","\"Okay.\"","Then, he asked her to sit for a while, while he took out some forms and started writing.","Si Nian sat next to him out of boredom, watching him sign.","They were all orders.","For the afternoon, to be signed now.","The man was still busy.","Si Nian didn't bother him.","She looked around the environment.","This wasn't her first time here, but this time the environment seemed even worse.","There was a basin on the floor nearby, with water in it.","The roof was leaking.","Si Nian looked up, and there were water stains and some marks on the roof.","This house was very old, and Zhou Yueshen had rented it and renovated it for use.","The surroundings had been plastered with lime, and the windows weren't big.","It looked like a small shop in the countryside.","He didn't have any requirements for his office environment himself.","So he just made do.","As Yu Dong said, the piglets' pens were better than his.","It had been raining heavily recently, and these houses were very old.","Although the breeding farm was newly built, because some ditches weren't done well, water easily accumulated.","Too damp an environment wasn't good for the piglets either.","They easily got sick.","During this time, Zhou Yueshen was also digging channels for drainage.","Fortunately, he had gained experience in breeding.","He knew what to do.","Plus, the breeding farms were newly built, so they didn't leak.","Seeing there were still so many orders, the impact probably wasn't too big.","Si Nian looked at the prices and said, \"The prices have dropped?\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded slightly.","\"There's swine fever at the breeding farm in the west of the city, and now many people are afraid to eat pork. Swine fever is a highly contagious and fatal virus that can quickly spread and infect the entire breeding farm. So recently, our breeding farm has been doing closed feeding, and we have to disinfect every day to prevent accidents.\"","He reached out and touched Si Nian's face.","\"I probably won't be able to go back for the next few days. I need to wait until this swine fever situation is resolved.\"","Zhou Yueshen's business was doing so well that it was bound to draw the envy of others.","Not to mention, at a critical juncture like this, if anything went wrong, it would mean total ruin. He couldn't afford a single mistake.","Especially when everyone else was facing disasters, his ability to keep things stable would inevitably thrust him into the eye of the storm, making him a prime target.","The piglets: What? The neighborhood next door got locked down?"]},{"number":355,"title":"Chapter 355: She Must Not Cause Trouble for Him","paragraphs":["After hearing this, Si Nian also fell silent.","Viruses, no matter the era, were extremely deadly.","Not to mention their high transmission rate, they were incredibly dangerous.","One careless mistake could lead to total annihilation.","Coming from the future, she had also experienced the torment of viruses and deeply understood the importance of lockdowns and isolation.","Si Nian was very worried. In past history, there were far too many instances of swine fever outbreaks.","The novel only mentioned the older man's pig farm; because he was a supporting character, it didn't detail what had actually happened.","At this moment, it was hard not to worry.","She felt she had come at a bad time.","It seemed like she couldn't do anything to help him.","Instead, she was just taking up his time.","She knew Zhou Yueshen wouldn't just leave her here and go off to work.","Si Nian wanted to leave, but meeting the soft gaze of the man looking at her, she felt reluctant to part.","...","Zhou Yueshen was often so busy that he forgot to eat.","Usually, it was Yu Dong who would call him.","Or bring the food directly to him.","Today, everyone thought the same. As soon as the food was ready, the first scoop was naturally saved for the factory manager.","But before they could pack it up and send it over, they saw Zhou Yueshen walking in.","There was only a cooking kitchen here, and it wasn't very big.","Usually, everyone just grabbed a small stool and sat down to eat.","The men weren't too particular about these things. After eating, they would find a spot to take a quick nap.","Only Zhou Yueshen had an office. Because he usually had a lot of work, he would always get his food and eat in his office.","Zhou Yueshen rarely smiled. He always wore a cold expression, so everyone was quite afraid of him.","Only Yu Dong dared to joke with him.","Seeing him arrive, the chatting and laughing crowd fell silent in unison and greeted him.","\"the Boss.\"","\"Why did the Boss come over in person today?\"","\"the Boss, I heard sister-in-law came to see you?\"","Zhou Yueshen gave a sound of acknowledgment and didn't say much else.","He stepped forward, grabbed two sets of bowls and chopsticks, served the food, and then left.","Seeing this, everyone understood.","So he had specially come over to get food for his wife.","They knew it. How could someone who usually forgot to eat because he was so busy suddenly come over to get food?","It turned out it was for his wife.","When Zhou Yueshen returned, Si Nian was sweeping the floor.","Seeing him approach, Si Nian said, \"It's a bit damp in here, which isn't good for your health. When you have time, you should patch up the roof.\"","The floor wasn't made of concrete to begin with, so it was very damp.","After saying that, she walked to the side and opened the window.","Who knew that before she could even push the window out, it would fall off with a clatter.","Si Nian: \"...\"","The office fell into a dead silence.","Zhou Yueshen let out a low cough, placed the food on the table, and said in a low voice, \"This building is a bit old, and the windows are broken. But I don't stay here often, so I haven't bothered fixing it.\"","Si Nian's mouth twitched.","Looking at the old mahogany window on the floor, she asked, \"What do we do now?\"","Zhou Yueshen replied, \"I'll just find someone to fix it later. You eat first.\"","Si Nian sighed and agreed.","She couldn't blame Li Yanhong for saying the environment was bad earlier.","Now it seemed there was a good reason for it.","The food tasted average, not great, but not terrible either.","The breeding farm never lacked meat. For most people, having meat at every meal was already a luxury.","But Si Nian was inherently a bit picky about food; after all, she considered herself a foodie.","Right now, she felt extremely cloyed after eating just a little.","Seeing that she couldn't eat anymore, Zhou Yueshen didn't mind. He poured her leftover food into his own bowl and finished it in a few bites.","Zhou Yueshen said, \"Everyone here eats pretty casually. We aren't very particular.\"","Si Nian nodded, indicating she understood.","However, she still suggested, \"This building is too old, and there's no telling when it might collapse. When the weather gets better, you should have someone renovate it so it's more comfortable for you to stay in.\"","Zhou Yueshen always listened to her, and this time was no exception; he agreed without refusing.","Although he didn't care about it himself, since Si Nian brought it up, he naturally took it to heart.","Even if it didn't matter to him, it was truly inconvenient when she occasionally visited and didn't even have a place to sit.","Si Nian added, \"Then get it done quickly. If you end up staying here for a long time in the future, I'll bring the kids to see you.\"","Previously in the village, the breeding farm was close by.","The children had grown bolder and would always run over to the farm.","Si Nian also frequently brought him meals.","Now that Zhou Yueshen was further away, he didn't need her to deliver food.","Seeing him in such an environment now made her heart ache.","They were living comfortably in a big house at home, enjoying life.","Yet he was working day and night, resting in such a cramped environment in the evenings.","Zhou Yueshen paused, then agreed.","Si Nian continued, \"If you trust me, I can help you manage the accounts, so you won't have to be so tired every day.\"","The people in Zhou Yueshen's factory were all rough men with little education.","Previously, Yu Dong managed it.","But Yu Dong had left. Although Li Yanhong had come, she naturally couldn't be as versatile as Yu Dong. Since he wasn't familiar with her, he didn't dare entrust it to her.","She could only handle business operations and such.","These matters naturally fell into Zhou Yueshen's hands.","Si Nian had just watched him checking the accounts, and it seemed quite simple.","After taking the college entrance examination, she planned to take a year off from school.","She would wait until Yaoyao went to preschool before returning to her studies.","She had already made plans to skip grades. After all, getting a university diploma wasn't difficult for her.","What Si Nian lacked was just the certificate itself.","Furthermore, she wanted to get into the best school.","In her own world, she was already excellent. Coming here, she naturally wouldn't settle for second best.","However, this was the first time Si Nian intervened in the affairs of Zhou Yueshen's factory.","She used to be lazy and never asked about it.","But now she felt that sitting back and enjoying the fruits of his labor wasn't very good.","At the end of the day, she was the boss's wife.","Zhou Yueshen hesitated for a moment. It wasn't that he didn't want to hand it over to Si Nian, but she had to take the college entrance examination, go to school, and take care of the kids. Could she handle being so busy?","If Si Nian knew he was thinking this, she would definitely state immediately that while she might be too busy for other things, counting money made her quite happy.","After all, this was their own family's money.","She had no interest in calculating for others.","But calculating for herself, her interest was massive.","Seeing that she was serious about the idea, Zhou Yueshen didn't dare say much more.","He was afraid Si Nian would think he didn't want to give it to her.","He sensitively realized that in matters like this, he had to listen to her.","Afraid she wouldn't understand.","Zhou Yueshen began to introduce the account management methods of the breeding farm for this period.","He always spoke concisely and to the point, his voice deep. Occasionally, his slender fingertips pointed to some marked places on the bills and some long-term cooperative accounts. He explained which accounts needed to be calculated immediately and which ones were settled monthly.","Si Nian listened quietly.","Extremely seriously.","This was Zhou Yueshen's factory.","She was his wife; she couldn't cause trouble for him."]},{"number":356,"title":"Chapter 356: Didn't We Agree to Sleep","paragraphs":["Zhou Yueshen spoke for a while before someone knocked on the door to discuss business.","Although there was a recent swine fever outbreak, it was impossible for people to truly stop eating pork.","Some restaurants and hotels still had a huge demand.","Without meat, they couldn't make anything.","Especially for those who couldn't enjoy a meal without meat.","Therefore, the visitors were still mostly business owners.","Perhaps worried about potential issues, they made a special trip to personally check on the situation.","Just to avoid any accidents.","Si Nian didn't go out. She sat in the office waiting for Zhou Yueshen. He had just mentioned that he would go back home tonight to grab some clothes.","Si Nian was waiting to go home together with him.","It was a holiday today, and with Little Dong and Little Han at home looking after their sister, she had nothing to worry about.","The office door wasn't closed. Si Nian looked over and saw a few young men. One of them handed Zhou Yueshen a cigarette, which he reached out to take. The two of them walked to the side with cigarettes in their mouths, talking about something unknown, but they seemed very familiar with each other.","Perhaps her gaze was too intense.","The man next to Zhou Yueshen glanced at Si Nian in the office.","He smiled and said, \"How is your wife so beautiful?\"","Zhou Yueshen cast a sidelong glance at the man.","He didn't reply.","Then he put out his cigarette, walked in, and placed his coat on the back of the chair Si Nian was leaning against. Many people were waiting for him outside.","Zhou Yueshen had specifically come in to greet her, and everyone was watching.","Their eyes carried a teasing glint.","Because it was the first time they had seen a woman in Zhou Yueshen's office.","Although they had heard he was married long ago, this man never mentioned his family affairs outside.","So everyone was quite curious about what kind of woman stood behind a man like him.","They never expected her to be so young and stunningly beautiful.","Everyone was saying that Factory Manager Zhou was truly blessed.","Zhou Yueshen didn't say much. He rummaged out a box of cookies from a nearby desk, opened it, and placed it in front of her.","Si Nian, still holding the ledger, paused, feeling as if this man was raising her like a child.","Zhou Yueshen was indeed afraid she would get bored and restless.","He also remembered she had eaten very little for lunch and would definitely be hungry.","These cookies were given by a client who visited before. He had never eaten them and had completely forgotten about them.","If Si Nian hadn't come, he wouldn't have remembered he had this stuff.","Zhou Yueshen said, \"I'll be right back.\"","Si Nian grabbed his arm. The man had taken off his coat, revealing thick, muscular arms with distinct, powerful lines. Si Nian signaled for him to bend down and whispered in his ear, \"I'll wait for you to come back and take a nap.\"","Zhou Yueshen's expression remained unchanged.","He lowered his eyes to look at her.","He said okay.","Si Nian didn't pester him, asking to tag along.","Zhou Yueshen had his own reasons for not letting her follow.","Si Nian couldn't guess them, but she wouldn't overthink it either.","Because in his eyes, she saw only herself.","Si Nian also didn't think she was unpresentable.","Seeing Zhou Yueshen go out, she continued looking at the ledger.","It wasn't actually difficult, and since Zhou Yueshen had taught her, she quickly understood it.","...","Meanwhile, at the Zhou family home.","Lunch was made by Zhou Zedong.","However, he had only learned how to make breakfast before; for lunch, he had merely been Si Nian's assistant.","Afraid he would forget how to do it, whenever Si Nian taught him, he would silently memorize it and then go back to his room to write it down in a notebook.","Zhou Zehan and Jiang Jiu came back from playing around, so hungry that their stomachs were touching their backs.","Seeing that Si Nian hadn't returned yet, they both wore bitter expressions.","\"Big brother, is Mom not coming back for lunch? Then what are we going to eat?\"","Zhou Zedong turned around, took out a notebook from the room, opened it, and handed it to him.","He spoke concisely, \"Order. I will only make one dish per person.\"","Zhou Zehan looked at the menu in the notebook and was dumbfounded!","His memory was still stuck on the fact that his brother only knew how to make pancakes.","He never knew his brother could actually cook so many things.","...","Inside the breeding farm.","After Si Nian finished reading, she tidied up Zhou Yueshen's desk. She didn't move his things, afraid that he wouldn't be used to it if she misplaced them. She just loved cleanliness and couldn't stand dust.","Inside Zhou Yueshen's office, separated by a curtain, there was a bed where he slept at night.","Zhou Yueshen didn't use a blanket when he slept, and he didn't feel cold either. It was mid-June now, and the days were exceptionally muggy and hot.","However, it was still cold at night when there were heavy rainstorms.","Si Nian had to be covered with a blanket to fall asleep.","Moreover, the houses here were generally low-built, and combined with the indoor dampness, it always felt chilly.","This resulted in a situation where it was hot outside but cool inside.","In such an environment, she figured she would develop rheumatism all over her body in less than a year.","Si Nian rummaged through a nearby cabinet and took out a fresh set of bedding. She had asked Zhou Yueshen to bring this over previously; they had them at home, so he didn't need to buy new ones.","However, the man didn't use them, so they had just been sitting here.","He probably only took them out in winter.","Si Nian changed the bedding, and it looked much more comfortable.","She would just take the replaced ones back later and wash them in the washing machine.","Once she started getting busy, she couldn't stop. She organized the clothes and the surrounding area neatly, instantly making the space feel much more spacious.","At this moment, a man came in to deliver an order form.","It required Zhou Yueshen's signature.","Since Zhou Yueshen wasn't there, Si Nian quickly walked out.","The other party didn't know her either. Suddenly seeing a stunningly beautiful woman, he was stunned for a moment.","He stuttered, \"You, you are...\"","Si Nian introduced herself and asked him what he needed from Zhou Yueshen.","Hearing that she was Factory Manager Zhou's wife, the man was even more surprised.","How could the factory manager's wife be so young?","Seeing Si Nian staring at him, he felt a bit embarrassed and hurriedly said he had an order form for Zhou Yueshen to sign.","Si Nian reached out, took it, and glanced at it. It was a new order.","However, she hadn't seen this client's name in Zhou Yueshen's ledger just now. Could it be a new client?","Si Nian didn't dare to sign it either. She told him to wait a moment and let Zhou Yueshen sign it when he returned.","Fortunately, Zhou Yueshen arrived quickly. The few men from earlier had already left, and he was alone.","He walked over, saw the man, and didn't ask any questions. He reached out to take the order form, glanced at it, didn't sign it, and told the man to take it back.","The man didn't dare to say anything; he quickly agreed and left.","Si Nian was a bit surprised but also relieved. Good thing she hadn't signed it for Zhou Yueshen just now.","She asked Zhou Yueshen, \"This is quite a large order. Why didn't you sign it?\"","Zhou Yueshen replied, \"This client is from the west side of the city. When we first came here, we had some conflicts. Now that there's a swine fever outbreak in the west side, them coming to me is not a good thing for our factory.\"","Indeed, modern business warfare was nothing more than framing each other.","As long as I ruin your reputation, I can dominate the market alone.","Now that there was a swine fever outbreak in the west side, while Zhou Yueshen's place was perfectly fine, and this client was a long-term client from the west side, there was no telling what kind of hidden motives they might have.","To prevent any accidents, Zhou Yueshen naturally had to be careful.","Right now, he just needed to break even.","After all, it was a critical period.","The two entered the room. Zhou Yueshen followed behind and coughed softly a few times.","His throat seemed a bit uncomfortable.","Si Nian turned her head to look at him: \"Are you feeling unwell?\"","Zhou Yueshen said, \"I might have caught a little cold.\"","Si Nian frowned. \"There might be more rain these next few days. It won't do to go on like this. You can't let your health break down. Do you have any medicine here?\"","Si Nian thought about getting him some medicine. She took a few quick steps and just as she pulled open a drawer to search, her arm was grabbed by him, and then she was pulled around to face him.","Si Nian was slightly stunned and looked up. Zhou Yueshen pressed her against the office desk, gripping her waist with both hands as he lowered his head.","\"Didn't you want to sleep?\"","Si Nian: Alright, alright, alright. I am after your body, and you are after mine too, aren't you..."]},{"number":357,"title":"Chapter 357: That hits hard, bro.","paragraphs":["Ambiguity flowed between the two as the temperature in the room rose. Si Nian opened her mouth, just about to say something, when Zhou Yueshen lowered his head and kissed her lips. His palm tightened, gripping her waist and lifting her slightly.","Si Nian tilted her neck back. Her lower back was pressed against the desk, leaving her with no room to retreat. Her chin angled slightly upward, forming a beautiful curve. Zhou Yueshen took advantage of the position, pressing against her and kissing her intermittently.","Clatter.","The ledger fell to the floor.","Si Nian snapped back to her senses and pushed him a little.","\"Don't, there are people outside.\"","Even though it was noon and everyone was resting.","Si Nian was still worried that someone might walk by and see them.","After all, the windows in this run-down office of his were broken.","Anyone walking by could see inside with a single glance.","Zhou Yueshen paused. He hadn't been intimate with her in a long time, and he was feeling a bit heated.","However, he also knew this wasn't the right place. He frowned slightly, suppressed his impulses, buried his head to kiss her fair, slender neck, and then wrapped his arm around her, pulling back the bed curtain and walking inside.","...","In the afternoon, Zhou Yueshen drove her home.","Si Nian felt stuffy. Just as she rolled down the window, she caught a whiff of a foul stench.","It smelled like rotting meat.","Si Nian frowned.","When she came in the morning, she definitely hadn't smelled this.","She hurriedly grabbed Zhou Yueshen's arm.","Zhou Yueshen had clearly smelled it too. The odor was so pungent that it was hard to ignore.","It was the stench of putrid flesh.","It was so overpowering it made one want to vomit.","Si Nian had a bad premonition.","Zhou Yueshen stopped the car. He didn't let her get out, instead walking toward the direction the smell was coming from by himself.","Not too far away, he stopped on a field ridge.","Si Nian could only see his back freeze.","But soon, he turned around and returned to the car.","Si Nian asked worriedly, \"Is there something there?\"","Zhou Yueshen started the car and drove off. Only when the smell faded did he say, \"In the water, there's a pile of dead pigs.\"","Although Si Nian had sensitively noticed something was wrong, she hadn't expected it to be this.","In an instant, her scalp went numb.","Did that mean someone had deliberately dragged pigs that died of swine fever all the way here to frame Zhou Yueshen's breeding farm?","Swine fever was highly contagious. Even though it was outside, it wasn't far away, and it was in the water. Where Zhou Yueshen's farm was located, rain easily caused water to accumulate. With rain expected these next few days, the water soaking those dead pigs would flow downstream, straight toward Zhou Yueshen's farm...","It was terrifying to think about.","Zhou Yueshen's farm was undergoing closed-off feeding recently, so no one was coming out, and naturally, no one had noticed.","By the time they found out, it would probably be too late.","Because tonight, there was going to be a massive rainstorm.","Si Nian said, \"What do we do now? Why don't you skip taking me back? I'll take the bus myself, and you hurry back to take care of it.\"","If they dealt with it now, there was still time.","If they waited, it would be too late.","Zhou Yueshen clearly hadn't expected their opponent's methods to be so vicious either.","If Si Nian hadn't come over, he probably wouldn't have discovered this.","Even though he knew it wasn't ideal to leave her at the bus station, there really was no time right now.","He gripped the steering wheel tightly with one hand, his eyes cold and dark.","When they had first arrived, they had avoided the provocations of their competitors whenever possible.","They didn't want to invite trouble.","But this time, Zhou Yueshen was truly furious.","He drove Si Nian to the station, held her hand without saying a word, his eyes growing even darker.","Si Nian knew he was definitely in a bad mood right now, so she didn't linger. She let go of his hand, got on the bus, and told him to hurry back.","Zhou Yueshen didn't reply. He watched her get on the bus, and as the vehicle started and slowly drove away, he turned, got into his car, stepped on the gas, turned the wheel, and drove off in one smooth motion.","Although Si Nian was very worried, she knew that for Zhou Yueshen to run such a big business, he definitely had his own methods.","Worrying was useless, and she couldn't help much anyway.","Upon returning home, the Second Child, who was sweeping the yard by the door, immediately dropped his broom and ran over.","\"Mom, you're back! Huh? Where's Dad?\"","Zhou Zehan tilted his head and looked behind her. Dad hadn't been home for several days.","Had Dad gone on a business trip again like before?","He blinked, feeling a pleasant surprise in his heart.","If that was the case, didn't that mean he could ride the long train with Mom to find Dad again? And he would get a vacation and not have to go to class! That would be great!","Seeing his face full of joy, Si Nian sighed helplessly.","\"Dad has some things to do. He'll be busy for a few days and will come back later.\"","\"Did Xiaohan miss Dad?\"","Zhou Zehan immediately nodded vigorously. \"I miss Dad! Mom, are we going to see Dad?\" If so, he was going to pack his new clothes this time!","Si Nian quickly said, \"We can't go see Dad right now. Dad will come back on his own in a few days.\"","There was swine fever near the farm; she certainly wasn't going to take the children there.","However, seeing the immediate disappointment on the Second Child's face, she was a little surprised.","When Zhou Yueshen was gone for so long before, she hadn't seen the children react much.","Occasionally asking about him was already the greatest respect they showed Zhou Yueshen.","Now it had only been a few days, and he missed him this much?","She reached out and rubbed the little guy's head. Her first order of business upon entering the house was to take a shower.","Even though she hadn't gotten close, after smelling that stench, Si Nian felt unclean all over and had been uncomfortable the whole ride.","That night, there was indeed another heavy rainstorm.","The trees outside rustled loudly in the wind.","Zhou Yueshen naturally didn't come back.","Instead, Yaoyao was awakened by the noise. She came knocking on her door with bare little feet, saying, \"Mommy, I'm scared.\"","Si Nian simply picked her up and brought her into the room to sleep with her.","Ever since Zhou Yueshen made a toddler bed for the little girl, she rarely slept with them anymore.","The thunder tonight was probably too loud, so it frightened her.","Si Nian held her, and soon the little girl fell asleep peacefully.","Exhaustion washed over her, and she drifted into a dream as well.","After the storm came a clear sky.","Early the next morning, the sun shone from the east, bringing beautiful, cloudless weather.","The air carried the scent of fresh grass and earth.","Having to go to work in such beautiful weather felt like a crime against nature.","As soon as Si Nian sat down, Wang Xiaoli came over and worriedly asked if her family's pig farm was okay.","The swine fever issue had been blowing up recently.","She heard that even the school didn't dare use pork anymore.","Wang Xiaoli knew Si Nian's husband ran a pig farm, so she was a bit concerned.","Si Nian shook her head, saying she wasn't too sure about the situation herself.","After all, since the incident happened yesterday, Zhou Yueshen hadn't contacted her.","It was hard to say what the exact situation was.","If those pigs that died from swine fever had been there since the morning or the middle of the night, and Zhou Yueshen's farm used running water, it would indeed be very dangerous.","Right now, she could only pray that the piglets were fine.","Otherwise, it would probably be a huge mess.","Seeing her like this, Wang Xiaoli knew the matter was truly serious.","Previously, rumors had just been spreading by word of mouth. People talked, but no one had seen anything with their own eyes.","Some people were still bold, thinking it was nothing.","Since pork was cheap right now, they bought more.","Hearing Si Nian say this, she realized she needed to quickly inform her troublesome mother-in-law to stop trying to score cheap deals.","Si Nian didn't have many classes that morning, so she simply went home early.","She stopped by the vegetable market on the way and noticed there were fewer pork stalls, though some still had people lining up to buy.","I heard the meat has been tested and there's no problem.","People didn't dare to eat it before, but now that they hear it's safe and cheap, naturally many people go to buy it.","Si Nian took a look and didn't stay long.","She bought some vegetables and went back. As for pork, she wasn't short of it; there was still a lot stored in the refrigerator at home.","These were previous stocks, so naturally she didn't worry.","Si Nian put the vegetables away, took out some pork bones from the refrigerator to make soup, and then threw a big bone to Da Huang.","\"Da Huang, how is it? Mom treats you well, right? At a time like this when others can't even afford meat, you still have bones to eat,\" Si Nian smiled while stroking its head.","Fang Hui, who originally wanted to come and ask if Si Nian's family still had meat, was speechless. \"Teacher Si, you are too careless. That's just an animal, how can you raise it like a son?\"","Si Nian's smile faded a bit: \"I like it.\"","Fang Hui choked, and said awkwardly: \"I heard about the swine fever recently, and I don't dare to buy meat outside. I heard your husband runs a pig farm, so your family shouldn't be short of meat. I want to buy some from you. My Bowen hasn't had meat for days. The child is still growing, how can he not eat meat?\"","Si Nian had some impression of Fang Bowen. She occasionally saw Fang Hui picking him up from school, but rarely saw the child come out to play.","He was even less sociable than her Xiaodong.","She shook her head: \"I'm sorry, I have many children at home, and there's nothing left.\"","It wasn't that she was really stingy and wouldn't even sell it.","It was just that the swine fever was serious now, and she worried that if Fang Hui bought it and had some problems after eating it, she would come to cause trouble for her.","Fang Hui curled her lips as expected, thinking Si Nian was stingy. It wasn't like she wasn't paying.","She was so willing to give meat to a dog, but not willing to sell it to her.","No wonder the people in the tube-shaped apartment building didn't have a good impression of her.","She didn't say much and turned away.","Since Si Nian was at home, she unfastened Da Huang's iron chain and let it stroll in the yard.","At this time, chewing on the bone, it followed Si Nian wherever she went.","Si Nian didn't let it out of the yard. Seeing someone passing by selling charcoal, she hurriedly ran out.","Just after buying the charcoal and preparing to go back inside, she saw Fu Qianqian pedaling a bicycle over.","Seeing Si Nian, she immediately waved to greet her, stopped the bicycle, and seeing people around, she asked in a low voice: \"Is your pig farm okay?\"","Si Nian neither nodded nor shook her head. \"You know too?\"","Fu Qianqian nodded: \"Last night our unit had a dinner party, and I ran into Yu Dong at the Youfu Restaurant. He told me.\"","Si Nian was surprised: \"Yu Dong?\"","Fu Qianqian said: \"Don't tell me you don't know. Yu Dong is the son of the boss of the largest restaurant in our city. I only found out yesterday. This guy hides deeply.\"","Si Nian generally knew something, but didn't ask much.","Hearing this now, she was also a bit surprised.","But she could also understand why Yu Dong's business ability was so good.","So he was the young boss of a big restaurant.","But it was quite a coincidence for these two to bump into each other while eating.","It wasn't that Si Nian couldn't see Yu Dong's intentions, but Fu Qianqian definitely couldn't.","She might as well say: \"Yu Dong is good-looking and has a good family background. Now that he is being urged to go home, he is probably busy getting married.\"","Fu Qianqian was pleasantly surprised: \"Really? Then won't we be able to attend a wedding banquet again?\"","Si Nian: \"...\" That was heartbreaking.","It really wasn't that she didn't want to help Yu Dong, but this girl Fu Qianqian simply didn't have the word \"love\" in her brain.","\"Your mom... bah, Aunt Si is sick, did you not go see her?\" Fu Qianqian asked. \"I heard that Aunt Si and Uncle Si are getting a divorce, and Aunt Si fell ill from anger. She's been in the hospital during this time, and Lin Sisi is taking care of her.\"","\"People in the courtyard are saying that you've moved to the city, not far from home, but when Aunt Si and her husband are divorcing, you don't help. When she's sick, you don't even visit, showing no affection at all. They say you are an ungrateful wretch, it's really awful.\"","Si Nian frowned. Without thinking, she guessed it must be Lin Sisi's doing.","She was out of prison and her reputation stank, so of course she had to find someone with a worse reputation to cover it up.","Not only ruining her reputation, but also making herself look filial...","Seeing her expression, Fu Qianqian sympathized with her: \"Before, when Lin Sisi was in prison, no one said anything about you. Now that she's back, it's like this all of a sudden. I don't believe she didn't do anything behind the scenes.\"","\"I say, Si Nian, what do you plan to do?\"","Now her husband's factory was also in trouble, and Si Nian was being gossiped about behind her back, literally attacked from front and back.","It was really too miserable.","Si Nian didn't care about her pitying expression. Carrying the charcoal and thinking, seeing no one passing by nearby, she simply said directly: \"To tell you the truth, I don't plan to do anything. I don't want to have any contact with the Si family and Lin Sisi.\"","Fu Qianqian immediately agreed: \"Right, I also think so. Once this person clings to you, you can't shake her off. Let me tell you, my brother was going to divorce her, but she and her mom used the college entrance examination to suppress us. Meaning that if my brother divorces her now, it will affect her taking the college entrance examination.\"","Fu Qianqian rolled her eyes hard: \"Before my brother was around, I didn't see her able to pass either.\"","Listening to her complaints, Si Nian also found it funny.","But according to the Fu family's face-saving nature, this moral kidnapping was the most suitable.","As for the divorce between Zhang Cuimei and Father Si, it was mentioned briefly in the novel, but it didn't make such a big fuss.","Speaking of which, this matter didn't give Lin Sisi a headache for nothing.","Liu Dongdong, who let the wolf into the house, not only targeted Fu Yang, but also Father Si.","Her sister had an affair with Father Si.","But in the novel, Lin Sisi's female lead halo was too strong, so this matter didn't cause any waves and was quickly resolved.","Father Si claimed to have been seduced, admitted his mistake later and was forgiven, and the family lived happily together.","In this era, there were too many cheating men. Many men still thought they were in ancient times, and with a little money they wished to have three wives and four concubines like in ancient times.","Women all knew, but for the sake of the family, they chose to endure.","But in the novel, it was because Lin Sisi stopped the loss in time that it didn't worsen.","Father Si and Mother Si definitely didn't make such a big fuss as to divorce.","This showed that during the time Lin Sisi was in prison, Liu Dongdong had done a lot of good deeds.","Without her mediating in the middle, Father Si definitely cheated.","Coupled with the fact that Lin Sisi was prepared to be divorced by the Fu family, Father Si felt she was useless, so he was eager to divorce now.","Maybe he could even have a son.","Si Nian just didn't understand why Lin Sisi, a perfectly fine female lead, focused all her attention on her. She wished she could stay a hundred thousand miles away from Lin Sisi, yet she insisted on getting involved.","On the contrary, no one had noticed anything wrong with Liu Dongdong beside her for such a long time.","She really didn't understand how she managed to get to that point in the novel.","Si Nian didn't answer Fu Qianqian's words, but said: \"I suspect my adoptive father is cheating, and that person is right in the family courtyard.\""]},{"number":358,"title":"Chapter 358: Flirting with Everyone","paragraphs":["Fu Qianqian's eyelids twitched, and her gossiping heart burned: Who, who, who? Auntie Liu or Aunt Wang? Last time I even saw Aunt Wang winking at my dad. My mom was so mad she didn't let my dad into their bedroom that night. I heard she winks at everyone she sees...","Si Nian: ...I don't think it's them.","Fu Qianqian: Then who is it?","Si Nian said, I'll tell you, but you have to do me a favor.","Fu Qianqian frowned. I won't do anything immoral.","Si Nian rolled her eyes at her. Don't worry.","With that, she whispered a few words into Fu Qianqian's ear.","All you have to do is find a chance to spread what I just told you to Lin Sisi. Once she hears it, she probably won't have the time to bother me anymore.","After listening, Fu Qianqian's face was full of shock. Aside from the shock, she also found it thrilling. She completely forgot that she had originally come over to mooch a meal and hurriedly pedaled away on her bicycle, promising she would definitely get it done.","Si Nian returned home, burned some charcoal in an iron basin, and set up a small iron rack at the door, preparing the ingredients for a courtyard barbecue.","By the time the children came home, she had already prepared all kinds of seasonings.","Spicy, sweet, there was a variety of flavors.","The children could eat whatever they wanted.","The children had never had barbecue like this before and were very excited. Rolling up their sleeves, they started grilling it themselves.","The meat sizzled with oil, and brushed with chili and five-spice powder, it made people drool with craving.","There had been an outbreak of swine fever recently, so everyone hadn't eaten meat for a long time.","It was the rush hour for getting off work and school, and the passing children and adults were all dazed by the tantalizing smell.","Next door, Fang Bowen, who was gnawing on bread, twitched his nose.","Saliva instantly secreted in his mouth.","He subconsciously looked up at Fang Hui sitting opposite him.","Fang Hui also wrinkled her nose, finding her food tasteless.","She now deeply regretted moving next to Si Nian's house.","Although she didn't have a good impression of Si Nian, Si Nian's cooking skills were simply too good.","At mealtimes, she could always smell all kinds of aromas that directly hit the taste buds.","They hadn't eaten pork for several days, and smelling this barbecue aroma now, they swallowed their saliva in disappointment with their own lack of restraint.","With the current swine fever, no one dared to eat pork.","Instead, they bought chicken, beef, and mutton.","But precisely because of this, the vendors jacked up the prices on the spot.","The already expensive meat became so pricey that even she couldn't afford it.","She had spent a lot of money renting this apartment, and later hiring a tutor for her son, signing him up for cram schools, and buying a radio.","Her savings of many years had been mostly spent.","Thinking about her current difficult situation, Fang Hui lost her appetite even more. She went into the study, found pen and paper, and started writing a letter.","...","Second Child and Jiang Jiu went out to show off, holding a large handful of meat skewers.","They stood eating for a while at one door, then at another. When they reached the entrance of the tube-shaped apartment building, the two stayed the longest.","The children who were lying on their stomachs or kneeling on the ground playing marbles inside the building could no longer sit still, casting covetous glances at them one after another.","In the past, if Zhou Zehan had held so many things in his hands, he would definitely have come over to share with them.","But ever since they listened to Da Zhuang and stopped playing with him, Zhou Zehan never gave them any more delicious food.","He didn't even share his birthday cake with them.","Although the families in the tube-shaped building had decent living conditions, they couldn't be considered rich.","Opportunities to eat meat were already rare in ordinary times.","Now, because of the swine fever, there were even fewer chances to eat meat.","Smelling this aroma, they swallowed mouthful after mouthful of saliva. They were simply intoxicated by the fragrance.","They regretted it. Had they known earlier, they never would have listened to Da Zhuang, never would have called Zhou Zehan a braggart, and never would have stopped playing with him.","Even if Zhou Zehan really was a braggart, he had indeed brought them food.","Unlike that Fang Bowen. Although he was said to be a little genius, he was very hard to get along with. He had visited twice before, and they thought his family was rich and would buy delicious food to share with them.","In the end, after they listened to Da Zhuang and played with him, he stopped coming and ignored them.","They had ended up losing both their second brother and Fang Bowen.","They stared eagerly at the meat in Zhou Zehan's hands, but at this moment, no one had the nerve to step forward and ask for a bite.","After all, last time they had made harsh remarks at the Zhou family's door, saying they would never play with him and Jiang Jiu again.","The group of children was filled with deep regret.","Zhou Zehan, having showed off enough, pulled Jiang Jiu along to head home.","He was terrified that the roasted meat would be eaten up by his older brother and younger sister.","Just as they reached the door, the two children spotted Fang Bowen.","Fang Bowen was leaning against the wall behind the Zhou family's door, seemingly peeking at something.","The two looked in the direction of his gaze in confusion, only to see that he was actually looking at the roasted meat in the courtyard.","\"Hey, are you hungry? Here.\"","Zhou Zehan handed over the roasted meat in his hand.","Fang Bowen was startled and almost lost his footing.","Turning around and seeing Zhou Zehan and Jiang Jiu staring at him, his small face immediately flushed red with shame.","Seeing the roasted meat handed over by Zhou Zehan, he swallowed his saliva unconvincingly but put on a tough front, \"Who... who cares about your meat? I am not hungry at all. I just dropped something. Yes, dropped something.\"","After saying that, with a bright red face, he stumbled and ran back home.","Zhou Zehan blinked blankly; it was the first time he had seen someone refuse meat when offered.","If it were him, who knows how happy he would be.","He hurriedly ran back home, his footsteps thudding.","Seeing his older brother skewering potato slices, he quickly ran over, \"Brother, I want to eat potatoes too.\"","Zhou Zedong looked up at him, saw his mouth covered in chili oil stains, and frowned in disgust.","He turned around, putting his back to him. \"I am skewering these for Mom. If you want to eat, skewer them yourself.\"","Si Nian did not eat much meat; she easily got sick of the greasiness.","Instead, she preferred vegetarian dishes.","Especially potatoes and dried tofu.","They were her absolute favorites.","Second Child used to dislike eating potatoes and dried tofu.","He thought meat tasted better.","But ever since he ate the potatoes and roasted dried tofu made by his mom, he loved them to death.","Back in their hometown when the fire was still burning, whenever he had free time, he would put a few slices of dried tofu on the stove to roast, dipping them in Si Nian's homemade five-spice chili powder.","It was so delicious that he almost swallowed his own tongue.","Now, besides meat, his favorites were roasted potatoes and roasted dried tofu.","These were also relatively popular and classic foods in their area.","Seeing that his brother was ignoring him, Zhou Zehan wiped his mouth, moved to the other side, and crouched down to skewer them himself.","Jiang Jiu also wiped his mouth, walked over to squat beside him, and said, \"Second Brother, I will roast potatoes for you.\"","Si Nian walked over with roasted meat and said, \"You two stop playing with water. If your clothes get wet, you will catch a cold. Xiaohan, you and Xiaojiu take these roasted ones to Grandpa and Grandma Jiang.\"","Second Child immediately stood up and reached out to take them.","Swallowing his saliva, he hurriedly delivered them to the Jiang family.","When he came back and saw his mom roasting potatoes, he immediately stuck close to her.","Acting spoiled, he said, Mom, Mom, I want to eat potatoes too.","Si Nian immediately smiled and asked, How many skewers do you want?","Xiao Han roughly counted on his fingers and said, Ten skewers will be enough. Mom said eating too much will give me a stomachache, so I will not eat too much.","Ten skewers is not too much?","This child was simply a bottomless pit.","He had just eaten so many meat skewers.","Si Nian found it amusing but let him have his way.","The child had not eaten well in the past, so this could be considered making up for it.","At first, she was quite worried that the child would eat too much and suffer from indigestion or get fat.","But after so long, although Xiao Han had put on some flesh, he was not fat; instead, his height was shooting up.","Si Nian noticed that this child's bone structure was unusually large.","In less than two years, his build was already larger than that of his peers.","Beside him, Jiang Jiu looked very delicate and refined.","No wonder this child could grow to over 180 centimeters in his past life despite being malnourished.","In this life, would he not grow to 190 centimeters, just like his dad?","Besides, he had loved sports since he was little and had a strong constitution.","Speaking of which, after all this time, apart from one toothache, even when the little guy caught a cold, he would basically recover by the next day.","She had to sigh in admiration at the strong physical fitness of a rural child.","Looking at Xiao Dong, on the other hand.","Si Nian looked at her eldest son.","Xiao Dong had not changed much; he just looked a bit fleshier, but his height had not increased as obviously as the Second Child.","He still looked thin.","Si Nian was a bit worried about whether the child was lacking some nutrients.","For instance, calcium deficiency or iron-deficiency anemia could cause this kind of situation.","It seemed she needed to find time to take him for a check-up.","Otherwise, if this child could only reach 170-something centimeters in this life, he would probably still be sad.","Si Nian also wanted them all to grow to 188 centimeters, the most perfect height.","Taking them out would give her so much face.","Si Nian thought about this while grilling the skewers.","Mom, Mom, Xiao Jiang and I just went to the tube-shaped apartment building while eating skewers. When Little Pig and the others saw us eating skewers, they drooled, but I did not pity them at all.","The Second Child stood beside Si Nian, scrambling to help while speaking.","Si Nian smiled. This child held quite a grudge. When Little Pig and his group came to cause trouble on his birthday before, the little guy did not say anything, but he had kept it in his heart.","He had treated those kids as friends, feeling happy and sad for them, but they ended up causing trouble on his birthday. The Second Child hated evil like an enemy.","Si Nian asked, Then who do you think is pitiful?","The Second Child thought for a moment and said, I think Fang Bowen is pitiful. I can see him doing homework in the study every day. He writes during the day, writes after school, writes at night, and even writes during the holidays...","As he spoke, he shuddered himself.","It was too terrifying. In the past, he thought it was scary enough that his brother studied every day.","He did not expect Fang Bowen to be even more terrifying than his brother.","Moreover, his mom did not know how to make delicious food.","When he ran into him in the morning, he saw Fang Bowen eating dry bread.","It did not look tasty at all.","Unlike himself, who got to eat all sorts of different breakfasts in rotation.","Comparing the two, Zhou Zehan felt that even though he was a bit clumsy and not as smart as Fang Bowen.","He was much happier than Fang Bowen.","Thinking about this, a rippling smile could not help but appear on the little guy's face.","Hearing Fang Bowen's name, Si Nian was momentarily stunned.","It was indeed true. Although she hadn't seen Fang Bowen often, the child seemed to have no playtime at all. She had seen a tutor coming over every day, and on weekends, Fang Hui would even take him out for extra tutoring classes.","He rarely went out and basically spent all his time reading and doing homework.","Such a life was simply suffocating.","Then she heard Second Child say, \"I just saw him hiding by our door. Fang Bowen definitely wanted to eat barbecue too. Mom's barbecue is so delicious, nobody dislikes it. But when I offered him some, he refused. He's so silly, turning down free food.\"","Si Nian paused for a moment.","She had run into the child a few times; he was just as aloof and arrogant as Fang Hui.","She didn't expect him to do something like this.","After all, he was still young. He might care about his pride on the surface, but deep down, he probably really wanted a bite.","Forget it, what did this have to do with her?","Si Nian shook her head and didn't dwell on it. There was no way Fang Hui would ever let her own biological son go hungry.","As soon as Fu Qianqian returned home, she heard the older women gossiping under the large locust tree in the family compound about the Si family's affairs.","Divorces were rare in the family compound, so there wasn't usually much gossip.","Now that someone was suddenly getting a divorce—and it was the highly controversial Si family at that—it naturally became the prime topic of conversation after meals.","Initially, they were just discussing why the couple was divorcing. Later, when Lin Sisi was released from prison, the topic shifted to her.","But at some point, the conversation had turned toward Si Nian.","\"Is she really that sick? She's been in the hospital for so long and still hasn't been discharged?\"","\"I heard she got so angry she developed appendicitis and needs surgery. The other day, Lin Sisi even came to me to borrow money, saying she would work part-time to pay me back.\"","\"Sigh, it's quite pitiful when you think about it. Encountering something like this right after getting out of prison. Lin Sisi hasn't been home for long, but she hasn't had even two days of peace.\"","\"Yeah, is there really a need to borrow money like this? Didn't her adopted daughter, Si Nian, move to the city? I heard she's working as a foreign language teacher at the foreign language elementary school, and her husband bought a big villa on Old East Street. She can't even spare this little bit of money? That's too heartless, isn't it?\"","\"She's so arrogant now. Now that she has money, she looks down on people. I heard that when Lin Sisi went to jail, the matter could have been settled privately. Who would have thought that even after the money was returned, she still wouldn't let it go and insisted on sending Lin Sisi to prison. As for the couple's divorce, she must be playing tricks behind the scenes. That girl truly has the heart of a viper.\"","Seeing their words becoming increasingly exaggerated, Fu Qianqian's face darkened. She stopped her bicycle and retorted, \"Bullshit! That's not what happened at all. I saw it all. Uncle Si divorced Aunt Si because she has no morals. She spoke up for human traffickers and got reported, which is why Uncle Si divorced her.\"","\"I even saw Uncle Si bring another woman home, which is what made Aunt Si so angry she fell ill. What does any of this have to do with Si Nian?\"","\"Lin Sisi stole money herself, and you're still speaking up for her. Be careful, or she might steal your money in the future too.\"","After saying that, she gave a cold snort, ignored the awkward expressions of the crowd, and rode away on her bicycle.","The group's faces turned pale and green.","It was extremely awkward.","Eventually, someone seemed to realize something and exclaimed in surprise, \"Did Deputy Battalion Commander Si really bring a woman home? Didn't Lin Sisi say that the couple was divorcing because of something Si Nian said to Deputy Battalion Commander Si?\"","\"Speaking of this, I actually just remembered something. Last time I passed by Battalion Commander Si's house, I saw a woman washing clothes at his door. But I heard she's his nanny's older sister, filling in because the nanny was sick...\"","\"No way, Battalion Commander Si actually took a fancy to the nanny's sister? No matter how bad Zhang Cuimei might be, he shouldn't go for a nanny.\"","\"Isn't that nanny Lin Sisi's friend? I heard she took her in out of pity. Who in our compound can afford a nanny? I remember thinking Battalion Commander Si's family was living quite extravagantly.\"","\"I remember too. She used to make food and send it over to the Fu family often, and she's quite pretty. I heard she even went to the Northwest before. During that time, it was her sister who came over to take care of Battalion Commander Si...\"","\"Hiss, a lone man and a lone woman together, if nothing really happened, why would Battalion Commander Si be in such a hurry to get a divorce?\"","Saying this, everyone exchanged a look.","Their eyes carried a hint of mutual understanding.","...","Si Nian was now teaching English to the kids in the gifted class.","Her son was in the gifted class.","When classes ended in the afternoon, they could go home together.","Today, however, Si Nian didn't plan to go straight home. Instead, she intended to take the children to the hospital for a physical checkup.","Just to see if they were healthy.","Eldest Child had only been to the hospital once, and that was when Si Nian was pushed down by Grandma Liu.","Hearing his mother say she was taking him for a checkup now, he couldn't help but feel a little nervous.","Was there something wrong with his body?","Otherwise, why would his mother take him for a medical checkup?","He thought to himself, feeling uneasy.","The two of them were holding Yaoyao's hand, waiting at the door for Zhou Zehan. It was this guy's turn to clean up today; everyone else had already left, but he still hadn't come out.","Si Nian looked around and suddenly noticed another small figure who hadn't left yet.","She looked over; it was Fang Bowen.","Fang Bowen didn't look too good; his face was rather pale.","Fang Hui had probably been delayed today and surprisingly hadn't arrived yet.","Seeming to realize his mother wasn't coming, Fang Bowen bit his lip, glanced at them, and started walking home alone with his backpack.","Si Nian frowned. Just as she withdrew her gaze, there was a thud. Looking back, Fang Bowen had collapsed on the ground—"]},{"number":359,"title":"Chapter 359: Food Poisoning","paragraphs":["Hospital.","\"What kind of parents are you? The child has food poisoning and you are only bringing him in now. Do you not know how dangerous this is?\"","As soon as the doctor walked out, he caught sight of Si Nian and started scolding her.","Si Nian replied calmly, \"I am not his parent, I am his teacher.\"","The doctor choked on his words. \"Uh... I am sorry. Where are the child's parents?\"","Si Nian said, \"The school has already been asked to contact the child's parent. Do not worry, when she gets here, please do not hold back. Scold her as much as you want.\"","Doctor: \"...\"","You have said everything, what else is there for me to say?","\"Mom, what is food poisoning? It will not be like what happened to me before, right?\" Hearing about food poisoning, Second Child's heart suddenly skipped a beat, and he looked at Si Nian in terror.","Seeing his fear, Si Nian just remembered that when the child was little, he had been poisoned by Zhou Yueshen's deranged ex-wife. He had almost died.","She quickly comforted him, \"Of course it is not exactly the same. Food poisoning can happen from eating spoiled and unclean food.\"","Second Child's gaze fell on Fang Bowen on the hospital bed, and he asked in confusion, \"Then why did he eat bad food?\"","Si Nian shook her head. \"Mom does not know either.\"","Although Fang Hui was strict with this child, she should not be treating him too poorly. How could he get food poisoning?","She wanted to ask the doctor a few more questions, but then she saw a group of people rushing over carrying children.","These children all had similar symptoms: vomiting, diarrhea, and a purplish complexion.","Seeing so many children, the doctor's face turned green. \"This is clearly food poisoning. What is going on today? Why are there so many children with food poisoning? What did they eat?\"","\"Boohoo, doctor, please save our children. They only ate a few pieces of pork and became like this, boohoo...\"","\"What, pork? Quick, bring them in.\"","Si Nian pulled the two children aside to make way, watching as the group of children was sent into the emergency room.","Second Child just took a curious glance and was shocked. He pulled Si Nian's hand and said, \"Mom, it is Da Zhuang and Little Pig and the others!\"","Si Nian had not noticed at first, but after her son said that, she realized that these children were exactly the group that often played together in the apartment building.","Everyone also noticed her and immediately cast hateful glares in her direction.","\"Damn those black-hearted pork vendors, actually selling us meat from pigs that died of swine fever. Si Nian, is this your husband's shady business? You will all die a horrible death!\"","\"Yesterday, her son ran over to show off his meat to my son, and when my son got home, he threw a tantrum demanding to eat meat. It is all their fault!\"","\"You pay for my son!\"","Hearing this, Si Nian's face darkened. Just as she was about to speak, Fang Hui, who had received the news, hurried over.","Hearing the curses from Da Zhuang's mother and the others, Fang Hui's face immediately fell. \"I was wondering how my son could get food poisoning. It must be because you, Si Nian, gave him meat yesterday, right!\"","When she just received the call from the school saying her son had fainted from food poisoning, Fang Hui almost passed out herself.","How could her perfectly fine son get food poisoning? She remembered that yesterday afternoon, the Zhou family was having a barbecue in the yard. It smelled so good that her son barely ate anything at home. Later, when she came out of the study, she saw her son returning from outside looking guilty, but she did not think much of it at the time.","Looking at it now, it must have been when she was not around that he was given something unclean to eat.","Fang Hui's face looked extremely awful.","Fang Hui's words made the crowd cast even more hostile glares at Si Nian.","Second Child grew anxious hearing her blame Si Nian, and quickly said, \"We did not give him anything to eat! I offered it to him, but he did not want it! Our meat is good meat!\"","Fang Hui, with bloodshot eyes, did not believe it. \"Who knows if you gave it to him or not.\"","Si Nian stopped her agitated son and slowly said, \"Do you know why I did not sell you meat yesterday when you offered to pay for it?\"","Fang Hui frowned. \"What do you mean?\"","Si Nian said, \"Because I wanted to prevent exactly this kind of thing from happening.\"","Fang Hui's face darkened.","\"If your son had eaten our meat yesterday afternoon, something would have happened last night. It is impossible for him to only faint this afternoon. You should understand this basic common sense.\"","Si Nian calmly stated the facts, then looked at the group of aunties from the apartment building.","\"If you suspect my husband, please take the proper legal channels and report it to the police station. We are willing to accept an investigation. But once it is proven that we are innocent, please be prepared in advance to pay the subsequent compensation fees.\"","She originally thought that since they were all neighbors, she would tolerate it if she could and did not want to make a big fuss.","But these people were really going too far, actually blaming this on them.","It was truly bizarre.","Hearing her tell them to call the police, the group of women suddenly fell silent.","They indeed had never seen the Zhou family selling pork around here.","Previously, some people from the apartment building wanted to find Zhou Yueshen, thinking that since they were all neighbors, they could get it a little cheaper.","But then they found out that Zhou Yueshen's farm was too far from here, so he had no intention of selling here.","Because of this, everyone was still gossiping privately, saying that the Zhou family was probably afraid they would haggle, so they deliberately did not open a shop here.","Privately, they all said the Zhou family was stingy.","Moreover, there were so many pig farmers in the city, who knew who it actually was?","If it was really a misunderstanding, would they not have to pay compensation?","Besides, everyone saw Si Nian's family eating barbecue yesterday, and their two children were perfectly fine...","For a moment, the whole group stopped talking.","Fang Hui, however, felt that Si Nian was just bluffing.","She was not as timid and afraid of trouble as these people from the apartment building.","Moreover, she never bought those messy junk foods outside for her son to eat, and her son had always been fine before.","For him to suddenly be like this now, it could only be because he ate something he should not have at the Zhou family's place yesterday afternoon.","Fang Hui stubbornly insisted and was determined to have it checked.","\"I have not bought any pork recently. My son has food poisoning now, and I really cannot think of anyone else but you.\"","She said coldly, \"Do not worry, if it has nothing to do with you, I will definitely apologize to you. But if it really is you, then please, Teacher Si, prepare in advance to compensate us and kneel down to apologize.\"","Her son was so excellent and had now entered the genius class. She heard that Si Nian's eldest son had also gotten in.","Maybe these two children were secretly jealous of her son's excellence and secretly forced him to eat something he should not have, causing this to happen.","Otherwise, how could her son inexplicably get food poisoning?","The more Fang Hui thought about it, the gloomier her face became.","Hearing this, Si Nian laughed out of anger. \"Alright. By the same logic, I accept your proposal. But if the test results show it was not because of us, then please, Miss Fang Hui, kneel down to apologize and compensate us as well.\"","Fang Hui looked disdainful. For a moment, sparks flew between the two of them, neither willing to back down.","Everyone held their breath.","After waiting for who knows how long, the doctor finally came out.","Fang Hui hurried forward and said, \"Doctor, doctor, how is my son? Was he also poisoned by swine fever meat?\"","The doctor froze for a moment and asked in confusion, \"You are?\"","Fang Hui said, \"I am Fang Bowen's parent. I just received a message from the school saying my son has food poisoning, and I suspect he also ate sick pork.\"","After saying that, she turned her head and cast a cold look at Si Nian."]},{"number":360,"title":"Chapter 360: As Bad as the Stepmother","paragraphs":["Hearing her words, the doctor's face immediately darkened, and her voice became much sharper. \"Oh, so you do know your son is poisoned? People who didn't know better would think his parents were dead. You didn't even know your child had food poisoning?\"","Fang Hui choked, her face flushing red from the scolding.","She hadn't expected this person's words to be so venomous. Embarrassed, she said, \"I... I've just been busy with work, and this was an accident. I suspect someone secretly fed my son diseased pork, which caused this.\"","\"Didn't those other children also get sick from eating diseased pork?\"","The doctor scoffed coldly. \"What nonsense are you spouting? Is the other kids' situation the same as your son's?\"","\"Your son was poisoned by eating spoiled bread; his symptoms are different from those children's. Your son's condition is much worse than theirs. The child had barely anything in his stomach. Even when we induced vomiting, he only threw up a little bit of bread mush, and it was sour! I don't know what kind of mother you are. You dress up all fancy, but your child can't even get a proper meal?\"","\"Also, here is the medical report. Food poisoning is only secondary. More importantly, he suffers from severe hypoglycemia, calcium deficiency, and extreme physical exhaustion, which led to his fainting. He needs to be hospitalized for observation for a period of time. Please go pay the fees first.\"","After saying that, the doctor rolled her eyes at Fang Hui, then walked over to Da Zhuang's mother and her group and started scolding them.","Her scolding was incredibly harsh.","The group of parents, who were usually quite arrogant, were now flushed red from the reprimand, unable to lift their heads.","Si Nian couldn't help but give a mental thumbs-up to this doctor who dared to speak her mind and scold them.","After a moment, she looked mockingly at the stiff Fang Hui.","\"Miss Fang Hui, you haven't forgotten what you just said, have you?\"","Fang Hui's face was deathly pale, and she looked extremely embarrassed.","She hadn't expected that her son really hadn't eaten pork, but was poisoned by eating bread.","Usually, her own cooking wasn't very good, and combined with being busy at work, she would just buy all sorts of bread for her son to keep at home.","Fang Hui had studied abroad, where she had developed the habit of drinking milk and eating bread.","She ate like this herself, and to maintain her figure, she basically stopped eating staple foods.","It was fine before; at least she had hired a nanny to come cook.","But after her money ran out, she rarely hired a nanny and cooked everything herself.","However, her cooking skills were not great, and her son didn't like eating it.","She just assumed her son was a picky eater.","Who would have thought...","Fang Hui tightly clutched the medical report in her hand.","Meeting Si Nian's mocking gaze, her face flushed red. \"I-I'm sorry... This, this was a misunderstanding on my part.\"","Fang Hui laughed awkwardly. \"I was just too worried just now. Concern leads to confusion, which is why I was so angry. Teacher Si, please be the bigger person and forgive my offense.\"","Si Nian sneered. \"I'm sorry, Miss Fang, but I'm exactly the kind of petty person who holds grudges.\"","\"If it weren't for the fact that I happened to bring my son to the hospital for a checkup today, you wouldn't have even known your son was in trouble. If you don't thank me, that's fine; I don't demand gratitude. I do good deeds to accumulate my own karma. But being falsely accused and bitten back is not something I can tolerate. Miss Fang, please kneel. I can accept it.\"","Fang Hui's face looked awful, her hands trembling with anger. \"Teacher Si, you should be forgiving when possible. I've already apologized. If that's not enough, I'll compensate you. We see each other around all the time, is there really a need to be so aggressive?\"","Si Nian refused to yield an inch. \"You really know how to joke. Did I suggest the kneeling apology? Wasn't this proposed by Miss Fang herself? Why is it that now you realize you're in the wrong, you're backing out and refusing to honor your word?\"","\"Is it that hard to admit you're an ungrateful person?\"","Fang Hui gritted her teeth in fury.","\"Mom...\" A weak voice sounded from behind, breaking the awkward situation.","The group turned around, only to see Fang Bowen standing by the hospital room door, his small face deathly pale, holding himself up against the doorframe.","\"Don't make my mom kneel. It's all my fault,\" Fang Bowen said, his eyes red as he looked at Si Nian.","If he hadn't sneaked out to peek yesterday afternoon, his mother wouldn't have misunderstood Teacher Si's family.","It was his fault.","Fang Hui saw him, abruptly turned and walked over.","Under everyone's astonished gazes, she slapped Fang Bowen across the face.","The crowd stood frozen in shock!","Fang Bowen sat on the ground, staring blankly at Fang Hui, motionless for a long time.","Fang Hui's face was almost distorted with rage. \"You still have the nerve to speak? If it weren't for you, would I be this humiliated? How many times have I told you? Don't sneak out by yourself. You just won't listen, will you? Apologize to your Auntie Si right now!\"","Si Nian was also stunned by Fang Hui's actions.","Seeing how Fang Hui usually took pride in her son, she had thought she treated Fang Bowen very well.","She never expected that when the child was in such a serious condition, her first reaction wouldn't be concern, but rather blaming and beating him.","At this moment, Si Nian suddenly understood why Second Child had said Fang Bowen was pitiful.","Being stuck with a mother like this, how could he not be pitiful? He really had the worst luck in the world.","Fang Bowen's small face was swollen, but he stubbornly held back his tears. Just as he was about to open his mouth, Si Nian said, \"There's no need. The child did nothing wrong.\"","Fang Bowen looked at her.","Si Nian looked away; anyone raising a child really couldn't bear to see such a thing.","She looked mockingly at Fang Hui. \"It must be hard on Miss Fang, pushing all the blame onto a child just to give yourself a way out. When it comes to being disgraceful, the child really can't compare to you.\"","Fang Hui's face turned livid with anger.","After Si Nian finished speaking, she didn't spare the group another glance and led the three terrified children away.","The doctor, recovering from her shock, was also furious and rushed forward. \"Hey, what kind of parent are you, hitting people! This is too much, are you even human?\"","Although things had been delayed today, Si Nian didn't want the trip to be in vain, so she simply had all three children examined.","However, the hospital was about to close, and with tomorrow and the day after being Saturday and Sunday, they would have to wait until Monday to pick up the results.","Si Nian simply took the children home first.","On the way back, Second Child had a solemn expression. \"Mom, did I do something wrong?\"","Si Nian paused for a moment. \"What do you mean, did something wrong?\"","Second Child pursed his lips and said, \"It's all my fault for showing off the meat skewers and giving meat to Fang Bowen, otherwise they wouldn't have blamed Mom.\"","Second Child was filled with remorse, hating himself for loving to show off so much.","Otherwise, when Fang Bowen, Da Zhuang, and the others got sick today, it wouldn't have been blamed on Mom and Dad.","Si Nian shook her head. \"You didn't do anything wrong, but it's true that we shouldn't interact with them in the future to avoid trouble.\"","Even though Si Nian said that, Second Child knew it was definitely still his fault.","He suddenly really disliked himself.","Just because life was happy now, he got complacent and showed off everywhere.","He had caused so much trouble for his family.","Seeing him stay silent, Si Nian patted his head.","\"Alright, stop thinking about it. It's all in the past.\"","Second Child still frowned. \"Mom, I have another question.\"","Si Nian: \"Go ahead.\"","Second Child said, \"Mom, do you think Auntie Fang is really Fang Bowen's mother?\"","Si Nian was taken aback. \"Why do you say that?\"","Second Child thought carefully and said, \"Because I think she's just as bad as my previous stepmother.\"","Si Nian fell silent.","Fang Hui had moved here alone with her child and never once mentioned her husband. It was only through the passing gossip of the apartment building's residents that people heard her family was incredibly wealthy, and that her husband was a rich man from Jing City.","They said he ran a business, was always busy, and things of that nature.","Everyone envied her and never gave it a second thought.","No one truly knew what kind of man Fang Bowen's father actually was.","Just as Si Nian was pondering this, a familiar car pulled up and stopped right in front of their group."]},{"number":361,"title":"Chapter 361: Si Nian is a Lucky Star","paragraphs":["Si Nian looked over in surprise, \"Zhou Yueshen?\"","The Second Child also called out happily, \"Dad!\"","Yaoyao: \"Dada!\"","Zhou Zedong: \"Dad.\"","Zhou Yueshen got out of the car, his gaze sweeping over Si Nian and the three children.","Seeing that they were fine, his nerves, which had been tense the whole way, finally relaxed.","After finishing his work at the factory, the first thing he did was rush home.","But it was already past working hours, and the house was completely empty.","Worried that something had happened, Zhou Yueshen took a trip to the school.","He learned from people at the school that Si Nian had taken a child to the hospital, saying the child had fainted.","Thinking something had happened to his three children, he hurried over to the hospital.","He didn't expect to run into her and the three children right here.","\"How is it, is everything okay? I just went to your school and heard that Little Dong or Little Han fainted?\" He frowned at the three rosy-cheeked children, who didn't look at all like they had just fainted.","Hearing this, Si Nian burst into laughter. \"Of course not. It wasn't Little Dong or Little Han, it was the neighbor's kid. I just happened to run into them and brought them to the hospital, but everything is fine now.\"","Zhou Zehan walked over, struggling to tilt his head up to look at Zhou Yueshen. \"Yeah, Dad, I wouldn't faint. I'm very strong. Mom said strong kids don't faint.\"","Zhou Yueshen looked down gently, bent over, and picked up his son, bouncing him a little. Indeed, the eight-year-old little guy already had quite a bit of weight to him.","He had been raised into a chubby little piglet by Si Nian.","\"It's good that everyone is fine.\"","Zhou Yueshen looked at Si Nian. \"Get in the car, I'll take you all home.\"","Si Nian agreed and got into the car holding her daughter.","Little Dong followed closely behind. The Second Child quickly slid down from his dad and tried to squeeze in to sit with Si Nian.","Zhou Yueshen grabbed him by the back collar and pulled him out.","\"Don't crowd your mom. Sit in the front.\"","With that, he opened the car door, stuffed him inside, and pulled the seatbelt over to buckle him in.","The Second Child turned his head and saw his older brother smiling at him.","He instantly became unhappy, pouting and looking complainingly at Zhou Yueshen, who was getting into the car next to him. \"Dad, why did you come back?\"","As Zhou Yueshen pulled his own seatbelt and buckled it, he tilted his head to look at him and asked in a low voice, \"What? You don't want Dad to come back?\"","The Second Child hurriedly shook his head. \"No, I was just thinking that if you weren't going to come back for a long time, we would take a long, long train with Mom to go see you.\"","He thought that since Zhou Yueshen hadn't been home for a long time, he must have gone on a far journey.","Gone to a very, very faraway place.","Zhou Yueshen let out a low chuckle, his chest vibrating slightly.","His voice was deep. \"That's very thoughtful of you.\"","The Second Child hummed, \"Of course, because Mom says I'm a good child with love and loyalty.\"","Zhou Yueshen turned his head and glanced at Si Nian.","Si Nian had an expression that said she had a headache.","The corners of his lips curled up, and he started the car.","The car soon stopped at their front door.","The Second Child ran out of the car like a little cannonball.","Zhou Zedong followed right behind him.","Zhou Yueshen parked the car and walked inside.","The family sat on the sofa. Si Nian poured Zhou Yueshen a cup of tea, walked over to sit beside him, and then asked, \"How are things at the factory?\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded slightly.","\"It's over now. The higher-ups are conducting massive inspections, and more than a dozen breeding farms have been shut down. Thanks to your visit that day, otherwise my farm probably wouldn't have survived either.\"","Si Nian was surprised. \"The higher-ups investigated?\"","Zhou Yueshen glanced at his son and daughter, who were fighting over the remote control, and withdrew his gaze.","\"Yes, right early in the morning on the second day after you left, the investigators came over.\"","They had narrowly escaped a disaster with this matter. Even though Zhou Yueshen had connections, if he had been labeled a malicious merchant, he would have faced a lot of trouble.","Fortunately, they found out in time that day and disposed of all those things.","The inspection also found no problems.","Because of this, everyone was praising Si Nian as a lucky star.","Someone who brought him good fortune.","Zhou Yueshen felt the same way.","After Si Nian came to his side, it seemed like all troublesome matters were easily resolved.","Si Nian was shocked.","Was it really such a coincidence?","Someone just happened to want to sabotage Zhou Yueshen's farm, and the very next day someone went to investigate. It was really hard not to suspect something fishy was going on.","If she hadn't gone over that day, and Zhou Yueshen hadn't left the farm, perhaps they truly wouldn't have discovered the plot.","But the opponent was quite capable too. How did they know that Zhou Yueshen and his team were currently doing closed-off feeding and not going out?","Just to prevent the meat from spoiling, Zhou Yueshen always slaughtered and processed everything in the morning and immediately sent it away.","They didn't deliver goods during the hot noon hours.","The opponent clearly knew about Zhou Yueshen's situation to come up with such an underhanded tactic.","This way, Zhou Yueshen and the others wouldn't notice any problems at all.","When the investigators went over the next day and found a pile of dead pigs there, even if the pigs inside the farm were fine, the blame would definitely fall on Zhou Yueshen's head.","\"Then since they investigated so many places, why is there still tainted meat flowing out? Many families thought it was fine, but after eating it, their kids were sent to the hospital.\"","Zhou Yueshen said, \"These symptoms aren't just happening here, which is why the higher-ups are taking it so seriously and cracking down on malicious manufacturers. But there are always people looking to make a quick buck, so they transfer this meat at low prices to those greedy for a bargain.\"","Si Nian took a sip of tea and sighed.","Zhou Yueshen glanced at her.","\"It will pass soon, don't worry.\"","Zhou Yueshen wasn't lying to her. The swine fever incident came quickly and left just as quickly.","After hearing that meat which had passed professional inspections was fine and safe to eat, everyone went back to line up at the supply and marketing cooperatives to buy meat.","After all, professionally inspected meat gave them peace of mind.","It was just that the daily supply was limited, so people had to rush for it.","Si Nian had originally been worried whether this would affect Zhou Yueshen's business.","After all, the incident of malicious merchants selling diseased pork had made the public vigilant. They preferred to pay a bit more at the cooperative rather than buy from private street vendors.","But soon, she realized her worries were for nothing.","The account bills Zhou Yueshen brought over actually contained cooperation orders from several supply and marketing cooperatives in the city.","In other words, the pork sold by these cooperatives was all supplied by Zhou Yueshen's factory.","She truly had worried for nothing. This man's ability to build a business and eventually make a fortune wasn't based entirely on luck.","While she herself didn't care much, the people in the tube-shaped apartment building started acting smug.","Hearing that everyone was now only eating pork that had been tested safe, within just a few days, a whole bunch of breeding farms went bankrupt, and their bosses fled.","Everyone assumed that the Zhou family definitely wouldn't be able to stay in business either.","Ever since the Zhou family moved here, they ate well and drank well every day, having meat at every meal. Even what their dog ate was better than what the neighbors had.","Now that they were finally about to go bankrupt, everyone was overjoyed.","Last time they even mocked them at the hospital, and now they were finally getting their comeuppance, right?","When the kids in the apartment building heard that the Second Child's family would no longer be able to afford meat, they were so happy they spun around in circles.","\"The Zhou family is bankrupt, the oldest is crying, the second has to farm, the third picks up trash, and Jiang Jiu still gets bullied~\"","A group of kids, emboldened by their numbers, deliberately surrounded the Second Child and Jiang Jiu on their way home, singing and dancing around them.","\"You're talking nonsense, my family isn't bankrupt!\"","The Second Child wanted nothing more than to step forward and beat them up, but the group of kids ran away as soon as they finished singing.","For a moment, he didn't know who to chase after."]},{"number":362,"title":"Chapter 362: Offending Someone","paragraphs":["The two kids gritted their teeth in childish anger.","Zhou Yueshen bought some groceries on his way home. As soon as he entered the house, he paused, seeing his son wiping away tears.","\"What's wrong?\"","Zhou Zehan wiped his tears and asked, \"Dad, is our family going bankrupt?\"","Zhou Yueshen was stunned. He frowned immediately, \"Who said that?\"","Zhou Zehan said miserably, \"Many people are saying it. They say no one is buying our pork anymore, that our pork is dirty and comes from sick pigs. Dad, do we have to go back to Xingfu Village?\"","Although he would be happy to go back to Xingfu Village, he couldn't bear to leave his friends.","Plus, there was so much good food in the city, and he hadn't tried it all yet.","Seeing Zhou Yueshen frown, he hurriedly explained, \"Dad, I don't mean I'd despise you for going bankrupt. Don't worry, even if you go bankrupt, I will still call you Dad.\"","Zhou Yueshen didn't know whether to laugh or cry, and he pinched the boy's little face with his large hand.","Zhou Zehan smiled at him, then said conflictedly, \"It's just that Mom still has to teach. If Mom doesn't go back, I can only choose Mom. When the time comes, can you please not force me to go with you?\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","He was touched for nothing.","Beside them, Zhou Zedong, who was reading a book, couldn't help but roll his eyes at his younger brother.","What a fool.","He retracted his gaze and continued reading, but his mind unconsciously dwelled on what his brother had said.","Just then, Zhou Yueshen's interest was piqued. He turned his head to look at him: \"What about Xiaodong? Will you go with Dad or Mom?\"","Xiaodong was usually sensible. He was genuinely curious—if he returned to the village, would this child follow him or his mother?","Zhou Yueshen had always believed his eldest son to be a very rational and sensible person.","Zhou Zedong froze for a moment and instinctively replied, \"Mom.\"","After saying that, even he was stunned. His little face quickly flushed red, and he hurriedly looked away, not daring to meet Zhou Yueshen's eyes. He had been very grateful to Zhou Yueshen since he was young, knowing it was Zhou Yueshen who had saved their three siblings from a living hell.","Even though Zhou Yueshen didn't know how to take care of them in the past, Zhou Zedong never blamed him.","Later, he even brought them back a wonderful mother.","He felt very happy now, but if he had to choose... rationally, he should go with his dad, but his body acted on its own.","Zhou Zedong thought hard and finally came up with a good solution. \"Dad, don't worry. If you can't make money anymore, I will. In the future, I'll send money back home for you to spend. My brother and I will also... will also go back to Xingfu Village to visit you during the holidays.\"","Second Child hurriedly chimed in, \"Yes, we will go see you.\"","Look at that, he even used the respectful 'you'.","Zhou Yueshen was both annoyed and amused.","Si Nian walked out holding a plate. Hearing Zhou Yueshen's low chuckle, she asked, \"What are you three talking about? You seem so happy.\"","Zhou Yueshen didn't interact much with the children, and it was Si Nian's first time seeing him so cheerful.","Zhou Zedong's little face turned red, and he didn't dare to speak.","Zhou Zehan, however, didn't think much of it. When Si Nian asked, he answered directly, \"Dad asked me and my brother whether we would go with him or Mom if he went bankrupt.\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"?\"","Was he the one who asked that question?","Hearing this, Si Nian immediately laughed, \"You're so bored that you're asking questions like this.\"","Zhou Yueshen felt like he had been thrown under the bus by his son. He rubbed his nose resentfully. \"I was just teasing them. I heard there are rumors outside lately that our family is going bankrupt.\"","Still smiling, Si Nian began applying cucumber slices from the plate onto her face, under the bewildered gazes of the father and sons.","Second Child: \"?\" Aren't those pickled cucumbers?","Why is Mom putting them on her face?","Meeting the dumbfounded stares of the one adult and two children, Si Nian coughed, \"This is my homemade cucumber face mask. It's cheap, comes in a big portion, and works well. My skin has been feeling a bit dry lately.\"","\"By the way, who just said our family is going bankrupt?\"","Second Child hurriedly raised his hand and said, \"It was Little Pig and his friends. They even sang a song to make fun of us, saying something like the Zhou family is going bankrupt, the oldest will cry, the second will farm, the third will pick up trash, and Jiang Jiu will be bullied... I'm so mad!\" He slammed his fist onto the sofa.","Si Nian said, \"Oh, them?\"","When passing by over the past few days, she had indeed noticed those people pointing at her and gossiping.","From time to time, they would cast gloating glances her way.","But she hadn't thought much of it.","Now, she could roughly guess the reason.","Zhou Yueshen hadn't interacted with the people in the neighborhood. Hearing his son say this, his smile faded, and his expression turned cold.","\"The people from the tenement building over there?\"","Si Nian nodded, \"Yes, the people from the tenement building. Xiaohan had some conflicts with the kids there before. The parents of those kids were greedy for a bargain and bought meat from sick pigs. When their kids got sick, they blamed it on us.\"","\"Now the authorities have issued a regulation, and people are no longer buying meat from outside stalls. Everyone goes to buy the pork that has been inspected by the supply and marketing cooperative. So they probably think our meat won't sell and we're going bankrupt.\"","Zhou Yueshen knew about the tenement building not far from their home; his second son used to love running over there to play.","He had thought they got along quite well.","He never expected this to be the case.","No wonder the boy was wiping away tears of grievance.","Although he said he wanted to stay with his mom, if something really happened, the children surely wouldn't want to be separated from their parents.","Zhou Yueshen lowered his eyes, concealing the coldness within them.","\"Since they despise us, they won't get to eat our meat from now on.\"","Si Nian tilted her head and glanced at him.","The older man was quite protective of his cubs.","The residents of the tenement building were originally waiting for the Zhou family to go bankrupt.","But who would have thought that instead of waiting for the Zhou family's bankruptcy, they would receive news of a meat price hike at the supply and marketing cooperative.","The crowd was dumbfounded, thinking to themselves that just a few days ago it was one yuan per pound, so how did it suddenly jump to one yuan and fifty cents?","They immediately refused to accept it and teamed up to go cause trouble at the cooperative.","The explanation given by the cooperative's leadership was, \"We changed suppliers. So many farms in our city have closed down recently, and pork supply was already falling short of demand. The few qualified factories were selected and partnered with by the higher-ups. The Zhou family's farm was willing to supply at the previous price, so the city's cooperatives all partnered with him.\"","\"And guess what?\"","The crowd: \"? What?\"","\"They said someone in our area was complaining that their pork wasn't good, so they stopped supplying us. We had to sign with another farm. Now this is the price everywhere outside. Eat it if you want, or leave it if you don't.\"","At this time, the pork supply was already insufficient. People had to line up every day to buy it, and each person could only get a small portion.","If you were late, you couldn't buy any at all.","Everyone had originally been very happy that the price hadn't gone up, because the other outside vendors selling inspected meat were charging exorbitant prices.","They had even gloated over others not being able to afford meat.","Well, look at them now.","The tables had turned, and they were the ones who couldn't afford meat.","\"Wait, who did you say supplied the meat originally?\"","The leader waved his hand impatiently: \"The Zhou family. I heard the boss lives right on Old East Street. Hey, don't tell me it was you bunch of old women who offended them?\"","The group from the tenement building: \"...\"","The aunties of the tenement building thought: Leader, you're a psychic, you guessed it right on the money."]},{"number":363,"title":"Chapter 363: I Also Saw Love","paragraphs":["A group of people walked toward the tenement building with miserable expressions. Seeing their regretful faces, Da Zhuang's mother felt unwilling to accept it. \"It's no big deal. We can just go to other co-ops to buy it. This isn't the only co-op around. I don't believe they can return all the goods to every co-op in the city.\"","Hearing this, everyone exchanged glances. Someone couldn't help but say, \"It's easy for you to say, Da Zhuang's mother. This is the only co-op in our neighborhood. Do you know how far the other co-ops are from here? Who would run seven or eight kilometers just for a meal of meat?\"","\"Exactly. There are many families living around every co-op. How would it ever be our turn to buy? By the time we get there, there won't even be meat scraps left.\"","Supply was already scarce right now. Even queuing up early in the morning here didn't guarantee you could buy any.","Going to other places to snatch it from others? Could they even win that fight?","It was simply asking for trouble.","Da Zhuang's mother choked on her words.","Someone couldn't help but suggest, \"Why don't we go apologize to the Zhou family? I don't think that Si Nian is a bad person.\"","\"Right, let's bring some gifts and apologize. We really did take our anger out on her before.\"","When the kids got sick from eating pork earlier, they happened to run into Si Nian, and Da Zhuang's mother wailed so loudly. Everyone subconsciously shifted their anger onto the Zhou family.","Now that the Zhou family was cooperating with the co-op to supply pork, it proved their meat was definitely fine.","They had misunderstood before.","Da Zhuang's mother's lips moved, her face written all over with reluctance.","But for a moment, she couldn't find any words to refute them.","The group decided to act on it immediately, hurrying back to prepare gifts to apologize at their door.","However, as soon as they ran downstairs, they heard their own children gathered together, singing and dancing.","\"Second Child, dark and black, ears perked up in anger, loves eating pork but not vegetables, going bankrupt in a miserable state is so cute.\"","The group of parents almost passed out.","They had wondered how they managed to offend them—even though they had gloated over their misfortune, it was all done in private. After all, they were older and cared about their face, not daring to say it to their faces.","So the main culprits were right here!","//","Si Nian went to No. 2 High School to hand in her homework. The other teachers were very satisfied, but the language arts teacher alone kept her behind to talk.","She seriously told her that the essays she wrote were not quite up to par.","Writing essays had always been Si Nian's weak point, not to mention she hadn't written this kind of thing for many years, so naturally, she couldn't produce the level of writing from her youth.","Because only a few people knew about Si Nian being a teacher at No. 2 High School, the other teachers didn't know she was a teacher.","They only knew that Si Nian had children and needed to take care of them at home, which was why she couldn't attend classes at school.","Although the other teachers initially disapproved, Si Nian's grades truly won them over. Plus, since the principal had agreed, what reason did they have to hold her back?","Anyway, even if she didn't come, she still did all the homework that the other students had.","As long as the submitted homework met the standards, they wouldn't say anything.","All along, Si Nian performed exceptionally well in all subjects.","Especially in English. The English teacher expressed that her beautiful English handwriting made her scalp tingle and feel ashamed of her own. When reading Si Nian's English essays, she even had to consult a dictionary because there were some words she didn't know.","Over time, she hadn't taught Si Nian anything; instead, she had learned quite a lot herself.","This made the English teacher so ashamed she wanted to resign.","The other teachers didn't have any issues with Si Nian either.","Of course, the language arts teacher didn't have a problem with Si Nian either; it was just that writing a poor essay would result in severe point deductions.","It would be fine normally, but if she lost points on her essay during the college entrance examination, the loss would outweigh the gain.","The essays Si Nian wrote completely lacked the youthful enthusiasm of a high school student. They were so mature that it made one involuntarily frown.","It didn't feel like it was written by a high schooler.","The thematic style of essays varies in every era, so it was no wonder the language arts teacher cared about this issue.","Si Nian felt a bit of a headache, but still said very obediently, \"Teacher, I might not be able to get away, but don't worry, I will read more of how others write when I get back.\"","The language arts teacher was just saying so; if Si Nian wasn't willing, she couldn't force her. But she did have a requirement. She rummaged through a large pile of homework next to her, pulled out a few essay notebooks, and handed them to her. \"These are excellent essays written by previous college entrance examinees from our school. Read them more and learn from them. I will check next week.\"","Si Nian accepted them gratefully. It seemed the teacher knew her problem and had prepared these for her in advance.","At this moment, she felt somewhat glad she hadn't entered No. 1 High School but No. 2 High School instead, because here, she had met a group of responsible and good teachers.","Si Nian: \"Thank you, teacher.\"","After handing in her homework, it was just in time for the high school classes to let out.","Many students walked over this way and happened to bump into Si Nian.","Because she was coming to school today, Si Nian dressed rather low-key: a simple short-sleeved shirt and jeans, paired with white sneakers. Her legs looked exceptionally long, yet not overly skinny, instead carrying a touch of voluptuous beauty.","Her hair was tied high in a ponytail, and she wore no makeup on her face. Her skin was white and tender, so supple it looked like water could be pinched out of it.","Furthermore, she was only nineteen herself. Students in this era started school late, so basically, there were people her age, and even older ones weren't unheard of.","A few green-looking teenage boys walked over from the teaching building hugging their books, and their eyes instantly went straight.","Si Nian walked past them, bringing a fragrant breeze.","This was something they couldn't smell on other girls at school.","Watching her leave, the boys found themselves unable to walk, almost simultaneously turning their heads to look at Si Nian.","Her back view was even more slender and moving.","When they snapped out of it, the students couldn't help but laugh and shove each other, wanting to go strike up a conversation with Si Nian.","Unfortunately, none of them had the courage to step forward. This girl was simply too beautiful. Her facial features were as bright and stunning as a flower of wealth in the mortal realm, while they were just the mud in the dirt.","\"I just saw her come out of the office. Which class is she from? There's no way I wouldn't know if our school had such a beautiful girl.\"","\"Right, could she be a newly transferred student?\"","Si Nian's age was about the same as theirs. Although her fashionable dress made people hesitate to approach, her age was obvious, so she definitely wasn't a teacher.","The boys got excited. Hugging their exercise books, they entered the office, only to see the language arts teacher there. Their hearts skipped a beat—could she be the language arts teacher's daughter?","The language arts teacher was packing up to go eat lunch. Seeing them come over, she said, \"Put them here and go eat.\"","The boys looked at each other, lacking the courage to ask out loud.","The language arts teacher was famously strict, after all.","Suddenly, they noticed a test paper on the desk with the name Si Nian.","Someone immediately asked, \"Teacher, who is Si Nian? A student from another class?\"","The language arts teacher didn't think much of it and replied, \"No, she's in our class. Your homeroom teacher accepted a repeating student a while ago. It's just that the student's family situation is a bit complicated, so she can't come to class and is self-studying at home. This is her test paper.\"","Since Si Nian was already married and had a child, it wouldn't be good for her reputation if word got around. Therefore, the teacher had only mentioned it in passing without going into detail.","The group exchanged glances, immediately understanding the situation.","The girl from just now was definitely the repeating student their literature teacher had talked about.","This was fantastic. A gorgeous girl had just joined their class.","\"She's so pretty,\" one of the boys marveled as they walked out.","Another boy, his face full of infatuation, said, \"All you guys see is a pretty face, but I'm different. I saw love.\"","The rest of the group: \"......\""]},{"number":364,"title":"Chapter 364: Making a Fool of Oneself","paragraphs":["Si Nian had just walked out of the gates of No. 2 High School when she sneezed.","Rubbing her nose, she wondered who was thinking about her again.","She casually looked up and glanced across the street, only to freeze in her tracks.","She saw Lin Sisi, who had recently been released from prison, walking out from inside. Beside her was a middle-aged man who looked like a teacher.","Si Nian immediately withdrew her gaze, adopting an \"out of sight, out of mind\" attitude, and pretended not to see them.","Lin Sisi did not notice her, but the teacher beside her did see Si Nian.","He frowned subconsciously because Si Nian had previously called the school mentioning her desire to repeat a year, and he had refused to accept her.","If he would not accept her, the other teachers naturally did not dare to accept her either.","But he never expected to see Si Nian at the gates of No. 2 High School.","No. 2 High School and their school had never gotten along; they were close in proximity and were rivals.","However, they had always been overshadowed by their No. 1 High School.","It had always been the students of No. 2 High School desperately trying to get into their school. There had never been a case of their school's students settling for No. 2 High School.","Because that was something that would be mocked.","Yet Si Nian had actually gone to No. 2 High School, which made the homeroom teacher suddenly feel a loss of face.","She had already married and become a stepmother; how did she still have the nerve to come to school? Was it not good enough to stay at home, serve her husband, and raise children?","An ordinary marriage would be one thing, but she was someone's stepmother.","She really was not afraid of making a fool of herself.","He could not help but shout, Si Nian, stop right there.","Si Nian was just about to go squeeze onto the bus and was a bit bewildered to be called out to.","Turning around, she saw that it was the male teacher next to Lin Sisi.","Hearing this voice, Lin Sisi was also stunned for a moment, then abruptly turned her head.","This was the first time the two had met since her release from prison.","Lin Sisi's gaze changed a myriad of times in an instant, looking extremely complicated.","Her eyes swept over her—that stunningly beautiful face, that graceful figure, that head of long, black hair...","There was not a single part of her that she did not envy.","Her hair had been cut short after she entered prison. Although it had grown out a bit now, it was still short, incredibly ugly, making her look like a tomboy.","Because of this, she wore a hat every day, not even daring to go see Fu Yang and the Fu family, terrified that her current appearance would disgust them.","But seeing the bright and captivating Si Nian here now, the mental fortress she had built for herself instantly collapsed.","Why did she get to live so well?","But then Lin Sisi raised her chin again, determined not to bow her head in front of Si Nian.","She feigned surprise and said, Sister Si Nian, why are you here?","Then she pretended to glance at No. 2 High School behind Si Nian and exclaimed in surprise, Are you at No. 2 High School? Why did you not come to No. 1 High School? I heard you are also taking the college entrance examination this year, and I was hoping we could study together.","Sure enough, Teacher Chen's expression beside her grew even uglier.","Si Nian, did you really go to No. 2 High School? He had only been guessing initially, because Si Nian had always been very proud in class and had a strong sense of self-esteem. Logically speaking, it should have been impossible for her to go to No. 2 High School.","Was this not bringing shame upon herself?","Si Nian had no memory of this man, but judging by his tone and attire, she could roughly guess who he was.","She stood firm and said, What is wrong with me going to No. 2 High School, sir?","As expected, Teacher Chen's face darkened further, and he immediately scolded, How can you be so worthless? Of all the places you could go, you just had to choose No. 2 High School. Our school and No. 2 High School have always been rivals. Are you trying to ruin my reputation?","Then, thinking of something, his tone became even gloomier: You are retaliating against me for not accepting you, so you deliberately went to No. 2 High School to anger me, right?","Si Nian looked baffled, but she also confirmed the identity of the teacher in front of her.","So this was the original owner's homeroom teacher whom she had called earlier.","However, the other party had explicitly rejected her at the time, refusing to accept her.","He was the one who refused to take her in. Why was he blaming her for going to No. 2 High School now?","Teacher Chen, please do not be angry. Sister Si Nian probably could not find anywhere else to go and had no choice but to go to No. 2 High School.","Teacher Chen snorted coldly and said, Transfer schools immediately. Our college entrance examination center is at No. 2 High School this year. You can go to any school, but do not come to No. 2 High School. Otherwise, if the other teachers see you here, how will I, your homeroom teacher, ever save face?","It would be fine if it were anyone else, but it just had to be Si Nian.","Si Nian used to be as beautiful as a flower, a top student, the English representative, and the face of the school. Because she was so pretty, she had hosted many events.","During high school, she had stolen all the limelight.","The teachers at the school... let alone the teachers, even the principal knew Si Nian.","Once upon a time, Teacher Chen had been proud of this student. Who knew that she would give up an easily attainable future for love? He had been extremely angry to begin with, and later, when Si Nian wretchedly became the stepmother to an old man in the countryside, he found it even more disgraceful.","Teacher Chen was a person who cared deeply about face. Naturally, he could not let her embarrass him at No. 2 High School.","Si Nian looked at Teacher Chen with an incredibly absurd expression and asked, Who are you?","Teacher Chen said angrily, I am your former homeroom teacher. Do not tell me you have forgotten me too?","Si Nian let out an Oh and said, So you are my former homeroom teacher.","She emphasized the word former heavily. Your tone made me think you were my parents, trying to control wherever I go.","The implication was: Whether I leave or stay, is it any of your business?","Teacher Chen's face turned green.","He pointed a trembling finger at the gates of No. 2 High School. Do you know where this is?","Si Nian replied, No. 2 High School.","Teacher Chen: ... I am asking, since you know this is No. 2 High School, why did you still go in? Do you not know that No. 2 High School is our school's rival?","Si Nian rolled her eyes at him dramatically. They are your rival, not mine. What the hell does that have to do with me?","Teacher Chen: You, you are truly ab... absurd.","Lin Sisi said anxiously, Sister Si Nian, stop talking. Are you trying to anger Teacher Chen to death?","Si Nian: If I had that ability, I would anger you to death first.","Lin Sisi: ...","Lin Sisi thought: Fine, fine, fine. You are really not leaving me any face at all."]},{"number":365,"title":"Chapter 365: Self-Abandonment","paragraphs":["Teacher Chen took a deep breath, a look of contempt on his face. \"You've really given up on yourself!\"","How could the old Si Nian ever say such a thing?","In the past, although Si Nian was proud, she was highly respectful to her teachers.","But look at her now, what has she become!","After all, she isn't a biological daughter. I heard she even became a stepmother to someone's kids; no wonder she has fallen so low.","Oh well.","\"Forget it, the college entrance examination is coming up, so I won't hold it against you. Marrying someone and becoming a stepmother is disgraceful, but as long as you don't spread it around, it's not unbearable. Come back to my class. Even if you don't do well on the exam, I won't blame you,\" Teacher Chen said in a patronizing tone.","Even if she did poorly in his own class, it wouldn't be as much of a joke as her doing poorly at another school.","In any case, he absolutely could not tolerate his student going to the No. 2 High School.","Lin Sisi, who was standing to the side, felt her heart tighten upon hearing this.","Didn't her mother warn Teacher Chen not to accept Si Nian?","Almost no one knew about her time in prison, except for the people in the family compound and the teachers.","If Si Nian returned to the school and intentionally spread this matter around, how could she ever show her face at school again?","Hearing this, Si Nian laughed out of sheer exasperation. \"Teacher, you still don't get it.\"","Teacher Chen frowned and said in displeasure, \"What do you mean?\"","Si Nian replied, \"Whether I go to No. 1 High School or No. 2 High School, it's my own choice. It's not about going wherever you want me to go.\"","\"You were my teacher in the past, but you are not my teacher now. I have no obligation to take orders from you.\"","\"Furthermore, my current teachers are great, at least far better than the kind who likes to point fingers at other people's private lives. I really should thank you for rejecting me back then; otherwise, I wouldn't have been able to attend such a good school.\"","\"Speaking of which, you cared so much about me being married and becoming a stepmother that you refused to accept me. But now I find it strange, you don't mind taking in someone who has been to prison, yet you despise someone who is married. Your taste is truly quite unusual, Teacher.\"","She looked at the two of them, whose faces had turned green, with a half-smile.","\"Since there's nothing else, I'll be going now.\"","Just as Si Nian finished speaking, the bus arrived.","She quickly walked over and got on the bus with the crowd.","Teacher Chen was furious.","If Zhang Cuimei hadn't come to his door time and time again, he wouldn't have accepted Lin Sisi.","Going to prison was truly too shameful.","He hadn't expected Si Nian to expose it. Right now, he felt thoroughly humiliated, his expression incredibly ugly.","Although Lin Sisi was also angry, she thought it was a good thing Si Nian had the sense not to come back; otherwise, her situation would be really troublesome.","Seeing Teacher Chen's ugly expression, she quickly comforted him, \"Teacher Chen, please don't be angry. Sister Si Nian might just be upset that you didn't accept her before, which is why she said those angry words. She didn't mean it.\"","Teacher Chen grew even angrier. \"What right does she have to be angry? Was anything I said wrong? Who told her, a perfectly good young maiden, to go and become someone's stepmother instead of doing something proper? If word gets out, I'll be laughed at too! Whose student is this shameless?\"","\"And now she ran off to No. 2 High School. She really won't be happy until she ruins my reputation as a homeroom teacher.\"","Teacher Chen was so angry he could barely stand steady.","Lin Sisi quickly said, \"Teacher Chen, don't worry. I'll ask my parents to persuade Sister Si Nian to come back. Sister Si Nian will definitely understand your good intentions.\"","Hearing her say this, Teacher Chen calmed down a bit. He thought about it and agreed, even if Si Nian didn't listen to him, she would surely listen to her adoptive parents, right?","He said, \"Actually, I'm not entirely worried just about her going to No. 2 High School, but about her grades. She used to have excellent grades at our school. I'm worried she'll raise the average score of No. 2 High School. If that really happens, everyone will know she was my student, and as her teacher, I will definitely be made a laughingstock. So, we absolutely cannot let her stay at No. 2 High School.\"","Teacher Chen was already feeling some regret.","Not just because Si Nian went to No. 2 High School, but because her grades were so outstanding, yet he had refused to accept her as a repeating student.","This led to Si Nian going to No. 2 High School to get back at him. That child was highly competitive; if she scored high on the college entrance exam because of this, it might even suppress their school's overall scores.","When that time came, he would lose all his dignity and reputation.","Therefore, even though he was so angry, he still wanted to get Si Nian to transfer back to their school.","At worst, he would just pretend not to see her to keep his peace of mind.","Anyway, it wasn't long until the college entrance examination.","Hearing this, Lin Sisi's expression also turned a bit ugly.","This wasn't just what Teacher Chen was worried about; it was her worry as well.","She was just about to say something when she heard Teacher Chen say, \"Speaking of which, you need to study hard too. I don't know exactly how your grades were before, but in our class, you can't be considered outstanding. I only accepted you for the sake of your parents. When it's time for the college entrance examination, don't embarrass me.\"","After saying that, Teacher Chen walked away arrogantly.","Lin Sisi was so angry her nose was practically crooked.","Even though Si Nian contradicted him so much, he was still praising her good grades and all.","She had studied so hard to please him, yet he actually said she couldn't be considered outstanding!","If she hadn't wasted time in prison, would she be like this?!","Although she was unwilling to accept it, Lin Sisi also knew that what Teacher Chen said was the truth.","Si Nian, Si Nian, it was all that damn Si Nian's fault for putting her in this dilemma.","If only she couldn't participate in the college entrance examination, that would be great.","//","Upon returning home, Si Nian was covered in hot sweat from being squeezed on the bus.","She went to Grandma Jiang's house to pick up Yaoyao and happened to see Grandpa Jiang sitting at the door playing chess.","Yaoyao was leaning nearby, watching, occasionally stretching out her chubby little hand to point at things. At these moments, Grandpa Jiang would patiently explain to her what it was.","After listening, the little girl would immediately show an expression of sudden realization.","Just as she pinched a chess piece and put it down, Si Nian's voice rang out.","\"Yaoyao.\"","\"Mama~\" The leaning little girl immediately stood up in excitement and ran toward Si Nian, her short little legs pattering on the ground.","Si Nian smiled, picked her up, and wiped the hot sweat from her forehead.","The weather was just too hot.","It seemed she needed to prepare something to cool down the heat.","Grandpa Jiang also heard the commotion. He looked up and smiled. \"Teacher Xiao Si is back.\"","Si Nian smiled and nodded. \"Yes, Uncle Jiang. Thank you and Auntie for going through the trouble to look after Yaoyao for me.\"","Grandpa Jiang laughed heartily. \"You're too polite. Your Yaoyao is so well-behaved. She doesn't cry or make a fuss. She's much more fun than our Little Jiang. I like this little girl. Come watch Grandpa play chess more often from now on, alright?\"","Yaoyao nodded and said, \"Mama~ Playing chess is so much fun.\"","Si Nian smiled and rubbed her head, telling her that if she liked it, she could play with Grandpa more often in the future. Then, she bid farewell to Grandpa Jiang and went home."]},{"number":366,"title":"Chapter 366: Lin Sisi's Doubt","paragraphs":["It was so hot that she couldn't stay outside for even two seconds.","Si Nian started tinkering with making mung bean slush again.","It was one of her favorite summer desserts.","Seeing the person leave, Grandpa Jiang lost his interest in playing chess.","It was rare to have someone keep him company while playing chess, asking a couple of questions from time to time—that was what made it interesting.","What was the fun in playing chess alone?","Just then, someone dropped by to visit. \"Lao Jiang, playing chess? Oh, who are you playing with to lose so miserably?\"","Grandpa Jiang rolled his eyes at the man. \"What nonsense are you spouting? I'm playing against myself...\"","Before he could finish his sentence, his gaze fell on the chessboard, and he was instantly stunned.","On the previously evenly matched board, a move had been made at some unknown point, poising to take his general.","And his general had absolutely no way to retreat, unable to escape.","This situation was a \"checkmate.\"","Grandpa Jiang was greatly shocked.","When was his chess setup broken?","He had never made this move, and the only person who had just touched the chess pieces was Yaoyao.","Could that little girl have made the move?","Impossible, impossible!","Yaoyao didn't even understand these things. Could she have bumped it by accident?","Even though he thought so, wasn't this too much of a coincidence?","Grandpa Jiang looked at the chessboard thoughtfully.","//","Si Nian stewed a large pot of mung bean soup and put it in the refrigerator to chill.","It would be ready to drink in a little while.","Turning around, she saw Yaoyao standing on her tiptoes playing with the radio, from which the voices of foreigners occasionally sounded.","Si Nian didn't think much of it. She withdrew her gaze, went back to her room, and brought out all the bedding to sun at the door. With such a bright sun, it was the perfect time to air out the quilts.","She even brought out Rhubarb's doghouse, scraped out a pile of dog hair, and placed it under the sun to kill the mites.","When about enough time had passed, the chilled mung bean soup was ready to drink.","Si Nian took a sip. The sweet taste flooded her mouth, and the icy coolness rushed straight to her head.","It was so delicious!","She scooped a bowl for Yaoyao to drink and delivered a large bowl next door to the Jiang family.","Grandpa Jiang was still sitting at the door, still staring at the chessboard.","Seeing Si Nian coming, he waved his hand and said, \"Teacher Xiao Si, come and take a look at my chess game.\"","Si Nian brought the mung bean soup over, glanced at it, and well... couldn't understand it.","She said honestly, \"Uncle Jiang, I don't know how to play Chinese chess.\"","Uncle Jiang paused for a moment and then asked, \"Then who in your family knows how?\"","Si Nian thought carefully and said, \"Probably no one in my family knows how. I'm not too sure either.\"","Grandpa Jiang sighed. \"I see. I was going to say that if someone in your family knew how to play, they could take some time to play a game with this old man.\"","It seemed he really was overthinking it. Yaoyao must have accidentally bumped it.","Otherwise, at such a young age, how could she possibly break his chess setup?","Si Nian smiled and poured him some mung bean soup. Grandpa Jiang took a sip, his eyes lighting up, and repeatedly praised how good it tasted.","Si Nian had cooked quite a lot, planning to have Zhou Yueshen pack some up and take it to share with everyone when he returned.","By the time she finished her chores, Yaoyao had already fallen asleep on the sofa.","The radio broadcast was still playing.","Si Nian turned off the radio, carried her daughter upstairs to sleep, and went back to her own room to read the essay collection her teacher had given her.","The college entrance examination was coming up soon, and she couldn't afford to be idle.","Recently, the director at the school had also been urging her, asking if she had any preferred teachers to recommend.","Because if Si Nian took the college entrance examination, she would have to resign.","Although the director said she could go back after she graduated in the future, that was all in the future, and nothing was certain.","Now that she was leaving, her position naturally needed to be filled.","Several teachers were interested and had dropped hints to her.","However, there was also Li Fengxian, who was staring fixedly at this position. Si Nian felt a massive headache coming on; no matter who she gave it to, she would end up offending someone.","//","When Lin Sisi returned home, Si's Father and Si's Mother were both at home.","Zhang Cuimei had already finished her surgery and returned home to recover. Although she had mostly recovered, her complexion looked even worse than before.","The reason was that early this morning, she had heard people gossiping about her family.","She didn't know how long it had been spreading, but the way these people looked at her was strange. She wasn't deaf, so naturally, she heard it all.","Although she had guessed that her husband might have someone else on the outside, she never expected it to be right under her nose.","Today, she heard about this matter.","And it was an opportunity she had handed over with her own hands.","Zhang Cuimei's face was indescribably ugly.","The news spread quickly, not to mention that it was among the military wives.","Naturally, it quickly reached the ears of Si's Father's superiors.","Si's Father had been warned and didn't dare to go out during this time, afraid of being caught with more evidence against him.","Facing his wife now, he also felt exceptionally guilty, and his attitude toward her had improved significantly.","Although Zhang Cuimei hated it to death, for the sake of her daughter, she had to pretend she knew nothing.","Lin Sisi keenly sensed that something was wrong and hurriedly sought out Zhang Cuimei to ask what had happened again.","She was studying from dawn to dusk every day now, so naturally, she didn't know what had happened.","She only felt that the atmosphere at home was very strange.","Zhang Cuimei gritted her teeth, pulled her into the room, and told her about Si's Father having an affair with Liu Dongdong's older sister.","Lin Sisi was dumbfounded and didn't believe it at all. \"Her sister has already been married to two men, and I heard she couldn't have children and was chased back home. She's a famous jinx in our village. How could my dad...\"","She hadn't heard about Liu Dongdong's sister coming to their house, because she was still in prison at that time.","Liu Dongdong had never mentioned it.","Although she had also guessed that her father definitely had someone, she never expected it to be Liu Dongdong's sister.","\"Who else could it be? When I went to the Northwest to visit Fu Yang, she came to our house every day to wash clothes and cook for your father. What a shameless vixen!\"","Zhang Cuimei was so angry that her insides hurt.","Because at the time, she was the one who insisted on taking Liu Dongdong with her, which led Liu Dongdong to ask her sister to come over and help.","Lin Sisi's face looked terrible. How could it turn out like this? In her past life, when Si Nian married Fu Yang, she had never mentioned anything about Si's Father having an affair.","She suddenly remembered the last time Liu Dongdong went to visit her, the marks she had seen on her body. Suddenly, her heart skipped a beat, and she asked anxiously, \"Mom, has Liu Dongdong found a boyfriend?\"","How would Zhang Cuimei know about such things? Her heart was full of resentment over her husband's affair, and she wished she could slaughter that adulterous pair.","Naturally, she hadn't paid any attention to Liu Dongdong.","Hearing this now, she said in confusion, \"I don't know. Who told you that? When she was here at our house, she stayed in the family compound all day long. Aside from buying groceries and cooking, she never went out. How could she have found a boyfriend? However, yesterday she did tell me that there was an emergency at home and she had to go back for a bit, so she asked for leave.\"","Lin Sisi's expression suddenly turned ugly.","An unbelievable thought flooded into her mind, but she was unwilling to believe it.","B-but, was it really such a coincidence? Liu Dongdong just happened to take a leave of absence, and then the news of her sister and her father having an affair spread out.","Could it be that Liu Dongdong had heard about this long ago, so she ran away in advance to avoid the storm?","Then who left those marks on her body?","The more Lin Sisi thought about it, the worse her expression became...","//","On Monday, Si Nian went to the hospital to pick up the children's health checkup reports.","Just as she stepped outside, she collided with a hurried figure.","The person had their head lowered and wore a face mask, tightly clutching a piece of paper in their hand.","Si Nian caught a glimpse and was taken aback. Wasn't that Liu Dongdong?"]},{"number":367,"title":"Chapter 367: Flustered","paragraphs":["Why did she look so panicked?","Liu Dongdong didn't seem to notice her.","Si Nian turned to look at the department sign; it was the gynecology department.","Her heart skipped a beat.","When she turned back around, Liu Dongdong was already gone.","Could she have seen it wrong?","In the novel, Liu Dongdong didn't have a partner and was always pining for the male lead, so there shouldn't have been any unexpected accidents.","Moreover, a man as arrogant as Fu Yang would be even less likely to do anything with her.","Si Nian rubbed her chin: Was she here to be treated for a gynecological disease?","She walked downstairs holding the medical reports. Reading them over, the health indexes of all three children met the standards. Eldest Child's slow development was due to a damaged foundation in early childhood, which could be fixed with focused nourishment.","Second Child had basically no issues and was strong and healthy.","Yaoyao was even slightly chubby.","No wonder she felt it was getting harder to carry her.","Si Nian put the reports into her pocket and went to the pharmacy to get some calcium and blood-replenishing medicine for Eldest Child.","When she was young, she was similar to Eldest Child—very weak and small—but didn't she grow to be nearly 170 centimeters tall anyway?","That was all because her parents forced her to take blood tonics and calcium pills.","In elementary school, she used to stand at the very front and sit in the first row.","But once she hit middle school, Si Nian had a sudden growth spurt and moved to the back row.","Therefore, Si Nian firmly believed that taking these supplements was necessary.","However, the prerequisite was to get checked first; prescribing the right medicine for the condition was the only way it would work (parents shouldn't just blindly copy this).","At the entrance of the Zhou family's home.","The middle-aged women from the tube-shaped apartment building came over carrying gifts, timing their visit for when Si Nian got off work.","The group looked somewhat anxious and uneasy.","They were worried that the Zhou family wouldn't forgive them.","Fang Hui came home from work and was a bit surprised to see this group of people holding vegetables and fruits, looking like they were paying a visit. She wondered if they were here to see her.","It really wasn't Fang Hui overthinking things, because these people usually loved to curry favor with her and would always say a few flattering words whenever they met.","Since her son had just been discharged from the hospital a couple of days ago, she thought they might be here to visit him.","Although Fang Hui didn't particularly want to socialize with these people, who wouldn't enjoy others going out of their way to flatter them?","She coughed and pretended to be clueless, asking, \"Why are you all here?\"","Seeing her, everyone exchanged glances and said awkwardly, \"Well, because of what happened a few days ago, we felt quite bad, so we thought we'd come over to apologize.\"","Fang Hui assumed they were talking about making her misunderstand Si Nian. She had completely lost face that day, and her expression darkened at the memory.","\"It's all in the past. There's nothing to apologize for.\"","Everyone exchanged glances again.","They didn't really want to apologize either. If the pork at the supply and marketing cooperative wasn't so expensive, would they even need to come apologize?","Although they heard Fang Hui's family was wealthy, seeing her heartless and unbothered attitude made everyone feel a bit uncomfortable.","After all, her family had money, so it didn't matter to them if pork was a bit pricey.","But it was different for them. Saving fifty cents a day could add up to a lot over a month.","They also remembered that the things Fang Hui said to Si Nian that day were much harsher than what they had said.","Perhaps Si Nian held a grudge against them by association, just because Fang Hui had gone too far and they had been associating with her.","Thinking of this, the way everyone looked at Fang Hui suddenly filled with dissatisfaction, and they mocked, \"You misunderstood Teacher Si that day. Doesn't Comrade Fang plan to apologize in person? We heard from the doctor that she was the one who brought your son to the hospital.\"","\"Exactly. We just misunderstood out of anxiety, but we didn't say anything as excessive as you did.\"","Fang Hui still had her chin raised. She hadn't expected their tone to change so suddenly. She was a bit bewildered, but once she realized what was happening, her face darkened: \"What do you mean by that?\"","\"Are we wrong? She saved you, but you bit the hand that fed you and attacked Teacher Si. You even wanted Teacher Si to kneel and apologize to you. It would be weird if Teacher Si wasn't angry.\"","\"Putting it that way, maybe she's the one who caused all this.\"","\"Yeah, we've gossiped before, but Teacher Si never targeted us.\"","The more everyone thought about it, the more they felt it was Fang Hui's fault.","As Fang Hui listened, she felt something was very wrong. Her face turned green, and she asked uncertainly, \"A-Aren't you here to visit my son?\"","Everyone was stunned for a moment, then sneered upon realizing her assumption: \"Comrade Fang, what are you thinking? Why would we come to see your son?\"","\"Exactly. First, we aren't relatives. Second, we aren't even close. There's no need for us to visit your son.\"","\"We are here to apologize to Teacher Si.\"","\"Doesn't Comrade Fang plan to apologize in person?\"","Everyone asked suspiciously.","Fang Hui's face turned pale and then green.","She hadn't even considered apologizing. After what happened that day, she had lost all her dignity.","She wished she could just detour around the Zhou family's home.","Rushing to their door to apologize now? Was she crazy?","Besides, she had already apologized that day. Why should she have to apologize again now?","These people were truly disgusting, acting like fence-sitters, swaying whichever way the wind blew.","They were clearly sucking up to her before, but now they pretended not to know her well.","Fang Hui was furious but too embarrassed to say it out loud.","After all, she still had to live here. Ruining her own reputation would do her no good.","So she suppressed her anger and smiled awkwardly, \"W-Well, it's just that I've been so busy lately and haven't had the time. Since everyone is apologizing, I might as well join you.\"","Lin Sisi, along with Si's Father and Si's Mother, rarely came over as a family. They didn't expect to bump into a group of people waiting at the entrance of the Zhou family's home.","They were taken aback for a moment.","The residents of the tube-shaped building had never seen them before either. Seeing this family of three approach, they were also a bit confused.","\"Who are you?\"","Zhang Cuimei frowned and said, \"We are Si Nian's adoptive parents. And who are you?\"","Looking at how this group was dressed, she could tell at a glance that they weren't wealthy.","She immediately raised her chin and put on airs.","Hearing this, everyone was very surprised.","Since the Zhou family moved here, very few people had come to visit them.","Even if someone did come, the neighbors didn't necessarily run into them.","They had assumed this family didn't have any relatives.","They didn't expect someone to suddenly show up at the door claiming to be adoptive parents.","Seeing the three of them dressed elegantly, it was obvious they weren't ordinary people.","They immediately believed them a bit more. Exchanging glances, they said flatteringly, \"So you are Teacher Si's parents.\"","\"Yes, yes, this is the first time we've met. We live in the apartment building; we are Teacher Si's neighbors.\"","The group stepped forward to greet them enthusiastically."]},{"number":368,"title":"Chapter 368: Intentionally Misleading","paragraphs":["This feeling of being flattered made Si's Father and Si's Mother feel as if they had returned to the past when Si Nian was still at home. Whenever relatives and friends came to visit, they would definitely curry favor with them just because they were Si Nian's parents.","Because Si Nian was not only outstanding, but also engaged to Fu Yang.","At that time, their Si family was in the limelight.","But ever since Si Nian left, this kind of situation had gradually disappeared.","Let alone flattering them, those people could not wait to avoid them.","At this moment, the two felt a fleeting sense of nostalgia.","Lin Sisi asked, \"Are you here to visit my sister Si Nian?\"","The couple looked over and indeed saw that these people were carrying gifts in their hands to varying degrees.","Si's Father put on the airs of a father and said, \"Since you're here to visit, why don't you go inside? This Nian Nian really is something.\"","Seeing their attitude, everyone was pleasantly surprised. They had been worried that Si Nian wouldn't be willing to forgive them.","They hurriedly smiled and said, \"We had a little misunderstanding with Teacher Si before, so we came to apologize to her. Alas, it's all because our children have loose tongues and said some unpleasant things. Now the Zhou family has stopped supplying pork to the supply and marketing cooperative, and prices have gone up. We know we were wrong, so we hurried over to apologize to Teacher Si, hoping she can be the bigger person and not hold it against the kids.\"","Hearing this, Si's Father immediately frowned. \"Absurd. To do such a thing just because of a few children, Nian Nian is too willful.\"","Lin Sisi also didn't expect Si Nian to be so good at offending people. Originally, when she first arrived and heard that Si Nian lived in such a nice house, she was extremely envious and jealous.","She didn't expect her relationship with the neighbors to be so poor.","She always wondered why she never liked Si Nian.","It turned out it wasn't just her; everyone felt the same way.","So she immediately said, \"Sister Si Nian is a bit petty, but she's not a bad person. Don't worry.\"","Zhang Cuimei also chimed in, \"Yes, that girl was spoiled by us when she was young. When she comes back, we'll give her a talking to.\"","Seeing how confident they were, everyone's hanging hearts finally relaxed, and they quickly expressed their gratitude.","Upon hearing that Si's Father was from the military compound, their gazes grew even more envious.","Words of flattery followed one after another.","When Si Nian returned, she saw so many people gathered at the door of her house.","She was taken aback for a moment.","Before she even stopped her bicycle, the group of people eagerly surrounded her, their faces full of flattery.","It was as if they weren't the same bitter and mean people from the hospital before.","Si's Father put on his airs even more, stepping forward to say, \"Nian Nian, you're off work?\"","Si Nian hadn't seen Si's Father for a long time. Seeing Zhang Cuimei and Lin Sisi following beside him, she frowned.","She thought to herself, could it be that when she ran into Lin Sisi at school, she went back and said something to the Si family, prompting them to come looking for her again?","Sure enough, it was better for Lin Sisi to stay in prison; at least back then, Si's Father and Si's Mother visited much less frequently.","Si Nian parked her bicycle and asked, \"Are you looking for me for something?\"","Si's Father said, \"There is a very important matter I need to discuss with you. But this is not the place to talk, and everyone is waiting for you to go inside. Open the door first.\"","Si Nian frowned, ignoring him, and instead asked the other residents of the apartment building, \"And what do all of you want?\"","The group of people from the building looked at each other, their expressions awkward.","\"Teacher Si, we came to apologize to you. The last time at the hospital, we misunderstood you, and we're truly sorry.\"","\"This is a little apology gift and a token of our sincerity. Please don't despise it.\"","Si Nian nodded. It seemed Zhou Yueshen's actions had gotten a response.","The only thing that could make these snobbish aunties and older sisters bow their heads was money.","She had also heard about the pork price increase at the cooperative.","She generously opened the door and took the items inside.","Then, under everyone's expectant gazes, she smiled and said, \"I've received the gifts, but you can take your sincerity back.\"","Everyone: \"...\"","Si's Father frowned, expressing his disapproval. \"What kind of attitude is this? It's just a small matter. Is there any need to throw a tantrum? How old are you now? Hurry up and tell your man to change the pork prices at the cooperative back. These are your neighbors; you're going too far.\"","Lin Sisi also said, \"That's right, Sister Si Nian. We've all heard about the swine fever a while ago. Everyone was just anxious and misunderstood. They all know they were wrong. Now that you've accepted the gifts, aren't you going to make some kind of response?\"","Si Nian asked in return, \"They're apologizing because they accidentally hurt me and the child at the time. Isn't an apology expected? Accepting the apology gift means that matter is in the past for me, but just because I'm over it doesn't mean Zhou Yueshen is.\"","After speaking, she looked at the group of stunned aunties. \"You're apologizing for the hospital incident, right?\"","Everyone nodded.","Si Nian smiled. \"Then what does that have to do with you cursing the Zhou family to go bankrupt behind our backs later on? My surname is Si, not Zhou. How could I possibly sway the thoughts of the Zhou family?\"","Everyone's faces instantly turned ugly.","Si's Father disagreed, saying, \"What Si family or Zhou family? You're already married. It's just a matter of you saying a single word. Is there a need to make it so troublesome?\"","\"Uncle, how can you say that? If Auntie told you not to have an affair, would you really not have an affair? It's not that simple; this is a matter of principle.\"","Si's Father's face instantly turned green.","Everyone else was also dumbfounded.","No way, isn't this man an official? How could he have an affair?","Si Nian ignored him and looked at the group from the apartment building. \"Do you want to take your things back?\"","Everyone looked at each other, none of them having the face to do so.","Si Nian was right. These gifts were for the hospital incident, which was a completely separate matter from cursing the Zhou family in private later.","If Si Nian really wanted to target them, she would have done so long ago, because they had gossiped about her in private early on, and their children had ostracized her son.","But they had always lived in peace.","This time, it must be because the rumors reached Director Zhou's ears that things turned out this way.","However, they didn't have the courage to go find that tall, burly man with the sharp gaze.","For a moment, they stood frozen in place.","Seeing their troubled expressions, Si Nian smiled and looked toward Si's Father's family. \"Auntie, Uncle, do you have some business with me?\"","Having been exposed by his adopted daughter, Si's Father's old face was completely flushed red.","He hadn't expected that this matter had actually reached Si Nian's ears.","His face looked extremely ugly.","He hurriedly said with a red face, \"Let's go inside to talk, let's go inside.\"","Si Nian didn't stop him and followed him inside.","Seeing that there was no hope, the others had no choice but to leave in disgrace.","They didn't even bother to greet Zhang Cuimei and the others.","And to think they believed these two adoptive parents had a lot of say and kept saying nice things to them.","Who knew things were actually like this.","He even had an affair.","No wonder Si Nian's family never interacted with them.","Truly bad luck.","Si's Father also felt the disdainful gazes of the group, and he was angry inside.","He couldn't help but make excuses for himself, \"You child, what nonsense are you spouting? That matter was just blind rumors spread by outsiders. If others don't believe me, do you, the daughter I raised for eighteen years, also not believe me?\"","Si Nian: \"I don't believe you.\"","Si's Father: \"...\"","Zhang Cuimei's face looked awful as she said in a grim voice, \"Enough, stop spouting nonsense. Your father isn't that kind of man.\"","Hearing this, Si Nian could not help but marvel at Zhang Cuimei.","Her husband was cheating right under her nose, yet she was still making excuses for him.","She truly deserved the title of the ultimate love-struck fool.","Feigning shock, Si Nian said, \"No way! I actually saw Liu Dongdong going to the gynecology department at the hospital today. I thought Uncle really had an affair with her, and that was why you guys were making such a fuss about getting a divorce.\"","\"What?!\"","As soon as those words dropped, the expressions of all three family members drastically changed!"]},{"number":369,"title":"Chapter 369: Considering a Job Change","paragraphs":["Si's Father was the first to react. His old face flushed red as he scolded, \"Nonsense! How could I possibly have an affair with Liu Dongdong!\"","The rumors were getting more and more outrageous. Liu Dongdong was the same age as his own daughter. If this spread, where would he put his old face?","However, Zhang Cuimei and Lin Sisi had completely different expressions.","Didn't Liu Dongdong say she had gone back to her hometown?","How could Si Nian have run into her at the hospital?","And in the gynecology department, no less.","What was an unmarried, childless young woman doing in the gynecology department?","Lin Sisi couldn't help but recall the hickey she had previously seen on Liu Dongdong.","Liu Dongdong hadn't just lied; she had secretly gone to the gynecology department.","If she truly hadn't done anything guilty, why would she need to deceive them?","And her sister inexplicably had an affair with her father.","Lin Sisi's mind instantly fell into chaos.","What exactly were these two sisters trying to do?","Although she had her suspicions, she had always comforted herself with the thought that a man as arrogant and clean-living as Fu Yang would never get involved with anyone else, even if he didn't like her.","Let alone someone like Liu Dongdong, who came from the countryside and had no education.","But now, with Si Nian bringing this up, true panic began to set in.","She had originally planned to wait for Liu Dongdong to return and ask her who this supposed boyfriend actually was.","If she could confirm who it was, it would prove that none of these matters had anything to do with Liu Dongdong.","Liu Dongdong had been by her side for so long. Since her rebirth, Liu Dongdong was the first person willing to help her. When she was in prison, it was Liu Dongdong who visited her frequently and brought her various things.","Lin Sisi had already treated her as a friend and had never suspected a thing.","But now, Liu Dongdong had lied.","Coupled with the fact that her sister was having an affair with Si's Father, Lin Sisi would have to be an idiot not to realize something was wrong.","An outstanding man like Fu Yang—what woman wouldn't like him? Liu Dongdong frequently went to deliver things to him; it would be abnormal if she didn't have any ulterior motives.","Yet she herself hadn't realized this problem at all, continuously asking Liu Dongdong to deliver food for her.","She had even naively believed that Fu Yang accepted the items simply because Liu Dongdong's cooking was good.","She had even confidently assumed that Fu Yang accepted them out of respect for her.","But looking back now, Si Nian's cooking used to be famous in the military compound, yet Fu Yang had never given it a second glance. If Fu Yang truly accepted things for the sake of his fiancée, he shouldn't have rejected Si Nian's.","Lin Sisi had previously felt smug about this.","But now, she felt an overwhelming sense of dread, as if she had invited a wolf into her own home.","People in this era were so reserved and conservative, and Liu Dongdong was especially timid, yet she had deliberately exposed that hickey to her.","Wasn't that a blatant provocation and show-off?","And to think she had genuinely believed Liu Dongdong had found a boyfriend and was happy for her.","The more Lin Sisi thought about it, the more she felt like she was going crazy.","Meanwhile, Zhang Cuimei was thinking: Could her husband have hooked up with Liu Dongdong in addition to her sister?","Her vision went dark, and she nearly fainted.","Si Nian looked at the colorful expressions of the family of three and smiled. \"Is that so? So Uncle's affair isn't with Liu Dongdong. Then what was she doing alone in the gynecology department? I saw her wearing a mask and a hat, looking very nervous. But since you all say it isn't so, I suppose I must have misunderstood.\"","\"Speaking of which, Liu Dongdong is already nineteen, yet there are no plans for her marriage. I heard from Fu Qianqian that, Auntie, you even took her all the way to the Northwest to personally care for Fu Yang. It seems you really value her. Maybe you can introduce her to a good marriage in the future; her hardships would finally pay off.\"","Lin Sisi's face grew increasingly pale.","How did she not know about this?","She had only heard from Zhang Cuimei that Fu Yang was injured and she rushed over to visit him.","She hadn't heard that Liu Dongdong went to personally care for him.","An unmarried young woman intimately caring for someone else's husband—did she have no shame?","Lin Sisi was so angry her face turned livid; she wished she could drag Liu Dongdong over and interrogate her immediately.","Hearing this, Zhang Cuimei felt something was off, but she had to admit Si Nian was right. Liu Dongdong was a nineteen-year-old maiden; it was indeed very strange that her family hadn't arranged a marriage for her yet.","But she felt Si Nian was being a busybody, so she said disdainfully, \"Why are you bringing this up? Sisi said Dongdong already has a boyfriend. Do you need to worry about it?\"","She must be overthinking. Her sister's matter might be clear from the rumors, but Liu Dongdong had always been working right under her nose. If there really was something going on with her husband, wouldn't she have seen it?","Zhang Cuimei felt Si Nian was deliberately trying to sow discord in their family.","She didn't dwell on Liu Dongdong's matter and directly changed the subject. \"Let's not talk about such things. Aren't you going to take the college entrance exam? What about your job? Are you just going to quit?\"","\"You were doing perfectly fine as a broadcaster before, but you insisted on selling the position to Fu Qianqian. Now you've finally gotten such a good job. Keep the goodies within the family; don't go foolishly selling it to someone else again. It's not worth it.\"","Si Nian knew that this family showing up at her door meant they were up to no good.","So they had come for her job.","Si Nian raised an eyebrow and continued to watch Zhang Cuimei's performance.","\"I have quite a few educated relatives on my side. You just tell the school that we'll find someone to cover your shifts ourselves. Then, when you graduate from college in the future, we'll give the job back to you. How about that? Isn't it a great deal?\"","Zhang Cuimei looked rather pleased with herself.","She had heard that Si Nian earned 90 yuan a month as a teacher, which was much higher than her previous broadcasting job.","Such a good opportunity naturally couldn't be given to an outsider.","If she introduced someone from her side of the family, they could earn 90 yuan a month! Over three or four years, that would add up to a fortune.","So when her daughter mentioned that Si Nian was taking the college entrance exam, Zhang Cuimei immediately worried that this spot would be snatched up by someone else.","This fool had already sold off her broadcasting job for cheap. If the buyer hadn't been Fu Qianqian, leaving her with no other options, Zhang Cuimei would definitely have caused a scene.","This time, naturally, she couldn't let the job slip away.","Si's Father didn't even care about losing face. He coughed and said, \"Yes, Nian Nian, your mother is right. Such a good job opportunity cannot be given away cheaply to others.\"","Zhang Cuimei coaxed, \"I heard from Sisi that the teachers at the First High School wouldn't accept you, so you had no choice but to go to the Second High School. Don't worry, as long as you listen to me, I'll handle this for you and guarantee you get back into the First High School.\"","After hearing this, Si Nian laughed. \"I was wondering why you came visiting out of the blue. Turns out you've got your eyes on my job.\"","The smiles on their faces instantly froze.","Zhang Cuimei said unhappily, \"What do you mean 'got our eyes on your job'? That sounds so awful. Aren't we doing this for your sake?\"","\"Exactly. When you come back later, you can go straight to work. What a wonderful thing.\""]},{"number":370,"title":"Chapter 370: Keep the benefits within the family.","paragraphs":["Si Nian sneered, \"If I give it to someone else, I can still come back and work as usual. Why should I give it to you?\"","Zhang Cuimei's face looked ugly: \"Good things should be kept within the family, don't you understand? And you call yourself an educated person, yet you don't even know such a simple truth.\"","Si Nian rubbed her chin: \"That's true, but if I remember correctly, the last time you, Auntie, cursed my son and said he deserved to be caught by human traffickers, I told you that I was cutting ties with you and we would have nothing more to do with each other. We are not related by blood, nor are we relatives. Why should I give it to you?\"","Lin Sisi said, \"Sister Si Nian, how can you say that? No matter what, my parents raised you for over a decade. You're going too far.\"","Si Nian replied, \"My parents also raised you for over a decade, and how did you treat them? Not only did you steal their three thousand yuan bride price, causing them to lose all face, but you also pushed their biological daughter into a fire pit to be a stepmother. When it comes to going too far, I am not even one ten-thousandth as bad as you, Lin Sisi.\"","Lin Sisi's face flushed red.","Si Nian couldn't even be bothered to argue with Lin Sisi anymore. She looked directly at Si's Father and Si's Mother and said, \"Lin Sisi caused the Lin family to have no peace, but what did I do wrong? I grew up obedient and sensible in the Si family. You wanted face, I gave you face. You wanted grades, I gave you grades. I even brought the commander's son right to your hands, giving up a readily available bright future. In the end, for the sake of your biological daughter, Lin Sisi, I went down to the countryside to marry in her place. What else do I owe you?\"","\"Before, you gave my job as a broadcaster to Lin Sisi without my consent. Now you are scheming for my teaching position. When have you ever truly cared about me, your adopted daughter? In your eyes, I am just an adopted daughter you seek out when useful and wish would roll far away when useless.\"","The couple's old faces flushed red at Si Nian's words.","They wanted to refute her, but everything Si Nian said was the undeniable truth.","\"I am doing very well at the Second High School now. I don't need you to put in a good word for me. I have always believed that gold will shine wherever it is. If the First High School doesn't want me, there are other places that will. You don't need to worry about it.\"","\"If there's nothing else, please leave.\"","The family of three walked out of the Zhou house with dark expressions.","Not only did they gain nothing from this trip, but they also completely lost face.","Although it was true that they had been somewhat in the wrong before and had made her suffer grievances.","But after all, they had raised her for over a decade. To actually kick them out like that was simply going too far.","Fang Hui came to the door of the Si house carrying things, and happened to run into the dejected family of three from the Si family.","She looked at the family curiously, wondering if they were relatives of the Zhou family.","Lin Sisi noticed her too, and her already ugly expression suddenly changed in shock.","Fang... Fang Hui?","Watching the Si family leave, Si Nian finally went out to the Jiang house to pick up Yaoyao.","Grandma Jiang had also seen the group of people who had just come to the Si house. As she hung up clothes, she asked her, \"Niannian, is everything alright? I just saw a lot of people at your door.\"","Grandma Jiang didn't interact much with the people in the tube-shaped apartment building. Although some were easy to get along with, this group of people were gossips when they had nothing to do, and they would dig into everyone's family affairs.","A while ago, when the swine fever was severe, she had even seen this group pointing fingers at the Zhou family.","Now that they had shown up at the door again, it was hard not to overthink it.","Si Nian shook her head and said it was nothing.","Not seeing Yaoyao, she asked, \"Aunt Jiang, where is that girl Yaoyao?\"","Grandma Jiang smiled and said, \"She's in the study playing chess with my old man. I heard the old man say that your Yaoyao has a great talent for Chinese chess, and he wants to teach her how to play. It's really funny. Yaoyao is only three years old, what kind of chess can she play? I think his bad habit is acting up again.\"","After saying that, Grandma Jiang sighed. In the past, when they lived in the family compound, the old man loved to play chess.","After retiring and moving here to the old house, they didn't know many people, and the surrounding relatives had all moved away. The old man couldn't find a playmate and was quite lonely.","He wouldn't even spare a little dumpling like her.","Hearing this, Si Nian's heart skipped a beat.","She still didn't know how to explain Yaoyao's photographic memory.","If she really learned chess just by looking at it, wouldn't Grandpa Jiang realize something was off?","Just a few days ago, those two old professors had come to ask her why she wasn't bringing Yaoyao to class anymore. Clearly, they still had designs on the little girl.","Si Nian was also worried that the older Yaoyao got, the more she would reveal, and eventually, she wouldn't be able to hide it. That was why she had recently reduced the time she spent taking her to school.","She didn't expect that leaving her at the Jiang house wouldn't be safe either.","However, the Jiang family were acquaintances, so there was no need to worry too much.","Thinking of this, Si Nian breathed a sigh of relief and hurried to call Yaoyao home.","\"Oh, Teacher Xiao Si is here. I was just about to have your aunt ask you if you still have any of that darned mung bean soup.\"","The old man sitting in front of the chessboard playing chess smiled and greeted Si Nian.","Si Nian glanced at Yaoyao, who was lying on the floor reading a book nearby. Seeing that she wasn't playing chess with the old man, she withdrew her gaze.","She smiled and said, \"Of course I do. I'll bring some over to you as soon as I get back.\"","\"Yaoyao, it's time to go home.\"","Yaoyao hurriedly stood up hugging the book, held it up, and asked the old man.","\"Grandpa, Grandpa, can I read this book?\"","Grandpa Jiang smiled and said, \"Of course you can. Take it back and read it. Just return it to me when you're done.\"","Grandpa Jiang didn't think much about the fact that Yaoyao could read. After all, Si Nian was a teacher, and he had heard that Si Nian's son had been smart since childhood. Therefore, a three-year-old recognizing words wasn't anything strange; his own son had been just as impressive when he was little.","Only after Si Nian led Yaoyao away did he stretch his back and stand up.","Grandma Jiang came in, looked at the chessboard in front of him, and said speechlessly, \"You didn't really play chess with that little girl Yaoyao, did you? She's still a child, don't make things difficult for her.\"","Grandpa Jiang glared at her. \"What do you know? Even though Yaoyao is a child, she's smart, no worse than your son. If you ask me, with a little training, she'll definitely be a Chinese chess master in time! I'm going to teach her secretly now, and then she'll amaze everyone.\"","Grandma Jiang: \"...Childish.\"","Ever since their grandson came back all day saying he wanted to study secretly like his second brother and then amaze everyone, this old man had picked up the phrase too.","Sure enough, birds of a feather flock together.","Si Nian took Yaoyao home, and only then did she look at the book the girl was holding.","It was actually a Chinese chess manual called \"Meng Ru Shen Ji\".","Si Nian was silent for a moment, then asked Yaoyao, \"Yaoyao, can you understand Grandpa's chess book?\"","Yaoyao nodded repeatedly, then shook her head somewhat in distress: \"I understand some of it, but not other parts. I'll ask my brother when he gets back.\"","Si Nian smiled. Although the little girl had been exposed to a lot, she hadn't undergone formal education after all, so there were definitely still many things she didn't understand.","Moreover, a book like \"Meng Ru Shen Ji\" was profound and complex. Many of the words and phrases were not something a child could comprehend."]},{"number":371,"title":"Chapter 371: Having tried your best is what matters most.","paragraphs":["Si Nian rubbed her head and said, \"Then if someone asks you if you can understand it in the future, what will you say?\"","Yaoyao tilted her head, \"I can't understand it, because Mommy says I'm still little. When I'm seven, I'll be able to understand it all.\"","Si Nian smiled and nodded: \"So sensible. Mommy will make you something delicious.\"","Delayed by the Si family's matters, Si Nian hadn't even had time to cook before the children finished their classes.","Yaoyao didn't even play with the radio today. While Si Nian was busy in the kitchen, she sat on the sofa hugging her book to read.","However, she didn't know how to read many of the characters, frowning as she looked at them.","Previously, at Grandpa Jiang's house, whenever there was a character she didn't know, she would ask Grandpa Jiang, and Grandpa Jiang would teach her.","But Mommy was busy, and her brothers hadn't come back yet...","Just as she was feeling distressed, Second Child returned.","Before he even entered the door, his loud voice could already be heard: \"Mommy, Mommy! I got 70.5 on my math test today.\"","Fang Bowen stood on the second floor. He was sick, so the school gave him time off, and he hadn't been to school for several days.","He heard Zhou Zehan's voice from afar.","He couldn't help but curl his lip. It's just seventy points, what's there to be happy about.","If he had only scored seventy points, he would have been beaten long ago.","Just as he was about to close the curtains, he saw Si Nian walk out.","Followed by her gentle voice, \"Our Little Han is so amazing now. What do you want to eat tonight? Mommy will make it for you.\"","\"Mommy, I want to eat braised pork!\"","Fang Bowen couldn't bear to listen anymore and pulled the curtains shut.","While eating dinner that night, he still couldn't figure it out in his head.","Why did Teacher Si praise Zhou Zehan when he only scored 70 points?","Yet, if he scored even one point less, he would be punished by his mother.","Fang Bowen couldn't help but ask Fang Hui, \"Mommy, if I scored seventy points, would you be angry?\"","Fang Hui immediately slammed her chopsticks down with a smack. \"What nonsense are you talking about? How could you possibly score only seventy points? How could the son of Fang Hui get such a low score!\"","Fang Bowen didn't dare to speak anymore.","He still didn't understand.","Why was it like this?","As soon as Si Nian went to the classroom the next day, she found a small figure standing at the door.","There was only one person this small in the genius class.","It was Fang Bowen.","\"Bowen, you came to school. Are you feeling better?\" Si Nian was his English teacher after all, so she couldn't pretend not to see him and greeted him.","Although Fang Bowen usually found the brothers unpleasing to the eye, he was very shy in front of Si Nian and gave a blushing \"Mhm.\"","Because of Fang Hui, Si Nian hadn't interacted much with this child either.","At this moment, they were momentarily speechless.","But seeing that he looked like he had something on his mind, she asked, \"What's wrong? Do you need me for something?\"","Fang Bowen slowly nodded, and after a long while, he said, \"Teacher Si... thank you.\"","Si Nian looked at him.","She saw him take another good while before saying, \"Thank you for taking me to the hospital last time and saving me.\"","Seeing that he was quite polite, Si Nian's previous displeasure dissipated a bit. After all, the other party was still a child. Although she disliked Fang Hui, she wouldn't take her anger out on a child. She smiled and said, \"You're welcome. It's what a teacher should do.\"","Fang Bowen stopped talking again.","Si Nian felt a bit of a headache. Seeing that class was about to start, she said, \"If there's nothing else, the teacher will go to class first.\"","Fang Bowen bit his lip and gave a quiet \"Mhm.\" Si Nian watched him twiddling his fingers, frowned, and turned around.","Having just taken a few steps, she heard Fang Bowen's weak voice behind her again: \"Teacher Si, Zhou Zehan only scored seventy points. Why weren't you angry, and why did you even praise him?\"","Si Nian was taken aback for a moment. She turned around, only to see Fang Bowen looking at her with a complicated expression.","She found it a bit baffling, thinking of the fact that Second Child had scored seventy points yesterday.","Could it be that Fang Bowen had seen it?","She paused, stood still, and then smiled, \"Why do you ask?\"","Fang Bowen's face was written all over with inner conflict: \"I have never scored seventy points, because my mother says that anyone who scores below 95 is a poor student and is not worthy of praise. But Zhou Zehan only scored seventy points, and you rewarded him.\"","Si Nian generally understood why he was asking this question.","Thinking of Fang Hui's educational style, she furrowed her brows tightly, took two steps forward, and said, \"Bowen, I don't know how your mother teaches you, and it's not my place to say much. But in my eyes, getting a hundred points isn't the most important thing; having tried your best is what truly matters.\""]},{"number":372,"title":"Chapter 372: I think I have a talent for this.","paragraphs":["After saying that, Si Nian patted his shoulder and entered the classroom.","Fang Bowen stood frozen in place.","Waiting until Si Nian's back disappeared from view, he lowered his head, pursed his lips, and whispered, \"But... I've been working really hard too.\"","It was just that Zhou Zehan's efforts were seen and acknowledged by Teacher Si. But his own efforts were completely ignored by his mother.","Teacher Si cared about the process, while his mother only cared about the results.","Over at the Si family home, Lin Sisi was in a state of turmoil.","She had completely lost the mood to study. The homework she handed in had even been repeatedly criticized.","It wasn't that she didn't want to study hard; her mind simply wasn't on it right now.","The things happening recently had already slipped out of her control.","If she didn't correct them in time, it might truly become irreversible.","Because of this, she feigned illness and took a few days off.","The other day, she had run into a familiar face at the door of Si Nian's house.","That's right, that woman was Fang Hui.","The woman who had changed her destiny in her previous life.","She never expected her to be right by Si Nian's side.","Fang Hui was a reporter. In their previous life, Si Nian's business had boomed, and having married Fu Yang, she had enjoyed boundless glory and success.","Fang Hui had once needed to interview Si Nian for a work assignment. Because of this, she neglected her own son, who reportedly died in an accident later on.","As a result, Fang Hui harbored a deep grudge against Si Nian and constantly wrote unfavorable reports about her.","Even the fact that Si Nian wasn't the biological daughter of the Si family was dug up by her.","However, she had discovered it too late. By the time Lin Sisi was found and informed of this, it was already too late.","At that time, Si Nian and Fu Yang were already a loving married couple, and the Si family was incredibly proud of her.","Only then did Lin Sisi realize that the woman she had once envied was actually the thief who had stolen her identity.","Later, she was reborn.","The very first thing Lin Sisi did upon her rebirth was to find Mother and Father Si to reclaim her true identity.","Her heart was set on making Si Nian, this endlessly glamorous eldest daughter, experience the suffering she had once endured.","She was so focused on planning traps for Si Nian that she completely forgot about Fang Hui, whom she had only met much later.","Yet, unexpectedly, she bumped into Fang Hui right at Si Nian's doorstep.","This shocked Lin Sisi greatly.","Because in her past life, Fang Hui hadn't appeared until many years later.","The Fang Hui of that time had looked somewhat wretched, her eyes brimming with resentment toward Si Nian. Whenever Si Nian was mentioned, she would frantically claim that Si Nian had ruined her life.","Her hatred for Si Nian was so deep that it led her to offend Fu Yang. Ultimately fired from her job, she sought out Lin Sisi, wanting her to step forward and help expose Si Nian's identity as a fake heiress, ready to fight Si Nian to the bitter end.","However, Lin Sisi had been reborn before she could seize that opportunity.","She never imagined Fang Hui would appear this early.","If she hadn't interviewed Si Nian yet, did that mean her son wasn't dead?","Then wouldn't that mean she didn't have a grudge against Si Nian?","Even though her rebirth had changed many things, Lin Sisi realized that almost everyone she had met in the past would still make an appearance.","In that case, she wasn't fighting alone.","If she had Fang Hui's help, perhaps her own reputation would improve, and Si Nian wouldn't be able to continue her glamorous life.","Of course, this matter couldn't be rushed. Now that she knew where Fang Hui was, she just needed to find an opportunity to approach her when the time was right.","Right now, the person occupying Lin Sisi's mind was Liu Dongdong. What exactly did Liu Dongdong go to the gynecology department for? Was it really just a simple gynecological issue like Si Nian had claimed?","But if that were the case, why did she bundle herself up so tightly, terrified of being recognized?","And who exactly was this boyfriend Liu Dongdong spoke of?","Why didn't her parents know anything about him?","Was there truly something going on between her and Fu Yang?","She would only find out once Liu Dongdong returned.","Lin Sisi had called the village. After learning that Liu Dongdong had never gone home, she became even more certain that Liu Dongdong wasn't as sincere to her as she appeared on the surface.","She had originally thought she was the one using Liu Dongdong, only to finally realize that she seemed to be the one being used.","Lin Sisi tried her hardest to suppress the panic rising within her. If she lost her composure, who else could help her?","She asked around the neighborhood and learned from the neighbors that Liu Dongdong basically stayed at the Si residence all the time, rarely going out except to buy groceries.","She did frequently deliver food to the Fu family, but everyone just assumed it was arranged by Mother and Father Si.","If she never went out, how could she have possibly met a boyfriend?","Lin Sisi nearly crushed her teeth from gritting them so hard.","Fortunately, on the third day, Liu Dongdong finally returned.","Lin Sisi immediately confronted her about her boyfriend.","Zhang Cuimei was also somewhat suspicious and asked directly, \"Dongdong, didn't you say you went back to your hometown? Why did someone say they saw you at the hospital's gynecology department? Is something wrong with your health?\"","A place like the gynecology department—when an unmarried, childless woman went there, she would inevitably be misunderstood.","Zhang Cuimei had been dwelling on this too, feeling that only girls who didn't respect themselves would go there.","Coupled with her daughter mentioning that Liu Dongdong had a boyfriend, she couldn't help but overthink it.","Which made her blurt out the question.","Liu Dongdong's expression shifted, but she quickly explained, \"I-I just went to deliver something for someone, I wasn't there to see a doctor myself.\"","Zhang Cuimei breathed a sigh of relief, but Lin Sisi didn't believe a word of it.","Delivering something required bundling up so tightly? And lying to them about going back to her hometown?","She asked suspiciously, \"What about that boyfriend of yours? What's his name? Bring him out so I can meet him; I'll help you see if he's a good match.\"","Liu Dongdong lowered her head. She had already guessed what was going on, and she knew that if she said she had one, Lin Sisi would definitely find a way to force her to bring him out. Thus, she said, \"W-We've already broken up. Actually, I've been in a bad mood these past few days because of this, which is why I wanted to take a break.\"","Lin Sisi said thoughtfully, \"Is that so? My mom even said she'd help you evaluate him, and if he wasn't any good, we'd introduce you to someone else. My mom knows quite a few good families. If you married into one, you'd definitely live a good life. Right, Mom?\"","Zhang Cuimei chimed in, \"Of course. Dongdong, you're not getting any younger. Having a pure, unmarried girl taking care of us all the time makes me feel bad. Don't worry, Dongdong, the ones Auntie introduces to you will definitely be good, and they won't look down on you for being from the countryside...\"","Liu Dongdong's face looked awful. \"O-Of course. It's just that I've just broken up, and I really...\"","Lin Sisi smiled. \"What does that matter? Out with the old, in with the new. Besides, it's just to let you meet them; it's not like you're being forced to marry them, right? This is my mom's good intention, after all.\"","Zhang Cuimei also felt a bit uncomfortable in her heart. If her daughter hadn't strongly insisted she help, she would never have introduced someone like Liu Dongdong to anyone.","Although Liu Dongdong took care of them, it didn't change the fact that she was an uneducated country bumpkin. Not only were her background conditions poor, but her older sister was even having an affair with Zhang Cuimei's husband.","If it weren't for the fact that she was her daughter's friend, she wouldn't have even let her stay.","And now, she was actually hesitating.","She really thought too highly of herself.","Hearing her daughter's words, she reluctantly gave face and agreed, \"That's right. An opportunity like this isn't something just anyone can get.\"","Lin Sisi pressed, \"Or could it be, Dongdong, that you're still pining over that boyfriend of yours, and that's why you're unwilling?\"","Liu Dongdong tightened her grip and forced a smile. \"How could that be...\"","Over at the Si family, everyone harbored their own ulterior motives.","However, things were incredibly peaceful on Si Nian's side.","Si Nian told Zhou Yueshen about the people from the apartment building coming over to apologize.","Zhou Yueshen's expression didn't change much, but afraid that she might feel pressured, he said, Give it some time and they will stop making a fuss. Don't worry.","Originally, Zhou Yueshen only wanted to teach these people a simple lesson. If he were to truly target them, it wouldn't bring any benefit to his own family either.","At the very least, he wanted them to know that the Zhou family was not someone they could casually offend or bully.","Now, not only the middle-aged women, but even Da Zhuang and his group of children had been taught a lesson and were forbidden from coming over to provoke Second Child.","The Zhou family enjoyed a lot more peace and quiet.","Sure enough, it didn't take long for the meat at the supply and marketing cooperative to return to its original price.","The sudden surge in meat prices was wrong to begin with. Seeing that these people had made enough of a profit, the higher-ups naturally had to put on a show of stepping in to prohibit price hikes, threatening fines and so on.","Thus, the price reverted to normal.","The people from the apartment building actually thought their apologies had worked.","They secretly decided in their hearts that no matter who they offended, they must never offend the Zhou family again.","Si Nian was about to take the college entrance examination, so the school allowed her to wrap up her work early. As for who would replace her, Si Nian let the director decide. After all, she had only been there for half a year and didn't know many people well.","The director didn't make things difficult for her.","Meanwhile, Second Child had sprained his ankle a few days ago and was recovering at home.","When Si Nian asked him how he sprained it, he said he was racing with his classmates and ran backward, only to trip over a stone.","Si Nian didn't know whether to be angry or amused.","Second Child wasn't sad at all about missing classes; in fact, he was quite happy.","He even said, If getting sick means I don't have to go to class, then I wish I were sick every day.","A while ago, when he saw that Fang Bowen didn't have to go to school because he was sick, he had been envious. He hadn't expected it to be his turn so soon.","The only thing that troubled him was that his younger sister would ask him every day how to read this character or pronounce that word.","Second Child obviously didn't know, but he was too embarrassed to admit it in front of his sister.","So he would secretly check the dictionary, only to discover that his sister was actually reading some sort of chess book.","In order to project a more authoritative older brother image in front of his sister, he even dug out all his secret savings and went to buy a Gomoku set.","Although it felt a bit different, he figured that since they were both board games, they should be more or less the same.","However, Second Child still didn't quite understand it. Right now, he and Jiang Jiu were hiding by the door, studying how to play.","While other kids had their butts in the air playing marbles, these two kids had their butts in the air playing Gomoku.","Kids were never quiet creatures; if they didn't understand, they would ask.","Every time Zhou Zehan made a move, Jiang Jiu would ask, Second Brother, why did you play here?","Second Brother, can't you play it on the side?","It's empty here, so I'll play here.","Just play wherever you see an empty spot.","Fang Bowen, who was passing by on his way home, listened until the veins on his forehead throbbed. He couldn't take it anymore.","You're so stupid!","Why were his older brother and younger sister so smart, yet Zhou Zehan was so stupid?","He turned around, pointed at the messy black and white pieces, and said, Playing here can block the white piece. This is the right move. When five black pieces are connected in a row, you win!","Second Child froze for a moment, then suddenly saw the light. Ah, I get it! I was wondering why it's called five-in-a-row. So you need to connect five pieces together.","I'm so smart! I think I definitely have a talent for this.","Fang Bowen: ...?"]},{"number":373,"title":"Chapter 373: Complacent","paragraphs":["The two children hadn't realized just how stupid they were yet.","Soon, they were chattering away in discussion.","They even said it was so simple that he had learned it in just two days.","Fang Bowen thought Zhou Zehan was already dumb enough, but he didn't expect Jiang Jiu to be even dumber.","Even after explaining it so clearly, he still didn't know how to play.","Unable to stand Zhou Zehan's smug look, he walked over and placed a white piece to block the spot where the Second Child was feeling so triumphant.","The Second Child was just a beginner. Being blocked all of a sudden left him completely dumbfounded.","He had finally managed to connect four pieces, only to be blocked to death.","This really put him in a tough spot.","Fang Bowen won in just a few moves.","The Second Child refused to accept defeat and asked for another round.","Fang Bowen also got interested, sitting on the ground to play with him.","In the end, Zhou Zehan proudly achieved a ten-game losing streak.","He lost so badly he practically lost his shirt.","When Zhou Zedong returned, he was a bit surprised to see the three children at the door.","The Second Child and Jiang Jiu made sense, but why was Fang Bowen there too?","Compared to Fang Bowen's upright sitting posture, his younger brother and Jiang Jiu were kneeling and sprawling on the ground.","Their poses were more bizarre than the other.","Feeling puzzled, he walked over and asked in a low voice, \"What are you doing?\"","\"Brother, brother, you're finally back!\"","The Second Child was on the verge of tears. If he lost this round, it would be an eleven-game losing streak. How could he face anyone in the future?","Fang Bowen was even a year younger than him!","\"We're playing a board game, help me beat him quickly!\"","\"If you win, I'll give you all my pocket money!\"","Jiang Jiu chimed in, \"Yeah, we'll give you all our pocket money!\"","Zhou Zedong glanced over. \"Gomoku?\"","\"Brother, you know Gomoku?\"","Zhou Zedong nodded.","Zhou Zehan wondered, \"Then why didn't I know about it?\"","If it weren't for his sister reading a book on chess, he wouldn't even know there were all sorts of board games.","\"Then do you know how to play, brother?\"","Zhou Zedong shook his head, \"Never played it.\"","Seeing disappointment written all over his brother's face, he asked again, \"All your pocket money?\"","He remembered that his brother had made quite a bit of money selling rabbits.","Jiang Jiu's family was also very rich.","A glint flashed in Zhou Zedong's eyes.","Zhou Zehan nodded repeatedly. \"Yes, but you have to beat him.\"","Feeling quite embarrassed, he leaned close to his brother's ear and whispered, \"I've already lost ten times. Don't tell Mom.\"","Zhou Zedong was speechless.","You actually have the nerve to say that.","Seeing Zhou Zedong, Fang Bowen's previously relaxed expression suddenly turned serious.","His posture stiffened a bit.","For some reason, he felt an inexplicable sense of oppression from Zhou Zehan's older brother.","He always felt he was very intimidating.","In the past, Fang Bowen didn't quite understand why he felt this way, but later he figured it out.","It was the aura exuded by someone stronger than him.","He could easily beat Zhou Zehan, but even if he tried his best, he probably couldn't beat Zhou Zedong.","But why was it that, deep down, he felt more excitement than fear?","Fang Bowen couldn't really explain this feeling.","But he didn't hate it; he even looked forward to it a little.","Zhou Zedong put down his backpack, sat over, and started playing against Fang Bowen.","Although they were assigned to the same class, he didn't interact much with Fang Bowen. He only knew this kid was very smart.","The knowledge he learned at seven was much more than what Zhou Zedong learned at ten.","Compared to peers of his age, he was indeed outstanding.","But Zhou Zedong felt he was a bit too eager for success, like pulling up seedlings to help them grow.","Of course, this wasn't something he cared about.","It was just that his idiot younger brother was being bullied like this, and as an older brother, he couldn't just turn a blind eye. It definitely wasn't for his brother's pocket money.","The two held white and black pieces respectively.","Gomoku was the simplest game; just hearing the name and taking a casual look was enough to learn it.","The difficulty lay entirely with the opponent.","Although it was Zhou Zedong's first time playing, his moves were very steady.","The two went back and forth, neither giving an inch.","Who knows how much time had passed. The Second Child and Jiang Jiu were watching until their eyelids grew heavy, yet the two of them still hadn't determined a winner.","The speed of their moves also grew slower and slower.","Si Nian was just wondering why the kids hadn't come home yet. The moment she stepped out, she almost tripped over them.","However, before she could speak, another sharp female voice rang out first: \"Fang Bowen, what are you doing?\"","Fang Bowen was startled, and the white piece in his hand clattered onto the board, messing up the game.","Zhou Zedong withdrew his gaze and looked up at him, seeing his face full of terror.","Only then did he realize that they had forgotten the time while playing; it was almost six o'clock.","Fang Hui, with a dark face, came over, yanked Fang Bowen up, and said angrily, \"Who told you to sit on the ground and play? Why didn't you go home when you arrived?\"","\"Have you finished your homework? The tutor is coming to teach soon, and you haven't practiced your piano either. I'll teach you to be so playful!\"","She smacked Fang Bowen heavily on the bottom twice.","The Second Child and Jiang Jiu were scared wide awake from their drowsiness. With a shudder, they hurriedly hid behind Zhou Zedong.","They were afraid that Fang Hui would beat them too in her anger.","They just didn't understand why Fang Bowen's mother was so agitated and even hit people. Fang Bowen's mother was so scary.","Fang Bowen admitted his mistake with a pale little face, \"Mom, I know I was wrong. I shouldn't have been playing around.\"","He felt a bit remorseful. How could he have been so playful that he forgot the time?","He originally planned to play for a little while and then go back, so his mom wouldn't notice.","But playing against Zhou Zedong was so engrossing that he lost track of time.","Seeing Zhou Zehan and Jiang Jiu looking at him in terror, he lowered his head and bit his lip, a sense of humiliation welling up inside him.","After her anger subsided, Fang Hui finally realized she was being stared at by so many people.","She withdrew her hand, put on a cold face, and said in a deep voice, \"Go back.\"","Fang Bowen didn't dare say another word. He quickly put on his backpack and ran home without looking back.","Fang Hui then smiled and said, \"I'm really sorry, Teacher Si. Did I scare you? I was just too worried. After all, you know what happened to my son a while ago. Sigh, I'm busy with work and sometimes don't have time to pick him up. He usually comes home on time. Since it was getting so late today and he hadn't come back, I got a bit worried. I didn't expect him to be right at the door.\"","Si Nian couldn't even be bothered to keep up appearances with her anymore.","In her eyes, Fang Hui was just like the parents from her own era in the future, wishing they could treat their children like spinning tops, keeping them spinning twenty-four hours a day.","No wonder Fang Bowen got sick. With a mother like this, it would be strange if the child didn't fall ill.","Although she was also puzzled as to why Fang Bowen was playing with her sons at the door, Fang Hui's actions were truly extreme.","\"So you were worried about your child. Anyone who didn't know better would think you were abusing him. Even as a stepmother, I wouldn't be able to casually beat and scold a six or seven-year-old child the way Miss Fang does.\"","Fang Hui's expression twisted for a moment before she smiled and said, \"I heard these children aren't your biological kids. Naturally, you wouldn't understand the worry we biological mothers feel for our children.\""]},{"number":374,"title":"Chapter 374: Would Rather Be a Stepmother","paragraphs":["Si Nian smiled. \"If a biological mother's worry leads her to hit her child, then I'd rather be a stepmother.\"","Seeing that Si Nian was not giving her an out, Fang Hui could no longer maintain her smile.","If she hadn't been in the wrong during the previous hospital incident, she wouldn't have even bothered talking so much to Si Nian.","After speaking, Si Nian ignored her and looked at the children. \"Little Dong, Little Han, go inside the house.\"","Sensing that they might have done something wrong, the children were a bit scared. They hurriedly packed up the Gomoku board and went inside.","Si Nian closed the door.","Although she felt sorry for Fang Bowen, it wasn't her place to say much.","After all, Fang Hui already disliked her.","If she said too much, the woman would just think she was being a busybody.","It was better to mock her a little; at least Fang Hui would be too embarrassed to hit her child in front of outsiders again.","As for what happened in private, she couldn't say. She just hoped Fang Hui still had some conscience left.","Si Nian's guess was right. When Fang Hui furiously saw her son sitting on the ground playing with the other children, she was so angry that she didn't even see clearly who they were.","That was why she got physical.","If she had known they were the sons of the Zhou family, she wouldn't have been so angry.","After all, everyone knew that Si Nian had saved her son. Letting her son interact with them now might stop people from gossiping.","She might even be able to build a connection with the Jiang family.","She noticed that the little grandson of the Jiang family really liked playing with the two children from the Zhou family.","She didn't know much about the Zhou family, but Fang Hui had inquired very clearly about the Jiang family.","After all, she was a reporter. The Jiang family had a retired chief and scientific researchers.","Befriending such a family would definitely be beneficial to her.","Now look what happened. She had made a fool of herself in front of others.","When Fang Hui returned home and saw her son sitting at the desk doing his homework while trembling, she finally seemed to realize she had gone too far. She rubbed his head and smiled. \"Bowen, Mommy shouldn't have hit you just now. Mommy was just too worried about you. Don't be mad...\"","Fang Bowen turned to look at her suspiciously. Seeing Fang Hui smiling at him, he subconsciously smiled back. \"Really? Then Mommy, can I...\"","Gathering his courage, he asked, \"Can I, can I play with them next time...\"","Before he could finish, Fang Hui's smile instantly darkened. \"No! What's so fun about that? It's a boring game. I want you to build a good relationship with the little grandson of the Jiang family, but you can't learn from them and idle your days away. The most important thing for you right now is studying. Alright, the tutor will be here to give you a lesson later. Hurry up and do your homework...\"","\"Mom, did we do something wrong?\"","As soon as Second Child entered the house, he couldn't help but ask Si Nian.","He kept feeling like he had done something wrong again.","If he hadn't insisted on playing Gomoku with Fang Bowen, he wouldn't have caused him to go home late and get beaten by his mother.","Si Nian was also a bit surprised and asked, \"Weren't you refusing to play with him before? Why did you suddenly start playing together?\"","Jiang Jiu hurriedly said, \"Auntie, Auntie, it's all my fault for being too stupid. Fang Bowen saw that I was too stupid and about to lose to second brother, so he helped me play. Later, second brother and I kept losing to him. When oldest brother came back, we wanted him to help us win it back, which is why we delayed his time.\"","He added, \"Don't blame second brother.\"","Si Nian nodded and didn't blame them. After all, it wasn't them who took the initiative to bother Fang Bowen.","Fang Bowen was young, and he probably just saw two kids his age playing board games and couldn't resist stepping in.","She was actually puzzled. \"Why did you suddenly start playing chess? You even know how to play this?\"","It was one thing for Yaoyao to learn Chinese chess with Grandpa Jiang recently, but how did Second Child also become interested in playing board games?","Didn't he usually play marbles or hide-and-seek with Jiang Jiu?","Second Child said guiltily, \"I thought I had some talent, so I wanted to play more.\"","Si Nian was speechless.","He had just said he lost to Fang Bowen.","Now he was saying he had talent.","She really hadn't noticed that this little guy was so confident in himself.","Next to them, Zhou Zedong's mouth also twitched.","Did you even need talent for Gomoku?","Right at that moment, Yaoyao ran over with a book in her arms, her footsteps going thud-thud. She held up the book and asked Zhou Zedong, \"Brother, Brother, how do you read this?\"","Second Child rushed to answer, \"I know, I know, I know this one.\"","\"'Three fish enter the hall'! This is too easy.\" He didn't even need to check a dictionary.","Hearing this, Zhou Zedong tilted his head to take a look. \"...This is called 'Three eels enter the hall'.\"","Second Child's face turned red at a visible speed.","Chinese people always recognized words by reading half the character, but who knew it was actually the other half!","A fifty percent chance, and he still missed. He was way too unlucky!","As the college entrance examination approached, Si Nian stopped going out and buried herself at home to study hard all day.","After buying bicycles for the children, she no longer needed to specially drop them off at school, nor did she have to pick them up in the afternoon.","She only needed to take care of Yaoyao every day.","Yaoyao didn't know many words, so it took her a very, very long time to read a book.","Mainly because she started with such a difficult one. She read it obsessively but also very slowly.","Unlike the English that Si Nian took her to classes to learn all day, this was the truly profound and extensive culture of China.","Si Nian thought that after finishing this Chinese chess book, Yaoyao would add at least a thousand words to her vocabulary.","When she read quietly, Si Nian felt that this child had the aura of a talented scholar.","She could already imagine how erudite and knowledgeable this child would be when she grew up.","The incident where Second Child got Fang Bowen beaten up seemed to have passed.","But he always felt bad about it in his heart.","Although Fang Bowen's personality wasn't that great, the guy hadn't actually caused him any real harm.","Instead, it had made him see through the hypocrisy of Little Pig and his group.","So when he was eating pancakes in the morning, he deliberately ate two less, secretly put them in a bag, and then squatted at the door waiting for Fang Bowen to appear.","Fang Bowen walked to school, and occasionally his mother would drop him off. Today, he finally managed to catch him alone.","Second Child rushed over like the wind, stuffed the egg pancakes into his arms, and spoke very quickly, \"For you. Sorry I got you hit that day.\"","After saying that, terrified of being seen, he sneaked back home guiltily.","Before Fang Bowen could even react, he just felt a warmth in his arms.","Immediately after, a rich aroma of eggs rushed into his nose.","He looked down and saw two golden egg pancakes in his hands.","It was something he had never eaten before.","He had seen these pancakes at the school gate.","He often saw Zhou Zehan and Jiang Jiu buying them, and his classmates loved eating them too. He would always smell them after class and couldn't help but swallow his saliva.","But his mother never allowed him to eat food from street stalls; she said it was junk food.","So no matter how much he wanted to eat it, Fang Bowen had never asked for it.","But right now, they were piping hot in his arms.","He was stunned for a moment, not even knowing where to put his hands.","No one had ever given him food before.","And it was from Zhou Zehan, whom he had always disliked.","He had even called him an idiot before.","And when they played chess, he had deliberately made him lose miserably.","But not only was he not angry, he even felt guilty about him getting hit by his mother and gave him food.","After quite some time had passed, Fang Bowen glanced back at his front door. Once he was certain that Fang Hui was not standing there, his face flushed and his heart raced as he stuffed the pancake under his clothes. Keeping his head down, he quickly hurried away."]},{"number":375,"title":"Chapter 375: Little Treasury","paragraphs":["Zhou Zedong walked out, looked at his younger brother's guilty expression, and asked him, \"What did you do?\"","Second Child's eyes darted left and right. \"N-nothing.\"","Zhou Zedong: ...","Forget it, he didn't ask any further.","Today they got a new English teacher. Since it wasn't his mother teaching him, Zhou Zedong was a little disappointed, but thinking that his mother wouldn't have to teach and work so hard, he quickly accepted the change of teachers.","The new teacher was also a woman, very gentle, but her teaching wasn't as amazing as his mother's.","After class, the other students were all very disappointed and gathered around to ask him when Teacher Si would come back.","Zhou Zedong felt a bit proud. He couldn't help but lift his chin and say he didn't know.","Everyone looked disappointed.","Zhou Zedong, however, was very happy. Now his mother would only teach him and wouldn't have to teach these annoying crybabies.","They were already in the third and fourth grades, yet they still acted spoiled and cried all day, always pretending to be pitiful in front of his mother. It was unbearable; they were even more annoying than his younger brother.","In a good mood, he took out his book to read, but he smelled a familiar scent.","He subconsciously followed the scent and saw Fang Bowen, who was sitting in the first row, holding an egg pancake and eating it.","He took small bites, his eyes looking a bit panicked as he glanced left and right from time to time.","It was exactly the same as his younger brother's guilty look from this morning.","Zhou Zedong instantly understood.","Si Nian taking the college entrance examination was a major event, so much so that the Lin family from her hometown even called her.","Usually, if there was nothing important, Lin's mother would just write letters.","The fact that she made a special phone call this time was enough to show how much importance they attached to this matter.","Although they had heard that Si Nian's academic performance was very good before, taking the college entrance examination had always been extremely difficult for them.","The number of children from the surrounding villages who could get into college could be counted on one hand.","Lin Sisi used to have such good grades, but even she didn't pass.","Si Nian also had a good idea of how difficult the college entrance exam was in this era. Recently, she had done a lot of past exam papers.","She had gone through all of them from the resumption of the college entrance examination to the present.","It wasn't exactly easy, but to her, it definitely wasn't hard either.","She was practically guaranteed to pass this year's exam.","Coupled with her mature mental age, Si Nian had never panicked at all.","After reassuring her family, she took her bankbook and went out to deposit money.","She now had her own bankbook. Besides Zhou Yueshen's money, Si Nian also deposited her own salary into her bankbook.","Having worked for six months at ninety a month, plus bonuses, she already had 600.","Si Nian hadn't deposited her previous earnings, so she brought them all along this time.","Six hundred yuan was considered a small fortune.","Adding the 8,800 bride price the man gave her, the 3,000 yuan Lin Sisi returned to her, and the 2,000 she got from selling her job.","Si Nian's bankbook already had over 10,000 yuan.","She was now a ten-thousand-yuan household herself.","She would save her own money and spend her man's money.","Rounding it off, it was equivalent to not spending any money at all.","Her bankbook was kept separate from Zhou Yueshen's, for fear that the man would see her little secret stash.","The more Si Nian thought about it, the sweeter she felt. Wasn't this exactly the life she had fantasized about in her previous life?","She never expected to achieve financial freedom in this impoverished era.","When Zhou Yueshen returned home, he heard Si Nian humming a strange song while cooking.","\"We are having a feast tonight.\"","Hearing the noise, Si Nian tilted her head and glanced at the man. Zhou Yueshen took off his jacket, revealing a white tank top underneath.","He casually wiped the sweat from his forehead. In June and July, the city was much hotter than the village.","Hearing her words, he gave Si Nian an extra glance and asked in a deep voice, \"Is today a special day?\"","In fact, they ate very well every day. Not to mention the children, even Zhou Yueshen had gained weight.","But because his body was all muscle, it wasn't obvious.","Si Nian subconsciously replied, \"Of course it's a good day. I saved... ahem, I'm about to take the college entrance exam, isn't that a good day?\"","Zhou Yueshen remembered this matter. After the swine fever passed recently, many factories were shut down overnight, causing their order volume to skyrocket, and he had been working from dawn to dusk every day.","By the time he got back, Si Nian would already be fast asleep.","He had almost forgotten that Si Nian was taking the college entrance exam.","He looked at the calendar nearby; it was June 25th.","That meant there were only a few days left.","However, she didn't seem nervous at all.","True, she had been a teacher after all.","Zhou Yueshen's voice was gentle.","\"Are you confident? What school are you planning to go to?\"","Si Nian stopped chopping vegetables and lowered her head slightly. A few strands of hair fell down, tickling her. \"I want to go to Jing University.\"","Zhou Yueshen suddenly froze.","He had thought that Si Nian's goal probably wouldn't be low.","But he didn't expect her to aim for the absolute highest standard.","After a moment of silence, he replied.","\"Okay.\"","Si Nian couldn't help but look back at him.","Zhou Yueshen was expressionless and didn't seem overly surprised.","She was, after all, someone repeating a year. For anyone else, just getting into any university would be considered incredible.","Let alone Jing University.","The best university in the country.","That was simply a fantasy.","But this man hadn't even considered such issues.","He didn't seem to think she was being whimsical either.","Si Nian withdrew her gaze and asked him, \"What do you think?\"","Zhou Yueshen chuckled softly, \"Of course it's good.\"","The top educational institution in the country, could he possibly say no?","\"Aren't you afraid that I'll run away once I go there?\"","Si Nian continued chopping vegetables, the kitchen knife pressing against the cutting board with a rat-a-tat-tat sound.","Zhou Yueshen fell silent again.","It wasn't that he didn't trust Si Nian; he just didn't have much confidence in himself.","If Si Nian was confident enough to go to such a good school, what kind of life couldn't she have?","Why would she need to take care of three children for him and be a stepmother?","For her, this was already a stain on her brilliant life.","After Si Nian finished speaking, she received no response.","Turning around, she saw the children standing at the kitchen door, looking at her in horror.","Si Nian's hand slipped while chopping, and she almost cut herself.","...Oh no.","Second Child cried and ran over first, hugging her thigh. \"Mom, please don't go. I won't be playful anymore, I will definitely study hard.\"","Si Nian immediately said, \"I'm not going anywhere. I was just joking with your dad.\"","Second Child didn't believe it. He was no longer a three-year-old child; he was already seven.","In the past, there was a child's mother in the village who said the same thing and then ran away secretly.","But those families were living very poorly, and they would beat their wives, which was why they ran away.","Could it be that Dad secretly bullied Mom, so Mom wanted to run away?","Second Child figured it out and immediately said, \"Mom, if you're going to run away, take me with you. I run fast, Dad will definitely not catch up to us.\"","\"Big Brother and Little Sister can stay with Dad, because they can't run fast and will hold us back.\"","\"Mom, don't worry, even if it's just me, I will be a filial son to you. I will raise a lot of rabbits to make money, buy you clothes and shoes, and I will study hard and never be naughty again.\"","Hearing this, Si Nian didn't know whether to laugh or cry.","Hearing their younger brother's crazy words, Zhou Zedong and Yaoyao both darkened their little faces.","Yaoyao came over and gave Zhou Zehan a push, her chubby little face quivering with anger. \"Second Brother is bad! I'm never talking to you again! I want to go with Mom too.\"","Zhou Zedong was older, after all. Though he was dissatisfied with his younger brother's words, he didn't dare say he would leave with their mother right in front of their father.","If he were to run away, he would do it secretly. He wouldn't be like his brother.","Even though that would make their father very pitiful, it didn't matter. He would secretly send him money in the future.","He absolutely wouldn't let his father become a pitiful, lonely old man.","Seeing that the three children were about to start arguing, Si Nian hurriedly stopped them.","\"Alright, alright, I'm really not leaving.\"","\"Mom, are you really not leaving?\"","\"Mom, if you don't leave, I won't leave either.\"","\"Mom, look, I even know how to recite poetry now. I can memorize two poems a day. I'll recite them for you.\"","\"I'll cook for you, Mom.\"","Si Nian looked at the three siblings and said, \"Okay, okay, whatever you say.\"","The three little ones saw that she really didn't look like she was going to run away, and only then did they truly relax.","\"Mom, go rest, I'll cook.\"","\"Okay.\"","Si Nian was pushed out of the kitchen by the Second Child. Behind them, Zhou Yueshen sighed helplessly. These kids didn't have their father in their eyes at all... Whatever.","That night, Si Nian swapped places with Zhou Yueshen, stating that she wanted to sleep on the other side.","Usually, it was the man on the left and the woman on the right, but today she insisted on taking Zhou Yueshen's spot.","Simply because from this position, she could see the cabinet where she kept her bankbook.","Looking at her bankbook, Si Nian fell asleep feeling completely satisfied.","Zhou Yueshen, on the other hand, couldn't sleep. Even though Si Nian said she was joking, he couldn't help but take it to heart.","Beijing University?","It really was far away...","After Lin Sisi returned, Liu Dongdong gradually disappeared from the family compound's sight.","Whenever anyone asked, Lin Sisi would explain, \"Her? My mom saw that she isn't getting any younger, so she found a few good families for her. She's probably busy with blind dates these days.\"","Hearing this, everyone felt that the Si family was quite nice. \"I heard that girl came from the countryside where you used to live. The fact that your mother still cares enough to find her a good family means she's benefiting from your good fortune.\"","\"Yes, she's already nineteen. It's time to find a husband's family for her.\"","\"If you ask me, her older sister is no good, so she's probably not very clean either. I saw her running over to the Fu family's house before. I'm not trying to ruin your relationship, but as an unmarried girl, Sisi, you should be careful.\"","Lin Sisi tightened her grip. It turned out that everyone knew about this, and she was the only one kept in the dark all along.","\"Alright, alright, let's not talk about that anymore. I heard Sisi is going to take the college entrance examination, right? Are you confident?\"","Lin Sisi was from the countryside and had even been to prison.","The fact that she was actually thinking about taking the college entrance examination now inevitably drew more attention to her.","After all, education in the countryside wasn't very good. It was said that in some villages, you couldn't even find a single college student.","For Lin Sisi to even consider taking the exam was quite surprising.","It had been more than a year since Lin Sisi was recognized and brought back, but people didn't know her very well. Now, they couldn't help but wonder just how capable she really was.","Was she really brave enough because she had good grades, or was she just putting on an act?","Lin Sisi, however, was quite confident. She said, \"I can't guarantee a top-tier prestigious university, but I can definitely get into a college. Thank you all for your concern.\"","Everyone was astonished to hear this.","Other people were always nervous and afraid during the college entrance examination, terrified that they wouldn't pass.","How could she be so certain that she would get in?","If she really could get into a university, then she wouldn't be considered a bad match for Fu Yang anymore.","\"Then we'll wait for your good news.\"","\"I heard that since Fu Yang came back from the Northwest, he's been staying at the military base for training and hasn't come back much. If he finds out you got into college, he'll definitely come back to celebrate with you, right?\"","\"Yeah, it's such a big deal.\"","Thinking of Fu Yang, everyone couldn't help but feel curious again.","They heard that something had happened back then; there was an accident during his mission, and Fu Yang was seriously injured.","Since that incident, Fu Yang rarely appeared in the public eye.","When Lin Sisi was released from prison, acquaintances came to visit, but not even a shadow of him was seen.","No one knew what was going on.","Hearing this, Lin Sisi lowered her head shyly.","She had also heard about Fu Yang's situation.","She figured that Fu Yang must have suffered quite a blow.","Lin Sisi had also gone to the Fu family to ask about the situation, but they were very dismissive.","Lin Sisi didn't know what was happening either.","Therefore, she was now eager to start the college entrance examination as soon as possible.","As long as her results came out and she got into a university, Fu Yang would surely look at her in a new light.","In her previous life, he had initially treated Si Nian like a mere vase, ignoring her just like he was doing to her now.","But later, after Si Nian left, didn't he fall in love with her anyway?","Lin Sisi felt that she understood Fu Yang very well. She knew that he liked independent women who could stand shoulder to shoulder with him.","On the eve of the college entrance examination, the Si family even specially invited acquaintances over for a meal.","Now, basically the entire family compound knew that Lin Sisi was going to take the exam.","The Fu family naturally knew as well, but they had no intention of showing any reaction.","Even if Lin Sisi turned into a flower, Mother Fu was in no mood to let her son continue his relationship with her.","Especially since the Si family was using Lin Sisi's college entrance examination as a threat to prevent them from getting a divorce, dragging it out time and time again.","Mr. and Mrs. Fu were both extremely angry.","If it weren't for the fact that they all lived in the same family compound and tearing each other's faces apart in a big scene would be too ugly, they absolutely would not have allowed this to happen.","Since Lin Sisi wanted to take the exam, fine. They would watch closely and see if she could actually achieve anything spectacular.","Since Si Nian was taking the college entrance examination, Yu Dong also volunteered, saying that he would treat his sister-in-law to a meal after the exams were over.","In the past, he always went to the Zhou family's house to freeload meals, but now he was a restaurant owner himself.","Yu Dong also planned to secretly learn some cooking recipes from Si Nian to make his restaurant flourish.","Actually, at first, Yu Dong was very annoyed at being forced to go home and inherit the restaurant.","His old man said that if he could make it successful, he would let him manage the family property in the future.","At the time, Yu Dong was thinking about how to run the restaurant into the ground. That way, his dad would realize that his son had no talent for business and wouldn't make him manage it anymore.","But later, when he saw Fu Qianqian's workplace organizing a meal at his restaurant and saw her surprised expression, Yu Dong changed his mind.","He decided he was going to make the restaurant flourish!","Si Nian taking the college entrance examination was also a major event for the Zhou family.","For the past few days, they hadn't let her do any chores, allowing Si Nian to prepare for the exam in peace.","In the evening, while Si Nian was calmly taking a bath, Zhou Yueshen had already started packing the stationery she would need for the exam."]},{"number":376,"title":"Chapter 376: Gifts and the College Entrance Examination","paragraphs":["The first subject was Chinese, which required the most writing.","Next was Math, which required scratch paper.","However, the school usually provided scratch paper to prevent cheating.","But to be safe, Zhou Yueshen felt he should prepare some in advance.","He rummaged through the desk but couldn't find a scratchpad.","Si Nian had a habit of working at her vanity table, where she also kept some books.","He bent down and opened the cabinet door. There was no paper or pen inside, but rather a new bankbook.","Zhou Yueshen paused.","Si Nian came out of the shower, drying her damp hair with one hand. She was wearing a silk nightgown. The warm orange light from above cascaded down, bathing her in a gentle, tangerine glow.","\"Zhou Yueshen, what are you doing?\"","Zhou Yueshen straightened up and turned around, his dark eyes falling on her.","Her hair had grown a bit long, draping wetly down her back.","Zhou Yueshen held up the pencil case in his hand. \"You have your exam tomorrow. I prepared some things you'll need. Take a look and see if anything is missing.\"","Si Nian stepped forward, still rubbing her hair, and peeked inside. It contained all kinds of pens, rulers, and erasers she would need.","They were all brand new.","Even the pencils were sharpened, with beautifully neat cuts.","It looked as if they had been sharpened with a mechanical sharpener.","She looked at it for a moment and smiled. \"That's pretty much everything.\"","Zhou Yueshen zipped it up and set the pencil case aside.","Then, he reached out, took the towel from her hand, and began drying her hair for her.","\"Are you nervous?\"","Si Nian replied calmly, \"Not nervous.\"","Hearing this, Zhou Yueshen chuckled softly. \"Go to sleep early tonight. I'll take you there tomorrow.\"","Surprised, Si Nian looked up at him. \"You're not going to work tomorrow?\"","During the day, Si Nian occasionally liked to put on a little makeup. It wasn't very obvious, but it gave her features a striking, almost aggressive beauty.","After her shower, she looked entirely soft. Without makeup, her skin was as smooth as a peeled egg, and her long eyelashes were clearly visible when Zhou Yueshen looked down.","Zhou Yueshen looked at her for a few seconds before speaking.","\"Work isn't as important as your college entrance exam. I've already let the factory know.\"","He didn't really have anyone around him taking the exam.","But he remembered when the army had a literacy campaign; since he was illiterate back then, he was sent to study.","At that time, they studied and took exams just like regular students.","He wasn't that particular himself, but later, when Yu Dong went to take the military academy exam, he saw Yu Dong's entire family go to support him.","For such an important event, of course they had to be there for her.","Thinking of this, Zhou Yueshen suddenly stopped what he was doing.","He walked over to the table and took a square box out of a bag.","He walked back and handed it to Si Nian.","\"This is a gift for you.\"","\"A gift?\"","Surprised, Si Nian reached out to take it. As she opened it, a faint fragrance drifted into her nose.","She was pleasantly surprised. \"Perfume?\"","Zhou Yueshen gave a slight nod. \"Yu Dong went on a business trip to Hong Kong a few days ago, and I asked him to bring it back. I don't know if you'll like it.\"","Si Nian sniffed it and said joyfully, \"It's my favorite red rose scent.\"","Because she usually loved taking petal baths and bought rose-scented body wash, she always had a faint fragrance lingering on her.","Zhou Yueshen didn't really know what women liked, but when Yu Dong asked if he wanted him to bring anything back this time, he suddenly realized something.","Si Nian always loved using fragrant things. When she came home, the whole house would smell sweet, and she even used petals in her baths.","So he figured she would like perfume.","Seeing her sweet smile, Zhou Yueshen's sharp features softened. He reached out to pat her head and chuckled softly, \"As long as you like it.\"","Si Nian nodded immediately. \"Thank you.\"","Although the original owner of this body was only nineteen, still young, and rarely used things like perfume.","But Si Nian herself was a mature woman. In her past life, perfume was her absolute favorite.","In this era, wearing perfume was a bit extravagant, especially since she had been living in the countryside before.","Over time, she had simply stopped using these things.","She never expected Zhou Yueshen to suddenly gift her a bottle of perfume.","Looking at the brand, it was imported too.","Si Nian said, \"On the day my results come out, I'm going to wear my prettiest dress and put on this perfume!\"","Zhou Yueshen smiled and said okay.","A tiny bottle of perfume had invisibly drawn the two of them closer once again.","Si Nian sat in the man's lap, letting him dry her hair while she opened the perfume to smell it again. It was a very subtle fragrance, without any hint of artificial essence or additives—light and elegant!","This man was so silly. He gave it to her right away without even noticing the price tag on the back.","Such a small bottle of classic French perfume actually cost two hundred yuan.","He was really generous.","A man willing to spend money on his woman would always score big points in her book.","The more Si Nian thought about it, the happier she became—even happier than if Zhou Yueshen had just handed her cash. Of course, she used to care more about money, but now that she wasn't lacking it, she started valuing these emotional comforts.","She couldn't help but look up and kiss the man on the chin, saying, \"Thank you.\"","Zhou Yueshen paused for a moment, then chuckled softly. \"Let's dry your hair first.\"","She needed to sleep early tonight.","The location of the college entrance exam changed every year, and all candidates were scattered to prevent acquaintances from cheating.","She heard it was at the No. 1 High School last year, and this year it was at the No. 2 High School.","Because of this, the first and second-year high school students were given days off to make room for them.","Si Nian was quite lucky. Students assigned to test here from other schools who lived far away had to arrange accommodation and so on.","During the exam period, no one wanted to travel too far, so students who lived far from home chose to board or find a nearby hotel.","Not a single minute or second could be wasted.","Many students even agreed to share a room to save money.","Si Nian lived quite far away too, but after Zhou Yueshen said he would drive her back and forth these few days, she dropped the idea of finding accommodation.","The primary school was also on break these two days, so the whole family rallied around Si Nian. Even the Jiang family next door constantly checked in on her.","Grandma Jiang even brought over a lot of food, telling her to rest, and if cooking was too much trouble, they could just go eat at her place.","Si Nian naturally declined, because Yu Dong's restaurant happened to be located not far past the No. 2 High School, less than a ten-minute drive away. Zhou Yueshen had already pre-ordered her meals there for three days.","This way, she wouldn't have to run around, and eating would be convenient.","For the exam, comfort was key. The weather was hot, and to avoid heatstroke, Si Nian changed into a simple yet beautiful dress and tied her hair into two braids, making her look youthful and vibrant.","Her bag was a rather large crossbody bag. She had bought it specifically when she was a teacher because she had to carry a lot of things every day.","Now, she used it to carry her stationery.","Breakfast was made by Zhou Yueshen himself: millet porridge, soup dumplings, eggs, and milk.","Simple and nutritious.","Si Nian was dressed so youthfully and radiantly that Li Yanhong, who came over early in the morning to deliver documents, couldn't help but take a few extra glances. Was this really how the factory manager's wife dressed at home?","She greeted Si Nian and hurried off after delivering the documents. With the factory director away, she, as his assistant, was as busy as a dog.","Walking out, Li Yanhong couldn't help but mutter to herself that she couldn't be blamed for mistaking the wife for the director's daughter. With that outfit, anyone would call her an innocent high school girl.","It really wasn't her fault for getting it wrong back then!","Even though the director never brought it up, seemingly letting it go, sometimes he still seemed quite annoyed with her.","Li Yanhong shivered. For the sake of this high salary, there was nothing she couldn't endure.","Keep it up, working girl!","Pumping herself up, Li Yanhong's eyes turned resolute as she marched toward the breeding farm like she was going to her doom.","The kids didn't understand how important the college entrance examination was. Right now, they were eating the porridge their dad cooked, drinking milk, and laughing out loud while watching TV.","Only Zhou Zedong and Zhou Yueshen wore serious expressions.","Even Zhou Zedong, who usually spoke very little, was unusually talkative today.","While talking, he took out the stationery he had prepared the night before from his schoolbag, piece by piece.","\"Mom, did you bring your pencil case?\"","\"Mom, I have sharpened pencils here.\"","\"Mom, this ruler is new, take it to use.\"","\"Mom...\"","\"Alright, alright, Little Dong. Your dad has already packed all these for me. Keep them for yourself,\" Si Nian said with a smile.","Zhou Zedong's hand paused, and he looked up at his dad.","Zhou Yueshen also looked back at him.","In the end, Zhou Zedong pursed his lips and put his things away.","After breakfast, the whole family got into the car together.","Because he was taking Si Nian, Zhou Yueshen had washed the car beforehand, making it sparkling clean.","It looked brand new.","There was no odd smell at all.","In the passenger seat, there were fruits, tissues, and snacks.","As if he was terrified she might go hungry.","Si Nian felt like she wasn't going to take the college entrance exam, but rather to ascend the throne.","She wanted to laugh, yet felt incredibly warm inside.","In her past life, when she took the exam, her family placed too much pressure and high hopes on her. Every day they pushed her to study hard, and no one cared about how she felt.","There was even an accident during the exam period. Because she was too nervous, she got a stomachache, which caused her to score poorly in English, her best subject.","Although she eventually got into a prestigious university, she didn't enter with the best grades.","Her parents still brought this up on the phone years after she started working.","But right now, Zhou Yueshen was just afraid she might feel even a trace of nervousness.","It was so nice.","The examination rooms had been assigned in advance, so Si Nian just needed to head straight there.","When she arrived, the school gate was packed with people.","A huge crowd of parents led their children, giving them instructions as they walked.","Because the college entrance exam was held here, almost all the nearby street vendors had gathered. The entrance of No. 2 High School had turned into a commercial street with rows of snacks that dazzled the eyes.","Si Nian also saw Brother Chen and his crew. A group of kids was crowded around them buying pancakes.","These kids were smart; they went wherever the business was booming.","They would probably make quite a bit over these few days.","Si Nian looked at her eldest son.","She wondered if he had called them over.","Sure enough, Brother Chen and the others soon spotted the family.","While busy making pancakes, they didn't forget to raise their hands and greet them: \"Brother Dong! Hello, Brother Dong's mom!\"","\"Good luck, Auntie!\"","\"Auntie will definitely ace the exam!\"","The other two also raised their spatulas and cheered.","These kids had eaten the food Si Nian sent them before, so now that they knew she was taking the college entrance exam, they naturally wanted to cheer her on.","Other people instantly turned their heads to look at Si Nian.","Si Nian couldn't help but smile; they were really an interesting bunch of kids.","Hearing the voices, Zhou Zehan finally reacted and said with a smile, \"Mom, Big Brother, look! Brother Chen and the others are here too.\"","Zhou Zedong didn't even want to reply to him. They had already finished their greetings, and you're only reacting now?","It was still early, an hour before the exam, yet so many people had already arrived.","Si Nian decided to take a stroll with Zhou Yueshen and the kids.","It was rare for the whole family to go out together so neatly.","\"Mom, look, sugar figures! The sugar figures you bought for me before.\"","Seeing someone making sugar figures, Second Child pointed in pleasant surprise.","He still remembered that last year, his mom had given him his very first sugar figure.","But before he could look longer, his attention was drawn to an uncle selling cotton candy nearby.","\"Wow, so this is how cotton candy is made. It's so pretty!\"","Yaoyao was also stirred up by her brother, her eyes unable to take it all in.","Seeing the cotton candy, she immediately squeezed in, clinging to the table with her second brother to watch the uncle make cotton candy.","Watching the cotton candy being bought by someone else, she immediately pulled on Zhou Zehan and said, \"Second Brother, Yaoyao wants one.\"","Zhou Zehan wanted one too, but he had no money.","He had given all his secretly saved money to his big brother.","But thinking of something, his eyes lit up. He turned around, tugged at his dad, who was holding hands with his mom, and raised his head to say, \"Dad, my sister says she wants to eat cotton candy.\"","He wasn't lying; his sister really did say she wanted to eat it.","Zhou Yueshen stopped, looked down at his sparkling eyes, and then glanced at his daughter clinging to the vendor's table. He took out a ten-yuan bill from his wallet, handed it to him, and said in a deep voice, \"Watch over your sister.\"","Dad was the most generous. Little Han pleasantly grabbed the ten-yuan bill and immediately took his sister to buy cotton candy.","In no time, the two kids were holding cotton candy in one hand, sugar figures in the other, and carrying candied haws.","By the time Si Nian noticed, the two kids had already eaten until their mouths were shiny and sticky.","She couldn't help but laugh, \"Eating so much sugar again, be careful of toothaches.\"","With a mouth full of sugar stains, Second Child said unconvincingly, \"No, I didn't eat any. I bought all these for my sister.\"","Si Nian pinched his little cheek. \"Your sister can't eat this much either. Alright, I'm confiscating these for now. We'll save them for tomorrow.\"","Zhou Yueshen rubbed his nose and changed the subject, \"It's getting late, let's go inside.\"","Si Nian smiled and nodded, also wanting to go to the examination room first to check out the situation.","Family members were allowed to enter the school grounds, but they couldn't enter the classrooms.","The seating arrangement was based on the previous year's exam scores. Since Si Nian had no previous scores, she was placed at the very back.","Her examination room was also in the last classroom, Class 10.","That meant everyone assigned here was either a poor student or a repeater.","They were from all sorts of schools.","By the time they went over, there were already many people there.","Both parents and teachers were present.","So Si Nian's family of several people didn't stand out.","However, just as the group stood still, they bumped into some acquaintances.","It was actually the Si family and Lin Sisi!","Si Nian was speechless. To run into them here of all places—it really was a small world for enemies.","Lin Sisi had obviously seen their family too. Seeing Zhou Yueshen and the kids following Si Nian, she almost couldn't recognize the children, who had changed so much after not seeing them for a year.","Her smile paused, and she stepped forward to greet her.","But soon, her gaze was drawn to something else.","Lin Sisi ran over with a look of pleasant surprise. \"Fu Yang, what are you doing here!\""]},{"number":377,"title":"Chapter 377: Cannon Fodder","paragraphs":["Everyone turned around in surprise to look.","Ever since the incident at the Northwest Military Region, Fu Yang had not appeared in the public eye for a long time.","Even Si Nian couldn't help but take an extra glance at him.","Fu Yang was followed by quite a few people.","In the novel, when the female lead took the college entrance examination, the male lead had guarded her closely.","He accompanied the female lead to take the exam, and when she was framed for cheating, he was the first to stand up and believe in her. In the end, the female lead's innocence was proven, and she was admitted to a top university in absolute glory.","That's right, as the great female protagonist, how could Lin Sisi possibly take the exam so smoothly?","The female lead was set up to be envied wherever she went, only to ruthlessly slap their faces in the end.","However, with the male lead's backing, none of that was a problem for her.","Only in this lifetime, Fu Yang and Lin Sisi didn't seem to be madly in love like they were in the novel.","She didn't expect Fu Yang to actually come in person. Was this the special treatment of a female protagonist?","Fu Yang seemed to feel her gaze. He ignored Lin Sisi and looked over at her instead.","Today, Si Nian was dressed very youthfully, with her hair in braids and carrying a satchel.","For a moment, it made him feel as if he were dreaming of the past, back when Si Nian was still in school. She used to dress just like this, young and playful.","She was always followed by many boys trying to please her, yet her eyes only ever had him.","She never made plans to hang out after school like others did, but sacrificed all her time for him.","Sometimes, she wouldn't even have time to change her clothes before rushing to bring him food.","Everyone said that no one was better at pleasing people than her.","At the time, Fu Yang only found her clingy and troublesome.","But now, seeing her standing so prettily in front of another man, his heart ached as if it had been pierced.","However, at this moment, she was also looking at him, but her gaze had long lost its initial adoration and worship.","All that remained was... the look of someone watching a good piece of gossip unfold.","Fu Yang's face darkened.","He retracted his gaze and ignored Lin Sisi, because he hadn't come to see Lin Sisi at all.","However, Lin Sisi was still talking to herself: I thought you were very busy and wouldn't have time to come, so I didn't dare to bother you.","She blushed and said, My college entrance exam isn't a very important matter. You don't need to worry about me.","As soon as she said this, everyone couldn't help but shift their confused gazes toward Fu Yang.","They had been saying that the patrol here wasn't originally assigned to Commander Fu, but he had taken it upon himself.","So it was for this girl?","However, before they could envy her and think too much, Fu Qianqian, who was standing to the side, rolled her eyes.","My brother is here to carry out a mission, okay? What does it have to do with you? Stop flattering yourself.","After saying that, she ignored Lin Sisi's instantly pale face and walked toward Si Nian. What a coincidence, Si Nian. Today my brother came over to patrol for a mission, and I was bored so I tagged along to look around. I didn't expect to run into you here. Oh right, you're here for the college entrance exam. Isn't that a coincidence?","Si Nian gave a fake smile. It is quite a coincidence.","She clearly wanted to come herself, yet deliberately pushed the excuse onto her brother.","Was it so hard to tell the truth?","Fu Qianqian thought she really hadn't seen through it and smiled smugly, Since we ran into each other, for the sake of how long we've known each other, I'll cheer you on before I leave. Who told me to be so nostalgic?","Si Nian rolled her eyes. Yes, yes, yes, you are the most nostalgic.","Fu Qianqian glanced again at Lin Sisi, who was trying to curry favor with her older brother, and muttered in a low voice, Don't you dare score lower than her, or don't blame me for laughing at you!","Si Nian also glanced at the group and withdrew her gaze. You never know.","After all, Lin Sisi looked very confident.","In the novel, her exam results were considered extremely good.","At least for someone from a rural village, it was a score that could amaze everyone.","In the novel, she used this very college entrance exam to turn her life around and completely solidify her status in the family courtyard.","Si Nian didn't really care how well she scored, but the two of them coincidentally ended up in the same exam room, which inevitably made her a bit worried that some accident might happen.","After all, the cannon fodder around the female lead always suffered the most miserable fates.","However, before she could think about it further, everyone started entering the classrooms to wait for the exam.","Si Nian felt someone pat her shoulder. She turned around to see Zhou Yueshen looking down at her.","Although he didn't speak, silence spoke volumes at this moment.","Perhaps Fu Qianqian's words just now made him worry that she would overthink things.","Si Nian gave him a reassuring look, followed her classmates into the exam room, found her seat, and sat down.","Lin Sisi was still thinking how nice it would be if Fu Yang could accompany her during the exam. However, Fu Yang didn't speak to her at all; he spent the whole time talking to the people behind him.","And then he left.","But Lin Sisi thought that Fu Yang still had her in his heart. Otherwise, why would a minor task like patrolling require him, Commander Fu, to personally step in?","Lin Sisi felt a sweet joy in her heart. She gazed reluctantly in the direction Fu Yang had left until someone nearby called out to her.","Lin Sisi looked back; it was a classmate from her class.","The classmate looked at her enviously and asked, Sisi, who was that?","She had seen it all: the man in military uniform, followed by so many people. Just from his aura, she knew he was no ordinary person.","Lin Sisi felt proud, but she couldn't well say that she was already married, so she had to say, That's my fiancé.","The other girl was astonished, and her gaze became even more envious. Yet, beneath that envy, there was a trace of jealousy that Lin Sisi failed to notice.","The group entered the exam room.","Lin Sisi spotted Si Nian at a glance.","Not only her, but many people were secretly turning their heads to peek at her.","It was truly because, among a crowd of drab and nervous people, her demeanor appeared far too bright and relaxed.","Coupled with her exquisitely beautiful face, it was hard not to stare.","Lin Sisi also loved beauty, but her hair was gone, and wearing a hat right now, she really couldn't be called pretty.","Seeing Si Nian looking so beautiful left a very sour taste in her mouth.","The first round of the exam soon began.","Everyone buried their heads in writing; some looked relaxed, while others looked distressed.","This time, Si Nian wasn't as casual as when she went for the preliminary tests.","The college entrance exam was very important, and absolutely nothing could go wrong.","She also couldn't be too high-profile, lest she be targeted.","Therefore, after finishing, she checked her work repeatedly and only handed in her paper after others started doing so.","Seeing that Si Nian actually handed in her paper after her, Lin Sisi's previously anxious heart suddenly relaxed.","Both she and Si Nian had attended high school, and she had even taken the college entrance exam once before, so relatively speaking, she was more experienced than Si Nian.","Although everyone praised Si Nian for being smart, she herself was reborn. How could she possibly lose to an eighteen or nineteen-year-old girl?","Thinking of this, her mind eased considerably.","When she went out, Si's Father and Si's Mother were very happy to see her come out first and asked her how she did on the exam.","Lin Sisi said modestly, It was alright, but there shouldn't be any problems.","Hearing her say this, Si's Father and Si's Mother both breathed a sigh of relief.","Fu Qianqian was dissatisfied with Lin Sisi's pretentious manner. Seeing that Si Nian actually came out after her, she was very unhappy.","\"Hey, Si Nian, why did you just come out? Is it that hard? The spotlight has all been stolen by Si Sisi!\"","She looked disappointed, wishing Si Nian had done better.","After all, in Fu Qianqian's eyes, she couldn't compare to Si Nian. But since she looked down on Lin Sisi, Lin Sisi was definitely worse than herself, and thus even less comparable to Si Nian.","But she didn't expect Si Nian to come out later.","Si Nian smiled and said, \"It's my first time taking the college entrance examination. Of course I'm nervous.\"","Hearing this, Lin Sisi looked over at her and said worriedly, \"Is Sister Si Nian alright? I thought she had finished writing a long time ago. I didn't expect her to come out after me.\"","Si's Father and Si's Mother then remembered that their adopted daughter was still standing nearby. Hearing their daughter say this, they felt a bit smug but couldn't show it. Instead, it reminded them to step forward and ask Si Nian how she did on the exam.","Si Nian replied, \"Not bad.\"","\"Not bad\" meant she didn't do well.","After all, if the old Si Nian had done well, she wouldn't be this modest.","The couple felt even happier in their hearts.","Looking at it this way, Si Nian definitely couldn't compare to their daughter.","True, although she had good grades before, she hadn't taken the college entrance examination. Over the past year, she had been taking care of children all day and working as a teacher; where would she find the time to study?","Unlike Sisi, who insisted on reading every day even while in prison.","It was really too hot at noon. Worried that Si Nian might get heatstroke, Zhou Yueshen went back to bring her some mung bean soup.","Fu Qianqian shamelessly shared some of the ice-cold mung bean soup and didn't even want to leave.","After downing a bowl of mung bean soup, Si Nian sighed in refreshing satisfaction.","The children, having waited all morning, hugged their bowls and drank two large bowls in a row.","Right after drinking, they clamored to go to the bathroom.","Zhou Yueshen took them to the bathroom. Shortly after, Yaoyao wanted to take a nap, so Zhou Yueshen found a grassy spot with thick shade and laid down his jacket for her to sleep on.","Si Nian couldn't bear to see them keeping watch over her and wanted them to go back and rest. However, seeing the man looking at her with a face full of concern, she couldn't bring herself to say a word.","Soon, the math exam began.","The students entered the classroom sweating profusely.","It was the height of summer. The morning was fine, but the afternoon was so hot that the smell of sweat was everywhere.","Si Nian could clearly feel people's irritable states.","The sticky air, the damp palms gripping the pens.","This midsummer was not that beautiful after all.","The bell signaling the start of the exam rang amidst the sweltering heat. The teachers walked in, holding exam papers in their arms and gripping fans in their hands.","They began to distribute the test papers one by one.","Like most people, Si Nian flipped through the paper back and forth first.","This year's college entrance examination was much harder than last year's.","Especially the math section; it was incredibly obvious.","Si Nian lowered her head and earnestly began to write. However, not long after, someone suddenly cried out in alarm. It turned out someone had fainted from heatstroke because it was too hot.","Everyone was startled, and the teachers hurriedly went to check on the student's condition.","This was a prime opportunity to cheat.","Si Nian subconsciously glanced around and could see quite a few people passing notes to each other.","She gasped. There were no surveillance cameras in this era; these students were truly bold.","But she didn't want to meddle in other people's business. After all, asking for trouble like this wouldn't bring her any benefits.","She could only pretend not to see it for the sake of her own peace of mind.","However, at this moment, our kind-hearted female lead stood up.","She loudly and righteously accused, \"How can you do this? What you are doing is wrong!\"","These words startled everyone, making their scalps tingle with fear.","Coincidentally, at this time, someone had gone to notify the patrolling staff that a student had fainted.","Fu Yang led some people over.","And witnessed this scene.","Si Nian: ...Is the exam room also part of your roleplay?","Can't we have some normal plotlines?","The teacher asked, \"Student, what is going on?\"","Lin Sisi said with a deeply pained expression, \"Teacher, just now, several students took advantage of this student fainting to secretly pass notes. I don't understand why these people would do this. Is this fair to those of us who work hard?\"","The teacher was quite shocked and then angrily said, \"Who was it? Take them out! If you take them out now, I can still give you a chance. If we find out ourselves, you will lose the opportunity to take the college entrance examination altogether! Is this how you trample on your own lives?\"","Everyone was terrified. Some timid ones immediately stood up, crying and saying they knew they were wrong.","However, this was no ordinary exam; cheating meant disqualification.","The offender was immediately taken away.","There was simply no second chance.","Those who had been considering confessing suddenly wouldn't dare admit it even if it cost them their lives.","Some teachers began to conduct random checks, and the atmosphere in the entire exam room became incredibly eerie and tense.","Fu Yang carried the fainted girl away. Nothing else was found, and everyone resumed the exam.","However, because of Lin Sisi's outburst just now, no one dared to cheat anymore. The teachers also became extremely strict, and the exam atmosphere was highly stressful.","Many people cried as they walked out after the exam, saying they hadn't performed well.","The next day's English exam was Si Nian's strong suit, but it was a weakness for most people present, including Lin Sisi.","Lin Sisi also knew about Si Nian working as a teacher, so she looked at Si Nian a lot more today.","She could be confident in other subjects, but not in English.","Previously, during a school speech, Lin Sisi had realized that the gap between her English and Si Nian's was not just a little bit.","Plus, since Si Nian was a teacher, Lin Sisi was even less of a match for her.","If Si Nian did well on the English exam, it would be extremely disadvantageous for her.","Lin Sisi watched Si Nian walk in, her hands tightening.","At this moment, however, she didn't notice the cold gaze behind her.","Soon, the exam began.","It started with the listening comprehension, which was extremely difficult for many people.","Everyone held their breath and listened carefully.","But for Si Nian, it was easier than eating a meal.","Lin Sisi watched her writing rapidly, and her heart tightened.","Just in that moment of distraction, the listening audio actually finished.","She hadn't heard clearly what was said at all, and now she didn't know what to write.","Inevitably, she left several questions blank.","However, at this moment, someone threw a note at Lin Sisi's feet.","A situation similar to yesterday's happened once again.","Someone raised their hand and said, \"Teacher, someone is cheating!\"","The teachers all looked in her direction.","Their faces were very grim.","Someone cheated yesterday, and now someone was cheating again today. These students were far too audacious.","They saw her pointing at the note at Lin Sisi's feet and saying, \"Teacher, I saw someone throw a note to her.\"","Lin Sisi hadn't yet realized that they were talking about her. She subconsciously turned her head and saw the person pointing at her.","And this person was actually her classmate.","She was instantly shocked.","Si Nian also turned her head to take a look. Her seat was slightly in front of Lin Sisi's, so she witnessed this scene.","Had the plot from the novel where the female lead gets framed arrived?","However, before she could enjoy the show, the person pointed at her and said, \"She was the one who passed it to Lin Sisi! I saw it with my own eyes!\"","Si Nian: \"?\""]},{"number":378,"title":"Chapter 378: Clarification (Revised and Expanded)","paragraphs":["Let alone her, even Lin Sisi herself was completely bewildered.","\"Wang Manqing, what, what are you saying?\" Lin Sisi asked blankly.","Lin Sisi had focused all her attention on Si Nian and hadn't noticed at all that someone was targeting her.","Let alone someone from her own class.","They had clearly just greeted each other yesterday.","The classmate named Wang Manqing sneered, \"Lin Sisi, stop acting so high and mighty. I saw it all. Before we even entered the classroom, you two were making eyes at each other. I knew you were going to cheat because your English has always been poor.\"","Si Nian: \"?\" When did she ever make eyes at Lin Sisi?","Although she noticed Lin Sisi frequently stealing glances at her today, it definitely didn't look like they were making eyes at each other, right?","The teacher picked up the piece of paper, opened it, and sure enough, it was a cheat sheet with answers written on it.","Her face instantly darkened.","Lin Sisi, who was just righteously condemning cheating students yesterday—the brave girl they had admired so much—was actually cheating today?","Wasn't this a joke?","The invigilator's face turned pale and green, looking terrible as she questioned, \"You two, what is going on here?\"","Lin Sisi hurriedly said, \"No, it's not like that. I really didn't cheat. Teacher, you have to believe me.\"","The teacher frowned, pulled her test paper over for a look, and as expected, many of Lin Sisi's listening comprehension questions were left blank.","And the answers on the paper in her hand were clearly the multiple-choice answers for the listening section that had just finished.","She then walked over to Si Nian's desk, flipped open her test paper, and saw that the listening questions were all completely filled out.","The teacher's face turned livid. \"How do you explain this!\"","The other students cast gloating looks at Lin Sisi.","The person who had snitched yesterday was caught cheating today. It served her right.","At this moment, Fu Yang and his group were passing by the classroom door.","The group noticed the commotion inside and frowned.","A student had fainted from heatstroke in this classroom yesterday, so they all took an extra look.","What happened today?","Fu Yang stopped in his tracks, just in time to hear the teacher's questioning.","\"Teacher, I really didn't cheat. I'm not that kind of person. Although we know each other, Si Nian is from No. 2 High School, and I'm from No. 1 High School. We don't interact normally.\"","Behind her, Wang Manqing sneered, \"Teacher, I have proof. I heard that the girl from No. 2 High School is the adopted daughter of Lin Sisi's parents. I don't need to explain their relationship, do I? Plus, I saw that girl talking to Lin Sisi at our school gate before. The two of them were probably preparing for today's cheating. I heard she even went to prison before, and now she's finding someone to help her cheat. She is simply too audacious!\"","Lin Sisi immediately glared at her. She hadn't expected Wang Manqing to be so hypocritical. She had seen her interacting with Si Nian long ago and purposely waited until now to frame her!","Lin Sisi didn't even know when she had offended this person, but she quickly remembered: because she had transferred in late, her parents had secretly slipped money to the teacher to give her private tutoring.","Therefore, the teacher usually took extra care of her.","Wang Manqing wasn't a repeating student, but rumor had it she was held back a year. Because of this, the homeroom teacher never had a good attitude toward her.","They were both latecomers, but the homeroom teacher treated them differently. So, while Wang Manqing appeared friendly on the surface, she had secretly hated her for a long time.","Was that why she wanted to frame her at this critical moment?","Lin Sisi was furious.","She hadn't expected that, even after being reborn for a second life, she would still be framed by such a low-level trick.","And it just so happened she hadn't written down the answers to those specific questions, causing the teacher to misunderstand.","Everyone else hadn't expected this situation either, looking at the two with sighs of disbelief.","The teacher also frowned and looked at Si Nian: \"Is what she said true? Are you her parents' adopted daughter?\"","If that were really the case, then the two of them collaborating to cheat would make sense.","Si Nian nodded: \"That's right, I am indeed the adopted daughter.\"","The crowd burst into an uproar.","\"But do you think I would help an enemy cheat?\"","\"An enemy?\" The teacher said in a deep voice. \"What do you mean?\"","\"Lin Sisi once stole three thousand yuan from my family, harmed my entire family, and forced me into marriage. Teacher, do you think I would help someone who ruined my life cheat?\"","\"Of course, I haven't done anything nice either. The reason Lin Sisi went to prison, as that classmate mentioned, was because I sent her there. She must hate my guts. How could she possibly ask me to help her cheat? This classmate should really understand our situation better before framing someone.\"","The crowd was completely stunned.","Lin Sisi's face flushed bright red.","Although these words could prove their innocence in this matter, her reputation was also ruined.","Wang Manqing was also shocked. She had only accidentally overheard the homeroom teacher complaining, which was how she knew about this.","But she never expected the situation to be like this.","However, she quickly reacted and said, \"Could what I saw with my own eyes be fake? If you weren't helping her cheat, could... could it be that you were intentionally trying to harm her?\"","Lin Sisi's eyes flickered as if she thought of something, and she immediately put on a shocked expression as she looked at Si Nian.","As if it really was Si Nian who had framed her.","She actually stayed silent.","Si Nian was amused by the absurdity. It was one thing for the person framing Lin Sisi to drag her down with them, but now they wanted to turn around and bite her instead?","She had also roughly guessed what trick the other party was using.","\"Since you put it that way, I'm going to have to take this seriously.\"","The teacher said, \"What do you have to say?\"","Si Nian looked at the teacher and said, \"Teacher, since the other party is so certain that I helped Lin Sisi cheat, then this cheat sheet must be filled with the answers to these questions. Everyone just started; we've only done the listening and fill-in-the-blank questions. They are all multiple-choice options, so handwriting might be hard to distinguish. But I don't believe that anyone besides me could get all these questions right.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, everyone cast astonished glances at her.","Wang Manqing looked disdainful. \"Anyone can talk big.\"","Si Nian ignored her and continued, \"I don't want to waste time. Teacher, please compare my test paper and this classmate's test paper with the answers written on the cheat sheet.\"","\"If there are blank questions, please check if she left them blank too. If there are incorrect answers, please check her test paper to see if her mistakes are exactly the same.\"","Hearing this, Wang Manqing's face instantly went pale.","She truly couldn't be sure that all her answers were correct.","Although her English wasn't terrible, it was definitely not top-tier. When she looked over the questions, she was confused by many of them.","That was why she figured Lin Sisi definitely wouldn't know them either.","Because they had joined the class at the same time, and Lin Sisi was clearly in a similar situation to her, yet the teacher treated Lin Sisi very well.","Meanwhile, the teacher always gave her looks of disdain and clear disgust.","The teacher even said that if it hadn't been for her parents kneeling and begging for pity, she wouldn't have been allowed to stay in their class.","She originally didn't quite understand why.","Until yesterday, when she saw Lin Sisi's parents driving a car to drop her off for the exam, along with her military officer fiancé who clearly had a high status.","She finally understood why Lin Sisi received special treatment while she didn't.","While Wang Manqing was in a daze, the teacher had already begun comparing the cheat sheet with Si Nian's exam paper.","Soon, the teacher frowned and cast a glance at Wang Manqing.","Then, she walked toward her.","Wang Manqing's breath hitched, her heart leaping into her throat.","After comparing them, the teacher understood everything.","This was entirely a scheme directed and acted out by this student to frame others.","She slammed her hand on the desk with a loud smack. \"Student, what do you have to say for yourself? The answers on this cheat sheet are exactly the same as yours, even the mistakes are identical!\"","Wang Manqing opened her mouth but couldn't utter a word.","Seeing this, what else could the others not understand?","She had thrown the cheat sheet at Lin Sisi's feet herself to frame her, and even tried to drag Si Nian down to be her scapegoat.","What a scheme to kill two birds with one stone.","It was simply too vicious.","The teacher was livid, her face turning pale with anger. \"Get out! Your qualification for the college entrance examination is revoked!\"","All the color drained from Wang Manqing's face, and she nearly fainted.","Seeing Si Nian looking at her coldly, Wang Manqing's lips trembled as she muttered to herself, \"No, it's impossible. Am I the only one at fault here? She just said she got all the questions right, how is that possible? Everyone knows that those of us sorted into this last group are the worst-performing repeating students. Even the top students wouldn't dare guarantee they made zero mistakes. For her to be so certain, she must have cheated too!\"","Seeing her acting like a cornered dog, the teacher grew even more furious, grabbing her and demanding she leave immediately.","However, everyone's suspicious gazes fell on Si Nian. It was true; although what Wang Manqing did was wrong, her last words weren't entirely unreasonable.","How could this person be so sure she got everything right?","Wasn't that a bit too arrogant?","The teacher who had just looked at Si Nian's paper also frowned, but there was no evidence.","She hated cheaters with a passion, so she didn't have a pleasant expression right now.","She stepped forward, reaching to take Si Nian's pen and stationery.","\"Teacher, what are you doing?\" Si Nian frowned.","\"I'm checking. Although you proved your innocence, the behavior of all three of you is highly suspicious.\"","The teacher said with a fierce glare.","Si Nian took a deep breath, suppressing her anger.","At that moment, someone spoke from the doorway, \"She didn't cheat.\"","The teacher turned around in astonishment to see a man holding a pale Wang Manqing with one hand, calmly stating, \"I can prove it.\"","Everyone exchanged glances. Fu Yang's attire made him someone they truly didn't dare underestimate.","They had all heard that to maintain the safety of the students and ensure the smooth progression of the college entrance exams, the school had specially hired guards for twenty-four-hour patrols to prevent any incidents.","Yesterday, several students had accidents, and it was these men who promptly sent them to the hospital.","The captain leading them was even a regimental commander from the military district.","Such a grand display wasn't something you saw every day.","Even the teachers couldn't help but take a few extra glances.","They became much more polite: \"Captain Fu, how can you be so sure? Did you see it just now?\"","Fu Yang glanced at Si Nian, then withdrew his gaze and said, \"Whether I saw it or not, it's impossible for her to cheat.\"","The teacher was stunned: \"B-but her behavior is truly suspicious. We can't let off any student who dares to cheat during the college entrance exam; that wouldn't be fair to everyone else.\"","Too lazy to say more, Fu Yang stated, \"She used to be the English teacher for the genius class at the Foreign Language Primary School. I'm not the only one who knows this; Lin Sisi knows it too. Although I don't know why she didn't speak up, if you don't believe me, you can look into it yourselves.\"","As soon as these words came out, everyone was dumbfounded.","\"A teacher at the Foreign Language Primary School?\"","\"How is that possible?\"","Everyone subconsciously turned back to look at Si Nian.","Everyone knew about the Foreign Language Primary School because it was the only one in the city center.","And the genius class at that! Rumor had it that the teachers for the genius class were personally recruited by the principal at a high price, and the head teachers were all at the professor level.","When this class was first established, it garnered a lot of attention.","But no one had ever connected it to this young woman sitting in the college entrance exam classroom.","However, considering the man's identity, it was impossible for him to lie to them.","Everyone couldn't help but look at Lin Sisi.","Lin Sisi never expected that Fu Yang coming over wasn't to speak up for her, but for Si Nian.","Her mind was buzzing right now.","Her face looked utterly awful.","Not only did Fu Yang speak up for Si Nian, but he also questioned why she hadn't spoken up for Si Nian.","Lin Sisi's face was deathly pale.","Seeing everyone looking at her suspiciously, she finally stammered, \"Y-yes, that's what I heard my parents say. I was too nervous just now and completely forgot about it.\"","Fu Yang cast a meaningful glance at her without saying a word, and walked away, dragging along Wang Manqing, who had framed them.","The examination room fell into a deathly silence.","The teacher who had just been clamoring to investigate Si Nian was left speechless.","Si Nian hadn't expected Fu Yang to speak up for her either, but she didn't mind. She simply opened her pencil case and draft notebook, generously letting the teacher inspect them.","Then, she went back to her writing.","This kind of thing was a complete waste of time for her.","Fortunately, she had a good mindset. Although she had been framed, she wasn't so panicked that she couldn't continue writing.","Lin Sisi's condition, on the other hand, was very poor.","Fu Yang's appearance had completely disrupted her train of thought.","She was completely out of it.","Since her cover was blown, Si Nian stopped pretending.","Once she finished writing and checking, she handed in her paper the moment the teacher said they could.","Everyone watched her walk out with dumbfounded expressions.","With such a big commotion, Zhou Yueshen and the others outside naturally found out about it.","However, they weren't on duty, so they couldn't get close.","Seeing Si Nian come out so quickly, he knew she had this subject in the bag.","After all, English was Si Nian's strongest subject.","As for Lin Sisi, she came out right at the very end of the allotted time.","She hadn't even finished writing.","Today Father Fu didn't come; only Zhang Cuimei was there.","Seeing that Lin Sisi hadn't come out, she had been anxious the whole time.","Once she finally came out, Zhang Cuimei hurried forward and said, \"Sisi, what happened just now? What's going on? Why are you only coming out now?\"","When she saw a girl being led out by Fu Yang and the others earlier, Zhang Cuimei's face had turned pale.","She was very worried that something had happened to her daughter.","Seeing that she wasn't speaking, she asked how she did on the exam.","Lin Sisi's mood was beyond terrible. She even suspected that Wang Manqing was someone Si Nian had hired to target her.","Otherwise, why did Si Nian end up with both fame and fortune, while she was the one being mocked and ridiculed?","Just as she was coming out, some candidates were pointing at her and making sarcastic remarks.","As if they were afraid she wouldn't hear them.","They said that Si Nian had helped prove her innocence, yet she hadn't said a word, almost causing Si Nian to be suspected.","They also said she deserved it, that she got her karma today for tattling yesterday.","Lin Sisi was furious.","Seeing Si Nian and the others laughing and talking, she didn't know what came over her, but she covered her face and ran away crying.","Si Nian watched her with a baffled expression.","She was the one who should be crying, right? What was up with that aggrieved look on Lin Sisi's face?","Si Nian couldn't even be bothered to think about it.","Their class had really been in the spotlight these past two days, and there were even more invigilators now.","It was probably reported by someone.","Si Nian didn't care either; she wasn't cheating anyway, so there was nothing to be afraid of.","The three-day exam quickly came to an end. The last few subjects weren't particularly difficult, and Si Nian took them with ease.","When she came out after the exam, Zhou Yueshen and the children were already waiting for her at the gate.","The sun in the west was still shining brightly. Although it was already afternoon, it was still very hot.","The children's hair was all wet.","Second Child was even more exaggerated, his face and nose covered in sweat.","Who knew where he had run off to play.","Seeing her come out, he skipped over to help her carry her bag.","After three days of exams, Si Nian did have some backaches.","At this time, Fu Qianqian appeared out of nowhere and walked up to Si Nian. Looking at her, under Si Nian's puzzled gaze, she said, \"Si Nian, how was it? How many points do you think you can get on this exam?\"","(Yesterday's review couldn't be changed, it was changed today. If it doesn't match, please look back.)"]},{"number":379,"title":"Chapter 379: Did You See Some Beautiful Woman","paragraphs":["Si Nian really hadn't thought about this. She said, \"I don't know either. I'll wait until I go to school tomorrow to estimate my score.\"","Now that the exams were over, she could go back to school to estimate her score. There was no rush.","Once she had a rough idea of her score, she could fill out her college applications.","Fu Qianqian was already getting impatient, even more nervous than if she were taking the exam herself.","She took a deep breath and said, \"It's fine, it's fine, don't be nervous. Even if you didn't do well, I won't laugh at you. Let's go eat first and relax.\"","She regretted saying the other day that she would laugh at Si Nian if she did poorly. It had just made her nervous.","In the past, if Si Nian felt confident, she would proudly declare after the exam that she definitely scored high.","But now she didn't even know, which meant it must have been very difficult, leaving her uncertain.","Si Nian watched her fan herself with one hand while trying to comfort her.","She thought to herself, You're the one who is nervous, aren't you?","Zhou Yueshen didn't ask much about the exam. After listening to the two of them talk,","he finally said, \"I'll go get the car first, and we'll go to a restaurant to eat.\"","Si Nian smiled and nodded. Second Child took the initiative to hold her hand and said, \"Mom, it's okay. Even if you don't get into college, it doesn't matter, because I won't get in either.\"","Si Nian laughed, \"Alright, stop cursing me.\"","After she spoke, Zhou Yueshen drove the car over.","Just as the group was about to leave, a few teachers came running over, their footsteps thudding.","\"Wait, wait, Student Si.\"","Si Nian turned her head and saw that they were teachers from No. 2 High School.","The teachers were sweating profusely from running, but they looked delighted.","\"Student Si, how did you do on the exam? Are you confident? Which school are you planning to go to?\"","Si Nian turned around and said, \"I think there shouldn't be any problems. As for the exact score, I'll tell you which school I'm aiming for when I come to school tomorrow to estimate my points.\"","\"Right, right, right, no rush. We'll talk about it tomorrow after the test papers are released and you estimate your score.\"","\"This year's college entrance examination was a bit difficult, but don't worry, with your abilities, there definitely won't be any problems.\"","The teachers made up their minds to go to the classroom early tomorrow when the students were estimating their scores, to help Si Nian see how many points she could get.","Hearing Si Nian's words, Fu Qianqian's nervous heart finally relaxed.","She knew Si Nian was a very proud person with strong self-esteem.","If she failed to get into college again this year, the blow to her would definitely be devastating.","Moreover, now there was Lin Sisi. If Lin Sisi got into college and she didn't, Fu Qianqian couldn't even imagine what the people in the family compound would say about Si Nian in the future.","Her face returned to a beaming smile. She gently nudged the teachers aside, linked arms with Si Nian, and said, \"Let's go, let's go, we're going to have a big feast to celebrate. We'll eat Yu Dong into bankruptcy!\"","The weather was too hot, and Si Nian didn't have much of an appetite, but seeing everyone so happy, she didn't want to be a wet blanket.","She nodded.","The teachers also said their goodbyes and left; they still had a ton of things to busy themselves with.","Si Nian opened the passenger door, only to see a bouquet of bright red roses resting on the seat.","Her eyes widened in surprise.","She subconsciously looked toward the man in the driver's seat.","Zhou Yueshen actually wasn't looking at her. His large hands gripped the steering wheel, and he sat up straight, though upon closer inspection, he looked a bit stiff.","Seeming to sense Si Nian's gaze on him, Zhou Yueshen had to tilt his head to look at her. He made a fist, coughed softly, and said in a low voice, \"I bought these flowers for you. I didn't know what kind of flowers you liked, so I bought red roses.\"","Si Nian saw his unnatural expression and shifting gaze. She figured the older man was feeling shy about giving flowers for the first time.","She couldn't hold back a laugh and got into the car, holding the flowers.","Lately, this man was understanding romance more and more.","Even though she knew Yu Dong had probably taught him, Si Nian was still happy.","Fu Qianqian sat in the back holding Yaoyao. Seeing the flowers, she exaggeratedly said, \"Wow, I'm so jealous. In the past, you were always the one giving flowers to others. I never thought there'd come a day when you'd receive them. The tables have truly turned.\"","Si Nian was speechless. Alright, if you don't know how to speak, just don't speak.","Zhou Yueshen tilted his head and glanced at her.","Fu Qianqian realized she had said the wrong thing and hurriedly made a zipping motion over her mouth, signaling that she knew she was wrong.","Yu Dong's restaurant could be described as magnificent; at first glance, it was clearly a place only the wealthy could afford to eat at.","The dishes prepared were also very sumptuous, but Si Nian had eaten all sorts of delicacies before, and combined with her lack of appetite, she didn't eat much.","By the time they finished eating and headed back, it was already dark. The children fell asleep leaning against the car seats, and Si Nian was yawning repeatedly, incredibly sleepy.","Once home, she fell asleep the moment her head hit the bed, not even having time to wash her face.","Although it seemed like she hadn't done much during the exams, the mental toll was immense.","In the time it took Zhou Yueshen to go in and run hot water for her, she had already fallen asleep by the time he came out.","Si Nian slept very soundly. With the relaxation that came after the exams ended, even her dreams were sweet.","Previously, worried she might forget the time for the college entrance exams, she had specifically set an alarm. However, she forgot to turn it off when she got back last night. It rang bright and early the next morning. The large hand resting on her waist moved away, grabbed the alarm clock nearby, and directly pressed it off.","Then, the arm wrapped around her waist once more.","Si Nian woke up instantly. Because of the exams over the past few days, her nerves were still a bit tense, and hearing the alarm made her wake up reflexively.","She opened her eyes and looked at the alarm clock by the bed; the time read eight-ten.","She was startled—it took half an hour to get there from here.","She subconsciously tried to get up.","But the large hand on her waist pressed her down, and she lay back again.","Her hand was still held by the man, his palm exceptionally hot.","Si Nian suddenly remembered that her college entrance exams were already over.","She was really sleep-addled.","She didn't even know when she had fallen asleep last night; she had been thinking about having the man wake her up to take a bath.","She definitely hadn't taken a bath, yet she was currently wearing pajamas.","She vaguely remembered someone wiping her face with a towel, her forehead occasionally brushing against the man's firm, cold jaw.","When she groggily opened her eyes, she was met with the man's familiar face.","\"Are you still sleepy? Do you want to go in the afternoon instead?\" Zhou Yueshen's deep voice sounded.","Si Nian shook her head. Although she really wanted to sleep a bit more, she had to go to school today to estimate her score.","She heard yesterday that the karaoke bars in the city hadn't closed all night and were packed with customers.","Many students went to let loose after finishing their exams.","Only Si Nian had absolutely no desire to get out of bed.","The children had classes today, so Zhou Yueshen dropped them off at school first before taking Si Nian to her school.","By the time she arrived at her classroom, almost all of her classmates were already there.","There was also a crowd of parents outside.","Everyone was huddled together in groups, checking their answers against each other.","Si Nian didn't recognize a single person. It couldn't be helped; although she had been enrolled at the school for a long time, this was her first time actually coming to the classroom.","And no one recognized her, either.","However, quite a few people cast their gazes upon her.","There were even a few boys nudging each other, gesturing to look at her.","When the homeroom teacher saw Si Nian arrive, he immediately stepped forward and said, \"Student Si Nian, you're here! Come quickly and check your answers to see how much you might score.\"","Based on Si Nian's previous test papers, if nothing went wrong in the college entrance examination, she would definitely be this year's biggest dark horse.","It was even possible that she could make No. 2 High School soar to new heights.","If they could produce a top scorer in the college entrance exam, all their hard work would finally pay off.","It would infuriate those arrogant snobs at First High School, letting them know what a great prospect they had lost.","The homeroom teacher pinned all his hopes on Si Nian. Disregarding the other students for the moment, he hurriedly pulled her aside to estimate her score.","Zhou Yueshen didn't follow her inside because the classroom was too crowded.","He was already tall and burly, taking up the space of two people; going in would only take up room.","Watching the students alternate between pleasant surprise and utter dismay, he couldn't help but frown.","He wondered how Si Nian's results were.","Her goal was Beijing University. In previous years, the number of college students from the city center who made it to Beijing University was extremely small.","Although he always knew Si Nian was excellent, he couldn't help but feel a little worried at this moment.","A few boys were secretly sizing him up.","Zhou Yueshen noticed their gazes and swept a glance over them.","As the group walked over, Zhou Yueshen's brow furrowed slightly. He stepped back a bit to make room.","Unexpectedly, the boys stopped right in front of him, looking for all the world like sons-in-law meeting their father-in-law.","Zhou Yueshen's brow remained furrowed. Once he confirmed they were looking for him, he asked in a low voice, \"Can I help you?\"","The boys were fidgeting and blushing slightly, occasionally glancing back at the crowd.","Under Zhou Yueshen's puzzled gaze, the boy pushed to the front finally scratched his head and spoke up: \"Hello, comrade. Could you help us ask your sister out to sing karaoke?\"","Zhou Yueshen was slightly taken aback.","He then replied, \"Sister? You've got the wrong person. I don't have a sister.\"","The boys froze for a moment. Recovering, they quickly asked, \"Isn't she your sister?\"","They looked at each other in dismay and muttered softly, \"Could she be your daughter?\"","Zhou Yueshen looked in the direction they were pointing.","He saw that familiar flash of white by the desk. Once he realized who it was, Zhou Yueshen's face instantly darkened.","Seeing his suddenly gloomy expression, the boys were frightened. Not daring to say another word, they hurriedly said, \"If it's not possible, never mind. Please don't be angry, sir.\"","After saying that, they scurried away with their tails between their legs.","They hadn't expected Student Si's father to be so young, yet have such an intense, terrifying aura.","They were originally too embarrassed to invite Student Si directly. Seeing her family member accompanying her, they had finally mustered the courage to approach him.","Who knew her parent would be even more intimidating than she was.","Zhou Yueshen's expression was truly awful. This was already the second time he had been mistaken for Si Nian's parent.","Si Nian finished estimating her score, deducting points for essays and some major questions where it was easy to lose marks. The total score for the science track in the 1983 college entrance exam was 710, and Si Nian estimated hers to be around 660.","Of course, this was excluding the easily deducted points and the essay.","She would only know the exact number when the results were released.","Hearing her calm voice, the homeroom teacher couldn't even hold his pen steady.","This year's exam was so difficult that their school probably wouldn't even produce two students who scored over six hundred.","Yet Si Nian, even after deducting points for the essay and tricky questions, still had 660 points!","Then the actual score would definitely be higher than this estimate!","\"Student Si, check it again to see if you made any mistakes.\"","Si Nian shook her head and said, \"No need, I have a pretty good idea in my head.\"","In fact, she felt she had basically made no mistakes. After all, she was someone who had already gone to college. She only gave this conservative estimate because she truly wasn't sure about the essay, but she didn't need to worry much about the rest.","Si Nian didn't dare state too high an estimated score, afraid of scaring the homeroom teacher.","She'd leave it at this for now; maybe she could give him a pleasant surprise when the time came.","\"Are you confident about the essay?\" the homeroom teacher asked with concern.","He had heard from the language teacher that essays were Si Nian's weak point.","He was a bit worried.","Si Nian replied, \"I can't say for sure, but it shouldn't be a big problem.\"","Anyway, she had put it out there; she definitely hadn't overestimated her score.","The homeroom teacher said excitedly, \"That's great, that's great. After you fill out your college application forms, go home and get some good rest. Wait for the scores to come out. Who knows, you might bring glory to our school this year.\"","Other students gathered around. \"Teacher, is she the student who is retaking the year?\"","\"What's your name? What's your estimated score?\"","As soon as Si Nian arrived, several teachers surrounded her to estimate her score, acting all shocked and amazed. It was hard for everyone not to notice.","Si Nian smiled. \"Over six hundred.\"","As soon as she spoke, the entire classroom fell into silence.","\"Over six hundred? That's too exaggerated. Aren't you a repeating student?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"I am.\"","\"I heard about it. The homeroom teacher said she transferred from First High School.\"","\"Are the students from First High School really that amazing? I heard they produce several top university students every year.\"","\"If even their repeating students are this incredible, doesn't that mean we're going to lose to First High School again this year?\"","It wasn't that everyone was jealous of her. It was just that after hearing Si Nian's score and remembering she was a repeater from First High School who was still this amazing, they couldn't help but feel a bit defeated.","Si Nian didn't know exactly what level First High School was at, so she didn't say much.","She planned to leave.","But a group of people crowded around her: \"We all heard from the homeroom teacher that due to special circumstances, you couldn't come to school for classes. You must have worked really hard, right?\"","\"Yeah, do you want to go sing karaoke with us later? The homeroom teacher said it's his treat.\"","\"Yeah, yeah! You're so pretty. Do you have a boyfriend?\"","\"Which school are you planning to go to?\"","These girls were in the prime of their youth. Now that they had struck up a conversation with Si Nian, they immediately started chattering away, incredibly excited.","The homeroom teacher pulled out the application forms from who knows where and signaled for everyone to be quiet.","\"Don't aim too high on your applications. After all, the cutoff scores are different every year. Everyone needs to choose carefully. I hope you can all get into your ideal schools.\"","Si Nian received her application form and, with almost no hesitation, filled in Beijing University and Tsinghua University.","She hardly considered any others.","She couldn't help it, because she used to be a student at this very school, only she attended it decades in the future.","Back then, she had barely scraped by to get in, which was a regret not only for her family but for herself as well.","This time, she naturally wanted to enter in a blaze of glory.","It had only been a few years since the college entrance exam was reinstated, and the scoring system was constantly being adjusted.","The cutoff scores were also different every year.","Many scores that would have gotten you in last year wouldn't be enough this year.","Of course, those with high scores certainly didn't need to worry about this issue. After all, for people like them, it wasn't the schools picking them; it was them picking the schools.","While the other students were still racking their brains over which school to choose, Si Nian had already filled out her desired schools and majors.","Zhou Yueshen was still waiting for her outside, so it wouldn't be good for Si Nian to delay here for too long.","Taking advantage of the fact that the homeroom teacher was surrounded by a bunch of students asking various questions and had no time to pay attention to her, Si Nian quickly slipped away.","Anyway, the application forms didn't have to be submitted immediately.","Zhou Yueshen was still standing at the door. He was in the exact same posture when she came out as when she had gone in.","Si Nian waved the application form in her hand at him and said, \"I applied for two schools, take a look.\"","Zhou Yueshen's face was dark and gloomy, but since he usually looked like this, Si Nian didn't notice anything wrong.","Zhou Yueshen took a glance at it. The first choice was Beijing University, and the second was Tsinghua University.","She had filled in the top two universities.","What could he possibly object to?","The two of them squeezed through the crowd and left the school.","It was already past ten o'clock, and the morning was unbearably hot.","Si Nian used her application form to fan herself. Suddenly finding herself with free time, she didn't know what to do for a moment.","So she turned her gaze to Zhou Yueshen beside her. His expression was somewhat strange, for reasons unknown.","Si Nian raised her hand and waved it in front of him before the man snapped back to reality.","Zhou Yueshen was slightly startled.","\"What's wrong?\"","Si Nian pouted and said, \"I was asking what we should do next, and you ignored me.\"","After speaking, she glanced around suspiciously and asked, \"Did you see some pretty girl and get lost in thought?\"","The corners of Zhou Yueshen's lips curled up slightly. \"I was just thinking about something.\"","Si Nian was puzzled. \"About what? Is something wrong at the farm?\"","Zhou Yueshen shook his head slightly and said, \"It's nothing.\"","\"Then are we going home, or...?\"","Zhou Yueshen walked over to where the car was parked, with Si Nian standing by his side. He opened the car door, and Si Nian got in. Zhou Yueshen got into the driver's seat from the other side. After a pause, he asked in a low voice, \"Nian Nian, do you want to go buy some clothes?\""]},{"number":380,"title":"Chapter 380: Shopping (Bug Hunting)","paragraphs":["Si Nian: \"...Huh?\"","\"The weather is getting hot,\" Zhou Yueshen added.","Si Nian paused the hand she was using to fan herself, touched her chin, and said, \"Yeah, it's getting hot. Time to buy new clothes!\"","Sometimes, the excuse to buy clothes is just that simple and unpretentious.","Mainly because Si Nian, being a woman, naturally loved shopping. No matter how many clothes she bought, she always felt like she had nothing to wear.","When Zhou Yueshen suddenly asked if she wanted to buy clothes, she was a bit puzzled.","But when he mentioned the hot weather, Si Nian's brain immediately filled in the blanks with a perfect justification.","Right, the college entrance exams were over, the weather was scorching, and her man was keeping her company. If he didn't buy her something, he would probably feel bad about it.","Si Nian said happily, \"Then let's go buy clothes, and let's get a fan too. It's too hot, Little Han and the others are sweating profusely every day.\"","After saying that, she looked at Zhou Yueshen. He was wearing his usual gray tank top. It was a bit old, and she had no idea what year he had bought it, but it was already fading from being washed so much.","It was hot, and the sun shone on his face, making his bronzed skin gleam.","He looked rough and rugged, but his skin wasn't bad at all. Perhaps due to years of hard work and exercise, his skin was surprisingly firm.","At thirty-one or thirty-two, there were no signs of sagging whatsoever.","It was truly enviable.","But with such thick skin, it was only normal for him to be sturdy and durable.","Si Nian said, \"It's rare for both of us to be free. Let's buy a bit more today.\"","Zhou Yueshen gave a simple \"Mhm.\"","He turned the car key and stepped on the gas pedal, while Si Nian pulled her seatbelt over and buckled it.","They drove all the way to the department store. More and more celebrities had been rising to fame in recent years, and summer was the prime time for marketing, so there were posters plastered outside.","The car pulled into the department store's parking lot. Zhou Yueshen turned off the engine and got out.","Si Nian followed right behind.","Zhou Yueshen subconsciously reached out to hold her hand, but Si Nian, finding it too hot, dodged him.","He was already like a human furnace in the winter, let alone in the summer.","His palms were scorchingly hot.","However, seeing Zhou Yueshen slightly taken aback, Si Nian smiled gently, reached out to hug his arm, and said affectionately, \"Zhou Yueshen, your arm is so cool.\"","After saying that, she rubbed her cheek against the man's arm, which had been cooled by the wind.","The corners of Zhou Yueshen's lips curled up slightly. He withdrew his gaze and let her lean against him as the two walked into the department store together.","After the college entrance exams ended, there were more young people out shopping.","There were also many new summer arrivals.","Sometimes, Si Nian really couldn't understand this era. People in the countryside were incredibly conservative; sometimes just wearing a skirt would invite gossip.","But the city was very fashionable. There was no shortage of short shorts and sexy camisoles.","These people were arguably at the forefront of fashion.","If these clothes were placed decades into the future, they would still be trendy.","Si Nian inherently loved brightly colored clothes. The moment she walked in, she couldn't hold back anymore. Pulling Zhou Yueshen along, she dove straight into a clothing store.","It was just a pity that there was no ocean nearby, so they couldn't go play at the beach.","Otherwise, her old graduation dream had always been to go see the sea.","There was no helping it; as a true southerner, her obsession was the ocean.","For this reason, Si Nian bought quite a few breezy dresses.","With so many people wearing them in the city, she didn't feel embarrassed at all.","It was just that her skin was too fair and her figure too good. When she was trying on clothes, the people around her couldn't tear their eyes away.","Zhou Yueshen's brows were furrowed so tightly they could crush a fly.","But seeing how much she really liked them, he couldn't say much. After all, Si Nian's happiness was the most important thing.","Zhou Yueshen and Si Nian were, after all, not of the same age, and there was a generation gap between them.","The women Zhou Yueshen had seen in the past were all conservative, and he had assumed all women were like that.","But he wouldn't disapprove of Si Nian just because she was different.","So, in the end, he bought everything she liked.","Maybe she would only wear them at home once they bought them?","Thinking like this, Zhou Yueshen's mood improved greatly.","The two walked out carrying bags. As they passed a menswear store, Zhou Yueshen paused for a moment.","But he didn't look at the clothing store; instead, he looked the other way.","Si Nian noticed it right away. She pulled him and said, \"Zhou Yueshen, look, there's a clothing store here. Let's take a look for you too.\"","Zhou Yueshen made a fist, coughed softly, and said in a low voice, \"I don't need to buy anything.\"","Si Nian immediately got anxious. \"What are you talking about? We have to buy something, we definitely have to, okay?\"","Zhou Yueshen said helplessly, \"Okay.\"","As soon as she went in, Si Nian subconsciously started picking things out. But soon she realized that Zhou Yueshen might not like what she liked, so she turned around and asked him, \"Zhou Yueshen, take a look and see if there are any styles you like.\"","Zhou Yueshen looked up and glanced around.","He withdrew his gaze. \"You can choose. Anything is fine with me.\"","Si Nian complained, \"But you hardly ever wore the ones I bought for you before.\"","Zhou Yueshen looked a bit embarrassed. \"They are a bit thick. I'll wear them in the winter.\"","Si Nian thought about it and realized it was true. The clothes she had bought for the man before were all relatively thick jackets.","They weren't convenient for working in, and he would only put them on during holidays or special occasions.","Now that it was summer, her main focus was on casual wear. If she bought him these, he would probably wear them.","She picked out several pieces, handed them to him, and asked, \"How about these?\"","Zhou Yueshen reached out, took them, and took a look. He didn't really understand fashion, because he never wore clothes to look good; it was purely out of necessity.","When Si Nian had bought clothes for him before, he had just let her pick whatever she wanted.","Now, however, he lowered his eyes and examined them seriously.","He also glanced at the people around him. Menswear was relatively expensive, and this ready-to-wear boutique was quite high-end—a place he never would have stepped into in the past.","His rough cotton and linen clothes felt completely out of place here.","Seeing the men coming in and out wearing clothes similar to what Si Nian had chosen for him, he nodded and went to try them on.","Zhou Yueshen was very tall, at least by southern standards. However, he had a great figure. Si Nian also noticed that this man had a long, lean waist; whenever he took off his clothes, she was absolutely mesmerized.","If he wore a dress shirt and suit pants with that ascetic look on his face, he would be unbelievably handsome.","It was just that her older man wore casual clothes so often and found suits restrictive, so Si Nian hadn't bought many for him.","Since it was rare for him to cooperate with her this time, Si Nian quickly picked out several shirts in various colors.","Seeing Zhou Yueshen go inside the fitting room, she smiled mischievously and squeezed in with him, claiming she was going to help him put them on.","The already small fitting room felt even more crowded.","She said she was helping him put on the clothes, but in reality, she secretly copped a few feels.","Zhou Yueshen was a bit uncomfortable, thinking that Si Nian assumed he didn't know how to wear this kind of clothing.","And that was why she had come in to help.","So when her hands reached over, he didn't suspect a thing.","Zhou Yueshen's skin leaned towards a bronze color; from being out in the sun so much, he was quite tanned.","Wearing a pure white shirt made him look even darker.","However, after changing into a gray shirt and a striped shirt, his attractiveness leveled up significantly.","He was so handsome that Si Nian almost got a nosebleed.","She pulled Zhou Yueshen out and said excitedly, \"President Zhou, President Zhou, look at how handsome you are today!\"","Before, he was Factory Manager Zhou, but after putting on the dress shirt and suit pants, Zhou Yueshen transformed into President Zhou.","Zhou Yueshen looked at himself in the mirror and was also slightly stunned.","Hearing Si Nian call Zhou Yueshen \"President Zhou,\" the people around them looked at Zhou Yueshen with entirely different expressions.","Plus, he was already tall and imposing; dressed like this, many people couldn't take their eyes off him.","A nearby staff member handed him some ties and said, \"President Zhou, would you like to try matching these ties?\"","Zhou Yueshen glanced at them.","Before he could speak, Si Nian had already started picking them out and holding them up against him to compare.","After comparing several, a smoky gray suited this man the best.","Si Nian quickly raised her hands and said, \"Come, President Zhou, lower your head.\"","Zhou Yueshen felt a bit helpless at her teasing, but he still obligingly lowered his head to let her tie it for him.","Si Nian stood on her tiptoes and reached out to tug at his collar.","Zhou Yueshen paused, resting his hand against the wall and looking down at her.","Si Nian carefully tied the tie for him. The collar wasn't fully buttoned, perhaps because he wasn't used to it and found the tie too tight.","His Adam's apple was faintly visible.","Si Nian swallowed hard; she finally understood how men felt when looking at beautiful women.","Her slender fingertips.","Twisted and turned.","She quickly finished tying the tie.","Zhou Yueshen could tell she really liked it.","Even though he felt a bit unaccustomed to wearing it.","But Yu Dong was right. Someone with such good taste as Si Nian definitely had a different perspective than him. Since she liked it, it meant this outfit was indeed quite good.","\"President Zhou, why are you looking at me like that? Is it because I'm too beautiful?\"","Seeing him staring at her without looking away, Si Nian hooked a finger around his tie, pulled it down slightly, and smiled, blinking her eyes. \"Want to come to my place tonight?\"","The staff member nearby almost tripped over their own feet.","Zhou Yueshen was amused by her and softly said okay.","Si Nian picked out two suits in different color palettes. Since he didn't wear them often, she didn't buy too many.","When Zhou Yueshen went to pay, she even rushed over to pay for him.","Although they say spending money on a man brings a lifetime of bad luck, love is mutual. He had always been the one giving, and she shouldn't just sit back and enjoy the fruits of his labor.","Zhou Yueshen didn't stop her; after all, Si Nian's little secret stash had accumulated quite a bit.","Of course, he didn't expose her.","After buying the clothes, the two went to pick out some summer clothes for the kids, bought a few fans, and then planned to head home.","With such a pile, the trunk was completely full.","To Si Nian's surprise, Zhou Yueshen didn't drive in the direction of home, but took a detour.","Arriving at the door of a barbershop, he finally spoke, \"Nian Nian, wait a moment, I'm going to get a haircut.\"","Si Nian glanced over, touched the tips of her hair, and said, \"I want to cut mine too, and I want a perm.\"","After saying that, she asked Zhou Yueshen with some uncertainty, \"Do you think I'd look good with curly hair?\"","Zhou Yueshen thought for a moment. Her usual straight hair made her look quite pure and innocent, while occasionally tying it up with some curls and wearing her pajamas made her look very sexy and charming.","He hesitated a bit.","But then he heard Si Nian say, \"But wouldn't getting a perm make me look too mature and old?\"","Zhou Yueshen immediately replied, \"No, it'll look good.\"","Big wavy curls were popular in this era. Si Nian's hair had grown long and was currently very straight, so she wanted to follow the local customs for once.","Besides, she was already a stunningly glamorous beauty, and big waves would be even sexier.","It would also make her look much more mature.","That way, walking beside the man, people wouldn't say she was his daughter anymore.","Seeing Zhou Yueshen so supportive, she decided to just do it.","Zhou Yueshen actually rarely went to barbershops.","If it weren't for his hair getting a bit unruly, he would usually just go to a roadside stall for a buzz cut.","But keeping it too short didn't look great either, which was why he came to the barbershop.","This place was also recommended by Yu Dong and the others.","Zhou Yueshen had never paid attention to these things before. Yu Dong had mentioned it in passing when they walked by, and for some reason, he remembered it today and came over.","Si Nian also liked getting manicures, but they didn't offer that service here. So, she simply bought some nail polish, planning to paint them herself when she got back.","She liked bright colors, so she bought several bottles in rose red, classic red, and so on.","Zhou Yueshen's hair was simple; it wasn't very long to begin with, so there weren't many styling options.","When asked how he wanted it cut, he just looked at Si Nian.","The barber immediately understood and came over to ask for Si Nian's opinion.","Zhou Yueshen actually looked very handsome with a buzz cut, but sometimes it just looked a bit too square and rigid.","Si Nian thought carefully and thought of her idol Edison Chen's buzz cut style.","She immediately described it to the barber.","There weren't many styles for short hair anyway, and a buzz cut style was simple, so the barber understood quickly.","He immediately smiled, nodded, and said okay.","Si Nian was arranged to get her hair washed, and then the female boss personally gave her the perm.","She had a lot of hair to begin with, and it was too long, so Si Nian had it trimmed slightly.","Big waves would look even prettier. When choosing the style, the boss lady repeatedly said it would definitely look good.","Getting a perm took quite a while. After Zhou Yueshen finished his haircut, he waited by her side.","Bored with nothing to do, Si Nian took out her nail polish and taught Zhou Yueshen how to apply it.","Zhou Yueshen listened to whatever she said and earnestly began painting her nails for her.","Despite not looking like a man who could do delicate work, he was actually very smart. He learned it after Si Nian taught him just once, and he was exceptionally careful, not getting any polish on her skin, and keeping the coats very smooth.","By the time Si Nian's perm was done, all ten of her fingers were painted. The rose red made her hands look even more slender and fair, stunningly beautiful.","Zhou Yueshen had never seen anyone wear nail polish so beautifully and elegantly. Such a bright color could easily look messy and tacky.","But on Si Nian, the color looked much more sophisticated.","The ring on her ring finger radiated a brilliant luster.","No wonder she liked bright colors so much; they truly suited her perfectly.","Zhou Yueshen held her hand, unable to bear letting it go, and didn't release it even after he was done.","Hair styling skills in this era were solid and genuine, unlike in the future where many lacked standard.","After Si Nian's hair was permed and washed, you could see a beautiful curl.","It didn't even need to be specially blow-dried into shape; it was very shiny even when it dried naturally.","The curly hair made her face look smaller and gave her an elegant aura.","By the time the two finished and headed home, it was already afternoon.","They had ended up spending the entire day out.","**","At the Si family home, Lin Sisi returned home very happy after estimating her exam scores.","Although her English score was a bit too low, her other subjects were quite good.","At the very least, she would definitely be able to get into university.","Moreover, she could get into a very good university within the province.","Even though it didn't meet her expectations, for someone who hadn't even attended university in her past life, just being able to go was already very good.","Furthermore, staying in the province meant she would be close by, making it convenient to cultivate her relationship with Fu Yang.","No matter how capable Si Nian was, she would probably only get into an ordinary university. She had heard that Fu Qianqian didn't even pass the university entrance exams, and Si Nian was only relatively good at English.","Plus, she hadn't been to school for a year, and without the advantage of past-life memories like herself, she definitely wouldn't be able to compete.","Even if she could get in, it would at most be a junior college or a second-rate university.","After all, she had the blessing of rebirth; it was impossible for her to be worse than Si Nian.","Lin Sisi informed her family. Even though the official results weren't out yet, the Si family was already planning to host a celebratory dinner.","On the other side, Zhou Yueshen was also planning to invite relatives and friends over for a meal.","Even though Si Nian's results hadn't come out yet, he had already gone ahead and informed the Lin family as well as their acquaintances."]},{"number":381,"title":"Chapter 381: Exam Results","paragraphs":["This was also what the Lin family had called to agree upon in advance.","After all, Si Nian was their daughter, and they were very concerned about how she did on her exams.","By letting them know early, they could prepare to come over and celebrate.","And they weren't the only ones preparing after the college entrance examination ended.","Even the newspaper agencies had received some inside information and were preparing to stake out for interviews on the day the results were announced.","Fang Hui was one of the people dispatched for these interviews.","She really didn't want to go. After all, there were simply too many impressive people in Jing City. It wasn't strange at all for top scorers from all over the country to gather there.","But this small city was different. If just one or two students made it to Tsinghua or Peking University, they couldn't wait for the whole world to know.","Making a fuss over nothing.","It gave her a feeling that it was quite unpresentable.","However, since she worked here now, even if she didn't want to, she had to go through the motions.","While she was busy, someone sent a letter to Fang Hui's workplace.","After reading it, Fang Hui's face was full of pleasant surprise.","After returning home, she noticed that the Si family next door seemed very lively.","Although Fang Hui had some friction with Si Nian, both were smart people. They usually tried to avoid contact, sometimes even pretending not to see each other.","It didn't get too ugly, since they lived close by and saw each other frequently.","Fang Hui certainly didn't like Si Nian either, but she didn't want to offend anyone. There were only a few families nearby, and the rest lived in tube-shaped apartments. She didn't want to interact with the people over there; the only family she wanted to curry favor with was the Jiang family.","Unfortunately, the Jiang family was very close to Si Nian and had a great relationship with her.","If she had a falling out with Si Nian, the Jiang family would also dislike her by association. One could imagine how uncomfortable her life here would become.","During this time, Si Nian hadn't gone to teach at the school. She heard that Si Nian had actually gone to take the college entrance examination.","Fang Hui couldn't understand it at all. She was already married; why was she taking the college entrance exam?","Could it be that since she failed last time, she would pass this time?","She had seen too many outstanding people in Jing City, and even her own son had to be excellent. So after hearing about this, Fang Hui felt that the standard of this foreign language elementary school wasn't that great either.","She had only sent her son there because she previously heard there were overseas returnee doctorates teaching there, and it was the only foreign language elementary school in the city center.","She never expected that Si Nian, an English teacher, was actually just a student who hadn't even attended college.","Fang Hui withdrew her gaze disdainfully.","When she got home, another letter was delivered, containing a stack of money inside.","Receiving two letters in a row, Fang Hui was somewhat pleasantly surprised. The end of the college entrance exam also meant universities were on break. No wonder that man was willing to reply to her letter.","He should be almost done with his work soon.","Fang Hui did not want to stay in this underdeveloped city.","Having seen better, how could she be willing to stay in such a place?","Receiving the man's reply made her feel increasingly anxious and eager.","The elementary school also began its final exams.","Fang Bowen had been under a lot of pressure these past few days and had even caught a cold.","He coughed while doing his homework.","When Fang Hui got home, the nanny she hired was cooking.","Seeing her return, the nanny immediately smiled and came forward to chat.","Fang Hui was very busy during this period. She had assignments and sometimes had to attend social engagements, only returning very late at night.","So she couldn't accompany her son to his exams.","Worried about a repeat of the last accident and afraid he would sneak out to play, she gritted her teeth and spent money to hire a nanny for him.","To help cook, take him to school, supervise his homework, and so on.","This saved Fang Hui a lot of worry.","\"Where is Bowen?\"","The nanny smiled and said, \"Bowen is reading in the study upstairs. Just as you instructed: finishes class at four-thirty, arrives home at five to practice piano for half an hour, does homework at six, eats dinner at six-thirty, rests for ten minutes before reading, reviews the teacher's notes at eight, and goes to bed punctually at nine...\"","Because the midterm exams were coming up, Fang Hui gave the tutor some time off.","They didn't need to come for the time being, which also allowed her son to rest a bit more.","Fang Hui was very satisfied.","The nanny smiled, \"Do you want to go up and see him?\"","Holding the thick stack of cash in her hand, Fang Hui shook her head. \"No need. I just came back to check and will be leaving shortly. I have another social engagement tonight and might come back very late. You can go home after Bowen goes to sleep.\"","The nanny immediately smiled and nodded. After Fang Hui left, the phone rang.","She hurried to answer it. Who knows what the other party said, but she left the villa with a smile.","After Fang Bowen finished his homework, he smelled the aroma of cooking from the Zhou family next door.","His stomach was growling with hunger. Seeing that it was getting dark and the nanny still hadn't called him for dinner, he couldn't hold it in anymore. He slid off his stool and went downstairs, covering his mouth as he coughed.","\"Cough, cough... Aunt Zhang, is dinner not ready yet?\"","Fang Bowen called out twice but received no response. Confused, he walked into the kitchen, only to find it completely empty.","Fang Bowen was a bit bewildered. He opened the refrigerator; there were vegetables and eggs inside, but he didn't know how to cook. He was really too hungry, so he dug out the bread slices Fang Hui had used for breakfast that morning.","Actually, he really disliked eating bread slices, but he was starving right now. He also struggled to get himself a glass of cold water, gulping it down, which finally made him feel a bit better.","His stomach felt icy cold.","Fang Bowen couldn't help but think of that early morning, and the piping hot egg pancake in his arms.","...","In the examination room the next day, the sound of coughing was incessant.","The invigilator couldn't help but frown and stepped forward to ask about the situation.","\"Student, are you alright?\"","Fang Bowen coughed until his little face was bright red, saying he was fine.","Zhou Zedong tilted his head and glanced at him.","He had already heard Fang Bowen coughing during yesterday's exam.","He didn't expect the cough to be even worse today.","He withdrew his gaze and continued writing on his exam paper.","Si Nian came today to pick up the two children from their midterm exams. She had nothing to do at home recently. Days without having to do homework or prepare lessons were incredibly comfortable.","This was her first time coming to the school since getting a new hairstyle, and she even specially put on makeup, striving to be the most stunning one among the parents.","Sure enough, among the crowd of parents waiting for their children's exams, she was the most eye-catching.","She clearly wasn't dressed overly extravagantly, yet she made it impossible for people to look away.","Si Nian also ran into Yuanyuan's mother, who had previously had a dispute with her son.","\"Oh, it really is Xiaoshuai's mother. I almost didn't recognize you. How come you've gotten even prettier after not seeing you for a while?\"","Si Nian was puzzled. \"Xiaoshuai's mother?\"","Yuanyuan's mother laughed, \"Pfft, I misspoke. Little Dong's mother.\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","After speaking, Yuanyuan's mother admiringly touched Si Nian's curly hair, stared at the lipstick on her lips, and then looked enviously at the nail polish on her fingers.","Truly, genuinely so beautiful.","Prettier than a big celebrity.","As soon as she arrived, she couldn't help but stare, wondering to herself whose parent this was to look so good. It turned out to be the mother of her daughter's desk-mate, Xiaoshuai.","Sigh, truly good genes in that family.","\"Where did you get your hair done? It looks so good, beautifully done.\"","\"What color is this lipstick? It makes your skin look so fair.\"","\"Where did you get this nail polish done?\"","Seeing her eager face, looking as if she was just short of asking for a purchase link, Si Nian smiled and said, \"I just got a perm at a random hair salon. The lipstick is cherry-colored, and I painted the nail polish myself.\"","\"Your skin is fair, so this color really suits you.\"","Yuanyuan's mother said shyly, \"Is... is it a bit too bright?\"","\"Not at all.\"","Yuanyuan's mother was rather plump, giving off an air of affluence.","Her skin was fair, suggesting her family was quite wealthy.","Yuanyuan's mother immediately became happy. She enthusiastically linked her arm with Si Nian's, praising her great taste and suggesting they go shopping for clothes together in the future.","She then asked how her son's grades were.","\"I've heard about it. It seems a lot happened with your child before. Yuanyuan also told me that Little Dong went to the genius class. Sigh, what a pity.\"","Si Nian was confused. \"A pity?\"","Yuanyuan's mother quickly covered her mouth.","Could she say that she had taken a liking to her son at first sight and wanted to snatch him home to be her son-in-law?","Facts proved that her own daughter was too clumsy. Half a semester had passed, and she hadn't even managed to exchange a few words with him.","She had originally thought that since they were young, children didn't have high standards for looks. Maybe some blind Prince Charming would take a liking to her daughter, starting a childhood sweetheart romance. Then she wouldn't have to worry about her daughter meeting a bad man in the future.","Unfortunately, imagination is beautiful, but reality is cruel.","She hurriedly changed the subject. \"I heard you resigned to take the college entrance exam or something? Did you take it?\"","Si Nian nodded.","\"How was it?\"","Si Nian smiled and said it was okay.","Yuanyuan's mother immediately said, \"Everyone knows your abilities. They all say you teach well and will definitely get into a good university. If you celebrate when the results come out, you must invite me. I want to share in the glory.\"","Si Nian felt a bit helpless but smiled and said she definitely would if there was a chance.","As they chatted, time quickly passed.","The children who had finished their exams started coming out one after another.","Si Nian saw her eldest son among the first batch.","Zhou Zedong walked up to her with his backpack and called out, \"Mom.\"","Si Nian's mouth was dry from chatting with Yuanyuan's mother. She was actually quite afraid of this kind of overly familiar person. It seemed impolite not to answer, but the more you answered, the more they talked, as if they had an endless supply of topics.","It exhausted her.","As soon as her son spoke, she immediately sighed in relief and smiled, \"Little Dong finished the exam? How was it? Was it difficult?\"","Zhou Zedong shook his head and said, \"Not difficult.\"","Si Nian looked again; Second Child and Jiang Jiu hadn't come out yet.","Jiang Wenqing had something to do today and couldn't accompany Jiang Jiu to the exam.","A couple of days ago, he had specially visited to ask for her help, asking her to keep an eye on Jiang Jiu for him.","Other children had parents accompanying them to the exam.","It was quite pitiful that Jiang Jiu didn't, so Si Nian naturally agreed.","Grandpa Jiang was getting old and hadn't been in good health recently, so Grandma Jiang had to take care of him.","Therefore, today Yaoyao was left with Zhou Yueshen to play at the breeding farm, while she came over to watch the boys.","Si Nian wasn't in a hurry. She checked the time; there was still half an hour before the exam ended.","Given Second Child's level, he probably wouldn't finish writing until the last second.","Zhou Zedong seemed used to it and stood quietly to the side waiting for his younger brother.","At this time, Si Nian saw Fang Bowen walking out while coughing.","She instinctively tilted her head and glanced around but didn't see Fang Hui's figure.","It was a bit strange. Fang Hui paid so much attention to her son's grades, yet she didn't come for today's midterm exam?","Fang Bowen didn't seem to be in a good state either.","Fang Bowen also noticed her, and his eyes immediately lit up. He seemed to want to come over and say hello.","But he was quickly interrupted.","\"Bowen, you finished your exam. Let's go, I'm taking you to your tutoring class. Your mother said you can't relax even after the exam. The tutoring class is so expensive, you have to study hard.\"","After saying that, the person pulled him away.","Yuanyuan's mother sighed in amazement from the side. \"As expected of a little genius. Tutoring classes are arranged right after the exam. No wonder he's so amazing.\"","The fact that a seven-year-old little genius had skipped grades to enter the fourth grade at the Foreign Language Primary School was not a trivial matter.","Since he was in her daughter's class, she had also heard some things about it.","This was her first time seeing him.","Si Nian withdrew her gaze and frowned.","This Fang Bowen was truly quite pitiful.","The child was still so young, yet they couldn't wait to cram all the knowledge into his brain.","Zhou Zedong also tilted his head to take a look but didn't say anything.","Soon, Yuanyuan also came out after finishing her exam.","Si Nian noticed that this little girl had lost some weight.","She looked much more delicate than before.","\"Oh my, Yuanyuan, how did you do on the exam?\" Yuanyuan's mother asked nervously.","Yuanyuan looked disappointed. \"Not very well.\"","Yuanyuan's mother: \"...\"","Why was there such a huge gap when they were both in the fourth grade?","Thinking of how Zhou Zedong looked so calm and fully in control when Si Nian asked him how he did...","Yuanyuan's mother felt that she shouldn't have asked her daughter how she did.","It was just asking for an insult.","At this moment, Yuanyuan also saw Zhou Zedong. Her eyes lit up, and she went forward to greet him, \"Zhou, classmate Zhou Zedong, long time no see!\"","She was very happy; she hadn't expected to run into Zhou Zedong.","Zhou Zedong was so amazing, currently being in the genius class.","To think that such an amazing person used to be her deskmate. Yuanyuan felt a sense of shared honor.","Zhou Zedong tilted his head, glanced at her, and frowned. \"You are?\"","Yuanyuan: \"...\"","\"I-I'm your deskmate, Wang Yuanyuan... Wang Yuanyuan from Class Four.\"","Yuanyuan was about to cry.","No matter what, they had been deskmates for a while.","It had only been a few months, and he already didn't recognize her.","It was too hurtful.","Zhou Zedong was slightly startled.","He then looked her up and down and said, \"You've lost weight.\"","His previous deskmate was very plump, he remembered, because when they shared a desk, she took up more than half the space.","And she liked to sneak snacks during class.","She would also ask him if he wanted some.","But she was very chubby back then, her facial features all squeezed together.","Now, she had slimmed down quite a bit.","Yuanyuan had been very sad, but hearing his words, she instantly became happy and blushed. \"Have... have I lost weight?\"","Zhou Zedong was concise. \"Yes.\"","Yuanyuan: \"Thank you.\"","Inner monologue: He still remembers that I used to be fat. It seems he doesn't completely hate me, otherwise why would he remember I was fat?","Yuanyuan poked her fingers together shyly and said, \"You've grown taller too, and you look even better.\"","Zhou Zedong gave her an odd look. \"Thank you.\"","As the two were talking, a pretty figure squeezed in. \"Classmate Zhou Zedong, you've finished your exam too. How did you do?\"","It was Chu Xiang'er.","Although Yuanyuan had lost weight, standing next to the slender Chu Xiang'er, she still looked much chubbier.","Seeing Chu Xiang'er's cheerful and enthusiastic demeanor, she awkwardly shifted her feet and made room.","Li Youcai also walked over, looking displeased.","He couldn't understand why Xiang'er was always so happy every time she saw Zhou Zedong.","Watching the group of children, Si Nian couldn't help but smile.","It seemed her son wasn't doing too badly socially after all.","The kids also noticed Si Nian.","They immediately stood up straight and behaved properly.","\"Hello, Teacher Si!\"","Si Nian smiled. \"Hello there, how did you all do on the exam?\"","Chu Xiang'er smiled shyly. \"It was okay, Teacher Si, but definitely not as good as classmate Zhou Zedong.\"","Li Youcai gave a cold snort and said proudly, \"Next time, I will definitely beat Zhou Zedong!\"","Si Nian smiled and rubbed both of their heads.","Chu Xianger chimed in, \"Teacher, Teacher! I heard from my grandpa that you took the college entrance exam too. You will definitely be celebrating when the results are out, right? Can we come and celebrate with you?\"","After saying that, she glanced at Zhou Zedong.","Si Nian hesitated for a moment.","But after thinking about it, she figured that once the results were out, she would inevitably invite the principal and the others for a meal anyway. So, she nodded and said, \"Of course. When the time comes, you can come along with the teachers.\"","By this time, Second Child and Jiang Jiu had also come out of the testing center.","Compared to the excitement of the other children, these two little guys looked utterly defeated.","Si Nian could not even bring herself to ask how their exams went.","Instead, she quickly pulled them along, promising to take them to the amusement park to play.","The two little guys were instantly revived on the spot.","That very evening, after the children finished their exams, Si Nian received a call from her homeroom teacher."]},{"number":382,"title":"Chapter 382: Chapter 381: The Results Are Really Out","paragraphs":["Si Nian was a bit bewildered when she picked up. Although a telephone was installed at home, very few people ever called.","Long-distance calls were expensive, so people still preferred writing letters. Unless it was something truly important, no one was willing to spend money on a phone call.","When she heard it was her homeroom teacher from the No. 2 Middle School, she knew immediately that the exam results must be out.","The homeroom teacher's voice was incredibly excited. Even through the phone, Si Nian could feel his voice trembling, even cracking a bit: 685 points, Si Nian! It's even higher than your estimate. You are the top science scorer, do you know that? The top scorer of our Yungui-Sichuan Province!","The homeroom teacher couldn't hide his excitement. He didn't even know how to express his joy, repeatedly saying the words top science scorer and claiming he was going to strike it rich.","His tone made it sound as if he was the one who got the top score.","Si Nian already had a rough idea when she estimated her score earlier, so she wasn't too surprised to hear this number. However, she was genuinely surprised to hear she was the top provincial scorer.","After all, she always believed that no matter the era, there would always be a few geniuses emerging out of nowhere.","She didn't consider herself a genius, but with the advantage of having taken the college entrance exam once before, it wasn't strange for her to get this score.","Waiting for the other party to finish his excited rant, she finally replied, I understand. Thank you, sir.","The homeroom teacher fell silent for a second, then asked uncertainly, Are you so happy that you've gone silly?","Otherwise, why wasn't she excited? Shouldn't hearing this score and finding out she was the top scorer make her so thrilled that blood rushed to her head and she jumped up and down on the spot?","How come her tone of voice hadn't changed at all?","He wanted her to know that when he first received the news, it took him an hour to recover. He couldn't even stand up, and his legs were still weak right now.","He couldn't believe that his own student was actually the provincial top science scorer.","Perfect scores in Physics, Chemistry, and English!","Si Nian chuckled and said, Not really. After all, I used to be a teacher too, so I have a strong psychological endurance.","Si Nian's words instantly made the homeroom teacher touch his nose in embarrassment.","Why did that sound like she was mocking him?","Recovering himself, he laughed, I'm just too happy. The results were supposed to come out tomorrow, but the principal called me asking for your contact information, so I knew right away they must be out. I'm really sorry for disturbing you with a call so late at night. Get some rest, and we'll talk about everything else at school tomorrow.","Si Nian said okay.","The homeroom teacher hurriedly added, Right, right, there might be reporters coming to our school tomorrow. The principal has also prepared a bonus for you. You'll probably have to go on stage to give a speech or something, so mentally prepare yourself for that.","Their principal had already sent out overnight notices to get the banners arranged.","After all, this was the first time in so many years they had produced a top scorer, and a provincial one at that. The banners were going to be super large, even placed at the back gate. They were determined not to miss a single blind spot, terrified that the No. 1 Middle School across the street wouldn't see them.","Although the news wouldn't officially break until tomorrow, it was estimated that most schools and media reporters who followed exam results had already received the inside scoop.","Si Nian listened to him ramble on for over half an hour. Seeing that she truly wasn't showing any excitement, the homeroom teacher finally hung up the phone in slight disappointment.","It was like the pain of sharing a massive piece of good news with someone, only for them to completely miss why you were so excited.","And this person was even the main character of that good news.","Unwilling to let it go, the homeroom teacher immediately dug out his notebook and called every teacher he knew in it.","Hello, Teacher Wang, good evening! Ah? How did you know our class produced the provincial top science scorer?","Treat me to dinner? No need, no need, I'm very busy. I have to go eat with the top science scorer tomorrow.","Isn't this Teacher Zhang from No. 1 Middle School? The city's top arts scorer is in your school, huh? I'm so jealous. Unlike us, we only managed to get the top science scorer, and it's for the whole province...","...","At the same time, the lights in the principal's office were still on.","Drink? Principal Zhang, you must be joking. I've quit drinking now; I need to set a good example for the students.","Principal Li, I won't be able to make it to our appointment tomorrow. You know how it is, our school produced the provincial top science scorer, and there are reporters coming to interview tomorrow.","Isn't this the Editor-in-Chief of the Guichuan Evening News? You want to interview me? I'm sorry, I've already promised the Editor-in-Chief of the Liberation Daily.",".......","Si Nian hung up the phone and turned her head to find Second Child looking at her curiously.","Mom, Mom, who called you?","Si Nian smiled and said, A teacher.","Second Child: A teacher? Do I know them?","Si Nian smiled and shook her head. You don't know him.","Second Child asked curiously, Is it a man or a woman?","Si Nian said, A male teacher. He's Mom's homeroom teacher.","Second Child immediately became alert.","A male teacher, a homeroom teacher?","And they talked on the phone for half an hour, making Mom so happy.","Mom didn't even talk on the phone with Dad for that long.","Just who was this homeroom teacher?","Now that the results were out, Si Nian felt a bit more relaxed.","There would probably be a lot to do tomorrow, so she needed to take a bath.","If there really were reporters interviewing her, wouldn't she be in the newspaper?","Thinking back to the figures from the old era she had seen in vintage newspapers...","Si Nian made up her mind. She had to dress up tomorrow and strive to be the most beautiful girl in the 1980s newspapers!","She clearly had the talent, but she insisted on standing out with her beauty.","With this thought in mind, Si Nian went upstairs to take a bath.","It was drizzling tonight, and when Zhou Yueshen returned, he was covered in dampness.","However, he had been coming back almost every day recently.","As soon as he entered the door, he saw Second Child with a bitter face.","Zhou Yueshen paused and looked down at him: Little Han, why aren't you asleep yet?","If he remembered correctly, his two sons had their mid-term exams today.","Could it be that he didn't do well on the exam, which was why the child had this expression?","Zhou Yueshen recalled that back in their hometown, Second Child's grades were always worlds apart from his eldest son's.","One was first place, the other was dead last.","In the past, the little guy didn't care much about grades.","But after coming to the city, he had grown up and cared about his pride.","If he didn't do well this time, he probably wouldn't even be able to sleep soundly.","Zhou Yueshen was just about to comfort him with a few words when Second Child looked up, gazing at his father with a face full of pity, and said, Dad, Mom was just on the phone with someone.","Under Zhou Yueshen's puzzled gaze, he added, A man. They talked for half an hour.","Zhou Yueshen: ......","Second Child was still thinking about how Si Nian had previously said she was going to run away. Although Mom said it was a joke, Second Child thought, how could anyone just make a joke like that out of nowhere?","Mom must be unhappy, which was why she said that. She probably wanted to pacify them first, and then sneak away when they weren't paying attention.","That was how the adults in the village tricked children.","And then the children would become orphans.","He didn't want to be an orphan.","Zhou Zehan looked at his father with an extremely complex expression, as if disappointed by his failure to meet expectations.","Because he felt that since he was so cute and obedient, Mom definitely wouldn't want to leave because of him.","Then it could only be because of his dad.","Zhou Yueshen was so exasperated by his son's look that he laughed.","He roughly rubbed Second Child's hair, turning it into a bird's nest, before saying in a deep voice, \"Don't talk nonsense.\"","Second Child stubbornly covered his head, giving a look that said: I've warned you anyway; if you don't take it to heart, don't blame me for running away with Mom.","As long as he could follow Mom, eat meat every day, and live in a villa, he was willing.","Zhou Yueshen ignored him, closed the door, and went upstairs.","Just as he changed his clothes, Si Nian walked out of the bathroom.","Si Nian was humming a tune.","The joy on her face could not be hidden.","Zhou Yueshen couldn't help but think of his son's words.","Si Nian had been on the phone with a man for half an hour.","And she was this happy?","It was so late, who would be calling her?","And chatting for so long?","Could it be a call from her hometown?","It shouldn't be. If it were a call from her hometown, Second Child wouldn't have misunderstood.","But no matter how much Zhou Yueshen thought about it, he couldn't think of any man around Si Nian.","After all, Si Nian's work environment was different from his. Of course, Zhou Yueshen didn't know who she interacted with.","Zhou Yueshen paused and asked tentatively, \"Niannian, did someone call you just now?\"","Si Nian had just been about to tell him about this. She didn't expect Zhou Yueshen to ask first, so she was a little surprised. \"How did you know?\"","Zhou Yueshen was slightly taken aback and said softly, \"Little Han told me.\"","Si Nian smiled and said, \"I was just about to tell you. I didn't expect Little Han to inform you first. It was a call from my homeroom teacher.\"","Zhou Yueshen immediately understood; it turned out to be a misunderstanding. \"The scores are out?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Yes, the homeroom teacher got the news and immediately called me. Guess how many points I scored.\"","Zhou Yueshen was silent for a moment. Seeing her so happy, the score definitely wouldn't be low.","\"Around 680?\"","Si Nian: \"...Talking to you is no fun at all. There are no surprises.\"","Zhou Yueshen chuckled softly, \"You estimated your score to be around 660, so you definitely underestimated it.\"","Si Nian smiled, \"It's 685! I'm the provincial top scorer in science. Is there any reward?\"","Zhou Yueshen froze for a moment. He knew it wouldn't be low, but he didn't expect it to be even higher than his own estimate.","But thinking about Si Nian's hard work during this period, he felt that this score was not surprising.","He was also happy for her!","\"What do you want?\"","Si Nian said, \"I haven't decided yet. I'll tell you when I do.\"","Zhou Yueshen gently agreed.","On the surface, the man looked even calmer than her.","Si Nian suddenly understood how her homeroom teacher felt when calling her.","Sharing such great news without getting a matching response was truly disappointing.","The older man was so calm that it made her feel less excited.","Zhou Yueshen asked her, \"Have you told your family?\"","Si Nian shook her head. \"Not yet, it's too late. My parents are definitely asleep at this hour. Although such good news should be shared with them immediately, if I tell them now, I'm afraid they won't be able to sleep tonight.\"","After hearing this, Zhou Yueshen agreed.","He nodded slightly.","Seeing Si Nian yawn, he said, \"You go to sleep first. I'll take you to school tomorrow.\"","Si Nian agreed. She absolutely refused to stay up late. Staying up late would give her eye bags and dark circles, affecting her performance tomorrow.","Zhou Yueshen waited until she fell asleep before going downstairs to send his son and daughter, who were watching TV, to bed.","Even though it wasn't even nine o'clock and the children didn't have school tomorrow, Zhou Yueshen simply wouldn't let them watch anymore.","He said that watching TV for too long was bad for children's eyes.","Seeing the two children wanting to act spoiled and protest, he added, \"Mom said so.\"","The two children sensibly shut their mouths immediately, holding hands as they went upstairs to sleep.","Seeing the two children enter their room, Zhou Yueshen finally breathed a sigh of relief. He walked over to the telephone and made a call.","\"Yes, I'm not going to the breeding farm tomorrow. My wife scored 685 on her exam; she's the provincial science top scorer.\"","\"Boss Wang, I won't be delivering meat tomorrow. My wife scored 685; she's the provincial science top scorer.\"","\"Yu Dong, your sister-in-law scored 685...\"","\"...\"","Early the next morning, when Si Nian came downstairs, she saw Zhou Yueshen standing by the phone making a call.","She yawned.","\"You're up so early?\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded and said, \"I'm calling Mom and Dad. It's good that you're awake.\"","He gestured for Si Nian to come over and take the phone.","Si Nian walked over and glanced at him.","Zhou Yueshen said, \"I haven't told them yet. You should tell them yourself.\"","The corners of Si Nian's mouth turned up. She took the phone and smiled, \"Mom, it's me. My college entrance exam results are out.\"","Lin's mother's tone was very excited, \"What's the score?\"","\"685 points. University won't be a problem.\"","\"If you have time, come over and have a meal together. I'll ask Zhou Yueshen to pick you up.\"","Lin's mother knew her daughter was certainly smart, but she hadn't expected her to be this amazing. She was so excited she could barely hold the phone steady.","She immediately said she would pack up and come over right away.","She also told Zhou Yueshen not to bother going back to pick them up; they would take a car themselves.","Now that the family's financial situation had improved, it wasn't like they couldn't afford the fare.","It would be too tiring for Zhou Yueshen to run back and forth.","Si Nian smiled and agreed.","As soon as she hung up, the phone immediately rang again.","It was the principal of No. 2 High School, asking when she would go over.","He asked if he should come and pick her up.","Si Nian hurriedly declined.","Just as she hung up, another call came in. It was the director of the Foreign Language Primary School.","The director had heard from the principal and asked where she was, saying the school wanted to treat her to a meal.","Si Nian answered five or six calls in a row and almost threw up.","She refused to answer any more calls that came after that.","Where on earth did these people get her phone number?","Zhou Yueshen looked at her with a smile and said, \"Let's eat first. Don't worry about it.\"","After he finished speaking, he unplugged the phone line.","The world was finally quiet.","The family ate breakfast as usual. Si Nian said, \"I have a very important piece of news to tell everyone today.\"","The children immediately looked over at her.","Second Child's heart filled with joy: \"Mom, are we going to the amusement park to play again today?\"","Si Nian glared at her son.","\"We just played for a whole afternoon yesterday. Haven't you played enough?\"","\"Mom, what's the good news?\" Eldest Child also cast a speechless glance at his younger brother and asked.","\"Mom's college entrance exam score is out. 685 points.\"","Si Nian looked proudly at the three children and said.","She finally had a chance to show off in front of these two future villain bosses.","Neither of the two children was stupid; they knew what the score meant.","Second Child was so shocked that his chopsticks dropped with a clatter: \"Mom, your score is so much higher than my brother's!\"","He had thought his brother's score of over two hundred and ninety points was already a lot.","He didn't expect his mother's to be even higher.","Zhou Zedong said in pleasant surprise, \"Mom, you're amazing. Doesn't that mean you can go to a very good university?\""]},{"number":383,"title":"Chapter 383: Chapter 382: Lin Sisi Goes to College","paragraphs":["Yaoyao bit her spoon in confusion and asked, \"Mom, what is a university?\"","Si Nian smiled and stroked her hair. \"A university is a school just like the one your brothers go to, except the people who go there are all adults.\"","Yaoyao nodded, half-understanding, and then said, \"Mom, then Yaoyao wants to go to a university too!\"","Previously, Si Nian took her to the elementary school all day. Yaoyao saw the students having classes and would sometimes join in.","The little kids all liked her, saying she was amazing, and would even share their candy with her.","A hint of yearning flickered in Yaoyao's big, bright eyes.","Second Child grew anxious. Mom was going to university. He had previously said that if Mom couldn't get into a university, then he wouldn't either, so he could stay with her.","But now, hearing that Mom had gotten in and his younger sister saying she wanted to go too, he immediately declared, \"Mom, I want to go to university too.\"","Although Zhou Zedong didn't say anything, his eyes were full of anticipation. He had been instilled with the idea that \"education changes one's destiny\" since he was a child, so he had always worked very hard.","Getting into a university could change his destiny. Even though his destiny had already been changed, his goal wouldn't waver because of it.","He looked at Si Nian with adoration in his eyes.","There were no college students in their village; he heard that even their homeroom teacher was only a high school graduate.","Yet, at school, he was highly respected, and everyone tried to please him.","In the future, he also wanted to get into a university like Mom, so even if he returned to the village, no one would mock him.","\"Mom, which university do you want to go to?\"","\"Peking University.\"","Zhou Zedong muttered, \"Peking University?\"","He made up his mind. He would go to Peking University in the future and attend the same school as Mom.","The family digested the good news and prepared to set off.","Originally, they thought it would be fine just to drop Si Nian off, but the kids followed her wherever she went.","Zhou Yueshen hadn't even said he was taking them along, but seeing Si Nian get into the car, the children familiarly climbed in after her.","Dragging the whole family along, Zhou Yueshen was completely helpless.","Da Huang had been unchained. Seeing the family about to leave, it also stuck its butt up and tried to squeeze in.","But its body was too big now, already the size of an adult Tibetan Mastiff. Although it could squeeze in, the three children would suffer.","Besides, going to a school where there were people everywhere, it wouldn't be good to bring it along. What if it scared someone?","Zhou Yueshen looked at Da Huang, who had already squeezed more than halfway in with its butt up and tail wagging, and the three children, feeling so troubled that his craving for a smoke was acting up.","\"Da Huang, get down.\"","Finally, he called out to it, and taking advantage of the moment Da Huang wagged its tail and hopped down to look at him expectantly, he slammed the car door shut.","Da Huang was tricked into the gate and stood behind the iron bars, wagging its tail.","Zhou Yueshen was just about to drive off when he heard the voice of Jiang Jiu from next door.","\"Uncle Zhou, Uncle Zhou.\"","Jiang Jiu ran over wearing a pair of overalls and a short-sleeved T-shirt.","He first glanced at Second Brother and the others in the car, then looked up expectantly at Zhou Yueshen, calling out sweetly, \"Uncle Zhou, Second Brother, where are you going?\"","Zhou Yueshen quite liked this little guy from next door.","He was cute, sensible, had a good relationship with his youngest son, and they stuck together every day.","He reached down to pat the little guy's head and said gently, \"Uncle is taking your Auntie Si and the others to school.\"","Jiang Jiu immediately asked expectantly, \"To school? Uncle, Uncle, can I go too?\"","Zhou Yueshen paused.","Although he quite liked the little guy, he wasn't good at babysitting for others.","Just as he was about to refuse, Jiang Jiu tugged at his hand and whined playfully, \"Uncle Zhou, Uncle Zhou, let me go with you. I'll be good and listen to you.\"","Zhou Yueshen was most afraid of sweet-talking children; none of the three kids at home would act spoiled like this.","A hint of stiffness appeared on his usually stern face.","Si Nian smiled and said, \"Let's take him along.\"","Second Child also leaned halfway out of the car and shouted to him loudly, \"Little Jiang, Little Jiang, I'm over here!\"","Jiang Jiu's eyes lit up. He immediately dropped Zhou Yueshen's hand and scampered over.","\"Second Brother, I want to sit with you.\"","Second Child immediately scooted over and patted the seat, saying, \"Okay, come on up.\"","Si Nian smiled at Zhou Yueshen, who walked over with a helpless look, and said, \"It's fine, kids don't take up much space.\"","After speaking, she saw Grandma Jiang walk out and greeted her.","And so, the large family set off towards No. 2 Middle School.","Meanwhile, on the other side.","At the Si family home.","The Si family, who were just getting ready to go to the school, received a phone call.","Zhang Cuimei was delighted to hear the homeroom teacher's voice.","\"What, Sisi scored 398? Then isn't a university guaranteed?\"","\"That's wonderful, teacher. Thank you so much, otherwise our Sisi might not have made it to college.\"","\"Adopted daughter? You mean Si Nian? Why are you asking about her?\"","\"She's not with me. Don't ask me about her affairs. I'm busy, I'm hanging up now.\"","Zhang Cuimei hung up impatiently. Why was the homeroom teacher inexplicably asking if Si Nian was at home?","Didn't he know that Si Nian had left the Si family a long time ago?","Zhang Cuimei now harbored great hostility towards Si Nian. Just hearing her name mentioned made her frown involuntarily.","Why bring her up on such a good day? Truly bad luck.","When Zhang Cuimei hung up, Lin Sisi and Si's Father both looked over at her.","Zhang Cuimei announced proudly, \"The scores are out. Sisi got 398. Getting into a university is definitely no problem!\"","Si's Father breathed a sigh of relief. To be honest, he had also been worried that Lin Sisi wouldn't pass, as that would be truly embarrassing.","He had always cared about his face, but Lin Sisi was from the countryside. If she passed, everyone would be happy; if she didn't, the whole family would lose face along with her.","Although this score wasn't great and might only get her into an average university, being able to go to a university these days was already very good.","At least it was better than a junior college.","He nodded with satisfaction. \"Not bad. For Sisi to get into a university under these circumstances, I am proud of you as a father.\"","Lin Sisi was a bit disappointed to hear this score.","If she hadn't had an accident with her English exam, she would definitely have scored over 400.","She might have even gotten into a very good undergraduate program.","But now, she could only go to an average school.","Forget it. As long as she could go to a university, that was enough.","Anyway, all she wanted was the diploma.","She was a college student now. It was worth noting that not many people in this family compound could get into a university.","Let alone the fact that she came from the countryside. Being able to surpass them meant she was already amazing.","Happy in her heart, Lin Sisi suddenly thought of something and asked Zhang Cuimei, who was already preparing to call people to celebrate, \"Mom, I just heard you mention Sister Si Nian. What happened to Sister Si Nian? Why did the teacher ask about her?\"","Zhang Cuimei frowned and said, \"Si Nian was also his student before. He probably just wanted to ask how she did on the exam. I don't know, so I ignored him.\"","Lin Sisi frowned and said worriedly, \"I wonder how Sister Si Nian did on the exam. We haven't heard any news from her.\"","\"Should we call and ask her?\"","Zhang Cuimei also frowned. That's right, given Si Nian's past personality, if she really did well on the exam, would she not inform them?","Could it be that she did so poorly she didn't have the face to call home?","Thinking of this possibility, Zhang Cuimei surprisingly felt an inexplicable sense of comfort.","\"Don't worry about her. She's already busy enough taking care of the kids at home, yet she still wants to take the university entrance exam. What a disgrace.\"","Si Nian used to be among the top students in the family compound and was quite proud, but no matter how capable she was, she hadn't been to school for a year. Even the No. 1 High School wouldn't accept her, so she had to settle for the ordinary No. 2 High School.","No. 2 High School historically had few good teachers, and its college admission rate was dismally low.","How could Si Nian, being there, possibly compare to Sisi at No. 1 High School?","Not to mention, she had privately paid the homeroom teacher to tutor Lin Sisi.","Si's Father heard the conversation between mother and daughter, but remained silent for a moment before saying with some pity for Si Nian, \"Don't say that. The child was also delayed by us.\"","Zhang Cuimei didn't feel guilty at all. \"It's a good thing she was delayed. Otherwise, since she's not our biological daughter, we'd still have to spend money to put her through university.\"","Si's Father wanted to say something else, but Zhang Cuimei, who now had the confidence of a daughter getting into university, interrupted him, \"Let's not talk about her. On such a great day, why do you keep bringing her up?\"","\"Sisi, later Mom will take you to buy new clothes, and tonight we'll have dinner with the family.\"","\"What are you sitting around for? Aren't you going out to notify the people in the family compound about dinner tonight?\"","\"Book a nice restaurant. Our Sisi really brought glory to us as a couple today.\"","Si's Father also felt this made sense. With their daughter's score, getting into a university within the province was definitely not a problem.","Thinking of this, Si's Father couldn't sit still anymore and went straight to the Fu family first.","When Fu Qianqian heard that Lin Sisi scored 398 points, she was so angry she couldn't even eat.","She immediately got up to call Si Nian.","Her heart was pounding, though. By now, the scores were definitely out, yet Si Nian hadn't reported the good news to her.","Did she really do poorly on the exam?","She called, but no one answered.","Fu Qianqian's heart became even more uneasy.","It's over, it's over.","Si Nian really did poorly.","She wasn't even answering the phone.","She must be absolutely devastated.","Although she was very unwilling to accept it, if she told her right now that Lin Sisi scored 398 and could get into university, would Si Nian get so angry she'd jump off a building?","Thinking of this possibility, Fu Qianqian couldn't sit still. She called in sick, claiming she had breast hyperplasia and needed to go to the hospital, then grabbed her bag and left the house.","Si's Father even asked her to go to some restaurant for dinner tonight.","Hah, she was full just from anger, why would she eat?","Fu Qianqian was about to leave with a displeased look on her face.","Fu Yang was rarely at home today. Hearing that Lin Sisi could get into university, he was also a bit stunned.","Then he saw his sister furiously making phone calls one moment, and anxiously asking for leave to rush out the next.","A trace of worry flashed in his eyes.","Could something have happened to Si Nian to make his sister make such an expression?","Lin Sisi's score was out, so Si Nian's must be out too.","Although he never doubted Si Nian's abilities, seeing his sister's behavior right now made him somewhat worried.","Could it be that Si Nian messed up the exam this time too?","Fu Yang sat there frowning, not even hearing a word of what Si's Father was saying.","They were very close to No. 2 High School here. Fu Yang was hesitating whether to go over and take a look when the phone rang.","He got up and answered the phone, only to hear his sister's screaming voice: \"Brother, something happened, something huge happened! Help—\"","The voice abruptly stopped—","Fu Yang's expression changed. He immediately grabbed his car keys and left the house without looking back.","Si's Father was in the middle of speaking, and the person just left.","His expression was very awkward, and he was a bit annoyed.","He had been talking here for ages, and not only did he not get a friendly response, but the guy actually left without even saying hello.","It was simply too much.","Mrs. Fu was also worried that something might have happened. Although she was a bit surprised to hear that Lin Sisi really got into university, she had long lost hope in Lin Sisi. Seeing her son leave, she figured it was time to discuss the divorce between the two families, so she agreed to the dinner.","While Si Nian, Zhou Yueshen, and their group were in the car, they could hear a loud speaker playing a song from far away, though they didn't know where it was coming from.","\"Sweet like honey, you smile so sweet like honey,","Like flowers blooming in the spring breeze,","Blooming in the spring breeze.","Where, oh where have I seen you before?","Your smile is so familiar,","But I can't remember for a moment...\"","Although Second Child was tone-deaf, he confidently sang along loudly: \"Sweet like honey, you smile so sweet like honey, like flowers blooming in the spring breeze, la la la la...\"","\"Little sister, come sing with me. One, two, start, sweet like honey...\"","Si Nian was so amused by him that she burst out laughing. She was just about to ask whose house was playing music so loudly when she tilted her head and saw that they had arrived at the school.","The singing was coming from inside the school.","From a distance, a red banner was hung at the school gate.","A large crowd was blocking the outside, looking up at the words on the banner.","There were also some people taking pictures with cameras.","Si Nian looked closely, and on it was an eye-catching line of large characters: Congratulations to Si Nian, a student who transferred from No. 1 High School to our Class One, Grade Twelve, for becoming the provincial top scorer in science with 685 points, and succeeding in the exams!","Si Nian's face instantly grew hot.","This, this, this was too huge!","Although she knew they would put up a banner, she didn't expect it to be this big.","Second Child curiously stretched his neck out and read it word by word: \"Congratulations to Si Nian, a student who transferred from No. 1 High School to our Class One, Grade Twelve, for becoming the science top scorer with 685 points, succeeding in the... Hey, how come this person's name is the same as Mom's?\"","Si Nian blushed and coughed, \"Keep a low profile, keep a low profile.\"","Zhou Yueshen saw it too. He tilted his head to glance at Si Nian and saw that she was actually blushing, which was rare.","It was his first time seeing it, and a trace of a smile flashed in his eyes.","With so many people, it was quite a grand display.","He spent ages just trying to find a parking spot.","Fortunately, none of these people knew who Si Nian was. As they walked past, they could still hear everyone's sighs of envy.","\"Si Nian, who is Si Nian?\"","\"How come I've never heard that our school has such an awesome person?\"","\"Didn't you see? She transferred from No. 1 High School.\"","\"Pfft, who put up this banner? Won't No. 1 High School start a fight if they see it?\"","\"But why would a student from No. 1 High School come to our school?\"","\"Who cares? Anyway, the provincial top scorer belongs to our school now, hahahaha.\"","Amidst the crowd's discussions, Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen led the kids into the school.","By now, the class was already in an uproar. The homeroom teacher was surrounded. Some students originally hadn't planned to come, but who knew that upon hearing their class produced the provincial science top scorer, they all rushed over.","Since she was from their class, it brought glory to all of them too.","Having the provincial science top scorer in their class was something they could brag about for three years once word got out.","There was even a banner at the classroom door: Old Immortal of the Constellations, With Boundless Magic, Helps Our Top Scorer Sweep Away Thousands.","The homeroom teacher was smiling so hard his eyes were invisible. He was wearing a suit and tie, and his hair was slicked back with pomade, reflecting the sunlight.","Seeing Si Nian arrive, he immediately went up to greet her.","\"Make way, make way, don't you see our science top scorer has arrived?\"","Passersby stopped in their tracks, and amidst the homeroom teacher's excessively loud shouts of \"science top scorer,\" they all turned to give Si Nian a salute of attention."]},{"number":384,"title":"Chapter 384: Chapter 383 The Reason","paragraphs":["The young homeroom teacher was smiling so hard his face scrunched up like a blooming chrysanthemum.","\"Si Nian, you're finally here! I've been waiting for you for ages.\"","\"Have you decided where to celebrate? The school can arrange it for you.\"","\"Oh, right, there's a speech on stage later. Don't be nervous. It's mainly just for you to share your experience and encourage the younger students. The principal even has a surprise for you at the end.\"","The homeroom teacher winked at her.","Si Nian paused and turned her head to look at Zhou Yueshen.","Zhou Yueshen nodded at her and said gently, \"Go ahead. I took the day off from work today to wait for you.\"","Only then did Si Nian nod and agree.","Meanwhile, Fu Yang's car had arrived at the entrance of High School No. 2.","From a distance, he could see a massive crowd. It was far too congested, making it impossible to drive through, so he had to park his car first.","With so many people around, he had no idea where Fu Qianqian had run off to. Upon receiving her call, Fu Yang had instinctively driven straight to High School No. 2, not even sure if she was actually here.","His mind had been preoccupied with worrying about Fu Qianqian's situation, so he hadn't noticed the stark contrast between the festive High School No. 2 and the deserted High School No. 1.","Today was the day the exam results were released, and the entrance to High School No. 2 was practically a sea of people.","Only now did he realize that a massive banner was strung up at High School No. 2, right above his head.","There were even reporters nearby carrying cameras to film the scene.","A continuous stream of people gathered around, all pointing at the words on the banner, buzzing with discussion and sighing in amazement.","Fu Yang instinctively looked up. In an instant, the surrounding air seemed to freeze, and the entire world went silent.","He opened his mouth but no sound came out. This man, who usually remained unfazed even if a mountain were collapsing in front of him, was now struck speechless by the glaring, massive characters on the banner.","He stood frozen in place.","Fu Qianqian popped out from who-knows-where, grabbing Fu Yang's hand and exclaiming in pleasant surprise, \"Brother! Brother, did you see that? Si Nian is the provincial top scorer in the science division! The provincial top scorer! 685 points! Oh my god, she's amazing!!!\"","Fu Qianqian danced with excitement. Seeing that Fu Yang had finally arrived, she immediately shared the good news.","Heaven knows that when she ran over to High School No. 2, she had just subconsciously glanced up and spotted the banner hanging over the main gate.","And written right on it was the name of her poor friend—the very one she had been worried might jump off a building!","Fu Qianqian thought she was still dreaming. Otherwise, how could Si Nian have become the provincial science top scorer?","Even if Si Nian had merely managed to get into a university, Fu Qianqian would have thought it was a miracle blessed by her ancestors.","After all, she had always believed that Si Nian was only slightly better at studying than she was.","Who would have thought that she would pull off such an incredible, jaw-dropping feat!","But to think she didn't even notify her about such huge, wonderful news, making her think something terrible had happened and causing her to run over here in a panic.","She never expected that instead of a scare, it would be such a massive surprise!","Seeing as she had made such a great achievement, Fu Qianqian decided not to hold it against her.","Hearing that the top scorer was going to give a speech on stage soon, she could hardly stand still.","She hurriedly dragged the still-dazed Fu Yang into High School No. 2.","Look, brother, just look at what a brilliant, dazzling pearl you've lost.","By now, the sports field was already packed with a sea of people.","High School No. 2 was open to the public today, allowing people from all schools to enter.","Word had spread that High School No. 2 had produced the provincial science top scorer, so almost everyone had rushed over to join in the excitement.","High School No. 1, which in previous years would be bustling and setting off firecrackers, had barely anyone around today.","The banner hanging at the entrance was simply too shocking—this provincial science top scorer was actually a transfer student from High School No. 1!","Let alone outsiders, even the people from High School No. 1 were curious about exactly which student this was. To think they would abandon High School No. 1 and run off to High School No. 2.","The students chattered endlessly. Some students from High School No. 1 even cursed High School No. 2 for going too far, saying it was utterly shameless of them to poach someone and then proudly flaunt it on a banner.","They believed that such an incredible student must have been deliberately poached by High School No. 2.","Their school had also produced a top scorer, but it was for the liberal arts division.","Right now, their spotlight was being completely and utterly crushed.","The students of High School No. 2 felt that their school wasn't the type to do such things, but today's banner was indeed written in an extremely exaggerated manner.","Plus, practically no student with good grades would ever give up High School No. 1 to choose High School No. 2. So, while they defended themselves, they also felt a bit guilty.","This was the most debated topic of the day, which was why quite a few reporters had shown up.","Since Si Nian was going on stage, she had dressed a bit more formally today and put on some light makeup.","First, the principal, directors, and others went on stage to give long, winded speeches, spit flying for ages, saving her for the grand finale.","Her homeroom teacher, worried she wouldn't know what to say, had prepared a script for her.","Si Nian took one look at it and felt a wave of speechless exasperation.","While she was sitting in silence, her name was called from the stage.","Deafening applause erupted.","Only then did Si Nian walk out.","Down off the stage, seated in the front row, the principal of High School No. 1 had a face as dark as the bottom of a pot, his mustache practically curling up in anger.","Beside him, the principal of the Foreign Language Elementary School was holding his granddaughter and smiling very happily.","Not minding stirring the pot, he poked right at the sore spot: \"I heard this provincial science top scorer was originally from your High School No. 1? How did she end up running over to High School No. 2?\"","The face of the High School No. 1 principal cycled through all the colors of the rainbow. He had only heard last night that High School No. 2 had produced a provincial science top scorer, and only then did he find out that this Si Nian was actually their former student.","With so many students in the school, there weren't many the principal could remember, but since Si Nian used to be the face of High School No. 1, he did have some impression of her.","Previously, for some unknown reason, she had stopped attending school, and he had even asked her homeroom teacher to visit her home and check on the situation.","But in the end, they never received a response.","Who would have thought that the very next year, she would run off to High School No. 2 and become the provincial top scorer.","This alone was enough to keep the principal awake all night in anger, turning several of his hairs white. When he was invited to High School No. 2 early this morning and saw that banner hanging up there, he nearly fainted from sheer fury.","Right now, his mouth twitched, but he couldn't utter a single word.","He believed that in those years, their school had valued Si Nian highly and focused on cultivating her.","But now High School No. 2 had stolen the limelight, and it was absolutely infuriating.","As a result, he even felt a bit of resentment towards Si Nian.","The moment Si Nian walked onto the stage, he glared over.","The noisy, clamoring crowd below the stage also fell into an instant silence.","It was truly because the bright, moving face and elegant temperament of the provincial science top scorer they had been gossiping about all morning were simply too stunning.","Bad enough that her academic performance was this outstanding, but she was actually this beautiful too? Was she going to let anyone else live?","Everyone stared blankly at Si Nian.","Si Nian coughed lightly and began to speak according to the script her homeroom teacher had given her.","After finishing, she offered her blessings and encouragement to the younger students.","At this moment, the reporters rushed forward in a flurry, aiming all their cameras at her to take pictures.","Out of nowhere, an unknown reporter suddenly asked loudly, \"Si Nian, I heard you were previously a student at High School No. 1. Why did you suddenly transfer to High School No. 2? Did something happen between you and High School No. 1? Or do you have some sort of grievance or opinion against them?\"","The moment these words were spoken, everyone snapped their heads toward the stage.","Standing behind the principal, Teacher Chen's face turned a ghastly shade of pale green.","Si Nian was silent for a moment, then calmly said, \"I don't have any objections or opinions about First High School. It's just that due to some personal reasons, the teachers at First High School were unwilling to accept me, so I came to Second High School. Second High School didn't mind my past and gave me this opportunity, for which I am very grateful to all the teachers.\"","Everyone was incredibly surprised.","It wasn't that Si Nian didn't want to go to First High School.","It was that First High School didn't want her.","They didn't even want someone this amazing; was First High School's threshold really that high?","Well, look at them now. Their school only produced a city-level top scorer in liberal arts this year, while Si Nian became the provincial top scorer in sciences.","This was truly a massive loss for them.","Hearing this, the principal of First High School immediately darkened his face and stood up. \"Why would you say that? How could our First High School not accept you? I still have some impression of you. When you were at our school before, you were considered the face of our school. When you stopped attending, I even specifically asked your homeroom teacher to visit your home and check on your situation.\"","Si Nian paused and looked at him.","Although she didn't have much memory of it, the original owner of her body had good academic grades, and someone with good grades wouldn't have a hard time at any school.","The principal couldn't be making things up either.","So she said, \"Principal, I did go to First High School first. After all, First High School is my alma mater. I absolutely do not mean to ruin First High School's reputation by saying this, but I called my homeroom teacher twice. He didn't answer once, and the other time he rejected me, which is why I chose to come to Second High School.\"","\"I don't mean to complain about you. My situation is indeed complicated, and I have no complaints that you didn't accept me.\"","As for Second High School's flashy, hate-drawing banner, it really had nothing to do with her.","Si Nian also knew that as the provincial top scorer in sciences, her every move was highly anticipated. If she said it was First High School's problem, it would cause massive trouble for First High School and ruin their school's reputation.","The words of a top scorer still held a lot of influence.","Although she had no good feelings toward that homeroom teacher, it didn't mean she would attack them because of it. So she said, \"If you don't believe me, you can ask my homeroom teacher. He knows this matter best.\"","Hearing this, the principal mostly understood.","No wonder when he asked Si Nian's former homeroom teacher this morning, the man was stammering. He had thought the other party was just unaware.","He didn't want to blame him.","He never expected that she was actually rejected.","It was their First High School that had handed the provincial top scorer over to someone else on a silver platter.","First High School seemed like a joke right now.","He glared fiercely at Teacher Chen standing in the back, his voice like ice shards: \"Teacher Chen, is what student Si said true?\"","Teacher Chen opened his mouth but couldn't say a single word.","He had thought Si Nian might do well on the exam, but he never expected her to do this well.","Early this morning, when he saw the banner, Teacher Chen knew things had blown up.","He had called the Si family wanting to ask about the situation, but the Si family just hung up on him without a word.","Now it was over; spilt milk could not be gathered.","Si Nian didn't say much more and was about to leave when the principal hurried forward to present her with the prize money.","The provincial top scorer in sciences, a scholarship of 2000, the Second High School principal's generous gesture once again pushed the atmosphere to a climax.","After all, he had used the title of the provincial top scorer to ruthlessly slap First High School's face.","The principal also felt quite embarrassed.","Si Nian was also a bit surprised.","Although in the future she had heard of some national top scorer getting a scholarship of a million or hundreds of thousands.","But she never expected that one day such a good thing would fall on her head.","When she stepped off the stage, she was dazed.","The school still had many things to attend to, so Si Nian said her goodbyes and left.","Zhou Yueshen had already booked a restaurant. The family planned to go home first to pick up the Lin family before heading to the restaurant.","She didn't know how many people Zhou Yueshen had invited. On Si Nian's side, she didn't have many relatives, and her family members had all been notified.","They would go over early to prepare.","Dinner was exactly at six in the evening.","They had also invited the principal, homeroom teacher, and others.","Seeing her step down from the stage, Fu Qianqian rushed over.","Fu Qianqian put away her envious expression, her eyes shining as she looked at Si Nian. \"Si Nian, how on earth did you manage to score so high? Oh my god, my sister is actually the provincial top scorer in sciences. This is too, too, too amazing!\"","She held Si Nian's hands. \"Before, I just felt you were a bit impressive, but I didn't expect you to be this impressive. If I had known you were this amazing, I would have studied more with you to rub off some of your exam luck. Maybe I could have gotten into college too.\"","Si Nian burst out laughing. \"I was in a rush this morning and didn't have time to notify you. It's great that you're here. Let's go to the restaurant for dinner tonight to celebrate.\"","The few little munchkins were also shocked seeing their mother's grand prestige.","They silently followed behind. When Second Child heard Fu Qianqian's words, he immediately grabbed Si Nian's other hand. He also wanted to rub off his mother's exam luck; maybe he could pass his exams too?","Fu Yang stood behind Fu Qianqian, looking at her with a complicated expression.","He seemed to have a thousand words to say, but in the end, only two words came out: \"Congratulations.\"","Si Nian was slightly taken aback, then said, \"Thank you.\"","She didn't say much more.","The relationship between the two had long been walking on thin ice.","Si Nian was no longer the person who used to follow behind him.","Fu Yang didn't speak further and turned to leave.","Fu Qianqian glanced back. At this moment, people were coming and going on the sports field, but she felt he looked like such a lonely man.","Fu Qianqian felt a bit sorry for her brother.","However, turning around to see Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen smiling and talking about something, she suddenly felt relieved.","Heh, serves him right.","As soon as Fu Yang returned home, he was notified to go to a restaurant for dinner.","His parents said they wanted to discuss the matter of their divorce.","He was silent for a moment before agreeing.","Meanwhile.","Lin Sisi was taken out by Zhang Cuimei to buy clothes and get her hair styled.","They made ample preparations.","Father Si even booked the best restaurant in the city center for her.","He said that everyone from the Si and Zhang families would come to celebrate for her.","Moreover, the Fu family had also agreed to come.","Just as the two arrived at the restaurant entrance, they noticed many cars parked outside and a large crowd of people.","There were also people decorating the restaurant.","Walking over, they found out that a certain provincial top scorer was going to celebrate at the restaurant. The second and third floors were fully booked, leaving only seats on the first floor.","Father Si had a hard time booking it, and it was only available before two o'clock; after two o'clock, the restaurant had to clear the venue.","If it weren't for the fact that other restaurants lacked prestige, Father Si wouldn't have wanted to compromise.","So they had to come during the day.","\"Isn't that Fu Yang?\" As soon as they arrived, they saw Fu Yang getting out of a car.","Lin Sisi hadn't expected Fu Yang to be here either, and her eyes lit up.","The group got out of their car.","Fu Yang was about to walk away when he heard the pleasantly surprised voices of Lin Sisi and Zhang Cuimei.","\"Xiao Fu, you came so early.\"","After all, Sisi's results were coming out today. Although the two of them had encountered an accident before, they were still people who had held a wedding and registered their marriage.","No matter how cold Fu Yang appeared on the surface, he surely cared about his daughter's grades, right?","Otherwise, why would he come over so quickly?","Thinking of this possibility, Zhang Cuimei immediately became happy.","Once her daughter's grades were out, she knew their relationship could definitely be salvaged.","Lin Sisi blushed; she had originally been worried that Fu Yang wouldn't be willing to come.","Today, dressed in casual clothes, he had lost his usual aloofness and seemed a bit more approachable.","The sunlight hit him, making his whole person radiate a dazzling glow.","He looked even more captivating.","Was this the man that someone as proud as Si Nian had chased after since childhood?","Lin Sisi's heart beat wildly as she said, \"Brother Fu Yang, you probably know my score by now, right?\"","She put on a disappointed expression. \"It is just a pity that I did not perform too well in two subjects, but it does not matter, I will work harder in the future.\"","Fu Yang glanced at her, his brows furrowing slightly.","Truth be told, he was not curious about Lin Sisi's grades at all.","If it were not for the matter of his divorce from Lin Sisi, he would not have even come over.","He was already in a bad mood today.","Then he heard Lin Sisi say, \"I wonder how Sister Si Nian did on her exam. Although I have not heard any news, with her abilities, there definitely will not be any problems. Maybe we can even get into the same university.\"","Fu Yang paused.","He looked at her weirdly and asked, \"You do not know what score Si Nian got?\"","Si Nian was the provincial top scorer in science, and she was actually worrying about this?","She scored a little over three hundred points and wanted to go to the same university as Si Nian? What kind of cosmic joke was this?","Even Fu Yang found it absurd. Where on earth did Lin Sisi get the confidence to compare herself to Si Nian?","Remembering the accident during the previous exam, a flash of disdain crossed his eyes as he looked at Lin Sisi.","Lin Sisi asked in confusion, \"Brother Fu Yang, do you know?\"","A hint of a mock smile appeared on the corner of Fu Yang's mouth. \"You should not be asking me this question.\"","He suddenly felt quite curious himself. If the Si family, who had gone to such great lengths to celebrate for Lin Sisi, found out Si Nian's score, the scene would probably be quite spectacular.","Fu Yang ignored them, turned around, and walked toward the restaurant.","Seeing his expression, Lin Sisi suddenly felt waves of unease.","Why would Fu Yang show such an expression?","Today, her teacher had notified her of her score, and she had not gone to school. She was entirely focused on following Zhang Cuimei out to buy clothes and dress up.","She really had not had the time to ask around about Si Nian's score.","Just as she was wondering whether to have Zhang Cuimei call and check the situation, people nearby suddenly came over pulling a banner. A male voice could be heard saying proudly, \"Ah, hang it up properly. This is my sister-in-law. Basking in my sister-in-law's good fortune as the provincial top scorer, we must make sure everyone passing by can see it.\"","She instinctively looked over. She recognized this man.","It was Yu Dong.","Suddenly, Lin Sisi froze in place.","Seeing that she was not moving, Zhang Cuimei frowned. \"Sisi, what are you spacing out for? Hurry up and let's go.\"","After saying that, seeing no reaction from Lin Sisi, she looked at her in confusion, only to see her head raised, staring fixedly right above, her face full of disbelief.","Confused, Zhang Cuimei followed her gaze upward. She was stunned for a moment, and then her eyes widened abruptly.","\"Congratulations to the provincial science top scorer, Class One Grade Twelve student Si Nian, for coming to our restaurant to celebrate...\"","Zhang Cuimei thought she had misread it and looked over again.","But there, dazzlingly displayed above, were the two large words: \"Si Nian\"!","There was a little accident today; I wrote, deleted, and rewrote, so it delayed the update time. I am very sorry.","This chapter is a large chapter of nearly five thousand words."]},{"number":385,"title":"Chapter 385: Crematorium","paragraphs":["The gifts in Zhang Cuimei's hands fell to the ground with a clatter, scattering everywhere.","The scene before her eyes seemed like a nightmare.","A nightmare enough to shake the very souls of the mother and daughter.","Si's Father found a place to park the car and walked over.","Seeing that the two hadn't gone in yet, he frowned. \"What are you standing around for? The guests are waiting!\"","After saying that, he subconsciously glanced up at the staff who were decorating the restaurant.","He felt a bit displeased.","They hadn't even left yet, and the restaurant was already starting to set things up.","They really didn't take them as guests seriously at all.","He wondered what kind of VIP guest had such grand style to make the most luxurious restaurant in the city center put on such a huge display.","Just as Si's Father was thinking this, he saw a banner being hung up.","When he saw the words \"Provincial Science Top Scorer\", he was instantly startled.","It was actually the provincial science top scorer; no wonder the restaurant was making such a big fuss.","Right, the college entrance examination results came out today, so the top scorer must have been announced too. But to think the provincial science top scorer was actually around here—it was truly a first for him to see.","The most impressive one Si's Father had ever seen was only a school top scorer.","And that was many years ago, basking in the glory of the Fu family, with Fu Yang's results.","He didn't expect to have such good luck today to run into the provincial science top scorer.","Si's Father felt a wave of envy as he thought about it. He couldn't blame them for having such a grand style; if it were him, he would definitely throw a massive banquet and announce it to the whole world too.","He wondered whose child was so impress...","Si's Father's envious gaze came to an abrupt halt the moment he saw the two familiar characters that followed.","\"Si... Si Si Nian?\"","His gaze shifted from blank to utterly shocked, his pupils trembling.","He stared blankly at the large characters on the banner.","His face was written all over with disbelief.","\"Si, Si Nian, is it really Nian Nian?!\" Si's Father's voice lost control as he spoke.","Zhang Cuimei was snapped back to reality by his shocked voice and immediately retorted, \"How is that possible!\"","\"No, impossible, how could it be her? Impossible, it must just be someone with the same name. How could she be the provincial science top scorer?\"","\"If she really became the provincial science top scorer, wouldn't she tell us?\"","\"Such a huge matter, there's no way we wouldn't know!\"","Zhang Cuimei said this while shaking her head, but her cracking voice and panicked expression made her words completely unconvincing.","Lin Sisi was bumped by someone unknown, abruptly snapping her out of the scene before her.","Suddenly her entire body went weak, and she almost collapsed onto the ground.","The scene before her was truly hard for her to accept, causing waves of dizziness in her brain.","How she wished that what was before her was just a dream, a nightmare.","But the tightening of her heart and the overwhelming sense of fear surfaced with absolute clarity.","The smug words she had just said in front of Fu Yang now felt like slaps, striking heavily across her face.","One after another, it hurt so much that her features almost twisted.","Zhang Cuimei was saying it might be someone with the same name, but that didn't comfort Lin Sisi in the slightest.","If that person Yu Dong wasn't standing there, she might have been able to console herself like that.","But who else could make Yu Dong call out \"Sister-in-law\" other than Si Nian?","In her previous life, she didn't have much of an impression of Yu Dong, only remembering that he would occasionally follow by Zhou Yueshen's side.","Because she disliked Zhou Yueshen and hated those children, Yu Dong didn't have a good impression of her either; the way he looked at her was always cold.","But now, he was proudly calling Si Nian \"Sister-in-law,\" putting up decorations to celebrate for her.","Who else could it be, if not Si Nian.","The family of three from the Si family stood frozen in place, unable to move for a long time.","The news before them was like a massive mountain pressing down heavily upon them, making it almost impossible to breathe.","Meanwhile, inside the restaurant.","Watching the staff hurrying to decorate the interior of the restaurant, the people from the Si and Zhang families, along with those called over from the family compound, were getting restless.","\"What's going on? Why haven't the Si couple arrived yet?\"","\"The guests have arrived, but the hosts are nowhere to be seen. How bizarre.\"","\"Forget it, forget it. Lin Sisi has finally seen the light at the end of the tunnel. It's a good thing she can go to college; they probably have a lot to take care of.\"","\"I heard they're clearing the place out at two o'clock. I'm worried the restaurant will kick us out when the time comes.\"","\"Who exactly is it, putting on such a huge show?\"","At this time, Zhou Yueshen and Si Nian also hurried over early to help.","Because the invited guests would head straight to the hotel, Zhou Yueshen had his sons wait at home for the Lin family, so they came over ahead of time.","Si Nian originally thought it would just be a family meal, at most including people from the school.","So she hadn't paid it much mind.","It wasn't until Zhou Yueshen said he wanted to come check out the restaurant that she realized this man had actually booked the entire place.","She stared at Zhou Yueshen in disbelief, at a loss for words.","She stood stunned for a few seconds.","She had just received the two thousand yuan prize money today, and she almost dropped it on the ground from shock.","She had previously heard that when Fu Qianqian's work unit came here to eat, a single table cost nearly fifty.","With Zhou Yueshen booking the whole place, how much money would that cost?","Besides, in Si Nian's memory, neither she nor Zhou Yueshen had many relatives.","Something that should have been settled with two or three tables—did it really require booking the whole venue?","Seeing her stare at him blankly, Zhou Yueshen lightly tugged at his collar to loosen it. He was still quite unaccustomed to wearing a dress shirt.","But today was an important day.","He turned his head to glance at her and asked, \"What's wrong?\"","Si Nian opened her mouth and asked slowly, \"Do we have a lot of relatives?\"","She had been to Yu Dong's family's restaurant; during the three days of her exams, she had both lunch and dinner there.","She remembered it was a very large restaurant.","Equivalent to a future five-star hotel.","A wave of dizziness washed over Si Nian.","Zhou Yueshen stayed silent for two seconds, then reached out and gently pressed her hand. \"Not many relatives, just some good friends and long-term business partners.\"","After saying that, he hesitated for a moment. \"Nian Nian, did you not want me to throw such a big event?\"","Actually, he had just casually invited people, but he didn't expect to know quite so many.","For such a big occasion, if he didn't invite them now, they would likely come knocking on his door complaining about it later.","He had forgotten to ask Si Nian what she wanted.","Maybe she just wanted to keep a low profile.","Zhou Yueshen frowned, wondering if it was still in time to call back and tell those people not to come.","Si Nian shook her head. It wasn't that she didn't want to; she simply felt heartache over the money.","Although having a celebratory meal was the right thing to do.","But right now, it felt more like hosting a wedding banquet.","The main thing was that she had only just found out and had no mental preparation whatsoever.","Zhou Yueshen added, \"If you don't want to, I'll have Yu Dong notify them not to come. He originally wanted to use your name to throw a massive free celebration anyway.\"","As soon as he finished speaking and was about to look at Si Nian, her hands suddenly gripped his. Zhou Yueshen froze slightly, turned his head, and heard her speak solemnly while looking at him with shining eyes: \"Yu Dong is right, such a good thing deserves a grand celebration. Let's hurry over.\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"......\"","The couple's car drove straight to the restaurant.","Si Nian's smile was brighter than the midday sun, and Zhou Yueshen cast strange glances at her from time to time.","Did he say something just now?","Why hadn't the corners of her mouth come down at all?","It wasn't that the two of them didn't want to bring the children, but Zhou Yueshen was afraid that they would be too busy here to take care of them.","So they simply left them all at home, planning to pick them up when it was time to eat.","As soon as they arrived at the restaurant, they saw a prominent banner and festive lanterns at the entrance. Those who didn't know better might have thought someone was getting married.","Passersby also gathered around to watch, causing the couple to miss the Si family of three still standing blankly at the door as their car brushed past.","Seeing them arrive, Yu Dong hurried forward to greet them and said with full confidence, \"Boss, see? You can rest assured leaving this to me. Is this banner big enough? If not, I'll have someone remake it. The tables upstairs are all set, thirty tables in total. It doesn't matter if it's not enough; the downstairs will be cleared out after two o'clock. Sunflower seeds, drinks, and everything else are all ready. I stayed up all night last night having people prepare this. How about it? I'm a good brother, right?\"","Zhou Yueshen ignored his boasting and instead looked at Si Nian. \"What do you think?\"","Si Nian observed carefully for a moment and nodded in great satisfaction. \"Not bad, not bad. Xiao Yu, having you around is truly your sister-in-law's blessing.\"","Yu Dong was completely baffled. Was it his illusion, or was his sister-in-law looking at him with an exceptionally kind and gentle gaze today?","Hearing this, Zhou Yueshen didn't say anything.","\"Let's go inside and take a look.\"","Si Nian acknowledged and followed him.","After taking two steps, she stepped back and said, \"By the way, Qianqian is coming later too. She said the food at your place is delicious and has been thinking about it. Help me entertain her well. I'm counting on you.\"","Yu Dong instantly shivered, the exhaustion of staying up all night vanishing in a flash. He smiled sweeter than a flower and started working even more desperately.","Si Nian hadn't expected Zhou Yueshen to plan for them to eat here last night, let alone decorate it so well.","It really gave them a lot of face.","More importantly, they didn't have to spend any money.","Having the boss's son as a friend was truly great.","But don't worry, since Dongzi let her take such advantage of him today, she would definitely cook him a good meal next time.","The two entered the door and happened to bump into the Si family and a group from the family compound waiting for the meal to start in the lobby.","Sweeping a glance over, there were still four or five tables set up.","Almost all the familiar faces from the family compound were there.","Everyone was currently waiting anxiously for Si's Father, Mother Si, and their family to arrive, occasionally staring at the door.","Who would have thought that instead of waiting for the Si family, they ended up waiting for Si Nian.","Instantly, the whole group quieted down.","Mrs. Fu was also talking with Father Fu. Seeing everyone quiet down, she couldn't help but look toward the two of them as well.","Seeing Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen, she was slightly stunned.","Then she frowned.","Could Zhang Cuimei have deliberately called Si Nian and her husband over too?","After that kind of thing happened with Lin Sisi, she still asked Si Nian to come to her daughter's college acceptance banquet.","It was really a bit too much.","She frowned, feeling more and more that the Si family were truly not decent people.","How could she have been so intent on sending her son into a fire pit back then?","It seemed that no matter what happened today, this marriage had to be annulled.","Fu Yang also paused when he saw the two of them.","He didn't say anything.","Instead, Zhang Cuimei's younger sister, Zhang Xiaoyun, sneered when she saw Si Nian.","\"Oh, isn't this Si Nian? Are you also here for our Sisi's college acceptance banquet?\"","Si Nian was also taken aback looking at this family.","She really hadn't expected the Si family to be here too.","But looking at this scene, could Lin Sisi have also gotten a good score?","She really was the female lead. Even after serving a year in prison, she could still get into college.","Everyone looked at Si Nian strangely.","Their memories of Si Nian were now basically stuck on the fact that she wasn't biological and her conflicts with Lin Sisi.","They hadn't really paid attention to her situation.","Seeing her actually show up now, they were also somewhat surprised.","They thought that given the situation between the two families, she shouldn't have come. Earlier, when Zhang Cuimei was seriously ill, it was said she didn't even go to take a look.","At this moment, the looks they gave her were somewhat disdainful.","Especially the people from the Zhang family's side, who disliked her exceptionally.","Si Nian, however, said calmly, \"I'm not here for the banquet.\"","Zhang Xiaoyun sneered, \"I figured as much. Why would my sister invite you to the banquet? You harmed them so miserably before; how do you have the nerve to show up here now?\"","Hearing this, everyone also felt it made sense. After all, they had raised her for over a decade. Even though Lin Sisi had done wrong, it was indeed too much.","\"She's not here to crash the party, is she?\"","\"I heard she didn't even take the college entrance exam before and can't even go to college. Sisi is still the amazing one, getting into college right after coming back and bringing honor to the Si family's ancestors. It's really a pity that the Si family raised her like that from a young age.\"","\"Exactly.\"","\"Si Nian, Auntie advises you, the past is in the past. When you were in our family compound before, everyone treated you pretty well, and we don't want you to keep making a fuss like this.\"","\"Yes, it hasn't been easy for Sisi either. We know you might not be resigned to just marrying into the countryside like this, but Sisi also lived a hard life in the countryside for over a decade. Just let her go.\"","\"Even if you make a fuss, it won't change the fact that she got into college.\"","Seeing so many people speaking up for her, Zhang Xiaoyun immediately got carried away with pride.","\"Did you hear that? Hurry up and leave, we don't welcome you.\"","Si Nian's face darkened with exasperation. Did these people have persecution paranoia?","She only felt that enemies truly met on a narrow path.","She could bump into the Si family no matter where she went.","Her good mood ruined in an instant, she said, \"Who said I'm here for Lin Sisi's banquet? It's not like only you can come to this restaurant. Did the Si family book the whole place?\"","Zhang Xiaoyun said smugly, \"Heh, although we didn't book the whole place, my brother-in-law is the only one who reserved seats here right now, and the place will be cleared out after two o'clock. If you didn't call to reserve in advance, naturally there are no seats for you.\"","\"If you really want to eat, when my sister and brother-in-law arrive later, I could put in a good word for you and let you two stay.\"","Zhou Yueshen also disliked the Si family. Seeing them being aggressive and suppressing Si Nian with faces full of disdain, he frowned slightly, put his arm around Si Nian, and said in a deep voice, \"Don't trouble yourself. We don't need it.\"","Zhang Xiaoyun thought the two were flying into a rage out of humiliation and gloated, \"Haha, don't be angry. I just pity you.\"","\"Oh right, I heard from my sister that you also took the college entrance exam. What was your score? Seeing the two of you all alone, don't tell me you didn't get into college. It was truly a waste of my sister and brother-in-law spending money to raise you from a young age. I didn't expect you to fail the college entrance exam two years in a row. It's truly too disappointing.\"","\"Although our Sisi came from the countryside, she still scored 398 on the exam this time, just shy of four hundred. And I heard that was even when she underperformed.\"","Zhang Xiaoyun showed off complacently.","Fu Yang was drinking tea and choked a bit upon hearing this.","After hearing this, Si Nian was taken aback at first, but then she burst into laughter. \"398?\"","She originally thought it was some amazing score, given how the Si family went to such great lengths.","In the end, it was only 398?","In the future, this score might not even get you into a second-tier university.","Si Nian thought Lin Sisi had scored incredibly well for Zhang Xiaoyun to be so smug.","Who would have thought it was 398?","She didn't usually smile, but at this moment, she really couldn't hold it back.","Zhang Xiaoyun didn't notice anything amiss and continued to gloat, \"Well? It doesn't feel good to be overshadowed, does it?\"","Si Nian nodded in agreement, \"No, it really doesn't.\"","To be compared to someone like her was nothing short of an insult.","Zhang Xiaoyun hadn't expected her to be so agreeable. She froze for a second, but just as she was about to speak, she saw Si's Father hurrying over.","She immediately stood up and shouted excitedly, \"Sister, brother-in-law, you're finally here! Look, Si Nian and that country husband of hers are here too. I think they look quite pathetic. Arriving at this hour, they probably couldn't even book a table. Why don't you have someone bring out two extra chairs for them?\""]},{"number":386,"title":"Chapter 386","paragraphs":["She emphasized the words \"country man\" through gritted teeth.","Si's Father hadn't expected to see Si Nian and her husband as soon as he walked in.","His expression was still a bit dazed.","After the initial shock, he zoned out for a moment, then felt a pang of regret, but ultimately, it all melted into pleasant surprise and disbelief.","He had been a little uncertain at first and wanted to rush over to ask what exactly was going on.","But he hadn't expected to bump into Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen right here.","If they could come here, then the matter must be true.","Si's Father's face was full of pleasant surprise.","After all, Si Nian being able to get into such an impressive school was all because he had been willing to spend money to cultivate her for over a decade.","Although it was a pity that she wasn't his biological daughter, what was the point of saying that now?","A large part of the credit for Si Nian achieving this honor belonged to him.","That was enough.","Both daughters had gotten into university, and one was even the provincial top scorer in science.","Si's Father couldn't even begin to imagine how much benefit and glory this would bring him.","He didn't even notice Zhang Xiaoyun's words. He anxiously stepped forward, looking at Si Nian with excitement, his eyes filled with an unprecedented affection and gentleness.","\"Niannian, you're here too. Why didn't you tell Dad earlier? I would have gone to pick you up.\"","\"You child, such a big deal, why didn't you notify us sooner?\"","\"It just so happens that Sisi is also celebrating here today, and everyone is here. We might as well celebrate together. A double blessing!\"","A double blessing?","The crowd was slightly stunned.","What did this mean?","Did this mean that Si Nian had also tested well?","Hearing this, Zhang Xiaoyun's heart skipped a beat.","She then frowned, extremely dissatisfied with her brother-in-law's behavior.","Previously, because he and her sister were clamoring for a divorce, their Zhang family had lost a lot of face.","Now, he was actually acting so chummy with Si Nian, this adopted daughter.","Tagging Si Nian along to celebrate at Sisi's celebration party, on what grounds?!","He really didn't put their Zhang family in his eyes at all.","Zhang Xiaoyun said angrily, \"No, I won't agree to this!\"","\"She's not even your biological child, and she's already married. Why should the Si family help her celebrate? Besides, she can't even compare to Sisi. What does she have to celebrate? Does she have no shame?\"","\"I was wondering why some people inexplicably appeared here. So this was their plan all along. Just how jealous are they of our Sisi's success to be so shameless?\"","Zhang Xiaoyun's words grew uglier by the second.","Si's Father finally snapped out of it. Looking up, he saw the people around him also frowning at him, echoing Zhang Xiaoyun in disapproval.","\"Yeah, Old Si, you're going a bit too far. It's too unfair to Sisi.\"","\"Isn't this a celebration for Sisi?\"","\"We know you're nostalgic, but no matter what, Si Nian is just an adopted daughter.\"","Si Nian wasn't angry at all. Waiting for them to finish, she smiled and said, \"Everyone is right, just an adopted daughter. Based on what happened before, Aunt Zhang and Uncle Si had already decided to completely sever ties with me. We have absolutely no relationship now. We just greet each other when we meet, so you don't need to be too polite to us.\"","\"Don't worry, we won't interrupt your celebration. We're going upstairs to eat.\"","After saying that, she tugged on Zhou Yueshen, and the two turned around and walked toward the second floor.","Zhang Xiaoyun finally felt comfortable. \"At least you know your place today.\"","If they really made a scene and caused the Zhang family to lose face, she wouldn't hold back.","Watching the two walking toward the second floor, everyone shook their heads.","\"Didn't they say the second floor was booked out and no one was allowed up? They're still going up to eat?\"","\"They probably don't know.\"","Although everyone said this, no one spoke up to remind them.","Mother Fu couldn't stand it anymore. Just as she was about to speak, Fu Yang beside her poured her a cup of tea, stopping her from talking.","\"Just watch.\"","Mother Fu was slightly stunned.","Si's Father realized what was happening and his face turned green. He hurriedly shouted, \"This is the Si family, not the Zhang family. It's not the place for a Zhang family member to speak.\"","After saying that, ignoring the astonished expressions of the crowd, he hurriedly chased after them.","\"Niannian, Niannian, son-in-law, don't go just yet.\"","\"I didn't mean it like that. Dad truly wants to celebrate for you!\"","Si Nian stopped in her tracks. Si's Father was instantly pleasantly surprised and hurried forward, saying, \"I know you suffered grievances because of Sisi before, but don't worry. In the future, as long as you want, I will still treat you as my biological daughter. You can come back whenever you want.\"","Zhang Cuimei and Lin Sisi, the mother and daughter who had just walked in, instantly turned pale upon hearing this.","Zhang Xiaoyun was also in disbelief and let out a scream. \"What, what did you say! Brother-in-law, what do you mean? You would rather have that adopted daughter than your own biological daughter, is that right?\"","The Zhang family members also stood up angrily, looking like they were about to start a fight.","However, at this moment, Si's Father didn't pay them any mind. Right now, to him, restoring his previously good relationship with Si Nian was the most important thing.","What was the Zhang family? He had long been unable to tolerate it and wanted a divorce.","If it weren't for the fact that they had leverage on him and he didn't dare make a big fuss, Si's Father wouldn't be so suffocated.","Now that he finally had such a good opportunity, the Zhang family was still looking for trouble. Were they trying to get him killed?","Zhang Cuimei was already having trouble processing everything. Compared to the shock of Si Nian becoming the provincial top scorer in science, her husband's attitude now chilled her to the bone.","He had only just found out, and it wasn't even completely confirmed yet, but her husband immediately sought to build a good relationship with Si Nian, casually abandoning her Sisi.","Then what did all of Sisi's hard work over this long period amount to?","Yes, Si Nian tested well, she admitted that, but this couldn't negate Sisi's efforts either.","Sisi was originally from the countryside. She had suffered so much there, and the education was so poor. For her to get into university was already incredible.","Si Nian merely had all the advantages of time, place, and people.","If such an education had been given to her Sisi from a young age, her Sisi wouldn't necessarily be worse than her.","Her husband was simply going too far.","This was practically making their mother-daughter duo unable to hold their heads up in front of all their relatives and friends.","Si Nian was annoyed. She interrupted the family's bickering with a deep voice, \"Everyone, feel free to argue or fight as you please, but please don't drag me and my husband into it. And Uncle Si, I call you Uncle out of respect for an elder, but that doesn't mean you can drag me into your family disputes time and time again. Since you have already given up on me, I will no longer be your daughter. I have my own biological parents, and they treat me very well. I hope you won't say such misleading things in the future.\"","\"Your Si family and my Lin family have long since settled our accounts. If you don't disturb my life, I will absolutely not appear in front of you. Let's part amicably.\"","After saying that, she couldn't be bothered to look at Si's Father's colorful expressions and went up to the second floor with Zhou Yueshen.","Seeing that they had actually gone up and no one stopped them, everyone was a bit surprised.","But right now, more attention was still on Si's Father.","Everyone looked at him in confusion and said, \"Si Nian is right. Both families have already agreed, and the household registrations have been moved. You are now two separate families, owing nothing to each other. Brother Si, you shouldn't force it anymore; it's not good for either Si Nian or Sisi.\"","\"Yeah, yeah, why are you trying to please her? Isn't she just a country bumpkin? She was lucky enough to live a good life for over a decade, she should be satisfied enough. You should just leave her alone.\"","The Zhang family members interrupted with dissatisfaction.","Si's Father's face turned green and purple. His relationship with Si Nian was already bad, and these people were desperately adding fuel to the fire here. He was almost dizzy with anger.","\"Yeah, everyone is still waiting to eat,\" Zhang Xiaoyun said disdainfully.","\"If it weren't for my sister, I wouldn't have even come.\"","These words instantly ignited the anger in Si's Father's heart. His fury erupted in a flash, and like a provoked beast, he roared uncontrollably.","\"Eat my ass, get the hell out of here!\"","After saying that, he was about to flip the table.","Everyone was terrified and stood up one after another to stop him.","They couldn't understand why he was throwing such a huge fit.","Zhang Xiaoyun screamed, her face pale with fright, and hid behind her husband.","She never knew Si's Father was such a terrifying person.","With such a scene, no one was in the mood to eat anymore, and they all stood up to take their leave.","This college entrance banquet was completely ruined.","Father Fu and Mother Fu exchanged a glance. They had originally planned to talk about their son's divorce, but Si's Father was acting too strangely today.","Given the current situation, it was simply outrageous. Even if they wanted to talk, they wouldn't know how to start.","So they also stood up and prepared to leave.","The group walked out of the restaurant angrily. They had wasted their time and suffered a fit of rage, wishing they could beat Si's Father up.","But some people wondered what exactly had happened. Si's Father wasn't like this before; he had never shown so much care for his adopted daughter, Si Nian, in the past.","Why did he suddenly change like this, as if Si Nian were his biological daughter?","Everyone was originally confused, but when they walked to the door, they all froze.","Father Fu and Mother Fu followed them out. Seeing everyone staring blankly above their heads, they also looked over in confusion.","The next second, they were stunned.","At this moment, even the two of them, who were used to seeing all kinds of grand scenes, had a look of shock in their eyes.","At this moment, they understood why Si's Father had been acting so bizarrely.","It turned out that Si Nian had actually become the top scorer in the provincial science college entrance examination.","The shock of the people around them was beyond words; they could hardly believe their eyes.","Especially the Zhang family members walking at the front, who were absolutely dumbfounded and in disbelief.","The surrounding air seemed to freeze, so oppressive that it was hard to breathe, and everyone's face turned ashen.","Lin Sisi looked at this scene, clutching her chest, almost fainting from anger.","She lost, completely defeated by Si Nian, becoming a loser trampled under her feet.","In this life, just like the previous one, she would forever live under Si Nian's shadow.","Obviously, she had already tried so hard.","In this life, she had worked so hard, but why did she still lose so miserably, so pathetically?","Lin Sisi's vision went black, and she actually fainted from sheer anger.","The scene fell into chaos.","Si Nian didn't take the Si family seriously at all, so she just treated this incident as a minor interlude. However, Yu Dong didn't expect that the people who came were from the Si family, and he felt very guilty at the moment. Because table reservations were managed by specific staff, he generally wouldn't ask much about such trivial matters.","Anyway, he had reminded the store manager under him to clear the place after two o'clock.","Who knew it would coincidentally be Lin Sisi's celebration banquet.","The people from the Si family actually mocked his sister-in-law. Were these people blind? Didn't they see the banner hanging at the door?","No matter how capable Lin Sisi was, could she compare to his sister-in-law?","It was really bad luck. Yu Dong threw a huge fit, not only replacing all the tables and chairs but also disinfecting the place.","He said he was afraid the bad luck from the Si family would affect everyone's mood.","Let's not mention what expressions those people had when they went back.","Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen saw that Yu Dong had prepared everything he needed to. This restaurant was often booked for banquets and the like, so they were very experienced. The drinks were all of the best quality, which gave them plenty of face.","It wasn't that Si Nian was reluctant to spend money; she just didn't want to be high-profile from the beginning. However, since everyone valued her so much, she couldn't be stingy. She immediately took out her own two thousand yuan and gave Yu Dong a big red envelope, thanking him for his hard work.","How could Yu Dong dare to accept it? The boss hadn't even settled the score with him for letting the Si family in yet.","He couldn't even imagine how difficult his days ahead would be.","Why would he accept money at this time? He immediately found an excuse and ran away.","Mother Lin's family arrived at the Zhou family's house at four o'clock in the afternoon.","Hearing that their daughter had become the provincial science top scorer, they were all very happy and put on their best clothes.","The two brothers, Lin Feng and Lin Yu, also came. Over the past year, the two guys had grown a lot taller, but they were quite lean and their skin was very dark. In contrast, it made Eldest Child and Second Child, who had stayed in the city for a year, look somewhat pale.","The children were exceptionally happy, running around the yard.","The Fang family.","In a dimly lit room, Fang Bowen lay on the bed, his face pale.","He felt his body alternating between hot and cold, and it was extremely uncomfortable.","Originally, his mother told him to do his homework properly at home, but he felt so awful that he couldn't help but sleep for a while, only to feel even worse when he woke up.","He was awakened by bursts of cheerful laughter.","As soon as he heard it, he knew it was the voices of Second Child and the others.","He groggily climbed up, ran to the window, and pulled open the curtains.","The dazzling sunlight instantly shone on him. He squinted his eyes at the glare and dazedly looked toward the yard next door.","He happened to see Second Child talking and laughing with a few unfamiliar peers. Whenever he brought people home, he would first take them on a tour to introduce the layout of his house, showing off the dogs, rabbits, and fish he raised.","Fang Bowen knew the whole routine by now.","He leaned against the window, trying hard to open his eyes wide as he watched Second Child lead those kids through the door. Next, they would definitely go to the rooms and the study in his house.","He didn't know what day it was today, for Teacher Si's house to be so lively.","No, in his memory, Teacher Si's house was always very lively.","The desolate one was his own home.","Fang Bowen's eyes carried an envy that he didn't even notice himself. He really wanted to ask, but he didn't dare to go; his mother didn't let him play with Second Child and the others.","Just as he was thinking, he heard Zhou Zedong's little-adult-like voice, \"Alright Xiaohan, stop messing around. Mom called and told us to go over with Little Uncle and the others.\"","Seeing that they were about to leave, Fang Bowen immediately stood up straight.","Where were they going?","He also saw his classmates, Li Youcai and the others.","Fang Bowen hurriedly ran downstairs and looked in the direction of the main gate.","Besides Eldest Child, Second Child, and the group of kids, there were also many adults, people from the Jiang family, and people he didn't know.","They were dressed festively, as if there was some joyous occasion, looking extremely lively.","Zhou Zedong was just about to get into the car when he suddenly heard two muffled coughs."]},{"number":387,"title":"Chapter 387: Chapter 386: Celebration Banquet","paragraphs":["He paused his steps and tilted his head, looking toward the direction of the sound.","It was the Fang family.","Was Fang Bowen still sick?","He hesitated for a moment, then turned and walked into the house.","\"Uncle, wait for me a moment.\"","Everyone looked at him in confusion as he ran into the house. Soon, he came back out holding some things and knocked on the Fang family's door.","On the other side, Fang Hui had been assigned to do an interview, but because she was staring blankly, she had actually let the person leave.","Now she was being reprimanded by her superior.","\"Our daily newspaper didn't even manage to book an interview in the first place. We finally saw the person, so why were you zoning out? Why didn't you chase after her for the interview?\"","\"That's the provincial science top scorer, the biggest dark horse this year. If we write about it in the paper, it will definitely sell out!\"","\"Fang Hui, I only gave you this great opportunity because you often accompanied me to social events before and performed well. Don't be ungrateful.\"","Fang Hui's face looked awful. To fight for work opportunities, she had indeed been attending social events everywhere lately, working from dawn to dusk.","When a top scorer emerges, a newspaper agency definitely has to interview them; after all, the college entrance examination is a highly anticipated major event every year.","At first, she thought it would just be an ordinary school top scorer. She never imagined it would be the provincial science top scorer, right here in their city center, so close by.","Her superior immediately assigned this important task to her.","Coupled with the grudge between First High and Second High, this matter was already highly controversial.","But they had also made ample preparations.","However, she never expected the main character to be Si Nian.","Fang Hui originally thought it was just someone with the same first and last name; she never expected it to actually be her.","When Si Nian went on stage to give a speech, she was completely dumbfounded.","It was unbelievable.","So much so that she only reacted after the person had left, let alone making her swallow her pride to interview Si Nian.","Wouldn't that be like asking for her life?","But if she didn't get the interview now, the higher-ups would give her trouble. She got a severe scolding as soon as she returned, and she was told to figure out a way to visit and interview her herself.","She had to write a report about the provincial science top scorer.","Fang Hui was furious, feeling more and more frustrated the more she thought about it.","Looking for Si Nian was impossible; she couldn't swallow her pride to do that.","But if she didn't look for her, she could look for people she knew.","Didn't they want her to write about the experiences and insights of the top scorer Si Nian? Then don't blame her for writing whatever she wanted.","\"Brother, what are you giving to Fang Bowen?\"","In the car, Second Child asked his brother curiously.","Zhou Zedong sat in the front holding his sister and ignored him.","Jiang Jiu leaned on the front seat and said, \"Is Fang Bowen sick? I saw him coughing his lungs out the other day.\"","Second Child also said, \"Fang Bowen is so weak. He gets sick all the time. I heard last time he got sick just from eating expired bread. When I was little, I ate moldy rice and didn't get sick.\"","He even looked a bit smug.","Beside them, Lin Feng and Lin Yu asked curiously, \"Who is Fang Bowen? Is he your friend? Aren't you going to invite him along?\"","Hearing this, the children exchanged glances.","Then they shook their heads and said, \"We don't dare. Fang Bowen's mother doesn't let him play with us.\"","\"Right, Fang Bowen is really good at playing chess.\"","\"And Fang Bowen is a genius. He started first grade when he was four.\"","\"He also knows English, he's better than me.\"","Lin Feng and Lin Yu were astounded to hear that there was such an amazing child in the world.","In the countryside, they only ever met kids with good grades.","They had never heard of anyone starting first grade at four and fourth grade at seven.","It was simply incredible.","Li Youcai scoffed, crossing his arms. \"What's so great about that? If I started learning at four, I might be even better than him.\"","Li Youcai was naturally prone to looking down on this and that.","Unless someone completely crushed him, he would never admit they were better than him.","Zhou Zedong had completely crushed him, so he didn't dare say anything about Zhou Zedong now.","But now some Fang Bowen guy popped up.","He immediately repeated history, showing disdain for Fang Bowen.","The few adults couldn't get a word in, but hearing that city kids were so amazing, they couldn't help but feel a bit envious.","Mother Lin subconsciously looked at her two sons and sure enough, saw them looking at Li Youcai and the others with shining eyes. Compared to their bright and neat appearances, her two children seemed a bit out of place even though they were wearing their best clothes.","Mother Lin suddenly felt a pang of heartache.","But she also knew her own capabilities; how could she compare to others?","However, she remembered that a year ago, Eldest Child and Second Child were also dark and skinny, but now a year had passed, and the two children had changed a lot.","Their auras were completely different.","And they had so many children as friends.","Sure enough, the change in environment had helped the two children shed their inferiority complexes and rustic vibes.","Inside the restaurant, quite a few guests had already arrived in succession.","However, Si Nian didn't know most of them; they were from Zhou Yueshen's side. There were business people, people from the breeding farm, and clients. Zhou Yueshen took her around to introduce them one by one.","Everyone was very envious that Zhou Yueshen had found such an amazing wife. She was beautiful and the provincial science top scorer; it was simply too impressive.","Originally, Zhou Yueshen was just an ordinary breeding farm boss.","But because of Si Nian's existence, his entire status had elevated significantly in the eyes of others.","He used to be Director Zhou, but now he was Boss Zhou.","Si Nian smiled and greeted them. Soon, she saw her brother driving over, leading a group of little kids.","As soon as the group of children arrived at the restaurant, they excitedly touched things here and looked around there.","\"Look, this is the banner put up for my mom.\"","\"My mom is the provincial science top scorer.\"","Second Child was the first to point at the banner hung over the restaurant's entrance, speaking proudly.","Everyone looked on with envy.","\"When I grow up, I'm going to be a top scorer too,\" Second Child said with lofty ambition.","However, after he finished speaking and wanted to see everyone's admiring gazes, the group of people had already followed his brother away.","Second Child: \"...\"","More and more guests arrived, and luxury cars drove over one after another.","Even reporters, who got the news from who knows where, ran over and started taking pictures here and there on the sidelines.","Seeing that it was almost time, Yu Dong brought out firecrackers and set them off.","The crackling sounds echoed through the entire street.","A group of children surrounded him, spinning around happily.","\"Uncle Yu, Uncle Yu, we want to play too.\"","Yu Dong said, \"No, this isn't something kids can play with.\"","After saying that, he carried the firecrackers to set them off on the other side.","The group of children followed behind him in a line, like chicks following a mother hen.","Zhou Zedong didn't follow his younger brother; instead, he followed his father to greet guests at the door.","\"This is my son, Zhou Zedong.\"","When Zhou Yueshen introduced him to others, he would nod politely and say, \"Hello, Uncle. I'll take you to the second floor.\"","Chu Xiang'er watched him with admiration from the side and said, \"Classmate Zhou Zedong is so amazing, he can even help entertain guests.\"","Li Youcai crossed his arms, the envy and jealousy practically dripping from his face: \"Tch, what's so amazing about that? I can do it too.\"","Chu Xiang'er ignored him. It wasn't until Zhou Zedong returned from leading people upstairs that she ran up to him and asked, \"Classmate Zhou Zedong, is there anything I can help you with?\"","Zhou Zedong shook his head, his face as calm as ever. \"No need, you guys go play.\"","After saying that, he saw the hesitant figures of Brother Chen and the other two at the door.","Zhou Zedong paused, then walked over.","Brother Chen and the other two were wearing new clothes, looking completely out of their element.","\"U-um, this is the gift we prepared for Auntie. Brother Dong, please give it to her for us. We won't go in.\"","Although they were invited over for a meal, how could the few of them dare to enter such a grand restaurant?","They had never even been inside a state-run restaurant, let alone a luxurious one like this.","It just looked so high-end and intimidating.","Even though they had tried their best to change into their best new clothes before coming, as soon as they arrived and saw others wearing suits and ties and driving luxury cars, a wave of inferiority washed over them.","They felt completely out of place here.","They had prepared a small basket of fruit candies and pastries for Si Nian, and now they felt even more embarrassed.","Zhou Zedong glanced at it and frowned.","\"You bought it, you give it to her yourself.\"","The few of them exchanged glances, their expressions troubled.","Zhou Zedong really didn't know how to entertain them. Dealing with adults was fine, but he just had nothing to talk about with people his own age.","So, he grabbed his younger brother, who was running all over the place, and told him to take the group upstairs.","Second Child saw Brother Chen and the others and acted very familiar with them.","\"Little uncle, look! They are the ones who sell pancakes at the gate of our school. They are delicious, and they are also my brother's good friends.\"","Lin Feng and Lin Yu were even more impressed.","Going to first grade at four years old was one thing, but starting a business at around the same age as them was something else.","The two children just felt that city people were truly amazing and formidable.","They looked at Brother Chen and the others with admiration and awe.","Si Nian came downstairs and ran into this group of children.","Seeing her two younger brothers, she paused and stepped forward, saying, \"Xiao Feng, Xiao Yu, hurry upstairs, it's time to eat.\"","\"Xiao Han, stop leading everyone running around too.\"","Zhou Zehan stuck out his tongue.","Si Nian led the group of children upstairs. There were quite a few of them, so she arranged for them to sit at one table, figuring a group of kids would have more to talk about.","She was really busy and was called away again shortly after.","Second Child was sitting with his younger sister when he heard someone beside him speaking to him.","\"Huh? Are you Classmate Zhou Zedong's younger brother? What's your name? Is she your younger sister?\"","Wang Yuanyuan was wearing a beautiful princess dress, sitting nearby. She was originally sitting with her mother, but her mother insisted on sending her over here, saying she should sit at the same table as Classmate Zhou Zedong. She didn't see Zhou Zedong, but she saw Li Youcai and the others, which made her a bit scared.","Just as she was feeling helpless and isolated, Zhou Zehan brought his sister over and sat down.","She only found out he was Zhou Zedong's brother after hearing Teacher Si speak, and she was amazed! The little sister he was holding in his arms was even more adorable. Seeing the little girl looking at her curiously and blinking, her childlike affection sprouted uncontrollably.","Chu Xiang'er, who was nearby, saw her talking to Zhou Zehan and also walked over. With wide eyes, she said, \"This is Classmate Zhou Zedong's younger sister, her name is Yaoyao.\"","After saying that, she reached out to touch Yaoyao.","Yaoyao shrank her head back, not liking being touched by people she wasn't familiar with.","Chu Xiang'er felt a bit wronged. \"Sister Yaoyao, don't you remember me? I just went to your house to play a moment ago. Let me hold you, okay?\"","Yaoyao chewed on her finger, turned her head, and hugged her own brother.","Zhou Zehan said quite proudly, \"My sister only lets me hold her.\"","At this moment, Zhou Zedong came upstairs.","Yaoyao immediately let go and ran over to hug Zhou Zedong.","Zhou Zehan: ...","The slap in the face couldn't have come any faster.","Seeing Zhou Zedong arrive, everyone gathered around him to talk.","Wang Yuanyuan, who had just mustered the courage to speak but got no response, sat there awkwardly.","At this moment, another child was brought over.","She was still wearing a Taekwondo training uniform, with sweat on her forehead.","Looking at the table full of little kids, she said disdainfully, \"No way, Uncle, I want to go to the adults' table.\"","Yu Dong, who was holding her hand, had a massive headache. \"You don't know any of those adults, it would be so awkward sitting together. Listen to your uncle, sit with Xiao Dong and Xiao Han. They are very easy to get along with.\"","Yu Dong also hadn't expected that while he was busy, his sister would suddenly call and ask him to pick up his niece from her Taekwondo class. It was all because they heard that his sister-in-law was holding a celebration party here, so they had him bring her over, saying she could rub off some good luck for her exams.","Yu Dong had no choice; he couldn't just leave his niece in the classroom, so he had to pick her up.","But he was very busy and had no way to take care of her.","Thinking that Eldest Child and Second Child were quite good at taking care of people, he hurriedly brought her upstairs.","He didn't expect this kid to be so unwilling.","Even though his niece was a child herself, the thing she hated most was little kids.","She said they loved to cry and make a fuss, which made her hands itch just looking at them.","It was bad enough that she had a fierce personality, but she had also been learning all sorts of Taekwondo and Judo since she was young. At such a tender age, she was already invincible across her entire kindergarten.","He coaxed her again, \"Weren't you curious about who your uncle's boss is? It's the father of these two. The sons of a man who can make your uncle call him boss surely can't be that bad, right?\"","The girl looked at him suspiciously. \"Isn't it just because you're too stupid?\"","Yu Dong: \"...\"","\"Forget it, I'll just go over there.\"","After saying that, she walked over and pulled out a chair to sit down herself.","Yu Dong wiped his sweat and, under the curious gazes of the group of children, said, \"Xiao Dong, Xiao Han, this is my niece, Qi He.\"","Second Child: \"Penguin?\"","He immediately received a cold glare.","Yu Dong instantly broke out in a cold sweat.","Heaven knows his niece absolutely hated it when people called her Penguin.","The last person who called her that had already been beaten into the hospital.","Second Child didn't notice anything wrong at all. He slid off the table, ran up to Qi He, and smiled, \"Your name is so cute, Penguin.\"","Qi He's eyebrows twitched. \"I am not called Penguin.\"","Li Youcai and Chu Xiang'er frowned as they looked at her. \"Qi He, why are you here too?\"","Second Child asked curiously, \"You guys know each other?\"","Li Youcai and Chu Xiang'er said, \"She used to be in the same kindergarten as us. She's very fierce and loves to fight. A lot of kids have been beaten up by her.\"","After Chu Xiang'er finished speaking, she frowned and said, \"You absolutely must not play with her.\"","Li Youcai added, \"She hates it most when people call her Penguin. She hits really hard.\"","Second Child: \"Ah, but didn't Uncle Yu say her name is Penguin?\"","Yu Dong hastily waved his hands and shook his head; he definitely did not say that!","Jiang Jiu carefully tugged at Second Child's sleeve and whispered, \"Second brother, it's Qi He, not Penguin.\"","Li Youcai gloated, \"She is a Taekwondo master and hits very hard. It's not too late for you to run now.\"","Second Child widened his eyes. \"Taekwondo? Is it very powerful? Is it great for fighting? Then Qi He, can you teach me?\"","Everyone: \"...\""]},{"number":388,"title":"Chapter 388: Investment","paragraphs":["The little girl cracked her knuckles, \"You're so annoying, go away.\"","Zhou Zedong also scolded, \"Little Han, sit down.\"","Zhou Zehan fell silent at once. He carefully glanced at his brother's expression, and seeing him frowning at him, he quickly covered his mouth and obediently walked to the side to sit down.","Li Youcai even laughed at him, \"If you don't leave, be careful you don't get beaten up. Besides, she transferred schools a long time ago; she can't teach you.\"","Qi He's family was very rich, and it was said they had moved to a big city to live a long time ago.","She probably only came back for the exams.","Qi He sneered coldly, \"I don't just beat up any idiot. If I'm going to hit someone, it's going to be the kind of bully who picks on the weak and fears the strong.\"","Li Youcai choked on his words.","When he was little, he thought Qi He was as pretty as a doll. In his ignorant youth, he had cornered Qi He and demanded she be his girlfriend, only to get severely beaten up.","To make matters worse, his family's background couldn't compare to hers, so even if his family wanted to seek justice for him, they couldn't.","Since then, he would always take a detour whenever he saw her.","After that, he stopped liking that type of girl. It was gentle and considerate girls like Xiang'er who were truly likable.","He wanted to say something but was afraid of getting hit. However, letting everyone know he was afraid of a girl would be too embarrassing, so he just gave a solitary cold snort and stopped talking.","For a moment, the group of children all quieted down.","Soon, the food was served.","After all, they were just children, and their attention was immediately diverted.","Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen didn't eat much; Zhou Yueshen spent the entire time entertaining the guests.","Aside from relatives and friends, many prominent bosses from the business world came, and even quite a few retired bigwigs.","Division Commander Jiang sat at the same table as Si Nian and the others, only then realizing that his neighbors actually had this kind of background.","The chiefs of the military region had all come, and they were all old acquaintances.","Director Li was also there.","No one expected that after looking around, they would all know each other. At this moment, they couldn't help but laugh at the coincidence.","\"So he used to be in the Northwest. I was just saying, if there was such a figure, how could I not know about him,\" Division Commander Jiang laughed.","\"Lao Jiang, you probably don't know his name, but you must have heard of the Three Heroes of the Northwest Military Region. Our Little Zhou was the captain of the Three Heroes team.\"","Division Commander Jiang was even more surprised, \"Then why didn't he stay in the military?\"","Logically speaking, with such abilities, if he had stayed in the military, he would definitely have achieved great things in the future.","He might even be more formidable than his own most promising student.","The other person also said with pity, \"Life is unpredictable, what a shame.\"","Director Li laughed, \"What's there to pity? In this life, happiness is the most important thing. Now that Little Zhou has such a happy family and can make money, what does he need those vanity things for?\"","Everyone also felt this made sense. In fact, many people didn't live very well after retiring from the military.","Not to mention someone like him who could build everything from scratch.","Boss Wang said, \"We recently opened a branch company in Jing City and even invited Little Zhou to buy shares. Does anyone want to invest?\"","The others rolled their eyes at him, \"Give it a rest, you profiteer. As soon as we meet, you want to squander the coffin money of us old men. Aren't you afraid of karma?\"","\"But if Little Zhou is willing to invest, could it be that Old Wang actually has good judgment this time?\"","After everyone expressed their disdain for Boss Wang, they also felt that Zhou Yueshen wouldn't invest blindly.","It must have been carefully considered.","\"Little Zhou, what do you think? Are you trying to expand your business all the way to Jing City?\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded slightly, \"In my early years, a friend of mine did business in Jing City, and I invested a few times. Jing City is developing rapidly. This time, Boss Wang also caught the scent of an opportunity and is opening a department store branch there, so I plan to invest and give it a try.\"","The breeding farm was now at a decent scale. Zhou Yueshen had hired a new assistant who had managed a company before and was quite experienced. All the positions were fully staffed.","He no longer needed to put all his energy into the breeding farm.","The returns from investing at the right time in an emerging trend would be massive.","Of course, it was also relatively dangerous.","Everyone exchanged glances and began to hesitate.","Hearing this, Si Nian tilted her head and glanced at Zhou Yueshen.","So Zhou Yueshen wasn't just running a breeding farm; he was also making investments on the side.","Zhou Yueshen would often slip her some pocket money, resulting in her rarely needing to withdraw money herself.","Money in this era was just too valuable; no matter how much she spent, it never seemed to run out.","She wondered where Zhou Yueshen kept all his investment money. He probably didn't use this bankbook.","Just as she was thinking, Zhou Yueshen placed a piece of pork rib into her bowl.","She tilted her head to look at the man.","Zhou Yueshen asked gently, \"Are you tired? Let's go home after we finish eating.\"","Having entertained so many people today, Si Nian was undoubtedly tired.","Si Nian wasn't tired at all; her mind was completely occupied with thoughts of how he was going to invest.","Hearing the man's caring words now, she suddenly felt guilty, coughed lightly, and said okay.","After dinner, everyone said their goodbyes and went home.","Only then did Si Nian have the time to look for the children.","Seeing Second Child and Jiang Jiu using boxes to pack leftover chicken legs and rice, she was a bit surprised. \"Little Han, what are you doing?\"","Zhou Zehan turned around and said, \"Mom, I'm saving this for Fang Bowen. I heard from my brother today that he caught a cold, so I want to pack some to take back and eat with him.\"","Si Nian was slightly taken aback. Fang Bowen was sick?","She frowned, \"Aren't you afraid his mom will see and get angry again?\"","Second Child gave a sly smile, \"Mom, don't worry. Fang Bowen's mom comes home very late every day. I'll secretly give it to him. I have experience.\"","After saying that, he put the box into his schoolbag.","Jiang Jiu also chimed in, \"Fang Bowen's mom isn't fierce to me at all. Before, when she met me, she even told me to go play with Fang Bowen.\"","Of course, he definitely wouldn't go by himself.","Si Nian generally understood what Fang Hui was thinking. On one hand, she hated her, but on the other hand, she wanted to curry favor with the Jiang family.","That was probably why she treated the children so differently.","Since the children all said so, if she tried to stop them, they would probably be unhappy.","If Jiang Jiu was the one delivering it, Fang Hui shouldn't have anything to say.","Lately, Fang Hui seemed to rarely be home and had even hired a nanny.","However, she still hadn't seen much of that child.","The Lin family stayed at the Zhou house.","Si Nian asked them to stay and play for a few days before going back, spending her days dragging her parents and two younger brothers out to buy clothes.","Second Child pestered her, saying, \"Mom, I want to learn Taekwondo too.\"","Si Nian didn't know where he had learned that word, but considering Second Child's boundless, unvented energy and high athletic talent, it would be good for him to learn some self-defense skills.","\"Then we have to ask your dad first.\"","Although Zhou Yueshen would definitely agree, Si Nian felt they still needed to ask for his opinion.","Lin Feng and Lin Yu were also very curious, but living in the countryside, they definitely didn't have access to such things.","They could only suppress their envious thoughts."]},{"number":389,"title":"Chapter 389: Made the Newspaper","paragraphs":["Si Nian's gaze swept over the two children before looking at Lin's mother. Mom, in the second half of the year, bring Little Feng and Little Yu to study in the city. I've already spoken to our director and principal; when the time comes, their tuition will be waived.","Lin's mother was surprised. How could that work? Although studying is very important, coming all the way here is just too far.","As soon as she said that, she felt a bit of regret. Glancing at the two children whose expressions went from pleasant surprise to disappointment, a wave of guilt washed over her.","Since coming to the city, Lin's mother had noticed the way her two children kept looking up to the eldest and second eldest children. It wasn't that she hadn't seen it.","She had just deliberately ignored it.","Although the family's income had stabilized and they had some savings, facing the unknown big city still brought a lot of pressure to the Lin family.","Si Nian frowned, recalling the plot of the novel. The two children originally wanted very much to attend school in the city, but because of their parents' poor financial conditions, they had hesitated. Lin Sisi had instigated trouble behind the scenes, making the two children feel that their parents didn't care about them, which even led to a cold war.","They only ended up coming because Lin Sisi said she was willing to pay for their tuition.","Therefore, the two children treated Lin Sisi like their benefactor.","But because of this, the already unwealthy family's situation worsened. Lin Sisi only paid the tuition, but the real expenses were the two children's basic living needs. The aristocratic primary school's accommodation and meals were very expensive, forcing her brother to work from dawn to dusk to earn money just to maintain his two younger brothers' livelihoods.","This eventually led to an accident, causing the parents' hair to turn white overnight.","The two children's ultimate achievements didn't disappoint anyone, but their hearts were filled only with gratitude toward Lin Sisi. They followed Lin Sisi's every lead, and upon graduation, they chose to stay in the city to help her. Yet, they forgot that the ones who truly supported them moving forward were their biological parents and brother.","Si Nian absolutely did not want her two younger brothers to become people like that.","She said, Mom, our family's current income is enough to support Little Feng and Little Yu studying in the city. Zhou Yueshen told me that the rural breeding farm will be completely handed over to Village Head Huo, and the business you do at home can be transferred to the city. There's more foot traffic here, so it's more profitable. Besides, Zhou Yueshen's breeding farm is here, which can help provide you with sales channels. You definitely won't earn any less than you do at home.","Little Feng and Little Yu are smart kids. They can receive a better education in the city. I've already found the opportunity for you. It's not my place to interfere with your decision, but Little Feng and Little Yu definitely want to go to school here. You and dad should think about it.","After speaking, she looked at her two younger brothers.","Lin Feng and Lin Yu both looked at them nervously.","Not daring to interrupt.","Although the opportunity was right in front of them, and who wouldn't want to stay in this bustling metropolis, they also knew their family's situation very well. Going bankrupt just to attend a good school was something they didn't even dare to think about.","Then they heard Si Nian say, Little Feng, Little Yu, this opportunity didn't come easily, and I hope you get a better education. Mom and Dad's hesitation isn't because they don't care about you. They are just thinking long-term, and everything they do is for your sake. It's not just about this little bit of tuition; your future living expenses, food, and clothing will all require a huge amount of money. You need to understand them.","Lin Feng and Lin Yu were slightly stunned.","But they quickly came back to their senses and nodded in shame, We understand, sis.","They had been overwhelmed by joy, losing their reason. Hearing their sister say that the tuition could be waived, they excitedly thought they could attend such a good school.","But they had forgotten that besides tuition, there were expenses for food, clothing, where to live, and how to survive. They had forgotten all of that.","All of these required money.","Mom, don't put yourself in a difficult position. It's okay if we go to school at home.","Right, even in the village, I will work very hard. Just like my sister, I'll become a top scholar for you.","The two children tugged at Lin's mother and said.","Lin's mother was moved to tears. Good children, you are both mommy's good children.","After speaking, she looked at Si Nian and said gratefully, Niannian, thank you.","Lin's mother was also worried that her indecisive nature would make her two sons resent her.","But after her daughter said this, she instantly figured things out.","Her daughter was right; being submissive and timid wouldn't accomplish anything great.","Even if not for herself, she had to let her two children walk on a brand-new, bright path.","Si Nian was also a bit worried. It wouldn't be long before she had to report to Beijing. She was hesitating whether to temporarily suspend her schooling or to go to school first.","After all, Yaoyao was still young. Although she could be sent to a preschool class, Zhou Yueshen didn't have time to take care of her.","Unfortunately, this place was too far from Beijing.","Before she could figure out this problem, a new one arose.","Just after seeing off the Lin family, Si Nian heard that she was in the newspaper.","However, what was written wasn't anything good. It was about her identity as the true and false wealthy daughter, claiming she sat back and enjoyed everything the Si family had provided, only to turn around and look down on her adoptive parents after turning her life around. It also said that for her own sake, she didn't hesitate to marry an old man with three children to be a stepmother. In short, it was all very ugly and mocking language.","It was written extensively at the very top of the daily newspaper.","There was also a conspicuous large headline: The Dirty Past Beneath the Brilliant Surface of No. 2 High School's Provincial Science Top Scholar, Si Nian.","Si Nian: ?","Dirty my ass.","Although she didn't know which newspaper agency wrote it, she was very clear that anyone who knew these things must be related to the Si family.","It made sense; when she celebrated, she didn't invite the Si family.","She hadn't planned to have any contact with them in the first place.","She never expected to be written off as an ungrateful wretch.","Originally, Si Nian didn't read the newspaper.","But Grandpa Jiang next door had the habit of reading the newspaper. When he saw it, he was very angry and hurried over to find her, which was how Si Nian found out.","Grandma Jiang was also very angry, scolding, Whose newspaper agency is this, writing such nonsense! It's too much!","Si Nian also found it strange, as she hadn't offended these newspaper agencies.","Could it be that Lin Sisi, out of exasperation, found someone to leak these things?","This matter caused quite a stir. Originally, over the past few days, many people had come to her door to give gifts and wanted to hire Si Nian as a tutor. As soon as this newspaper came out, no one came anymore.","The people in the tube-shaped apartment building began looking at her with strange eyes again.","Grandma Jiang looked at Si Nian with concern, Aren't you angry?","Si Nian smiled and said, What's there to be angry about?","She turned around and sued the newspaper agency.","The good thing about daily newspapers in this day and age was that it would be clearly marked on them who published them.","The four words Sunshine Daily were impressively written on it.","She didn't know whose company it was, and Si Nian didn't plan to investigate exactly who it was.","Taking up the weapon of the law was the only way to protect herself.","Did the other party think she would be scared? They really overthought it. The cyberbullying of the future was much more terrifying than this. She had seen plenty of it; what was this in comparison?","Never mind the rest, but saying she bullied the true wealthy daughter, Lin Sisi, and calling her heartless and ungrateful?","This could not be tolerated.","Even in this era, the pressure of public opinion was immense.","The other party was truly vicious, actually using this method to ruin her reputation.","Moreover, she herself was the provincial top science scholar. If things blew up, it might even affect her university admission when the time came.","They were trying to destroy her future!","Captain Li was furious when he found out about this. Since he had personally handled the cases involving Lin Sisi and Si Nian, he felt it was absolutely outrageous for a newspaper to indiscriminately smear her reputation like this.","Sunshine Daily had surpassed its sales targets just two days after the issue was published. Fang Hui had even earned a bonus and was just getting ready to head out and celebrate when the police suddenly showed up.","The officers stated that they were suspected of spreading rumors and defamation.","Completely bewildered, the entire group was hauled off to the police station."]},{"number":390,"title":"Chapter 390: The Mysterious Man","paragraphs":["The principal of No. 2 High School was also very angry when he learned about this incident.","Everyone could see what kind of person Si Nian was.","How could she be as hateful as the newspaper wrote?","The principal immediately contacted the newspaper to ask about the situation. Although there were some newspapers these days that would write bad things to attract attention, Si Nian was the provincial top scorer in science, a newly famous figure.","They shouldn't have dared to write so exaggeratedly.","He even suspected that someone was playing tricks behind the scenes.","Could it be that No. 1 High School was still holding a grudge against Si Nian for coming to their school, and them showing it off?","Otherwise, apart from No. 1 High School having the ability to find a newspaper to smear Si Nian, ordinary people shouldn't dare to do so.","Originally, the principal was worried that something might happen, so he hurriedly called Si Nian to ask about her situation.","Who knew he would hear that she went to the police station to sue the Sunshine Newspaper.","The principal immediately rushed over with the director.","No matter the reason, he would protect his student.","Zhou Yueshen heard about this from Yu Dong in the afternoon and hurried home.","When he got home, he heard that Si Nian had already gone to the police station to report the case.","Although he knew Si Nian was very independent and strong—otherwise she wouldn't have chosen to report it immediately upon seeing the newspaper—the more she didn't need to rely on him, the more useless he felt.","The children were all at home, very worried.","Although they didn't read newspapers, they had also heard about this.","It was such a joyous event just a few days ago, how could it be spread so terribly by others?","But Si Nian didn't take them with her, so they could only stay at home.","Seeing Zhou Yueshen return, the Second Child threw himself over, hugged his thigh, and cried, \"Dad, someone is bad, they scolded Mom.\"","\"Mom is not that kind of person at all.\"","Zhou Yueshen had already heard about this. Frowning tightly, he patted his shoulder: \"Dad knows. You and your brother stay home and look after your sister. I'll go pick up your mom.\"","The Second Child wiped his tears, feeling very angry and wronged.","Why would such a good person like Mom be bullied? It was really too much.","He must become a police officer in the future and catch all these bad guys.","After speaking, Zhou Yueshen took the car keys and went out again.","\"Big brother, I really want to go with Dad.\"","Zhou Zedong looked at his father's departing back and withdrew his gaze, \"Alright, with Dad there, Mom will definitely be fine.\"","After speaking, he walked into the kitchen.","The Second Child followed eagerly: \"Big brother, what are you doing?\"","Zhou Zedong didn't look at him, continuing to wash the rice and busy himself: \"Cooking. Once the food is ready, Mom and Dad can eat when they come back.\"","The Second Child's eyes lit up: \"Yeah, then I'll help you.\"","\"No need, go buy some groceries for me, we don't have enough vegetables at home.\"","After speaking, he took out fifty cents and handed it to him.","The Second Child's eyes lit up. Fifty cents, wouldn't the rest be...","His beautiful thoughts were shattered by Zhou Zedong before they could finish, \"Remember to return the change to me.\"","The Second Child: .....","\"Big brother is so stingy.\"","Zhou Zehan complained while carrying the vegetable basket to buy groceries.","Just as he finished buying and returned, he saw a strange man standing by the road, wearing a black suit, a hat, and glasses.","He couldn't help but take a glance. It was such a hot day, why was someone still wearing a coat?","With just that glance, the other party looked over at him.","The other party paused for a second, then asked, \"Little friend, excuse me, is Old East Street here?\"","Zhou Zehan came back to his senses and pointed at the sign behind him, \"Uncle, you're so silly, isn't it written on the sign behind you?\"","The man chuckled softly, \"Oh yes, my eyesight is bad, I didn't see it. Do you live in here too?\"","The Second Child frowned. He looked the man up and down. The man was wearing a suit and a watch, looking very wealthy. Compared to the foul-mouthed human traffickers from last time, it was a world of difference.","And the man in front of him was very cultured and gentle.","That suit was the same as the one his dad bought before, the one his mom bought for him. The Second Child had secretly opened it to look; one piece cost seventy or eighty yuan, much more expensive than his clothes.","Could it be that the threshold for human traffickers was so high now?","He blinked and didn't answer the man's question, but instead asked back, \"Uncle, why are you asking this?\"","The man smiled and nodded, \"I just want to ask you if the Fang family is inside.\"","\"I'm here to find my family.\"","The Second Child was slightly stunned: \"The Fang family?\"","He said in surprise: \"Could it be that you are Fang Bowen's dad?\"","The man paused and said, \"Yes, you know my Bowen?\"","The Second Child immediately turned his little face serious: \"Uncle, if you are Fang Bowen's dad, then you should quickly go see him. He's going to die of illness, coughing every day.\"","\"Aunt Fang is so bad, she's not good to him at all. She locks him up at home alone and doesn't let him play with us.\"","Last time he and Jiang Jiu brought food to Fang Bowen, they saw that Fang Bowen had lost weight.","He looked just as weak as when he fainted before.","Although he didn't interact much with Fang Bowen, he always felt that Fang Bowen was so pitiful.","The man's brow furrowed, \"Is that so? Please trouble yourself to lead the way for me, little friend.\"","......","At the police station.","The editor-in-chief who wrote this article for the newspaper and the reporter were both brought to the police station to await questioning.","Fang Hui sat to the side, completely dazed.","She didn't understand how she ended up in the station.","Captain Li placed the newspaper in front of the group and asked in a deep voice, \"Who wrote this article?\"","Everyone looked at each other. Although they already had guesses, they were still shocked at this moment.","They all looked towards the editor-in-chief.","The editor-in-chief's eyes immediately tightened, and he hurriedly said, \"Although I wrote and published it, the person who did the interview was Fang Hui. I wrote it based on the content of her interview.\"","After speaking, his eyes turned cold. He originally thought he had gotten a highly sensational report that could give their newspaper a huge boost in sales.","Who would have thought that something would go wrong in just two days.","He was both angry and afraid. \"Fang Hui, didn't you say that the content of these interviews was true? Why would the police say we are framing and spreading rumors?\"","He was also surprised when he saw Fang Hui's interview content at the time, but Fang Hui was certain it was correct, saying it was said by Si Nian's relatives, and many people knew about these things, so he wrote it out.","Who would have thought they would be sued at the police station.","Fang Hui's face was alternately pale and green.","At this time, Si Nian came over.","She saw Fang Hui, whose face didn't look very good, at a glance.","It really made Si Nian pause for a moment, because she truly didn't expect it to be her.","Seeing her now, she remembered that someone seemed to have mentioned before that Fang Hui worked at a newspaper.","But although there was some friction between the two of them, neither usually caused trouble for the other, and they had always lived in peace.","How much hatred and resentment did Fang Hui have to write about her like this?","No matter what, she definitely couldn't escape involvement in this matter."]},{"number":391,"title":"Chapter 391: Fang Hui Arrested","paragraphs":["Although some unpleasant things had happened before, Si Nian had never really bothered to argue with her. Even when Fang Hui couldn't bring herself to apologize, Si Nian didn't say anything.","But this time, she had truly gone too far.","How could Si Nian possibly continue to tolerate it?","\"Sis—ahem, Comrade Si Nian, these are the people who fabricated that article. What do you plan to do? Settle it privately or...\"","Si Nian withdrew her gaze. \"Settle it privately?\"","She sneered. \"How is that possible? They've completely ruined my reputation. If I stay silent and settle it privately, everyone will believe I'm really that kind of person.\"","Captain Li nodded in agreement. \"That makes sense. So, what's your plan?\"","\"Of course, I'm going to take their newspaper to court, demand a public apology and compensation, and send the culprit who maliciously slandered me and caused severe consequences to prison for proper reform. Let society teach her how to behave!\"","As soon as these words came out, the faces of the newspaper staff turned pale.","If this matter was indeed false, then their spreading of rumors would be undeniable proof.","But they never expected it to escalate to the court, to such an exaggerated extent.","The editor-in-chief immediately became anxious. \"Th-this, Comrade Si, is it? We also got this information from an interview. It has nothing to do with us!\"","Si Nian looked at him. He was a middle-aged man, currently staring at her with a look of terror. Si Nian glanced at Fang Hui, whose face was pale, and said coldly, \"An interview? So your interviews consist of indiscriminately smearing someone in the newspaper, spreading rumors, and selling them in large quantities? You used my reputation as the provincial science top scorer to make a fortune, which constitutes the illegal use of another person's name for profit. This is already a crime, and you're telling me it has nothing to do with you?\"","\"I don't care what others told you, but the ones who illegally profited from this are you, and none of you can escape.\"","\"Before harming others, at least go learn some law first, right, Miss Fang?\"","Captain Li was surprised. \"You two know each other?\"","Si Nian said, \"This Miss Fang lives right next door to my house. We had some friction before. She came to make trouble for my family because of the swine fever incident, only to find out she was in the wrong. She still hasn't apologized.\"","\"I didn't bother to argue with her, but I didn't expect her to come knocking on my door again. It's truly a narrow path for enemies.\"","Fang Hui's face turned green and white at her words. \"Y-you don't be too aggressive, Si Nian. Yes, last time was a misunderstanding, but this time, I didn't do it on purpose either. These interview contents are absolutely true, no rumors at all. If you are really as open and honest as you say, why would your relatives say such things about you?\"","Si Nian stroked her chin. \"My relatives? Which relatives? If you don't say, how do I know if you're just making things up?\"","Fang Hui snorted coldly. \"Nonsense, of course it's from the family compound, the relatives of the Si family. Do you dare say you're not the adopted daughter of the Si family? The people on your mother's side told me all about your past. You were cultivated by the Si family with a lot of money since you were young, but now that you're successful, you cast your adoptive parents aside, not even inviting them to your celebration party. Isn't such ungrateful behavior too much? Am I wrong?\"","\"You even deliberately held the celebration party in the same restaurant as the biological daughter of the Si family, intentionally suppressing her, mocking her, and driving her to faint.\"","\"But you forgot that your achievements today originally belonged to her!\"","Fang Hui accused angrily. She had always felt that Si Nian was a very domineering person, but she didn't expect her to treat her family like this too. It was simply too much, too disgusting.","After hearing this, Si Nian couldn't help but look at Fang Hui in astonishment. \"I made Lin Sisi faint from anger?\"","Fang Hui sneered. \"Of course, your behavior is so shameful!\"","Si Nian: \"Such a good thing actually happened!\"","Fang Hui: \"......\"","Everyone: \"......\"","\"Captain Li, did you hear that? She admitted it herself. Doesn't this prove that our newspaper didn't write nonsense?\"","If Captain Li didn't know what had happened before, he would have thought Si Nian was going too far right now.","Seeing her heartless attitude, he couldn't help but cough, using his fist to hide the smile at the corner of his mouth, and said sternly, \"What does Lin Sisi fainting from anger have to do with her? It's just that she's not as skilled. Her own tolerance is too poor, why blame others? It's really inappropriate for you to exaggerate this and blame it on Sis—Comrade Si.\"","Fang Hui: \"? But she obviously deliberately provoked Lin Sisi, causing the accident. How can we not blame her?\"","\"The Si family raised her for so many years, pouring their hearts and blood into cultivating her. Not only did she not repay their kindness, but she also did such a thing. This is extremely malicious behavior!\"","Si Nian shook her head speechlessly. \"You mean, because I became the provincial science top scorer, I have to hide it quietly and not let Lin Sisi see it, right? And if she sees it and faints from anger, it means I deliberately showed off and provoked her? Miss Fang is truly worthy of being a paparazzi, you really know how to make things up.\"","Fang Hui gritted her teeth in anger. \"You!\"","She actually called her a sneaky paparazzi. This was simply an insult to her.","Captain Li nodded in agreement. \"Exactly, this is a great and joyous event. What does it have to do with anyone else if she fainted from being provoked? Who can she blame if she didn't do well on the exam? Your newspaper is also strange, blaming someone else for doing too well?\"","Fang Hui hurriedly said, \"Of course, there's more than that. Her relatives know what she did before.\"","Si Nian said, \"Sorry, Miss Fang, I cut ties with the Si family a long time ago. As for the reason, it's very simple. The Si family personally sent me to the countryside to get married for the sake of their biological daughter.\"","She paused for two seconds and continued, \"And this marriage arrangement was originally agreed to by Lin Sisi herself. But after she found out she was the biological daughter of the Si family, she regretted it, stole the man's bride price, and together with the Si family forced me to marry into the Zhou family. That's why I became a stepmother at such a young age, not because of the disgusting reason you mentioned, that I was willing to be a stepmother for profit. The people in the family compound also know about this, and this is the reason why we cut ties.\"","\"As for the relative you mentioned, she should also know about this. What, didn't she tell you these key points? She only focused on speaking ill of me? Let me guess, this person is either from the Si family or a relative from the Zhang family, right? Could it be my adoptive mother's sister, Zhang Xiaoyun? She's disliked me for a long time, after all, her daughter can't compare to me, and Lin Sisi was also overshadowed by me. She's always been unable to hold her head high in front of me...\"","Fang Hui's face was full of shock.","Looking at her expression, Si Nian knew she guessed right.","It really was Zhang Xiaoyun.","Captain Li snorted coldly. \"I was the one who handled the case of Lin Sisi stealing the three thousand yuan bride price. She was sent to prison for a year because of it. I thought she would improve, but I didn't expect a dog can't change its habit of eating shit.\"","\"Miss Fang, as a police officer, I am much clearer on these matters than you are. The entire family compound knows how the Si family, terrified that Comrade Si would refuse to leave and cause their biological daughter to suffer, forced her to marry down into a rural village. Hah, now that they see she has become the top scorer in the university entrance exams, they regret it and have resorted to smearing her name. And you people, without bothering to get the facts straight and without a shred of evidence, published these claims in the daily newspaper and sold them to the masses. Comrade Si is absolutely right. Your actions already constitute a crime, and we have the full authority to arrest you and bring you to justice.\""]},{"number":392,"title":"Chapter 392: Summer Vacation","paragraphs":["Fang Hui's face instantly lost its color, turning as white as a sheet.","In this moment, she finally felt genuine panic.","If she really went to jail, she would be completely ruined.","Yes, she had always disliked Si Nian and felt aggrieved this time, so she remembered the people from the apartment building who went to apologize to Si Nian and ran into her adoptive parents' family.","The people from the apartment building had just casually mentioned that her adoptive parents were very pretentious, that they actually had a bad relationship with Si Nian, and that Si Nian didn't care about them at all. Fang Hui happened to overhear this and got an idea.","She thought she could go do an interview and maybe get some useful information.","She happened to run into the Zhang family, who had attended Lin Sisi's celebration banquet that day, and took the opportunity to interview them.","Hearing that she was a reporter, the other party hid nothing and told her everything.","No one in the Zhang family refuted anything; they even said that what Si Nian did was known to everyone in the family courtyard.","Combined with Fang Hui's own prejudiced impression of Si Nian, she didn't think there was anything wrong with it.","So she gave the interview content to the editor-in-chief, which resulted in this article.","Actually, she just wanted to teach Si Nian a lesson in passing, to make her less arrogant and smug in the future.","But she forgot that Si Nian's status as the provincial top scorer in science was already attractive enough. Plus, it hadn't been long since the scores were released, so once their newspaper went on sale, it was bought in large quantities and quickly broke sales records.","She thought that with such a big fuss, Si Nian would be too ashamed to face anyone.","Who knew that she would turn around and sue them right to the police station.","And the investigators could even testify for her.","Meanwhile, her simple interview had become evidence of framing and spreading rumors about others!","Such decisive measures caught even Fang Hui completely off guard.","She was instantly beaten and caught unprepared.","She hadn't even fully recovered from this incident, and now she was going to jail?","No, how could this be possible!","Fang Hui shrieked, losing her composure: You can't blame me for this. Her relatives said it. You can't push all the blame onto me!","Si Nian nodded and said, You're right. Those relatives did say it, but you are the one who actually spread it and profited illegally. What does it have to do with them?","You think you're smart, playing both me and the Zhang family in the palm of your hand, but you didn't know that you were the one being used as a pawn. Fang Hui, do you think you are very righteous?","Si Nian looked at her with a face full of mockery.","Indeed, if this matter were investigated, the one who profited was the Sunshine Daily. Although the person who spread the word was Zhang Xiaoyun, as long as Zhang Xiaoyun knew about it, she would definitely deny it to the death. By then, no one would have any evidence, and the rumors had already been spread anyway.","Furthermore, Zhang Xiaoyun didn't take a single cent of the profit, so she wouldn't be considered breaking the law, just having a loose tongue.","The stupid one was Fang Hui herself, who took the initiative to show up, thinking she was being a great help.","After hearing this, Fang Hui was completely stunned.","She hadn't even thought about this problem.","She thought she was using people, but now, after Si Nian pointed it out, she suddenly woke up to the fact that from the very beginning, the stupid one was herself!","At this moment, Fang Hui's face looked like dead ashes.","Now that it had been exposed as a fabricated rumor, the Sunshine Daily immediately stated: We didn't want to ruin someone's reputation like this either. Our original intention was just to get first-hand news. We know we were wrong.","Captain Li ignored them; only a ghost would believe these people's words.","Si Nian didn't say much either. Anyway, her demands were laid out right there: the newspaper must stop sales, publicly apologize, admit to spreading rumors, compensate for all losses, and the rumor-monger must go to jail.","She would not accept any mediation.","Dropping these words, she left.","The honor she had painstakingly earned, her first achievement in this world, was used by others to make a fuss. This had already crossed Si Nian's bottom line, and of course, she couldn't tolerate it.","Especially since Fang Hui had done this time and time again.","If she didn't settle the score, they would really think she was easy to bully.","Si Nian left the police station without looking back.","Just as she walked out, Zhou Yueshen and the principal of No. 2 High School hurried over.","The three of them bumped right into each other.","Seeing her walk out of the station looking fine, compared to Zhou Yueshen's calmness, the principal looked anxious: How is it, Little Si? This newspaper is simply acting recklessly. I only found out about this today. Are you okay? Don't take it to heart, we all believe in you. I will definitely get this sorted out for you. Don't worry, just go home and wait with peace of mind.","No matter how you looked at her, Si Nian didn't seem like the terrible person described in the newspaper. Because the school had produced a provincial top scorer in science, the principal had been invited to dinners these past few days and was hungover all day.","So he hadn't noticed it immediately.","Now he was very regretful.","Si Nian said calmly, No need, Principal. This matter is already over.","The principal looked confused, Huh? Over?","Si Nian nodded: The instigators have already been caught and are just waiting for trial.","The principal was even more dumbfounded. After all, it had only been an hour or so since he learned about this, and it was already over?","There was absolutely no chance for him to step in?","R-really over?","Si Nian nodded: Yes, we already have evidence to prove my innocence. They can't escape.","The principal snapped back to his senses and immediately said in a deep voice, Hmph, that's too much. We absolutely cannot let these people off!","The people are still inside, right? I want to see what kind of monsters dare to write about my student like this. I'll definitely teach them a lesson!","After saying that, he angrily rushed inside.","Si Nian shook her head helplessly, feeling a wave of warmth in her heart.","She didn't expect the principal to come all the way here to comfort her.","After all, she hadn't spent much time at No. 2 High School. If it were No. 1 High School, if they knew about this, they would probably wish they could immediately cut ties with her.","Oh well.","She withdrew her gaze and looked at Zhou Yueshen.","The wind was quite strong, blowing his shirt collar messy. It was obvious he had come in a hurry.","Recently, in order to get used to wearing dress shirts, Zhou Yueshen had been trying very hard to wear them every day.","Zhou Yueshen's expression was cold and stern. He looked at her quietly for a few seconds, walked up the steps, took the bag from her hand, and said, Let's go home.","Si Nian gave a sound of agreement, stepped forward, bent down, and got into the car.","With Captain Li there, he would definitely help ensure she wasn't bullied, and Si Nian would handle the rest herself.","It wasn't as if she was actually a nineteen-year-old who would be scared facing so many people.","Although in Zhou Yueshen's eyes, Si Nian wasn't very old, from her previous way of dealing with things, he could tell that since she chose to come here, she definitely had her own capabilities.","Zhou Yueshen didn't need to ask much.","And the result wouldn't change.","The car started.","And drove off.","Si Nian looked at his rolled-up cuffs and thick arms. Speaking of which, this dress shirt was really slimming; you couldn't tell at all that underneath it was such a lean and muscular physique.","But dress shirts were ultimately inconvenient for work and were only suitable for banquets.","Si Nian glanced at the man's handsome, stern side profile and said, You don't have to wear it every day. Just wear whatever makes you comfortable. After all, it must be very inconvenient to work in these clothes, right?","Ever since she took him to buy a dress shirt last time and praised him for looking handsome, Zhou Yueshen practically wanted to tattoo the clothes onto his body.","He wore them every day.","Although wearing it like this to drive and go out was indeed very handsome and classy.","But considering he ran a pig farm, the image of him wearing a dress shirt and holding a machete to slaughter pigs was too vivid for Si Nian to even dare imagine.","Zhou Yueshen held the steering wheel with one hand, his voice gentle. Then I won't work.","Si Nian fell silent for a few seconds.","He won't work?","Was this something a workaholic older man would say?","Si Nian almost suspected he had been possessed.","Zhou Yueshen didn't explain further, and Si Nian didn't ask.","Since Zhou Yueshen said so, he must have his own reasons.","In the blink of an eye, the two arrived home.","Before they even stepped through the door, they smelled the aroma of food.","With no adults at home, the only one who could have entered the kitchen was the Eldest Child.","After all, the kitchen was still quite dangerous for children. Usually, Si Nian only let the kids help out; only the Eldest Child knew how to cook.","The Second Child loved to eat, which complemented this perfectly. He was just too clumsy, so Si Nian didn't dare let him learn those troublesome tasks.","He could only do simple things.","But judging by this smell, her professional level-ten foodie nose rated it at least a six out of ten.","The Second Child could score a two at most—barely edible.","A six was, of course, the work of our little student Dong.","Si Nian felt that at this rate, it wouldn't be long before she could retire and let the Eldest Child take the throne.","As soon as they got home, the children chattered as they crowded around.","It was the Second Child, Jiang Jiu, and the others.","Surprisingly, they weren't playing or watching TV; the house was incredibly quiet.","The Eldest Child really knew how to manage the household.","Si Nian liked this child more and more.","Mom, are you okay? What happened to the bad guy? Did he get his retribution?","The Second Child asked with righteous indignation.","Si Nian smiled. Of course, Mom has already sent the bad guy to the police station. This incident teaches us that when we are bullied, our first counterattack shouldn't be to hit back, but to call the police. Only by taking up the weapon of the law can we better protect ourselves.","The two children exchanged a glance, their eyes sparkling with admiration.","The weapon of the law is so powerful! I want to get the weapon of the law in the future.","But what does the weapon of the law look like, Second Brother?","Si Nian: Uh... well...","Is it possible that this is just a figure of speech and not a physical object?","Si Nian drew another little red flower on the Eldest Child's little red flower board.","A good child who cooked naturally deserved a reward.","However, looking at the Eldest Child's fully collected red flowers again, she felt troubled. She had already given everything she could; what else could she give him?","If he had too many things, the child wouldn't cherish them.","Therefore, Si Nian had to give something practical that both children knew was hard to get.","Speaking of this, she remembered the Second Child saying he wanted to learn Taekwondo.","It was naturally beneficial for children to learn some skills. Of course, Si Nian wouldn't force them to learn just for these benefits; it was best to prescribe the right medicine for the right condition.","The Second Child was very suited to learn something physical. He was simple-minded anyway, so since he couldn't win with his brains, he could only rely on his physical skills.","Since he had such a good talent, it couldn't be wasted.","She had stayed in the countryside for so long that she forgot that even in the 1980s, everything that should be available was available.","Look at Fang Bowen; his schedule was fully packed all day, and he didn't forget to study even during the summer vacation.","She couldn't let the two children just play for two months during the summer and winter holidays like they did in the countryside.","After thinking it over, Si Nian came up with the following arrangements for the two children.","First, take advantage of the holiday to focus on cultivating the Eldest Child's culinary development, not limited to stir-frying, quick-frying, sautéing, deep-frying, and boiling... Second, send the Second Child, who was full of unvented energy, to learn Taekwondo and increase his training time. Since he wanted to develop in this direction, he couldn't rely solely on talent; acquired effort was also extremely important. Incorrect exercise methods would only damage his foundation.","Third... cancel Yaoyao's daily candy supply. The little girl was already sensible and couldn't be spoiled all day. Si Nian was also afraid of raising her into a brat who threw tantrums if she didn't get candy. She would start having her learn some simple pinyin and characters before rewarding her with candy, letting her know that food shouldn't be gained without working for it.","No matter how smart she was, what use was it if she couldn't even write?","With these clauses drafted in her mind, Si Nian discussed them with Zhou Yueshen.","These points were all tailored to the children's situations, and Zhou Yueshen thought they made a lot of sense after hearing them.","Learning through fun and rewards meant they could gain both knowledge and prizes; the children would definitely keep moving forward.","As for the Second Child wanting to learn Taekwondo and such, Zhou Yueshen said there was no need to send him away; he could teach him himself.","Si Nian slapped her forehead. Right, wasn't there a professional expert right in front of her?","Why spend a ton of money sending him to a training class?","Actually, she had previously seen a news video of a child being beaten to death by a coach while learning martial arts.","Thinking about it now still made her a bit scared.","After all, this wasn't something you could do just by moving your fingers.","Leaving it to one of their own was the most reassuring.","As for what to teach, Zhou Yueshen definitely knew, so Si Nian didn't ask further.","When the Second Child heard that his father was going to teach him, he was a bit bewildered. He pulled Si Nian and asked, Mom, am I going to learn how to slaughter pigs with Dad?","Si Nian: ...Of course not. Your father used to be a soldier, and his combat skills are amazing. If you learn from him, you'll definitely be invincible in the future.","The Second Child's mind automatically developed a fantasy of ruling the world.","So much so that he treated his pig-slaughtering father like a martial arts master, confidently declaring that he would drain his father of all his skills.","Thus, the two brothers divided the labor: Zhou Zedong learned culinary skills from Si Nian, and the Second Child learned martial arts from Zhou Yueshen. Their summer vacation life had begun.","Both children were very satisfied with this arrangement; after all, it was what they wanted to learn. Exercise was routine for the Second Child. Back in their hometown, he loved running all over the mountains. After moving to the city, he couldn't run around everywhere because of human traffickers, so he could only play with Jiang Jiu to vent his energy, but this was far from enough for him.","But now it was different. At 5:30 in the morning, Zhou Yueshen hauled him out of bed, and he went out running with a bewildered face. A single run was a five-kilometer cross-country jog. Although this wasn't a problem for the Second Child, no one told him he had to wake up early to run.","Once he started running, his sleepiness vanished. Zhou Yueshen didn't wait for him, and he was scared on his own. After all, there was no one on the streets at 5:30, which felt quite terrifying, so he had to try hard to keep up behind his dad.","Fortunately, his stamina wasn't bad, so he didn't worry about falling behind.","After finishing the run, he was completely dazed.","Seeing that he had only broken a light sweat and was much more outstanding than the new recruits he used to train, Zhou Yueshen finally realized that this child might truly have a talent in this area.","So he handed him a broom and told him to sweep the entire house.","It was true that the Second Child liked exercising, but it was also true that he disliked cleaning.","Hearing his dad's words now, he looked utterly bewildered.","Weren't they supposed to be learning Taekwondo to become invincible in the world? How did it turn into cleaning the house?","Under his son's suspicious gaze, Zhou Yueshen added without blushing or skipping a beat, \"Running exercises the whole body, but sweeping and mopping the floor can train your arm muscles. That way, your punches will be much more powerful in the future.\"","Second Child's eyes widened in sudden realization. \"I get it now. I'll go clean right away.\"","Watching his son sprint away, the corners of Zhou Yueshen's lips curled into a faint smile as he turned and walked away."]},{"number":393,"title":"Chapter 393: Jealousy Distorts One's Features","paragraphs":["When Si Nian and Zhou Zedong got up, Second Child was exhausted and fast asleep on the sofa.","Si Nian was a bit puzzled, \"Did Little Han not go back to his room last night? Why is he sleeping here?\"","Zhou Zedong thought carefully and said uncertainly, \"He did, didn't he?\"","The first thing he subconsciously did after getting up was to sweep the dust off the floor in the house.","Because his younger sister and brother both liked to crawl around and play on the floor, if the floor wasn't cleaned every day, they would get their clothes dirty.","However, the mop was actually still dripping wet, and there were traces of water from the faucet on the floor.","At this moment, even someone as smart as him was a bit confused.","Could his younger brother have become so diligent that he got up early in the morning to clean up?","When Si Nian heard about this, she also felt quite amazed.","Consequently, she drew a little red flower in Second Child's little red flower chart.","A child who usually liked to sleep in actually knew to get up early and clean; of course, he had to be rewarded.","When Second Child woke up, he found he had earned an extra little red flower.","He was completely thrilled.","He hadn't expected that getting up early to jog would earn him a little red flower. At this rate, wouldn't his little red flowers soon surpass his older brother's?","It was just that getting up alone was so boring. His dad didn't like to talk, and he was a chatterbox, so holding his tongue all morning was agonizing.","So, Second Child immediately ran out to find Jiang Jiu, saying he wanted to teach him martial arts.","Jiang Jiu was instantly tempted, and the two agreed to wake up at five o'clock the next morning.","This way, they could both learn and have someone to chat with. It was simply too wonderful.","Just as the two were discussing it, they saw a man walk out of the Fang family's house next door, carrying some things in his hands.","Jiang Jiu was a bit surprised, \"Who is that?\" It was the first time he had seen a man at the Fang house.","Second Child said, \"I know, that is Fang Bowen's dad.\"","Jiang Jiu was shocked, \"Fang Bowen's dad? Fang Bowen has a dad? I thought he only had a mom.\"","Second Child asked in confusion, \"Why do you say that?\"","Jiang Jiu whispered secretly, \"Look, Fang Bowen's surname is Fang, and Auntie Fang's surname is also Fang. I heard that only children without dads take their mother's surname. Look at me, my mom and dad got divorced, so I took my dad's surname, and my little brother took my mom's surname.\"","Second Child was astonished.","Then if that man wasn't Fang Bowen's dad, could he be a fraud?","He immediately rushed over and blocked the man who was about to leave.","The man paused slightly. His hair was a bit long, covering his eyelids, and he wore gold-rimmed glasses, making it somewhat hard to read his expression.","However, it was only brief before he spoke first, \"Little boy, is something the matter?\"","Second Child asked suspiciously, \"Uncle, is Fang Bowen really your son?\"","The other party paused, \"Why do you ask?\"","\"Because Fang Bowen takes his mom's surname. Is your surname also Fang?\"","At these words, the man let out a low chuckle, \"Of course, little Bowen is indeed my son. It's just that your Auntie Fang and I aren't married. As for the specific reasons, children shouldn't know.\"","Second Child looked at him, half-understanding. He could sense that this man didn't seem like a bad person, but he still felt something was weird, though he couldn't put his finger on it.","\"Then what about Fang Bowen? Where is he? I'll ask him.\"","He tilted his head and looked toward the house.","The other party was silent for a moment and said, \"Little Bowen is sick. I took him to the hospital yesterday, and he's still there now. Do you want to go see him?\"","Second Child also knew that Fang Bowen was sick; he always looked sickly. The last time he and Jiang Jiu brought him food, Fang Bowen said he didn't want it, but in reality, the lunchbox disappeared after they left.","Then he was nowhere to be seen.","He rolled his eyes and came up with an excuse, \"Little Jiang's lunchbox was left with him. We aren't going to see him, just to ask for the lunchbox back.\"","The man smiled, \"Alright.\"","Second Child ran back home to tell Si Nian.","When Si Nian heard that Fang Bowen's dad had come home, she was also very surprised.","She watched her son pack snacks into his schoolbag, followed him out the door, and looked suspiciously at the man outside.","The man was looking down at an expensive watch on his wrist. He was wearing a custom-tailored suit that looked very pricey at a glance.","He was a wealthy man.","He was about the same age as Zhou Yueshen, but compared to Zhou Yueshen's sharp edge, he was much more restrained and gentle.","Si Nian stepped forward, and the other party immediately noticed her.","He paused first, then greeted her, \"Hello, you must be Teacher Si, right?\"","Si Nian was surprised, \"Yes, and you are?\"","The man chuckled softly, \"I am little Bowen's dad, Xiao Yi. When I took him to the hospital last night, he mentioned you.\"","Si Nian understood, but it was still a bit awkward. She had sent Fang Hui to the police station herself, and now she was waiting for trial. Yet her husband had returned and was greeting her.","Hmm... Could it be that he didn't know about Fang Hui yet?","She quietly observed the man; he indeed bore some resemblance to Fang Bowen.","The man seemed to see through her thoughts and said, \"I already know about what happened between you and Fang Hui. However, I don't plan to intervene. After all, this was indeed her fault, but she is little Bowen's mother in the end, so I hope Teacher Si can show some mercy.\"","Si Nian was even more surprised. So he already knew?","His wife had gotten into such trouble, yet this man could still be so calm?","Si Nian was truly shocked, but the other party looked very wealthy. If he really wanted to help, Fang Hui definitely wouldn't be in any trouble.","Si Nian's judgment of people was still very accurate.","For Fang Hui to come to an unfamiliar place as a single mother, live in such a big house, and send her son to the best school—it was absolutely impossible to do that just on a reporter's salary.","But since Fang Bowen took Fang Hui's surname, and the fact that the man didn't show a hint of emotion when mentioning Fang Hui, Si Nian instantly seemed to understand something.","She nodded, \"If she has the sense to apologize and compensate, I naturally won't hold a grudge. As for the rest, whatever the law decides is what counts.\"","The other party gave a slight nod and didn't say much else.","He looked like he had no intention of discussing it further.","Si Nian felt slightly relieved and looked at her son and Jiang Jiu.","\"Go on, come back early.\"","The hospital was quite close to here. Plus, since the other party had immediately taken Fang Bowen to the hospital upon arriving, he definitely cared about the child and wasn't a bad person.","Si Nian also felt safe letting the two children go along to visit.","Second Child and Jiang Jiu couldn't understand what the two adults were talking about and were still discussing what they had brought.","However, Second Child said to Si Nian, \"Mom, I'll just go ask for the lunchbox and come back,\" using a tone that suggested he wasn't close to Fang Bowen at all.","Si Nian smiled and nodded.","The man hailed a car, and the two children immediately squeezed in, then waved goodbye to Si Nian.","Si Nian watched them leave before heading back into the house.","Just then, Captain Li called her to inform her that the court session would start tomorrow.","Because the evidence was complete, there would definitely be no problems on her side.","Upon contacting the Fang family, she found that no one from Fang Hui's side had any intention of coming over.","Fang Hui could only choose to appeal after the verdict was given.","The Sunshine Daily had already halted its sales, tactfully stating that all profits would be used to compensate her, and they came forward to explain the rumor-mongering incident.","The newspapers should be out by now, and they asked if she had seen them.","Si Nian really had not seen them. She was currently guiding Eldest Child on how to stew soup, while also teaching Yaoyao how to write.","After Captain Li hung up the phone, she asked Eldest Child to go buy some newspapers.","Sure enough, Eldest Child bought back a few newspapers, all of which contained the clarification statements and apologies that Sunshine Daily had rushed out overnight.","In addition, another newspaper wrote about how she was framed by her adoptive parents' family after becoming the provincial top scorer in sciences, along with interviews with Captain Li, the principal, and others.","Principal of No. 2 High School: \"Yes, they were simply jealous that Student Si won the top scorer title. Jealousy twists people's true nature.\"","Captain Li: \"According to a relative, A certain Zhang, the motive for the crime is suspected to be that Comrade Si achieved the top scorer title while the Si family's own daughter only got average grades, which infuriated the other party into holding a grudge against the victim. The suspects have been brought to justice, and we hope the public will stop causing harm to the victim...\"","Si Nian almost burst out laughing.","Several consecutive newspapers corroborated this matter, and some newspaper agencies even stepped forward to express their support for her, stating they believed in her character, and so on.","Although she did not know who was helping her behind the scenes, judging from the situation, the storm surrounding this incident should soon pass.","...","Second Child and Jiang Jiu only realized upon arriving at the hospital that Fang Bowen's situation was not as simple as they had imagined.","He was actually still unconscious.","The two had even brought a Gobang set, planning to play chess with Fang Bowen.","Seeing Fang Bowen lying on the bed looking so tiny, with tubes inserted into his body and his small face terrifyingly pale, the excitement they had felt all the way there instantly vanished into thin air.","The two only knew that Fang Bowen had been sick for a long time, but they did not expect it to be this serious.","Xiao Yi led the two quiet children to sit down on the side, and then heard Zhou Zehan ask, \"Uncle Xiao, is Fang Bowen okay?\"","Xiao Yi gave a slight nod. \"He is fine, he has passed the critical stage.\"","His expression was slightly grave. Fang Bowen's condition had originally been just a common cold, but because it went untreated for a long time, it had developed into pneumonia.","It was extremely severe.","When he went over yesterday, he found the child coughing incessantly with a stubborn high fever.","Surprisingly, there were only a few cold medicine boxes in the house.","Fang Hui was nowhere to be found, leaving only a nanny behind.","He asked the nanny, but she said she did not know either, because she usually only helped with cooking and sending Fang Bowen to tutoring classes.","Although the teacher mentioned he had a slight cough, Fang Hui only came back late at night every day. The nanny could not possibly wait for her to return before leaving, so she just ignored it.","She thought it was just a simple cold and cough.","Little did she expect it to be this serious.","Furthermore, the child did not say where he felt uncomfortable.","With a cold face, Xiao Yi sent the child to the hospital, which was when the pneumonia was diagnosed.","A seven-year-old child getting pneumonia; he really did not know how Fang Hui had been taking care of the kid.","Fang Hui did not return all night. After looking into it, Xiao Yi found out that the woman had been taken to the police station for spreading rumors.","Last night, in order to keep the child awake and prevent him from falling into a coma, he kept trying to find topics to talk about, asking him about his life here.","As a result, Fang Bowen's face only showed a hint of vitality when he mentioned Teacher Si's family next door.","Xiao Yi's expression was very ugly.","This was also the reason he decided to give up on Fang Hui.","Helping a woman so vicious that she could not even take good care of her own biological son would be aiding and abetting a tyrant.","And having her come here in the first place was just to investigate some matters.","Now, his objective had been achieved.","Fang Hui was entirely worthless.","Xiao Yi's gaze swept past Second Child and was quickly withdrawn.","Fang Bowen woke up in the afternoon.","As soon as he woke up, he heard two familiar voices.","He struggled to open his eyes and saw Second Child and Jiang Jiu sitting by the hospital bed, playing Gobang.","He thought he was dreaming and closed his eyes again.","Because he had dreamed of such a scene before.","He did not want to wake up right now.","It was not until a pair of warm, large hands landed on his forehead. \"Are you awake?\"","Only then did he uncertainly open his eyes and see the man in front of him.","He recognized him. When he was very young, his mother had pointed to this dazzling man in the newspaper and told him that this was his father.","But she also told him that he had to study hard and become a very smart child before his father would acknowledge him.","So he had always studied very hard, and sure enough, his father had come looking for him.","Fang Bowen widened his eyes.","Second Child and Jiang Jiu immediately leaned over, staring at him with wide eyes.","\"Fang Bowen, you are awake?\"","\"Fang Bowen, are you okay?\"","\"Do you want some candy?\"","\"I have cookies too.\"","He blinked hard to keep himself from crying.","He awkwardly turned his head away. \"I... I won't eat your stuff.\"","The two children exchanged glances. \"Okay then, if you do not want it, forget it.\"","After saying that, they put the snacks away.","Fang Bowen: \"...\"","After Second Child returned home, he told Si Nian about Fang Bowen.","Si Nian had heard that the child had a cold, but she had not expected it to be a severe illness like pneumonia, and she was quite shocked.","One week later.","Xiao Yi led Fang Bowen by the hand and came over carrying a lot of gifts.","Fang Bowen's face was still a bit pale, but he looked much better and was no longer coughing.","Seeing Second Child and the others, his expression was still a bit awkward.","But when he saw Si Nian, he politely greeted her first, \"Hello, Teacher Si.\"","Si Nian nodded with a sigh. \"Are you feeling better, Student Fang?\"","Xiao Yi nodded, his expression solemn. \"Thank you so much for your care. The child said that the cold medicine he took earlier was given by you. If it were not for your medicine, I am afraid this child would not have made it through.\"","Si Nian was surprised. \"Cold medicine?\"","Xiao Yi nodded. \"The child had been running a fever on and off for a long time. He said he only felt a bit better after taking some medicine, and that the medicine was given by you.\"","Fang Bowen said somewhat shyly, \"Yes, it was given to me by Zhou Zedong. He said that if I felt very hot all over and kept coughing, I would get better if I took it. So I took it, and then I really did get better.\"","He used to get fevers at night, but he got a bit better those two days when he took the medicine.","But later, when the medicine ran out, he stopped taking it, and then it started all over again.","Si Nian turned to look at Zhou Zedong, who was walking out.","Zhou Zedong was quite calm and said, \"When my younger brother was sick before, his symptoms were very similar to Fang Bowen's, so I thought I would let him try taking it.\"","He had carefully examined that cold medicine; it could treat many problems, and even if someone took it without being sick, they would be fine.","That was why he dared to give it to Fang Bowen.","Si Nian was even more astonished.","She had thought that only Second Child would be soft-hearted enough to secretly give Fang Bowen food.","She did not expect that Little Dong would actually secretly give him medicine too.","But what she expected even less was that Fang Bowen's condition was so serious that he had contracted pneumonia.","Thinking about it for a moment, Si Nian felt her hair stand on end.","Because if Fang Bowen's father had not happened to come here and take him to the hospital, and with Fang Hui being detained, wouldn't Fang Bowen have been in grave danger?","If something really happened because of this, she would never have peace for the rest of her life!"]},{"number":394,"title":"Chapter 394: Compensation","paragraphs":["Thinking of this possibility, Si Nian couldn't help but feel grateful to the two children. They were truly her lucky stars.","Fang Bowen was fine, and without any of them, this outcome would have been impossible.","In the hospital.","Lin Sisi had been admitted to the hospital again.","Si Nian had become the provincial top scorer in the science college entrance examination, and she was so angry that she hadn't eaten for three days and three nights.","Now she was sent here for an IV drip.","Zhang Cuimei looked as if she had aged a dozen years, her hair turning white.","Obviously, this blow didn't just affect Lin Sisi; it had a huge impact on her as well.","In her impression, Si Nian was just a little smarter than others. When Si Nian wanted to take the college entrance examination before, Zhang Cuimei even mocked her for making a fool of herself.","She never expected that in such a short time, she would be slapped in the face so hard.","A few days ago, when a newspaper wrote about Si Nian being an ungrateful wretch, Zhang Cuimei felt that she had finally vented her anger.","But unexpectedly, in just a few days, the newspaper was sued, and she heard that the rumor-mongers had all been arrested.","What was said was right, to begin with. She had raised her for over ten years, and her glorious achievements were all thanks to the Si family. What right did she have to disown her?","Zhang Cuimei had excitedly wanted to find someone to share and complain about how Si Nian treated them and Lin Sisi.","But upon hearing that the rumor-mongers had been sued in court and that the matter was extremely serious—even her sister Zhang Xiaoyun, who spread the rumors, was suspended and sent home due to the severe impact of the incident—Zhang Cuimei didn't dare say a single bad word about Si Nian anymore.","She could only sulk in silence.","She was so angry that she would even wake up from her dreams in the middle of the night.","She didn't know how things had come to this point. Actually, in the past, she just felt a lack of closeness with Si Nian, but she still loved this adopted daughter very much.","She couldn't understand how everything had changed like this in just over a year.","Passing nurses were still discussing the matter: I heard that this provincial science top scorer had it really tough. Her path to the college entrance examination was full of bumps. She finally managed to become the top scorer, only to be slandered by the adoptive parents who abandoned her. It's truly despicable.","Fortunately, the public's eyes are sharp. I heard that Tsinghua and Peking University have already sent people to recruit her, and other universities are also waiting for their chance. To get such a score, she must have been very smart before. If she hadn't been forced into marriage, her future would definitely be extremely bright.","Hearing this, Zhang Cuimei's face turned green.","The way they said it, it sounded as if it was their fault for not letting Si Nian take the college entrance examination.","Back then, didn't Si Nian happily drop out of school upon hearing that she could marry Fu Yang?","How could anyone blame them?","Besides, what was the use of a girl getting such good grades? She would still be married off in the future anyway.","They didn't even think about who had been willing to spend money to cultivate her!","These people were still talking bad about them behind their backs. It was truly hateful!","Zhang Cuimei couldn't swallow her anger, nor could she vent it. She almost suffocated herself.","Then she thought about how Si Nian had prestigious universities like Tsinghua and Peking University fighting over her as soon as the scores came out, while her own daughter still had no news due to the impact of this incident. She couldn't help but feel a deep sorrow.","Since being provoked by Si Nian that day, her daughter had refused to eat and had lost a whole circle of weight.","It was truly heartbreaking.","The Fu family was still pushing for the divorce. If her daughter hadn't been sick, she probably would have been forced to divorce by now!","The more Zhang Cuimei thought about it, the angrier she became.","Divorce was absolutely out of the question.","Fu Yang was her last trump card.","Meanwhile, at the Fu family.","Upon learning that Lin Sisi was lingering in the hospital and refusing to divorce, Father Fu and his wife looked terrible.","How did I not know before that this family was so shameless? It was agreed upon before Lin Sisi got out of prison, and now that the college entrance examination is over, she's still pretending! It's absolutely disgusting!","Mrs. Zheng was so angry that her face turned livid.","Father Fu also had a gloomy expression. Since Lin Sisi hadn't done anything like cheating or wronging the man, as long as she stubbornly refused, this marriage would indeed be difficult to dissolve.","They also disdained using underhanded methods.","But seeing that their son was already twenty-six, if this continued, when would they ever hold a grandchild?","Compared to their urgency, Fu Yang appeared very calm.","After losing Si Nian, he always felt that the people around him were somewhat lacking.","He would never have that kind of emotion-stirring feeling for anyone else again.","So whether he divorced or not didn't have much of an impact on him.","It could even help him block the annoyance of his parents forcing him to marry.","If this Lin Sisi left, there would be a second and a third Lin Sisi.","Fu Yang didn't want to waste his time on these matters.","His life wasn't just about getting married.","It was just that the Si family's shameless behavior was indeed infuriating.","After thinking for a moment, he spoke in a deep voice, If she won't divorce, then so be it. It doesn't matter, as long as she doesn't regret it.","The couple froze for a moment and asked with furrowed brows, What does that mean? If you don't divorce, are you going to be tied down by her for the rest of your life?","What kind of marriage is this? You have neither affection nor children.","Fu Yang said, It doesn't matter. Without her, you would still force me to marry anyway. Given my mother's taste in daughters-in-law, the next one might not be much better than Lin Sisi. Since she's happy to keep it this way, why should we force it? I'm leaving anyway.","Mrs. Zheng rolled her eyes in anger at her son. You brat, if you had found someone yourself, would I need to worry? Besides, how is my taste bad? Look at how great Si Nian was. Look at how beautiful and educated she is, enjoying all the glory right now. If you hadn't kept dragging your feet, you two would have been married long ago. How would it ever have been Lin Sisi's turn?","Fu Yang frowned and said nothing more.","Instead, Father Fu asked in a deep voice, Have you thought this through?","Fu Yang nodded, Yes. My life should be dedicated to the country. What's the point of doing it for a woman?","Mrs. Zheng became anxious, What kind of riddles are you father and son playing?","Father Fu sighed, Let him be.","It turned out that Fu Yang had applied to be transferred to the remote Northwest Military Region for further study.","Originally, Father Fu did not agree.","But looking at his stubborn son, he felt that perhaps it was for the best.","Since his last trip to the Northwest, he had changed a lot and matured significantly.","Since he wanted to go, it must be because there was something he wanted there.","Why use a woman to tie him down?","Hearing this news, even Fu Qianqian, who had been gloating on the sidelines, was shocked.","Her brother was actually going to the Northwest Military Region, and it was the kind of trip where he wouldn't come home for several years.","Suddenly, she couldn't laugh anymore.","Only now did she remember her brother's good points.","Although she was always bickering with Fu Yang, mocking him and complaining about him.","But Fu Yang was actually quite good to her; he was willing to buy her things and give her money to spend.","Without her brother, her pocket money would be cut in half.","Even though she was working now, she still needed her brother's financial support.","Now that her brother was leaving, there would be no one to give her money.","So sad...","Fu Yang: ...","The Zhou family.","Division Commander Jiang was currently visiting the Zhou family's courtyard.","Zhou Yueshen was on the side taking care of the children. Si Nian had been very busy lately, with schools coming to their door all day offering gifts and extending olive branches.","Therefore, the task of looking after the children was thrown to him.","Si Nian didn't know why he was suddenly no longer busy. According to Zhou Yueshen, he wanted to change his approach to making money.","Because Si Nian had once said that people who make big money always use their brains, not their hands.","So now he had recruited many talented people to manage the company. He no longer did the manual work himself; he only needed to check the daily ledgers sent by his assistant.","Zhou Yueshen was slowly transitioning the breeding farm to a free-range model.","Because once Si Nian's admission letter arrived, they would face a major issue.","That was whether Si Nian would take a leave of absence or start school right away.","Yaoyao could already read some words now and could attend preschool.","But with Si Nian not at home, it would ultimately be inconvenient.","If they were going to Beijing, he had to make preparations in advance.","Of course, regardless of the decision, Zhou Yueshen felt there wouldn't be any major problems.","Second Child and Jiang Jiu were practicing the horse stance in the courtyard.","Compared to Second Child's stability, Jiang Jiu's legs were shaking like leaves.","He didn't have much muscle. Even after exercising for a few days, his stamina couldn't keep up.","Second Child was also sweating profusely, but his legs were very strong. He could hold the stance for forty to fifty minutes on his very first try.","It made Si Nian's scalp tingle just watching them. If she were to do this pose, her legs would probably start shaking in less than a minute.","Yaoyao was learning to play chess with Division Commander Jiang.","Meanwhile, Zhou Zedong was following Si Nian in the kitchen, experimenting with delicious food.","Division Commander Jiang claimed he was just bringing his grandson over to play, but in reality, he was secretly imparting knowledge to Yaoyao.","Looking at the three well-occupied children, he couldn't help but sigh, It really is better to have parents at home. Look at how sensible and smart your children are. Little Zhou is capable, Teacher Xiao Si is smart, and your future children will probably be even more of geniuses.","Zhou Yueshen paused.","Then he said, We might not have children.","Division Commander Jiang was stunned for a moment. He had heard that these three children were the orphans of Zhou Yueshen's late sister.","In other words, Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen didn't have children of their own yet.","Si Nian was still young, so there was no worry for her.","But Zhou Yueshen was already thirty-one or thirty-two.","If this continued...","Although he felt it was a bit of a pity, it was a matter between husband and wife, not something outsiders could interfere with.","Moreover, Si Nian was about to go to university now, so it was really hard to say.","He sighed and said no more.","At this moment, Si Nian was still on the phone.","It was Peking University calling.","They would have someone call her every few hours, claiming they were worried she was being harassed by other universities.","They also said the leaders and professors sent to deliver her admission letter were already on a plane, telling her not to listen to the deceptive words of other schools.","They were terrified she would be snatched away.","They even promised that whatever demands other schools met, they would double them.","It was no wonder Peking University was so nervous.","Over the past few days, several universities had come to her door.","Bonuses and gifts were minor things.","Some said that as long as she enrolled, they could guarantee her three children a direct path to university.","This was a massive guarantee.","But Si Nian did not let this overwhelming wealth and privilege cloud her judgment.","The three children were all very smart. As long as they wanted to, they could definitely test into schools no worse than hers.","So she did not agree.","Furthermore, she knew well that whatever other schools were willing to offer, Peking University could definitely match.","She just needed to wait peacefully.","The main thing was that Zhou Yueshen was at home. This man always wore a cold expression, and those so-called leaders and professors felt intimidated when they saw him.","They didn't dare to push Si Nian too hard.","So things remained relatively peaceful.","Fu Qianqian came to Si Nian's house crying.","Si Nian was startled and asked her what had happened.","Looking heartbroken, Fu Qianqian stuffed two rose cakes into her mouth before saying, My brother is leaving. He is being transferred to the Northwest and might not be back for three or four years. I really can't bear to see him go.","Si Nian was also surprised to hear this.","Fu Yang was actually leaving.","However, seeing how Fu Qianqian usually complained about her brother mercilessly, she had thought Fu Qianqian would be happy if Fu Yang left.","To Si Nian, aside from a bit of surprise, this news didn't evoke any strong feelings.","After all, she wasn't the original owner of this body and didn't have a shred of affection for Fu Yang.","So she comforted her, It's okay, it's not like you'll never see him again.","Fu Qianqian retorted angrily, How is it okay? It's a disaster! If he leaves, I won't be able to spend his money anymore. I'll have to buy five or six fewer new clothes a month. Do you know what a huge blow that is to a beauty-loving girl?","Si Nian: ...","Then, remembering that Si Nian was also leaving, and for three or four years at that, Fu Qianqian was suddenly overcome with grief.","She started crying again.","The loss of money was one thing, but now she couldn't even freeload meals anymore.","Si Nian rolled her eyes so hard they almost got stuck.","Actually, she was thinking that since Zhou Yueshen, while in this city, could so coincidentally stumble upon houses that would be slated for demolition in the future.","Then if she went to Beijing, could she also buy some courtyard houses at a low price?","One must know that decades later, the price of courtyard houses would be ridiculously expensive.","Although the money she had on her now, combined with what Zhou Yueshen had given her, amounted to over a hundred thousand, which was an astronomical sum in this era.","By 2023, this amount wouldn't even be enough for a down payment.","She didn't know how much Zhou Yueshen had made, and she had never asked.","But if there really was such an opportunity, she wanted Zhou Yueshen to make a move.","Being able to sit back and collect money without having to work oneself to the bone running to the breeding farm, while also being able to focus more on the children's education at home, wouldn't that kind of life be better?","The more Si Nian thought about it, the more tempted she became.","It had to be said that the learning process was tedious.","No matter what one was learning.","Second Child had been learning martial arts from his father for ten days.","Not only had he not learned a single move, but he spent all day running and doing the horse stance.","He was already restless by nature, so he quickly lost interest.","It was entirely his father's imposing presence that kept him in line.","Now, taking advantage of Zhou Yueshen going upstairs to work, he immediately slacked off.","Just as he was about to run out the door, he bumped into Captain Li, who had come to deliver Fang Hui's verdict and compensation money.","Because Si Nian was now considered a very famous figure in the province. Her brilliant achievements not only brought glory to herself and her school but also gave the entire province a great deal of prestige.","Because this city was located in a plateau region with rugged terrain, its development had always been slow.","As the saying goes, If you want to get rich, build roads first. However, building roads here, given the reality that there wasn't an inch of flat land, was far more difficult than in any other province.","As a result, people had always assumed that the locals here were still living in conditions where they lit candles for light and rode pigs to school.","By achieving such a high score, Si Nian naturally brought honor to this city.","Now the whole country knew that this inconspicuous city had produced the provincial top scorer in the science track, ranking in the top three nationally for total score, and currently holding the record for the most subjects with perfect scores.","The leaders, of course, could not tolerate anyone smearing her reputation.","Therefore, the Sunshine Daily suffered miserably this time.","Not only were they directly shut down, but Fang Hui was also sentenced to three months in prison."]},{"number":395,"title":"Chapter 395: Daily Life (Adjusted Fang Hui's Prison Term)","paragraphs":["The compensation amounted to eight hundred and twenty.","Earning this much in just two days of sales was incredible.","One could only imagine how terrifying the sales volume was.","However, Si Nian was somewhat surprised by Fang Hui's sentence.","She had thought that paying compensation would lead to a maximum detention of a dozen days or so.","She didn't expect her to be sentenced to three months.","This was quite an unexpected outcome.","Although she didn't want to offend people, Fang Hui had brought this upon herself this time. It served her right, and Si Nian didn't feel sorry for her at all.","After Captain Li finished discussing this matter with her, he chatted with Zhou Yueshen for a while before saying his goodbyes and leaving.","Zhou Zehan and Jiang Jiu ran in laughing and joking. Zhou Yueshen glanced at him and stood up, saying, \"Xiaohan, come here.\"","Si Nian had just come out of the kitchen with tea. She hadn't expected Captain Li to leave so quickly. Seeing Second Child looking bewildered as his father called him over, she finally snapped back to reality. Wasn't Second Child training outside? How did he end up playing with Jiang Jiu after just a brief moment out of sight?","Si Nian observed Zhou Yueshen's expression; his face was as calm as ever.","Since she had known him, Si Nian had never seen Zhou Yueshen lose his temper at them.","He had always been very gentle with the children, but seeing how quickly Second Child and Jiang Jiu behaved themselves, it was clear that Zhou Yueshen had lost his temper before.","They were especially afraid when Zhou Yueshen was expressionless.","They obviously knew he was in a bad mood and didn't dare to fool around.","For instance, right now, she felt that Zhou Yueshen looked no different from usual.","But the two children instantly went to stand facing the wall as a punishment.","Si Nian raised her eyebrows slightly.","Although Jiang Jiu was dragged over by Second Child, he also treated Zhou Yueshen like a master.","It was bad enough that his daily training was less than his second brother's, but seeing his second brother playing around just now, he had also stopped taking it seriously.","This was what made Uncle Zhou angry.","He used to envy his second brother for having such a mighty and strong father.","But now he found him terrifying.","Uncle Zhou's anger was much scarier than his own father's.","Because in front of his father, it was always him getting angry and his father coaxing him.","Second Child also stood against the wall with his hands behind his back, his face full of guilt.","He had thought that he wouldn't be discovered if he sneaked off to play for a while.","Seeing Si Nian, his older brother, and his younger sister looking at him, his small face instantly flushed red.","The guilt of doing something wrong rushed over him in an instant.","\"Dad, I know I was wrong. I won't be lazy anymore.\"","Zhou Yueshen gave him an expressionless side-glance and said calmly, \"We'll talk about the future later. Just do what's in front of you well.\"","Second Child nodded.","Si Nian didn't say anything either. Standing facing the wall wasn't a severe punishment.","Second Child was still immature, so letting him temper himself with Zhou Yueshen for a while was a good thing.","Second Child thought the punishment was over with just standing against the wall, but he didn't expect the training to be different the next day.","Zhou Yueshen tied sandbags to his arms and legs, while Jiang Jiu didn't have any.","Jiang Jiu still couldn't even run five kilometers.","Usually, Second Child would run in the front, acting very smug.","But now his body felt heavy, as if he were carrying a mountain on his back.","It wasn't long before his legs felt incredibly sore.","Second Child felt very wronged, thinking his father was using his public office to avenge private wrongs. When he got home and saw that Si Nian was awake, he immediately ran over to complain.","\"Mom, Mom, look at what Dad tied to me. Dad is too petty.\"","Si Nian looked down and saw that the little guy had sandbags tied to his arms and legs.","She was a bit surprised.","Wasn't it a bit exaggerated to start weight-bearing running at such a young age?","After Second Child finished speaking, he pointed at Zhou Yueshen and said, \"Dad is running ahead effortlessly and laughing at me...\"","Before he could finish his sentence, several thuds sounded in front of Zhou Yueshen. A few iron blocks fell to the ground, smashing the stones paved on the floor.","Second Child was speechless.","Zhou Yueshen then looked at him and said lightly, \"If you don't want to use sandbags, do you want to use these?\"","Second Child smiled stiffly, \"...Mom, I actually really like running with sandbags tied to me. It's not tiring at all.\"","Si Nian burst out laughing, \"Alright, your dad isn't bullying you on purpose. It's just that you've been running for so long, you need to make some progress. You can't just keep running like that forever.\"","Second Child nodded hurriedly, \"I'll listen to Mom.\"","Zhou Yueshen proved with his strength that your dad is still your dad. In the following days, Second Child was as tired as a dog every day.","Let alone running with sandbags, Zhou Yueshen found it troublesome and specifically had someone custom-make iron blocks suitable for children for him to wear on his wrists and ankles.","He had to wear them every day while sleeping, eating, and running.","At first, Second Child also felt they were very heavy and sore, finding it extremely strenuous.","But habit is a very terrifying thing.","It wasn't long before he stopped feeling them, and his morning runs became easier and easier.","He was very proud of this and even showed off to his older brother, who looked like a househusband, \"Brother, look, I can wear two kilograms now, easy peasy.\"","Zhou Zedong was engrossed in cooking and studying every day and hadn't paid attention to how his younger brother was training.","Only then did he notice the iron blocks on his wrists. \"What's the use of that?\"","Second Child instantly lost his voice.","He didn't know what the use was either; anyway, his dad told him to wear them, so he wore them.","If he had to say what the use was, he couldn't explain the reason behind it.","Seeing his older brother withdraw his gaze with a look of disinterest, he suddenly felt very defeated.","He had been training with his dad for over half a month, and his older brother had already learned how to cook a dozen or twenty dishes, but he hadn't learned a single martial arts move.","He had originally hoped that once he learned some moves, he could show off how awesome he was in front of his older brother.","But he found himself just spinning his wheels in the same place.","Second Child became anxious again and went to find Zhou Yueshen, saying, \"Dad, I'm used to these now. Can I learn some moves now?\"","Zhou Yueshen was standing at the door. A chubby man handed him something, which he took before sending the man away.","Hearing this, he nodded slightly and said in a deep voice, \"It is time for the next step. I had a new set made for you.\"","After saying that, he took out larger iron blocks from the bag and put them on his wrists.","Second Child was speechless.","Next door, Fang Bowen leaned against the window, resting his chin on his hands, and curiously asked Xiao Yi beside him, \"Dad, what do you think Second Child and Jiang Jiu are doing every day? Why do they have to do horse stances in the yard every day? Do they do something wrong every day?\"","In Fang Bowen's memory, one would only be punished with a horse stance for doing something wrong.","During this period while he was recovering at home, Xiao Yi had canceled the nanny and all his classes.","He didn't have to go to school, and his mom wasn't home. His dad said that from now on, he would live with him.","His mom had done something wrong and couldn't come back for the time being.","Although Fang Bowen was a bit reluctant to part, he preferred the feeling of being with his dad.","His dad would never force him to learn things he didn't like, and he would buy him lots of delicious food and treat him well.","He even let him play with Second Child and the others.","Now that he didn't have to study every day, he had free time and deliberately ran to the balcony where Second Child and the others could see him, hoping they would see him and call him over to play Gomoku.","The last game of chess he played with Zhou Zedong hadn't been decided yet, and he was still thinking about it.","But it had been so long, and not only did Second Child and the others not invite him to play, but he also had no idea what they were busy with every day. Fang Bowen felt a bit disappointed.","Xiao Yi glanced over at the yard next door and saw Zhou Yueshen putting iron weights on the child's hands. He was slightly surprised.","Actually, he had noticed lately that Zhou Yueshen would take the two children out for a jog early in the morning.","However, this wasn't really strange; many families in the city placed a strong emphasis on their children's physical exercise.","But using weights was what surprised him.","Wasn't this child only seven years old?","Furthermore, these were usually only used in professional training.","Wasn't this a bit too early?","But seeing Zhou Yueshen in a tank top, showing off his muscular physique, Xiao Yi seemed to understand something.","He smiled faintly and rubbed his son's head. \"He is exercising. Physical exercise is an indispensable part of life; it can improve your immunity. Once you fully recover, Daddy will also take you out to exercise, so you won't get sick in the future.\"","Fang Bowen immediately cheered up.","Second Child looked so healthy, and he wanted to be just as healthy as Second Child.","Second Child was very likable, and he would definitely be likable too.","Second Child, currently holding a horse stance, was still suspecting that his dad was just brushing him off: \"Dad, is this kind of exercise really useful?\"","Zhou Yueshen was watering the flowers Si Nian had planted. Hearing this, he paused.","He casually picked up a brick from the ground and punched it.","Smash. The brick shattered all over the ground.","Second Child's mouth dropped open in astonishment: \"...\"","Having silently stabilized his son's emotions, Zhou Yueshen turned around, only to see Si Nian standing at the doorway, staring at him with the same look of astonishment.","Looking at her shattered brick on the ground, Si Nian opened her mouth: \"Zhou Yueshen, that was a patterned brick I specially custom-ordered to decorate the yard.\"","Zhou Yueshen stiffened. \"I... didn't do it on purpose.\"","After saying that, he was about to step forward, but with that movement, the water hose yanked a flowerpot down, resulting in another loud crash.","Si Nian: \"Ah! That was the rose I've been growing for over half a year.\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","The series of crashes in the yard drew the attention of both neighboring families, who looked over.","\"What's going on at the Zhou house today? What broke?\"","\"Dad, did you hear the sound of something breaking?\"","Xiao Yi glanced down from upstairs at Zhou Yueshen's slightly frantic back and chuckled softly: \"I heard it. It was the sound of your Uncle Zhou's heart breaking.\"","At this moment, as if things weren't chaotic enough, the phone rang.","Looking at the angered Si Nian, Zhou Yueshen stood still for a moment before choosing to go and end the noisy ringing.","But he heard Yu Dong's tearful voice on the other end: \"the Boss, I'm heartbroken.\"","Zhou Yueshen: ?","Yu Dong: \"I saw it. Qianqian came to our restaurant to eat with another man.\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","Zhou Yueshen frowned. \"What does her eating with a man have to do with you being heartbroken?\"","Yu Dong was extremely depressed: \"How does it not? I only went back home to inherit the family fortune so I could pursue her, and now she's with another guy. How could I not be sad!\"","A rare flash of surprise crossed Zhou Yueshen's face: \"You like Fu Qianqian?\"","Yu Dong: \"? You didn't know?\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"?\"","Yu Dong was exasperated: \"Wasn't I obvious enough? Any good brother could tell, but you didn't see it!\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...I didn't see it.\"","However, he finally understood, and a bit of sympathy for Yu Dong crept into his tone.","Hearing this, Yu Dong almost burst into tears. \"the Boss, I called you looking for comfort, not for you to stab me in the heart.\"","\"But don't tell Eldest Sister-in-law about this. I'm afraid she'll laugh at me. However, could you help me ask Eldest Sister-in-law to find out how far along Qianqian and that man have progressed?\"","Zhou Yueshen fell silent.","He subconsciously tilted his head to look at the slender figure on the sofa.","His brows furrowed slightly.","He realized his current situation was even more miserable than Yu Dong's.","But thinking of the relationship between Fu Qianqian and Si Nian, he coughed and called out softly: \"Niannian, Yu Dong is looking for you.\"","Si Nian was still a little angry. Her precious rose had already formed buds, and just like that, it was gone.","But hearing that Yu Dong was looking for her, she couldn't just ignore it, so she stood up, walked over to Zhou Yueshen, and asked with a frown: \"What does he want with me!\"","Her tone was not good at all.","Zhou Yueshen's eyelids twitched, and he subconsciously said: \"He's heartbroken and wants you to help him reconcile with Fu Qianqian.\"","Yu Dong: \"?\"","What kind of wild rumor was this?","Hearing this, Si Nian was instantly surprised.","Forgetting her anger at Zhou Yueshen, she stepped forward and asked gossipy: \"When did those two start dating?\"","Zhou Yueshen shook his head, indicating he didn't know.","Seeing her get closer, he subconsciously wrapped his arm around her shoulder. Seeing that she didn't push him away, his brows gradually relaxed, and he handed the receiver to her ear.","Si Nian spoke to Yu Dong while holding onto his hand, \"Yu Dong, what's going on between you and Qianqian?\"","Yu Dong wanted to cry but had no tears: \"Eldest Sister-in-law, there's no such thing. the Boss doesn't know the situation and is talking nonsense, don't believe him.\"","Si Nian cast a suspicious glance at Zhou Yueshen.","Zhou Yueshen's dark eyes flickered, actually looking a bit guilty.","Si Nian shot him a look that said 'I'll settle this with you later', and only then did she take the time to understand Yu Dong's situation.","It turned out that this morning, Yu Dong was happily going to the restaurant, only to see Fu Qianqian and a pretentious man in a suit going to his family's restaurant to eat.","That wasn't even the worst part.","The worst part was that the man was treating her to a meal, and Fu Qianqian enthusiastically said that since she was friends with him, they could get a 40% discount on the meal!","Who could understand his pain?","After listening, Si Nian also felt that he was quite a miserable guy.","She coughed and said she would help him ask about the situation, but she couldn't help much beyond that.","After all, it wasn't appropriate for Si Nian to interfere in other people's romantic affairs.","She also didn't want to play matchmaker and force the two together.","It was best to let these things take their natural course.","However, Yu Dong's feelings were indeed too inconspicuous. If he hadn't asked her privately, Si Nian wouldn't have even known he had his eyes on Fu Qianqian.","After promising the utterly distraught Yu Dong, Si Nian hung up the phone.","Zhou Yueshen immediately let go of her.","Before Si Nian could find fault with him, he said: \"I'll go see how Xiao Dong is doing with the cooking.\"","Then he went into the kitchen.","Si Nian sighed. This man seemed honest on the surface, but in reality, he was quite sly.","She went out to see Second Child still exercising there, covered in sweat, and called him inside to wash his hands and eat.","Just as she was about to enter the kitchen to help, she saw blood on Zhou Yueshen's hand.","Si Nian was startled. \"What happened to you? Did you cut your hand?\"","Zhou Yueshen gave an \"Mhm.\"","He added: \"I was just thinking about going to buy a new flowerpot. If there are any patterns you like, I'll go look for them for you.\"","Hearing this, Si Nian frowned. She knew a man who had professionally cut meat for thirty years without ever injuring himself wouldn't be this careless. Was it really because she had given him attitude earlier that made him overthink? Was that why he was so anxious to go buy a flowerpot?","Was I being a little too harsh? Si Nian thought with a twinge of guilt as she looked for some gauze to bandage his wound. Alright, I don't really blame you. That rose can survive if it is planted in the dirt. Since the vase is broken, let's just plant it alongside the vegetables.","Zhou Yueshen murmured his agreement.","The atmosphere between the two had just softened as they walked out together.","Then they saw Second Child, who had just washed his hands and sat at the table, stirring the pot without a care in the world. Mom, Mom! Dad didn't break your brick on purpose. He was just showing me how tough he is. He also ruined the flower you spent half a year growing. Dad is really so careless, not meticulous like me. I am very careful when I water Mom's roses every day.","Zhou Yueshen: ...","President Zhou: His fists clenched."]},{"number":396,"title":"Chapter 396: Fang Bowen's Departure","paragraphs":["Zhou Yueshen: \"......\"","He rubbed his brow. When did this kid learn to be so mischievous? He was truly harder to please than his mother.","Now he even dared to secretly criticize him.","It seemed he had been too gentle with him.","Si Nian smiled and cast a sidelong glance at Zhou Yueshen, saying, \"Little Han is right. Your dad is too careless. From now on, Mom's roses will all be raised by Little Han.\"","Zhou Yueshen choked on his words again.","They had just agreed not to be mad anymore.","Well, it turned out that Little Han's grudge-holding nature was learned from Nian Nian.","Having received his mother's praise, the Second Child was immediately even happier.","He wasn't even afraid of his dad's stoic face anymore, and happily ate two more bowls of rice.","After criticizing his dad, he still wasn't satisfied, and went on to crusade against his older brother. \"Big brother, the rice you cook doesn't smell as good as Mom's. Mom's cooking is tastier.\"","Zhou Zedong shot him a dark, sidelong glance.","Turning around, he modestly said to Si Nian, \"Mom, I will study even harder.\"","Si Nian patted his head and told him to take his time. Looking at the Second Child with his nose pointing to the sky, she realized he was truly spoiled by her.","Offending his dad wasn't enough for him just now; he also wanted to offend his older brother.","Thinking of this, Si Nian deliberately kept a straight face and said, \"Little Han, you are the younger brother. You can't point fingers at your older brother. He already did a very good job.\"","\"Taking away one little red flower will serve as a lesson. Don't let it happen again, understand?\"","Zhou Zehan's smug smile instantly froze.","Before he could pretend to be pitiful, Si Nian said, \"Nothing can be accomplished without rules. From now on, if you say the wrong thing or do the wrong thing, you must accept punishment. If you do well, I will reward you with a little red flower. If you do wrong, I will similarly take one back. Understand?\"","\"Through his own hard work, Little Dong now has ten little red flowers, which can be exchanged for a reward. Take a day off tomorrow. Studying all day isn't good either.\"","\"Little Han only has five flowers. With one deducted, you have four left. Keep working hard.\"","\"Do you have any questions?\"","The two children: \"......\" How could they dare to have any questions.","They would thank the heavens as long as their little red flowers weren't deducted.","Zhou Zehan regretted it to death.","If he had known this would happen, he wouldn't have said his brother's rice wasn't as tasty as his mom's.","Boohoo, he was wrong!","Si Nian added, \"Right, besides you two, your younger sister also has little red flowers. Yesterday she recited three poems, earning one little red flower. Today she finished learning a hundred characters, earning another. Now your sister already has two little red flowers.\"","Yaoyao happily raised her spoon: \"Little red flower~ Little red flower~ I'm going to surpass bad second brother.\"","The little girl still remembered when the Second Child said he was going to secretly run away with Mom and leave them behind.","Ever since then, Yaoyao felt that her second brother was a little baddie.","Zhou Zehan's little face flushed red with shame.","He hurriedly shoveled rice into his mouth. No, he had to work hard to get back the lost little red flower.","Watching his youngest son's deflated expression, the corners of Zhou Yueshen's mouth curled up into an arc.","However, the next second, he couldn't escape his doom either. Si Nian finally turned her head and said to him, \"Zhou Yueshen, you broke a brick and a vase today. That won't do. I'm publicly criticizing you this once. Next time you break my things, you'll sleep with the Second Child.\"","Zhou Yueshen's smile instantly froze, and he nodded with a wooden face.","The Second Child immediately became happy.","At night, Zhou Yueshen took the initiative to boil water for Si Nian to take a bath.","Si Nian never made it very obvious when she was angry, but she wasn't petty either. Her anger came quickly and faded just as fast.","If you tactfully admitted your mistake, she might forgive you immediately.","But the most terrifying thing about women isn't their anger, but their tendency to bring up old scores.","Si Nian was originally happily preparing to take a bath, but seeing the water in the tub struck a chord and reminded her of her roses. Although Zhou Yueshen had already planted them in the soil, flowers could easily die if not careful when repotting.","She had thought that if this rose plant survived, it would prove she had a talent for growing flowers and plants. In the future, not only could she create a rose garden, but she could also take rose baths all the time.","However, while her imagination was so beautiful, reality was cruel.","So she began to torment Zhou Yueshen.","Resting her hands against the edge of the bathtub, she called out, \"Zhou Yueshen, the water is a bit cold.\"","In the room, Zhou Yueshen, who was coaxing their daughter to sleep, heard the noise and immediately went downstairs to bring up hot water.","The bathroom was steaming hot, and the scorching summer heat and the air instantly condensed into mist on the man's body.","On such a hot day, only Si Nian would take a hot bath.","Zhou Yueshen always took cold showers.","\"What's wrong?\"","He looked at Si Nian's slightly furrowed brows and asked in a low voice.","Si Nian sighed, \"I want to take a rose bath.\"","In the past, when she was tired from work, she would always go home and prepare bathwater, inevitably accompanied by flower petals and red wine.","She enjoyed the solitary tipsiness.","Yet now, looking at this older man, the solitude was gone, the red wine was gone, and the atmospheric fragrant roses were gone too.","Zhou Yueshen: \"......\" She was actually still brooding over this matter.","Zhou Yueshen pulled a bath towel from the rack next to him and said in a low voice, \"It's hot, don't soak for too long.\"","Si Nian liked the temperature a bit high, and since the day was hot, soaking too long would make her whole body go soft.","He leaned over and gently wiped the water droplets from her face.","\"Put on your clothes. I'll take Yaoyao back to her room to sleep.\"","Si Nian hummed a response, and watching him walk out with slightly hurried steps, she finally revealed a sly smile.","By the time Zhou Yueshen took their daughter back to her room to sleep and returned, Si Nian was already lying down, looking as if she had fallen asleep.","Helplessly, he went into the bathroom to wash up, before pulling back the covers to get into bed and pulling her into his arms to hold her.","Si Nian couldn't pretend anymore and kicked him. \"It's hot. Don't touch me.\"","Zhou Yueshen almost laughed out of frustration.","The Second Child was still working hard at this moment. Zhou Zedong was doing his homework, and seeing that he still looked so energetic, he couldn't help but say, \"Mom said exercising at night will stop you from growing taller.\"","The Second Child instantly froze.","He immediately got into bed to sleep.","In less than two minutes, he started snoring.","The next day, Zhou Yueshen didn't need to drag him out of bed; the Second Child got up on his own.","His hard-working appearance made even the older man raise an eyebrow.","\"Dad, I'm going to run six kilometers today. Don't try to talk me out of it.\"","Since he couldn't train at night, he had to exercise more during the day.","Zhou Yueshen: \"......\"","\"Dad, I'll do squats for another half an hour today. I'm not tired at all.\"","Although Jiang Jiu couldn't keep up, after this period of exercise, his physical stamina had also improved a lot.","His soft, chubby flesh had even started to firm up a bit.","After Zhou Yueshen finished training his son, he went out again.","Although he had been spending more and more time at home recently, he still mostly had to go out to do things during the day.","He was running around outside every day.","But the Second Child couldn't rest easy; Zhou Yueshen had also left homework for him.","Zhou Zedong was resting today and took his younger sister out to the amusement park to play.","Watching his younger brother do push-ups, he didn't show the slightest hint of embarrassment.","The Second Child ground his missing teeth in frustration.","Si Nian felt that she had been a bit decadent lately. She didn't need to work or study, just occasionally read books and take care of the kids.","The three children were now becoming more and more sensible; they could cook and clean the house.","Zhou Yueshen was coming home more often to help out with the chores, so for a while, she couldn't find anything to do.","Now, the idlest ones in the whole family were her and Da Huang.","All day long, it was just eating and sleeping, sleeping and eating.","She vaguely felt that she had gained quite a bit of weight around her belly.","Just as she was lying on the lounge chair soaking up the sun, there was a knock on the door.","She looked over and saw it was the Fang family from next door.","It was Xiao Yi and Fang Bowen. Fang Bowen was wearing a backpack, and Xiao Yi was carrying a luggage bag in his hand.","Si Nian raised an eyebrow slightly, stood up, and went over to greet them.","\"Comrade Xiao, student Fang Bowen, are you heading out?\"","Second Child also cast a curious glance over.","Xiao Yi swept his gaze across the courtyard, and seeing that it was only Si Nian and Second Child, he said, \"Yes, I plan to take little Bowen back to Beijing. Staying here any longer isn't a long-term solution. I came specifically to say goodbye to you and to thank you for taking care of Bowen before.\"","Holding his father's hand, Fang Bowen's expression was a bit complicated, carrying a faint hint of reluctance to part: \"Teacher Si, I am leaving with my dad. I will remember you.\"","Si Nian smiled and patted his head.","Looking at Fang Bowen, his complexion had indeed improved a lot.","It seemed Xiao Yi had planned to take Fang Bowen away earlier, but because the boy's health was poor, he had been recuperating here.","It made sense; a place like Beijing was more suitable for this child.","As for Fang Hui, it seemed she would have to serve a few months in prison here before she could leave.","\"Alright, your teacher will remember you too.\"","Xiao Yi withdrew his gaze from the courtyard and said, \"Teacher Si, I've heard quite a bit about your situation. Congratulations on becoming the provincial top scorer in the science college entrance exam this time. You'll probably choose to go to Beijing for your future development as well, right?\"","Si Nian nodded slightly.","Previously, the school had delivered her admission letter in such an exaggerated manner that it caused a sensation throughout the entire neighborhood, so it wasn't surprising that Xiao Yi had seen it.","Of course, Si Nian didn't plan to celebrate it again, so she hadn't mentioned the matter since.","Xiao Yi said, \"To tell you the truth, I serve as a law professor at Beijing University. If you ever need anything or require any help, you can contact me.\"","Si Nian was slightly surprised.","She knew Xiao Yi was an intellectual just by looking at him.","But she hadn't expected him to be a professor.","No wonder he only came now; the universities were currently on summer break.","Although surprised, Si Nian didn't say much and just nodded slightly.","Her unperturbed demeanor made Xiao Yi take an extra look at her. He left his business card and phone number, saying sincerely, \"I hope there will be a chance for us to meet again in the future.\"","Si Nian smiled, nodded, and said definitely.","After speaking, Xiao Yi looked at his son.","Fang Bowen bit his lip, looking somewhat conflicted.","He looked at Second Child, who was eavesdropping in the distance, wanting to say something.","But he couldn't bring himself to say it.","Xiao Yi smiled and asked, \"Bowen, aren't you going to say anything to your little friend?\"","\"You're leaving, and in the future... you might never see him again.\"","As soon as those last words were spoken, Fang Bowen's eyes instantly turned red.","Actually, growing up, he had never made any friends.","Because his mother didn't let him play with kids who had bad grades, he was always studying and had never made a true friend.","Second Child was the first person to play with him.","It was the first time he had received food from someone else.","The first time he played Gomoku with someone his own age.","The first time someone came to visit him when he was sick.","Fang Bowen was actually very happy in his heart, but even though his dad had given him so much time, he hadn't been able to take the initiative to come over and play with them even once to fulfill his final wish.","Hearing his dad say they might never see each other again, he suddenly felt very sad, and tears welled up uncontrollably.","He blinked and choked out, \"I... I, Dad, I can't say it.\"","Seeing him cry, Si Nian quickly turned and called Second Child over.","Second Child was still confused. Seeing Fang Bowen turn his face away to cry secretly, he asked in bewilderment, \"What's wrong, Mom? Why is Fang Bowen crying?\"","Fang Bowen said loudly, \"I, I'm not crying.\"","Second Child said, \"You are clearly crying.\"","Fang Bowen had been very sad just a moment ago, but now he somehow couldn't cry anymore.","Si Nian explained, \"Fang Bowen is leaving with his dad to live in a city far away.\"","\"Fang Bowen wants to say goodbye to you.\"","Upon hearing this, Second Child's expression immediately grew solemn. \"Is he taking a long, long train to a place very far away?\"","Si Nian nodded.","Second Child instantly felt a bit sad as well. Although he hadn't interacted with Fang Bowen much, he already considered him a friend.","\"Mom, does he have to leave?\"","Unable to say words of parting, he asked Si Nian miserably.","Si Nian shook her head.","Second Child asked again, \"Mom, then will he ever come back?\"","Si Nian shook her head again.","Second Child fell silent.","For a moment, he didn't know what to do.","Usually the one to liven up the atmosphere, he was now too sad to say a single word.","Fang Bowen felt like crying again. Seeing him with his head down and lips pursed, he said, \"Idiot, what's there to be sad about? We're not even that close anyway.\"","Second Child pouted, \"Of course I'm sad. I haven't even beaten you at Gomoku yet.\"","Fang Bowen: \".....\"","Xiao Yi laughed, \"Alright now. If you want to meet, it won't be that hard. Auntie Si will be going to Beijing in the future too. If it's meant to be, you'll naturally see each other again. Let's go.\"","Si Nian nodded slightly.","Fang Bowen clenched his small fists, though his mouth remained very stubborn: \"I don't want to see him at all. I just can't bear to leave Teacher Si.\"","After saying that, he looked at Zhou Zehan's expression and added, \"You, you need to study hard from now on.\"","With that, he turned around heartlessly.","Wearing an expression that said he had nothing more to add.","Si Nian couldn't help but be amused.","It wasn't until the two silhouettes, one large and one small, had walked far away that Si Nian looked down at her son.","Only to see him wearing a look of deep disappointment: \"Mom, tell me, why do people always have to part ways?\""]},{"number":397,"title":"Chapter 397: Misunderstanding","paragraphs":["Si Nian was slightly stunned.","Then she said, \"Because everyone has their own life. Besides friends, Fang Bowen has his family, who are even more important. He will spend his future with them. We are just passers-by in his life. With a bit of luck, maybe we will meet again in the future, but Fang Bowen's father is right: this parting might be for a lifetime.\"","Zhou Yuehan seemed to only half-understand, but he said seriously, \"Mom, I will never leave you for my whole life.\"","Si Nian smiled and rubbed his head. There was no need for her to say much about things so far in the future.","When he grew up, he would naturally understand.","In early August, the weather was hot and stuffy.","Lin's mother called Si Nian, saying she had discussed with her father about sending the two children to the city for school in the second half of the year.","The two younger brothers were very happy on the phone.","Only then did Si Nian realize it was already August.","In late August, around the twenties, she would have to report to Jing University.","Zhou Yueshen had also been busy from dawn to dusk these past few days, and she had forgotten to discuss going to Jing City with him.","Si Nian had already made up her mind.","There were two choices, and no matter which one Zhou Yueshen chose, she would be fine with it.","First, she could go report to the university, take a leave of absence, and come back to continue her studies when the children were a bit older.","Second, she could hire a nanny to take care of the children, go report to the university, and finish her college courses in a year or two.","Since she had already been to college once, graduating early wouldn't be difficult.","But she couldn't just not go.","Although she was reluctant to part with the children, sometimes there was no other way.","Life couldn't always go exactly as one wished.","Coming to this era and being able to live such a carefree and happy life for a period of time, she owed a lot to the older man's help.","Moreover, she had promised him before that she could take a leave of absence first and wait until the children were older to study.","She couldn't go back on her word.","Therefore, no matter what Zhou Yueshen chose, she could accept it.","It just so happened that her parents were coming into the city to do business. If they came, they could help take care of the children, which would be good.","Family members were always much more reliable.","While thinking about this, Si Nian rode her bicycle to the hospital for a physical examination.","The hospital wasn't far, so she couldn't be bothered to take a taxi.","After refusing her little tag-alongs, she rode off quickly on her bicycle.","After all, it was a hospital. Bringing a few little cubs and having to look after them would affect her efficiency.","Because the college entrance examination was over and most people had received their admission notices, there were quite a few students who came early to get their medical examination reports.","Si Nian didn't expect to run into a group of students who came together for their check-ups, and that they would recognize her.","When they greeted her, Si Nian looked around to see if there was anyone else nearby. Only after confirming they were talking to her did she ask, \"Who are you?\"","Several young men and women of her age looked at her excitedly. \"Student Si Nian, don't you recognize us? We are your classmates.\"","Hearing this, Si Nian couldn't help but feel embarrassed.","Although they were classmates, she hadn't attended a single class, except for going to the classroom twice after the college entrance exams.","She didn't know a single one of them at all.","At this moment, she couldn't name any of them.","She could only say awkwardly, \"Hello.\"","\"I heard you got into Jing University. You're so amazing!\"","\"With her scores, she deserves to go anywhere. Look at how ignorant you are.\"","\"Yeah, yeah. Although we also got in, it's just to second-rate schools. There's no harm without comparison.\"","Si Nian didn't know what to say, so she could only nod and agree politely.","Seeing that she didn't talk much, the few boys couldn't find anything to say for a moment. They pushed each other back and forth, and one of them was pushed forward.","His face was completely red.","Seeing his expression, Si Nian raised an eyebrow. \"What's wrong?\"","He scratched his head, looking youthful and inexperienced.","\"I-I'm sorry, Student Si. Last time we wanted to invite you to go singing, but your father seemed a bit unhappy. We don't know if he blamed you for it. If he did, we want to apologize to you.\"","Si Nian: \"? My father? Who?\"","He replied, \"On the day we checked the answers. You were busy checking answers with the homeroom teacher, and we didn't want to bother you, so we went to ask your father.\"","Hearing this, Si Nian thought about it for a long time before she realized what they meant. Her mouth twitched as she said, \"Are you talking about the man who went with me?\"","\"Yes.\"","The others chimed in as well.","\"Speaking of which, Comrade Si, your dad looks so young!\"","\"Yeah, he looks no different from a thirty-year-old, and he's very fit and sturdy. No wonder he raised you so well.\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","Stop talking.","If they continued, she wouldn't be able to look Zhou Yueshen in the eye anymore.","So that day when Zhou Yueshen suddenly wanted to buy new clothes and get his hair done, it was because of this?","And that was the reason he wore that white shirt every day even though it didn't fit perfectly?","Si Nian rubbed her forehead.","Seeing the group's serious expressions, she sighed.","\"You misunderstood.\"","\"Ah? Misunderstood?\"","The group exchanged glances.","\"Does that mean your dad didn't blame you?\"","\"That's great. I've been a bit worried about this all along.\"","After all, for Si Nian to get such good grades without even attending school, they guessed that her family must be very strict.","Let alone allowing her to do things like going out to sing.","Si Nian looked at the clear and innocent faces in front of her and said with a headache, \"What I mean is, he is not my dad.\"","Before they could speak, she added, \"He is my husband.\"","The group instantly performed a disappearing smile trick right there: \"...\"","Just as Si Nian finished speaking, her name was called.","She immediately went in for her physical examination.","It was over quickly.","She nodded slightly to the group, who were still standing there with their mouths open in shock, and left first.","As soon as she walked out of the hospital, she saw Fu Qianqian getting out of a car.","Si Nian was slightly stunned.","Previously, Yu Dong had told her about Fu Qianqian eating with a man, thinking that Fu Qianqian was dating someone.","Si Nian had consistently believed this was a misunderstanding.","After all, she felt that someone with Fu Qianqian's personality didn't seem like the type to understand romance and date.","Instead, she seemed like someone who wanted to grow old alone.","So she had always maintained a skeptical attitude.","She didn't expect that right now, she was actually with a man and had come to the hospital.","When she saw the man get out of the car, Si Nian was even more surprised.","It was actually Wu Ren'ai?","Her gaze shifted between the two of them, and then she looked back at the hospital. Had their relationship already progressed to this stage?","Fu Qianqian also saw her and looked surprised. \"Si Nian, why are you here?\"","Wu Ren'ai also looked up at her, his face full of pleasant surprise.","Si Nian's expression was peculiar. \"I'm here for a physical examination. But what about you? Why did you come to the hospital, and with Teacher Wu?\"","Speaking of which, Wu Ren'ai had known her since childhood, so he definitely knew Fu Qianqian as well.","Fu Qianqian held her stomach and groaned a couple of times. \"I ate too much, and my stomach is painfully bloated, so I came to the hospital to get it checked.\"","Si Nian: \"...\" How could someone of her age eat so much that they had to go to the hospital?","\"Then why are you two together...\"","Si Nian originally didn't want to ask about this kind of topic, but since Yu Dong had asked for her help, she had to find out the truth for him anyway.","To let him give up with a clear understanding.","Fu Qianqian said with a complicated expression, \"Sigh, it's a complicated story.\"","Before she could finish her sentence, someone walked over. \"Qianqian, are you alright? Oh my, come inside quickly and let Auntie take a look.\"","With that, she glared at her son standing to the side. \"What are you just standing there for? Hurry up and help Qianqian inside.\" Seeing that his attention was elsewhere, she finally noticed Si Nian. She froze for a moment, then frowned slightly. \"Why is it you?\"","Meeting the woman's displeased gaze, Si Nian asked in confusion, \"And you are?\"","The woman scoffed, \"Oh, look at you, so successful now that you don't even remember the people from the compound. Truly, important people have short memories.\"","Fu Qianqian whispered, \"That's Wu Ren'ai's mother, the one who has disliked you since we were kids.\"","Si Nian was slightly taken aback.","Even the original owner of this body didn't remember things from so long ago, so how could she possibly know?","Seeing her bewildered expression, Fu Qianqian whispered another reminder.","It was mostly because when they were young, Wu Ren'ai used to follow Si Nian around like a lost puppy, completely mesmerized by her. However, Si Nian looked down on him and chased after Fu Yang instead.","The Wu family held a grudge over this, feeling that Si Nian had unrealistically high standards and was a snob.","But even ten bulls couldn't drag their son away from his crush on her. Left with no choice, they sent him abroad to study. Yet, after coming back, he still pined for Si Nian. Just like Fu Yang, he was twenty-five or twenty-six and refused to get married.","Because of this, Mother Wu was extremely furious.","She had never thought highly of the old Si Nian. Even though in the eyes of outsiders, Si Nian was the smartest girl in the compound, her son had been a genius since childhood, a peer of Fu Yang, and now he even held a PhD.","Even if Si Nian had scored the highest in the college entrance exams, it was nothing special to her.","Moreover, Si Nian was now married and a stepmother to three children. The fact that her son was still longing for such a woman made Mother Wu feel even more uncomfortable.","Recently, since Fu Yang had run away, the pressure to get married had fallen onto Fu Qianqian's shoulders.","She was nineteen now, no longer young, and had reached the right age.","The Wu family was also busy looking for a match. The Fu family's background was definitely well-matched with theirs, so after some back-and-forth, they thought of setting the two up.","Besides, the two had known each other since childhood.","Mother Wu was now treating Fu Qianqian like her own daughter-in-law.","Who would have thought they would bump into Si Nian at this moment, and that her son would be staring at her with such an infatuated look? How could Mother Wu possibly feel happy about this?","Si Nian was also speechless.","Wu Ren'ai was extremely embarrassed. Forgetting to even say hello, he hurriedly tugged at his mother and said, \"Mom, what nonsense are you talking about? Si Nian isn't that kind of person.\"","Si Nian said, \"Your mother is right. I really did forget her.\"","Mother Wu was speechless.","Pointing at her with a trembling finger, she said, \"You, just look at her!\"","Wu Ren'ai's mouth twitched. \"That's enough, Mom. Let's go inside and get Qianqian checked out quickly.\"","Si Nian pulled Fu Qianqian aside and asked about the situation between the two of them.","She honestly couldn't see a hint of romantic chemistry between them; they didn't match at all.","Fu Qianqian said, \"No, we aren't dating.\"","Si Nian looked at her suspiciously, \"Then why did you go out to eat with him?\"","Fu Qianqian replied, \"A free meal is a free meal. Why wouldn't I eat it?\"","Si Nian was speechless. \"I surrender to you.\"","Did she not know that Yu Dong's hair was turning white from worrying over this very matter?","Poor Yu Dong. Falling for someone so dense must be karma from a past life.","However, since there were no feelings involved, it shouldn't be a big deal.","Wu Ren'ai didn't look like he was capable of being in a relationship anyway.","Si Nian sighed and left.","Fu Qianqian was made very uncomfortable by Mother Wu's overwhelming enthusiasm. Seeing Si Nian leave, and feeling that she had digested her food enough, she quickly made her escape as well.","Mother Wu thought she was upset, which made sense. Her blind date was staring at another woman right in front of her, completely ignoring the fact that she was feeling unwell. What girl could tolerate that?","The more she thought about it, the angrier she got. She pinched Wu Ren'ai's ear hard. \"You stubborn fool! She is already married. What is the use of pining after her? What is wrong with Qianqian? She is a broadcaster now, a proper job. How does she not compare to that Si Nian?\"","Wu Ren'ai hissed in pain. Hearing this, he frowned and said, \"I don't think there is anything bad about her, I just think she is a bit dense.\"","Mother Wu was speechless.","When Fu Qianqian returned home and Ms. Zheng saw she was alone, she was quite angry. \"What happened? Why did you come back by yourself? Where is Little Wu?\"","Fu Qianqian threw her hands up. \"It didn't work out.\"","Ms. Zheng said angrily, \"What do you mean? Didn't you two go out to eat together? He is such a good person, honest and smart, and he is a teacher. What are you dissatisfied with?\"","Fu Qianqian said, \"I am not really dissatisfied, I just feel like he is a bit lacking in love...\"","Ms. Zheng was speechless.","Returning home, Si Nian placed all her medical checkup reports on the table.","The children gathered around to look, and it stated that all indicators were normal.","Second Child showed off the few words he knew in his head, teaching Yaoyao how to read them.","After training with Zhou Yueshen for a month, the child had lost some weight and gotten quite a bit tanner.","Because he had to do homework, his recent training sessions had decreased a bit.","Only now did he have the free time to show off.","Si Nian called Yu Dong and told him about the situation between Fu Qianqian and Wu Ren'ai.","Knowing that he hadn't lost his chance at love, Yu Dong finally breathed a sigh of relief.","Si Nian added, \"But even without Wu Ren'ai, there will be others. After all, Fu Qianqian is not young anymore and has reached marriageable age. If you do not make a move, the next time she goes out to eat with someone else, I won't be able to help you ask about it.\"","Yu Dong immediately deflated. \"Then what should I do? I... I don't know how to court her.\"","Si Nian said, \"Isn't courting her easy?\"","It was just that he was overcomplicating Fu Qianqian in his own mind.","\"Next time you invite her to eat, I guarantee she will go.\"","Yu Dong replied, \"I thought about that too, but I can't just invite her out to eat every single time.\"","Si Nian said, \"Let me teach you. In the future, when you go look for her, do not say you are treating her to a meal. Tell her you have developed a new dish and invite her to be your taste tester. This way, every time you make a new dish, you can ask her to come over. It is relaxed and will not seem awkward.\"","\"If she agrees, you can find an opportunity to invite her to watch a movie or go to an amusement park under the pretext of thanking her for her help. If you two still cannot get along after all that, then there is nothing more I can do to help. It would just mean you are not suitable for each other, and you should find someone else.\"","Just as Si Nian finished speaking, she heard a man's deep voice behind her. \"What is not suitable?\"","She turned around to look. Zhou Yueshen had returned at some unknown point and was standing right behind her.","He was holding her medical report in his hand.","Si Nian paused for a moment. Hearing Yu Dong's excited voice on the other end of the line, she casually dismissed him.","Glancing at the report in Zhou Yueshen's hand, she said, \"You are back. Perfect timing, I have something to tell you.\""]},{"number":398,"title":"Chapter 398: Sitting at Home, Money Falls from the Sky (5000)","paragraphs":["Zhou Yueshen paused slightly, then said, \"What a coincidence, I have something to tell you too.\"","Si Nian looked at him.","He had something to tell her?","What was it?","Speaking of which, why did he come back so early today?","Si Nian asked curiously, \"What is it?\"","Zhou Yueshen put down the medical report in his hand and said, \"A few friends and I partnered up for some new business.\"","Si Nian had a vague impression of it. \"Is it the investment you mentioned before?\"","Zhou Yueshen gave a slight nod.","\"Actually, when we first came to the city, we started discussing investments. The areas of investment included some real estate and electrical appliance manufacturing factories.\"","\"But with investment comes risk. A brother of mine has over a dozen houses he can't sell, and now he's stuck with them.\"","\"As for the appliance factory, we have the right channels, so we did make some profit. We've been reaping the dividends for the past half year.\"","After saying that, Zhou Yueshen pulled a bankbook out of his pocket and handed it to Si Nian.","\"This is a new account I opened. The dividends are inside. You can keep it.\"","Si Nian: Huh? What?","She was just sitting at home, and money literally fell from the sky.","She slowly took the bankbook and opened it to take a look.","She figured that for a few months' work, the dividend should be around a few thousand yuan, right?","Although she didn't know how big the manufacturing business Zhou Yueshen mentioned was.","Her fingertips flipped open the bankbook.","Si Nian looked at the numbers on it.","Her hand trembled.","Units, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten thousands, hundred thousands... Three hundred thousand!","It was actually three hundred thousand yuan in total?","She thought she had seen two extra zeros and counted again.","Then she snapped her head up to look at Zhou Yueshen. \"Th-three hundred thousand? You earned this in just a few months?\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded slightly. \"That's right. Electrical appliances are a highly profitable industry in the city. Many people use them now, and the prices are high.\"","\"They have the channels for this, so they sell very well.\"","Speaking of which, Zhou Yueshen had been running a breeding farm for a long time.","Even with all those channels, he hadn't earned this much.","Yet in just these past few months, he had made hundreds of thousands purely from investments. No wonder so many people were willing to spend money on investments, and it was no wonder Si Nian was shocked.","At the time, he had casually invested a few tens of thousands of yuan.","Since his friend was in trouble, he hadn't expected to get so much in dividends back.","Of course, he was the largest shareholder, so he received the largest share.","This friend's family had originally gone into business, so he picked it up very quickly.","Although he had suffered losses a few times before.","But this time, he found the right direction and made a fortune all at once.","Zhou Yueshen also gained some experience from this.","During this time, he had been working from dawn to dusk, and not just busying himself with the farm.","Si Nian couldn't react for a long while. Although there were multi-millionaires and billionaires in every era, to her right now, hundreds of thousands was already an incredibly huge sum of money.","While she was still working hard to save money, her man had brought back hundreds of thousands.","Comparing oneself to others really was maddening!","Si Nian looked at Zhou Yueshen with mixed feelings. \"Then what's the deal with those houses losing money? Are the losses heavy? Where are they located?\"","In this era, there were certainly people buying and selling houses. Some who became wealthy would move to better places, and if they really had no use for their old houses, they would sell them.","However, this situation was relatively rare.","After all, those who could afford to live in better places were not short of money. To buy this kind of house, one had to rely on connections and introductions.","There weren't that many procedures in this era; a simple transaction and transfer between the two parties was enough.","There were no restrictions either.","Although housing prices weren't high, ordinary people still couldn't afford them.","Therefore, many people smelled the business opportunities back then and secretly bought a lot of properties at cheap prices.","In the end, they became billionaires in one fell swoop.","Because later on, physical housing distribution was stopped, housing distribution monetization was gradually implemented, and once the commercial housing market was launched, these houses began to appreciate in value.","Zhou Yueshen's expression remained unchanged as he slowly said, \"They aren't here. They're in Beijing—some old houses and courtyard homes over there. My friend got scammed as soon as he took over. Previously, an acquaintance of his specialized in this line of work, but this time the guy took the money and ran. Those who were eager to sell had paid quite a bit of money, and now the trouble has found its way to my friend.\"","\"Courtyard homes are meant for large families to live together, so they aren't cheap. Unless people are short of money or face unforeseen circumstances, they generally don't sell them. A single set costs tens of thousands, which ordinary people can't afford, so now everyone is clamoring for compensation.\"","Si Nian was even more shocked.","\"Courtyard homes?\"","Zhou Yueshen gave a slight nod.","\"He plans to sell them off cheaply. After all, those people signed contracts with his acquaintance. If they're hard to sell, he can only sell them at a loss and subsidize the difference himself, or pay compensation according to the contracts.\"","\"He asked if I wanted him to save one for me. I figured since you're heading to Beijing for school anyway, I had him keep one with a courtyard.\"","Si Nian hurriedly said, \"Wouldn't it be a pity to sell them at a low price?\"","Zhou Yueshen replied, \"He doesn't have the time to manage these. He wants to focus on developing the manufacturing and appliance side.\"","Si Nian immediately said, \"Then why don't you take them over from him? Look, a place like Beijing will develop rapidly in the future. Keeping these houses, even if you just rent them out, won't be a loss.\"","Si Nian couldn't very well tell Zhou Yueshen directly that in the future, a single one of these houses would be worth over a hundred million.","Even the ones in poor locations would start at tens of millions.","She had originally been agonizing over how to find the right channels if she wanted to seize the opportunity to buy some.","And now Zhou Yueshen had delivered them right to her doorstep?","Zhou Yueshen saw through her thoughts almost instantly. \"You want them?\"","Si Nian nodded and said, \"I just have a feeling that these houses will be worth a lot of money in the future.\"","Zhou Yueshen pondered for a moment. Si Nian wasn't a capricious person. Since she said so, she definitely had her own ideas.","So he said, \"Alright, I'll go talk to him and save them for you.\"","Si Nian hadn't expected him to agree without even asking why she wanted to do this.","These houses weren't cheap. If they took all of them, who knew how much it would cost.","Si Nian couldn't just watch this golden opportunity slip through her fingers.","But Zhou Yueshen's unconditional support made her feel even more secure and reassured.","She looked at him with complex eyes and said, \"Zhou Yueshen, aren't you going to ask me why? What if we buy them and get stuck with them? There are so many houses, after all.\"","\"Even though I said that, no one can predict the future for sure, right?\"","Zhou Yueshen said, \"It is a bit much, but putting them under your name will give you some security. Renting them out in the future will also bring in a considerable income. You'll be studying there for four years; having more money is never a bad thing.\"","\"If you don't want to work in the future but feel bored, being a landlord and collecting rent is also an option.\"","Si Nian felt deeply moved, but she wasn't that greedy. After all, she was the one who knew the truth of the future.","So she said, \"Of course we can't put all of them under my name. Xiaodong, Xiaohan, and Yaoyao will each get one. That way, they'll have some security when they grow up. We'll split the rest equally between the two of us.\"","Seeing how she absolutely didn't want them to lose out, Zhou Yueshen chuckled softly and agreed.","It wasn't like he couldn't afford this amount of money. Although these houses might not make any money for the time being and could only be rented out, keeping them meant that if anything happened in the future, they could at least recoup their costs by reselling them.","He looked at Si Nian and asked in a low voice, \"What did you want to tell me?\"","Si Nian snapped out of her daydream of becoming a super billionaire, finally remembering what she had planned.","So, she told him and the children about her decision.","At first, the children didn't quite understand what they were saying about houses and such.","None of them paid much attention.","But now, upon hearing Si Nian say she was going to university, they all immediately whipped their heads around to look at her, their faces filled with tension.","They all knew that the university their mother had gotten into was very far away, in the capital city.","She would only be able to come home during the holidays.","Of course, they didn't want her to go.","But their father had said that it was the best school in the country.","They couldn't stop their mother from going just because they couldn't bear to part with her.","He also forbade them from bringing it up, afraid of putting pressure on Si Nian.","So, none of the children dared to mention this matter.","They hadn't expected Si Nian to bring it up herself today.","And she even let them choose.","They didn't want to pick either of the two options. Couldn't they just stay with their mother forever?","Why did their mother have to take a leave of absence to stay home and take care of them? They could also take a break from school to go take care of her.","They were still young; it wouldn't matter if they took their time with their studies.","But their mother had already reached the final step.","Yet she had to take a step back for their sake.","If their father didn't let their mother go and made her suspend her studies, then they would never speak to him again.","Zhou Yueshen listened quietly until she finished, then spoke calmly, \"I've thought about this.\"","He looked at Si Nian and said in a deep voice, \"I plan to take the children and go to Jing City with you.\"","\"I've already found a house.\"","\"Transferring schools won't be a hassle, and I also want to go out and make a living there for a few years.\"","She had always been moving forward, and Zhou Yueshen had tried hard to catch up with her.","But later he realized that with his status as a pig farmer, it was too difficult.","That was why he had wavered when a friend invited him to invest.","In the past, he never believed in such things.","But Si Nian's appearance made him take that step.","And it was precisely this step that allowed him to stand by her side without hesitation, walking shoulder to shoulder with her indefinitely.","When the children heard this.","They were also extremely happy.","Second Child bounced up and down, saying, \"Dad, Dad, does that mean I can ride the long train again?\"","Seeing the excited and expectant smiles on the children's faces, Zhou Yueshen knew he had made the right decision.","Because no matter which option Si Nian had given, it would always leave some regret.","The children couldn't bear to leave her, and neither could he.","But making her stay behind, Zhou Yueshen couldn't do such a thing.","Of course, he wasn't unprepared for the move to Jing City.","The breeding farm couldn't be disbanded; their roots were in this city, and they would definitely return in the future.","The breeding farm in their hometown had now increased the villagers' income, and Zhou Yueshen had invested half of the profits into building rural roads.","While other villages still had muddy, potholed paths, their village already had paved roads.","Driving had become much more convenient.","As his own life got better, it was only natural to help boost the village's economic development.","It was all worth it; even if there was no return, it could be considered accumulating good karma.","Zhou Yueshen had killed too many animals, and his hands were stained with blood.","If doing these good deeds could earn merit, he hoped it would all fall upon Si Nian and the children.","Then it would be worth it.","He patted his son's head and said, \"Of course.\"","Ever since learning that the whole family was moving north, the household became lively again.","However, upon hearing the news, Jiang Jiu grew sadder by the day.","Although Second Child comforted him, saying that he would definitely come back in the future, and that his dad had said they could return here as soon as his mom finished university.","It was only a few years, not a lifetime of separation.","It was better than never seeing each other again, right?","Second Child felt that he was already a mature man.","Although he really hated to leave Jiang Jiu, he wanted to be by his mother's side even more.","Because Jiang Jiu had his grandparents and his dad by his side.","But if his mom went to university alone, she would be all by herself, which would be too lonely and pitiful.","His mom was right; everyone had family members to keep them company, and friends came second.","Seeing that his sadness couldn't make them stay, Jiang Jiu knew that they were truly going to part ways this time,","and he didn't even eat when he went home.","He knew that once his Second Brother and the others left, he would go back to how he was before.","He didn't want his Second Brother to leave.","Even though his dad was now willing to come home and spend time with him.","In Jiang Jiu's heart, his Second Brother was more important than his dad.","So he made a decision. He secretly packed a bag, smashed his piggy bank, wrote a letter to his family, and went to the Zhou house with his backpack.","There were still ten days before departure.","But Zhou Zehan couldn't wait to ride the train.","The previous train ride had given him a very novel experience, and he had been thinking about it ever since.","\"Big Brother, let's bring the Gomoku board this time so we can play chess on the train.\"","\"Big Brother, how many clothes are you planning to bring?\"","\"Big Brother, can you help me pack my new clothes? I feel like they won't fit in my backpack.\"","He bounced around happily, but after his excitement, he became melancholic again.","\"Sigh... If only Little Jiang could come with us.\"","Zhou Zedong couldn't be bothered with him.","Because he was leaving, he was planning to write down more new recipes and cooking methods over the next few days to hand over to Brother Chen and the others.","That way, even if they sold pancakes for a few years, people wouldn't get tired of them.","Although he was leaving, the stall was the first business he had invested in.","So he couldn't just abandon it.","Because the decision was made late, he had no time to entertain his younger brother right now.","Si Nian was downstairs tending to her little vegetable garden.","Although she didn't plant much, it was still enough to feed their family.","It was lush, green, and very pretty.","She moved them all together so that when her parents came over, they could grow vegetables to eat, which would also save some money.","While she was watering the plants, a small figure suddenly approached.","Si Nian thought it was Second Child. Just as she was about to speak, she met Jiang Jiu's anxious gaze.","She froze for a moment. Jiang Jiu was wearing a hat, a tracksuit, sneakers, a watch on his wrist, and a backpack—looking exactly like he was ready for a long journey.","Just as she was about to ask if he was looking for Second Child to play, Jiang Jiu pulled out a large handful of pocket money and coins from his pocket and handed them to her: \"Auntie Si, I'll give you all my money. Can you take me to Jing City with you?\"","Si Nian was stunned.","Looking at the money in the child's hands, although it was in loose change, there were also about a dozen ten-yuan bills.","Then she heard Jiang Jiu say, \"I have money. You don't need to pay for me.\"","Si Nian snapped back to reality, feeling a massive headache coming on: \"Little Jiang, are you reluctant to part with Little Han?\"","Jiang Jiu nodded heavily and choked out, \"Yeah! I want to go to school and play with Second Brother.\"","Si Nian's eyes filled with complex emotions: \"What about your grandparents and your dad?\"","Jiang Jiu was silent for a moment before saying, \"I'll come back to visit them in the future.\"","Si Nian: \"......\"","What a fiercely filial child.","This kid was probably led astray by Eldest Child and Second Child.","Just as she was wondering what to do, Jiang Wenqing came running over anxiously from a distance.","In his hand, he was still holding his son's runaway letter.","It said that he was leaving to go to the faraway North with his Second Brother, telling them not to worry, and that he would come back to visit them once he made some money.","Jiang Wenqing was scared to death and hurried over.","Fortunately, the person was still there. Seeing Si Nian's helpless expression, he hurried forward and apologized, \"I'm sorry, Teacher Si, for troubling you. I didn't expect this to happen either.\"","\"Xiao Jiu, let's go home first. We need to have a good talk about this.\"","Jiang Wenqing rarely looked so serious.","Only then did Jiang Jiu start to feel a little afraid. After the impulse passed, he realized how scary his behavior had been.","A few days ago, because Auntie Si and her family were leaving, his grandparents and his dad had all been taking care of him with extreme caution.","They didn't even scold him when he slept over at Second Brother's house and didn't come home at night.","They would also buy him all kinds of food and toys every day.","Even if he accidentally did something wrong, they wouldn't get angry.","This was what had made him so bold.","Now, seeing Auntie Si looking troubled and his dad looking stern, he finally knew fear.","Biting his lip, he followed his father home.","Jiang Wenqing let go of his hand. Looking at his son's somewhat fearful eyes, he couldn't help but soften his voice, \"Xiao Jiu, do you really want to go to Jing City?\"","Jiang Jiu didn't speak.","Jiang Wenqing sighed, \"Alright, it's not that Dad really doesn't want to let you go. Your mom and younger brother are settled in Jing City, and your maternal grandparents are there too. Because of Dad's work, I just haven't taken you there. If you really want to go, I can take you.\"","Jiang Jiu's eyes immediately widened.","\"Really? Not only can I go with Second Brother, but I can also see Mom?\"","He was even more unfamiliar with the word \"Mom\" than he was with \"Dad\".","Jiang Jiu and his younger brother were twins. Their parents divorced right after they were born, and each parent took one child.","They were both workaholics, so he ended up living with his grandparents.","Although he didn't have much affection for her, Jiang Jiu couldn't help but feel a surge of happiness and anticipation.","He had finally gotten to know Second Brother and his family. Before they could spend much time together and grow up alongside each other, they were leaving, leaving him all alone here.","Although Second Brother said he would come back, in a few years, Second Brother would definitely make better friends and forget all about him.","Just thinking of this possibility made him so upset that he couldn't sleep.","Seeing his face turn to joy, Jiang Wenqing said, \"It works out well. Your grandparents are getting older and don't have the energy to take care of you anymore. This will let them have a good rest for a few years.\"","Once it was decided, Jiang Jiu immediately ran off happily to find Second Brother to share the good news.","Si Nian had still been a bit worried, but she never expected to hear that Jiang Jiu was coming along too.","She was incredibly surprised.","To think they wouldn't have to separate this time?","Da Huang, who was already an adult dog, rested his chin on his front paws and watched the family playing happily in the yard: There is no longer a Dog Mom in the world, and no one understands me, Da Huang."]},{"number":399,"title":"Chapter 399: Zhou Yueshen Offered Far Too Much","paragraphs":["Let's not talk about what Da Huang was thinking; no one could tell anyway.","On the other hand, Lin Sisi, who had been recovering for over a month, finally pulled herself together.","She had originally thought that in this life, as long as she returned to the Si family, her life would definitely be full of highlights just like Si Nian's.","But she forgot that Si Nian had received over a decade of education since childhood, which couldn't be beaten by her short one or two years of effort.","Although she had suffered many losses and lost a lot of face. Although she still couldn't sleep from jealousy and couldn't eat from distress whenever she thought about it.","She was someone who had been reborn for a second life, after all. How could she let herself become decadent because of this?","Furthermore, she had also gotten into college in this life.","Her original intention was just to get a college degree.","As long as she had this degree, combined with her knowledge of the future, she definitely wouldn't be worse than Si Nian.","Lin Sisi also thought of some business opportunities. In her previous life, Si Nian made a fortune in the garment factory and beauty industries.","In this life, Si Nian went to school, so she definitely lost the opportunity to do business.","Coupled with the lack of the Fu family's backing, it would be hard for her to build anything.","And now, all these things were in her own hands.","The most important thing now was to ease her relationship with Fu Yang. If she could give birth to a child for the Fu family, her status would naturally be secure.","She had initially worried that Si Nian would return to the city and compete with her for Fu Yang.","But seeing how sweetly Zhou Yueshen and she were getting along now, the two of them must have already done everything.","There was absolutely no chance for her and Fu Yang anymore.","Without Si Nian as a stumbling block, winning over Fu Yang was only a matter of time.","She had been foolish before, unable to resist comparing herself to Si Nian after being provoked by a few words, losing her mind and making mistakes because she was always overshadowed by her.","Looking back now, she was really too stupid.","Since Si Nian got into such a good university, she would definitely go to study.","During this time, she could find someone to invest in her business while attending school here.","By the time Si Nian returned, she might have already made a lot of money.","She wouldn't be any worse off than her.","Thinking this way, Lin Sisi felt much more at ease.","In the future, a degree wouldn't be a big deal; it just sounded enviable when mentioned.","But no matter how good the degree was, it was useless if you couldn't make money.","She enjoyed all the advantages of timing, location, and human relations, and she didn't even bother to compare herself to Si Nian.","Lin Sisi tidied herself up and planned to visit Fu Yang.","However, just as she had prepared all her lines, she heard that Fu Yang had been transferred to a remote military region, and his return date was unknown.","How could this be! This was something that hadn't happened in her previous life.","Lin Sisi refused to believe it.","However, Mrs. Zheng mocked, What's so strange about this? Military marriages are just like this, gathering little and parting much. Let alone a few months, not seeing each other for years is common. If you can't stand it, you can apply for a divorce.","She was already annoyed enough about this matter.","And Lin Sisi actually had the nerve to come to her door and ask.","At this moment, Mrs. Zheng felt that she had the potential to be a vicious mother-in-law.","Lin Sisi was completely stunned.","Fu Yang had actually been transferred away.","And his return date was unknown.","Listening to Mother Fu's tone, it seemed she really didn't know when he would be back.","Her vision went dark.","**","Time flew by.","The Lin family packed their bags and moved over.","They originally planned to rent a place outside, but Zhou Yueshen said that since they were going to Beijing with their daughter, it would be a waste to leave the house empty, so he let them live there.","It would be better to have them help watch the house, lest thieves break in to steal things while they were away.","Many things in the house couldn't be taken away, after all, the place they were going to was so far.","Lin's father and Lin's mother originally wanted to refuse, but upon hearing this, they felt it made sense and agreed.","They also said they had decided that in a few years, when conditions improved, they planned to buy a house for their eldest brother to live in.","Si Nian strongly agreed and even helped them pick a location.","Lin's mother and Lin's father had always doted on their daughter; they listened to whatever Si Nian said.","It was just that thinking about their daughter leaving again made them reluctant to part.","During the few days they had been here, Si Nian had been sleeping with Lin's mother.","At night, the mother and daughter would talk all night long.","Their relationship had become much closer than before.","Although she was reluctant, thinking that her daughter was going to college, and a prestigious one at that, Lin's mother became happy again.","For such a great and joyous event, what was there to be sad about?","Besides, her daughter said she would come back after finishing her studies.","She wasn't quite used to the North either and preferred to retire in the spring-like Yungui-Sichuan area.","Lin's mother joked about her thinking about retirement at such a young age.","Si Nian didn't say it out loud, but she thought to herself, I don't want to either, it's just that Zhou Yueshen gives me way too much.","The mother and daughter stuck together for a few days, and it was soon time to set off.","Lin's mother chased her daughter out of the room, telling her to go back to her own room to sleep.","Leaving a dumbfounded Si Nian who didn't understand why. Wasn't she just thinking of keeping her company for a few more days since she was about to leave?","Lin's mother was sharp; it wasn't like she was oblivious like her daughter. Little Zhou was just too embarrassed to say anything. As someone with experience, how could she not understand that hesitant look in his eyes every time he stared at her daughter?","Turning around, Zhou Yueshen was standing at the door. He coughed lightly and asked her, Are you coming back to sleep?","Si Nian hugged her pillow and said, Otherwise, are you going to let me sleep in the hallway?","Zhou Yueshen chuckled lightly and looked at her leisurely.","I helped you pack some things. See if there's anything else left to pack.","Si Nian walked into the room and looked at the suitcase, which was full of dresses. My goodness, when did she get so many clothes?","Looking at Zhou Yueshen's, he just had a small military bag, and it wasn't even full.","She hurriedly took all the clothes out and said, Too many, too many. Why bring so much? It's so hard to carry.","She took out a large pile and put in the ones she commonly used, but even so, they couldn't fit.","Si Nian had to stuff them into Zhou Yueshen's luggage bag.","Zhou Yueshen didn't think it was much, but seeing Si Nian's expression of fearing trouble, he didn't tell her that Lin's mother had even prepared quilts for her.","Saying that buying them over there would be troublesome.","They bought train tickets because it was too dangerous for one person to drive. After all, Zhou Yueshen was the only experienced driver in the car. Si Nian knew how to drive, but she didn't have a driver's license.","Not to mention, Zhou Yueshen wouldn't let her drive anyway.","Therefore, taking the train became the most convenient method.","After packing for a long time, Si Nian was exhausted. She turned her body, tugged at Zhou Yueshen's sleeve, and said pitifully, I'm tired, I want to sleep.","Zhou Yueshen smiled softly, his voice very deep and pleasant. He got up to help her pack her skincare products.","After finishing with Si Nian's things, he went to pack for his daughter.","Second Child and Eldest Child packed their own things.","Over the next few days, Zhou Yueshen ran around handling procedures and other tasks for the two children.","When Zhou Yueshen was at home, Si Nian usually didn't have to do anything.","Lin's mother looked at the children—one cooking, one cleaning, and even the youngest practicing calligraphy—and then looked at her daughter, half-lying on the sofa, eating fruit washed by her son, and watching TV like a princess: .....","It was truly... too enviable.","Originally, everyone thought that Si Nian marrying into such a family was really too unfair to her.","But now, from Lin's mother's perspective, the ones being wronged were these children.","Well, she didn't quite understand the educational methods of young people, but that didn't stop her from being envious.","So she started bossing her two sons around like old oxen.","Everything went smoothly.","However, something unusual happened over the past few days.","Perhaps everyone was being too obvious, and Da Huang sensed that something was wrong.","Its mental state suddenly deteriorated over the past few days.","It wouldn't even eat.","Sometimes it would whimper inexplicably.","It acted like the world was ending, going a bit crazy.","It was hard for the family to ignore.","Therefore, on the night before their departure, everyone discussed whether Da Huang should stay or go.","Lin's mother felt that they could help take good care of Da Huang, and it would definitely be fine.","The main issue was the distance—they didn't know how to bring it along.","Could dogs even go on trains?","The train ride was long, and even if they could bring it, how would they handle its eating, drinking, and bathroom needs?","In any case, it would be extremely troublesome.","Si Nian had naturally thought about this problem too.","It was too difficult, so she selectively handed the decision over to Dahuang's dad, Zhou Yueshen.","After all, he was the one who had brought Da Huang home to raise, so it was best for him to decide whether it stayed or went.","Given their last trip to the Northwest, when leaving Da Huang behind resulted in the poor thing going on a hunger strike, Zhou Yueshen realized he couldn't just do that again.","The children raised their hands, hoping Da Huang could go with them.","Second Child said, \"A family should be together, neat and tidy.\"","His firm tone instantly made everyone who was hesitating feel ashamed.","Although Zhou Zedong wasn't as brave as his younger brother, he also loved Da Huang very much and didn't want to leave it home alone.","Even though Da Huang had an incredibly fierce exterior.","Everyone knew that its heart was very fragile.","The moment it sensed something was wrong, it would go on a hunger strike.","It was harder to please than a child.","So, as the head of the family, Zhou Yueshen made the final decision: they would take Da Huang with them.","He knew a truck driver who specifically ran routes to the capital.","Paying someone to transport the dog wouldn't be a problem.","Sometimes having good connections was just that great.","On the day of departure, the Lin family accompanied them to the train station to see them off.","Lin's mother was very reluctant to see them go, holding onto Si Nian and saying a lot of things.","Zhou Yueshen didn't have any relatives to see him off; compared to Si Nian who was surrounded by people, he looked a bit lonely.","The children felt that their father was so pitiful, so they all took the initiative to walk over and hold his hands.","Even his best bro, Yu Dong, didn't come to see him off.","If you asked why, it was because Yu Dong was busy chasing his future wife lately.","He spent all day researching delicious food and had long forgotten his old buddy Zhou Yueshen.","He now understood why Zhou Yueshen had neglected him so much when he first got married.","Back then, he thought Zhou Yueshen was valuing romance over friendship and wasn't a good guy.","Yu Dong now: I'm not a good guy either.","Zhou Yueshen: \"......\"","Jiang Jiu and Second Child were each wearing hats. Jiang Jiu even had a camera hanging around his neck and was wearing glasses—who knows when he bought them. The two children held hands and took pictures.","Leaving the elderly Jiang couple to sadly bid farewell to Jiang Wenqing.","The two kids didn't realize they would be gone for a long time; they were currently very excited, full of curiosity about the new city.","It didn't seem like they were moving to live in another city; it looked more like they were going on a vacation.","Jiang Wenqing had a very weak temperament; his son didn't react at all when he called out.","But the moment Zhou Yueshen spoke, the two children instantly behaved and didn't dare run around.","Jiang Wenqing: Sometimes being a father is truly a helpless endeavor.","Zhou Yueshen merely called out, and Zhou Zehan and Jiang Jiu stood at attention, saying loudly, \"We won't run around anymore!\"","Soon, the train arrived.","Zhou Yueshen and Jiang Wenqing led the group of little munchkins onto the train, one at the front and one at the back.","Terrified that an accident might happen.","With the men around, Si Nian didn't have much to do; the things she carried the most were the snacks Zhou Yueshen had bought for her.","The family boarded the train one by one. The train let out a roar and soon chugged away.","Goodbye, Yungui Chuan City.","The train wasn't fast. This time, Zhou Yueshen had bought tickets in advance and managed to get quite a few sleeper berths.","However, because it was the back-to-school season, many students were heading to their schools to register.","So they only managed to buy four sleeper tickets.","Fortunately, the children were small, so they could squeeze in and sleep.","It didn't matter if the two men slept or not; at least they had seats.","It was better than those who had to stand.","This era was just that cruel; even without a seat, having to stand for over thirty hours, people still scrambled to buy tickets.","Si Nian and the children had taken the train before, so they were fine.","Jiang Jiu, however, unexpectedly got motion sickness. After looking at the scenery outside the window with Second Child for a while, he started throwing up.","Jiang Wenqing gave him some motion sickness medicine, which made him feel a bit better.","But he had no energy left to play. This was also Jiang Jiu's first time on a train. He had originally heard from his second brother that the long train was a lot of fun, but who would have thought it would be so uncomfortable to ride. He lay there weakly and soon fell asleep.","The people of this time were simple and honest. Although the train was noisy, it was also lively. Everyone was very enthusiastic and didn't mind the noise.","Anyone could strike up a conversation with anyone else.","Some people even shared food. Knowing they were going on a long journey, people had brought cards and invited Jiang Wenqing and Zhou Yueshen to play.","Meanwhile, the Gomoku set brought by Second Child also attracted the attention of a group of kids, who gathered around to play with him.","It was just that he couldn't understand what some of them were saying, as they babbled away.","Second Child found it very headache-inducing. Finally, imitating his older brother, he used his broken Mandarin to ask, \"Can you speak Mandarin?\"","Some children couldn't and replied in their dialect, \"I don't speak it.\" It was like a chicken talking to a duck, which made a group of adults burst into laughter.","Si Nian was beautiful, so it was inevitable that she drew attention. Anyone passing by who saw her couldn't help but take a few extra glances.","After walking away, they would pinch the person next to them and say, \"Did you see that? Did you see? That woman looks just like a big movie star. She's so beautiful. How did she curl her hair like that? Do you think I'd look good with curls like that?\"","\"......\"","Zhou Yueshen was worried about Si Nian and the kids, so after being pulled away to play cards for a bit, he came back.","Si Nian was a bit sleepy. Seeing him return, she immediately handed Yaoyao to him and said, \"I'm going to sleep first. If Yaoyao needs to use the bathroom, remember to take her. Don't let her wet her pants.\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded slightly, his voice deep as he said, \"Get some sleep, but don't sleep too much, or you won't be able to sleep tonight.\"","Si Nian mumbled a response and fell asleep the moment her head hit the pillow.","Zhou Yueshen held his daughter and looked at the scenery outside.","Yaoyao was still young after all, and with the train rocking back and forth, she soon fell asleep too.","Even though the child was three years old, to prevent accidents, Zhou Yueshen still changed her into a diaper before putting her on the bed.","A little while later, he went to wake Si Nian up. Si Nian slapped his hand away and pulled the blanket over her head.","Under these circumstances, it was obvious she shouldn't be provoked.","Zhou Yueshen didn't try to wake her again.","As a result, by the time Si Nian woke up, it was already evening.","Zhou Yueshen had bought boxed meals. Now that they had money, he was willing to spend it on the children.","But he made instant noodles for himself.","Si Nian hadn't expected to sleep for so long. She looked at him with a face full of grievance and demanded, \"Why didn't you wake me up?\""]},{"number":400,"title":"Chapter 400: Arrival","paragraphs":["Zhou Yueshen gave a wry smile, \"I did call you.\"","Si Nian had an expression of 'how come I didn't hear it'.","After she spoke, she reached out to pinch Zhou Yueshen's face.","\"Comrade Zhou, you are a big, burly man. You are not allowed to be so gentle next time.\"","She also knew that Zhou Yueshen definitely couldn't bear to wake her up.","If he really wanted to wake her, he would definitely have just lifted her right out of bed like he did with Second Child.","Of course, Zhou Yueshen would absolutely never be that rough with her.","Looking again at the fragrant instant noodles in his hands, and then at her own boxed lunch, she felt even more unhappy. How could a boxed lunch be as tasty as instant noodles?","\"I want to eat yours.\"","Zhou Yueshen was slightly stunned. Why would she want to eat unhealthy instant noodles instead of a proper meal?","As a result, the other children also chimed in, \"Dad, I want to eat instant noodles too.\"","The last time they took the train, Si Nian had bought some for them.","They were spicy, fragrant, and delicious.","Originally, the children's tastes had been on the milder side.","But Si Nian loved to cook all sorts of delicious food, so now they loved eating sour, sweet, and spicy things, and the only thing they refused to eat was anything bitter.","Hearing his second brother's words, Jiang Jiu immediately said to Jiang Wenqing, who was feeding him beside him, \"Dad, I want to eat instant noodles too.\"","Jiang Wenqing immediately and gently said yes.","Seeing his son looking so uncomfortable made his heart ache terribly.","At this moment, even if Jiang Jiu wanted the stars in the sky, he would pluck them down for him.","Zhou Yueshen handed the instant noodles to Si Nian, reached out to take her boxed lunch, and scarfed down a few bites. Hearing his son clamoring to eat it, he shot him a sideways glance. \"No talking while eating or sleeping. If you don't want to eat, go to sleep. I'm not going to spoil you.\"","Zhou Zehan: \"...\"","Jiang Wenqing, who was getting up to make instant noodles and spoil his son: \"...\" Why was he suddenly sweating bullets?","After eating, everyone started to feel bored, and a group of young people took the lead in singing songs.","\"Unity is strength, unity is strength, this strength is iron, this strength is steel, harder than iron, stronger than steel...\"","Si Nian: \"...\" It turns out that liking to sing on a train transcends eras.","She glanced over curiously; it was a group of youths.","They were probably students heading to school to register.","They were full of majestic momentum and brimming with youth.","It was truly enviable.","Si Nian clapped along.","After the singing finished, the atmosphere in the carriage became lively again.","Seeing Second Child and the group of kids playing Gomoku, a few young men and women gathered around to watch.","Seeing Zhou Zedong defeat everyone without a rival, they rubbed their hands together eagerly, expressing their desire to take him down a notch.","However, while their imaginations were glorious, reality was cruel.","After losing several consecutive games, they were laughed at by the crowd.","\"Lao Chen, can you do this or not? You can't even beat a ten-year-old kid.\"","Xiao Chen was sweating profusely. \"What do you guys know? This is a master. I simply can't outplay him; there's killing intent at every turn!\"","After he finished speaking, he looked at Zhou Zedong and smiled ingratiatingly, \"Kid Bro, you're amazing. This little brother concedes defeat.\"","A girl nearby said to Si Nian, \"Wow, your younger brother is so smart and handsome. If only I were a few years younger.\"","\"Tch, you're not that much older. I'm only seventeen, I can do an older-woman-younger-man romance.\"","Si Nian let out a dry laugh. \"...That's my son.\"","Don't be too crazy now.","Her Little Dong was only eleven years old!","The other party: \"Cough, cough, cough!\"","They originally thought she was an older sister making a joke.","Who knew they had made the joke right in front of the mother.","The girls blushed in embarrassment and ran away shyly.","Zhou Zedong looked blankly at the people who had run off.","They finally made it to nightfall, yet Si Nian wasn't sleepy at all.","The children were already fast asleep, and Si Nian deeply envied their sleep quality.","Zhou Yueshen was still keeping her company. Si Nian felt a bit embarrassed; he had been taking care of the kids all day and was already very tired, yet he still had to look after her now.","She gave Zhou Yueshen a push, telling him to go to sleep.","Her bed just happened to be empty.","The bed was too small; it could only fit one person.","Zhou Yueshen fetched some hot water with fragrant floral tea steeped in it, and handed it to her.","\"I'm not sleepy.\"","Beside them, Jiang Wenqing felt very awkward. Not wanting to be a third wheel, he hurriedly said he was going to check on his son and ran off.","Zhou Yueshen made some room and motioned for her to sit over.","Si Nian walked over and leaned on his shoulder.","By now it was dark, and the carriage was very dim.","Neither of them spoke.","Si Nian thought she wouldn't be able to sleep, but unexpectedly, leaning against the man, smelling his familiar scent, and feeling the swaying of the train, she actually drifted off into a daze.","When she woke up, it was already the next day.","The children were lining up to brush their teeth and wash their faces.","Si Nian rubbed her eyes and got up. Zhou Yueshen had already bought food and returned.","\"Mom, we are eating instant noodles today.\"","Second Child happily hugged his instant noodles, held them up, and said to Si Nian.","Si Nian smiled and rubbed his head.","She got up to wash.","The train did not arrive at the Beijing railway station until the evening.","The children were so sleepy they could barely keep their eyes open.","Zhou Yueshen and Jiang Wenqing each held one by the hand and carried one.","It was hard to catch a cab at this hour, but fortunately, Zhou Yueshen had contacted a friend in advance, and someone drove over to pick them up.","Jiang Wenqing had requested a transfer here himself, and someone from his work unit also drove over to take him to his residence.","And so, the group parted ways.","After getting in the car, even Si Nian felt a bit sleepy.","She leaned against the children and fell asleep together with them.","The car bumped along the road. She didn't know how long they had been driving, but they finally arrived at the courtyard house Zhou Yueshen had bought at 1:00 AM.","The surrounding environment wasn't good. Although it was a courtyard house, outside were all old hutongs and alleys, and cars couldn't drive in.","It was narrow and messy.","There weren't even any streetlights.","The children shivered and, except for Yaoyao, all woke up completely.","To think that their first impression of the big city they had looked forward to would be like this.","Zhou Yueshen held his sleeping daughter in one arm and held Si Nian's hand with the other.","Second Child tightly gripped his older brother's clothes.","No joke, this scene was exactly like the ghost movies he had seen on discs.","It was too scary qwq.","The driver who picked them up helped carry the luggage, otherwise they would have had to make two trips.","Looking at this environment, Si Nian finally understood why Zhou Yueshen's friend couldn't sell the place.","If they weren't totally out of options, who would buy this kind of house nowadays?","After walking for about ten minutes, they finally arrived at the courtyard house.","The area of this courtyard house wasn't particularly large. The driver explained that it wasn't that there was no road, but rather the main road was broken and under repair, so they had to walk through the small alleys.","Looking at it now, the situation wasn't that bad.","However, when Si Nian took the key and reached out to open the door, with a clatter, the door lock fell off.","The driver's heart skipped a beat, and he said guiltily, \"There are a lot of thieves around here. Many families' door locks have been sawed off.\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","Zhou Yueshen handed the child to her and said, \"You and the kids stay put for a moment. I'll go take a look first.\"","Si Nian immediately froze. That's right, this house had been unoccupied, and the lock had been broken. It was entirely possible that a thief was living inside.","She had seen news like this before, where hobos or thieves would secretly sneak into empty houses to live. There was one case where someone lived there for ten years before being discovered.","It was simply too terrifying.","It seemed that the security in Beijing wasn't as good as people made it out to be.","Zhou Yueshen walked in and scanned the area. The courtyard wasn't too messy, but the inside of the house looked like it had been completely ransacked.","Sure enough, a thief had broken in.","Fortunately, the intruder was already gone.","He stepped inside and turned on the lights before finally letting Si Nian and the children enter.","Initially, Si Nian had been worried that Zhou Yueshen might have been scammed. However, upon stepping inside, she realized that the house was actually quite new. It had obviously been cleaned recently, only to be turned upside down and left in a mess by the burglar.","The house featured a traditional courtyard-style architecture, with rooms built on all four sides enclosing a central courtyard. Had it been daytime, she surely would have marveled at its beautiful, antique charm."]}]);
